where is dunkirk beach located on a map,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Veere', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Dunkirk.html', 'http://azure-ro.tk/dating-direct-downey-idaho.html', 'https://www.methadoneclinicsusa.com/dunkirk-in', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Noum%C3%A9a.html', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Grenoble.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Papeete']","Dunkirk (/ dʌnˈkɜːrk, ˈdʌnkɜːrk /; French: Dunkerque (dœ̃kɛʁk); Dutch: Duinkerke (n) (ˈdœyŋkɛr (ə) kə (n)) (listen)) is a commune in the Nord department in northern France. It lies 10 kilometres (6.2 mi) from the Belgian border. The population of the city (commune) at the 2016 census was 91,412 inhabitants.","Sister cities of Dunkirk
Dunkirk (French: Dunkerque, pronounced: [dœ̃kɛʁk]; Dutch: Duinkerke(n) [ˈdœynkɛrkə(n)]; Flemish: [ˈdyŋkarkə]) is a commune in the Nord department in northern France. It lies 10 kilometres (6.2 mi) from the Belgian border. The population of the city (commune) at the 1999 census was 70,850 inhabitants (71,300 inhabitants according to February 2004 estimates). The population of the metropolitan area was 265,974 inhabitants according to the 1999 census.
