when does the activation of a motor neuron occur in a stretch reflex,"['https://www.lecturio.com/magazine/muscle-nerve-fiber-properties/', 'https://med.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Anatomy_and_Physiology/Book%3A_Anatomy_and_Physiology_(OpenStax)/Unit_3%3A_Regulation%2C_Integration%2C_and_Control/14%3A_The_Somatic_Nervous_System/14.3%3A_Motor_Processing', 'https://sportsscientists.com/2007/11/muscle-cramps-part-iii/', 'https://woman.thenest.com/disadvantages-active-stretching-21573.html']","When a muscle lengthens, the muscle spindle is stretched and its nerve activity increases. This increases alpha motor neuron activity, causing the muscle fibers to contract and thus resist the stretching. A secondary set of neurons also causes the opposing muscle to relax. The reflex functions to maintain the muscle at a constant length.","404 Not Found We're sorry, but we can't find the page you're looking for. Let's get you back on track. The best place to start again is our homepage. If you're certain this page should exist, please let our support team know at support@lecturio.com so we can help. Best, your Lecturio team [SEP_DOC] 14.3: Motor Processing
