is the wind coming from or going to,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Atmospheric_science', 'https://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/9/11/1203/htm', 'https://community.windy.com/topic/4/about-windy/219', 'https://help.weatherflow.com/hc/en-us/articles/208644807-WEATHERmeter-Technical-Specifications', 'http://sportdocbox.com/Sailing/71433066-Wind-and-air-pressure.html', 'https://www.naturphilosophie.co.uk/global-winds-coriolis-effect-ever-changing-atmospheric-system/?share=google-plus-1', 'http://rp5.md/docs/descript/en']","Wind direction is reported by the direction from which it originates. For example, a northerly wind blows from the north to the south. Wind direction is usually reported in cardinal directions or in azimuth degrees. Wind direction is measured in degrees clockwise from due north. Consequently, a wind blowing from the north has a wind direction of 0 degrees; a wind blowing from the east has a wind direction of 90 degrees; a wind blowing from the south has a wind direction of 180 degrees; and a wind blowing from the west has a wind direction of 270 degrees. In general, wind directions are measured in units from 0 ° to 360 °, but can alternatively be expressed from-180 ° to 180 °.","Access Denied Access Denied You don't have permission to access ""http://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/9/11/1203/htm"" on this server. Reference #18.53532217.1777860177.2d4e670a https://errors.edgesuite.net/18.53532217.1777860177.2d4e670a [SEP_DOC] About Windy
