Canton Tower – China
Canton tower is 600 metre tall and it’s multi-purpose observation tower in China. It was the tallest structure in China prior to the topping out of Shanghai Tower on 3 August 2013. It is now the third tallest tower and the fifth-tallest freestanding structure in the world.
