Ostankino Tower is a television and radio tower in Moscow, Russia. The height of the tower is 540 metre. It is currently the tallest freestanding structure in Europe and eighth tallest in the world.
Ostankino was built to mark the 50th anniversary of the October Revolution. It is named after the Ostankino district of Moscow. Construction began in 1963 and was completed in 1967.
