Version 6.05
Version 6.05 is a minor revision from version 6.04. The main issue
addressed was a problem where sources between 0 and -1 deg dec had the
wrong sign of dec in sources.vlba. There are also a couple of
bug fixes in the plot routines and new Arecibo entries in freq.dat. It was released on June 8, 2006.
- Correct sign of declination for many sources in the range 0 to -1 degrees.
June 2, 2006 RCW.
- Complete update of Arecibo frequency data from Chris Salter June 5, 2006.
- Fix plot programs to deal with multiple setups properly and to fix a recent
bug in the setting of plot scales. Franco Tinarelli, June 7, 2006.
- Reflect offending line when there is a syntax crror. June 8, 2006 RCW.
