what is simmondsia chinensis (jojoba) seed oil,"['https://www.marketplace3000.org/2019/04/07/the-best-skin-care-products-soaps/', 'http://www.drshapiroshairinstitute.com/definitions/def_jojoba-oil.php', 'https://www.marketplace3000.org/home/english-blog-marketplace3000/buy-organic-natural-products/', 'http://serenitydrop.com/best-jojoba-oil/', 'http://www.allingredientsplus.com/product/jojoba-oil/', 'https://pureessential.us/products/jojoba-oil-golden-organic-1', 'https://www.zocalotion.com/pages/ingredients']","Jojoba oil / həˈhoʊbə / (listen) is the liquid produced in the seed of the Simmondsia chinensis (Jojoba) plant, a shrub, which is native to southern Arizona, southern California, and northwestern Mexico. The oil makes up approximately 50% of the jojoba seed by weight. The terms ""jojoba oil"" and ""jojoba wax"" are often used interchangeably because the wax visually appears to be a mobile oil, but as a wax it is composed almost entirely (~ 97%) of mono-esters of long-chain fatty acids and alcohols, accompanied by only a tiny fraction of triglyceride esters. This composition accounts for its extreme shelf-life stability and extraordinary resistance to high temperatures, compared with true vegetable oils.","Jojoba Oil can be used as a hair gel - it helps get rid of hardened crystals which contribute to poor blood circulation and hair loss
Wikipedia says that jojoba oil is ""liquid wax produced in the seed of the jojoba (Simmondsia chinensis) plant, a shrub native to southern Arizona, southern California and northwestern Mexico. The oil makes up approximately 50% of the jojoba seed by weight."" It is useful in the cosmetic industry (it replaced whale oil) and is a natural fungicide.
