History [SEP_DOC] 9-Day Washington DC to New York, U.S. Capitol, Ottawa City, Montreal, Thousand Islands, Corning & Niagara Falls Tour (Free Airport Pickup - NY/NJ OUT)
Tour Code: GOL-WDC-160A
Duration: 9 Day(s) / 8 Night(s)
Tour Guide: Chinese, English
Quality: Budget
Departure City
Destination
Return City
Overview
Experience: UNESCO, Family
Extra (Excluded): Wifi, Meal etc...
Tour Guide:Chinese, English
Join the guided bus tour starting from Washington D.C. We will visit Lincoln Memorial, Vietnam Veterans Memorial, the Korean War Memorial, International Spy Museum, DC cruise, Washington Monument, the World War II Memorial, the Thomas Jefferson Memorial, Smithsonian Institution, Corning, Niagara Falls, Skyline Tower, Toronto, CN Tower, Lake Ontario, China Town, Thousand Island, Ottawa, Canadian museum, Rideau Canal, National War Memorial, Peace Tower, Montreal, Olympic Stadium, Quebec, Montmorency River, Montmorency River, Cambridge, Harvard University, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Boston, Old Trinity Cathedral, Hancock Building, Boston Athenaeum, Boston Park, Swan Lake Park, Boston harbor, New York City , One World Observatory, Hudson River, Wall Street, Trinity Church, New York Stock ExchangeTimes Square,Metropolitan Museum,Madame Tussauds and much more excitement.Good transportation and Professional tour guide will be provided to visitors.
- Only the guides and drivers who have COVID 19 negative can provide services from now onwards. Drivers and Guides will wear the mask. They will disinfect the bus daily. Travelers will have to wear the mask and their temperature will be monitored regularly. Travelers will be provided with hand sanitizer and wipes. We recommend travelers to bring their own hand sanitizer also. Bus sitting will be based on the standards set by the Government.
Itinerary
The first day of the tour is only for your reference, the tour schedule is subject to change upon your arrival. Thanks for choosing your trip with us! Visitors will Arrive at Dulles International Airport (IAD), our professional tour guide will meet you at the Baggage Claim area. You will take our shuttle to the hotel and have some rest. Complimentary airport pick-up service is provided to visitors between 9:00 AM - 10:00 PM. You might need to wait for other visitors. Paid pick-up service is also available for the other time or other airports. Visitors who arrive at the hotel before 5:00 PM can enjoy an optional night tour ($25/person, minimum 4 people). Night stay will be at the hotel.
Complimentary transfer excludes service fee $10/per person
Hotel: Holiday Inn/Crowne Plaza/Shippen Place Hotel or Similar.
Attractions
Washington DC is the capital city of the United States and is also a popular attraction. With the help of Washington DC Night Tours, tourists can enjoy and see everything that the city has to offer.
ITINERARY:
(Summer Itinerary: Apply when DC cruise resume)
U.S. Capitol (Inside Visit, 90 mins) → Lincoln Memorial, Korean War Memorial, Vietnam Veterans Memorial (40 mins) → White House (Outside Visit, 20 mins) → DC Sightseeing Cruise (Optional, 60 mins) → Freely visit and explore Smithsonian Institution Museums (150 mins, without tour guide's escort, Recommend National Air and Space Museum, National Museum of Natural History and so on.) → The tour guide will pick up the guest at the air and Space Museum to the dinner place.
We will also pass by The World War II Memorial, the Thomas Jefferson Memorial etc.
Special Notes: DC Sightseeing Cruise is usually to be closed from Jan to Mar.
(Winter Itinerary: Apply when DC cruise closed)
U.S. Capitol (Inside Visit, 90 mins) → Lincoln Memorial, Korean War Memorial, Vietnam Veterans Memorial (40 mins) → White House (Outside Visit, 20 mins) → Freely visit and explore Smithsonian Institution Museums (180 mins, without tour guide's escort, Recommend National Air and Space Museum, National Museum of Natural History and so on.) → The tour guide will pick up the guest at the air and Space Museum to the dinner place.
We will also pass by The World War II Memorial, the Thomas Jefferson Memorial etc.
Special Notes:
1. DC Sightseeing Cruise is usually to be closed from Jan to Mar.
2. If U.S. Capitol closed to visitors, we will see the exterior of the building from outside. The Capitol Visitor Center is open to visitors from 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Monday through Saturday except for Thanksgiving Day, Christmas Day, New Year's and on Inauguration Day.
Hotel: Holiday Inn/Crowne Plaza/Shippen Place Hotel or Similar.
Attractions
DC Cruise starts from March 15th, and there will be cherry blossom cruises. The boat tours are remarkable, and you can view the monuments and blossoms, besides enjoy at the bar having blossom drink specials. The monuments mesmerize as you see from moonlight cruises.
This memorial of Korean War Veterans is built in honors of those marines who fought for their country. A nice place with good architecture located south of the Reflecting Pool at the National Mall where you can see many artifacts.
The Library of Congress is a research library officially serving the United States Congress and is the United States the de facto national library. It is the oldest federal cultural institution. It is a beautiful building and visiting during Spring/Summer is time-consuming as it is crowded. The reading room view from the balcony is superb.
Refers to the monument constructed in honor of Abraham Lincoln who was the 16th president of United States of America. The monument is situated at the west of national Mall in Washington.
The World War II Memorial is memorial that was established in order to commemorate the fellow Americans who served the armed forces during the World War II.
It is one of the utmost communicating museums in the world; the Newseum experience also touches the development of electric communiqué from the birth of wireless, to the scientific tools of the existing and the upcoming. It’s unique.
Lies on the coasts of Virginia's Potomac River, and similar to Seattle, tourists can enjoy the mesmerizing sights of Washington, by Potomac Cruise which is truly a place for a relaxing and enjoyable sightseeing experience of the capital city of America.
The Smithsonian Institution is located in Washington Dc, USA with museums including world’s largest museum also known as Smithsonian museum and research centers. It is also called “United States National Museum”.
This is a Thomas Jefferson Memorial; he served as the third president of the United States. This remarkable neoclassical building has been standing since 1943. It has been estimated that more than 2 million people visit the memorial each year.
The building is founded in 1789, located in Washington, DC and open to the public except for weekend days, is the seat of Supreme Court and judicial branch. It features all the qualities that attract a tourist in DC. Visitors wait for hours to get into this supremely beautiful building. Two justice statues are located on both sides of US Supreme Court building in foreground. Every year local and international tourists visit this place to feast their eyes.
Everyday hundreds of tourists and natives visit Vietnam Veterans Memorial to honor the veterans who lost their lives in Vietnam War. Built not much long ago, it is a place where you can see memorials and artifacts.
Washington DC is the capital city of the United States and is also a popular attraction. With the help of Washington DC Night Tours, tourists can enjoy and see everything that the city has to offer.
On the National Mall in Washington, Washington Monument is an obelisk designated in October 1966. More than 600,000 visitors visit this park every year. It has been reopened for tourists after repairing due to earthquake and hurricane in Virginia.
The federal capital of America which is a District of Columbia is said to be as Washington DC. The state is approved in the year 1790. It has 409 feet highest elevation. The district has 22nd rank among other states of US.
White House is an official residence/house of president of America and the place where every government’s strategies and plans devised. The architecture of this somehow classical mansion is a global icon.
We will arrive at one of Fortune Global 500’s headquarters, Corning, to visit the Museum of Glass, which is dedicated to the history, art, and science behind glassmaking. After lunch, we are going to see the renowned Niagara Falls. Overlooking American Fall, the Horseshoe Fall and the Bridal Veil Fall, you will be astounded by the deafening roar of the falls. It’s the combination of height and volume that makes Niagara Falls so beautiful.
Itinerary：
Corning Museum of Glass (Optional, 90 mins) → Niagara Falls State Park → Maid of the Mist (Optional, 30 mins) → US Niagara IMAX Movie (Optional, 30 mins) → Niagara Falls In-depth tour (Optional, 120mins, include Old Fort Niagara(60mins) and Whirlpool State Park(15mins) ) → Niagara Falls Night Tour (Optional, 90 mins)
Special notes:
1. If not join the Niagara In-depth Tour, you can stay at the Niagara Falls State Park with longer free time.
2. We will watch the IMAX Movie and take Niagara Falls Cruise either in U.S. or in Canada but for only once, which is subject to change upon actual situation.
3. Maid of the Mist usually opens during late April to early November.
4. If the Maid of the Mist is closes, we will visit Niagara Falls Jetboat (Optional, 60 mins) instead. Niagara Jetboat tour will be closed if the weather is extremer or river icy condition. Kids must be 4-year-old or above to be on board for safety concerns.
Hotel：Adam's Mark BuffaloOr Radisson Hotel Niagara Falls-Grand IslandOr DoubleTree by Hilton Hotel Buffalo - AmherstOr equivalent
Attractions
The American Falls is part of the three waterfalls that make up the Niagara Falls. It lets visitors enjoy an exhilarating experience of its beautiful surroundings and fascinating history.
Falling from a height of 181 feet, the rushing waters of the beautiful Bridal falls, located between Goat Island and Luna Island, drench you with their beauty and spray.
A glass-made museum located in the NYC is known as Corning Museum of Glass. The science, history and art of the glass can be seen at this place.
Corning is a city that is located in Steuben County in New York, it is situated on the Chemung River. The population of the city is around 11,000 and the city is named after Erastus Corning.
The place is sometimes also referred to as Canadian falls. Potentially the Horseshoe Falls are the part and parcel of the famous NiagaraFalls and is located on the Niagara River. It is known as the Canadian Falls due to its location in Canada.
Niagara Falls is a very famous spot for tourists, one thing to do there is to go on a Jet Boat Ride. This is a very exciting thing to do in Niagara Fall as it is a really different experience.
Maid of the Mist Boat is a famous water ride that runs in Niagara Falls. The boat tour provide beautiful scenic views to the visitors.
Niagara Adventure Movie Theater is built in the Niagara Falls State Park which is located in the City of Niagara Falls. It was built in 1885 and is a really famous tourists attraction,
Niagara Falls comprises of mainly three waterfalls, the American Falls, Bridal Veil Falls, Horseshoe Falls. The Niagara Falls Scenic Tour explores the top-notch charms of Niagara Falls, as well as get soaked in the mists of gigantic waterfalls while discovering the beauty of this world’s wonder.
For over 75 years, visitors from across the globe come to Niagara Falls, They have been able to witness the impressive nighttime illumination of the American and Horseshoe falls. Every season visitors get to experience the autumn in a new way. Complete night-view of Niagara Falls on some summer evenings might be limited or not available because of the late sunset time and the US Federal Government rules on the driving hours.
Situated close to Youngstown in New York, US, Old Fort Niagara is a reinforcement constructed to safeguard the interests of New France in America. The Niagara fall and the museum have made the place even more attractive.
On the north of the city of Niagara Falls, there is a park located in Niagara County known as Whirlpool State Park. From the hiking to the picnic tables and pavilions, everything can be enjoyed at this park.
In the morning, guests will continue sightseeing in the Niagara Falls. We will cross the border to Canada through the Rainbow Bridge. You will also watch a dramatic 45-minute IMAX film which will further discover the culture and history of the Niagara Fall! Later, take the ride to the top of the Skylon Tower which is 775 feet above the falls! Relax and enjoy your meal at the 360-degree Revolving Dining Room. After lunch, guests will arrive in Toronto - the largest city and financial center of Canada
Itinerary:
Hornblower Niagara Cruise (Optional, 30 mins) → Skylon Tower, Lunch (Optional, 100 mins) → CN tower (Optional, 60 mins) → Mariposa Toronto Harbor Cruise (Optional, 60 mins) → Toronto Chinese Dinner (Optional, 60 mins)
If time allows, we will visit Ripley's Aquarium of Canada (Optional, 60mins).
We will also pass by: Rainbow Bridge, Toronto City Hall
Special notes:
1. We will take Niagara Falls Cruise either in U.S. or in Canada but for only once, which is subject to change upon actual situation.
2. Hornblower Niagara Cruise usually opens during late April to early November,
3. Admission to the Ride-to-the-Top and Indoor/Outdoor Observation Deck Niagara Falls attractions is FREE when dining at Skylon Tower.
Hotel: Crowne Plaza /Marriott/Don Valley hotel or Similar.
Attractions
The CN tower is a concrete communications tower and is 553 meters tall, it was built on old railway lands and was completed in 1976 and became the world’s largest freestanding structure.
Food is something that is enjoyed by each and every person, if you like French food then the French Banquet is the place for you. It is located in Quebec and serves really great and delicious food.
In the heart of Niagara Gorge, a thrilling boat tour takes travelers from Canada to Great Gorge. This exciting tour is known as Hornblower Niagara Cruise.
In the premises of Niagara Falls, there is film theatre known as IMAX Theatre. People visit this theatre to enjoy live shows and movies related to Niagara’s History.
Maid of the Mist Boat Ride is one of the most beautiful boat rides that you will ever have. If you happen to go on this ride then you will surely cherish it as one of the most memorable moments.
If you want to see and enjoy everything that the Toronto Harbor has to offer then you should probably seek help from Mariposa Cruises. This service will give you a detailed tour or cruise of the Toronto Harbor that you should enjoy.
Niagara Falls is situated on the border of Canada and the United States, this is why there is an other City of Niagara Falls that is situated on the Western Bank of the river in Ontario Canada.
The Rainbow Bridge also known as the Niagara Falls International in United States is a world famous tourist site and connects the east of US to the west of Canada.
Ripley’s Aquarium of Canada is a public aquarium located in Toronto, Ontario. The aquarium is owned by Ripley Entertainment and is one of the three aquariums owned by the company.
At the Skylon Tower situated at the Niagara Falls in Ontario Canada, there lies a revolving restaurant which is about 775ft above the Niagara Falls. It gives one rotation per hour and meal is served with leisure.
The Skylon Tower is located in the Niagara Falls at Ontario in Canada. It is headed towards the sky and gives a 360 degree of the Niagara Falls. The tower is 263 meters above the Niagara Falls.
Toronto City Hall represents the history of the city and the creation of itself. It has a volume of things for its visitors to learn about from Council Chambers to Podium Green Roof.
Toronto Dinner, especially the dinner cruise offers a unique dining experience. Visitors can dance and dine the night watching the sun set under the starry skies. The visitors are sure to spend a memorable evening on this breathtaking skyline watching the city’s waterfront and sounds from the harbor on the waterfront.
Situated along the south northern coast of the Lake Ontario, Toronto is great and culturally diverse. The green trees and ravines, trails and parks and recreation are the things attracting visitors in a great number.
In the morning, guests will enjoy the beauty of Thousand Islands on a cruise boat (summer only). We will be driving on Highway 401 along St. Lawrence River and reach Canada’s Capital and political center, Ottawa. Next, we will go to Montreal for dinner, known as “Paris of North America”, a French-speaking and second largest city of Canada. After sunset, we will go to the grand Notre-Dame Basilica for night view.
