 Industry Together Under One Roof News May 1, 2026 0 Gifts India Expo, India’s leading B2B exhibition for corporate,... Popular Payments Heroes League (PHL) 2026 Announces Upcoming Corporate Cricket Showcase at Press Conference in Dyaus Court, Bhubaneswar Sports May 2, 2026 0 Axis Bank Comes Onboard as Title Sponsor for PHL... TIME Honors PADI as TIME100 Companies Industry Leader in Sustainability AI May 1, 2026 0 Iconic magazine recognizes the world’s largest diving organization for reshaping travel, citizen science, and ocean conservation... Gifts India Expo 2026 Opens Visitor Registrations for 32nd Edition, Bringing the Entire Gifting Industry Together Under One Roof News May 1, 2026 0 Gifts India Expo, India’s leading B2B exhibition for corporate,... Sitemap Home Business Tech Education Interviews and Features Others Books CSR Environment Entertainment Health and Wellness Finance Hospitality International Lifestyle Sports Startup Travel © 2022 tagDiv. All Rights Reserved. Made with Newspaper Theme. Get $10 by answering a Simple Survey. Click Here [SEP_DOC] Barium nitrate has a lot of uses, you know what, do you want to know barium nitrate, you want to find out what the barium nitrate is used in the industry, following the small addendum we go to understand:
Barium nitrate is the nitrate of barium, the formula is BA (NO3) 2. Barium nitrate is a colorless or white cubic crystal, dissolved in water and concentrated sulfuric acid, insoluble in alcohols and concentrated nitric acid. Barium nitrate is heated to decompose and release oxygen, and contact with organic matter, friction or impact can cause combustion or explosion. As with other soluble, barium nitrate is poisonous and must be noted when used.
Barium nitrate is widely used in many fields, in the inorganic industry for the manufacture of various barium salts (such as barium chloride, barium sulfate, barium carbonate, etc.), barium oxide, barium peroxide and so on. Glass industry is used as glass coloring agent. The defence industry is used to make explosives, green flares and tracer. Low temperature salt bath for metal heat treatment in metallurgical industry. Ceramic industry is used to make glaze medicine. Light industry is used to make green fireworks. Used as oxidant in chemical production. Analytical chemistry for the determination of sulphuric acid and chromic acid. It is also used in the electronics and pharmaceutical industries.
Barium nitrate is often used to make fireworks, fireworks, green fireworks, green flares, military munitions, analytical reagents, tracer, optical glass, pottery uranium, low-temperature salt bath, barium salt, barium nitrate can also be used for the manufacture of barium oxide, barium peroxide and other barium salts, but also for the manufacture of optical glass and pottery glaze medicine. Can be used as explosives, green fireworks, flares and tracer. can also be used in anti-corrosion, chemical reagents and medicine, but also for metal heat treatment of low-temperature salt bath.
But like all soluble barium compounds, ingestion or inhalation of barium nitrate is poisonous. Symptoms of poisoning include muscle contraction (especially in the face and neck), vomiting, diarrhea, abdominal pain, muscular fibrillation, anxiety, weakness, labored breathing, arrhythmia and convulsions. Heart failure or respiratory failure that occurs after a few hours or days of exposure to barium nitrate may cause death. Barium nitrate may also cause damage to the kidneys."
