- a boost regulator which has the effect that the non-touch thermometers 100 , 200 and 300 in FIG. 1-3 , the non-touch thermometer 2400 in FIG. 24 , the hand-held device 2100 in FIG. 21 and/or the computer 2200 in FIG.
- the non-touch thermometers 100 , 200 and 300 in FIG. 1-3 , the non-touch thermometer 2400 in FIG. 24 , the hand-held device 2100 in FIG. 21 and/or the computer 2200 in FIG. 22 are started by the operator, at block 606 , only the microprocessor 102 , microprocessor 2404 In FIG. 24 , main processor 2102 in FIG. 21 or processing unit 2204 in FIG. 22 , digital infrared sensor 108 , and low power LCD (e.g. display device 114 ) are turned on for the first 1 second, at block 608 , to take the temperature measurement via the digital infrared sensor 108 and generate the body core temperature result via the microprocessor 102 in FIG. 1-3 , microprocessor 2404 in FIG.
