thin the Kingdom of Denmark, located between the Arctic and Atlantic Oceans, east of the Canadian Arctic Archipelago. Though physiographically a part of the continent of North America, Greenland has been ethnically, politically and culturally associated with Europe (specifically Norway and Denmark, the colonial powers, as well as the nearby island of Iceland) for more than a millennium. In 2008, the people of Greenland passed a referendum supporting greater autonomy; 75% of votes cast were in favour. Greenland is, in area, the world's largest island, over three-quarters of which is covered by the only contemporary ice sheet outside of Antarctica.  Read about Greenland in the Wikipedia Latitude: 69° 38' 7.50"" NLongitude: -42° 10' 25.29"" W Population: 56,375 Capital: Nuuk Country ISO codes: GL / GRL / 304 Oficial languages: Danish (da), English (en), Kalaallisut; Greenlandic (kl) Oficial coin(s): Krone (DKK)  GPS coordinates of Greenland Download as JSON  DD CoordinatesDMS CoordinatesGEOHASH CoordinatesUTM Coordinates23W 609732.42472369 7727754.4944558  Places of interest in Greenland 1 Airport in GreenlandShow all airports of Greenland in the mapManiitsoq airport ( JSU )Maniitsoq airport (JSU), Greenland Show in map Show coordinates1 Natural park in GreenlandShow all natural parks of Greenland in the mapNortheast Greenland National ParkNortheast Greenland National Park, Greenland Show in map Show coordinates © Latitude.to (v1.68-gg) 2026 Disclaimer and errors Cookies policy Articles by country"
