We have a selection of series for you to delve into or find out more about. These range from Marvel’s Jessica Jones to recently released GLOW. Sci-fi, comedy, crime drama and animation; there will be something for everyone!
In no particular order, let’s get started.
1. Orange Is The New Black
Orange Is The New Black (OITNB) is a comedy crime drama series that first premiered on the 11th July 2013 on Netflix. It’s adapted from Piper Kerman’s memoir, Orange Is the New Black: My Year in a Women’s Prison (2010), about her experiences at a federal women’s prison. The Netflix series revolves around Piper Chapman, and how she has to survive in prison, adapting to overcome multiple different struggles. Episodes often feature flashbacks from significant inmates’ or prison guards’ pasts, that come to explain how they ended up in prison or to develop their backstory. An aspect Orange Is The New Black focuses closely on is how overcrowding, guard brutality and funding cuts affect the prisoners’ health and well-being. One of the main conflicts running throughout the series is when the warden’s efforts to give the prisoners their basic needs conflicts with the business interests of MCC, a private prison company. There’s no doubt in saying that Orange Is The New Black has become one of the streaming services’ most popular original series. For its second season, the series received four Emmy nominations, including Outstanding Drama Series. The series has also received six Golden Globe nominations, an American Film Institute Award and a Peabody Award.
For fans of: Breaking Bad, How To Get Away With Murder, The Get Down, House of Cards
2. Jessica Jones
Marvel’s Jessica Jones is an action crime drama series that first premiered on the 20th November 2015. It’s based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name and is set in the Marvel Cinematic Universe. The series stars Jessica Jones, a former superhero who reboots her life by opening her own detective agency and becoming a private investigator; dealing with cases that involve people with incredible abilities. IGN has named Jessica Jones the best Netflix original programming series released to date. In January 2016, Netflix renewed Jessica Jones for a second season.
For fans of: Gotham, Iron Fist, Luke Cage
3. Santa Clarita Diet
Santa Clarita Diet is a comedy horror series that premiered on the 3rd February 2017, with 10 episodes in its first season. It portrays the lives of Sheila and Joel Hammond who are real estate agents in Santa Clarita, California. Their lives change and take a dark turn when Sheila, played by Drew Barrymore, goes through a transformation – becoming a zombie. The first season has received generally positive reviews, but there has been criticism for the number of graphic scenes. In late March 2017, Netflix announced that the series had been renewed for a second season, which will premiere in 2018.
For fans of: Shaun of the Dead, Scary Movie, Scream Queens, A Series of Unfortunate Events
https://youtu.be/xjRnbOgoAUQ
4. BoJack Horseman
One of the most different ones compared to the rest on this list is BoJack Horseman. BoJack Horseman is a comedy drama series in the form of animation. The series’ first season premiered on the 22nd August 2014, with a Christmas special premiering on the 19th December. It stars Will Arnett as the title character, BoJack Horseman, with the supporting cast including Aaron Paul, Paul F. Tompkins, Alison Brie and Amy Sedaris. The series is set in an alternate world where humans and humanoid-esque animals live side by side. BoJack Horseman was the star of a sitcom in the ’90s, Horsin’ Around, but is now washed up, complaining about anything, living in Hollywood (later known as ‘Hollywoo’), trying to make a return to celebrity relevance. The series is known for its dark comedy and satirical nature. BoJack Horseman currently has three seasons but has been renewed for a fourth, scheduled to premiere in the summer of 2017.
For fans of: Bob’s Burgers, Rick and Morty, American Dad, Family Guy
5. The Get Down
The Get Down is an American musical drama series. It premiered its first part that contained six episodes on the 12th August 2016. The series is set in the Bronx in the 1970s and follows the rise of hip-hop and disco music through the eyes of teenagers. The second part of the first season that contained five episodes was released on the 7th April 2017. In May 2017, Netflix announced that The Get Down would not be renewed for another season, but that doesn’t mean you can’t enjoy what’s already been made!
For fans of: Orange Is The New Black, Dear White People, Nashville, Eyewitness
https://youtu.be/usv442G6H8A
6. GLOW
One of the newest Netflix originals is GLOW. GLOW is a comedy drama series set in Los Angeles, 1985 and premiered on the 23rd June 2017. The series revolves around a fictionalisation of the GLOW wrestling league from the 1980s. The creators of the show, Liz Flahive and Carly Mensch, came across the 2012 documentary GLOW: The Story of the Gorgeous Ladies of Wrestling. They found the storyline intriguing as a way of exploring the aftermath of the 1970s Women’s Liberation Movement. A tension that’s maintained in the series is whether or not the league was exploiting or empowering women.
For fans of: Stranger Things, Orange Is The New Black
https://youtu.be/AZqDO6cTYVY
7. Stranger Things
I’m sure you all know about Stranger Things by now, but if you haven’t seen it and need more convincing, or want to find out more, continue reading! Stranger Things is a sci-fi, horror drama series that was released on the 15th July 2016. It’s created, written, directed and co-executive produced by the Duffer Brothers. The first season stars Winona Ryder, David Harbour, Millie Bobby Brown, Natalia Dyer, Charlie Heaton, Finn Wolfhard and Noah Schnapp. The series is set in the fictional town of Hawkins, Indiana in the 1980s. The first season focuses on the investigation of the disappearance of a young boy, and what terrifying dark forces his family, friends and the local police chief have to face in order to get him back, along with the sudden appearance of a telekinetic young girl. Stranger Things has quickly become one of Netflix’s most popular series, receiving positive reviews regarding its atmosphere, soundtrack, acting and homages to 1980s genre films. In August 2016, Netflix renewed the series for a second season, which is set the be released in October 2017.
For fans of: The X-Files, Black Mirror, Breaking Bad, Narcos, The Walking Dead
https://youtu.be/XWxyRG_tckY
8. Daredevil
Daredevil is an action, crime drama based on the Marvel Comics of the same name. It was released on Netflix on the 10th April 2015, with the second season being released on the 18th March 2016. The series is set in the Marvel Cinematic Universe and Matt Murdock, otherwise known as Daredevil, fighting crime as a blind lawyer by day, and vigilante by night, with his other senses enhanced. Daredevil has been nominated for five Primetime Emmy Awards 2016 and has won the 2016 Saturn Award for Best New Media Television Series. In July 2016, Daredevil was renewed for a third season.
For fans of: Gotham, Iron Fist, Luke Cage
9. Black Mirror
Black Mirror is a British sci-fi thriller anthology series created by Charlie Brooker. It’s dark and satirical themes examine society, specifically that related to the consequences of new technology. Each episode is standalone and typically takes place within an alternate reality, or somewhere within the near future. Black Mirror provides different concepts, ideas and thought-provoking situations that will leave you seeing the world in a whole new light. The series was first broadcast on Channel 4 in 2011, but in late 2015, Netflix commissioned the third season.
For fans of: Sherlock, True Detective, Humans, Doctor Who
10. A Series of Unfortunate Events
A Series of Unfortunate Events is another recently released Netflix original. It’s a dark comedy drama series based on the children’s novel series of the same name by Lemony Snicket. The show is an adventure drama series that stars Neil Patrick Harris, Patrick Warburton, Malina Weissman, Louis Hynes and K. Todd Freeman. The first season premiered on the 13th January 2017 and consists of eight episodes that are adapted around the first four books of the series. The premise of the series surrounds the Baudelaire children who have been placed into the care of their distant relative, Count Olaf, after their parents were killed in a mysterious fire. A Series of Unfortunate Events has been renewed for a second and third season.
For fans of: Stranger Things, The OA, Sense8, Santa Clarita Diet, 13 Reasons Why"
how long has jose mourinho been a manager for manchester united,"['https://shop.thecircusart.it/product/allenatore-jose-mourinho/', 'https://community.sigames.com/tags/mourinho/', 'http://dailyentertainment.com/highest-paid-football-managers-in-the-world-2014/', 'http://mrbigband.info/fresh-post/jose-mourinho-coat.htm', 'http://watchetdesign.com/Chinese-translation-community/201012/03-216.html', 'http://scan.lusu.co.uk/index.php/2019/02/04/jose-mourinho-from-the-special-one-to-the-one-left-behind/', 'https://www.dummysports.com/list-of-serie-a-winners/']","In 2008, Mourinho moved to Serie A club Internazionale. Within three months he had won his first Italian honour, the Supercoppa Italiana, and completed the season by winning the Serie A title. In 2009 -- 10, Inter became the first Italian club to win the treble of Serie A, Coppa Italia and the Champions League, also the first time Inter had won the latter competition since 1965. He is one of only five coaches to have won the European Cup with two different teams, along with Ernst Happel, Ottmar Hitzfeld, Jupp Heynckes and Carlo Ancelotti. He won the first ever FIFA World Coach of the Year Award in 2010. He then signed with Real Madrid in 2010, winning the Copa del Rey in his first season. The following year, he won the La Liga and became the fifth coach, after Tomislav Ivić, Ernst Happel, Giovanni Trapattoni and Eric Gerets, to have won league titles in at least four different countries: Portugal, England, Italy and Spain. After leaving Madrid in June 2013, Mourinho returned to England to manage Chelsea for a second spell, during which they won another league championship, but was sacked on 17 December 2015, after a poor run of results left Chelsea just outside the relegation zone. Following several months out of the game after losing his job at Chelsea for the second time, Mourinho was confirmed as the new manager of Manchester United on 27 May 2016.","Highest Paid Football Managers In The World This Season
Top 10 Highest Paid Soccer Managers In The World this season
Who are the highest paid Football Managers in the world this season? It is amazing how much money there is spent in Football, From sponsorship to Players Wages millions are spent each season, with all the buzz of the latest clubs signings and how much football clubs spent over the just closed transfer window.
We pretty much know how much the players are getting paid, but what about the Club Managers? Who is the highest paid Football Manager? With all the talk of Footballers wages and fee’s we overlook the fact the Football Clubs appointed managers are paid quite a fair bit, that’s why I decided to investigate how who are the top earners to see if they are worth what they are getting paid. Who do you think is the The Highest Paid Football Managers In The World this season?
Top 10 highest paid football managers in the World this season
Let us all take a look at the 10 Highest Paid Football/Soccer Managers In The World this season:
10. Manuel Pellegrini – Manchester City – £3.54 million per year
Manuel Pellegrini led Villarreal to a third place finish in La Liga in 04/05, a Champions League semi-final in 05/06 and a second place finish in La Liga in 07/08 he attracted attention from top clubs like Real Madrid, Pellegrini took over the Spanish Giants and Led them to finish just three points behind rivals Barcelona, he then left the Spanish heavyweights to take over as boss at Malaga in 2010, Pellegrini led them to a fourth place finish in the league and the quarter-finals of the 12/13 Champions League, Pellegrini was then offered the top job at Manchester City where he signed a three year deal and continues to manage the club still today whopping in a nice wage of £3.54 million per year.
9. Jurgen Klopp – Borussia Dortmund – £3.66 million per year
Jurgen Klopp has been the saviour of Borussia Dortmund, The German football manager and former player took Borussia Dortmund from the struggling side it was into the dynamic top club it is today. Klopp took the German side all the way in 2011 and 2012 winning the Bundesliga, Jurgen then went on to take the side win the DFB–Pokal in 2012 and the DFL–Supercup in 2013, Klopp really gained notoriety when he took Borussia Dortmund to the Champions League, they went on to play against Real Madrid, Manchester City and Ajax, without losing a game and then beating Real Madrid in the semi–finals of the 12/13 Champions League. Dortmund lost the final to Bayern Munich 2-1. A very sought after Football Manager Jurgen Klopp rakes in an very nice £3.66 million per year
8. Tata Martino – FC Barcelona – £4.59 million per year
Tata Martino is well know for favouring very high pressing and attacking style of football, this was the perfect choice for Barcelona who appointed him as Manager in 2013 on a two-year contract, they knew he was the right man for the job when Barcelona defeated Levante 7-0 in his first match as manager of the 2013/14 La Liga season, by the end of the same month Tata Martino had gone undefeated in Barca’s first 16 matches. He is currently Manager of the Argentine National Team.
7. Arsene Wenger – Arsenal – £7.55 million per year
This French football manager and former player. He has been the manager of Arsenal since 1996, an astonishing honour in itself, Arsene Wenger is the club’s longest-serving manager and the most successful Football Manager Arsenal has ever had in the terms of major titles won,
6. Marcello Lippi – Guangzhou Evergrande – £9.05 million per year
