what is the purpose of a mise en place list,"['https://theteachingfactor.wordpress.com/tag/genius-hour/', 'https://the5oclockrush.com/2014/04/30/the-chefs-secret-is/', 'https://www.mise-en-place.ca/', 'http://seasonalandholidayrecipeexchange.weebly.com/linky-parties--tips/archives/04-2015', 'https://maggiesvitamins.blog/tag/cooking-from-scratch/', 'https://app.robly.com/archive?id=ec8a19fa3c665ed4847efe5f781c9e8f&v=true', 'https://www.maggieclairedesigns.com/blog-1']","Mise en place (French pronunciation: ​ (mi zɑ̃ ˈplas)) is a French culinary phrase which means ""putting in place"" or ""everything in its place."" It refers to the set up required before cooking, and is often used in professional kitchens to refer to organizing and arranging the ingredients (e.g., cuts of meat, relishes, sauces, par-cooked items, spices, freshly chopped vegetables, and other components) that a cook will require for the menu items that are expected to be prepared during a shift.","“The Bear” is a compelling TV series on Hulu that offers many lessons about creativity, passion, and the pursuit of excellence—principles that can be effectively applied to teaching Genius Hour and passion projects in the classroom. This past month I binged all three seasons and was most compelled the way Carmy nurtured his chefs in Season 2. Here are some key takeaways from the series that teachers can use to nurture students’ curiosity and drive:
1. The Power of Passion and Purpose
- Lesson: The main character, Carmen “Carmy” Berzatto, returns to his family’s struggling restaurant out of a deep sense of responsibility and passion for cooking. His dedication to his craft drives him to improve the restaurant despite numerous challenges.
- Application: Encourage students to choose projects that they are genuinely passionate about during Genius Hour. Emphasize the importance of pursuing something that matters to them personally, as this intrinsic motivation can lead to deeper engagement and more meaningful learning experiences.
2. Embracing Failure as a Learning Opportunity
- Lesson: Throughout the series, Carmy and his team face numerous setbacks and failures. However, each failure is treated as a learning experience, an opportunity to grow and refine their skills.
- Application: Teach students that failure is a natural part of the learning process. In Genius Hour, students should be encouraged to take risks and experiment, knowing that setbacks are valuable for gaining insights and improving their work. Celebrate the lessons learned from mistakes as much as the successes.
3. Collaboration and Teamwork
- Lesson: The kitchen in “The Bear” is a high-pressure environment where teamwork is crucial. Each member of the team has a role to play, and success depends on effective communication, trust, and collaboration.
- Application: Foster a collaborative environment in your classroom where students can work together on their passion projects. Encourage them to share ideas, offer feedback, and support each other’s efforts. Highlight how collaboration can lead to better outcomes and innovative solutions.
4. Attention to Detail and Craftsmanship
- Lesson: Carmy’s meticulous attention to detail and his commitment to excellence in every dish he prepares is a recurring theme in the series. This focus on craftsmanship is what sets his work apart.
- Application: Encourage students to take pride in their work by paying attention to details and striving for quality in their projects. Teach them that doing something well, even if it’s challenging, is rewarding and worthwhile. Provide them with the tools and resources they need to refine their projects and achieve a high standard.
5. Resilience and Perseverance
- Lesson: The characters in “The Bear” face numerous obstacles, both personal and professional. Their resilience and determination to overcome these challenges are key to their growth and success.
- Application: Teach students the importance of perseverance in pursuing their passion projects. Help them develop resilience by encouraging them to keep going even when they encounter difficulties. Share stories of famous inventors, artists, and scientists who persisted despite setbacks, reinforcing the idea that resilience is a critical component of success.
6. Finding Inspiration in Unexpected Places
- Lesson: The series often shows how inspiration can come from unexpected sources, whether it’s a conversation with a colleague, a memory, or even a mistake in the kitchen.
- Application: Encourage students to keep an open mind and seek inspiration from a variety of sources. During Genius Hour, they can explore different subjects, talk to people with diverse experiences, and observe the world around them to fuel their creativity and curiosity. Emphasize the importance of being curious and looking for connections between seemingly unrelated ideas.
7. The Importance of Reflecting on Progress
- Lesson: Carmy frequently reflects on his journey, thinking about what he has learned and how he can improve. This self-reflection helps him stay focused on his goals and make informed decisions.
- Application: Incorporate regular reflection into the Genius Hour process. Have students periodically assess their progress, reflect on what they’ve learned, and think about how they can improve. Reflection helps students internalize their learning and stay motivated as they work on their projects.
8. Balancing Structure with Creativity
- Lesson: While the kitchen in “The Bear” has strict rules and procedures, there is also room for creativity and innovation. This balance is essential for both consistency and growth.
- Application: Provide students with a structured framework for their passion projects, but also give them the freedom to explore and innovate. This balance will help them stay organized while also allowing their creativity to flourish. For example, set deadlines and goals but leave the specifics of how they achieve those goals up to them.
9. Investing in Growth and Education
- Lesson: In “The Bear,” Carmy recognizes the potential in his team and takes proactive steps to help them grow by sending them to culinary school or encouraging them to learn new skills. He understands that investing in their education will not only improve their craft but also empower them to contribute more effectively to the team.
- Application: Encourage students to seek out additional resources, workshops, or learning opportunities that can help them develop their skills and deepen their understanding of their passion projects. Just as Carmy invests in his team’s education, provide students with access to books, online courses, or mentorship that can enhance their learning experience. Emphasize the importance of continuous learning and growth, and support students in finding opportunities that align with their interests.
10. Mentorship and Guidance
- Lesson: Carmy acts as a mentor to the chefs in his kitchen, offering guidance, sharing his expertise, and helping them navigate the challenges of the culinary world. His mentorship is crucial in helping them develop confidence and refine their skills.
- Application: Create a mentorship dynamic in the classroom by pairing students with more experienced peers, community members, or even yourself as the teacher. This mentorship can help guide students through their passion projects, providing them with advice, feedback, and encouragement. Just as Carmy helps his team grow through mentorship, fostering a supportive environment where students can learn from others will enhance their learning and help them achieve their goals.
I can go back again and watch all three seasons. There are so many small moments of where learning takes the center stage to the high anxiety moments within The Bear as it gets off the ground. I particularly love all the flashbacks that Carmy has with the chefs who taught him over the years – the celebrity chef cameos are wonderful. The time and individualized attention they provided Carmy helped him to master his craft and become the world renowned chef that he is known for. I think about these lessons and how we can create a nurturing environment that not only encourages students to pursue their passions but also provides them with the tools, guidance, and support they need to grow and succeed in their endeavors. [SEP_DOC] Build a website. Sell your stuff. Write a blog. And so much more.
