what are the requirements to be in the state senate the house,"['http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/treasurers-home-york-3.html', 'http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/dwelling-3.html', 'http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/tag/texas', 'http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/tag/membership', 'http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/united-states-home-of-representatives.html', 'http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/properties-for-sale-in-and-around-bolton.html', 'http://www.bestwatchesunder1000.net/is-canceled-will-finish-run-after-season-8-2.html']","Article I, Section 2 of the Constitution sets three qualifications for representatives. Each representative must: (1) be at least twenty-five years old; (2) have been a citizen of the United States for the past seven years; and (3) be (at the time of the election) an inhabitant of the state he or she represents. Members are not required to live in the districts they represent, but they traditionally do. The age and citizenship qualifications for representatives are less than those for senators. The constitutional requirements of Article I, Section 2 for election to Congress are the maximum requirements that can be imposed on a candidate. Therefore, Article I, Section 5, which permits each House to be the judge of the qualifications of its own members does not permit either House to establish additional qualifications. Likewise a State could not establish additional qualifications.",what are the requirements to be in the state senate the house
