ntent Jump to Recipe These healthier Air Fryer Pork Chops are crispy on the outside, yet deliciously tender and juicy on the inside. And so much faster than cooking in the oven or on the stovetop! You’ll also love Air Fryer Fried Chicken, Crispy Air Fryer Chicken Drumsticks and Air Fryer an Air Fryer Chicken Thighs. (GF, LC, K) Suitable for Keto, Gluten Free, and Low Carb diets. Post Includes Weight Watchers points. Facebook X Pinterest LinkedIn Flipboard This delectable Juicy Air Fryer Pork Chops recipe is easy to throw together in just a few minutes. As in season them, throw them in the air fryer and 9 quick minutes later you end up with two perfectly golden pork chops ready to serve. It is a great recipe to make for dinner tonight. Crispy Air Fryer Pork Chops These juicy pork chops, made from basic pantry ingredients are something special. Because unlike deep-frying and baking, when you air fry pork chops, it actually makes the outside crispier, yet the insides stays super moist. The flavorful crispy breading is a combination of almond flour (or plain flour), creole seasoning and Parmesan cheese. But you can use other seasonings to your taste. It is a great main course recipe that can be served with a salad or cauliflower to keep it low carb or rice and potatoes and more. And if you love pork chops you’ll also love crispy Air Fryer Bacon and these Air Fryer Pork Tenderloin and even Air Fryer Chicken Thighs loved by the whole family. Why Make This Recipe They cook perfectly – crispy on the outside, yet the inside stays super moist.They are made from affordable and simple pantry stapes.meal prep-friendly – prep ahead for quick cooking or quick week night suppers or family lunches. Perfect for serving up at your big Mardi Gras celebration meal, these best pork chops are everything that delicious pork chops should be. Ingredient Notes Pork Chops – This recipe calls for boneless chops but you can use bone in pork chops. Whilst this recipe uses medium chops you can use thick cut chops but you would have to adjust cook time. Thinner chops would cook too quickly.Flour – Use all purpose flour or almond flour (if low carb).Seasoning – paprika, creole or cajun seasoning and Italian seasoning give these a great flavor.Parmesan – freshly grated parmesan or store bought grated will both work Ready to learn just how easy it is to make these Pork Chops In Air Fryer? Gather your ingredients and let’s get started……… How To Cook Pork Chops In Air Fryer Get the complete ingredients list and instructions from the recipe card below. Preheat the air fryer to 350 degrees F / 180 degrees C.Mix together almond flour, Parmesan cheese, paprika, Herbs de Provence, Cajun / Creole or another seasoning in a medium bowl.Lightly spray both sides of the meat with a a little olive oil (or if following a calorie-controlled diet, some cooking spray).Cover both sides of the pork chops with the coating mix, then place pork chops in the air fryer basket. Make sure these are not touching.Air fry anytime between 8 minutes to 12 minutes, depending on the thickness of pork chops flipping halfway through. These here took 9 minutes. When cooking these the first time, I recommend aiming for 10 minutes and then checking.Remove the meat from the basket and serve. Recipe Tips A few handy tips to help you air fry pork chops well: Pat the chops dry with paper towels so that the seasoning sticks.Make sure the pork chops are not touching. This allows maximum air circulation inside the fryer, so your chops will cook evenly and turn out nicely crispy.This recipe makes enough seasoning mix to season 4 pork chops, but I like lots of seasoning on meat so I used extra when making just 2.Double or triple the recipe – although you may need to cook these in batches. Ideally bread the remaining chops for the second batch just before cooking. And more tips……. Thick cut pork chops will take a little bit more time to cook than thin pork chops.Air fryer temperatures can vary depending on the make and model, so it is important to always check your food for doneness. And when cooking meats, always check the internal temperature using a meat thermometer to ensure it has reached a safe temperature. Delicious Variations Vary the seasoning – you could use another dry rub or seasoning like Italian seasoning, Add heat – with chili powder, cayenne, chipotle or more. Storage Make ahead – season raw meat and keep in the fridge. But only add flour just before cooking.Store – Store cooled leftover pork chops an airtight container in the fridge for 3-4 days. Freeze – wrap each cooled pork chops individually in plastic wrap or foil. Then transfer to a freezer bag, remove all the air and freeze for up to 3 month. Thaw – overnight in the fridge and reheat in the air fryer for a couple of minutes until warmed through. FAQs How to Coat Your Air Fried Pork Chops? Getting the coating right can be the difference between cris [SEP_DOC] Cast Iron Skillet Potato Slices - My Kitchen Serenity Jump to Recipe Print Recipe It doesn't get much easier than Cast Iron Skillet Potato Slices! A simple, classic potato side dish recipe that you and your family will love. Simply slice the potatoes, pour melted butter on top, add some herbs and parmesan cheese. Bake until hot and creamy. Slice (tip - use a mandolin) and bake potatoes have been a family favorite for generations. By adding flavor boosters like butter, herbs, and parmesan cheese you really step this recipe up! These crispy skillet potatoes make a perfect side for just about anything, especially my Baked Pineapple Salmon. That sweet, sticky glaze and golden roasted salmon go hand in hand with savory potatoes. My Broccoli Cauliflower Salad makes a bright, creamy contrast to hot side dishes like these potatoes. Jump to:Why You'll Love This RecipeWhy This Recipe Works Best Seasoning for these PotatoesIngredients with NotesEquipment NeededHow to Make Cast Iron Skillet Potato SlicesRecipe TipsFrequently Asked QuestionsMore Easy RecipesRecipeComments Why You'll Love This Recipe What makes this recipe stand out even further is the addition of herbs de province. This wonderful combination of herbs such as rosemary, oregano, and thyme further compliments this tasty potato recipe! Bake in a small cast iron skillet or square casserole dish! Baked potatoes and baked beans seem to go together well (like PBandJ!). If you are needing two side dishes for your meal, consider making my Baked Beans with Bacon and Ground Beef recipe. They both are baked in the oven at the same temperature in about the same amount of time. Easy peasy! Sausage is a great main entree to serve with potatoes. Try my easy Brats in the Oven recipe. Delicious and super easy! Why This Recipe Works Cast Iron Skillet Potato Slices is so easy, and you probably already have the ingredients on hand. While roasted potatoes are very popular now, this recipe is a classic. Slicing the potatoes and baking them in the oven, covered with foil, is an old time favorite method that will never go out of style. This is the way I remember eating potatoes as a kid. Potatoes can be served with just about anything. A perfect side dish for pork chops, baked chicken, or meatloaf! Try them with my Reverse Seared New York Strip! Best Seasoning for these Potatoes This recipe calls for Herbes de Provence. It's a mixture of dried herbs and most often contains rosemary, oregano, thyme, savory, and marjoram. It adds a delicious flavor to all types of meats and vegetables. Herbes de Provence also adds a delicious aroma to your home during baking! According to Culinarylore.com, Julia Child brought the term herbes de provence to the American vocabulary. Read their article What is Herbes de Provence here. Ingredients with Notes please scroll down to the recipe card for ingredient details Russett (Baking) Potatoes - I prefer the large baking potatoes but you can use red potatoes, Yukon gold potatoes, or simply your favorite Butter - makes the potatoes creamy and flavorful Herbes de Provence - for the flavor blast! Use dried Italian Seasoning if that's all you have Shredded Parmesan Cheese - you may use grated parmesan cheese as well Salt and Pepper - for added flavor, just use your personal, favorite amount of seasonings Equipment Needed Small cast-iron skillet or 8"" x 11"" casserole dish Mandolin (preferred) or sharp kitchen knife Measuring spoons How to Make Cast Iron Skillet Potato Slices The simplicity of this recipe is the beauty of this recipe! Roasted parmesan potatoes with butter and herbs is super easy to make! (1) Evenly slice the potatoes and place them in a small cast iron skillet or casserole dish that has been brushed with ½ teaspoon olive oil. (2) Pour melted butter on top. Sprinkle herbs, salt, and pepper on top. (3) Sprinkle parmesan cheese on top. Cover with foil, and bake at 400F for about 40 minutes. That's it! The butter and herbs make these potatoes creamy and full of flavor! Recipe Tips Use a mandolin, like this one by OXO, to slice the potatoes evenly. I like using a mandolin because it's faster and safer than using a kitchen knife. You can easily double or triple this recipe for a larger crowd. You can peel the potatoes first or leave the skin on if you prefer. Add a teaspoon of fresh, minced garlic before baking! Everybody loves bacon so why not sprinkle some cooked and crumbled bacon on top? I wouldn't turn that down! Frequently Asked Questions What can I substitute for herbs de provence? You could substitute with dried Italian seasoning if you can't find herbs de provence. It's not exactly the same thing but it's fairly close. Which potatoes are best for baking? This recipe calls for russet potatoes because they're low in moisture which makes them light, fluffy, and oh so creamy! How do you store leftovers? Store any leftover baked potatoes in airtight containers in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. I prefer to use BPA-free glass containers wit"
