Namibian newspaper ""The Namibian"" is reporting that new traffic fines are coming in force on Friday, 17 Dec 2010. It was confirmed by the Commanding Officer of the Namibian Police’s Traffic Law Enforcement Division, Deputy Commissioner Ralph Ludwig. [src.]
New traffic fines (from 17 Dec 2010):
Talking on cellphone while driving - N$2000
Failure to stop at red traffic light - N$2500
Failure to stop at stop sign - N$1500
Not wearing seatbelt - N$1000
Reckless or negligent driving - N$4000
Driving vehicle that is not roadworthy - N$2000
