where is malta located on the europe map,"['https://latitude.to/map/mt/malta', 'http://www.islandtrips.co.uk/onlineagency/agentonline-EU_Malta.php', 'https://www.consularcorps.gi/malta-franco-cassar-loporto/', 'https://www.e-architect.co.uk/malta/malta-index', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/what-continent-is-malta-in.html', 'https://www.4truth.ca/sabbath-school/sabbath-school-2015/ssl-2015-1st-half/9-fruit-of-the-spirit-part-1/', 'https://www.easyvisa.com.ng/']","Coordinates: 35 ° 53 ′ N 14 ° 30 ′ E ﻿ / ﻿ 35.883 ° N 14.500 ° E ﻿ / 35.883; 14.500 Malta (/ ˈmɒltə / (listen); Maltese: (ˈmɐltɐ)), officially known as the Republic of Malta (Maltese: Repubblika ta' Malta), is a Southern European island country consisting of an archipelago in the Mediterranean Sea. It lies 80 km (50 mi) south of Italy, 284 km (176 mi) east of Tunisia, and 333 km (207 mi) north of Libya. The country covers just over 316 km (122 sq mi), with a population of just under 450,000, making it one of the world's smallest and most densely populated countries. The capital of Malta is Valletta, which at 0.8 km, is the smallest national capital in the European Union by area. Malta has one national language, which is Maltese, and English as an official language.","GPS coordinates of Malta. Latitude: 35.9440 Longitude: 14.3795 Latitude and longitude of Malta Malte (FR) Malta (DE) Malta (ES)  Satellite map of Malta Malta (/ˈmɒltə/), officially the Republic of Malta (Maltese: Repubblika ta' Malta, pronounced [rɛˈpʊbb.lɪ.kɐ ˈtɐ ˈmɐl.tɐ]), is a Southern European island country comprising an archipelago of a few islands in the Mediterranean Sea. It lies 80 km (50 mi) south of Sicily, 284 km (176 mi) east of Tunisia, and 333 km (207 mi) north of Libya. The country covers just over 316 km2 (122 sq mi), with a population of around 450,000, making it one of the world's smallest and most densely populated countries. The capital of Malta is Valletta, which at 0.8 km2, is the smallest national capital in the European Union. Malta has two official languages: Maltese and English.  Read about Malta in the Wikipedia Latitude: 35° 56' 38.46"" NLongitude: 14° 22' 46.29"" E Population: 403,000 Capital: Valletta Country ISO codes: MT / MLT / 470 Oficial languages: English (en), Maltese (mt) Oficial coin(s): Euro (EUR)  GPS coordinates of Malta Download as JSON  DD CoordinatesDMS CoordinatesGEOHASH CoordinatesUTM Coordinates33S 444038.15082724 3977917.066054  Places of interest in Malta 1 Airport in MaltaShow all airports of Malta in the mapXewkija Heliport ( GZM )Xewkija Heliport (GZM), Triq Ta' Lambert, Ghajnsielem, Malta Show in map Show coordinates1 Natural park in MaltaShow all natural parks of Malta in the mapTa' Qali National ParkTa' Qali National Park, Ħ'Attard, Malta Show in map Show coordinates © Latitude.to (v1.68-gg) 2026 Disclaimer and errors Cookies policy Articles by country"
who wrote the lyrics of philippine national anthem,"['http://juniormarvel.tk/lupang-hinirang-sheet.html', 'https://philippinestravelsite.com/national-anthem-philippines-lupang-hinirang/', 'http://www.worldnationalanthem.com/philippines-national-anthem-vocal-lupang-hinirang/', 'http://allahyolunda.tk/dating-old-listerine-bottles.html', 'https://pinoycollection.com/lupang-hinirang-lyrics/']","""Lupang Hinirang"" ((ˈlupaŋ hiˈniɾaŋ); originally in Spanish: Patria Adorada (ˈpatɾja aðoˈɾaða); English: ""Chosen Land"") is the national anthem of the Philippines. Its music was composed in 1898 by Julián Felipe, and the lyrics were adapted from the Spanish poem Filipinas, written by José Palma in 1899. Originally written it did not have lyrics when it was adopted as the anthem of the revolutionary First Philippine Republic and subsequently played during the proclamation of Philippine independence on June 12, 1898.","TouristSecrets | Philippines | TouristSecrets uPhone Cheap eSIM for 150+ Countries 🇯🇵 🇹🇭 🇬🇧 🇺🇸 🇩🇪 Code: SECRETS5 — 5% off Get eSIM → HomeTravel DestinationsAsiaPhilippines Philippines Philippines Secrets Of Apo Island’s Coral Garden Research Stations Philippines TouristSecrets | Philippines Travel Guide | TouristSecrets Philippines The Origins of Tourism in the Philippines Philippines Understanding the Travel Document Number in a Philippine Passport Philippines Hidden Gems: Manila’s Must-Visit Malls Philippines Is Lino Brocka The Philippines’ Greatest Director? Philippines 10 Must-Read Gems In Modern Philippine Literature Philippines The Hidden Meanings Behind The Philippine Flag Philippines The Fascinating Journey Of The Jeepney To Filipino Icon Status Philippines The Hidden Secrets Of Arnis: The Philippines’ National Sport And Martial Art Philippines What To Do With A Long Layover In Manilla Philippines Mantayupan Falls In Barili, Cebu: Complete Guide Philippines Mainit Hot Springs In Malabuyoc: Best Cebu Hot Spring Philippines Lusno Falls In Cebu: Hidden Waterf