what is the role of rna polymerase during transcription,"['https://www.shomusbiology.com/molecular-biology.html', 'https://study.com/academy/lesson/the-central-dogma-of-biology-definition-theory-quiz.html', 'https://www.encyclopedia.com/science/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/ribonucleic-acid-rna-1', 'http://pak500.blogspot.com/2010/01/', 'https://www.omicsonline.org/genetic-syndromes-and-gene-therapy/transcription-top-open-access-journals.php', 'https://info.transcriptionwing.com/general-transcription-guide-for-freelancers', 'https://asheekeyscienceblog.com/2017/09/09/get-transcribed-in-style-the-ctd-that-everyones-talking-about/']","Transcription is the first step of gene expression, in which a particular segment of DNA is copied into RNA (especially mRNA) by the enzyme RNA polymerase. Both DNA and RNA are nucleic acids, which use base pairs of nucleotides as a complementary language. During transcription, a DNA sequence is read by an RNA polymerase, which produces a complementary, antiparallel RNA strand called a primary transcript.",Molecular Biology - Shomu's Biology Google+ Home DVD store Video lectures Bioinformatics Virology Microbiology Evolutionary Biology Immunology and cancer Biology Ecology and env. Biology CSIR NET Human Physiology Genetics Developmental Biology Biological techniques Biotatistics Molecular Biology Bio-blog Recombinant DNA technology Biochemistry Biotechnology Assignment help NET coaching Contact Me Bio-zone Bio-Materials About me Courses Courses Personal transaction page Support Shomu's biology Report Bio-Tutorials Cell Biology Molecular Biology Macromolecules Of Life General Microbiology Biochemistry Genetics Evolutionary Biology Chemical Context of Life Microbiological Techniques Developmental Biology Gene Therapy Bioinformatics Genomics Industrial Microbiology Immunology Basics of Biology Recombinant DNA technology Biotechnology Plant Biology Population Genetics Ecology General Microbiology Evolutionary Biology Cell Biol