who wrote the man who shot liberty valance,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Gertrude_Astor', 'http://myhdmoviespoint.com/the-man-who-shot-liberty-valance-1962', 'http://loneroad.info/viewtopic.php?t=40552', 'http://thevoid99.blogspot.com/2017/07/the-man-who-shot-liberty-valance.html', 'http://www.cbcshafter.org/mikesblog/2016/4/7/december-2014', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/A_Medal_for_Benny', 'http://www.shadyoldlady.com/location/1927']","The Man Who Shot Liberty Valance / ˈvaləns / is a 1962 American Western film directed by John Ford starring James Stewart and John Wayne. The black-and-white film was released by Paramount Pictures. The screenplay by James Warner Bellah and Willis Goldbeck was adapted from a short story written by Dorothy M. Johnson. The supporting cast features Vera Miles, Lee Marvin, Edmond O'Brien, Andy Devine, John Carradine, Woody Strode, Strother Martin, and Lee Van Cleef.","Gertrude Astor - WikiVisually WikiVisually Infinite photos and videos for every Wiki article · Find something interesting to watch in seconds WikiVisually Infinite photos and videos for every Wiki article · Find something interesting to watch in seconds Celebrities British Monarchs Orders and Medals History by Country Recovered Treasures Largest Empires Wars and Battles Great Museums World Banknotes Best Campuses Great Cities Sports Kings of France Richest US Counties Rare Coins Countries of the World Wonders of Nature Great Artists Crown Jewels Famous Castles Largest Palaces Animals Presidents Tallest Buildings Supercars Ancient Marvels more top lists History Gertrude Astor Videos Photos Gertrude Astor was an American motion picture character actress, who began her career playing trombone in a woman's band. Astor in Beyond the Rocks (1922) Gertrude Astor (center) with Herbert Barrington and Al Ernest Garcia Gertrude Astor, Colleen Moore and Richard Dix filming The Wall Flower (1922) Gertrude Astor and Tyler Brooke in Laughing Ladies (1925 film) The Strong Man Videos Photos The Strong Man is a 1926 American silent comedy film starring Harry Langdon, who produced the film. It was directed by Frank Capra in his feature debut. Jumbo lobby card Image: The Strong Man (1926 lobby card 1) Image: The Strong Man (1926 lobby card 2)"
what's the population of the florida keys,"['https://caribbean-tour.com/Information-about-Florida-Keys-(USA).html', 'http://www.mediaman.com.au/profiles/florida_keys.html', 'https://miamiboatrent.com/contact_miami_boat_rent/', 'http://webot.org/info/en/?search=Florida_Keys', 'http://www.travelblat.com/florida-keys-resorts/', 'https://sheepdogchurchsecurity.net/united-states-of-america/florida/general/church-security-in-florida-keys-florida/', 'https://www.mangrovemonkey.com/florida-keys/']","More than 95 percent of the land area lies in Monroe County, but a small portion extends northeast into Miami-Dade County, such as Totten Key. The total land area is 137.3 square miles (356 km). As of the 2010 census the population was 73,090 with an average density of 532.34 per square mile (205.54 / km), although much of the population is concentrated in a few areas of much higher density, such as the city of Key West, which has 32% of the entire population of the Keys. The US Census population estimate for 2014 is 77,136.","404 - File or directory not found. Server Error 404 - File or directory not found. The resource you are looking for might have been removed, had its name changed, or is temporarily unavailable."
