roles of chairman of the board of directors,"['https://wikivivid.com/wiki/Ferrari', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=bilderbergcommittee.org&ads=1&title=Bilderberg+committee&auto=Bilderberg+committee&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Bilderberg+committee&pagenum=3', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/President_(corporate_title)', 'https://www.lucidmeetings.com/glossary/chair', 'http://igdolazabal.com/jean-yves-le-gall-ariane-dating.php', 'http://www.ugandashippers.com/chairmans-message', 'http://www.ugandashippers.com/company-profile']","The chairman (also chairperson, chairwoman or chair) is the highest officer of an organized group such as a board, a committee, or a deliberative assembly. The person holding the office is typically elected or appointed by the members of the group. The chairman presides over meetings of the assembled group and conducts its business in an orderly fashion. When the group is not in session, the officer's duties often include acting as its head, its representative to the outside world and its spokesperson. In some organizations, this position is also called president (or other title), in others, where a board appoints a president (or other title), the two different terms are used for distinctly different positions.","Bilderberg Committee Tweet this page share on Facebook Monday, 04 May 2026 WN Trending News Bing Podcasts: Email this Page Play all in Full Screen Show More Related Videos back Most Related Most Recent Most Popular Top Rated expand screen to full width repeat playlist shuffle replay video clear playlist restore images list PLAYLIST TIME: EXPLORE WN.com Advanced Search Education Cities.com Dubai.com TravelAgents.com Weather World Photos Cheese.com Broadcasts.com Metas.com Students.com Emissions.com Population.com Domaines.com Wages.com Help | About WN | Privacy Policy | Contact | Feedback | Jobs | Students | Email this page | Newsletter | © WN 2026 All Rights Reserved, World News Inc Connect: × ×