who starred in the original rocky horror picture show,"['http://party-net.info/?page_id=27924', 'https://www.hashlocker.eu/tag/barry-bostwick/', 'http://nerdipop.co.za/the-rocky-horror-picture-show-a-little-history/', 'https://happyvalleyshop.com/products/absolute-treasures-the-rocky-horror-picture-show-complete-soundtrack-from-the-original-movie-limited-red-vinyl', 'https://milehicon482016.sched.com/event/8cSo/rocky-horror-picture-show-british-version', 'https://delawarescene.com/event/23792/the-rocky-horror-picture-show', 'https://www.venturatheater.net/event/1636183-burlesque-jambor-tease-ventura/']","The Rocky Horror Picture Show is a 1975 musical science-fiction horror-comedy film by 20th Century Fox produced by Lou Adler and Michael White and directed by Jim Sharman. The screenplay was written by Sharman and actor Richard O'Brien, who is also a member of the cast. The film is based on the 1973 musical stage production The Rocky Horror Show, with music, book, and lyrics by O'Brien. The production is a parody tribute to the science fiction and horror B movies of the 1930s through to the early 1970s. Along with O'Brien, the film stars Tim Curry, Susan Sarandon, and Barry Bostwick and is narrated by Charles Gray with cast members from the original Royal Court Theatre, Roxy Theatre, and Belasco Theatre productions.",who starred in the original rocky horror picture show
who played emperor in return of the jedi,"['http://encyclopedia2.thefreedictionary.com/Emperor+Palpatine', 'http://www.punchdrunkcritics.com/2019/04/palpatines-surprise-return-for-star.html', 'https://www.cnet.com/news/star-wars-episode-9-rise-of-skywalker-sees-emperor-palpatine-rise-again/', 'https://www.newsarama.com/44742-is-emperor-palpatine-returning-in-star-wars-the-rise-of-skywalker.html', 'https://comicsnewsboom.com/2019/04/12/is-emperor-palpatine-returning-in-star-wars-the-rise-of-skywalker/', 'https://www.popsugar.co.uk/entertainment/Palpatine-Star-Wars-Episode-9-Rise-Skywalker-46027133', 'https://www.latimes.com/entertainment/herocomplex/la-et-hc-the-times-star-wars-style-guide-20151130-story.html']","After a minor part in the film Dragonslayer, McDiarmid was cast by George Lucas in Return of the Jedi as Emperor Palpatine, the main villain. Sixteen years after appearing in Return of the Jedi, he reprised the role as the character's younger incarnation of Senator Palpatine and Sith Lord Darth Sidious in the prequel films: The Phantom Menace, Attack of the Clones, and Revenge of the Sith. The prequels had him play two faces to his character; he re-created his diabolical interpretation of Palpatine from Return of the Jedi when playing Darth Sidious, the Chancellor's Sith alter ego, but created a pleasant, charming character in Palpatine's public persona.","Page not found – Punch Drunk Critics Facebook Instagram Mail Twitter Youtube Featured News Trailers Images Box Office Reviews Travis John Cortland Jake Khalil Ronny Interviews TV Contests Giveaways Screenings Podcasts Cinema Royale Uncategorized Contact Us Search Sign in Welcome! Log into your account your username your password Forgot your password? Get help Password recovery Recover your password your email A password will be e-mailed to you. Punch Drunk Critics AD Featured News Trailers Images Box Office Reviews Travis John Cortland Jake Khalil Ronny Interviews TV Contests Giveaways Screenings Podcasts 