the father the son and the holy spirit symbol,"['https://christianity.stackexchange.com/questions/31434/to-understand-the-the-bible-is-the-word-of-god', 'https://christianblogs.christianet.com/1419189452.htm', 'https://www.thebarainitiative.com/holy-trinity-church-london-england/', 'http://bibleiq.com/bible/bible_keywords/l/logos.htm', 'https://godsloveandlaw.com/2017/06/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Trinitarian.html', 'https://www.look4wardstore.com/blogs/news/power-of-3-guiding-principal-of-universe']","The Christian doctrine of the Trinity (Latin: Trinitas, lit.' triad', from trinus, ""threefold"") holds that God is three consubstantial persons or hypostases -- the Father, the Son (Jesus Christ), and the Holy Spirit -- as ""one God in three Divine Persons"". The three persons are distinct, yet are one ""substance, essence or nature"" (homoousios). In this context, a ""nature"" is what one is, whereas a ""person"" is who one is. The opposing view is referred to as Nontrinitarianism.",the father the son and the holy spirit symbol
what is the difference between nad and nadh,"['https://www.leebio.com/product/1094/beta-nicotinamide-adenine-dinucleotide-nadh-reduced-form-disodium-salt-943-20', 'https://www.essaysexperts.net/blog/category/essay-help/', 'http://www.breastcancerstudyandsupport.org/part-iii---vitamin-c-ascorbic-acid-feed-white-blood-cells.html', 'https://vestanutra.com/vproducts/what-is-nadh/', 'https://genexformulas.com/blogs/news/nmn', 'http://www.isoquercetin.net/nad/', 'http://web.archive.org/web/20150725005613/http:/www.thelibertybeacon.com/tag/cancer/']","In metabolism, nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide is involved in redox reactions, carrying electrons from one reaction to another. The coenzyme is, therefore, found in two forms in cells: NAD is an oxidizing agent -- it accepts electrons from other molecules and becomes reduced. This reaction forms NADH, which can then be used as a reducing agent to donate electrons. These electron transfer reactions are the main function of NAD. However, it is also used in other cellular processes, the most notable one being a substrate of enzymes that add or remove chemical groups from proteins, in posttranslational modifications. Because of the importance of these functions, the enzymes involved in NAD metabolism are targets for drug discovery.","Lee BioSolutions - Error Default | LeeBio.com 404 Unfortunately, the page you requested does not exist on the site This could have occurred for the following reasons: You made a mistake when typing the page address (URL) You clicked a broken or incorrect link The requested page has never been on the website or has been deleted Here are some helpful links instead: Home Antigens / Enzymes Biologicals Biochemicals Antibodies Lee Biosolutions, Inc Medix Biochemica USA Inc. 10850 Metro Court Maryland Heights, MO USA 63043 Phone: (314).968.1091 Fax: (314).968.9851 Email: Email us Orders & Accounts My Account Ordering Shipping Information Our Company Certifications & Licenses Community Outreach Management