where is the las vegas football stadium being built,"['https://www.shelterrealty.com/2017/05/16/oakland-raiders-release-details-on-construction-of-new-las-vegas-stadium/', 'https://www.azcentral.com/story/sports/2019/01/25/pac-12-football-championship-site-moving/2680647002/', 'https://www.bbcr.com/bbcr-gets-to-vegas-for-the-first-show/', 'https://barchanfoundation.com/projects/projects?filter%5Bcategory_id%5D=1', 'https://opportunitydb.com/2019/02/nfl-stadiums-eligible-for-opportunity-zones-tax-break/', 'http://www.atlantatribune.com/2013/08/06/will-the-new-stadium-rise-up-in-time/', 'https://vegasinc.lasvegassun.com/business/2018/feb/08/room-tax-challenges-could-be-a-hit-to-raiders-stad/']","Las Vegas Stadium is the working name for a domed stadium under construction in Paradise, Nevada for the Las Vegas Raiders of the National Football League (NFL) and the UNLV Rebels football team of the University of Nevada, Las Vegas (UNLV). It is located on about 62 acres west of Mandalay Bay at Russell Road and Hacienda Avenue and between Polaris Avenue and Dean Martin Drive, just west of Interstate 15. Construction of the $1.8 billion stadium began in September 2017 and is expected to be completed in time for the 2020 NFL season.",where is the las vegas football stadium being built
where does the australian prime minister live in sydney,"['http://trolltours.com.au/2019/04/07/mugdha-vinayak-06-04-19-harbour-bridge-trike-tour/', 'https://thomaskellner.com/info/buildings/australia/kirribilli-house-sydney/', 'http://eatyourheartoutboston.com/queensland/how-to-get-to-admiralty-house-kirribilli.php', 'http://derekfarmer.com.au/lower-north-shore-real-estate/kirribilli/', 'http://wildwalks.com/bushwalking-and-hiking-in-nsw/sydney-harbour-north-side/harbour-bridge-to-taronga-zoo.html', 'https://glenferrielodge.com/attractions/', 'https://thetwoboomersabroad.com/2017/11/19/sydney-victoria-and-the-adelaide-hills/']","Kirribilli House is the secondary official residence of the Prime Minister of Australia. Located in Sydney, New South Wales, the house is at the far eastern end of Kirribilli Avenue in the harbourside suburb of Kirribilli. It is one of two official Prime Ministerial residences, the primary official residence being The Lodge in Canberra, Australian Capital Territory.","Mugdha + Vinayak 06.04.19 - Harbour Bridge trike tour - troll tours You are here: Home1 / Blog2 / Gallery3 / Mugdha + Vinayak 06.04.19 – Harbour Bridge trike tour We organised a Harbour Bridge trike tour for our passengers. They are visiting Sydney and thought it would be the best way to see the iconic Harbour Bridge and Sydney Harbour. They are right – it is the best way! Harbour Bridge trike tour Craig picked them up from Circular Quay and rode over the Sydney Harbour Bridge. It is something we never ever tire of, no matter how many times we ride over it. Tilt your head back a little to really see the wonderful arches and steel work. It is such a different experience than driving over the bridge with a roof over your head, blocking a lot of the view. Their first stop was Blues Point. It has wonderful views looking eastward over Sydney Harbour. There is an unrestricted view of both the Sydney Harbour Bridge and the Sydney Opera House. Kirribilli House Then they rode to Jeffrey Street Wharf at Kirribilli. The same suburb which has ‘Kirribilli House’, the secondary official residence of the Prime Minister of Australia. the primary official residence being The Lodge in Canberra, Australian Capital Territory. See below for more information. There is another wonderful view across Sydney Harbour to the Opera House and the city. If there is time, we ride under the north end of the bridge, past the entrance road which goes to Luna Park and past North Sydney Olympic Pool. They continued back over the Harbour Bridge before being dropped off at Circular Quay. The Harbour Bridge trike tour is a great ride and a fun experience. https://www.trolltours.com.au/product/harbour-bridge-ride/ ‘Kirribilli House’ was built in 1854, a Gothic-style structure, a twin-gabled dwelling or cottage ornée – on the land’s highest spot. In 1956 Kirribilli House was set aside as a residence for the use of Australia’s Prime Ministers, when they need to perform public duties and extend official hospitality on behalf of the government during stays in Sydney. https://www.trolltours.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/Harley-Harbour-Bridge-trike-tour-MuVi1.jpg 540 720 Kat https://www.trolltours.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/logo.png Kat2019-04-07 17:06:562019-04-07 17:07:13Mugdha + Vinayak 06.04.19 – Harbour Bridge trike tour Troll ToursBook Now Tours & Prices FAQs FacebookContact Us Troll Tours Pty Ltd P.O Box 227, Leichhardt NSW 2040, Australia Phone 02 9568 3082 Mobile 0410 464 740 Email trevor@trolltours.com.au Office Hours 8am to 8pm, 7 days a week There’s nothing like a Harley or trike ride with Troll Tours! We are fully accredited with the NSW Government: Accreditation No. 37123. Disability Friendly! Link to: Susan + Tina 03.04.19 – Harley Eastern Panorama tour Link to: Susan + Tina 03.04.19 – Harley Eastern Panorama tour Susan + Tina 03.04.19 – Harley Eastern Panorama tour Link to: Jenny 07.04.19 – Manly Northern beaches Harley tour Link to: Jenny 07.04.19 – Manly N