what band is stillwater based on in almost famous,"['https://guysandgoodhealth.com/2017/09/07/almost-famous-tiny-dancer/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'https://www.thecinemaholic.com/movies-about-writers/', 'http://www.movie-mine.com/mm_info.php?/en/almost_famous', 'https://rjdent.wordpress.com/category/music/', 'https://wandervogeldiary.wordpress.com/2016/05/', 'https://www.allaboutmovies.com.au/index.php/poster-formats/day-bill-posters/item/87870-almost-famous-movie-poster-rare-original-daybill-2000-kate-hudson-billy-crudup', 'https://culturecove.co.uk/2015/08/29/almost-famous-2000-film-review/']","The film is based on Crowe's experiences touring with rock bands Poco, The Allman Brothers Band, Led Zeppelin, Eagles and Lynyrd Skynyrd. Crowe has discussed how during this period he lost his virginity, fell in love, and met his heroes -- experiences that are shared by William Miller (Patrick Fugit), the boyish main character of the film.","10 Best Movies About Writers | Top Writer Films - The Cinemaholic 10 Best Writer Movies of All Time Aditya Mandhane September 19, 2017 FacebookTwitterPinterestRedditEmail These are the geniuses who, even within the most minuscule acts of the universe, find a story worth telling. Which makes their own stories cinema-worthy ones. Even among the artistic fraternity, writers command a fascination of their own, partly because of their generally reclusive nature (Capote and Fitzgerald being some mighty exceptions) and partly due to the enigma about writing itself. Right from the profound poets and to stellar screenwriters, the society has always been in awe of the people who put their pens to pads (or fingers to keys) in search of a masterpiece. As an aspiring (read: wannabe) writer, till I find my own masterpiece to chase after, the least I can do is marvel about some cinematic gems focusing on writers, real or fictional, and daydream a little (except about the Number 10 entry!). Here is the list of top movies about writers ever. You can watch several of these best writer movies on Netflix, Hulu or Amazon Prime. 10. Misery (1990) Every writer’s worst nightmare; a delusional fan. This 1990 psychological thriller is based on a 1987 novel of the same name penned by the maestro Stephen King. A psychotic fan holding her favorite author captive and making him write stories as she wants them is chilling enough to hear, but Kathy Bates (who won an Oscar for her role) ups the tempo with her eccentric rendition. In a scene. she gasps “God I love you!” right after she slams the writer’s ankle with a sledgehammer to keep him from escaping, showing obsession and mania in equal measure. A film which can make any writer paranoid about someone saying “I’m your number one fan!” Read More: Best Movie Musicals of All Time 9. Moulin Rouge (2001) Star-crossed lovers; a young English poet, Christian, and the star of the Moulin Rouge, Satine, in the Bohemian setting of the Montmartre Quarter of Paris, during La Belle Epoque (“The Golden Era”) of France. A romance can rarely have a more intriguing mise-en-scène. ‘Moulin Rouge’ manages to be immensely exuberant, yet bold and passionate, even in the middle of its decadent milieu, thanks to the scorching union of Nicole Kidman and Ewan McGregor. And all the fervent, profound dialogues and songs are bound to make any connaisseur of romance novels swoon. Read More: Best Nonlinear Movies of All Time 8. The Help (2011) In a list full of stories either glorifying or dramatizing the craft of writing, this 2011 all-women ensemble is one of the rare stories which truly show the might of the pen. The film and recounts the story of a young white aspiring journalist Eugenia “Skeeter” Phelan. and her unlikely bond with two black maids, Aibileen Clark and Minny Jackson, during the Civil Rights era in 1962 Jackson, Mississippi. In an attempt to become a legitimate journalist and writer, Skeeter decides to write a book from the point of view "
