what is articles of association and memorandum of association,"['https://thereisnodebt.wordpress.com/2016/01/22/poland-terrorism-obedience-sustainable-development-the-loss-of-freedoms-for-the-people-of-the-world-and-the-simple-solution-part-iv/', 'http://www.startup.pk/uncategorized/how-to-register-a-private-company-in-pakistan/', 'https://www.lyonswilson-solicitors.co.uk/news/what%E2%80%99s-the-best-structure-for-a-new-business/', 'https://ca4you01.blogspot.com/2017/08/Best-private-limited-company-registration-company.html', 'https://desperatefounder.com/legal-toolkit-for-hong-kong-startups/', 'https://www.financialwatchngr.com/2018/01/18/step-step-guide-obtain-expatriate-quota-business-permit-nigeria/', 'https://www.healyconsultants.com/india-company-registration/other-information/']","In corporate governance, a company's articles of association (AoA, called articles of incorporation in some jurisdictions) is a document which, along with the memorandum of association (in cases where the memorandum exists) form the company's constitution, defines the responsibilities of the directors, the kind of business to be undertaken, and the means by which the shareholders exert control over the board of directors.","POLAND, TERRORISM, OBEDIENCE, SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT, THE LOSS OF FREEDOMS FOR THE PEOPLE OF THE WORLD, AND THE SIMPLE SOLUTION – PART IV | there is no debt THEY MUST FIND IT DIFFICULT, THOSE WHO HAVE TAKEN AUTHORITY AS TRUTH, RATHER THAN TRUTH AS AUTHORITY – Gerald Massey ____ “And thus I clothe my naked villainy With odd old ends stol’n out of holy writ; And seem a saint, when most I play the devil.” ― William Shakespeare, Richard III ~ REFERENCE MATERIAL: The Simple Solution https://thereisnodebt.wordpress.com/2015/12/07/poland-terrorism-obedience-sustainable-development-the-loss-of-freedoms-for-the-people-of-the-world-and-the-simple-solution-part-ii/ _______ FOR EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES ONLY – From the previous postings on the tyrannical consequences of mythological delusions and their symbolism, it becomes surprisingly noteworthy how far their reach extends in the everyday innocence of people’s lives – Pointed hat https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pointed_hat The Self-Ennobling Ones, their self-validating clergy, together with their agent provocateurs, show great skill in the invocation of ‘enchantments of illusion’ for those to believe that they have won their freedom, while they remain subservient We read – The Phrygian cap is a soft conical cap with the top pulled forward, associated in antiquity with several peoples in Eastern Europe and Anatolia, including Phrygia, Dacia and the Balkans. In early modern Europe it came to signify freedom and the pursuit of liberty through a confusion with the pileus, the felt cap of manumitted (emancipated) slaves of ancient Rome. Accordingly, the Phrygian cap is sometimes called a liberty cap; in artistic representations it signifies freedom and the pursuit of liberty. Phrygian Cap https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phrygian_cap We read – The pileus was especially associated with the manumission of slaves, who wore it upon their liberation. It became emblematic of liberty and freedom from bondage.[2] During the classic revival of the 18th and 19th centuries it was widely confused with the Phrygian cap Pileus (hat) https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pileus_(hat) We read – Manumission, from manumit, is the act of a slave owner freeing his slaves. Manumission https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manumission Of the Phrygian culture, we read, subheading, ‘Culture’, 2nd paragraph – The “Great Mother”, Cybele, as the Greeks and Romans knew her, was originally worshiped in the mountains of Phrygia, where she was known as “Mountain Mother”. Phrygia https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phrygia Of Cybele, we come to learn that she is an Underworld Goddess, on reading, 2nd paragraph – She was partially assimilated to aspects of the Earth-goddess Gaia, her Minoan equivalent Rhea, and the Harvest-Mother goddess Demeter. She 