the purpose of the hanging gardens of babylon,"['https://chaldeannation.com/blog/2016/06/13/building-the-hanging-gardens-of-babylon-in-france/', 'https://petesfavouritethings.blog/category/history/ancient-near-eastern-history/', 'http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/Hanging_gardens', 'https://www.needsomefun.net/7-wonders-of-world/', 'https://www.driftwoodfashion.com/art/', 'https://www.nigerianinfopedia.com/ancient-wonders-of-the-world/', 'https://www.playbuzz.com/emilynew10/which-of-the-seven-wonders-of-the-world-encapsulates-your-spirit']","According to one legend, Nebuchadnezzar II built the Hanging Gardens for his Median wife, Queen Amytis, because she missed the green hills and valleys of her homeland. He also built a grand palace that came to be known as ""The Marvel of the Mankind"". Stephanie Dalley suggests that the original garden may have been a well-documented one that Assyrian King Sennacherib (704 -- 681 BC) built in his capital city of Nineveh on the River Tigris, near the modern city of Mosul.","Building the Hanging Gardens of Babylon … in France! | Chaldean Nation Sign in Home World Featured Health Opinion Food & Recipes Books Archives ChaldoPhobia الاخبار More Language History Culture Books ChaldoPhobia History Language News People Chaldean Identity in Historical Documents Sign in Welcome!Log into your account your username your password Forgot your password? Password recovery Recover your password your email Search Monday, January 5, 2026 Sign in / JoinAdvertisement Blog Contact us LOG IN Welcome! Log into your account Forgot your password? Recover your password Chaldean Nation Home World News Open Letter to President Of United States, Donald J. Trump From… History Chaldean Martyr Day … October 6th News CECA Open Letter to the Honorable Nechirvan Barzani News CECA President Letter to Mr. Harvey, International Religious Freedom Archives Chaldean People in 339 AD Featured AllHealth Health 3,000 Year Old Chaldean Babylonian Recipe For Fumigation Against Epilepsy Opinion Food & Recipes Books Archives ChaldoPhobia الاخبار More Language History Culture AllBooksChaldoPhobiaHistoryLanguageNewsPeople News Open Letter to President Of United States, Donald J. Trump From… History Chaldean Martyr Day … October 6th News CECA Open Letter to the Honorable Nechirvan Barzani News رسالة سكان العراق الأصليين “الكلدان” إلى الحكومة العراقية Chaldean Identity in Historical Documents Home World News Building the Hanging Gardens of Babylon … in France! World News Share on Facebook Tweet on Twitter Chaldean Architecture Paris France – June 2016 Artists and architects from France converged to build this beautiful Hanging Gardens of Babylon. Reflecting the ingenious mind of the Chaldean people, native people of Mesopotamia Iraq. “The Chaldean Marvel of Mankind” The Hanging Gardens of Babylon, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, is the only one whose location has not been definitively established.[1] The Hanging Gardens were a distinctive feature of Chaldean Babylon. They were a great source of pride to the people. Possibly built by Chaldean King Nebuchadnezzar II in 600 BC, the gardens are believed to have been a remarkable feat of engineering: an ascending series of tiered gardens containing all manner of trees, shrubs, and vines. The gardens were said to have looked like a large green mountain constructed of mud bricks. Traditionally they were said to have been built in the Chaldean city of Babylon, near present-day Hillah,Babil province, in Mesopotamia Iraq. The Chaldean Babylonian priest Berossus, writing in about 290 BC and quoted later by Josephus, attributed the gardens to the Neo-Babylonian Chaldean King Nebuchadnezzar II, who ruled between 605 BC and 562 BC. There are no extant Babylonian texts which mention the gardens, and no definitive archaeological evidence has been found in Babylon of the Chaldeans. According to one legend, Chaldean King Nebuchadnezzar II built the Hanging Gardens for his Median wife, Queen Amytis, 