what is a good whip in major league baseball,"['https://www.kansascity.com/sports/spt-columns-blogs/judging-the-royals/article31386050.html', 'https://www.majorleaguefantasysports.com/2015/06/16/thats-amore-national-league-central-the-cardinals-are-strolling-down-injury-lane/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Innings_pitched.html', 'https://www.betfirm.com/baseball-handicapping-stats/', 'https://mashable.com/2016/09/30/jose-fernandez-cy-young/', 'http://fullertontitans.com/sports/m-basebl/2012-13/releases/2013042547avwo', 'https://captaincalculator.com/sports/baseball/walks-and-hits-per-inning-pitched-calculator/']","In baseball statistics, walks plus hits per inning pitched (WHIP) is a sabermetric measurement of the number of baserunners a pitcher has allowed per inning pitched. WHIP reflects a pitcher's propensity for allowing batters to reach base, therefore a lower WHIP indicates better performance. WHIP is calculated by adding the number of walks and hits allowed and dividing this sum by the number of innings pitched.",what is a good whip in major league baseball
