as a statistical unit of measure what does sigma represents,"['https://www.donkcowan.com/blog/2017/5/28/machine-learning-mathematics', 'http://bhckp.info/vylu/how-to-calculate-stock-standard-deviation-297.php', 'http://platinum-line.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=33590', 'https://mathbitsnotebook.com/Algebra1/StatisticsData/STSD.html', 'https://edge.sagepub.com/field-adventures-in-stats/student-resources/chapter-8/jigsaw%E2%80%99s-puzzle-solutions', 'https://oag.govt.nz/2014/local-govt/appendix2.htm', 'https://darynholmes.wordpress.com/2014/02/27/commitment-considered-harmful/']","In statistics, the standard deviation (SD, also represented by the Greek letter sigma σ or the Latin letter s) is a measure that is used to quantify the amount of variation or dispersion of a set of data values. A low standard deviation indicates that the data points tend to be close to the mean (also called the expected value) of the set, while a high standard deviation indicates that the data points are spread out over a wider range of values.",as a statistical unit of measure what does sigma represents
what is the meaning of ain't in english,"['https://aphilomathsjournal.wordpress.com/tag/spelling/', 'https://www.englishclub.com/esl-forums/viewtopic.php?f=139&t=43447']","The word ain't is a contraction for am not, is not, are not, has not, and have not in the common English language vernacular. In some dialects ain't is also used as a contraction of do not, does not, and did not. The development of ain't for the various forms of to be not, to have not, and to do not occurred independently, at different times. The usage of ain't for the forms of to be not was established by the mid-18th century, and for the forms of to have not by the early 19th century.",what is the meaning of ain't in english
where does the term santa claus come from,"['https://allairevillage.org/2017/12/22/origins-of-santa-claus/', 'https://wuzakeq.bigskyquartet.com/write-a-letter-to-santa-online-printable-7960so.html', 'http://makingwings.net/libraryhandouts/santaclaus.html', 'http://www.ruralmessenger.com/blogs/frank-buchman/a-cowboys-faith-time-to-remember-why/', 'https://grannyrobertsonscookbook.com/2013/12/21/santa-by-any-other-name/', 'http://thebibleofmysteries.blogspot.com/2010/12/all-about-santa-claus.html']","Pre-modern representations of the gift-giver from Church history and folklore, notably St Nicholas (known in Dutch as Sinterklaas), merged with the English character Father Christmas to create the character known to Americans and the rest of the English-speaking world as ""Santa Claus"" (a phonetic derivation of ""Sinterklaas"").",where does the term santa claus come from
does england have the same seasons as the us,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Throne_of_Charlemagne', 'http://hesis.mapto.ru/bibliography/essays-on-summer-season-for-kids', 'http://www.sheaky.com/2009/09/bye-summer-hello-fall.html', 'http://www.sloansemester.org/season', 'http://metaglossary.com/define/summer', 'http://picture-newsletter.com/seasons/index.htm', 'https://www.thefreedictionary.com/summer']","During May, June, and July, the Northern Hemisphere is exposed to more direct sunlight because the hemisphere faces the Sun. The same is true of the Southern Hemisphere in November, December, and January. It is Earth's axial tilt that causes the Sun to be higher in the sky during the summer months, which increases the solar flux. However, due to seasonal lag, June, July, and August are the warmest months in the Northern Hemisphere while December, January, and February are the warmest months in the Southern Hemisphere.",does england have the same seasons as the us
where is sierra leone located on a map,"['https://www.mapsland.com/africa/sierra-leone', 'http://www.jesusdelivers.com/deliverance-missions/sierra-leone-2013', 'http://www.easybranches.pro/yachts/destinations/africa/', 'https://www.travelerbase.com/index.php?proc=search&term=10%20Best%20Places%20to%20Visit%20in%20Sierra%20Leone', 'https://aho.org/countries/sierra-leone/', 'http://www.hellosanya.com/news/476.html', 'https://www.grace.ie/once-project-in-sierra-leone/']","Sierra Leone (/ siːˈɛərə liːˈoʊniː,-liːˈoʊn / (listen)), officially the Republic of Sierra Leone, is a country in West Africa. It is bordered by Guinea to the north-east, Liberia to the south-east, and the Atlantic Ocean to the south-west. Sierra Leone has a tropical climate, with a diverse environment ranging from savannah to rainforests. The country has a total area of 71,740 km (27,699 sq mi) and a population of 7,075,641 (based on 2015 national census). It is a constitutional republic with a directly elected president and a unicameral legislature.",where is sierra leone located on a map
