who started the practice of gerrymandering back in 1812 and what state was he from,"['http://www.untrans.eu/english/words/gerrymandering.html', 'http://hitchhikersgui.de/Gerrymandering', 'https://pjmedia.com/zombie/2010/11/10/gerrymandering-101/?singlepage=true', 'https://www.localjewishnews.com/2015/10/25/susans-suggestions-for-the-elections-tuesday-november-3-2015/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Gerrymandering.html', 'http://timip.co.uk/newtmandering/', 'https://www.heissatopia.com/2016/05/jerrymeandering-into-future.html']","The word gerrymander (originally written Gerry-mander) was used for the first time in the Boston Gazette on 26 March 1812. The word was created in reaction to a redrawing of Massachusetts state senate election districts under Governor Elbridge Gerry (/ ˈɡɛri /; 1744 -- 1814). In 1812, Governor Gerry signed a bill that redistricted Massachusetts to benefit his Democratic-Republican Party. When mapped, one of the contorted districts in the Boston area was said to resemble the shape of a mythological salamander.",who started the practice of gerrymandering back in 1812 and what state was he from
when was the game snakes and ladders invented,"['http://birchsidestudios.com/435-essay-on-my-favourite-game-snake-and-ladder.php', 'http://marsvenusinstitute.com/adders-and-ladders-online-dating.php', 'http://www.princeton.edu/~achaney/tmve/wiki100k/docs/Snakes_and_ladders.html', 'http://gambiter.com/tabletop/History_games.html', 'https://thegenealogyofstyle.wordpress.com/tag/bradley/']","Snakes and Ladders originated in India as part of a family of dice board games that included Gyan chauper and pachisi (present-day Ludo and Parcheesi). The game made its way to England and was sold as ""Snakes and Ladders"", then the basic concept was introduced in the United States as Chutes and Ladders (an ""improved new version of England's famous indoor sport"") by game pioneer Milton Bradley in 1943.",when was the game snakes and ladders invented
whats the difference between bok choi and pak choi,"['https://theweatheredgreytable.com/bok-choy/', 'http://jiomom.com/seeds/chinese-cabbage/', 'http://www.ozpolitic.com/gardening/pak-choy.html', 'https://ro-systemreviews.com/hydroponics-for-beginners/', 'https://action-reaction-training.com/category/recipes/fish/', 'http://www.livebettergarden.com/2013/03/chinese-cabbage-or-bok-choy.html', 'https://www.foodsforbetterhealth.com/bok-choy-nutrition-facts-benefits-and-side-effects-38202']","Other than the ambiguous term ""Chinese cabbage"", the most widely used name in North America for the chinensis variety is bok choy (from the Cantonese, literally meaning ""white vegetable""; also spelled pak choi, bok choi, and pak choy). In the UK and South Africa, the term pak choi is used. Less commonly, the descriptive English names Chinese chard, Chinese mustard, celery mustard, and spoon cabbage are also employed.",whats the difference between bok choi and pak choi
where do the new star trek fit into series,"['http://www.celebtwitternews.com/everything-about-star-trek-discovery/8444/', 'https://taylornetworkofpodcasts.com/2017/01/04/star-trek-discovery-what-we-know-so-far/', 'https://wikipops.com/?wiki=Star+Trek%3A+Discovery', 'https://www.distractify.com/entertainment/2017/09/26/1Eu8zB/star-trek-viewers', 'https://www.khatrimazas.com/star-trek-discovery-season-1-download/', 'http://vfxspecialists.com/12-star-trek-films-and-series-that-were-nearly-made/', 'https://www.geeky-gadgets.com/star-trek-discovery-season-one-24-07-2017/']","Star Trek: Discovery is an American television series created for CBS All Access by Bryan Fuller and Alex Kurtzman. It is the first series developed specifically for that service, and the first Star Trek series since Star Trek: Enterprise concluded in 2005. Set roughly a decade before the events of the original Star Trek series and separate from the timeline of the concurrently produced feature films, Discovery explores the Federation -- Klingon war while following the crew of the USS Discovery. Gretchen J. Berg and Aaron Harberts serve as showrunners on the series, with producing support from Akiva Goldsman.",where do the new star trek fit into series
why did the ruler of kashmir join india,"['https://mediaindia.eu/business-politics/kashmir-remains-the-flash-point-between-india-and-pakistan/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?pagenum=2&ads=1&title=Kashmir+post&auto=Kashmir+post&author=system&domain_name=kashmirpost.com&standalone=1&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Kashmir+post', 'http://kashmirtravelservice.com/kashmir.html', 'https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/topic/pakistan-occupied-kashmir', 'https://chartercenter.eu/kashmir-gold.html', 'http://wonderfulpakistan.com/administrative-unites-of-pakistan/azad-kashmir-pakistan/', 'https://www.mintpressnews.com/how-hindu-nationalism-intensified-indias-brutal-repression-of-kashmir/238559/']","At the time of the British withdrawal from India, Maharaja Hari Singh, the ruler of the state, preferred to become independent and remain neutral between the successor dominions of India and Pakistan. However, an uprising in the western districts of the State followed by an attack by raiders from the neighbouring Northwest Frontier Province, supported by Pakistan, put an end to his plans for independence. On 26 October 1947, the Maharaja signed the Instrument of Accession joining the Dominion of India in return for military aid. The western and northern districts presently known as Azad Kashmir and Gilgit-Baltistan passed to the control of Pakistan, while the remaining territory became the Indian state Jammu and Kashmir.",why did the ruler of kashmir join india
what the meaning of hair of the dog,"['http://energysip.com/dr_hair.html', 'http://www.tmcreative.co/']","""Hair of the dog"", short for ""Hair of the dog that bit you"", is a colloquial expression in the English language predominantly used to refer to alcohol that is consumed with the aim of lessening the effects of a hangover.",what the meaning of hair of the dog
what are we celebrating when we celebrate labor day,"['http://www.multibriefs.com/briefs/CASE/CASE090318.php', 'http://seasidereunion65.info/valentines-day-weekend-2019.html', 'http://www.loveofthegameproductions.com/2017/09/', 'https://www.dreamcalendars.com/when-is/labor-day', 'http://blog.drapestyle.com/tag/custom-drapery-supplier/page/7/', 'https://www.distractify.com/politics/2017/09/06/Z1PuEA8/labor-day-graph', 'https://www.spinweld.com/spinweld-honors-labor-day/']","Labor Day in the United States is a public holiday celebrated on the first Monday in September. It honors the American labor movement and the contributions that workers have made to the strength, prosperity, laws and well-being of the country. It is the Monday of the long weekend known as Labor Day Weekend and it is considered the unofficial end of summer in the United States. It is recognized as a federal holiday.",what are we celebrating when we celebrate labor day
why was the first battle of the marne important,"['https://majormike.us/2016/09/05/today-in-history-71/', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/First_Battle_of_the_Marne', 'http://yeovilhistory.info/eason-samuelphillip.htm', 'http://yeovilhistory.info/gray-edward.htm', 'http://yeovilhistory.info/sparks-william.htm', 'https://majormike.us/subjects/reign-of-terror/', 'http://www.neverseenbooks.com/?tag=autochromes']","The Battle of the Marne (French: Première bataille de la Marne, also known as the Miracle of the Marne, Le Miracle de la Marne) was a World War I battle fought from 6 -- 10 September 1914. It resulted in an Allied victory against the German armies in the west. The battle was the culmination of the German advance into France and pursuit of the Allied armies which followed the Battle of the Frontiers in August and had reached the eastern outskirts of Paris. A counter-attack by six French armies and the British Expeditionary Force (BEF) along the Marne River forced the Imperial German Army to retreat north-west, leading to the First Battle of the Aisne and the Race to the Sea. The battle was a victory for the Allied Powers but led to four years of trench warfare stalemate on the Western Front.","This Page Does Not Exist This Page Does Not Exist Sorry, the page you are looking for could not be found. It's just an accident that was not intentional."
when was the lyrical ballads published why is this volume important,"['https://www.kobo.com/ch/fr/ebook/coleridge-and-wordsworth-lyrical-ballads-other-poems-including-their-thoughts-on-the-principles-of-poetry', 'https://www.hazararights.com/', 'http://www.klloveley.com/category/author-journal/', 'http://www.justquiz.co.uk/2014/03/64-questionsnews-about-my-wqc-practice.html', 'http://www.indepthinfo.com/history/romanticism.htm', 'https://schoolbag.info/literature/world/67.html', 'https://www.pdf-2-flashbook.com/books/506141961/lyrical-ballads-with-other-poems-1800-volume-2.pdf']","Lyrical Ballads, with a Few Other Poems is a collection of poems by William Wordsworth and Samuel Taylor Coleridge, first published in 1798 and generally considered to have marked the beginning of the English Romantic movement in literature. The immediate effect on critics was modest, but it became and remains a landmark, changing the course of English literature and poetry.",when was the lyrical ballads published why is this volume important
what is the last season of the big bang theory,"['https://tastedive.com/show/Young-Sheldon', 'https://www.retro100.com/pop-culture/tv-collectibles/big-bang-theory-collectibles-bobbleheads-action-figures/', 'http://mp4moviez.desi/movie/7464/The_big_bang_theory_season_10_complate_720p_bluray.html', 'https://femcompetitor.com/mayim-bialik-sensational-actress-passionate-activist/', 'https://news.meaws.com/news/tags/big-bang-theory', 'http://hadrians-wall.tk/collect-information-about-carbon-dating-method-and-radioactive-isotopes.html', 'http://www.bloggersworld.in/top-most-watched-tv-shows-in-the-world-2/']","In March 2017, CBS renewed the series for two additional seasons, bringing its total to twelve, and running through the 2018 -- 19 television season.",what is the last season of the big bang theory
what is a dream and why do we dream,"['https://vashvariant.info/dream-of-colors-painting-print-on-wrapped-canvas.cgi', 'http://findingbetter.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=22592', 'http://www.futureofmankind.co.uk/Billy_Meier/Creativity', 'http://www.smashinglists.com/10-ways-to-control-your-dreams/', 'https://xajenarelax.agronumericus.com/freudian-psychoanalysis-of-victors-dream-in-frankenstein-94313zo9280.html', 'http://www.culex.dk/modules/onair/detail.php?ext=info&oa_id=32', 'http://googledictionary.freecollocation.com/meaning?word=dream']","A dream is a succession of images, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. The content and purpose of dreams are not fully understood, though they have been a topic of scientific speculation, as well as a subject of philosophical and religious interest, throughout recorded history. Dream interpretation is the attempt at drawing meaning from dreams and searching for an underlying message. The scientific study of dreams is called oneirology.",what is a dream and why do we dream
how did jack o lanterns get their name,"['http://plheineman.net/willwisp.htm', ""https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Will-o'-the-wisp.html"", 'https://m.dailyjigsawpuzzles.net/halloween-jigsaws/happy-halloween_2206.html', 'https://monsterologist.com/blogs/news/stingy-jack-and-the-origin-of-the-jack-o-lantern']","The term jack-o'-lantern was originally used to describe the visual phenomenon ignis fatuus (lit., ""foolish fire"") known as a will-o'-the-wisp in English folklore. Used especially in East England, its earliest known use dates to the 1660s. The term ""will-o'-the-wisp"" uses ""wisp"" (a bundle of sticks or paper sometimes used as a torch) and the proper name ""Will"": thus, ""Will-of-the-torch."" The term jack-o'-lantern is of the same construction: ""Jack of (the) lantern.""",how did jack o lanterns get their name
where are the papillary and dermal layers located,"['http://www.hoajonline.com/dermatolaspects/subject/Dermal_structures', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Animal_skin', 'https://www.reskin.eu/?page_id=1632', 'http://www.diamondsmarts.com/some_helpful_information_about_dry_skin_356800a.html', 'http://www.boisfortertc.com/best_free_tips_on_taking_care_of_your_dry_skin_356818a.html', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Skin', 'https://www.disabled-world.com/health/dermatology/skin/']","The dermis or corium is a layer of skin between the epidermis (with which it makes up the cutis) and subcutaneous tissues, that primarily consists of dense irregular connective tissue and cushions the body from stress and strain. It is divided into two layers, the superficial area adjacent to the epidermis called the papillary region and a deep thicker area known as the reticular dermis. The dermis is tightly connected to the epidermis through a basement membrane. Structural components of the dermis are collagen, elastic fibers, and extrafibrillar matrix. It also contains mechanoreceptors that provide the sense of touch and thermoreceptors that provide the sense of heat. In addition, hair follicles, sweat glands, sebaceous glands, apocrine glands, lymphatic vessels and blood vessels are present in the dermis. Those blood vessels provide nourishment and waste removal for both dermal and epidermal cells.",where are the papillary and dermal layers located
where did the term high noon come from,"['http://www.rockart-va.org/blackberry.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Noon', 'https://www.climateprediction.net/climate-science/glossary/tropics/', 'https://mediamonitors.net/direction-of-al-qiblah/', 'https://www.arlingtoncardinal.com/2017/12/astronomical-winter-arrives-today-at-1044-am-cst-with-the-winter-solstice-and-the-harp-twins/', 'https://blog.poseidonexpeditions.com/mysteries-of-the-polar-circles/', 'https://www.clarityforlife.training/solstice.html']","Solar noon (informally high noon) is the moment when the Sun contacts the observer's meridian, reaching its highest position above the horizon on that day (""Sun transit time""). This is also the origin of the terms ante meridiem (a.m.) and post meridiem (p.m.), as noted below. The Sun is directly overhead at solar noon at the Equator on the equinoxes, at the Tropic of Cancer (latitude 23 ° 26 ′ 13.0"" N) on the June solstice and at the Tropic of Capricorn (23 ° 26 ′ 13.0"" S) on the December solstice. In the Northern Hemisphere, north of the Tropic of Cancer, the Sun is due south of the observer at solar noon; in the Southern Hemisphere, south of the Tropic of Capricorn, it is due north.",where did the term high noon come from
the abilene paradox the management of agreement summary,"['http://www.strategistblog.com/2017/01/managing-agreement.html', 'https://pioneerproductions.blogspot.com/2015/06/the-bus-to-abilene.html', 'https://tractorpoint.com/forum/tractor-project-howto/189352/1/Rear-Log-Splitter-Build-Project-Part-2.html', 'http://ptable.blogspot.com/2015/09/', 'https://www.wolfmotivation.com/programs/mismanaged-agreement-the-abilene-paradox-workshop', 'http://anythingbeautiful.blogspot.com/2012/03/', 'http://www.petergmcdermott.com/2012/03/24/youre-doing-it-wrong-and-thats-okay/']","In the Abilene paradox, a group of people collectively decide on a course of action that is counter to the preferences of many or all of the individuals in the group. It involves a common breakdown of group communication in which each member mistakenly believes that their own preferences are counter to the group's and, therefore, does not raise objections. A common phrase relating to the Abilene Paradox is a desire not to ""rock the boat"". This differs from groupthink in that the Abilene paradox is characterized by an inability to manage agreement.",the abilene paradox the management of agreement summary
who is the main actress in animal kingdom,"['https://www.shoutbii.com/2019/01/download-animal-kingdom-season-3.html', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&pagenum=3&ads=1&author=system&auto=Africa+acrobats&standalone=1&domain_name=africaacrobats.com&title=Africa+acrobats&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Africa+acrobats', 'http://hotdvdmovies.com/animal-kingdom-season-1-dvd-box-set-p-1682.html', 'http://lindsey-moran.squarespace.com/television', 'http://babycareclub.org/torrent-hdrip-movies.html', 'https://hollywoodhiccups.com/2016/05/25/the-young-and-the-restless-news-camryn-grimes-to-appear-in-tnts-new-drama-animal-kingdom/']","Animal Kingdom is an American drama television series developed by Jonathan Lisco. It is based on the 2010 Australian film of the same name by David Michôd, who is executive producer for the series, alongside Liz Watts who also produced the movie. The series follows a 17-year-old boy, who, after the death of his mother, moves in with his estranged relatives, the Codys, a criminal family clan governed by matriarch Smurf. Ellen Barkin portrays the leading role of Janine ""Smurf"" Cody, played by Jacki Weaver in the 2010 film.",who is the main actress in animal kingdom
the inalienable rights in the declaration of independence are,"['https://fivedotoh.com/2018/07/02/god-given-liberties/', 'https://awildernessvoice.blog/category/the-pursuit-of-happiness/', 'http://www.happysonship.com/anyone-truly-happy/', 'http://rivieraucc.org/overcome-evil-with-good-932017/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence', 'http://www.tacticalchristianity.org/blog/chasing-happiness', 'http://essayagency.club/what-happiness-means-to-me-essay/']","""Life, Liberty and the pursuit of Happiness"" is a well-known phrase in the United States Declaration of Independence. The phrase gives three examples of the ""unalienable rights"" which the Declaration says have been given to all human beings by their Creator, and which governments are created to protect.",the inalienable rights in the declaration of independence are
what did the fair pay act of 2009 do,"['http://whitehouse.blogs.cnn.com/2012/10/10/potuss-schedule-for-wednesday-october-10-2012/', 'https://www.thewrap.com/lilly-ledbetter-equal-pay-champion-agrees-biopic-film-rachel-feldman-76761/', 'http://www.catinspections.com/webstats/annual/pdf/download-%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BF%D1%83%D0%BB%D1%8F%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%8F-%D1%8D%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%B8%D1%8F-%5B%D0%A3%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%B1.-%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%B8%D0%B5-%D0%B4%D0%BB%D1%8F-%D0%B1%D0%B8%D0%BE%D0%BB.-%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%86.-%D1%83%D0%BD-%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%B2%5D.html', 'https://www.fisherphillips.com/Keystone-Employment-Law/2016/03', 'http://archive.constantcontact.com/fs114/1110936525962/archive/1112675534318.html', 'https://sg.answers.yahoo.com/question/index?qid=20100402043128AA9Si7k', 'https://www.funwithfinancials.net/do-we-need-a-4th-wave-of-feminism-for-nonprofits/']","The Lilly Ledbetter Fair Pay Act of 2009 (Pub. L. 111 -- 2, S. 181) is a federal statute in the United States that was the first bill signed into law by President Barack Obama on January 29, 2009. The Act amends the Civil Rights Act of 1964. The new act states that the 180-day statute of limitations for filing an equal-pay lawsuit regarding pay discrimination resets with each new paycheck affected by that discriminatory action. The law directly addressed Ledbetter v. Goodyear Tire & Rubber Co., 550 U.S. 618 (2007), a U.S. Supreme Court decision that the statute of limitations for presenting an equal-pay lawsuit begins on the date that the employer makes the initial discriminatory wage decision, not at the date of the most recent paycheck.",what did the fair pay act of 2009 do
what do you call a person from croatia,"['https://dnaconsultants.com/croatian/', 'http://www.legal500.com/firms/11986-wolf-theiss-rechtsanwalte-gmbh-cokg/offices/13155-vienna-austria/profile', 'https://www.avivadirectory.com/Regional/Europe/Bosnia-Herzegovina/', 'https://napafoodandvine.com/slivovitz-traditional-czech-hooch/', 'https://www.translatebyhumans.com/en/services/translation/ukrainian', 'https://www.cyndislist.com/czech/professionals/', 'https://www.tpa-group.at/en/press/tpa-celebrates-40-years-of-experience/']","Croats (/ ˈkroʊæt, ˈkroʊɑːt /; Croatian: Hrvati, pronounced (xr̩ʋăːti)) are a nation and South Slavic ethnic group located at the crossroads of Central Europe and the Balkans. Croats mainly live in Croatia and Bosnia and Herzegovina, but are an officially recognized minority in Austria, Czech Republic, Hungary, Poland, Italy, Montenegro, Romania, Serbia, Slovenia, and Slovakia. Responding to political, social and economic pressure, many Croats have migrated throughout Europe (especially Germany, Austria, Switzerland, France and Italy) and the Americas (particularly the United States, Canada, Argentina, and Chile), establishing a diaspora.",what do you call a person from croatia
who started the ganesh chaturthi festival in india,"['http://e-coexist.com/ecoexist-foundation/eco-ganesh/', 'http://shivagod.in/ganesha/', 'http://smk-group.ru/2910330383.html']","It is unclear when the festival started, it became a major social and public event with sponsorship of Shivaji after Mughal-Maratha wars, and again in the 19th century after public appeal by Indian freedom fighter Lokmanya Tilak, who championed it as a means to circumvent the colonial British government ban on Hindu gatherings through its anti-public assembly legislation in 1892.",who started the ganesh chaturthi festival in india
what are the names of florida georgia line singers,"['https://www.successfulsinging.com/backing-tracks/florida-georgia-line/', 'https://concertful.com/tour/florida-georgia-line/', 'https://hercountrymusic.com/florida-georgia-line-tour-dates/', 'http://www.sanbernardinoamphitheater.com/events/florida-georgia-line-dan-and-shay-morgan-wallen/', 'http://stmaartencarrentalguide.com/transportation/florida-georgia-line-get-your-shine-on-ringtone.php', 'http://www.tinleyparkamphitheater.com/events/florida-georgia-line-dan-and-shay-morgan-wallen/', 'https://millionairesconcierge.com/services/florida-georgia-line-in-concert']","Florida Georgia Line (sometimes abbreviated as FGL) is an American country music duo consisting of vocalists Tyler Hubbard and Brian Kelley. Their 2012 debut single ""Cruise"", which remains their most popular song, broke two major sales records: it was downloaded over seven million times, making it the first country song ever to receive the Diamond certification, and it became the best-selling digital country song of all time, with 24 weeks at number one, until it was surpassed in July 2017 by Sam Hunt's ""Body Like a Back Road"". ""Cruise"" helped to pioneer a style of country music known as ""bro-country"", which incorporates production elements from rock and hip-hop music, and tends to cover subject matter such as partying, drinking, driving trucks and romantic attraction. Much of their subsequent music has been tagged with the ""bro-country"" label as well.",what are the names of florida georgia line singers
who was the person known to find the first calculation of pi when was it,"['https://findwords.info/term/pi', 'http://pi.co.uk/category/uncategorized/', 'http://tesla-institute.com/index.php/what-is-electricity/14-tesla-institute/429-pi-number', 'http://sciencenewsarticles.org/1351648/pi-derivation/', 'http://search-computing.eu/86837-college-essays-on-yourself/', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=who+created+pie+in+math&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'http://www.historyof.net/history-of-pi.html']","Ancient civilizations required fairly accurate computed values for π for practical reasons, including the Egyptians and Babylonians. Around 250 BC the Greek mathematician Archimedes created an algorithm for calculating it. It was approximated to seven digits, using geometrical techniques, in Chinese mathematics, and to about five digits in Indian mathematics in the 5th century AD. The historically first exact formula for π, based on infinite series, was not available until a millennium later, when in the 14th century the Madhava -- Leibniz series was discovered in Indian mathematics. In the 20th and 21st centuries, mathematicians and computer scientists discovered new approaches that, when combined with increasing computational power, extended the decimal representation of π to many trillions of digits after the decimal point. Practically all scientific applications require no more than a few hundred digits of π, and many substantially fewer, so the primary motivation for these computations is the quest to find more efficient algorithms for calculating lengthy numeric series, as well as the desire to break records. The extensive calculations involved have also been used to test supercomputers and high-precision multiplication algorithms.",who was the person known to find the first calculation of pi when was it
where is the trailing arm on a car,"['http://metaglossary.com/define/trailing+arm', 'https://www.scribd.com/document/319762258/trailer-ebs', 'https://www.holmegaardresource.com/stainless-steel-rear-auxillary-return-heater-hose-connector-for-grand-caravan-town-country/', 'http://madabout-kitcars.com/kitcar/kb.php?aid=207', 'https://livetvguide.net/4-3-chevy-wiring-harness.html', 'http://www.buggiesgonewild.com/electric-club-car/76788-2006-club-car-precedent-48v.html', 'http://ticktickvroom.com/brabus-850-6-0-biturbo-ibusiness-a-rolling-office-that-will-roll-at-217-mph/']","A trailing-arm suspension, sometimes referred as trailing-link is a vehicle suspension design in which one or more arms (or ""links"") are connected between (and perpendicular to and forward of) the axle and a pivot point (located on the chassis of a motor vehicle). It is typically used on the rear axle of a motor vehicle. A leading arm, as used on the Citroën 2CV and the M422 Mighty Mite, has an arm connected between (and perpendicular to, and to the rear of) the axle and the chassis. It is used on the front axle.",where is the trailing arm on a car
