who won the world cup in russia 2018,"['https://amarkhata.com/final-photos-fifa-2018-world-cup/', 'https://b2b.partcommunity.com/community/knowledge/en/index/page/2', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Antoine_Griezmann', 'http://www.onlinenewsheardnow.com/croatia-tops-england-to-advance-in-world-cup-boasting-about-teams-victory/4377/', 'https://sputniknews.com/nizhny-novgorod-worldcup-2018/201807061066102546-fifa-world-cup-uruguay-france/', 'https://www.dw.com/en/euro-2016-paris-joining-the-party-as-french-belief-grows/a-19369067', 'http://indamotion.com/news/view/27865/france-vs-belgium.html']","Before 2018, France's only World Cup victory was in 1998 -- though they had also reached the final in 2006 -- while Croatia were playing in their first World Cup final. Both teams had defeated former World Cup champions on their way to the final: France defeated 1930 and 1950 winners Uruguay, Croatia defeated 1966 winners England and both teams defeated 1978 and 1986 winners Argentina. Croatia became the third Eastern European nation to reach the World Cup final, and the first since Czechoslovakia lost the final in 1962 to Brazil.",who won the world cup in russia 2018
who played scum of the earth on wkrp,['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Jimmy_Robinson'],"Michael Des Barres from the band performed songs on the fourth episode of the first season of the sitcom WKRP in Cincinnati as part of the fictional hoodlum rock group ""Scum of the Earth"". Michael Des Barres and two other actors played the part of the band during most of the TV show, but the band Detective performed on the end of the show segment.",who played scum of the earth on wkrp
who sings i could be the one avicii,"['http://if-yu.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=14970', 'https://musiconvinyl.blogspot.com/2014/12/', 'http://youtubekonverter.com/video/sdmL1sEm1FY/britney-spears-oopsi-did-it-again-full-album-2000', 'https://www.rockpeaks.com/artists/y/Years-Years', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=5&ads=1&author=system&auto=Coconut+farm&standalone=1&domain_name=coconutfarm.org&title=Coconut+farm&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Coconut+farm', 'https://sheetmusic-free.com/i-took-a-pill-in-ibiza-sheet-music-mike-posner/', 'https://multimedia-english.com/videos/music/all-about-that-bass-meghan-trainor-5687']","""I Could Be the One"" is a song by Swedish DJ Avicii and Dutch DJ Nicky Romero, which features uncredited vocals from Swedish singer Noonie Bao. The song was released as a digital download in Sweden and the Netherlands on 26 December 2012. It peaked at number three on the Swedish Singles Chart. Internationally, the single topped the charts in Hungary and the United Kingdom, peaked within the top 10 in Australia, Belgium, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Finland, the Netherlands, Norway and the Republic of Ireland and the top 20 of the charts in Austria and New Zealand.",who sings i could be the one avicii
what is the difference between igcse and a level,"['http://www.3dhometutors.com/', 'https://cnx.sbs.ac.th/cambridge-igcse-2/', 'http://searchassociatesusa.org/Resources/Glossary.aspx', 'http://samhainternationalschool.com/IGCSE.aspx', 'https://www.berlin-international-school.de/igcse-bis-en/articles/igcse.html', 'https://www.ntk.edu.hk/en/academics_offerings/course-selection-guide', 'https://www.reachivy.com/study-abroad/top-HS-degrees/IGCSE.html']","Its academic worth is comparable to many secondary school curricula worldwide, such as England's GCSE, the North American GED or high school diploma, Hong Kong's HKCEE, Singapore's O-Level, and the Indian CBSE or ICSE courses. The IGCSE prepares students for further academic study, including progression to A Level and BTEC Level 3 study, Cambridge Pre-U, IB Diploma Programme and other equivalents. It is recognised by academic institutions and employers around the world and is considered by many institutions as equivalent to the standard GCSE.",what is the difference between igcse and a level
where does mcgill university rank in the world,"['http://www.infogalactic.com/info/McGill_University', 'https://www.cs.mcgill.ca/~xueliu/site/reputation_and_rankings.html', 'https://readtiger.com/wkp/en/University_of_Alberta', 'http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/McGill_University', 'https://yocket.in/university-reviews/university-of-newcastle-2953/medicine', 'http://wikien3.appspot.com/wiki/University_of_Illinois_at_Chicago', 'https://www.therightu.com/university/university-of-illinois-chicago']","Internationally, McGill ranked 32nd in the world and 2nd in Canada in the 2018 QS World University Rankings. It was ranked 42nd in the world by the 2016-2017 Times Higher Education World University Rankings and 63rd in the world by the Academic Ranking of World Universities (ARWU) 2016. Times Higher Education also ranked McGill 18th in the world in its 2016 Global Employability University Rankings. In the 2011 Emerging / Trendence Global Employability Ranking, McGill was ranked the 19th finest in the world, and 1st in Canada, for popularity among major employers. In the 2008 College Prowler Online rankings for Academics at North American universities, McGill earned an A-for Academics; making it the only Canadian school to achieve a grade above a B-.",where does mcgill university rank in the world
what caribbean country shares an island with haiti,"['http://booking-otel.ru/index.php?p=4&lang=en&country=57', 'https://www.freedomcircle.com/place/haiti', 'http://www.kolumnmagazine.com/2016/10/11/hurricane-matthews-devastation-haiti-forces-un-call-120m-aid/', 'https://palliativkinder.at/cultivating-hope-in-haiti/', 'https://demo.raratheme.com/benevolent-pro/2016/05/20/cultivating-hope-in-haiti/', 'https://www.mapsland.com/north-america/haiti', 'http://www.phototurism.com/photo_turism/?q=en/haiti']","Haiti (/ ˈheɪti / (listen); French: Haïti (a. iti); Haitian Creole: Ayiti (ajiti)), officially the Republic of Haiti (French: République d'Haïti; Haitian Creole: Repiblik Ayiti) and formerly called Hayti, is a sovereign state located on the island of Hispaniola in the Greater Antilles archipelago of the Caribbean Sea. It occupies the western three-eighths of the island, which it shares with the Dominican Republic. Haiti is 27,750 square kilometres (10,714 sq mi) in size and has an estimated 10.8 million people, making it the most populous country in the Caribbean Community (CARICOM) and the second-most populous country in the Caribbean as a whole. The region was originally inhabited by the indigenous Taíno people. Spain landed on the island on 5 December 1492 during the first voyage of Christopher Columbus across the Atlantic. When Columbus initially landed in Haiti, he had thought he had found India or China. On Christmas Day 1492, Columbus' flagship the Santa Maria ran aground north of what is now Limonade. As a consequence, Columbus ordered his men to salvage what they could from the ship, and he created the first European settlement in the Americas, naming it La Navidad after the day the ship was destroyed.",where is haiti located on the world map
where is the largest most extensive rainforest in the world located,"['https://ourplnt.com/tag/amazon/', 'http://www.the-office.com/bedtime-story/amazon.htm', 'https://www.10interestingfacts.com/10-interesting-facts-about-amazon-rainforest.html', 'http://www.allrefer.com/7-natural-wonders-of-nature-in-the-world', 'http://www.brazil4u.tours/location/amazon-rainforest/', 'http://www.merinews.com/article/amazon-rainforest-marvel-of-nature-and-unrivaled-ecosystem-in-size-and-diversity/15931799.shtml', 'http://www.traveltobrazil.org/post/10-places-of-famous-attractions-in-brazil.html']","The Amazon rainforest (Portuguese: Floresta Amazônica or Amazônia; Spanish: Selva Amazónica, Amazonía or usually Amazonia; French: Forêt amazonienne; Dutch: Amazoneregenwoud), also known in English as Amazonia or the Amazon Jungle, is a moist broadleaf forest in the Amazon biome that covers most of the Amazon basin of South America. This basin encompasses 7,000,000 square kilometres (2,700,000 sq mi), of which 5,500,000 square kilometres (2,100,000 sq mi) are covered by the rainforest. This region includes territory belonging to nine nations. The majority of the forest is contained within Brazil, with 60% of the rainforest, followed by Peru with 13%, Colombia with 10%, and with minor amounts in Venezuela, Ecuador, Bolivia, Guyana, Suriname and French Guiana. States or departments in four nations contain ""Amazonas"" in their names. The Amazon represents over half of the planet's remaining rainforests, and comprises the largest and most biodiverse tract of tropical rainforest in the world, with an estimated 390 billion individual trees divided into 16,000 species.",where is the largest most extensive rainforest in the world located
what is the story of the sixth sense,"['http://www.artandpopularculture.com/The_Sixth_Sense', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=what+is+the+6th+sense&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'http://portlandinsight.org/node/4478', 'http://www.windexpo.org/?cat=2', 'http://movienasha.com/top-18-best-thriller-movies-of-hollywood-of-all-time/', 'https://www.playbuzz.com/avibwx10/the-9-best-psychological-horror-movies-of-all-time', 'https://cinema.mu/movie-article-reviews-and-cinema-news/split-movie-review/']","The Sixth Sense is a 1999 American supernatural horror-thriller film written and directed by M. Night Shyamalan. The film tells the story of Cole Sear (Haley Joel Osment), a troubled, isolated boy who is able to see and talk to the dead, and an equally troubled child psychologist named Malcolm Crowe (Bruce Willis) who tries to help him. The film established Shyamalan as a writer and director, and introduced the cinema public to his traits, most notably his affinity for surprise endings.",what is the story of the sixth sense
what is australia's system of government called,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Monarchy_of_Australia', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/8th_Division_(Australia)', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Charles_Perkins_Centre', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/prime-ministers-of-australia-through-history.html', 'https://hubpages.com/politics/The-Australian-Political-Parties', 'https://www.visas.com.pk/australia/government-of-australia', 'https://www.immigrationoverseas.com/visa-forum/press-release/the-migration-statistics-of-australia-immigration-10.aspx']","The Government of the Commonwealth of Australia (also referred to as the Australian Government, the Commonwealth Government, the Federal Government, and formally Her Majesty's Government) is the government of the Commonwealth of Australia, a federal parliamentary constitutional monarchy.",what is australia's system of government called
where did the name 7 up come from,"['http://belgiquesets.servemp3.com:8000/wordpress/archives/15294', 'https://www.chicagotribune.com/suburbs/post-tribune/news/ct-ptb-potempa-column-st-0708-story.html']","A myth exists that the 7 Up name comes from the drink having a pH over 7. That would make it neutral or basic on the scale; however, this is not the case, as the 7 Up pH is close to 3.79, similar to other drinks of the type. The real origin of the name is unclear, though Britvic claims that the name comes from the seven main ingredients in the drink, while others have claimed that the number was a coded reference to the lithium contained in the original recipe, which has an atomic mass around 7. Britvic also claims that the name be a result of the fact that 7 Up was bottled in 7-ounce bottles (Coca-Cola and most other soft drinks were bottled in 6-ounce bottles).",where did the name 7 up come from
long term effects of alcohol and the brain,"['http://cheminitaly.markmorvant.com/health-impact-of-alcohol/', 'https://www.selfdecode.com/chemical/ethanol/?utm_source=seo', 'http://bps-research-digest.blogspot.com/2014/08/the-stability-of-your-personality-peaks.html?showComment=1407993543520', 'https://www.stopyouraddiction.com/drug-information/alcohol/alcohol-effects/', 'https://nygamarujifus.agronumericus.com/teenage-alcoholism-in-america-96442se9124.html', 'https://www.premilife.com/diseases/psychiatric-disorders/alcoholismo/', 'http://www.mynutramart.com/high_cholesterol']","The long-term effects of alcohol (also known formally as ethanol) consumption range from cardioprotective health benefits for low to moderate alcohol consumption in industrialized societies with higher rates of cardiovascular disease to severe detrimental effects in cases of chronic alcohol abuse. Health effects associated with alcohol intake in large amounts include an increased risk of alcoholism, malnutrition, chronic pancreatitis, alcoholic liver disease and cancer. In addition, damage to the central nervous system and peripheral nervous system can occur from chronic alcohol abuse. The long-term use of alcohol is capable of damaging nearly every organ and system in the body. The developing adolescent brain is particularly vulnerable to the toxic effects of alcohol. In addition, the developing fetal brain is also vulnerable, and fetal alcohol spectrum disorders (FASDs) may result if pregnant mothers consume alcohol.",long term effects of alcohol and the brain
what states are in the chesapeake bay watershed,"['https://cfpub.epa.gov/ncer_abstracts/index.cfm/fuseaction/display.rfatext/rfa_id/543', 'https://www.governing.com/columns/washington-watch/gov-clean-water-pollution-lakes-rivers.html', 'http://ephenryecocenter.com/homeowners/why-eco/chesapeake-bay-watershed.aspx', 'https://www.earthmagazine.org/tags/atmosphere?page=2', 'https://www.choosecleanwater.org/sign-on-letters-1/tag/2017', 'https://www.greenbiz.com/blog/2009/05/22/case-water-quality-markets-chesapeake-bay', 'https://www.dailypress.com/news/science/dp-nws--pruitt-bay-about-face-20170123-story.html']","The Chesapeake Bay Watershed at 64,299 sq mi (166,530 km) is the largest watershed of the Atlantic Seaboard of North America and includes much of Virginia and Maryland, as well as parts of West Virginia, Delaware, Pennsylvania, and New York and all of Washington, DC.",what states are in the chesapeake bay watershed
what is the metropolitan area in new york,"['http://androidmods.ml/new-york-and-co-free-shipping-163.php', 'https://leearchive.info/news.php?action=show&id=24216', 'https://romp18.info/new-york-jets-black-carbon-fiber-license-plate-frame-set.htm', 'http://vashikaranandblackmagic.in/cone/5839-dore-westbury-mill-for-sale.html', 'https://www.amicidelbargello.it/dore_westbury_mill_plans_40547.html', 'https://www.biggerpockets.com/forums/48/topics/510449-proponents-for-appreciation-strategy?page=2', 'http://www.nyenvironmentreport.com/making-sense-of-news-that-new-york-is-the-most-wasteful-megacity-on-the-planet/']","The New York metropolitan area, also referred to as the Tri-State Area, is the largest metropolitan area in the world by urban landmass, at 4,495 mi (11,642 km). The metropolitan area includes New York City (the most populous city in the United States), Long Island, and the Mid and Lower Hudson Valley in the state of New York; the five largest cities in New Jersey: Newark, Jersey City, Paterson, Elizabeth, and Edison, and their vicinities; six of the seven largest cities in Connecticut: Bridgeport, New Haven, Stamford, Waterbury, Norwalk, and Danbury, and their vicinities.",what is the metropolitan area in new york
who starred in close encounters of the third kind,"['https://www.theblackvault.com/casefiles/steven-spielberg-talks-ufos-close-encounters-third-kind/', 'http://thebigbangweb.com/25-jingle-incontri-ravvicinati%20.php', 'http://copycateffect.blogspot.com/2013/01/twinning.html', 'https://www.lastexittonowhere.com/catalogue/mayflower-project-woven-patch_7601/', 'http://www.annmariethomas.me.uk/2017/08/new-wave-science-fiction-films.html', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/11-16/all', 'https://www.greenbank-hotel.co.uk/our-hotel/blog/whats-on-in-february-in-cornwall/']","Close Encounters of the Third Kind is a 1977 American science fiction film written and directed by Steven Spielberg, and starring Richard Dreyfuss, Melinda Dillon, Teri Garr, Bob Balaban, Cary Guffey, and François Truffaut. It tells the story of Roy Neary, an everyday blue-collar worker in Indiana, whose life changes after an encounter with an unidentified flying object (UFO).",who starred in close encounters of the third kind
who scored the goals for manchester united against west ham,"['http://www.kaosbolaonline.com/2011/11/manchesterunitedfc20102011.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Sergio_Ag%C3%BCero', 'http://fentonia.com/chicharito-the-biography-of-javier-hern-andez-worrall-frank.html', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Javier_Hern%C3%A1ndez', 'https://buzznigeria.com/7-things-never-knew-joseph-yobo/', 'https://informationcradle.com/europe/kevin-de-bruyne/', 'http://www.kaosbolaonline.com/2011/11/liverpoolfc20102011.html']","On 25 January, Hernández scored the equalising goal of a 3 -- 2 comeback away win over Blackpool. Four days later he scored his first FA Cup goal as he netted the winner in a 2 -- 1 away victory over Southampton. Hernández netted twice in a 4 -- 0 away win over Wigan on 26 February. Eight days later, he netted a late consolation goal in a 3 -- 1 derby defeat away to Liverpool. Hernández netted twice in a 2 -- 1 home win over Marseille on 15 March, sending United through to the quarter-finals of the Champions League. On 2 April, he scored the final goal against West Ham United as they came from two goals down to claim a 4 -- 2 away win. On 8 April, Hernández was revealed as a contender for the PFA Young Player of the Year award alongside teammate Nani. Four days later, He opened the scoring in the 2 -- 1 quarter-final win over Chelsea in the Champions League, with the game ending 3 -- 1 on aggregate, sending United through to the semi-finals. He continued his goal scoring form on 23 April scoring the winning goal with a header in the 1 -- 0 home win over Everton.",who scored the goals for manchester united against west ham
what is the name of the river in the garden of eden,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Garden_of_Eden.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Throne_of_Charlemagne', 'http://viddy.com/garden-of-eden-utopia.html', 'http://layittoheart.com/septuagint.html', 'https://gnosticwarrior.com/greek-dna.html', 'http://www.bible-prophecy.com/2012/turkey2012.htm', 'http://www.blainerobison.com/endtimes/revnotes20.htm']","Genesis 2: 10 -- 14 lists four rivers in association with the garden of Eden: Pishon, Gihon, the Tigris, and the Euphrates. It also refers to the land of Cush -- translated / interpreted as Ethiopia, but thought by some to equate to Cossaea, a Greek name for the land of the Kassites. These lands lie north of Elam, immediately to the east of ancient Babylon, which, unlike Ethiopia, does lie within the region being described. In Antiquities of the Jews, the first-century Jewish historian Josephus identifies the Pishon as what ""the Greeks called Ganges"" and the Geon (Gehon) as the Nile.",what is the name of the river in the garden of eden
when does ovulation occur in the ovarian cycle,"['https://cornfs-programs.ucoz.ru/forum/174-258-8', 'https://ivfprescriptions.com/discount-ivf-prescription-drugs-you-can-purchase-from-ivf-prescriptions/', 'https://shycart.com/scat-ovulation-test-kits-91-116', 'https://www.hfe.co.uk/blog/menstruation-and-its-effect-on-exercise-performance/', 'http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/triptorelin+pamoate', 'https://stonecrestfp.com/hl/?/19675/Hypogonadism', 'https://www.elawoman.com/bhopal/doctor/dr-vijay-lakshmi-verma']","Estrogen levels peak towards the end of the follicular phase. This causes a surge in levels of luteinizing hormone (LH) and follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH). This lasts from 24 to 36 hours, and results in the rupture of the ovarian follicles, causing the oocyte to be released from the ovary.",when does ovulation occur in the ovarian cycle
who replaced tom brady when he was hurt,"['http://www.broncosforums.com/forums/archive/index.php/t-34169.html?s=a8f920ff5a5040a929553d0437970b78', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/FedEx_Air_%26_Ground_NFL_Players_of_the_Week', 'https://southernbeau.wordpress.com/category/jarrett-boykin/', 'https://salutemag.com/2016/02/05/new-england-patriots-exit-interview/', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Josh_McDaniels', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Josh_McDaniels.html', 'http://www.carinsurancequote.net/matt-cassel.html']","Cassel became the Patriots' starting quarterback after Week 1 of the 2008 season after then reigning NFL MVP Tom Brady suffered a season-ending knee injury. According to ESPN research, he is the only known quarterback in NFL history to start an NFL game at quarterback without ever starting as a quarterback in college. In February 2009, the Patriots used their franchise tag on Cassel, extending him a one-year contract worth over $14 million, the largest one-year contract for an offensive player in NFL history. Later that offseason, the Patriots made a trade which sent Cassel to the Kansas City Chiefs, who signed him to a 6-year, $62.7 million contract in July 2009. In 2010, Cassel led the Chiefs to their first AFC West divisional championship in seven years, and earned a Pro Bowl berth in the process.",who replaced tom brady when he was hurt
what is the difference between panther and mountain lion,"['http://theworldofanimals.proboards.com/thread/661/cougar-deinonychus-antirrhopus', 'https://dramaslovsgmail.wordpress.com/2017/05/03/cougar-%EA%B0%95%EB%8F%99%EC%98%A4%ED%94%BC-%EA%B0%95%EB%8F%99%EA%B1%B4%EB%A7%88-%EC%98%A4%ED%94%BC%EC%93%B0-opss3-com/', 'http://denise.dreamwidth.org/71796.html', 'http://explainwell.org/index.php/table-of-contents-synthesize-text/reading-the-text/', 'http://starsica.blogspot.com/2008/12/cougar-puma-concolor-part-i.html', 'http://wildlife-animals.com/cougar/commuter-bags.php', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Mount_Assiniboine_Provincial_Park']","The cougar (Puma concolor), also commonly known as the puma, mountain lion, panther or catamount, is a large felid of the subfamily Felinae native to the Americas. Its range, from the Canadian Yukon to the southern Andes of South America, is the widest of any large wild terrestrial mammal in the Western Hemisphere. An adaptable, generalist species, the cougar is found in most American habitat types. It is the biggest cat in North America, and the second-heaviest cat in the New World after the jaguar. Secretive and largely solitary by nature, the cougar is properly considered both nocturnal and crepuscular, although daytime sightings do occur. The cougar is more closely related to smaller felines, including the domestic cat (subfamily Felinae), than to any species of subfamily Pantherinae, of which only the jaguar is native to the Americas.",what is the difference between panther and mountain lion
how do you get a free kick in high school football,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Fair_catch_kick', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Fair_catch_kick.html', 'https://wikimili.com/en/American_football', 'https://blog.nfhsnetwork.com/posts/little-known-rule-results-in-60-yard-field-goal-in-georgia-high-school-playoff-game', 'https://www.englishclub.com/vocabulary/sports-rugby.htm', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/American_football_rules', 'http://www.manchestertitans.co.uk/game/rules/']","The fair catch kick is a rule at the professional and high school levels of American football that allows a team that has just made a fair catch to attempt a free kick from the spot of the catch. The kick must be either a place kick or a drop kick, and if it passes over the crossbar and between the goalposts of the defensive team's goal, a field goal, worth three points, is scored to the offensive team.",how do you get a free kick in high school football
who sang with pentatonix on their christmas special,"['http://runnerwithanappetite.com/3707.html', 'https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-country/see-pentatonix-reba-mcentires-reggae-infused-winter-wonderland-191744/']","On December 14, 2016, the group hosted their first Christmas special, titled around their current album, A Pentatonix Christmas Special. The hour-long special aired on NBC and featured guest appearances by Reba McEntire, Dolly Parton, and Kelly Clarkson.","Page not found – Rolling Stone × Skip to main content 404 OOPS! Something went wrong here! Try searching for it here... Rolling Stone is a part of Penske Media Corporation. © 2026 Rolling Stone, LLC. All rights reserved. Powered by WordPress.com VIP ad"
who is the most recorded artist in history,"['http://www.top10encyclopedia.com/Detail/Top-10-Best-Bollywood-Singers-In-India-10', 'https://www.culturalindia.net/indian-music/indian-singers/asha-bhosle.html', 'https://mytebox.com/Story-Images/Asha-Bhosle.aspx', 'http://www.tollywoodcelebrities.in/2018/01/Asha-Bhosle-Family-Husband-Son-Daughter-Father-Mother-Age-Height-Biography-Profile-Wedding-Photos.html', 'https://www.gkdigest.com/2018/02/asha-bhosle-honoured-with-5th-yash.html', 'http://profiles.lakshmansruthi.com/index1.php?uid=128', 'http://forumjudi.site/eso-shyamala-sundara-95/']","Renowned for her voice range and often credited for her versatility, Bhosle's work includes film music, pop, ghazals, bhajans, traditional Indian classical music, folk songs, qawwalis, and Rabindra Sangeets. Apart from Hindi, she has sung in over 20 Indian and foreign languages. In 2006, Asha Bhosle stated that she had sung over 12,000 songs, a figure repeated by several other sources. In 2011, she was officially acknowledged by the Guinness Book of World Records as the most recorded artist in music history. The Government of India honoured her with the Dadasaheb Phalke Award in 2000 and the Padma Vibhushan in 2008. In 2013, she made her debut as an actress in the film Mai, and received critical acclaim for her performance.",who is the most recorded artist in history
when is the next game of thrones book coming,"['http://agenciatm.info/?newsid=37386', 'http://bignedviga.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=37782', 'https://www.forbes.com/sites/danafeldman/2019/04/11/game-of-thrones-by-the-numbers', 'http://emmijormalainen.com/', 'https://www.freshminds.co.uk/whats-fresh/post/2017/11/03/meet-the-new-2018-ones-to-watch', 'https://blogs.bookforum.com/paper/2017/02/27/', 'https://createdtoread.com/book-review-the-unlikely-heroics-of-sam-holloway-by-rhys-thomas/']","Martin believes the last two volumes of the series will be books of 1,500 + manuscript pages each. They will take readers farther north than any of the previous books, and the Others will appear in The Winds of Winter. Martin has refrained from making hard estimates for the final release date of the novel. In April 2018, Martin revealed that the book would not be published in 2018.",when is the next game of thrones book coming
the girl in star wars the force awakens,"['https://www.cosplaynow.com/rey-costume-for-star-wars-the-force-awakens-cosplay.html', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/star-wars-characters-original-trilogy-sequel-trilogy/', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/star-wars-characters-deserve-spin-offs/', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/hottest-fictional-female-characters/', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/movie-characters-hire-kill-barney-dinosaur/', 'https://crisisonearthprime.com/2015/12/17/star-wars-the-force-awakens-review/', 'https://www.generationstarwars.com/2015/12/']","Rey is a fictional character in the Star Wars franchise, portrayed by English actress Daisy Ridley. First appearing as the main character in Star Wars: Episode VII -- The Force Awakens, Rey is a scavenger who was left behind on the planet Jakku when she was a child, and later becomes involved with the Resistance's conflict with the First Order when her solitary life is interrupted by BB-8, the droid of ace Resistance pilot Poe Dameron, and a runaway Stormtrooper named Finn.",the girl in star wars the force awakens
the works progress administration was created in order to,"['http://worknotatlast.blogspot.com/2015/05/coos-bay-to-newport-oregon.html', 'http://mypostcards.frankchang.org/2014/12/swim-for-health-in-safe-and-pure-pools.html', 'http://midwestbookreview.com/lbw/aug_14.htm', 'http://hellenicgenealogygeek.blogspot.com/2018/08/the-role-of-greek-american-kafeneion-in.html', 'http://www.gqs.gr/the-kafenneion-in-us-and-crime/', 'http://www.spiritofappalachia.com/historic-public-art.html', 'http://edenfieldhouse.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=37&Itemid=208&lang=en']","The Works Progress Administration (WPA; renamed in 1939 as the Work Projects Administration) was the largest and most ambitious American New Deal agency, employing millions of people (mostly unskilled men) to carry out public works projects, including the construction of public buildings and roads. In a much smaller project, Federal Project Number One, the WPA employed musicians, artists, writers, actors and directors in large arts, drama, media, and literacy projects.",the works progress administration was created in order to
meaning of 18 roses and 18 candles in a debut,"['http://corinnemolly.blogspot.com/2018/05/celebrating-little-things-in-life.html', 'http://justbcause.com/2012/12/03/18th-birthday-debut-message/', 'http://justbcause.com/2015/04/27/18th-birthday-message-to-debutante/', 'https://littlefrogprince.wordpress.com/page/2/']","The debut (/ dɛˈbuː /) is a traditional Filipino coming-of-age celebration which celebrates a young woman's 18th birthday, the age of maturity in the Philippines.",meaning of 18 roses and 18 candles in a debut
who plays the joker in batman the dark knight,"['https://watchmoviesnow.co/actor/heath-ledger/', 'https://jiji-blog.com/2018/08/26-incredible-persons-from-australia/', 'http://www.michaelkorsoutletninc.com/2018/10/heath-andrew-ledger_3.html', 'http://hrvcanada.blogspot.com/2011/12/heath-ledger.html', 'https://targetedindividualscanada.com/2011/12/30/heath-ledger/', 'http://fizzshevzenko.blogspot.com/2009/04/blog-post_20.html?widgetType=BlogArchive&widgetId=BlogArchive1&action=toggle&dir=open&toggle=MONTHLY-1233475200000&toggleopen=MONTHLY-1238569200000', 'https://celebsline.com/jamie-foxx/']","Ledger died on 22 January 2008 from an accidental intoxication from prescription drugs. A few months before his death, Ledger had finished filming his performance as The Joker in The Dark Knight. His death occurred during editing of The Dark Knight and in the midst of filming his last role as Tony in The Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus. His untimely death cast a shadow over the subsequent promotion of the $185 million Batman production. Ledger received numerous posthumous accolades for his critically acclaimed performance in the film, including the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, a Best Actor International Award at the 2008 Australian Film Institute Awards (for which he became the first actor to win an award posthumously), the 2008 Los Angeles Film Critics Association Award for Best Supporting Actor, the 2009 Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor -- Motion Picture, and the 2009 BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor.",who plays the joker in batman the dark knight
when do cars need to be smogged in california,"['http://smogstersmog.com/smog-check-woodland-hills/amp/', 'https://www.johnnysautoservice.com/smog-test-san-dimas/', 'https://www.gishgallop.com/trump-rules-california-smog-checks-unconstitutional/', 'http://charmed-friends.tk/map33.html', 'https://gooddaysacramento.cbslocal.com/2018/12/31/you-can-wait-an-extra-two-years-to-get-your-car-smog-checked/', 'http://geo-mexico.com/?tag=pollution', 'http://domvip.tk/best-new-dating-songs.html']","The California Smog Check Program requires vehicles that were manufactured in 1976 or later to participate in the biennial (every two years) smog check program in participating counties. The program's stated aim is to reduce air pollution from vehicles by ensuring that cars with excessive emissions are repaired in accordance with federal and state guidelines. With some exceptions, gasoline-powered vehicles that are six years old or newer are not required to participate; instead, these vehicles pay a smog abatement fee for the first 6 years in place of being required to pass a smog check. The six-year exception does not apply to nonresident (previously registered out-of-state) vehicles being registered in California for the first time, diesel vehicles 1998 model or newer and weighing 14,000 lbs or less, or specially constructed vehicles 1976 and newer. The program is a joint effort between the California Air Resources Board, the California Bureau of Automotive Repair, and the California Department of Motor Vehicles.",when do cars need to be smogged in california
who are the teams in the acc conference,"['https://sportstechie.net/the-acc-digital-network-releases-final-top-10-must-see-moments-of-the-year-list/', 'https://lasvegasseo2.info/top-of-the-world-florida-state-seminoles-youth-garnet-offroad-trucker-snapback-hat.php', 'https://lasvegasseo1.info/nike-boise-state-broncos-royal-coaches-sideline-dri-fit-polo.html', 'https://izeby.info/nike-carolina-panthers-black-circuit-sideline-performance-pants.html', 'https://gracie04.info/west-virginia-mountaineers-29-x-43-double-sided-jersey-foil-house-flag.html', 'http://besttoppers.com/atlantic-coast-conference/', 'https://news.syr.edu/blog/2019/02/13/syracuse-university-sweet-sixteen-finalists-announced-for-the-campus-acc-inventure-prize-competition/']","The Atlantic Coast Conference (ACC) is a collegiate athletic conference in the United States of America in which its fifteen member universities compete in the National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA)'s Division I, with its football teams competing in the Football Bowl Subdivision (FBS), the highest levels for athletic competition in US-based collegiate sports. The ACC sponsors competition in twenty-five sports with many of its member institutions' athletic programs held in high regard nationally. Current members of the conference are Boston College, Clemson University, Duke University, Georgia Institute of Technology, Florida State University, North Carolina State University, Syracuse University, the University of Louisville, the University of Miami, the University of North Carolina, the University of Notre Dame, the University of Pittsburgh, the University of Virginia, Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University, and Wake Forest University.",who are the teams in the acc conference
displacement as a vector with defined direction and distance,['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Displacement_vector.html'],A displacement is a vector whose length is the shortest distance from the initial to the final position of a point P. It quantifies both the distance and direction of an imaginary motion along a straight line from the initial position to the final position of the point.,displacement as a vector with defined direction and distance
what nations were members of the allied powers,"['https://comoxairforcemuseum.ca/remembrance-week-the-allies-of-world-war-ii/', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/allies-of-world-war-ii', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=alliedenterprises.com&ads=1&title=Allied+enterprises&auto=Allied+enterprises&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Allied+enterprises&pagenum=4', 'http://www.okddayallies.co/history/', 'https://war.wikia.org/wiki/Pearl_Harbour', 'https://ourjourneypeterborough.org/?s=WWI', 'https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-united-states-and-the-holocaust-1942-45?parent=en%2F25566']","At the start of the war on 1 September 1939, the Allies consisted of France, Poland and the United Kingdom, and dependent states, such as British India. Within days they were joined by the independent Dominions of the British Commonwealth: Australia, Canada, New Zealand and South Africa. After the start of the German invasion of North Europe till the Balkan Campaign, the Netherlands, Belgium, Greece, and Yugoslavia joined the Allies. After first having cooperated with Germany in invading Poland whilst remaining neutral in the Allied-Axis conflict, the Soviet Union perforce joined the Allies in June 1941 after being invaded by Germany. The United States provided war materiel and money all along, and officially joined in December 1941 after the Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor. China had already been in a prolonged war with Japan since the Marco Polo Bridge Incident of 1937, but officially joined the Allies in 1941.",what nations were members of the allied powers
what type of money is used in china,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Ancient_Chinese_coinage.html', 'https://forum.duolingo.com/comment/25226291/%E4%BA%94%E5%85%83', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Chinese_yuan', 'https://www.weizmannforex.com/foreign-currency-exchange/cny', 'http://news.goldseek.com/GoldSeek/1412604119.php', 'http://www.countrycurrencyrates.com/en/convert/RON/CNY/1100', 'http://mlmconsultant.info/search?q=Exchange%20rmb%20in%20china']","The renminbi (Ab.: RMB; simplified Chinese: 人民币; traditional Chinese: 人民幣; pinyin: rénmínbì; literally: ""people's currency""; sign: 元; code: CNY) is the official currency of the People's Republic of China. The yuan (Chinese: 元; pinyin: yuán) is the basic unit of the renminbi, but is also used to refer to the Chinese currency generally, especially in international contexts where ""Chinese yuan"" is widely used to refer to the renminbi. The distinction between the terms renminbi and yuan is similar to that between sterling and pound, which respectively refer to the British currency and its primary unit. One yuan is subdivided into 10 jiao (Chinese: 角; pinyin: jiǎo), and a jiao in turn is subdivided into 10 fen (Chinese: 分; pinyin: fēn). The renminbi is issued by the People's Bank of China, the monetary authority of China.",what type of money is used in china
define and compare gross primary production and net primary production,"['https://www.lawa.org.nz/learn/glossary/p/primary-production/', 'https://www.reef2reef.com/ams/ultimate-filtration-algae-turf-scrubbers.88/', 'http://bossanova.club/cadena-trofica-95/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Last_Glacial_Period', 'https://www.learner.org/courses/envsci/glossary/definition.php?invariant=primary_producers', 'https://www.earthwiseaware.org/a-muddy-affair-mangroves/', 'http://botanystudies.com/bryophytes-test-questions-exams/']","In ecology, primary production is the synthesis of organic compounds from atmospheric or aqueous carbon dioxide. It principally occurs through the process of photosynthesis, which uses light as its source of energy, but it also occurs through chemosynthesis, which uses the oxidation or reduction of inorganic chemical compounds as its source of energy. Almost all life on Earth relies directly or indirectly on primary production. The organisms responsible for primary production are known as primary producers or autotrophs, and form the base of the food chain. In terrestrial ecoregions, these are mainly plants, while in aquatic ecoregions algae predominate in this role. Ecologists distinguish primary production as either net or gross, the former accounting for losses to processes such as cellular respiration, the latter not.",define and compare gross primary production and net primary production
when was swachh bharat started who initiated it,"['http://www.mangaloretoday.com/main/Mangaluru-Coast-Guard-Wives-Welfare-Association-CGWWA-celebrates-Tatrakshika-day.html', 'http://whiteworldexpeditions.com/leave-no-trace', 'https://www.brainyias.com/swachh-bharat-abhiyan-50th-current-affairs-class-ias-2019/', 'http://mahendrafoundationtrust.com/?page_id=283', 'https://auraiya.nic.in/event/swachh-bharat-abhiyan/', 'https://smartcity.eletsonline.com/karnatakas-kolar-district-is-first-to-achieve-100-odf-target/', 'https://ecofriend.com/8-extremely-powerful-and-inspiring-environment-movements-from-india.html']","The campaign was officially launched on 2 October 2014 at Rajghat, New Delhi by Prime Minister Narendra Modi. It is India's largest cleanliness drive to date with 3 million government employees, school students, and college students from all parts of India participating in 4,041 statutory cities, towns and associated rural areas. Modi has called the campaign ""Satyagrah se Swachhagrah"" in reference to Gandhi's ""Champaran Satyagraha"" launched on 10 April 1917.",when was swachh bharat started who initiated it
what does it mean to be ordinarily resident in the uk,['https://www.celsiummobility.com/medical-care'],"The official guidance issued to the NHS states: A person is ordinarily resident if they are normally residing in the UK (apart from temporary or occasional absences), and their residence here has been adopted voluntarily and for settled purposes as part of the regular order of their life for the time being, whether for short or long duration.",what does it mean to be ordinarily resident in the uk
what island lies south east of belfast between ireland and england,"['http://www.fact-index.com/i/ir/irish_sea.html', 'https://www.aferry.co.uk/dublin-holyhead-ferry.htm', 'https://www.aferry.co.uk/pembroke-rosslare-ferry.htm', 'https://berclas.co.uk/getting-here/', 'https://www.travelresponder.com/ireland-holiday-rentals/c473', 'http://www.holyhead.ports-guides.com/ferry_companies.html', 'https://www.aferry.co.uk/rosslare-pembroke-ferry.htm']","Ferry connections from Wales to Ireland across the Irish Sea include Fishguard Harbour and Pembroke to Rosslare, Holyhead to Dún Laoghaire and Holyhead to Dublin. From Scotland, Cairnryan connects with both Belfast and Larne. There is also a connection between Liverpool and Belfast via the Isle of Man or direct from Birkenhead. The world's largest car ferry, Ulysses, is operated by Irish Ferries on the Dublin Port -- Holyhead route; Stena Line also operates between Britain and Ireland.",what island lies south east of belfast between ireland and england
what is google drive and how it works,"['https://www.sekerenews.com/google-drive-sign-in-everything-you-need-to-know/', 'https://www.tech-recipes.com/rx/category/internet/google/page/2/', 'https://www.imobie.com/cloud-tips/icloud-vs-google-drive.htm', 'http://www.gmailinformation.com/google-drive-customer-service-number.html', 'https://www.cimasg.com/2019/01/cloud-storage-legal-firms/', 'https://westportlibrary.libguides.com/GoogleDriveResources', 'http://lpcity.tk/sheets-google.html']","Google Drive is a file storage and synchronization service developed by Google. Launched on April 24, 2012, Google Drive allows users to store files on their servers, synchronize files across devices, and share files. In addition to a website, Google Drive offers apps with offline capabilities for Windows and macOS computers, and Android and iOS smartphones and tablets. Google Drive encompasses Google Docs, Sheets and Slides, an office suite that permits collaborative editing of documents, spreadsheets, presentations, drawings, forms, and more. Files created and edited through the office suite are saved in Google Drive.",what is google drive and how it works
where did the black death first appear in europe,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Pandemic', 'https://www.carmanvalleyleader.com/news/local-news/incredible-creatures-the-dark-side-of-mans-relationship-with-insects', 'https://www.cuvsi.com/2017/03/identification-of-arthropod-parasites.html', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Tatar_invasions']","Plague was reportedly first introduced to Europe via Genoese traders at the port city of Kaffa in the Crimea in 1347. After a protracted siege, during which the Mongol army under Jani Beg was suffering from the disease, the army catapulted the infected corpses over the city walls of Kaffa to infect the inhabitants. The Genoese traders fled, taking the plague by ship into Sicily and the south of Europe, whence it spread north. Whether or not this hypothesis is accurate, it is clear that several existing conditions such as war, famine, and weather contributed to the severity of the Black Death.",where did the black death first appear in europe
what caused the end of the cuban missile crisis,"['https://www.preceden.com/timelines/169901-cold-war-events-timeline', 'https://returntothe50s.weebly.com/politics-in-the-1940s-50s-and-60s.html', 'http://216.234.169.69/l%E2%80%99azienda-di-logistica-intergroup-regala-ai-dipendenti-una-giornata-extra-di-ferie-nel-giorno-del-lo', 'http://macroom.ie/lee-valley-outlook-archive-2013/48-lee-valley-outlook-dec-19-2013-v10e26']","When all offensive missiles and Ilyushin Il-28 light bombers had been withdrawn from Cuba, the blockade was formally ended on November 21, 1962. The negotiations between the United States and the Soviet Union pointed out the necessity of a quick, clear, and direct communication line between Washington and Moscow. As a result, the Moscow -- Washington hotline was established. A series of agreements reduced U.S. -- Soviet tensions for several years until the United States and Russia began to build their nuclear arsenal even further.",what caused the end of the cuban missile crisis
where does the name canary wharf come from,"['https://www.silverdoorapartments.com/blog/interesting-canary-wharf/', 'http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Canary_Wharf', 'https://www.beritague.com/tag/business-articles', 'https://www.junkshopbusiness.com/canary-wharf-at-evening.html', 'https://privateinvestigator.co.uk/greater-london/canary-wharf/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/City_Hall,_London', 'https://www.wrightapartments.co.uk/canary-wharf-apartment/']","Canary Wharf itself takes its name from No. 32 berth of the West Wood Quay of the Import Dock. This was built in 1936 for Fruit Lines Ltd, a subsidiary of Fred Olsen Lines for the Mediterranean and Canary Islands fruit trade. The Canary islands were so named after the large dogs found there by the Spanish (Gran Canaria from Canine) and as it is located on the Isle of Dogs, the quay and warehouse were given the name Canary Wharf.",where does the name canary wharf come from
what does do you own real estate mean,"['http://www.du-salariat-au-business.com/real-estate/', 'http://cyres.us/real-estate/robie-real-estate-salmon-idaho/', 'http://www.cyres.us/real-estate/best-crm-for-real-estate-investor/', 'https://personalinjurylawyers.pw/real-estate/how-to-get-a-commercial-real-estate-license-in-florida/', 'http://www.cyres.us/real-estate/zillow-commercial-real-estate-listings/', 'https://www.cyres.us/real-estate/hawaii-real-estate-license-exam/', 'https://www.ballabongroup.com/real-estate/weekend-real-estate-classes-near-me/']","Real estate is ""property consisting of land and the buildings on it, along with its natural resources such as crops, minerals or water; immovable property of this nature; an interest vested in this (also) an item of real property, (more generally) buildings or housing in general. Also: the business of real estate; the profession of buying, selling, or renting land, buildings, or housing."" It is a legal term used in jurisdictions whose legal system is derived from English common law, such as India, the United Kingdom, United States, Canada, Pakistan, Australia, and New Zealand.",what does do you own real estate mean
when did parties formally appear on the political scene,"['https://wn.com/Reformed_Political_Party', 'https://www.wikiplanet.click/enciclopedia/en/Political_party', 'https://en.wikipedi0.org/wiki/Two-party_system', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1747_British_general_election', 'https://kimwingerei.com/the-party-is-dead-long-live-democracy/']","The first political factions, cohering around a basic, if fluid, set of principles, emerged from the Exclusion Crisis and Glorious Revolution in late 17th century England. The Whigs supported Protestant constitutional monarchy against absolute rule; the Tories, originating in the Royalist (or ""Cavalier"") faction of the English Civil War, were conservative royalist supporters of a strong monarchy as a counterbalance to the republican tendencies of Whigs, who were the dominant political faction for most of the first half of the 18th century; the Whigs supported the Hanoverian succession of 1715 against the Jacobite supporters of the deposed Roman Catholic Stuart dynasty, and were able to purge Tory politicians from important government positions after the failed Jacobite rising of 1715. The leader of the Whigs was Robert Walpole, who maintained control of the government in the period 1721 -- 1742; his protégé was Henry Pelham (1743 -- 1754).",when did parties formally appear on the political scene
how does paul end his second letter to the thessalonians,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Second_Epistle_to_the_Thessalonians.html', 'https://www.calvaryhillsboro.org/watch-listen/messages/2016-07-13-2-thessalonians-1-1-3-18', 'https://centralchristianblog.com/tag/timothy/', 'https://earlychurchhistory.org/communication/letters-of-paul-the-apostle/', 'https://biblehub.com/nasb/2_thessalonians/3.htm', 'https://biblehub.com/p/nas/esv/2_thessalonians/3.shtml', 'https://stjmbc.com/expositions-from-the-book-of-second-thessalonians/']","Paul ends this letter by saying, ""I, Paul, write this greeting with my own hand, and this is a distinguishing mark in every letter; this is the way I write. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all"" (2 Thess 3: 17 -- 18). Macarthur writes, ""Paul added an identifying signature (cf. 1 Cor. 16: 21; Col. 4: 18) so his readers could be sure he was truly the author.""",how does paul end his second letter to the thessalonians
what is the origin of punch and judy,"['http://unclebrian.co.uk/index.php?act=84&tag=Punch_and_Judy', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Puppetry', 'https://allaboutheaven.org/symbols/punch-and-judy/123', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2015/05/09/', 'https://adinparadise.wordpress.com/2012/07/', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Comedy', 'http://idaretosoar.com/notebook-actors-dating.php']","The Punch and Judy show has roots in the 16th-century Italian commedia dell'arte. The figure of Punch is derived from the Neapolitan stock character of Pulcinella, which was anglicized to Punchinello. He is a manifestation of the Lord of Misrule and Trickster figures of deep-rooted mythologies. Punch's wife was originally called ""Joan.""",what is the origin of punch and judy
what is the definition of the british commonwealth,"['https://syskool.com/commonwealth-of-nations/', 'http://www.pmdnews.lk/chogm-2015/', 'https://m.jagranjosh.com/general-knowledge-international-organizations-and-headquarters-1320657317-1?ref=amp_list_rel_cat', 'https://antigua-barbuda.com/governor-generals-commonwealth-day-speech', 'https://thelonsdalebattalion.co.uk/wiki/Commonwealth', 'https://smarthistory.org/presentation-of-fijian-mats-and-tapa-cloths-to-queen-elizabeth-ii/', 'http://www.a1flags.com.au/flag/world/miscellaneous/commonwealth-of-nations']","The Commonwealth of Nations, formerly (1931 -- 1949) the British Commonwealth, also known as simply the Commonwealth, is an intergovernmental organisation of 53 member states that are mostly former territories of the British Empire. The Commonwealth operates by intergovernmental consensus of the member states, organised through the Commonwealth Secretariat and non-governmental organisations, organised through the Commonwealth Foundation.",what is the definition of the british commonwealth
where do the terms left and right come from,"['https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-worldhistory/chapter/constitutional-monarchy/', 'http://factmyth.com/the-origin-of-the-political-terms-left-and-right/', 'https://thinkwingradio.com/2017/02/20/thinkwing-mon2202017-9pm-kpfthouston-90-1fm-topics-not-my-presidents-day-what-happens-in-sweden-a-govt-by-generals-billionaires-what-sayeth-the-1st/', 'https://uk.blastingnews.com/politics/2017/07/a-brief-history-of-ideology-the-origins-of-the-terms-left-and-right-wing-001853287.html', 'http://floors4u.eu/20938-right-of-revolution.html', 'http://www.caleidoscope.in/caleidoscope-blog/is-there-ideology-in-indian-politics', 'http://factmyth.com/tag/american-politics/']","The terms ""left"" and ""right"" appeared during the French Revolution of 1789 when members of the National Assembly divided into supporters of the king to the president's right and supporters of the revolution to his left. One deputy, the Baron de Gauville, explained: ""We began to recognize each other: those who were loyal to religion and the king took up positions to the right of the chair so as to avoid the shouts, oaths, and indecencies that enjoyed free rein in the opposing camp"". However, the Right opposed the seating arrangement because they believed that deputies should support private or general interests but should not form factions or political parties. The contemporary press occasionally used the terms ""left"" and ""right"" to refer to the opposing sides.",where do the terms left and right come from
what is the trace of a square matrix,"['http://freejabber.com/linear-algebra-determinant/', 'http://freejabber.com/linear-algebra-eigenvalues/', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=diagonal+matrix+example&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir']","In linear algebra, the trace of an n-by-n square matrix A is defined to be the sum of the elements on the main diagonal (the diagonal from the upper left to the lower right) of A, i.e.,",what is the trace of a square matrix
what is the difference between texas holdem and poker,"['https://www.thestinggaming.com.au/texas-holdem/', 'http://www.casinopartylouisville.com/poker-texas-holdem/', 'https://www.hardrockcasinotulsa.com/casino/poker', 'http://ourgreenlife.info/news.php?action=show&id=44385', 'http://freeonline-games.net/poker/55735-texas-holdem-poker-information.html', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=texasholdemno.com&ads=1&title=Texasholdem+no&auto=Texasholdem+no&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Texasholdem+no&pagenum=2', 'http://www.luckia.hr/en/texas-holdem-poker.aspx']","Texas hold' em (also known as Texas holdem, hold' em, and holdem) is a variation of the card game of poker. Two cards, known as the hole cards, are dealt face down to each player, and then five community cards are dealt face up in three stages. The stages consist of a series of three cards (""the flop""), later an additional single card (""the turn"" or ""fourth street""), and a final card (""the river"" or ""fifth street""). Each player seeks the best five card poker hand from any combination of the seven cards of the five community cards and their own two hole cards. If a player's best five-card poker hand consists only of the five community cards and none of the player's hole cards, it is called ""playing the board"". If you play the board on the river, then you can do no better than tie the other player(s) in the game if no player can make a better hand than the board represents, using either or both hole cards. Players have betting options to check, call, raise, or fold. Rounds of betting take place before the flop is dealt and after each subsequent deal.",what is the difference between texas holdem and poker
what building was used for the nakatomi plaza in the movie die hard,"['https://www.mighway.com/us/en/region/california/southern-california/los-angeles/century-city/', 'https://www.shortlist.com/entertainment/films/20-things-you-probably-didnt-know-about-die-hard/89955']",The building has been featured in at least four major motion pictures released by Fox. Its most famous appearance was in the 1988 action film Die Hard as the fictional Nakatomi Plaza in which its damage was accomplished using a scale model. The plaza and a neighboring building are the main setting for the rock & roll comedy Airheads. Fox Plaza was also one of the buildings brought down at the end of Fight Club.,what building was used for the nakatomi plaza in the movie die hard
difference between attorney general and solicitor general us,"['https://www.news.civilserviceindia.com/tushar-mehta-appointed-as-the-new-solicitor-general-of-india/', 'https://9sblog.com/attorney/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=newsreport.com&ads=1&title=News+report&auto=News+report&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=News+report&pagenum=2', 'https://www.indiabix.com/current-affairs/2018-10-11/', 'https://www.bankersadda.com/2018/10/current-affairs-11th-october-2018-daily.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Attorney-General_for_Australia', 'https://www.robertbuckland.co.uk/news/roberts-weekly-swindon-advertiser-article-4-january-2017']","A Solicitor General or Solicitor-General, in common law countries, is usually a legal officer who is the chief representative of a regional or national government in courtroom proceedings. In systems that have an Attorney General (or equivalent position), the Solicitor General is often the second-ranked law officer of the state and a deputy of the Attorney General. The extent to which a Solicitor General actually provides legal advice to or represents the government in court varies from jurisdiction to jurisdiction, and sometimes between individual office holders in the same jurisdiction.",difference between attorney general and solicitor general us
is the fargo tv show the same as the movie,"['https://www.jpc.de/jpcng/poprock/detail/-/art/filmmusik-soundtracks-fargo-season-3/hnum/7781590', 'https://findvideo.biz/show/Fargo', 'https://www.musiconvinyl.com/news/new-releases-week-41', 'https://www.cordcuttingreviews.com/stream-fargo-online/', 'https://watchmoviecom.com/crime/fargo.php', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Martin_Freeman', 'http://julesland.net46.net/fargo-2seasson-torrent/']","Fargo is an American black comedy -- crime drama anthology television series created and primarily written by Noah Hawley. The show is inspired by the eponymous 1996 film written and directed by the Coen brothers, who serve as executive producers on the series alongside Hawley. The series premiered on April 15, 2014, on FX, and follows an anthology format, with each season set in a different era, and with a different story and mostly new characters and cast, although there is minor overlap. Each season shares a common chronology with the original film.",is the fargo tv show the same as the movie
who was the leader who struggled for india's independence,"['https://es.scribd.com/document/392220515/Aikido-Kids-Guide-0', 'http://indianindependenceday.com/2019/07/best-happy-independence-day.html', 'https://independenceday.co.in/2018/05/26/225/', 'http://maryannadelosh.netii.net/kartu-surf-sahara/', 'https://www.scribd.com/document/161879689/ACMA-Activity-Report-2011-12', 'https://engineering.jhu.edu/faculty/dredze-mark/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Self_Employed_Women%27s_Association']","The first organised militant movements were in Bengal, but they later took root in the newly formed Indian National Congress with prominent moderate leaders seeking only their basic right to appear for Indian Civil Service (British India) examinations, as well as more rights, economic in nature, for the people of the soil. The early part of the 20th century saw a more radical approach towards political self-rule proposed by leaders such as the Lal, Bal, Pal and Aurobindo Ghosh, V.O. Chidambaram Pillai. The last stages of the self-rule struggle from the 1920s onwards saw Congress adopt Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi's policy of nonviolence and civil disobedience, and several other campaigns. Nationalists like Subhash Chandra Bose, Bhagat Singh, Bagha Jatin preached armed revolution to achieve self-rule. Poets and writers such as Subramania Bharati, Rabindranath Tagore, Muhammad Iqbal, Josh Malihabadi, Mohammad Ali Jouhar, Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay and Kazi Nazrul Islam used literature, poetry and speech as a tool for political awareness. Feminists such as Sarojini Naidu and Begum Rokeya promoted the emancipation of Indian women and their participation in national politics. B.R. Ambedkar championed the cause of the disadvantaged sections of Indian society within the larger self-rule movement. The period of the Second World War saw the peak of the campaigns by the Quit India Movement led by Congress, and the Indian National Army movement led by Subhas Chandra Bose.",who was the leader who struggled for india's independence
how many times did the first russian orbit the earth,"['https://b2b.partcommunity.com/community/knowledge/en/detail/8829/Yuri+Gagarin', 'https://connectwww.com/50th-anniversary-of-first-human-spaceflight-google-doodle/901/', 'http://onenewsbox.com/category/history/', 'http://www.toprankseoblog.com/2011/04/', 'https://www.astrotheme.com/birthdays/march-9.htm', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Soviet_Information_Bureau', 'https://celebritydead.com/2019/03/27/yuri-gagarin/']","Yuri Alekseyevich Gagarin (Russian: Ю́рий Алексе́евич Гага́рин, IPA: (ˈjʉrjɪj ɐljɪˈksjejɪvjɪtɕ ɡɐˈɡarjɪn); 9 March 1934 -- 27 March 1968) was a Soviet pilot and cosmonaut. He was the first human to journey into outer space when his Vostok spacecraft completed an orbit of the Earth on 12 April 1961.",how many times did the first russian orbit the earth
what is special about the song ae mere watan ke logo,"['http://it15.net/2017/03/28/india-%E4%B8%AD%E5%9B%BD%E5%91%98%E5%B7%A5%E6%AF%81%E5%8D%B0%E5%BA%A6%E5%9B%BD%E6%97%97%E6%89%94%E5%9E%83%E5%9C%BE%E6%A1%B6-oppo%E5%88%86%E5%85%AC%E5%8F%B8%E9%81%AD%E5%8C%85%E5%9B%B4/', 'http://www.singersagarika.com/2019/04/07/immortal-patriotic-song-aye-mere-watan-logon/', 'http://missliterati.com/aye-mere-watan-ke-logo.html', 'http://www.expressions-kt.in/2014/08/freedom-melodified-independence-day.html', 'http://participal.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=21180', 'http://mastermotion.info/?newsid=30967', 'http://policeexpert.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=35897']","""Aye Mere Watan Ke Logo"" (Hindi: ऐ मेरे वतन के लोगों; ""O' people of my country"") is a Hindi patriotic song written by Kavi Pradeep, composed by C. Ramchandra, and performed by ()). The song commemorates Indian soldiers who died during the Sino-Indian War in 1962. The song was first performed live by Mangeshkar on 27 January 1963 at the National Stadium in New Delhi in the presence of President Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan and Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru, on account of Republic Day (26 January) 1963, which was just two months after the end of the war.",what is special about the song ae mere watan ke logo
where is the kuiper belt and what is found in it,"['https://missionbackupearth.com/tv-series/locations/kuiper-belt/', 'https://www.slideshare.net/saibharath3701/solar-system-by-saibharath', 'http://thierfelderwilliams.com/peppercornearthplanets/kuiperbelt.html', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Neptune', 'https://culturesways.com/universe/galaxy-and-planet/pluto-kuiper-belt-solar-system/', 'http://psi.edu/about/targets_keywords/71', 'https://www.crystalinks.com/kuiperbelt.html']","The Kuiper belt (/ ˈkaɪpər /), occasionally called the Edgeworth -- Kuiper belt, is a circumstellar disc in the outer Solar System, extending from the orbit of Neptune (at 30 AU) to approximately 50 AU from the Sun. It is similar to the asteroid belt, but is far larger -- 20 times as wide and 20 to 200 times as massive. Like the asteroid belt, it consists mainly of small bodies or remnants from when the Solar System formed. While many asteroids are composed primarily of rock and metal, most Kuiper belt objects are composed largely of frozen volatiles (termed ""ices""), such as methane, ammonia and water. The Kuiper belt is home to three officially recognized dwarf planets: Pluto, Haumea and Makemake. Some of the Solar System's moons, such as Neptune's Triton and Saturn's Phoebe, may have originated in the region.",where is the kuiper belt and what is found in it
where does the phrase going postal come from,"['http://zetatalk.com/newsletr/issue523.htm', 'https://upge.wn.com/?from=santaclaritapost.com&ads=1&title=Santa+clarita+post&auto=Santa+clarita+post&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Santa+clarita+post&pagenum=5', 'http://www.arhataosho.com/index.php/2009/02/18/going-postal/', 'https://jpfmovies.com/2010/04/30/kevin-costner-the-postman-refuse-and-return-to-sender/', 'https://performancemanagementcompanyblog.com/category/engagement-2/un-engagement/', 'https://www.universalclass.com/articles/business/workplace-violence-and-the-role-of-culture.htm']","The expression derives from a series of incidents from 1986 onward in which United States Postal Service (USPS) workers shot and killed managers, fellow workers, and members of the police or general public in acts of mass murder. Between 1970 and 1997, more than 40 people were killed by current or former employees in at least 20 incidents of workplace rage.",where does the phrase going postal come from
what is the meaning of the name kevin,"['https://www.behindthename.com/names/tag/the_office_us_characters', 'https://harrypotter.fandom.com/wiki/Kevin_Whitby', 'https://www.corupriesthood.com/the-morrigan/']","Kevin (/ ˈkɛvɪn /) is the anglicized form of the Irish masculine given name Caoimhín ((kiːvjiːnj), Middle Irish: Caoimhghín (kəiṽjʝiːnj), Old Irish: Cóemgein (koiṽjɣjinj), latinized Coemgenus), composed of Irish caomh (Old Irish cóem) ""dear; noble"" and-gin (Old Irish gein) ""birth"".",what is the meaning of the name kevin
what do you mean by wireless communication technologies,"['https://engineering.eckovation.com/wireless-communication-project-topics/', 'http://alqawasmi.org/?page_id=17', 'https://africasportnews.com/the-information-age-the-computer-age/', 'https://mdtcreative.com/2016/11/13/the-freedom-of-wireless-technology-2/', 'https://www.algororeports.com/blogs/wireless-audio-devices-market-trend', 'http://computech.co.id/index.php?route=product/category&path=20', 'https://thenextweb.com/vocabulary/wireless/']","Wireless communication, or sometimes simply wireless, is the transfer of information or power between two or more points that are not connected by an electrical conductor. The most common wireless technologies use radio waves. With radio waves distances can be short, such as a few meters for Bluetooth or as far as millions of kilometers for deep-space radio communications. It encompasses various types of fixed, mobile, and portable applications, including two-way radios, cellular telephones, personal digital assistants (PDAs), and wireless networking. Other examples of applications of radio wireless technology include GPS units, garage door openers, wireless computer mice, keyboards and headsets, headphones, radio receivers, satellite television, broadcast television and cordless telephones. Somewhat less common methods of achieving wireless communications include the use of other electromagnetic wireless technologies, such as light, magnetic, or electric fields or the use of sound.",what do you mean by wireless communication technologies
what is the approximate diameter of earth's core,"['https://www.reference.com/web?q=facts+about+the+earth%26%2339%3Bs+inner+core&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://reality348.wordpress.com/2016/03/26/17-why-is-the-stratosphere-warm/', 'https://2risk.wordpress.com/', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=What+Is+the+Temperature+of+the+Earth%27s+Inner+Core%3F&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'http://www.happyvideonetwork.com/doc-down-to-the-earths-core-hd-national-geographic/', 'https://cleantechnica.com/2014/06/18/spain-portugal-feed-just-geothermal-energy/', 'http://www.physics-astronomy.com/2014/05/most-amazing-exoplanets.html']","The Earth's inner core is the Earth's innermost part. It is primarily a solid ball with a radius of about 1,220 kilometres (760 miles), which is about 70% of the Moon's radius. It is composed of an iron -- nickel alloy and some other elements. The temperature at the inner core's surface is approximately 5,700 K (5,430 ° C), which is about the temperature at the surface of the Sun.",what is the approximate diameter of earth's core
can i use a hydraulic pump as a motor,"['https://conceptdraw.com/a1117c3/preview--Design%20elements%20-%20Hydraulic%20pumps%20and%20motors', 'http://controlledmotion.com/hydraulics/pumpsmotorsdrives.html', 'https://lacortedimaregnano.it/hydraulic_eccentric_motors/Wed_30077.html', 'http://www.damecomm.com/hydraulic-motors-pumps.html', 'http://in10.com.br/hydraulic-wiring-schematics.html', 'http://www.whitehouseproductsltd.com/motors.aspx', 'http://kgmmvd.org.in/8622_hydraulic-driven-track-mobile-crusher-india.html']","Conceptually, a hydraulic motor should be interchangeable with a hydraulic pump because it performs the opposite function-similar to the way a DC electric motor is theoretically interchangeable with a DC electrical generator. However, most hydraulic pumps cannot be used as hydraulic motors because they cannot be backdriven. Also, a hydraulic motor is usually designed for working pressure at both sides of the motor.",can i use a hydraulic pump as a motor
what is the meaning of directive principles of state policy,"['http://www.gkplanet.in/2016/01/directive-principles-of-state-policy.html', 'https://www.himalaiiasclasses.com/blog/upsc-ncert-indian-polity-citizenship-directive-principles-of-the-state-policy-and-fundamental-duties-notes-part-1/', 'https://www.grim-funeral.com/the-principles-of-the-constitution/', 'http://employmentnews.gov.in/NewEmp/MoreContentNew.aspx?n=Editorial&k=89', 'https://www.sscexamtutor.com/2015/09/gk-quiz-for-ssc-chsl-fci-exam-with.html', 'https://www.civilserviceindia.com/subject/Law/notes/fundamental-right-principles.html', 'http://www.appscgroup1.com/2010/09/directive-principles-of-state-policy-1.html']","The Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are the guidelines or principles given to the federal institutes governing the state of India, to be kept in citation while framing laws and policies. These provisions, contained in Part IV (Article 36-51) of the Constitution of India, are not enforceable by any court, but the principles laid down therein are considered irrefutable in the governance of the country, making it the duty of the State to apply these principles in making laws to establish a just society in the country. The principles have been inspired by the Directive Principles given in the Constitution of Ireland relate to social justice, economic welfare, foreign policy, and legal and administrative matters.",what is the meaning of directive principles of state policy
when do you become a private in the army,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Private_(rank)', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/File:E8b_USAF_1STSGT2.svg', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Specialist_(rank).html', 'http://airborneangler.com/2012/06/11/shakespeare-shall-sustain-thee/']","In the U.S. Army, private is used for the two lowest enlisted ranks, just below private first class. The lowest rank is ""private E-1"" (PV1) and sometimes referred to as recruit, but also held by some soldiers after punishment through the Uniform Code of Military Justice or prisoners after conviction until they are discharged. A PV1 wears no uniform insignia; since the advent of the Army Combat Uniform, the term ""fuzzy"" has come into vogue, referring to the blank velcro patch on the ACU where the rank would normally be placed. The second rank, private E-2 (PV2), wears a single chevron, known colloquially as ""mosquito wings"". Advancement to the PV2 is automatic after six months' time in service, but may get shortened to four months if given a waiver. A person who earned the Eagle Scout award, the Gold Award, or completed at least two years of JROTC may enlist at any time at the rank of PV2. The term of address, ""Private"", may be properly applied to any Army soldier E-1 (PV1) to E-3 (PFC). It should also be noted that while a soldier is currently in Initial Enlistment Training, he or she will often be referred to as ""Private"" by the training cadre, regardless of actual rank, even if the soldier enlisted as a Specialist / E-4.",when do you become a private in the army
who built the canadian museum for human rights,"['http://asperfoundation.com/hrhs-program/', 'https://www.greensociety.ca/buy-weed-online-manitoba/', 'https://www.realestateforums.com/winnipegref/en/programs/program-archive/2012-program.html']","Established in 2008 through the enactment of Bill C-42, an amendment of the Canadian Museums Act, the Canadian Museum for Human Rights is the first new national museum created in Canada since 1967, and it is the first new national museum ever to be located outside the National Capital Region.",who built the canadian museum for human rights
what do the lyrics to zombie by the cranberries mean,"['https://worldrockcountdown.com/page/3', 'https://tuneoftheday.blogspot.com/2018/03/', 'https://guitaranimal.com/learn/zombie/the-cranberries/', 'https://www.jinglejanglejungle.net/2014/10/rocktober-11-2014-cranberries.html', 'https://www.podcastfakenews.com/i-cant-believe-its-not-news-episode-guide-blog/episode-22', 'http://florenciaadolphsen.host22.com/?article=cranberries_analyse', 'http://www.patrickcomerford.com/2019_01_15_archive.html']","""Zombie"" is a protest song by Irish rock band The Cranberries, written about the 1993 IRA bombing in Warrington, and in memory of two young victims, Johnathan Ball and Tim Parry. It was released in September 1994 as the lead single from their second studio album, No Need to Argue (1994). It preceded the release of No Need to Argue by two weeks. The song was written by the band's lead singer Dolores O'Riordan, and reached No. 1 on the charts in Australia, Belgium, France, Denmark and Germany.",what do the lyrics to zombie by the cranberries mean
when did the united states win its independence,"['https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2013/07/04/', 'https://redrite.co.uk/independence-day/', 'https://www.learning-english-online.net/more/cultural-studies/holidays/usa/independence-day/', 'http://duanehatch.com/pray-for-usa/', 'https://liviaspacedotcom.wordpress.com/freedom-teachings-2/factually-speaking-a-july-4th-usa-independence-day-gift-of-clarity-from-the-amcc-mceo-ga/', 'https://greetingsu.me/american-independence-day-wishes-messages-ecards-greetings-quotes-sayings-for-whatsapp-facebook-twitter/', 'http://www.fundoogeek.com/2011/07/happy-independence-day-usa.html']","During the American Revolution, the legal separation of the Thirteen Colonies from Great Britain in 1776 actually occurred on July 2, when the Second Continental Congress voted to approve a resolution of independence that had been proposed in June by Richard Henry Lee of Virginia declaring the United States independent from Great Britain rule. After voting for independence, Congress turned its attention to the Declaration of Independence, a statement explaining this decision, which had been prepared by a Committee of Five, with Thomas Jefferson as its principal author. Congress debated and revised the wording of the Declaration, finally approving it two days later on July 4. A day earlier, John Adams had written to his wife Abigail:",when did the united states win its independence
who launched the khilafat movement why was the movement launched,"['https://moralupbringing.com/tag/ottoman-empire/', 'https://www.theguesspapers.com/pakistan-studies-solved-past-paper-2nd-year-2014-karachi-board-15811', 'https://www.iastoppers.com/day16-static-flash-cards-modern-indian-history-70-days-war-plan/', 'http://www.cssforum.com.pk/386748-post13.html', 'https://www.theguesspapers.com/pak-study-solved-past-paper-2nd-year-2012-karachi-board-private-16625', 'http://wwwnfiecomblogspotcom.blogspot.com/2013/04/maulana-muhammad-abdul-hamid-qadri.html', 'https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/tamil/vishwaroopam-2-movie-release-kamal-haasan-live-updates-5300046/']","The Khilafat movement (1919 -- 22) was a pan-Islamic, political protest campaign launched by Muslims of India to influence the British government not to abolish the Ottoman Caliphate.",who launched the khilafat movement why was the movement launched
first indian man to step on the moon,"['https://www.lookchup.com/57e443d9e669b8f1d41327cc50dcbcac', 'https://itsmajja.com/shah-rukh-khan-likely-to-share-screen-space-with-vijay/', 'https://scroll.in/reel/899882/shah-rukh-khan-roped-in-for-rakesh-sharma-biopic-report', 'https://showmastersonline.com/forums/index.php?/profile/106643-runningambassador/', 'http://punjabdata.com/Punjab-General-Knowledge-3.aspx', 'https://www.financialexpress.com/lifestyle/science/man-mission-to-space-to-have-3-crew-members-will-be-in-space-for-5-7-days-isro-chief/1295493/', 'http://brahmand.com/news/Man-mission-to-space-to-have-3-crew-members-will-be-in-space-for-57-days-ISRO-chief/16530/1/17.html']","Rakesh Sharma, AC, Hero of the Soviet Union (born 13 January 1949), is a former Indian Air Force pilot who flew aboard Soyuz T-11, launched on 2 April 1984, as part of the Intercosmos programme. Sharma is the only Indian citizen to travel in space.",first indian man to step on the moon
due process clause of the fourteenth amendment summary,"['https://deceptionamuk.com/category/albert-pike/', 'https://politicsdissected.wonderhowto.com/news/no-transparency-no-trust-0133936/', 'https://www.independentsentinel.com/an-increasingly-radicalized-mark-levin-were-not-living-in-a-constitutional-republic/', 'https://smleo.com/2014/05/06/the-greatest-contraction-of-american-democracy/', 'http://www.debito.org/?p=9619', 'https://taxandbusinessonline.villanova.edu/blog/constitutional-issues-in-state-and-local-taxes/', 'https://www.landusedevelopments.com/2019/01/court-rejects-citizens-groups-challenge-venice-development-permitting-process/']","The Due Process Clause prohibits state and local government officials from depriving persons of life, liberty, or property without legislative authorization. This clause has also been used by the federal judiciary to make most of the Bill of Rights applicable to the states, as well as to recognize substantive and procedural requirements that state laws must satisfy.",due process clause of the fourteenth amendment summary
what is the moral of the blind man and the elephant,"['https://dannyozment.com/cant-see-the-forest-for-the-trees-the-dangers-of-proximity-blindness-2/', 'http://deolaonline.com/the-big-elephant-in-the-political-circus/', 'http://digital-leadership-associates.passle.net/post/102fepd/content-marketing-how-to-explain-it-to-your-business-colleagues', 'http://party-net.info/?page_id=46151', 'https://shepherdhoodwin.com/perspective/soul-age-what-it-is-and-isnt/', 'https://www.ecepaa.eu/our-projects/ongoing-projects/ihavet/', 'http://www.wirelessone.news/mimo-2/1064-at-t-cfo-skeptical-on-fixed-millimeter-wave']","The parable of the blind men and an elephant originated in ancient Indian subcontinent, from where it has widely diffused. It is a story of a group of blind men, who have never come across an elephant before, learn and conceptualize what the elephant is like by touching it. Each blind man feels a different part of the elephant body, but only one part, such as the side or the tusk. They then describe the elephant based on their partial experience and their descriptions are in complete disagreement on what an elephant is. In some versions they come to suspect that the other person is dishonest and they come to blows. The moral of the parable is that humans have a tendency to project their partial experiences as the whole truth, ignore other people's partial experiences, and one should consider that one may be partially right and may have partial information.",what is the moral of the blind man and the elephant
who sing how long will i love you,"['https://www.happysheetmusic.com/product/how-long-will-i-love-you-sheet-music', 'https://fifthharmony.fandom.com/wiki/Anything_Could_Happen', 'http://eaglemtngolfacademy.com/comics/index3.php', 'https://adrienneelishamusic.com/song-no-need-download', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Calvin_Harris', 'http://pianoriffs.blogspot.com/2012/12/blog-post_3702.html', 'http://hmfly.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=7068']","""How Long Will I Love You?"" is a song by folk-rock band The Waterboys from their fifth studio album, Room to Roam (1990). Written by Mike Scott, it was released as the album's lead single. The song was subsequently covered by English singer Ellie Goulding and released as the second single from her album Halcyon Days (2013). Goulding's version is included on the soundtrack to the 2013 film About Time, which also features a different cover by Jon Boden, Sam Sweeney and Ben Coleman.",who sing how long will i love you
how much of the earth is covered by marine biomes and how many types are there,"['http://www.qatarmarine.net/diving-environment/marine-ecology/', 'https://phys.org/tags/marine+ecosystems/', 'https://www.cevents.info/natural-resources-and-energy-team-paperangheny-erfbheprf-naq-raretl-grnz-cncre.asp', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Seamount', 'https://www.humansandnature.org/washed-up-on-the-shores-of-lake-michigan', 'https://shannonvaut.com/2017/06/page/5/', 'http://foto-koshkin.ml/jadec/planets-homework-help-bazo.php']","Marine ecosystems are among the largest of Earth's aquatic ecosystems. Examples include salt marshes, intertidal zones, estuaries, lagoons, mangroves, coral reefs, the deep sea, and the sea floor. They can be contrasted with freshwater ecosystems, which have a lower salt content. Marine waters cover two-thirds of the surface of the Earth. Such places are considered ecosystems because the plant life supports the animal life and vice versa. See food chains.",how much of the earth is covered by marine biomes and how many types are there
what is the cause of the battle of bunker hill,"['https://www.flytees.biz/products/bunker-hill-t-shirt', 'http://myriverside.sd43.bc.ca/mariod2015/category/grade-9/socials-9/', 'http://cheersboston.blogspot.com/2009/06/']","On June 13, 1775, the leaders of the colonial forces besieging Boston learned that the British were planning to send troops out from the city to fortify the unoccupied hills surrounding the city, which would give them control of Boston Harbor. In response, 1,200 colonial troops under the command of William Prescott stealthily occupied Bunker Hill and Breed's Hill. During the night, the colonists constructed a strong redoubt on Breed's Hill, as well as smaller fortified lines across the Charlestown Peninsula.",what is the cause of the battle of bunker hill
what is the objective of consumer protection act 1986,"['http://europe-ecologie-aube.ning.com/profiles/blogs/aims-and-objectives-of-consumer-protection-act-1986-pdf-free', 'http://bashaoor.com/need-of-consumer-protection-act/', 'https://www.consumer-voice.org/consumer-protection-act-1986/', 'http://www.beingskilled.com/questions/what-consumer-protection-act-1986', 'https://www.management4all.org/2014/02/govt-control-on-business.html', 'http://www.lawleader.in/IndianLawView/10008/Consumer-Protection-Act-1986', 'https://www.shipmethis.com/2014/07/consumercourt.html']","Consumer Protection Act, 1986 is an Act of the Parliament of India enacted in 1986 to protect the interests of consumers in India. It makes provision for the establishment of consumer councils and other authorities for the settlement of consumers' disputes and for matters connected therewith also.",what is the objective of consumer protection act 1986
where did the brand name adidas come from,"['https://eoamodeling.com.ng/2019/04/14/dark-history-of-adidas/', 'https://www.theanswerbank.co.uk/Sport/article/adidas/', 'https://www.thenewsgeeks.com/top-brands-strategy/', 'https://www.blackfriday.co.uk/adidas-black-friday', 'https://kraftonline.ru/www-adidas-comfeedback-adidas-customer-satisfaction-survey']","The brothers split up in 1947, with Rudi forming a new firm that he called Ruda -- from Rudolf Dassler, later rebranded Puma, and Adi forming a company formally registered as Adidas AG from Adi Dassler on 18 August 1949. Although it is a popular urban myth that the name is an acronym for All Day I Dream About Sports, that phrase is a ""backronym""; in reality the name is actually a portmanteau formed from ""Adi"" (a nickname for Adolf) and ""Das"" (from ""Dassler"").",where did the brand name adidas come from
what kind of political system does pakistan have,"['http://theimaginarycompany.com/essay-on-terrorism-in-pakistan-in-urdu', 'https://panuk.org/pakistan-adoption/about-pakistan', 'http://www.nyulawglobal.org/globalex/Costa_Rica.html', 'http://www.turpalencia.com/the-government-of-spain-today/', 'https://www.llrx.com/2002/04/features-researching-tajik-law-a-guide-to-the-tajik-legal-system/', 'https://freedomhouse.org/report/countries-crossroads/2005/syria', 'http://www.danielpipes.org/221/partisan-politics-will-break-the-washington-gridlock']","The politics of Pakistan takes place within the framework established by the constitution. The country is a federal parliamentary republic in which provincial governments enjoy a high degree of autonomy and residuary powers. Executive power is vested with the national cabinet which is headed by the prime minister, who works coherently along with the bicameral parliament and the judicature. Stipulations set by the constitution provide a delicate check and balance of sharing powers between executive, legislative, and judicial branches of the government.",what kind of political system does pakistan have
why is there a statue of liberty in odaiba,"['https://www.360cities.net/image/statue-de-la-libert-colmar-alsace-france-7121', 'https://ourladyliberty.wordpress.com/tag/statue-of-liberty/', 'http://www.atokyolifestyle.com/2015/03/odaiba-seaside-park.html', 'http://www.cascadianabroad.com/2014/07/29/where-are-we/']","The French Statue of Liberty from the Île aux Cygnes came to Odaiba, Tokyo, from April 1998 to May 1999 in commemoration of ""The French year in Japan"". Because of its popularity, in 2000 a replica of the French Statue of Liberty was erected at the same place. Also in Japan, a small Statue of Liberty is in the Amerika-mura (American Village) shopping district in Osaka, Japan. Another replica is in Oirase near the town of Shimoda south of Misawa in Aomori Prefecture, where the United States has an 8,000-person U.S. Air Force base. A replica of the Statue of Liberty in Ishinomaki, Miyagi Prefecture, was damaged by the 2011 Tōhoku earthquake and tsunami.",why is there a statue of liberty in odaiba
when was the last time chicago went to the superbowl,"['http://noticiasmvs.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=27917', 'https://sportsteamhistory.com/timeline/super-bowl-xxxii-winner-1996', 'https://sportsteamhistory.com/indianapolis-colts', 'https://logoeps.com/super-bowl-xliv-logo-vector-eps/34595/', 'http://commercialheaven.com/commercials/odd/', 'http://renardown-oa.cf/super-bowl-sunday-foods-kejy.php', 'https://sportsteamhistory.com/new-england-patriots']","Super Bowl XLI was an American football game played between the American Football Conference (AFC) champion Indianapolis Colts and the National Football Conference (NFC) champion Chicago Bears to decide the National Football League (NFL) champion for the 2006 season. The Colts defeated the Bears by the score of 29 -- 17. The game was played on February 4, 2007 at Dolphin Stadium in Miami Gardens, Florida.",when was the last time chicago went to the superbowl
when do you meet the mother in himym,"['https://wn.com/The_Mother_Hips', 'http://coinsbtc.tk/goxyw/how-i-met-your-mother-season-8-finale-reaction-27.php', 'http://outtatheblueband.com/reel/mother-how-i-met-your-online-account.php', 'http://dalydelightscakery.com/humor/himym-robins-mom-on-how-i-met.php', 'http://desnuda.top/Lyndsy%20Fonseca', 'http://desnuda.top/Rachel%20Bilson']","Tracy McConnell (colloquial: ""The Mother"") is the title character from the CBS television sitcom How I Met Your Mother. The show, narrated by Future Ted (Bob Saget), tells the story of how Ted Mosby (Josh Radnor) met The Mother. Tracy McConnell appears in eight episodes, from ""Lucky Penny"" to ""The Time Travelers"", as an unseen character; she was first seen fully in ""Something New"" and was promoted to a main character in season 9. The Mother is played by Cristin Milioti.",when do you meet the mother in himym
what happens when you dont rotate your tires,"['http://tsauto.com.sg/index.php', 'https://www.subaruoflethbridge.com/tire-rotation/', 'https://lexbrodiestire.com/tire-rotation-tips', 'https://burtbrothers.com/blog/rotating-tires-regularly/', 'http://preauto.com/home/tire-rotation/', 'https://www.tyrereview.com.au/tyre-advice/tyre-rotation', 'https://www.haddadhyundai.com/service/frequently-asked-questions.htm']","The weight on the front and rear axles differs which causes uneven wear. With the majority of cars having the engine in front, the front tires typically bear more weight than the rear tires. Front-wheel drive vehicles have not only the engine but also the transaxle in front, adding to the weight differential. Moreover, additional stress is placed disproportionately on the front tires by braking and steering. Thus, tire rotation needs to occur more frequently for front-wheel drive vehicles.",what happens when you dont rotate your tires
who played roscoe p coltrane on dukes of hazzard,"['https://www.bbparcodelcilento.com/people/79301-james-best', 'https://thereaderwiki.com/en/James_Best']","One of the busiest actors in Hollywood, who began his contract career with Universal Studios in 1949, Best's long career began in films in 1950, appearing primarily in Westerns, playing opposite Audie Murphy in Kansas Raiders (1950), The Cimarron Kid (1952) and The Quick Gun (1964), Raymond Massey in Seven Angry Men (1955), George Montgomery in Last of the Badman (1957), Frank Lovejoy in Cole Younger Gunfighter (1958), and Randolph Scott in Ride Lonesome (1959). He also starred in the science fiction cult movie, The Killer Shrews (1959) and its sequel, Return of the Killer Shrews (2012). He is most noted as playing bumbling Sheriff Rosco Pervis Coltrane in the action / comedy Dukes of Hazzard, a role that he revised in The Dukes of Hazzard: Reunion! (1997) as his character was now ""boss"" of Hazzard County as well as sheriff & again in The Dukes of Hazzard: Hazzard in Hollywood (2000).",who played roscoe p coltrane on dukes of hazzard
when is the darkest day of the year,"['http://www.javadtaghia.com/educational/calendar/seasonsmeteorologicalvsastronomical', 'https://springwolf.net/tag/religion/', 'http://www.feby.com/blog/midwinter-full-moon-friday', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/June_20', 'https://www.yourghoststories.com/real-ghost-story.php?story=25786', 'https://www.drikpanchang.com/seasons/season-summer-solstice-timings.html?geoname-id=1127110', 'http://www.hokulea.com/education-at-sea/polynesian-navigation/the-star-compass/']","The winter solstice (or hibernal solstice), also known as midwinter, is an astronomical phenomenon marking the day with the shortest period of daylight and the longest night of the year. It occurs when one of the Earth's poles has its maximum tilt away from the Sun. It happens twice yearly, once in each hemisphere. In the Northern Hemisphere this is the December solstice and in the Southern Hemisphere this is the June solstice.",when is the darkest day of the year
who fought a war against sweden to expand russia's size,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Great_Northern_War.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Great_Northern_War', 'http://www.zum.de/whkmla/region/scandinavia/xsweden.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Charles_XII_of_Sweden', 'http://www.vettius64.com/karolus-rex-king-karl-xii-sweden-1682-1718/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Scandinavia', 'http://onmilitarymatters.com/pages/dfcatalog.php?period=1600']","The war began when an alliance of Denmark -- Norway, Saxony, Poland and Russia, sensing an opportunity as Sweden was ruled by the young Charles XII, declared war on the Swedish Empire and launched a threefold attack on Swedish Holstein-Gottorp, Swedish Livonia, and Swedish Ingria. Sweden parried the Danish and Russian attacks at Travendal (August 1700) and Narva (November 1700) respectively, and in a counter-offensive pushed Augustus II's forces through the Polish -- Lithuanian Commonwealth to Saxony, dethroning Augustus on the way (September 1706) and forcing him to acknowledge defeat in the Treaty of Altranstädt (October 1706). The treaty also secured the extradition and execution of Johann Reinhold Patkul, architect of the alliance seven years earlier. Meanwhile the forces of Peter I had recovered from defeat at Narva and gained ground in Sweden's Baltic provinces, where they cemented Russian access to the Baltic Sea by founding Saint Petersburg in 1703. Charles XII moved from Saxony into Russia to confront Peter, but the campaign ended in 1709 with the destruction of the main Swedish army at the decisive Battle of Poltava (in present-day Ukraine) and Charles' exile in the Ottoman town of Bender. The Ottoman Empire defeated the Russian-Moldavian army in the Pruth River Campaign, but that peace treaty was in the end without great consequence to Russia's position.",who fought a war against sweden to expand russia's size
what is a cyclone known as in american continent,"['https://www.spaceotechnologies.com/project/tornado-checklist/', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/23475', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Natural_disaster', 'http://ininet.org/meaning-of-disaster-management-type-of-disaster-present-synari.html', 'https://www.sampspeak.in/2016/03/is-demolition-tougher-than-construction.html', 'https://larisaenglishclub.com/audio-resources/larisa-english-club-28-audio-version/', 'https://www.switchedonkids.com.au/product/4m-kidzlabs-tornado-maker/']","A tornado is a violently rotating column of air that is in contact with both the surface of the earth and a cumulonimbus cloud or, in rare cases, the base of a cumulus cloud. Also referred to as twisters, a collequial term in America, or cyclones, although the word cyclone is used in meteorology, in a wider sense, to name any closed low-pressure circulation.",what is a cyclone known as in american continent
name the writer and singer of the song aye mere vatan ke logo,"['http://it15.net/2017/03/28/india-%E4%B8%AD%E5%9B%BD%E5%91%98%E5%B7%A5%E6%AF%81%E5%8D%B0%E5%BA%A6%E5%9B%BD%E6%97%97%E6%89%94%E5%9E%83%E5%9C%BE%E6%A1%B6-oppo%E5%88%86%E5%85%AC%E5%8F%B8%E9%81%AD%E5%8C%85%E5%9B%B4/', 'http://www.singersagarika.com/2019/04/07/immortal-patriotic-song-aye-mere-watan-logon/', 'http://missliterati.com/aye-mere-watan-ke-logo.html', 'http://participal.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=21180', 'http://mastermotion.info/?newsid=30967', 'http://www.expressions-kt.in/2014/08/freedom-melodified-independence-day.html', 'https://blog.venuelook.com/republic-day-songs.html']","""Aye Mere Watan Ke Logo"" (Hindi: ऐ मेरे वतन के लोगों; ""O' people of my country"") is a Hindi patriotic song written by Kavi Pradeep, composed by C. Ramchandra, and performed by Lata Mangeshkar. The song commemorates Indian soldiers who died during the Sino-Indian War in 1962. The song was first performed live by Mangeshkar on 27 January 1963 at the National Stadium in New Delhi in the presence of President Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan and Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru, on account of Republic Day (26 January) 1963, which was just two months after the end of the war.",what is special about the song ae mere watan ke logo
who called sardar patel as iron man of india,"['https://duexpress.in/nss-sri-venkateswara-college-celebrates-national-unity-day-2018/', 'http://gk4banking.blogspot.com/2017/02/national-unity-day.html', 'https://www.newscrust.com/2018/10/salute-to-man-of-unity.html', 'https://bhaskarchakravorti.com/2016/11/08/indians-in-sudan-celebrate-national-unity-day/', 'https://www.meenakshiworldschool.com/event/national-unity-day-115', 'https://www.bankersadda.com/p/frequently-asked-questions-of-static_496.html', 'https://testbook.com/blog/important-current-affairs-quiz-1st-november-2017/']","Rashtriya Ekta Diwas (National Unity Day) was introduced by the Government of India and inaugurated by Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi in 2014. The intent is to pay tribute to Patel, who was instrumental in keeping India united. It is to be celebrated on 31 October every year as annual commemoration of the birthday of the Iron Man of India Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, one of the founding leaders of Republic of India. The official statement for Rashtriya Ekta Diwas by the Home Ministry of India cites that the National Unity Day ""will provide an opportunity to re-affirm the inherent strength and resilience of our nation to withstand the actual and potential threats to the unity, integrity and security of our country.""",who called sardar patel as iron man of india
what are the titles of the hobbit trilogy,"['https://www.mkvcinemas.cz/the-hobbit-all-parts-download-part-1-2-3-brrip-dual-audio-hindi-english-esub-400mb-480p-700mb-720p/', 'http://alternativefanart.com/fanart/movie-tv/the_hobbit_trilogy-alternative_movie_posters-collection.php', 'http://fullboxoffice.blogspot.com/2013/01/most-expected-movies-of-2013.html', 'http://e-perfume.tk/big-casino-wins-2.html', 'http://gsbkerala.tk/roulette-dinnerware-sams-club.html', 'http://hollidays.tk/blackjack-minecraft-skin.html', 'http://djalberto.tk/sibaya-casino-durban-south-africa.html']","The Hobbit is a film series consisting of three high fantasy adventure films directed by Peter Jackson. They are based on the 1937 novel The Hobbit by J.R.R. Tolkien, with large portions of the trilogy inspired by the appendices to The Return of the King, which expand on the story told in The Hobbit, as well as new material and characters written especially for the films. Together they act as a prequel to Jackson's The Lord of the Rings film trilogy. The films are subtitled An Unexpected Journey (2012), The Desolation of Smaug (2013), and The Battle of the Five Armies (2014).",what are the titles of the hobbit trilogy
where did the reign of maharana pratap take palace,['http://glowmagazineonline.com/victoria/story-of-maharana-pratap-in-hindi-pdf.php'],"Pratap Singh I (pronunciation (help info)) (9 May 1540 -- 19 January 1597) popularly known as Maharana Pratap, was a Rajput king of Mewar, a region in north-western India in the present day state of Rajasthan.",where did the reign of maharana pratap take palace
how many countries play in world series baseball,"['http://www.thefullwiki.org/World_Series', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/35616', 'https://forum.gaytorrent.ru/index.php?topic=44047.0', 'https://foreigndaze.com/2014/06/27/the-game-is-still-on/', 'https://www.topendsports.com/events/sport-events.htm']","Despite its name, the World Series remains solely the championship of the major-league baseball teams in the United States and Canada, although MLB, its players, and North American media sometimes informally refer to World Series winners as ""world champions of baseball"".",how many countries play in world series baseball
who presents the green jacket to the us masters winner,"['https://inevaroli.eu/pga-masters.html', 'http://www.online-golf-betting-gambling-wagering.com/Masters_Golf_Gambling_Odds.htm', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Masters_Tournament', 'https://sportseventstravel.co.uk/golf/us-masters-2018-augusta-essentials/']","In addition to a cash prize, the winner of the tournament is presented with a distinctive green jacket, formally awarded since 1949, and informally acquired by the champions for many years before that. The green sport coat is the official attire worn by members of Augusta National while on the club grounds; each Masters winner becomes an honorary member of the club. The recipient of the green jacket has it presented to him inside the Butler Cabin soon after the end of the tournament, and the presentation is then repeated outside near the 18th green in front of the patrons. Winners keep their jacket for the first year after their first victory, then return it to the club to wear whenever they visit. The tradition began in 1949, when Sam Snead won his first of three Masters titles.",who presents the green jacket to the us masters winner
what part of south america is venezuela located in,"['http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/19903', 'https://www.islablancacondo.com/venezuela/', 'http://1host2u.ir/Y/Wiki.php?eterm=Venezuela', 'http://globalcitymap.com/south-america/venezuela-map.html', 'https://www.propertyportal.com/venezuela-property-and-venezuelan-real-estate-for-sale-and-to-rent', 'http://factmontster.com/interesting-facts-about-venezuela-fun-facts-venezuela/', 'http://www.nookl.com/page/Venezuela']","Venezuela (/ ˌvɛnəˈzweɪlə / (listen) VEN-ə-ZWAYL-ə; American Spanish: (beneˈswela)), officially the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela (Spanish: República Bolivariana de Venezuela), is a federal republic on the northern coast of South America, bordered by Colombia on the west, Brazil on the south, Guyana on the east, the Dutch Lesser Antilles to the north and Trinidad and Tobago to the north-east. Venezuela covers 916,445 km (353,841 sq mi) and has over 31 million (31,568,179) people. The country has extremely high biodiversity and is ranked 7th in the world's list of nations with the most number of species. There are habitats ranging from the Andes Mountains in the west to the Amazon Basin rain-forest in the south via extensive llanos plains, the Caribbean coast and the Orinoco River Delta in the east.",what part of south america is venezuela located in
what type of comedy is the three stooges,"['http://www.lyricszoo.com/the-three-stooges/', 'https://live-tv-channels.org/tvchannels/us-3-stooges-channel.html', 'http://baby-rina.blogspot.com/2012/04/three-stooges-2012.html?showComment=1475594254150', 'http://worldmime.org/en/about-mime/vipersonalities/105-vipersonalities/309-the-three-stooges', 'http://www.walkoffame.com/the-three-stooges', 'http://www.beingretro.com/2013/05/why-is-it-women-dont-like-three-stooges.html', 'http://www.classictvshowsondvd.com/topic-12-Coming-Soon.php/The-Three-Stooges-The-Complete-Series-DVD-Boxset-Freeshipping-294115.php']","The Three Stooges were an American vaudeville and comedy team active from 1922 until 1970, best known for their 190 short subject films by Columbia Pictures that have been regularly airing on television since 1958. Their hallmark was physical farce and slapstick. In films, the stooges were commonly known by their actual first names. There were a total of six stooges over the act's run (with only three active at any given time), but Moe Howard and Larry Fine were the mainstays throughout the ensemble's nearly fifty-year run and the pivotal ""third Stooge"" was played by (in order of appearance) Shemp Howard, Curly Howard, Joe Besser, or Curly Joe DeRita.",what type of comedy is the three stooges
how did the founders create a constitution that could be adapted for the future,"['https://definitions.uslegal.com/l/living-constitution/', 'http://seikyusho.jp/how-is-the-constitution-a-living-document.html', 'http://www.hlynes.com/2009/05/27/a-tour-of-the-minor-parties-3-socialist-labour-party/', 'https://politicalstudys.com/american-judicial-system/', 'https://repository.mruni.eu/handle/007/13043', 'https://www.cpalanka.org/the-centre-for-policy-alternatives-vs-kabir-hashim-and-others-sc-fr-application-no-54-2016/', 'https://www.cato-unbound.org/2005/12/19/william-niskanen/one-more-round-17th-constitutional-interpretation']","While the arguments for the Living Constitution vary, they can generally be broken into two categories. First, the pragmatist view contends that interpreting the Constitution in accordance with its original meaning or intent is sometimes unacceptable as a policy matter, and thus that an evolving interpretation is necessary. The second, relating to intent, contends that the constitutional framers specifically wrote the Constitution in broad and flexible terms to create such a dynamic, ""living"" document. Opponents of the idea often argue that the Constitution should be changed through the amendment process, and that allowing judges to determine an ever-changing meaning of the constitution undermines democracy. The primary alternative to the Living Constitution is most commonly described as originalism.",how did the founders create a constitution that could be adapted for the future
when did the new world translation come out,"['http://wwebb.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=34322', 'https://en.m.wikiquote.org/wiki/New_World_Translation_of_the_Holy_Scriptures', 'https://faithandselfdefense.com/2016/10/23/a-reading-plan-for-christian-apologists-part-2/', 'https://wol.jw.org/en/wol/d/r1/lp-e/2009727', 'http://lettersofchrist.com/witnessing_to_jehovahs_witnesses.htm', 'https://wol.jw.org/en/wol/d/r1/lp-e/1001070205', 'http://www.religionfacts.com/new-world-translation']","The New World Translation of the Holy Scriptures (NWT) is a translation of the Bible published by the Watch Tower Bible and Tract Society. The New Testament portion was released in 1950, as The New World Translation of the Christian Greek Scriptures, with the complete Bible released in 1961; it is used and distributed by Jehovah's Witnesses. Though it is not the first Bible to be published by the group, it is their first original translation of ancient Classical Hebrew, Koine Greek, and Old Aramaic biblical texts. As of January 2017, the Watch Tower Society has published 217 million copies of the New World Translation in whole or in part in more than 150 languages.",when did the new world translation come out
which ruler of bengal found the ancient university called vikramshila,"['https://syskool.com/vikramasila-university/', 'http://francegoldfrancs.com/585ad_merovingians_dynasty_quentovic_ancient_france_town_gold_frank_coin_i71730.htm', 'http://www.baroda.com/gujarattouristspots/champaner.php', 'http://www.99mustsee.com/India/Champaner-Tourism-Gujarat-8741']",Vikramashila was founded by Pāla king Dharmapala in the late 8th or early 9th century. It prospered for about four centuries before it was destroyed by Bakhtiyar Khilji along with the other major centres of Buddhism in India around 1200.,which ruler of bengal found the ancient university called vikramshila
when might the administration of aspirin be contraindicated,"['http://pharmaknow.com/contraindications-and-adverse-effects-of-aspirin/', 'https://www.prescriptionpoint.com/online-pharmacy/buy-drug-online/amaryl/', 'http://busanlottedfs.com/sodium-acetylsalicylate.html', 'https://psychology.wikia.org/wiki/Aspirin', 'http://www.allmedicalinfo.com/lyrics/circulation-problems/common-side-effects-1311.html', 'http://emeditube.in/archive/24_9_15.html', 'https://www.naturalnews.com/025650_aspirin_blood_drug.html']","Aspirin should not be taken by people who are allergic to ibuprofen or naproxen, or who have salicylate intolerance or a more generalized drug intolerance to NSAIDs, and caution should be exercised in those with asthma or NSAID-precipitated bronchospasm. Owing to its effect on the stomach lining, manufacturers recommend people with peptic ulcers, mild diabetes, or gastritis seek medical advice before using aspirin. Even if none of these conditions is present, the risk of stomach bleeding is still increased when aspirin is taken with alcohol or warfarin. People with hemophilia or other bleeding tendencies should not take aspirin or other salicylates. Aspirin is known to cause hemolytic anemia in people who have the genetic disease glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase deficiency, particularly in large doses and depending on the severity of the disease. Use of aspirin during dengue fever is not recommended owing to increased bleeding tendency. People with kidney disease, hyperuricemia, or gout should not take aspirin because it inhibits the kidneys' ability to excrete uric acid, thus may exacerbate these conditions. Aspirin should not be given to children or adolescents to control cold or influenza symptoms, as this has been linked with Reye's syndrome.",when might the administration of aspirin be contraindicated
who said greed for lack of a better word is good,['https://pigsfly.info/2016/04/10/australias-version-panama-papers/'],"Gekko has become a symbol in popular culture for unrestrained greed (with the signature line, ""Greed, for lack of a better word, is good""), often in fields outside corporate finance.",who said greed for lack of a better word is good
when did microwave ovens become popular in homes,"['https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2018/12/06/', 'https://www.irwinquagmirewart.com/irwin-the-frogs-little-blog/cooking-made-quick', 'http://jo-annemotherandnanna.blogspot.com/2018/05/', 'http://ir.cftri.com/1662/', 'http://voxphilly.com/8-ways-in-which-microwave-cooking-suits-the-modern-lifestyle/853/', 'http://www.askphysics.com/principle-of-working-of-microwave-oven/', 'https://www.latestdeals.co.uk/tags/microwave']","Percy Spencer is generally credited with inventing the modern microwave oven after World War II from radar technology developed during the war. Named the ""Radarange"", it was first sold in 1946. Raytheon later licensed its patents for a home-use microwave oven that was first introduced by Tappan in 1955, but these units were still too large and expensive for general home use. The countertop microwave oven was first introduced in 1967 by the Amana Corporation, and their use has spread into commercial and residential kitchens around the world. In addition to their use in cooking food, types of microwave ovens are used for heating in many industrial processes.",when did microwave ovens become popular in homes
what notes are in the key of d minor,"['http://www.omnilexica.com/?q=G-Minor', 'http://classiccat.com/dictionary/d_minor.php', 'https://wn.com/Violin_Concerto_in_E_minor', 'http://classiccat.com/dictionary/d_major.php', 'https://wn.com/Sonata_in_E_Minor', 'http://timbertsch.com/press/', 'http://kgargar.tk/quartet-mozart-piano-sheet.html']","D minor is a minor scale based on D, consisting of the pitches D, E, F, G, A, B ♭, and C. Its key signature has one flat. Its relative major is F major and its parallel major is D major.",what notes are in the key of d minor
when was the new world trade center built,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Empire_State_Building', 'https://www.turipo.com/views/tripPage.php?trip_id=251', 'https://www.whrtny.com/top-5-tallest-buildings-new-york/', 'https://datavizblog.com/2014/02/11/architecture-the-empire-state-building/', 'https://cocochlo.blog/tag/usa/', 'http://iaa-ngo.com/2019/02/freedom-tower-2006/', 'http://fancytagcloud.demo.offlajn.com/index.php/component/tags/tag/7-tallest']","The building's architect was David Childs, whose firm Skidmore, Owings & Merrill (SOM) also designed the Burj Khalifa and the Willis Tower. The construction of below-ground utility relocations, footings, and foundations for the new building began on April 27, 2006. One World Trade Center became the tallest structure in New York City on April 30, 2012, when it surpassed the height of the Empire State Building. The tower's steel structure was topped out on August 30, 2012. On May 10, 2013, the final component of the skyscraper's spire was installed, making the building, including its spire, reach a total height of 1,776 feet (541 m). Its height in feet is a deliberate reference to the year when the United States Declaration of Independence was signed. The building opened on November 3, 2014; the One World Observatory opened on May 29, 2015.",when was the new world trade center built
government with a prime minister and two houses of parliament,"['https://www.elevenjournals.com/zoek?search_category=Praktijk', 'http://www.flickr.com/photos/mauricedb/2706292588/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Law_of_the_United_Kingdom', 'https://www.q-files.com/geography/population/government-of-the-united-kingdom/', 'https://sputniknews.com/europe/201706081054433561-uk-parliamentary-election-process/', 'https://www.olneytheatre.org/labour-love-context-guide', 'https://anglictina-maturita.cz/the-united-kingdom-otazka-z-anglictiny/']","The parliament is bicameral, consisting of an upper house (the House of Lords) and a lower house (the House of Commons). The Sovereign forms the third component of the legislature (the Queen-in-Parliament). The House of Lords includes two different types of members: the Lords Spiritual, consisting of the most senior bishops of the Church of England, and the Lords Temporal, consisting mainly of life peers, appointed by the Sovereign on the advice of the Prime Minister, and of 92 hereditary peers, sitting either by virtue of holding a royal office, or by being elected by their fellow hereditary peers. Prior to the opening of the Supreme Court in October 2009, the House of Lords also performed a judicial role through the Law Lords.",government with a prime minister and two houses of parliament
where is rhode island located in the united states,"['http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Rhode_Island', 'http://www.gmanemwwcomicsenc.uk/home/chapters-of-the-encyclopedia/by-categories/publishers-category/dc-comics/rhode-island-county-dc-comics', 'http://townwalls.com/state-Rhode-Island_RI-US.aspx', 'https://www.seniorguidance.org/assisted-living/rhode-island/', 'https://www.europa-eu60.com/salve-regina-university-rhode-island/', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=What+Was+Education+Like+in+Colonial+Rhode+Island%3F&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://onestoplashes.com/ri/']","Rhode Island (/ ˌroʊd-/ (listen)), officially the State of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations, is a state in the New England region of the United States. It is the smallest in area, the 7th least populous, and the 2nd most densely populated of the 50 states -- but its official name is the longest. Rhode Island is bordered by Connecticut to the west, Massachusetts to the north and east, and the Atlantic Ocean to the south via Rhode Island Sound and Block Island Sound. It also shares a small maritime border with New York. Providence is the state capital and most populous city in Rhode Island.",where is rhode island located in the united states
where does the term houston we have a problem,"['https://ourplnt.com/spacewalker-russian-film/', 'http://www.cerebra.com.tr/en/insights-news-insights-houston-we-have-a-problem-acfe-2018-report-reveals-incredibly-large-fraud-losses.html', 'https://ourplnt.com/tag/apollo-13/']","""Houston, we have a problem"" is a popular but erroneous quote from the radio communications between the Apollo 13 astronaut John (""Jack"") Swigert and the NASA Mission Control Center (""Houston"") during the Apollo 13 spaceflight, as the astronauts asked about their discovery of the explosion that doubted in their spacecraft. The erroneous wording was popularized by the 1995 film Apollo 13, a dramatization of the Apollo 13 mission, in which actor Tom Hanks, portraying Mission Commander Jim Lovell, uses that wording, which became one of the film's taglines.",where does the term houston we have a problem
an important difference between cpi and the gdp deflator is,"['https://socialrol.blogspot.com/2018/07/how-to-calculate-gdp.html', 'https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gdppricedeflator.asp', 'https://pt.scribd.com/document/352569365/Chap-002', 'http://www.economywatch.com/economic-statistics/Gabon/GDP_Deflator/', 'http://www.economywatch.com/economic-statistics/Euro-Area/GDP_Deflator/', 'http://roomsexy.info/dudol/how-to-calculate-price-index-for-gdp-vub.php', 'http://baby-387.info/lllv/how-to-calculate-real-gdp-with-price-index-foti.php']","Like the consumer price index (CPI), the GDP deflator is a measure of price inflation / deflation with respect to a specific base year; the GDP deflator of the base year itself is equal to 100. Unlike the CPI, the GDP deflator is not based on a fixed basket of goods and services; the ""basket"" for the GDP deflator is allowed to change from year to year with people's consumption and investment patterns.",an important difference between cpi and the gdp deflator is
what is harry potter and the cursed child book about,"['https://www.intelligenthq.com/best-shows-catch-broadway-month/', 'https://www.inquisitr.com/4938520/harry-potter-and-the-cursed-child-star-says-donald-trump-cant-watch-but-anybody-else-can/', 'https://farmanblogs.wordpress.com/category/literature/', 'https://www.eventticketscenter.com/harry-potter-and-the-cursed-child-tickets/6934/c', 'https://www.coachtransportgroup.com/blog/category/theatre/', 'https://bookstr.com/article/london-cast-of-harry-potter-and-the-cursed-child-reprising-roles-for-broadway/', 'https://www.uppstudio.com/epages/940355124.sf/en_GB/?ObjectPath=/Shops/940355124/Products/0286/SubProducts/0286-0087']","The story begins nineteen years after the events of Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows and follows Harry Potter, now a Ministry of Magic employee, and his younger son Albus Severus Potter, who is about to attend Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.",what is harry potter and the cursed child book about
who was born and died on halley's comet,"['http://thequotesforlife.com/keep-away-from-people-who-try-to-belittle-your-ambitions-small-people-always-do-that-but-the-really-great-make-you-feel-that-you-too-can-become-great-mark-twain/', 'https://www.lifeadvancer.com/portfolio_tags/mark-twain/', 'https://catsoncatnip.co/blogs/cats/mark-twain-cats', 'http://www.melissafoxmedia.com/melissafoxblog/2017/4/14/on-location-hannibal-mo', 'http://carolsnotebook.com/2018/05/04/the-innocents-abroad-by-mark-twain/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'http://m.dreamscity.net/t58145.html', 'http://www.mathisfunforum.com/viewtopic.php?pid=376618']","Twain was born shortly after an appearance of Halley's Comet, and he predicted that he would ""go out with it"" as well; he died the day after the comet returned. He was lauded as the ""greatest humorist this country has produced"", and William Faulkner called him ""the father of American literature"".",who was born and died on halley's comet
who played brooks in the movie shawshank redemption,"['http://www.saciol.com/o/g/tim_robbins', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/James_Whitmore.html', 'https://heightline.com/tony-danza-net-worth-age-awards/']","In 1994, Whitmore played the role of librarian Brooks Hatlen in the critically acclaimed and Academy Award-nominated 1994 Frank Darabont film starring Tim Robbins and Morgan Freeman, The Shawshank Redemption. Two years later, he co-starred in the 1996 horror / sci-fi film The Relic. In 1999, he played Raymond Oz in two episodes of The Practice, earning an Emmy Award for Outstanding Guest Actor in a Drama Series.",who played brooks in the movie shawshank redemption
when did the us place an embargo on cuba,"['https://www.vacation-travel-adventure.com/2013/03/', 'http://viewpoint.world/register/79/do-you-support-president-obamas-move-to-lift-the-trade-and-travel-embargo-on-cuba', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/1962/2/united-states-economic-blockade-against-cuba-becomes-near-total-embargo', 'https://www.gktoday.in/gk/united-states-embargo-against-cuba/', 'https://www.staugustine.com/opinions/2013-12-22/guest-columnr-lets-end-cuban-embargo', 'https://www.studentnewsdaily.com/world-current-events/cuba-ukraine-and-the-pa/print/?part=article', 'http://cubajournal.co/why-regularly-scheduled-us-cuba-flights-are-only-a-matter-of-time/']","The United States embargo against Cuba (in Cuba called el bloqueo, ""the blockade"") is a commercial, economic, and financial embargo imposed by the United States on Cuba. An embargo was first imposed by the United States on sale of arms to Cuba on March 14, 1958, during the Fulgencio Batista regime. Again on October 19, 1960 (almost two years after the Batista regime was deposed by the Cuban Revolution) the U.S. placed an embargo on exports to Cuba except for food and medicine after Cuba nationalized American-owned Cuban oil refineries without compensation. On February 7, 1962 the embargo was extended to include almost all imports. Currently, the Cuban embargo is enforced mainly through six statutes: the Trading with the Enemy Act of 1917, the Foreign Assistance Act of 1961, the Cuban Assets Control Regulations of 1963, the Cuban Democracy Act of 1992, the Helms -- Burton Act of 1996, and the Trade Sanctions Reform and Export Enhancement Act of 2000. The stated purpose of the Cuban Democracy Act of 1992 is to maintain sanctions on Cuba as long as the Cuban government refuses to move toward ""democratization and greater respect for human rights"". The Helms -- Burton Act further restricted United States citizens from doing business in or with Cuba, and mandated restrictions on giving public or private assistance to any successor government in Havana unless and until certain claims against the Cuban government were met. In 1999, President Bill Clinton expanded the trade embargo by also disallowing foreign subsidiaries of U.S. companies to trade with Cuba. In 2000, Clinton authorized the sale of ""humanitarian"" U.S. products to Cuba.","Cecilia Clark's Journal Skip to main content Posts Showing posts from March, 2013 Show all Featured September 28, 2023 New Website, New Blog, but the Old Blog Archive remains: September 28, 2023 After many years of wanting a real website, this month I finally have a website designed by the very knowledgeable Rey Rey Rodriguez ( TheMindOfReyRey ). My old blog, Vacation-Travel-Adventure .com continues with the same address but it is located in the ""Archives"" tab on my new website https://www.ceciliaclark.com/ . The new blog which is a continuation but with much better resolution for 4K screens is now at https://www.ceciliaclark.com/blog . Share Get link Facebook X Pinterest Email Other Apps Post a Comment Read more March 25, 2013 North Carolina to Washington DC: March 18-25, 2013 Share Get link Facebook X Pinterest Email Other Apps Post a Comment March 18, 2013 Florida: March 9-18, 2013 Share Get link Facebook X Pinterest Email Other Apps Post a Comment March 09, 2013 Last Days in Havana, Cuba: March 9, 2013 Share Get link Facebook X Pinterest Email Other Apps Post a Comment March 07, 2013 Ciego de Avila, Cuba: March 5-7, 2013 Share Get link Facebook X Pinterest Email Other Apps Post a Comment Newer Posts Older Posts Home [SEP_DOC] Attention Required! | Cloudflare Please enable cookies. Sorry, you have been blocked You are unable to access viewpoint.world Why have I been blocked? This website is using a security service to protect itself from online attacks. The action you just performed triggered the security solution. There are several actions that could trigger this block including submitting a certain word or phrase, a SQL command or malformed data. What can I do to resolve this? You can email the site owner to let them know you were blocked. Please include what you were doing when this page came up and the Cloudflare Ray ID found at the bottom of this page. Cloudflare Ray ID: 9f69106a79703dc5 • Your IP: Click to reveal 111.95.123.158 • Performance & security by Cloudflare"
what advantage does a list have over an array,"['https://www.programmingtunes.com/linked-lists-with-applications-in-c/', 'http://www.java2novice.com/data-structures-in-java/linked-list/', 'https://aticleworld.com/introduction-to-linked-list/']","The principal benefit of a linked list over a conventional array is that the list elements can easily be inserted or removed without reallocation or reorganization of the entire structure because the data items need not be stored contiguously in memory or on disk, while an array has to be declared in the source code, before compiling and running the program. Linked lists allow insertion and removal of nodes at any point in the list, and can do so with a constant number of operations if the link previous to the link being added or removed is maintained during list traversal.",what advantage does a list have over an array
who played roseanne's sister jackie on roseanne,"['http://rock-cafe.info/posts/laurie-metcalf-and-matt-roth-6c6175726965.html', 'https://www.clickthecity.com/movies/profile/ZGs9n4/taylor-schilling', 'https://www.wndrwmn.com/uzo-aduba', 'https://www.cbsnews.com/pictures/nifty-at-50/9/', 'http://bellingenwritersfestival.com.au/rachel-ward/', 'https://www.thecelebworth.com/10-famous-celebrities-who-have-stretch-marks/5/', 'http://www.latinaparadise.com/eva-longoria/biography-profile-3/']","Metcalf began her career with the Steppenwolf Theater Company and frequently works in Chicago theater, including the 1983 revival of Balm in Gilead. From 1988 to 1997 and in 2018, Metcalf played the role of Jackie Harris on the ABC sitcom Roseanne, for which she won three Primetime Emmy Awards for Outstanding Supporting Actress in a Comedy Series (1992 -- 1994). She also was nominated for two Golden Globe Awards. A ten-time Emmy Award nominee, Metcalf's television credits include 3rd Rock from the Sun, The Norm Show, Frasier, Desperate Housewives, and The Big Bang Theory. From 2013 to 2015, she played a leading role of Dr. Jenna James in the HBO comedy series Getting On, for which she received critical acclaim and a nomination for the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Lead Actress in a Comedy Series.",who played roseanne's sister jackie on roseanne
what are the objectives of the games scrabble,"['https://au.fabtintoys.com/scrabble/', 'http://einfach-reisen.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=14572', 'http://musicalwork.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=38991', 'https://scrabblewordfinder.vip/blog/', 'http://www.boardgamesmessiah.com/board-games-scrabble/', 'http://edelstahlhaube.eu/more-scrabble_zc.html', 'http://ahligizi.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=9128']","Scrabble is a word game in which two to four players score points by placing tiles bearing a single letter onto a board divided into a 15 × 15 grid of squares. The tiles must form words which, in crossword fashion, read left to right in rows or downwards in columns, and be defined in a standard dictionary or lexicon.",what are the objectives of the games scrabble
what is the windows deployment services (wds) role,"['http://hmfly.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=32426', 'https://www.technig.com/configure-wds-on-windows-server-2016-windows-deployment/', 'http://findingbetter.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=16263', 'http://trendguide-free.info/?newsid=49110', 'http://aurelius-global.com/microsoft-technologies/windows-deployment-online-training.php', 'https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/aa967394(v=vs.85)', 'http://www.aidanfinn.com/?p=13210']","Windows Deployment Services is a server technology from Microsoft for network-based installation of Windows operating systems. It is the successor to Remote Installation Services. WDS is intended to be used for remotely deploying Windows Vista, Windows 7, Windows 8, Windows Server 2008, Windows Server 2012 and Windows Server 2016, but also supports other operating systems because unlike its predecessor RIS, which was a method of automating the installation process, WDS uses disk imaging, in particular the Windows Imaging Format (WIM). WDS is included as a Server Role in all 32-bit and 64-bit versions of Windows Server 2008, and is included as an optionally installable component with Windows Server 2003 Service Pack 2.",what is the windows deployment services (wds) role
who played the leprechaun in the leprechaun movie,"['https://heightline.com/warwick-davis-wife-children-net-worth/', 'https://showtimechallenge.co.uk/news-warwick-davis-to-host-48hourmillie/', 'https://www.ucp.ac.uk/honorary-graduates/', 'http://www.backstagepass.biz/2012/09/priscilla-presley-warwick-davis-jarred.html', 'https://www.fanpal.com/celeb/Warwick+Davis/', 'https://geekmom.com/2014/10/supporting-creatures-labyrinth/', 'http://nerdsdrinkwhiskey.com/news/tag/Kevin+Smith']","Warwick Ashley Davis (born 3 February 1970) is an English actor, television presenter, writer, director and producer. He played the title characters in Willow and the Leprechaun film series, the Ewok Wicket in Star Wars Episode VI: Return of the Jedi and Professor Filius Flitwick and Griphook in the Harry Potter films. Davis also starred as a fictionalised version of himself in the sitcom Life's Too Short, written and directed by Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant.",who played the leprechaun in the leprechaun movie
when did the 12 disciples become the 12 apostles,"['http://thecobbsix.com/author/BradleyCobb/page/48/?add-to-cart=471', 'https://herald-magazine.com/2013-marapril-table-of-contents/through-the-eyes-of-the-master-from-fishermen-to-devout-women/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Commissioning_of_the_Twelve_Apostles', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Ministry_of_Jesus', 'https://www.gsflo.org/blog/kingdomsurrender', 'https://ebible.com/questions/15378-why-does-god-delegate-his-work-to-angels?back=1', 'https://www.compellingtruth.org/twelve-disciples-apostles.html']","The commissioning of the Twelve Apostles is an episode in the ministry of Jesus that appears in all three Synoptic Gospels: Matthew 10: 1 -- 4, Mark 3: 13 -- 19 and Luke 6: 12 -- 16. It relates the initial selection of the Twelve Apostles among the disciples of Jesus.",when did the 12 disciples become the 12 apostles
how did the cold war effect the soviet union,"['https://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/193287', 'https://www.cs.mcgill.ca/~rwest/wikispeedia/wpcd/wp/c/Cold_War.htm', 'https://selfstudyhistory.com/2015/01/20/world-history-cold-war-and-contemporary-world-history/?replytocom=261', 'https://knowledge.allbest.ru/history/2c0a65635b3ad68a5d53b88521306d26_0.html', 'http://fouman.com/Y/Wiki.php?eterm=Cold%20War', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Cold%20War', 'http://longreads.tni.org/state-of-power-2019/global-finance/']","After Russia embarked on economic reforms in the 1990s, it suffered a financial crisis and a recession more severe than the United States and Germany had experienced during the Great Depression. Russian living standards have worsened overall in the post -- Cold War years, although the economy has resumed growth since 1995.",how did the cold war effect the soviet union
when does the femoral artery become the popliteal artery,"['http://www.healthcaretip.com/2017/07/Popliteal-pulse-Definition-Point-location-Rate-Palpation-Landmark.html', 'https://statpearls.com/kb/viewarticle/32247/', 'http://eatyourheartoutboston.com/northern-territory/how-to-find-popliteal-pulse.php', 'https://www.newyorkpersonalinjuryattorneysblog.com/medical_malpractice_failure_to/', 'https://healthjade.com/popliteal-artery/', 'https://insightsimaging.springeropen.com/articles/10.1007/s13244-016-0513-6', 'https://www.healthline.com/human-body-maps/saphenous-branch-descending-genicular-arter/male']","The popliteal artery is a deeply placed continuation of the femoral artery after it passes through the adductor hiatus, or opening in the distal portion of the adductor magnus muscle. It courses through the popliteal fossa and ends at the lower border of the popliteus muscle, where it branches into the anterior and posterior tibial arteries.",when does the femoral artery become the popliteal artery
what is the extent of the mid ocean ridge system,"['http://www.factsinside.com/longest-mountain-range-in-the-world-is-under-water/', 'https://www.bankersadda.com/p/frequently-asked-questions-of-static_484.html']","The mid-ocean ridges of the world are connected and form the Ocean Ridge, a single global mid-oceanic ridge system that is part of every ocean, making it the longest mountain range in the world. The continuous mountain range is 65,000 km (40,400 mi) long (several times longer than the Andes, the longest continental mountain range), and the total length of the oceanic ridge system is 80,000 km (49,700 mi) long.",what is the extent of the mid ocean ridge system
who started the 1857 great mutiny in india,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Shorncliffe_Army_Camp', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Bihar_Regiment', 'http://www.amroha.co.in/blog/page/3/', 'https://www.mintageworld.com/media/detail/6879-gwalior-fort-was-captured/', 'https://www.ijopona.org/news/5-mutiny/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Indian_Rebellion_of_1857', 'http://newsweekpakistan.com/a-life-in-watercolors/']","The Indian Rebellion of 1857 was a major, but ultimately unsuccessful, uprising in India in 1857 -- 58 against the rule of the British East India Company, which functioned as a sovereign power on behalf of the British Crown. The rebellion began on 10 May 1857 in the form of a mutiny of sepoys of the Company's army in the garrison town of Meerut, 40 miles northeast of Delhi (now Old Delhi). It then erupted into other mutinies and civilian rebellions chiefly in the upper Gangetic plain and central India, though incidents of revolt also occurred farther north and east. The rebellion posed a considerable threat to British power in that region, and was contained only with the rebels' defeat in Gwalior on 20 June 1858. On 1 November 1858, the British granted amnesty to all rebels not involved in murder, though they did not declare the hostilities formally to have ended until 8 July 1859. The rebellion is known by many names, including the Sepoy Mutiny, the Indian Mutiny, the Great Rebellion, the Revolt of 1857, the Indian Insurrection, and India's First War of Independence.",who started the 1857 great mutiny in india
who gave the beatles their name in april 1960,"['https://whspawprint.com/2019/03/29/the-worlds-most-lovable-band-the-beatles/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Lucy_(Australopithecus)', 'https://www.abqjew.net/2015/09/greatest-meetings-ever.html', 'https://preview.arraythemes.com/author/full-width/', 'http://bagskart.com/were-the-beatles-on-drugs.html', 'https://www.mediamusicmania.com/2017/03/The-Beatles-English-MP3-Music-Download.html', 'https://www.liverpoolpicturebook.com/2013/02/george-harrison.html']","In March 1957, John Lennon, then aged sixteen, formed a skiffle group with several friends from Quarry Bank High School. They briefly called themselves the Blackjacks, before changing their name to the Quarrymen after discovering that a respected local group was already using the other name. Fifteen-year-old Paul McCartney joined as a rhythm guitarist shortly after he and Lennon met that July. In February 1958, McCartney invited his friend George Harrison to watch the band. The fifteen-year-old auditioned for Lennon, impressing him with his playing, but Lennon initially thought Harrison was too young to join them. After a month of Harrison's persistence, during a second meeting, arranged by McCartney, he performed the lead guitar part for the instrumental ""Raunchy"" on the upper deck of a Liverpool bus, and they enlisted him as their lead guitarist. By January 1959, Lennon's Quarry Bank friends had left the group, and he began studies at the Liverpool College of Art. The three guitarists, billing themselves at least three times as Johnny and the Moondogs, were playing rock and roll whenever they could find a drummer. Lennon's art school friend Stuart Sutcliffe, who had recently sold one of his paintings and was persuaded to purchase a bass guitar, joined in January 1960, and it was him who suggested changing the band's name to Beatals, as a tribute to Buddy Holly and the Crickets. They used the name until May, when they became the Silver Beetles, before undertaking a brief tour of Scotland as the backing group for pop singer and fellow Liverpudlian Johnny Gentle. By early July, they had changed their name to the Silver Beatles and by the middle of August to the Beatles.","Lucy (Australopithecus) - WikiVisually WikiVisually Infinite photos and videos for every Wiki article · Find something interesting to watch in seconds WikiVisually Infinite photos and videos for every Wiki article · Find something interesting to watch in seconds History by Country Famous Castles Celebrities Recovered Treasures Wars and Battles Sports Rare Coins Largest Palaces Largest Empires Tallest Buildings Great Artists Great Museums Ancient Marvels Presidents Orders and Medals British Monarchs Best Campuses Great Cities World Banknotes Countries of the World Wonders of Nature Supercars Richest US Counties Kings of France Animals Crown Jewels more top lists History Lucy (Australopithecus) Videos Photos AL 288-1, commonly known as Lucy or Dinkʼinesh, is a collection of several hundred pieces of fossilized bone comprising 40 percent of the skeleton of a female of the hominin species Australopithecus afarensis. It was discovered in 1974 in Ethiopia, at Hadar, a site in the Awash Valley of the Afar Triangle, by Donald Johanson, a paleoanthropologist of the Cleveland Museum of Natural History. Lucy (Australopithecus) Side view of cast of Lucy in the Naturmuseum Senckenberg Cast of Lucy in Mexico Lucy skeleton reconstruction at the Cleveland Museum of Natural History Australopithecus afarensis Videos Photos Australopithecus afarensis is an extinct species of australopithecine which lived from about 3.9–2.9 million years ago (mya) in the Pliocene of East Africa. The first fossils were discovered in the 1930s, but major fossil finds would not take place until the 1970s. From 1972 to 1977, the International Afar Research Expedition—led by anthropologists Maurice Taieb, Donald Johanson and Yves Coppens—unearthed several hundreds of hominin specimens in Hadar, Ethiopia, the most significant being the exceedingly well-preserved skeleton AL 288-1 (""Lucy"") and the site AL 333. Beginning in 1974, Mary Leakey led an expedition into Laetoli, Tanzania, and notably recovered fossil trackways. In 1978, the species was first described, but this was followed by arguments for splitting the wealth of specimens into different species given the wide range of variation which had been attributed to sexual dimorphism. A. afarensis probably descended from A. anamensis and is hypothesised to have given rise to Homo, though the latter is debated. Australopithecus afarensis The holotype LH 4 ""Lucy"" skeleton DIK-1-1 skeleton; notice the diverging left big toe bone"
where did the name trinidad and tobago come from,"['http://truthtroubles.com/tag/caribbean/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Moruga', 'https://www.deltasoutherncolorado.com/disaster-cleanup-and-repair-services-in-trinidad-co.html', 'http://andrea-campanile.info/52644-dating-sivusto-trinidad-ja-tobago/', 'http://advocatusatheist.blogspot.com/2010/09/']","Historian E.L. Joseph claimed that Trinidad's Amerindian name was Cairi or ""Land of the Humming Bird"", derived from the Arawak name for hummingbird, ierèttê or yerettê. However, Boomert claims that neither cairi nor caeri means hummingbird and tukusi or tucuchi does. Others have reported that kairi and iere simply mean island. Christopher Columbus renamed it ""La Isla de la Trinidad"" (""The Island of the Trinity""), fulfilling a vow made before setting out on his third voyage of exploration. Tobago's cigar-like shape may have given it its Spanish name (cabaco, tavaco, tobacco) and possibly its Amerindian names of Aloubaéra (black conch) and Urupaina (big snail), although the English pronunciation is / təˈbeɪɡoʊ /, rhyming with lumbago, sago, and ""may go"".",where did the name trinidad and tobago come from
who wrote the song because the night belongs to lovers,"['http://borntolisten.com/2017/09/06/20-songs-released-in-1978-you-must-hear/?replytocom=543', 'https://wfgr.com/because-the-night-by-patti-smith-classic-hit-or-miss/', 'http://desnuda.top/Shirley%20Manson', 'http://flatpress-fr.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=8495', 'http://www.superstarparty.com/2013/06/cascada-because-night-official-video.html', 'http://www.songspeak.com/come-on-now-try-and-understand-the-way-i-feel-im-the-orkin-man/comment-page-2/', 'http://guardiabermellon.tk/because-the-night-drum-sheet-music.html']","""Because the Night"" is a song written by Bruce Springsteen and Patti Smith that was first released in 1978 as a single off the Patti Smith Group album Easter. It rose to number 13 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart, as well as number five in the United Kingdom, and helped propel sales of Easter to mainstream success -- even as Smith was deciding to retire from a life of constant touring. In 1987, the song was ranked number 116 on NME magazine's list of ""The Top 150 Singles of All Time"". It remains one of the best-known songs of Smith's catalog.",who wrote the song because the night belongs to lovers
what are the main political parties of canada,"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Politics_of_Canada', 'http://techsciencenews.com/directory/wp/c/Canada.htm', 'https://alchetron.com/Saskatchewan', 'https://catholicconscience.org/canada-political-system/', 'http://eidmubarak2014.tk/john-howard-society-of-ontario-fact-sheets.html', 'http://www.referat-web.ru/referat61926.html', 'https://knowledge.allbest.ru/geography/2c0b65625b2ac78a5d53a89421216c27_0.html']","The two dominant political parties in Canada have historically been the Liberal Party of Canada and Conservative Party of Canada (or its predecessors), however, the social democratic New Democratic Party (NDP) has risen to prominence, and even threatened to upset the two other established parties during the 2011 federal election and the 2015 federal election. Smaller parties like the Quebec nationalist Bloc Québécois, and the Green Party of Canada have also been able to exert their own influence over the political process. Far-right and Far-left politics has never been a prominent force in Canadian society.",what are the main political parties of canada
can police tap your cell phone text messages,"['http://dietitianoffice.com/sports-games/phone-tap-software.php', 'http://wang-xin.info/?newsid=5807', 'https://smashupgraphics.com/is-there-spyware-in-your-android/', 'https://evprogramas.com/author/admin/page/3/', 'https://f1-rocketboy.com/detect-if-your-cellphone-is-being-tapped/', 'http://possibilitiesbook.com/ebooks-reviews-videos/', 'http://possibilitiesbook.com/sea-to-shining-sea/']","Cellphone surveillance, also known as cellphone spying, may involve the tracking, bugging, monitoring, interception and recording of conversations and text messages on mobile phones. It also encompasses the monitoring of people's movements, which can be tracked using mobile phone signals when phones are turned on. In the United States, law enforcement agencies can legally monitor the movements of people from their mobile phone signals upon obtaining a court order to do so. Cellphone spying software is software that is surreptitiously installed on mobile phones that can enable these actions.",can police tap your cell phone text messages
how many teams go to champions league from each country,"['https://www.tvsportguide.com/football/champions-league/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?from=revealtrailer.com&ads=1&title=Reveal+trailer&auto=Reveal+trailer&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Reveal+trailer&pagenum=5', 'http://crictoday.com/detail/5-reasons-why-real-madrid-will-be-able-to-defend-their-champions-league-title', 'https://vipsportmaster.com/%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A1%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B9%8C%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%81-2018/', 'https://www.cgcreativeshop.com/chi-sono/digital-graphics/2443-star-ball-champions-league-metallic-free.html', 'https://iffhs.com/dev/7370/history-of-europe-clubs-champions-league-real-madrid-cf-and-cristiano-ronaldo-on-top/', 'https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuropaleague/news/newsid=2444525.html']","Introduced in 1992, the competition replaced the European Champion Clubs' Cup, or simply European Cup, which had run since 1955, adding a group stage to the competition and allowing multiple entrants from certain countries. The pre-1992 competition was initially a straight knockout tournament open only to the champion club of each country. During the 1990s, the format was expanded, incorporating a round-robin group stage to include clubs that finished runner-up of some nations' top-level league. While most of Europe's national leagues can still only enter their national league champion, Europe's strongest national leagues now provide up to five teams for the competition. Clubs that finish next-in-line in each nation's top level league, having not qualified for the UEFA Champions League competition, are eligible for the next-level UEFA Europa League competition.",how many teams go to champions league from each country
where does red hair and freckles come from,"['http://gingeridols.com/red-hair-history/', 'https://www.ibdna.co.nz/tests/british-dna-test/', 'https://viralnewsforall.com/2016/11/26/freckled-girls-with-amazing-looks/', 'https://vactruth.com/2016/06/16/infant-died-8-vaccine-doses/', 'https://www.cosmo.ph/beauty/skin/freckle-facts-src-intl-a859-20170519']","The MC1R recessive variant gene that gives people red hair generally results in skin that is unable to tan. Because of the natural tanning reaction to the sun's ultraviolet light and high amounts of pheomelanin in the skin, freckles are a common but not all-inclusive feature of red-haired people. Eighty percent of redheads have an MC1R gene variant.",where does red hair and freckles come from
where did arby's get it's name,"['https://signnn.com/listing-inventory/arbys-absolute-triple-net-property-for-sale-fast-food-tennessee-310-853-1353/', 'https://topfranchise.com/products/arby-s-sandwich-shop-franchise/', 'https://finditsek.com/moneycontrol-ultimate-business-quiz-60-test-knowledge/', 'https://burgersdogspizza.com/tag/fast-food/', 'http://sukahp.com/9367-Maze-Interior-No-Hat-Rack-White-Contemporary-Closet-Storage_Mirrors.html', 'https://find.mapmuse.com/brand/arbys']","Arby's was founded in Boardman, Ohio, on July 23, 1964, by Forrest (1922 -- 2008) and Leroy Raffel, owners of a restaurant equipment business who thought there was a market opportunity for a fast food franchise based on a food other than hamburgers. The brothers wanted to call their restaurants ""Big Tex"", but that name was already used by an Akron business. Instead, they chose the name ""Arby's,"" based on R.B., the initials of Raffel Brothers.",where did arby's get it's name
what are the organs of male reproductive system,"['https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/200545.php', 'https://uzinggo.com/making-sperm-eggs-meiosis/cell-division/life-science', 'https://www.entranceindia.com/entrance/cbse-class-8-science-syllabus/', 'https://animals.jrank.org/pages/316/Amphiumas-Amphiumidae-THREE-TOED-AMPHIUMA-Amphiuma-tridactylum-SPECIES-ACCOUNT.html', 'https://actionlife.org/life-issues/reproductive-technologies/item/159-embryology-inconvenient-facts', 'http://www.radiodhoom.us/tag/how-do-i-get-health-insurance/']","The main male sex organs are the penis and the testicles which produce semen and sperm, which, as part of sexual intercourse, fertilize an ovum in the female's body; the fertilized ovum (zygote) develops into a fetus, which is later born as an infant.",what are the organs of male reproductive system
when do you hear crackles in the lungs,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Crackles.html', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Wheeze', 'http://www.symcat.com/symptoms/abnormal-breathing-sounds', 'https://mpkb.org/home/diseases/sarcoidosis', 'http://policeexpert.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=38858']","Crackles, crepitations, or rales (/ ˈrɑːlz / (listen) RAHLZ or / ˈrælz / RALZ) are the clicking, rattling, or crackling noises that may be made by one or both lungs of a human with a respiratory disease during inhalation. They are often heard only with a stethoscope (""on auscultation""). Bilateral crackles refers to the presence of crackles in both lungs.",when do you hear crackles in the lungs
what is the difference between cardinal and intermediate directions,"['https://upge.wn.com/?from=southasialife.com&pagenum=4&language_id=1&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=south_asia_life', 'https://getawaytips.azcentral.com/what-is-intermediate-directions-12377316.html', 'http://nitasrandomthoughts.info/south-australia/how-to-draw-a-rose-youtubecom-watch-v-wrkkhwjub4.php', 'http://geokov.com/Education/compass-directions-azimuth.aspx', 'https://www.nationalgeographic.org/activity/sun-earth-and-cardinal-directions/', 'https://familypedia.wikia.org/wiki/Grand_Rapids,_Michigan', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Grand_Rapids,_Michigan']","The four cardinal directions or cardinal points are the directions north, east, south, and west, commonly denoted by their initials, N, E, S, W. East and west are at right angles to north and south, with east being in the clockwise direction of rotation from north and west being directly opposite east. Points between the cardinal directions form the points of the compass. The intermediate (intercardinal or ordinal) directions are northeast (NE), southeast (SE), southwest (SW), and northwest (NW). The intermediate direction of every set of intercardinal and cardinal direction is called a secondary-intercardinal direction, the eight shortest points in the compass rose that is shown to the right -- i.e., NNE, ENE, ESE, etc.",what is the difference between cardinal and intermediate directions
what is dte and dce in rs 232,"['http://editsworld.com/rs-232/', 'https://www.gsat.us/support/glossary', 'https://www.codeguru.com/columns/vb/programming-an-rs-232-scale-with-visual-basic.html', 'https://www.futureelectronics.com/c/semiconductors/signal-interface--rs-232', 'http://tokyoexcellia.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=34458', 'http://3sttechnologies.com/course_embedded-systems.php', 'http://infogalactic.com/info/RS-232']","In telecommunications, RS-232, Recommended Standard 232 is a standard introduced in 1960 for serial communication transmission of data. It formally defines the signals connecting between a DTE (data terminal equipment) such as a computer terminal, and a DCE (data circuit-terminating equipment or data communication equipment), such as a modem. The RS-232 standard had been commonly used in computer serial ports. The standard defines the electrical characteristics and timing of signals, the meaning of signals, and the physical size and pinout of connectors. The current version of the standard is TIA-232-F Interface Between Data Terminal Equipment and Data Circuit-Terminating Equipment Employing Serial Binary Data Interchange, issued in 1997.",what is dte and dce in rs 232
who are the characters of entourage based on,"['http://oxylife.blogspot.com/2009/07/watch-entourage-season-6-episode-3.html', 'https://www.buydvdus.com/product-Entourage-Seasons-1-3-DVD-Boxset-1351.html']","According to Mark Wahlberg, Entourage was initially conceived when his assistant asked if he could film Wahlberg and his friends, calling them ""hilarious."" Other reports credit Eric Weinstein, a long-time friend of Wahlberg, with the idea of filming the actor's group of friends. However, according to Donnie Carroll, who was the inspiration for the Turtle character, the idea for a show involving an actor and his friends had come from him. It had originated as a book idea, centered on Carroll's own life and his experiences with Wahlberg, titled From the' Hood to Hollywood, A Soldier's Story.",who are the characters of entourage based on
who composed the music for the dark knight,"['http://mechleybrostents.com/racing/batman-begins-ost-rar.php', 'http://prestigetilecleaners.com/music/the-dark-knight-rises-full-album.php', 'http://legendotel.com/sports-games/the-dark-knight-rises-music-album.php', 'http://mumbaidirectory.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=14153', 'http://www.burningflame.net/2010/10/live-souvenirs-from-mute.html', 'http://digitalmediafx.com/Features/PeterPanReturntoNeverland.html', 'https://www.forcedexposure.com/Catalog/the-kvb-minus-one-lp/AUK.109LP.html']","The Dark Knight: Original Motion Picture Soundtrack is the soundtrack album to the 2008 film of the same name, which is a sequel to Christopher Nolan's 2005 film Batman Begins. The soundtrack was released on July 15, 2008, in three editions: CD, limited edition CD digipak, and digital download. The 2-CD Special Edition was released on December 9, 2008, along with the DVD. A limited edition 180-gram vinyl LP was released on August 12, 2008. The soundtrack was composed by Batman Begins collaborators Hans Zimmer and James Newton Howard and recorded in April 2008.",who composed the music for the dark knight
when did the tuskegee syphilis study start and end,"['https://myamazingdiscoveries.com/category/uncategorized/page/3/', 'https://brickcitylive.com/features/kitta-macpherson/newark-takes-on-alzheimers/', 'https://stewartsynopsis.com/charter-school-experiments/', 'https://cng.ncsu.edu/training-guides/spa-guide/regulatory-compliance/', 'http://copylinemagazine.com/2011/10/28/prostate-cancer-another-tuskegee-experiment/', 'http://www.voicesinbioethics.net/arts-media-in-bioethics/2014/07/03/chronicling-the-tuskegee-syphilis-study-through-art', 'https://caprockrestoration.com/content-restoration/']","The Tuskegee Study of Untreated Syphilis in the Negro Male, also known as the Tuskegee Syphilis Study or Tuskegee Syphilis Experiment (/ tʌsˈkiːɡiː / tus-KEE-ghee) was an infamous clinical study conducted between 1932 and 1972 by the U.S. Public Health Service. The purpose of this study was to observe the natural progression of untreated syphilis in rural African-American men in Alabama under the guise of receiving free health care from the United States government. The study was conducted to understand the disease's natural history throughout time and to also determine proper treatment dosage for specific people and the best time to receive injections of treatments.",when did the tuskegee syphilis study start and end
when was the endangered species act originally passed and what was its purpose,"['https://www.newsgram.com/endangered-species-act/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Habitat', 'https://blog.lauraerickson.com/2014/08/', 'https://www.kauainenehcp.com/esa.html', 'https://bladenonline.com/national-endangered-species-day-third-friday-in-may/', 'https://blogs.umass.edu/natsci397a-eross/recommendations-for-improving-the-delisting-of-species-under-the-endangered-species-act/comment-page-1/', 'http://www.endangered.org/campaigns/protecting-the-endangered-species-act/']","The Endangered Species Act of 1973 (ESA; 16 U.S.C. § 1531 et seq.) is one of the few dozens of US environmental laws passed in the 1970s, and serves as the enacting legislation to carry out the provisions outlined in The Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES). Designed to protect critically imperiled species from extinction as a ""consequence of economic growth and development untempered by adequate concern and conservation"", the ESA was signed into law by President Richard Nixon on December 28, 1973. The U.S. Supreme Court found that ""the plain intent of Congress in enacting"" the ESA ""was to halt and reverse the trend toward species extinction, whatever the cost."" The Act is administered by two federal agencies, the United States Fish and Wildlife Service (FWS) and the Commerce Department's National Marine Fisheries Service (NMFS).",when was the endangered species act originally passed and what was its purpose
what is the story behind cartier love bracelet,"['https://intheircloset.com/tag/bangles', 'http://www.jssirite.com/blog/cartier-love', 'http://www.solitairemagazine.com/portraits-of-valentine/', 'http://www.preetaagarwal.com/jewellery-trends/portraits-of-valentines/', 'http://www.sharkattackfashionblog.com/2014/09/event-cartier-hommage-aux-icones.html', 'https://jewelryindustryinformation.wordpress.com/tag/richard-burton/', 'http://www.amoregioielli.ru/en/suited-to-summer-time-put-on-to-indicate-off-replica-love-cartie-n63/']","Unlike traditional bracelets, which are either wide enough to slip them over the hand onto the wrist or can readily be opened in order to put them on, the Love bracelet is designed to be opened only by using a special screwdriver that is supplied with every bracelet. The screwdriver is also available in the form of a necklace, allowing the bracelet to be ""locked"" onto one person, while the ""key"" is kept around the neck of another, as a symbol for their commitment to their relationship.",what is the story behind cartier love bracelet
who was involved in the battle of marston moor,"['http://www.selbyandainsty.com/constituency/', 'https://fr.scribd.com/document/149763319/English-Civil-War', 'http://www.pureyorkshire.co.uk/yorkshire/listings/l0177.php', 'https://legal-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/Covenanters', 'http://knowledgemasti.com/spooky-lighthouses-around-the-globe/', 'http://www.hddocumentary.com/history-channel-line-of-fire-volume-three-2002-10of12-hannibals-great-triumph/', 'http://bitaboutbritain.com/business-directory/wpbdp_category/battlefields/']","The Battle of Marston Moor was fought on 2 July 1644, during the First English Civil War of 1642 -- 1646. The combined forces of the English Parliamentarians under Lord Fairfax and the Earl of Manchester and the Scottish Covenanters under the Earl of Leven defeated the Royalists commanded by Prince Rupert of the Rhine and the Marquess of Newcastle.",who was involved in the battle of marston moor
what is the red dot on forehead mean,"['http://uptodatenews.in/importance-of-wearing-bindi/', 'http://thehouseofsusanna.blogspot.com/2013/09/', 'http://www.savemymarriagequickly.net/indian-weddings/', 'http://www.fashionncare.com/selena-gomez-bindi-singer-under-fire-for-wearing-bindi-during-mtv.html', 'http://www.stylingstars.com/2017/07/page/3/', 'http://indiaaura.com/india/india-notes/indian-women-dot-on-forehead/', 'https://www.india9.com/i9show/-Assam/Sanskrit-35967.htm']","Traditionally, the area between the eyebrows (where the bindi is placed) is said to be the sixth chakra, ajna, the seat of ""concealed wisdom"". The bindi is said to retain energy and strengthen concentration. The bindi also represents the third eye. The Nasadiya Sukta of the Rig Veda, the earliest known Sanskrit text, mentions the word Bindu.",what is the red dot on forehead mean
what is the income limit for non creamy layer,"['https://www.civilserviceindia.com/subject/Political-Science/notes/statutory-institutions-commissions-national-backward-classes-commission.html', 'https://www.legalresolved.com/indian-kanoon/interesting-read/criteria-for-obc-non-creamy-layer', 'http://msasoi.blogspot.com/2013/05/revision-of-income-criteria-to-exclude.html', 'http://www.tnpscguru.in/2017/09/tnpsc-daily-current-affairs-september-for-group-2a-group-2-group-1-vao-group-4_19.html', 'http://blogs.worldbank.org/endpovertyinsouthasia/does-south-asia-run-risk-rising-inflation', 'https://www.indiainfoline.com/company/nitesh-estates-ltd-egm-balance-sheet/directors-report/28894', 'https://currentaffairs.gktoday.in/cso-releases-provisional-estimates-national-income-financial-year-2013-14-06201413466.html']","The creamy layer (income) criteria were defined as annual family income from all sources more than 100,000 rupees (₹ or INR, together abbreviated Rs 1 lakh) per annum in 1993, and revised to ₹ 2.5 lakh (2004), then ₹ 4.5 lakh (2008), Rs 6 lakh (2013) and Rs 8 lakh (2017). In October 2015, the National Commission for Backward Classes (NCBC) proposed that a person belonging to OBC with an annual family income of up to Rs 15 lakh should be considered as the minimum ceiling for OBC. The NCBC also recommended the sub-division of OBCs into' backward',' more backward', and' extremely backward' blocs and divide 27% quota amongst them in proportion to their population, to ensure that stronger OBCs don't corner the quota benefits.",what is the income limit for non creamy layer
when were seat belts first put in cars,"['http://cms.exchangeandmart.co.uk/safety-and-tech-we-take-for-granted/', 'http://www.cleanairpa.org/methane_reductions_lessons_from_crash_test_dummy', 'http://socalautonews.com/article_SeatBeltTechnology.php']","American car manufacturers Nash (in 1949) and Ford (in 1955) offered seat belts as options, while Swedish Saab first introduced seat belts as standard in 1958. After the Saab GT 750 was introduced at the New York Motor Show in 1958 with safety belts fitted as standard, the practice became commonplace.",when were seat belts first put in cars
meaning of colours in the south african flag,"['http://zafor.org/flagg/', 'https://wikisouthafrica.co.za/south-africa-flag/', 'https://wikisouthafrica.co.za/south-african-national-symbols/', 'http://soweto.imbizotours.co.za/frequently-asked-questions-south-africa/', 'https://www.pakistantoday.com.pk/2011/01/14/cjp-claims-he-stood-ground-against-dictator/', 'http://www.cullimoredutton.co.uk/news', 'https://networth2013.com/nelson-mandela-net-worth/']","Three of the colours -- black, green and yellow -- are found in the flag of the African National Congress. The other three -- red, white and blue -- are used in the modern flag of the Netherlands and the flag of the United Kingdom; the colours white and blue were also found in the old flag of South Africa. Former South African President F.W. de Klerk, who proclaimed the new flag on 20 April 1994, stated in his autobiography, The Last Trek: a New Beginning, that chilli red was chosen instead of plain red (which Anglo-Africans would have preferred) or orange (as Afrikaners would have preferred).",meaning of colours in the south african flag
what is the meaning of iqr in math,"['https://hyperleap.com/topic/Interquartile_range', 'http://www.emcdda.europa.eu/best-practice/treatment/cannabis-users', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=determining+interquartile+range&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir']","In descriptive statistics, the interquartile range (IQR), also called the midspread or middle 50%, or technically H-spread, is a measure of statistical dispersion, being equal to the difference between 75th and 25th percentiles, or between upper and lower quartiles, IQR = Q − Q. In other words, the IQR is the first quartile subtracted from the third quartile; these quartiles can be clearly seen on a box plot on the data. It is a trimmed estimator, defined as the 25% trimmed range, and is the most significant basic robust measure of scale.",what is the meaning of iqr in math
do county judges in texas have to be lawyers,"['https://weberscustominteriors.com/the-texas-judicial-system-the-texas-judicial-system-has-been-called-one-of-the-most-complex-in-the-united-states/', 'http://www.busby-lee.com/bankruptinfoblog/austin-county-court-at-law/', 'https://www.martincountytx.com/154/District-Judge', 'http://www.northamericanfamilylaw.com/expert-directory/michael-busby/', 'https://blog.fordbergner.com/2010/01/', 'http://www.svmblaw.com/summary-appeals.html', 'https://www.farrensheehanlaw.com/2017/11/11/types-of-probate-courts-in-texas/']","County court judges are not required to be licensed attorneys. Due to this, defendants in counties which only have the traditional constitutional county court may ask to have their cases transferred to that county's district court for trial if the district judge consents (1). However, defendants in counties with the county court at law structure do not have this option, as the county court at law judges are required to have law degrees.",do county judges in texas have to be lawyers
what is the concept of day light saving,"['http://harleyportal.info/?newsid=902', 'http://suresuccess.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=8470', 'https://www.change.org/p/province-of-nova-scotia-let-s-save-time-eliminate-the-change', 'https://www.pasoroblesmarathon.com/daylight-savings-usa-history/', 'https://www.rubywilbur.com/day-light-saving-history-usa/', 'https://devblog.dymel.pl/2017/03/30/operating-on-time-utc/', 'https://www.tutusdiary.com/?p=2129']","Daylight saving time (abbreviated DST), commonly referred to as daylight savings time in speech, and known as summer time in some countries, is the practice of advancing clocks during summer months so that evening daylight lasts longer, while sacrificing normal sunrise times. Typically, regions that use daylight saving time adjust clocks forward one hour close to the start of spring and adjust them backward in the autumn to standard time.",what is the concept of day light saving
when were emergency powers used in india and why,"['https://www.newsgram.com/india-is-indira-and-indira-is-india-for-this-slogan-bjp-demands-sorry/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Ahmad_Kutty.html', 'https://socialrol.blogspot.com/2018/06/emergency-in-india.html', 'http://earlytimesnews.com/newsdet.aspx?q=143873', 'http://www.catchnews.com/national-news/emergency-period-should-be-taught-at-educational-institutions-vp-naidu-119627.html', 'https://www.ritiriwaz.com/indira-gandhi-first-female-prime-minister-of-india/', 'https://www.komparify.com/entertainment/tags/hindi-drama-history-movies']","In India, ""the Emergency"" refers to a 21-month period from 1975 to 1977 when Prime Minister Indira Gandhi had a state of emergency declared across the country. Officially issued by President Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed under Article 352 of the Constitution because of the prevailing ""internal disturbance"", the Emergency was in effect from 25 June 1975 until its withdrawal on 21 March 1977. The order bestowed upon the Prime Minister the authority to rule by decree, allowing elections to be suspended and civil liberties to be curbed. For much of the Emergency, most of Gandhi's political opponents were imprisoned and the press was censored. Several other human rights violations were reported from the time, including a forced mass-sterilization campaign spearheaded by Sanjay Gandhi, the Prime Minister's son. The Emergency is one of the most controversial periods of independent India's history.",when were emergency powers used in india and why
which big cat does not have the ability to produce full throated roar,"['http://www.naturetalkies.com/2018/03/03/why-do-we-celebrate-un-world-wildlife-day/', 'https://www.foap.com/image-photo/ars/page-4', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Big_cat', 'http://www.creationwiki.org/Big_cat', 'https://wanttoknowit.com/where-do-leopards-live/', 'https://technology.amis.nl/2018/01/14/the-zoo-programming-languages-named-after-animals/', 'http://www.felineconservation.org/2016_wild_feline_census.html']","The informal term ""big cat"" is typically used to refer to any of the four largest (living) members of the entire Panthera genus. Among the five total species within the Panthera genus, these four are the only cats that are able to roar. In descending order of their maximum potential size, these four species are: tigers, lions, jaguars, and leopards, with the tiger (Panthera tigris) being the largest. A more liberal and expansive definition is sometimes used which may include the snow leopard, puma, clouded leopard, Sunda clouded leopard and / or cheetah, although these added species do not roar.",which big cat does not have the ability to produce full throated roar
what is the story of new god of war,"['https://entertainmentslike.com/6070/god-of-war/', 'http://blog.recovery-android.com/5-must-know-games-2018/', 'https://www.buttondown.tv/gaming/reviews/gamespot-reinventing-god-of-war/', 'https://gameoverpros.com/god-of-war-ps4-cheats/', 'http://acercharger.tk/chow-yun-fat-poker.html', 'http://crocky.tk/casino-enschede-entree.html', 'http://maceonline.tk/banff-casino-resort.html']","God of War is a third-person action-adventure game developed by Santa Monica Studio and published by Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE). Released on April 20, 2018, for the PlayStation 4 (PS4) console, it is the eighth installment in the God of War series, the eighth chronologically, and the sequel to 2010's God of War III. Unlike previous games, which were loosely based on Greek mythology, this game is loosely based on Norse mythology. The main protagonists are Kratos, the former Greek God of War, and his young son Atreus. Following the death of Kratos' second wife and Atreus' mother, they journey to fulfill her promise and spread her ashes at the highest peak of the nine realms. Kratos keeps his troubled past a secret from Atreus, who is unaware of his divine nature. Along their journey, they encounter monsters and gods of the Norse world.",what is the story of new god of war
what is the population of st. john's newfoundland,"['https://addr.ws/st-john-s-newfoundland-and-labrador--stjohns-ca.html', 'https://www.encyclopediavirginia.org/Cities_of_Virginia', 'https://www.justtraveldeals.ca/air-canada-updates-schedule-following-the-grounding-of-the-boeing-737-max-aircraft', 'https://www.northcoastfinancialinc.com/hard-money-lenders-california/', 'http://www.septicinstallationpros.com/middletown-septic-system-services-10940.html', 'https://crosscountrymoversgroup.com/moving-to-or-from-washington-d-c/', 'http://www.illinoishsglorydays.com/id521.html']","Its name has been attributed to the Nativity of John the Baptist, when John Cabot was believed to have sailed into the harbour in 1497 and to a Basque fishing town with the same name. Existing on maps as early as 1519, it is one of the oldest European settlements in North America. It was officially incorporated as a city in 1888. With a metropolitan population of approximately 219,207 (as of July 1, 2017), the St. John's Metropolitan Area is Canada's 20th largest metropolitan area and the second largest Census Metropolitan Area (CMA) in Atlantic Canada, after Halifax.",what is the population of st. john's newfoundland
what do you mean by 32 bit operating system,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/128-bit', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/18-bit', 'https://www.thewebomania.com/blog/difference-between/32-bit-vs-64-bit-os/', 'https://digitalrewards.ihg.com/pt/ebooks/details/537040-64-bit-computing-high-impact-strategies-what-you-need-to-know-definitions-adoptions-impact-benefits-maturity-vendors', 'http://wu-taichi.info/?page_id=10659', 'http://markojevtic.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=2584', 'https://www.seminarsonly.com/IT/Intel-Core-I7-Processor.php']","In computer architecture, 32-bit integers, memory addresses, or other data units are those that are 32 bits (4 octets) wide. Also, 32-bit CPU and ALU architectures are those that are based on registers, address buses, or data buses of that size. 32-bit microcomputers are computers in which 32-bit microprocessors are the norm.",what do you mean by 32 bit operating system
where did slaves in the bahamas come from,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Afro-Barbadian.html', 'http://www.archaeologyantigua.org/index.php/archaeological-background/historical-period', 'http://gen-rise.com/2017/10/', 'https://bmcgenomics.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12864-016-2520-x', 'https://www.polgeonow.com/2017/02/morocco-rejoins-african-union-members-map.html', 'https://www.viejolazaro.com/en/content/4-about-us']","Most of the enslaved Africans brought to The Bahamas were West African. Slaves came from West Central Africa (3,967 Africans), the Bight of Biafra (1,751 Africans), Sierra Leone (1,187 Africans), the Bight of Benin (1,044 Africans), the Windward Coast (1,030 Africans), Senegambia (806 Africans) and from the Gold Coast (484 Africans).",where did slaves in the bahamas come from
why was the pyramid built in front of the louvre,"['https://modernmarvels.in/europe/27-louvre-pyramid', 'https://thearchiblog.wordpress.com/tag/i-m-pei/', 'https://larryrichey.smugmug.com/Black-and-White-Photography', 'https://virtualworldtour.net/louvre-pyramid-paris-france', 'http://www.10things.eu/10-general-facts-about-visiting-the-louvre-museum/', 'https://bclphoto.net/category/cities/paris/', 'https://www.sydspics.com/France/i-D3mGWLX']","Commissioned by the President of France, François Mitterrand, in 1984, it was designed by the architect I.M. Pei. The structure, which was constructed entirely with glass segments and metal poles, reaches a height of 21.6 metres (71 ft). Its square base has sides of 34 metres (112 ft) and a base surface area of 1,000 square metres (11,000 sq ft). It consists of 603 rhombus-shaped and 70 triangular glass segments. The pyramid structure was engineered by Nicolet Chartrand Knoll Ltd. of Montreal (Pyramid Structure / Design Consultant) and Rice Francis Ritchie of Paris (Pyramid Structure / Construction Phase).",why was the pyramid built in front of the louvre
why is coordinated universal time utc and not cut,"['http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/99264', 'http://croftangleart.com/shop/what-is-cut-time-zone.php', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Coordinated_Universal_Time', 'http://www.blogdesignsbydani.com/topic/official-world-time', 'https://www.scribd.com/document/61858653/Radio-Abbreveation', 'https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?53918', 'http://cidadedesaopaulo.com/v2/planeje/guia-pratico/?lang=en']","The official abbreviation for Coordinated Universal Time is UTC. This abbreviation arose from a desire by the International Telecommunication Union and the International Astronomical Union to use the same abbreviation in all languages. English speakers originally proposed CUT (for ""coordinated universal time""), while French speakers proposed TUC (for ""temps universel coordonné""). The compromise that emerged was UTC, which conforms to the pattern for the abbreviations of the variants of Universal Time (UT0, UT1, UT2, UT1R, etc.).",why is coordinated universal time utc and not cut
who introduced the idea of using mass-produced interchangeable parts in manufacturing (points 3),"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Mass_production', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Mass_production', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Decorative_arts']","Crossbows made with bronze parts were produced in China during the Warring States period. The Qin Emperor unified China at least in part by equipping large armies with these weapons, which were equipped with a sophisticated trigger mechanism made of interchangeable parts. Ships of war were produced on a large scale at a moderate cost by the Carthaginians in their excellent harbors, allowing them to efficiently maintain their control of the Mediterranean. The Venetians themselves also produced ships using prefabricated parts and assembly lines many centuries later. The Venetian Arsenal apparently produced nearly one ship every day, in what was effectively the world's first factory which, at its height, employed 16,000 people. Mass production in the publishing industry has been commonplace since the Gutenberg Bible was published using a printing press in the mid-15th century.",who introduced the idea of using mass-produced interchangeable parts in manufacturing (points 3)
legal amount of weed to grow in uk,"['http://relegalize.info/directory/doctors-clinics/countries/uk.shtml', 'https://all-about-cannabis.co.uk/tag/cannabis/', 'http://www.knowcannabis.org.uk/cannabis4/', 'https://www.leafly.com/news/politics/faq-utah-proposition-2-would-legalize-medical-marijuana', 'https://cannabis-seeds-uk-direct.11il.com/', 'http://kmpro.org/british-columbia/how-to-grow-a-weed-plant-outside-uk.php', 'https://www.decisionpointcenter.com/about-us/blog/2018/january/two-new-studies-expose-dangers-of-cannabis-use/']","Cannabis is illegal to possess, grow, distribute or sell in the UK. It is a Class B drug, with penalties for unlicensed dealing, unlicensed production and unlicensed trafficking of up to 14 years in prison, an unlimited fine, or both. The maximum penalty for possession of cannabis is five years in prison and an unlimited fine. A ""Cannabis warning"" can be issued for small amounts of cannabis (generally less than 1 ounce of herbal cannabis, or a slightly higher quantity of hashish) if it is found to be for personal use. This entails the police keeping a record, albeit one which carries no fine and does not show up on standard DBS Check. From 2004 to 2009 it was a Class C drug.",legal amount of weed to grow in uk
73rd amendment to the constitution of india deals with,"['http://jobstpoint.in/up-panchayat-raj-notification-2017-rojgar-sewak/', 'http://www.constructionupdate.com/News/111759', 'http://www.rasexam.com/2010/12/gramsevak-jobs-by-rajasthan-panchayati.html', 'http://www.axewords.com/article/114-panchayati-raj-idealspowers-and-responsibilities-in-indian-system.html', 'https://www.mkgandhi.org/articles/village_development.html', 'http://www.nuevadiplomacia.cl/?p=10600', 'https://sites.google.com/site/panchayatirajup/']","In India, the Panchayati Raj now functions as a system of governance in which gram panchayats are the basic units of local administration. The system has three levels: Gram Panchayat (village level), Mandal Parishad or Block Samiti or Panchayat Samiti (block level), and Zila Parishad (district level). It was formalized in 1992 by the 73rd amendment to the Indian Constitution. Currently, the Panchayati Raj system exists in all states except Nagaland, Meghalaya, and Mizoram, and in all Union Territories except Delhi.",73rd amendment to the constitution of india deals with
when is the full version of h1z1 coming out,"['http://newtorrentgame.com/h1z1-crack-download-pc/', 'https://www.wallpaperpimper.com/entertainment/games/h1z1', 'https://defkey.com/dayz-shortcuts', 'https://milyin.com/creations/509/', 'http://dhua.tk/images-casino-chips.html', 'http://caoliu66.tk/casino-johnstown-pa.html', 'http://123hacks.xmlfile.us/%F0%9F%98%B1fortnite-hack-2018-working-free%F0%9F%98%B1-anti-battleye-%E2%98%91%EF%B8%8F-aimbot-esp-%F0%9F%94%A529-03-2018/']","After three years of being in early access for Microsoft Windows, it officially released as a free-to-play game in February 2018. H1Z1 was released for the PlayStation 4 in August 2018, and will be released for the Xbox One at a later date.",when is the full version of h1z1 coming out
the cast of the kingsman the golden circle,"['http://www.biodatacave.com/2017/09/kingsman-golden-circle-englsh-movie.html', 'http://www.movie2kmovies.com/watch-kingsman-the-golden-circle/', 'https://floridadailypost.com/movie-reviews-kingsman-the-golden-circle/', 'http://www.film-arcade.net/2017/09/kingsman-golden-circle-review-by-tim.html', 'https://www.99hdfilms.com/kingsman-the-golden-circle-hindi-dubbed-movie-2017-torrent/', 'https://www.fxguide.com/featured/bots-and-the-kingsman-at-spi/', 'https://www.mark-heringer.com/2018/12/kingsman-2-golden-circle.html']","Kingsman: The Golden Circle is a 2017 action spy comedy film produced and directed by Matthew Vaughn and written by Vaughn and Jane Goldman. It is a sequel to Kingsman: The Secret Service (2014), which is based on the comic book series Kingsman, created by Dave Gibbons and Mark Millar. The film features Colin Firth, Taron Egerton, Mark Strong, Edward Holcroft, Sophie Cookson, and Hanna Alström reprising their roles from the first film, with Julianne Moore, Halle Berry, Pedro Pascal, Elton John, Channing Tatum, and Jeff Bridges joining the cast. The plot follows the members of Kingsman needing to team up with their American counterpart, Statesman, after the world is held hostage by a new threat.",the cast of the kingsman the golden circle
who has won the most ballon d or,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Deportivo_de_La_Coru%C3%B1a', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Ballon_d%27Or_(1956%E2%80%932009)', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Ballon_d%27Or', 'https://t.guardian.ng/sport/players-capable-of-usurping-lionel-messi-cristiano-ronaldo-in-ballon-dor-titles-race/', 'https://inewsnetwork.net/5283/sports/winner-of-la-liga-2018/', 'http://sokkaa.com/merit-top-5-goalkeepers-who-deserved-to-win-fifa-ballon-dor-award/', 'https://www.gentside.co.uk/football/the-ballon-d-or-2018-votes-have-been-leaked-and-the-results-are-very-surprising_art2105.html']","Stanley Matthews of Blackpool was the inaugural winner of the Ballon d'Or. Prior to 1995, the award was often known in English language media as the European Footballer of the Year award. Milan's George Weah, the only African recipient, became the first non-European to win the award in the year that rules of eligibility were changed. Ronaldo of Internazionale became the first South American winner two years later. Lionel Messi and Cristiano Ronaldo have won the award a record five times each. Three players have won the award three times each: Johan Cruyff of Ajax and Barcelona, Michel Platini of Juventus and Marco van Basten of Milan. With seven awards each, Dutch and German players won the most Ballons d'Or. Spanish club Barcelona has the most winners, with 11 wins.",who has won the most ballon d or
when did the wall street crash start and end,"['https://b2150.gq/a299/', 'https://www.ajc.com/news/national/these-are-the-biggest-stock-market-crashes-history/XAS0qPBaFbTY25OGZV4jXK/', 'https://www.winoverdepression.com/depression-era-stock-market-chart/', 'https://majormike.us/2016/10/29/today-in-history-102916/', 'https://www.timetoast.com/timelines/significant-events-of-the-20th-century--2', 'http://my.timepage.org/?p=1231', 'http://wiki.mises.org/wiki/Wall_Street_Crash_of_1929']","The Wall Street Crash of 1929, also known as the Stock Market Crash of 1929 or the Great Crash, is the stock market crash that occurred in late October, 1929. It started on October 24 (""Black Thursday"") and continued until October 29, 1929 (""Black Tuesday""), when share prices on the New York Stock Exchange collapsed.",when did the wall street crash start and end
was the emancipation proclamation before or after the civil war,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Abraham_Lincoln', 'http://countystation.com/calendar1?mc_id=1379', 'https://majormike.us/2017/01/01/today-in-history-010117/', 'https://majormike.us/2018/01/01/today-in-history-010118/', 'http://bracketts.org/ep-emancipation.htm', 'https://history.stackexchange.com/questions/47686/what-did-the-emancipation-proclamation-exactly-do', 'https://infactcollaborative.com/science/10-interesting-facts-about-the-emancipation-proclamation.html']","The Emancipation Proclamation, or Proclamation 95, was a presidential proclamation and executive order issued by President Abraham Lincoln on January 1, 1863. It changed the federal legal status of more than 3 million enslaved people in the designated areas of the South from slave to free. As soon as a slave escaped the control of the Confederate government, by running away or through advances of federal troops, the slave became legally free. Ultimately, the rebel surrender liberated and resulted in the proclamation's application to all of the designated slaves. It did not cover slaves in Union areas that were freed by state action (or by the 13th amendment in December 1865). It was issued as a war measure during the American Civil War, directed to all of the areas in rebellion and all segments of the executive branch (including the Army and Navy) of the United States.",was the emancipation proclamation before or after the civil war
what is the principle of the gram stain,"['https://pittsburgh-psc.org/lab-report-1/', 'http://www.akshardhool.com/2013/11/a-breakthrough-in-controlling-plastic.html', 'https://www.studymode.com/essays/Gram-Staining-1456177.html', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/gram-stain-procedure-4147683', 'http://blog.microscopeworld.com/2015/06/microscopy-gram-staining.html', 'http://www.emdmillipore.com/PR/en/products/ivd-oem-materials-reagents/microscopy/bacteriology/gram-bacteria-staining/GWCb.qB.DegAAAFAWuhkiQpx,nav', 'https://www.usmslab.com/microbiology-lab-resources-library/microbiology-dictionary/']","Gram stain or Gram staining, also called Gram's method, is a method of staining used to distinguish and classify bacterial species into two large groups (gram-positive and gram-negative). The name comes from the Danish bacteriologist Hans Christian Gram, who developed the technique.",what is the principle of the gram stain
when did the cleveland cavaliers win the nba championship,"['https://christopherpierznik.com/2018/02/01/lebron-has-spoiled-us-with-his-greatness/', 'https://moblog.whmsoft.net/en/Hot_Trends.php?keyword=Blew+a+31&language=english', 'https://wwos.nine.com.au/news/digging-deep-win-or-lose/48b8d3b0-d7ea-453a-944f-d2f34620cc32', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/2016_NBA_Finals.html', 'https://www.championshipringforsale.com/cleveland-cavaliers-2016-national-basketball-gemstone-championship-ring-nban2016', 'http://newarena.com/sports/the-13-scariest-athletes-of-all-time/', 'https://www.portsmouth-dailytimes.com/opinion/389/lebron-james-legacy-is-still-intact']","The win by the Cavaliers was the first major professional sports championship won by a team based in Cleveland since 1964, and the first-ever championship won by the Cavaliers franchise. NBA Finals MVP winner LeBron James propelled the Cavaliers to the historic comeback. James had a historically great Finals performance, becoming the first player in NBA history to lead all players in a playoff series in points, rebounds, assists, steals and blocks. James' heroics coupled with the suspense of Cleveland's comeback have led many sports critics to deem the 2016 NBA Finals as one of the most exciting in recent history.",when did the cleveland cavaliers win the nba championship
why is harley quinn in love with the joker,"['http://movie-info-collection.blogspot.com/2013/06/harley-quinn-dc-comics-character-review.html', 'http://dailycosplay.com/2016/May/11b.html', 'http://www.papercraftsquare.com/batman-harley-quinn-free-paper-toy-download.html', 'https://scarletspidercostume.wordpress.com/tag/harley-quinn-costumes/', 'http://ronveenstra.com/2012/07/the-new-batman-adventures/', 'http://edmontonwargamer.blogspot.com/2015/03/power-legion-phone-booth-fubar.html', 'http://www.misfittoys.net/posts/batman-harley-quinn-and-joker-vynl-figure-2-pack-2/']","Harleen becomes fascinated with the Joker while working at Arkham Asylum and volunteers to help treat him. She falls hopelessly in love with the Joker during their sessions, and she helps him escape from the asylum more than once. When Batman returns a badly injured Joker to Arkham, Harleen dons a jester costume to become Harley Quinn, the Joker's sidekick. The Joker frequently insults, ignores, hurts and even tries to kill Harley, but she always comes back to him, convinced that he truly loves her.",why is harley quinn in love with the joker
where is the us open golf tournament held,['https://www.internationaljet.com/fly-private-charter-to-the-2018-us-golf-open.html'],"The 2018 United States Open Championship was the 118th U.S. Open, held June 14 -- 17 at Shinnecock Hills Golf Club in Shinnecock Hills, New York, about eighty miles (130 km) east of New York City on Long Island; it was the fifth time the U.S. Open was held at this course.",where is the us open golf tournament held
mary of soul she sailed on a day,"['http://amortyzator.tk/skye-boat-song-alto-sax-sheet-music.html', 'https://www.eastnorschool.co.uk/newsletters/friday-29th-march-2019/', 'http://www.celticangelmusic.com/skye-boat/', 'https://rapalje.com/tag/folk-band-music/', 'https://www.europeworldchampionship2014.com/song-lyrics-travel/', 'http://plheineman.net/skyeboat.htm', 'http://www.poparchives.com.au/460/glen-ingram-with-the-hi-five/skye-boat-song']","""The Skye Boat Song"" is a Scottish folk song, which can be played as a waltz, recalling the escape of Prince Charles Edward Stuart (Bonnie Prince Charlie) from Uist to the Isle of Skye after his defeat at the Battle of Culloden in 1746.",mary of soul she sailed on a day
what part of the cow does brisket come from,"['https://cuisinebank.com/smoked-brisket-internal-temp/', 'https://peedbroscorp.com/import/beef/brisket/', 'http://wikirecipedia.com/brisket-will-improve-your-life/', 'https://www.grassfedbeefontario.com/category/BEEF100grassfed/', 'https://www.halalpastures.com/brisket-roast-organic-100-grass-fed/', 'https://www.barrypopik.com/index.php/new_york_city/entry/brisket_taco', 'https://authorericjohnson.com/2014/11/22/cookery-rhymes-the-king-had-a-platter/']","Brisket is a cut of meat from the breast or lower chest of beef or veal. The beef brisket is one of the nine beef primal cuts, though the precise definition of the cut differs internationally. The brisket muscles include the superficial and deep pectorals. As cattle do not have collar bones, these muscles support about 60% of the body weight of standing / moving cattle. This requires a significant amount of connective tissue, so the resulting meat must be cooked correctly to tenderize the connective tissue.",what part of the cow does brisket come from
is the east coast on est or edt,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Eastern_Time_Zone', 'http://pheeds.com/info/guide/d/da/daylight_saving_time.html', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/275416', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1958%E2%80%9359_Connecticut_Huskies_men%27s_basketball_team', 'https://lyonheart.us/articles/understanding-time-zones/', 'https://www.freightwaves.com/news/economics/flashack-friday-extra-daylight-saving-time', 'https://eshelmanlegalgroup.com/daylight-saving-time.php']","The Uniform Time Act of 1966 ruled that daylight saving time would run from the last Sunday of April until the last Sunday in October in the United States. The act was amended to make the first Sunday in April the beginning of daylight saving time as of 1987. The Energy Policy Act of 2005 extended daylight saving time in the United States beginning in 2007. So local times change at 2: 00 a.m. EST to 3: 00 a.m. EDT on the second Sunday in March and return at 2: 00 a.m. EDT to 1: 00 a.m. EST on the first Sunday in November. In Canada, the time changes as it does in the United States.",is the east coast on est or edt
looney tunes is tweety a boy or a girl,"['https://shop.thecircusart.it/product/titty-cat-silvestro/', 'http://ur.fanpop.com/clubs/tweety-bird', 'https://www.cgcreativeshop.com/vectors/free-vectors-download/2543-tweety-looney-tunes-free-vector-download.html', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/animal-looney-tunes-character/', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/characters-should-destroy-tv-set-liv-maddie/', 'http://hi.fanpop.com/clubs/tweety-bird', 'http://id.fanpop.com/clubs/tweety-bird']","Tweety (short for Tweety Pie) is an animated fictional yellow canary in the Warner Bros. Looney Tunes and Merrie Melodies series of animated cartoons. The name ""Tweety"" is a play on words, as it originally meant ""sweetie"", along with ""tweet"" being a typical English onomatopoeia for the sounds of birds. His characteristics are based on Red Skelton's famous ""Mean Widdle Kid."" Tweety appeared in 47 cartoons during the golden age.",looney tunes is tweety a boy or a girl
where did the tradition of knocking on wood come from,"['http://twinpeaks.popapostle.com/html/episodes/Lets-Rock.htm', 'http://oaks.nvg.org/folk-arts.html']","The origin of the custom may be in Germanic folklore, wherein supernatural beings are thought to live in trees, and can be invoked for protection.",where did the tradition of knocking on wood come from
what does the name asher mean in the bible,"['http://revivimen.yhb.org.il/page/3/', 'http://vancehavner.com/biography/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'http://www.thevineyard.org.au/home/vineyard-articles/110-miracle-all-the-way', 'http://www.wogministries.com/rachel-had-it-all-but-was-not-content/', 'http://www.thevineyard.org.au/home/vineyard-articles/360-in-the-beginning', 'https://mwebantu.news/zambia-crossroads-christus-regna-saturnia-regna/', 'https://wn.com/Yaakov_Asher']","The text of the Torah states that the name of Asher means happy / blessing, implying a derivation from the Hebrew term osher in two variations -- beoshri (meaning in my good fortune), and ishsheruni, which textual scholars attribute to different sources -- one to the Yahwist and the other to the Elohist. The Bible states that at his birth Leah exclaimed, ""Happy am I! for the daughters will call me happy: so she called his name Asher,"" meaning happy. (Genesis 30: 13). Some scholars argue that the name of Asher may have to do with a deity originally worshipped by the tribe, either Asherah, or Ashur, the chief Assyrian deity; the latter possibility is cognate with Asher.",what does the name asher mean in the bible
where does nitrogen come from in an ecosystem,"['https://www.gitab.com.np/2018/03/nitrogen-cycle.html', 'https://www.scientistcindy.com/biogeochemical-recycling.html', 'https://ejje.weblio.jp/content/nitrogen+cycle', 'https://www.maximumyield.com/definition/1711/nitrogen-cycle', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Nitrogen_cycle', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Nitrogen_cycle', 'https://www.harunyahya.com/en/books/152365/Atlas-of-Creation-Vol4/chapter/14250/Stromatolites-39-million-year-old-living-marvels-that-refute-the-theory-of-evolution']","The nitrogen cycle is the biogeochemical cycle by which nitrogen is converted into multiple chemical forms as it circulates among the atmosphere, terrestrial, and marine ecosystems. The conversion of nitrogen can be carried out through both biological and physical processes. Important processes in the nitrogen cycle include fixation, ammonification, nitrification, and denitrification. The majority of Earth's atmosphere (78%) is nitrogen, making it the largest source of nitrogen. However, atmospheric nitrogen has limited availability for biological use, leading to a scarcity of usable nitrogen in many types of ecosystems.",where does nitrogen come from in an ecosystem
when does the movie city of lies come out,"['https://www.rap-n-blues.com/city-of-lies-trailer/69347/', 'https://www.b-willis.net/career/films/air-strike-2018/', 'https://www.theislanderonline.com.au/story/5516633/depp-sued-for-allegedly-punching-film-crew/', 'https://1045freshradio.ca/news/4322666/johnny-depp-sued-location-manager/%3C%25=%20song.itunes%20%25%3E/']","City of Lies is an upcoming American biographical crime film directed by Brad Furman and written by Christian Contreras. It is based on the book LAbyrinth by Randall Sullivan, about the murder investigations of Tupac Shakur and The Notorious B.I.G. The film stars Johnny Depp as retired detective LAPD Russell Poole, with Forest Whitaker, Rockmond Dunbar and Neil Brown Jr. also starring. Originally set to be released on September 7, 2018 by Global Road Entertainment, it was pulled off the schedule in August 2018; no new date has been announced.",when does the movie city of lies come out
portrait of an artist as a young man short summary,"['http://s4.pstorrent.org/a-price-below-rubies-%E2%80%93-jewish-women-as-rebels-amp-radicals-cobee/', 'http://www.kindlefreebooks.co.uk/2014/08/portrait-of-artist-as-young-man-by.html', 'https://www.chapters.indigo.ca/en-ca/books/a-portrait-of-the-artist/9788026849865-item.html', 'https://printedmatterhastings.com/2018/12/24/for-those-looking-for-a-special-gift-we-have-signed-copies-of-local-author-jake-arnotts-the-fatal-tree-a-rumbunctious-narrative-of-venery-theft-death-and-a-devil-may-care-braggadocio-its/', 'https://ebooki.swiatczytnikow.pl/ebook/9783962552282,james-joyce--a-portrait-of-the-artist-as-a-young-man-the-pink-classics.html', 'https://uae.souq.com/ae-en/a-portrait-of-the-artist-as-a-young-man-literary-modernism-by-james-joyce-paperback-21338577/i/', 'https://imagenesconfrasestiernas.xyz/book/show/26166703-portrait-of-the-artist-as-a-young-man']","A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man is the first novel by Irish writer James Joyce. A Künstlerroman in a modernist style, it traces the religious and intellectual awakening of young Stephen Dedalus, a fictional alter ego of Joyce and an allusion to Daedalus, the consummate craftsman of Greek mythology. Stephen questions and rebels against the Catholic and Irish conventions under which he has grown, culminating in his self-exile from Ireland to Europe. The work uses techniques that Joyce developed more fully in Ulysses (1922) and Finnegans Wake (1939).",portrait of an artist as a young man short summary
how long did it take to write the australian constitution,"['http://covenersleague.com/component/k2/item/231-australian-constitution-government-high-treason', 'https://www.charteraustralia.org.au/', 'https://www.thecultureconcept.com/australia-day-pursuing-life-liberty-and-happiness-for-all', 'https://www.telanganaa.in/2018/05/ap-panchayat-raj-secretary-recruitment-appsc-jobs.html', 'https://www.ozassignments.com/solution/mlc707-commercial-corporations-law-assessment', 'http://marketshop.ooo/term-paper-writing/page-189-2018-09-09.html', 'https://www.abcassignmenthelp.com/business-law-case-study-examples']","The Constitution of Australia is the supreme law under which the government of the Commonwealth of Australia operates, including its relationship to the States of Australia. It consists of several documents. The most important is the Constitution of the Commonwealth of Australia, which is referred to as the ""Constitution"" in the remainder of this article. The Constitution was approved in a series of referendums held over 1898 -- 1900 by the people of the Australian colonies, and the approved draft was enacted as a section of the Commonwealth of Australia Constitution Act 1900 (Imp), an Act of the Parliament of the United Kingdom.",how long did it take to write the australian constitution
where is the ozark plateau located on a map,"['https://www.spectroom.com/category/171219001-mountains-and-mountain-ranges', 'http://gangsterz.tk/3-million-live-roulette-spins.html', 'http://licert.tk/edc-orlando-time-slots.html', 'http://ivantedesco.tk/boot-hill-casino-new-years-eve.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Mountain', 'http://artedmachado.tk/casino-oneida.html', 'http://bienhoa.tk/casino-innsbruck-moes.html']","The Ozark Plateaus, simply referred to as the Ozarks, are a mountainous region in the U.S. states of Arkansas, Missouri, Oklahoma, and Kansas. The Ozarks cover a significant portion of northern Arkansas and southern Missouri, extending from Interstate 40 in Arkansas to the suburbs of St. Louis. A portion of the Ozarks extends into northeastern Oklahoma and extreme southeastern Kansas.",where is the ozark plateau located on a map
who invented coca cola and why is it called coca cola,"['http://strip349.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=34265', 'https://easyadhd-guide2.info/trademark-global-coca-cola-100th-anniversary-pub-table.aspx', 'http://wstie.eu/02/share-a-coke-online-coupon-code_z4/', 'https://www.abdulaamer.com/top-4-inspiring-digital-marketing-case-studies-2017/', 'https://newfeelthebeat.nl/crawler/36846/green-coke-mechine-142.html', 'http://a-k-b.info/13/1950001-coca-cola-green-before-coloring.html', 'https://artfactory.com/product/vintage-coca-cola-porcelain-sign/']","Coca-Cola, or Coke, is a carbonated soft drink produced by The Coca-Cola Company. Originally intended as a patent medicine, it was invented in the late 19th century by John Pemberton and was bought out by businessman Asa Griggs Candler, whose marketing tactics led Coca-Cola to its dominance of the world soft-drink market throughout the 20th century. The drink's name refers to two of its original ingredients, which were kola nuts (a source of caffeine) and coca leaves. The current formula of Coca-Cola remains a trade secret, although a variety of reported recipes and experimental recreations have been published.",who invented coca cola and why is it called coca cola
what is the lingula and where is it located,['https://www.imaios.com/fr/e-Anatomy/Structures-anatomiques/Ramus-de-la-mandibule'],"The margin of the mandibular foramen is irregular; it presents in front a prominent ridge, surmounted by a sharp spine, the lingula of the mandible which gives attachment to the sphenomandibular ligament; at its lower and back part is a notch from which the mylohyoid groove runs obliquely downward and forward, and lodges the mylohyoid vessels and nerve.",what is the lingula and where is it located
