who did bill goldberg play professional football for,"['https://articlebio.com/bill-goldberg', 'https://www.deseretnews.com/top/1154/30/Cam-Quayle-Tight-End-Weber-State-Football-players-from-Utah-colleges-drafted-to-the-NFL-in-the.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Eric_Ball_(American_football).html', 'http://www.newyorksportsplus.com/2012/08/32-in-32-new-york-jets.html', 'https://www.smarkoutmoment.com/2018/12/from-field-to-ring-5-pro-wrestlers-with.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Bob_Christian.html']","He played for the Los Angeles Rams in the 1990 NFL season, followed by a stint with the CFL Sacramento Gold Miners and Atlanta Falcons from 1992 to 1994. After being cut from the Falcons, in 1995 he was selected by the new expansion team, the Carolina Panthers, in the 1995 NFL expansion draft, but never played a game with the team. He was the first player to have been cut by the Panthers.",who did bill goldberg play professional football for
what degree do you get in med school,"['https://wikimili.com/en/List_of_colleges_and_universities_in_Delaware', 'https://www.k12academics.com/k12-academics-mid-year-report-2016', 'https://www.k12academics.com/national-directories/medical-schools', 'https://www.wisdomjobs.com/e-university/medical-school-interview-questions.html', 'http://www.lake-rescue.org/medical-faculties-in-the-philippines-part-one.html', 'http://zutatensildenafil.com/2017/06', 'http://www.ffaong.com/tag/students']","A medical school is a tertiary educational institution -- or part of such an institution -- that teaches medicine, and awards a professional degree for physicians and surgeons. Such medical degrees include the Bachelor of Medicine, Bachelor of Surgery (MBBS, MBChB, BMBS), Doctor of Medicine (MD), Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO), or Doctor of Podiatric Medicine (DPM). Many medical schools offer additional degrees, such as a Doctor of Philosophy (Ph. D), Master's degree (M.Sc), a physician assistant program, or other post-secondary education.",what degree do you get in med school
what does your iq have to be to get into mensa,"['http://ontheline.com/australian-capital-territory/how-to-tell-if-your-iq-score-is-good.php', 'https://listsurge.com/top-15-toughest-exams-world/', 'https://www.foxnews.com/tech/robots-will-be-100-times-smarter-than-humans-in-30-years-tech-exec-says', 'https://www.test-guide.com/do-you-really-understand-iq-test-scores.html', 'http://www.rationalresponders.com/forum/34152', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Mensa_International.html', 'http://planetcar.net.br/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=4073%3Atop-international-o-tempero-brasileiro-de-lucas-di-grassi&catid=37%3Apelobrasil&limitstart=1']","Mensa's requirement for membership is a score at or above the 98th percentile on certain standardised IQ or other approved intelligence tests, such as the Stanford -- Binet Intelligence Scales. The minimum accepted score on the Stanford -- Binet is 132, while for the Cattell it is 148. Most IQ tests are designed to yield a mean score of 100 with a standard deviation of 15; the 98th-percentile score under these conditions is 130.",what does your iq have to be to get into mensa
when does avergers infinity war come out on dvd,"['https://alchetron.com/Captain-America:-Civil-War', 'http://digitalbits.com/tag/avengers-age-of-ultron-4k', 'http://frontrowfeatures.com/news/avengers-infinity-war-affairs-state-home-entertainment-plus-giveaways-24116.html', 'https://sg.style.yahoo.com/avengers-infinity-war-blu-ray-details-revealed-145246694.html', 'http://www.adventuresbydaddy.com/2018/08/14/avengers-infinity-war-blu-ray/', 'https://www.gamespot.com/gallery/avengers-infinity-war-25-facts-we-learned-from-the/2900-2179/', 'https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/black-panther-premiere-began-a-standing-ovation-1080047']","Avengers: Infinity War was released on digital download by Walt Disney Studios Home Entertainment on July 31, 2018, and on Ultra HD Blu-ray, Blu-ray, and DVD on August 14. The digital and Blu-ray releases include behind-the-scenes featurettes, audio commentary, deleted scenes, and a blooper reel. The digital release also features a roundtable discussion between MCU directors the Russos, Jon Favreau, Joss Whedon, James Gunn, Ryan Coogler, Peyton Reed, and Taika Waititi.",when does avergers infinity war come out on dvd
where was the starting point of the oregon trail,"['http://stahlgluingroller.com/freebooks.php?q=buy-%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B-%D0%BE-%D0%BA%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B8%2C-%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B8-%D0%9A%D1%83%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%8F-%D0%BA%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%B0-%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC%D1%8F%D1%82%D0%B8.html', 'http://wyandottedaily.com/flood-warnings-in-place-for-wyandotte-county-todays-weather-to-be-sunny-and-58/', 'http://www.lustron.org/images/images/ebooks/download-The-Bestseller-Code%3A-Anatomy-of-the-Blockbuster-Novel-2016/', 'http://webmail.vbt.com.br/freebooks.php?q=Network-geeks%3A-how-they-built-the-Internet-2013.html', 'https://lamberttractor.com/']","While the first few parties organized and departed from Elm Grove, the Oregon Trail's primary starting point was Independence, Missouri, or Kansas City (Missouri), on the Missouri River. Later, several feeder trails led across Kansas, and some towns became starting points, including Weston, Missouri, Fort Leavenworth, Kansas, Atchison, Kansas, St. Joseph, Missouri, and Omaha, Nebraska.",where was the starting point of the oregon trail
when did the first horses come to america,"['https://joyofmuseums.com/museums/united-states-of-america/washington-d-c/smithsonian-american-art-museum/historical-objects-and-exhibits-of-the-smithsonian-american-art-museum/buffalo-hunt-on-the-southwestern-prairies-by-john-mix-stanley/', 'http://science-store.com/ga3-domestic/north_american-horses.htm', 'https://ethnology.wordpress.com/category/north-american-tribescultures/cheyenne/', 'https://www.mbequineservices.com/dietary-changes-and-the-evolution-of-the-horse/', 'http://tracks.endurance.net/2017/10/', 'https://www.animalfactsencyclopedia.com/Mustang-horse.html']","The horse evolved in the Americas, but became extinct between 8,000 and 12,000 years ago. When the Spanish arrived on the American mainland in the 16th century, they brought horses with them and re-established the animals on the continent.",when did the first horses come to america
when is the jetsons supposed to take place,"['https://unitedparamountnetworkupn.fandom.com/wiki/The_Jetsons', 'http://www.timescaribbeanonline.com/nevis-has-a-date-with-geothermal-energy/', 'http://blog.acpinternist.org/2013/02/rosie-reincarnated.html', 'http://ebook4rent.tw/jet-screamer-voice.html']","The Jetsons are a family residing in Orbit City. The city's architecture is rendered in the Googie style, and all homes and businesses are raised high above the ground on adjustable columns. George Jetson lives with his family in the Skypad Apartments: his wife Jane is a homemaker, their teenage daughter Judy attends Orbit High School, and their son Elroy attends Little Dipper School. Housekeeping is seen to by a robot maid, Rosie, which handles chores not otherwise rendered trivial by the home's numerous push-button Space Age-envisioned conveniences. The family has a dog named Astro, that like Scooby Doo talks with an initial consonant mutation in which every word begins with an ""R"", as if speaking with a growl.",when is the jetsons supposed to take place
what is lagging and leading power factor in generator,['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Power_factor.html'],"There is also a difference between a lagging and leading power factor. The terms refer to whether the phase of the current is leading or lagging the phase of the voltage. A lagging power factor signifies that the load is inductive, as the load will ""consume"" reactive power, and therefore the reactive component Q (\ displaystyle Q) is positive as reactive power travels through the circuit and is ""consumed"" by the inductive load. A leading power factor signifies that the load is capacitive, as the load ""supplies"" reactive power, and therefore the reactive component Q (\ displaystyle Q) is negative as reactive power is being supplied to the circuit.",what is lagging and leading power factor in generator
when does a cure for wellness come out,['http://www.hdland.in/%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%84%D9%88%D8%AF-%D9%81%DB%8C%D9%84%D9%85-miss-peregrines-home-for-peculiar-children-2016/'],"The film premiered on December 10, 2016, at the Butt-Numb-A-Thon Film Festival in Austin, Texas, and was theatrically released in the United States on February 17, 2017, by 20th Century Fox, after initially being slated for September 23, 2016.",when does a cure for wellness come out
who wrote the song the house of the rising sun,"['https://www.spectroom.com/daily/07-13/all', 'http://tokumei10.blogspot.com/2019/02/16louis-xvi.html', 'http://amortyzator.tk/ho-lee-sheet-metal-nashville.html', 'https://chrisnole.com/house-of-the-rising-sun-sheet-music', 'https://www.eurohitlist.eu/category/hot-100-number-one-singles-of-1964/', 'https://www.mangore.com/house-of-the-rising-sun-1-5-266', 'http://alldylan.com/tag/the-songs-he-didnt-write/']","""The House of the Rising Sun"" is a traditional folk song, sometimes called ""Rising Sun Blues"". It tells of a life gone wrong in New Orleans; many versions also urge a sibling to avoid the same fate. The most successful commercial version, recorded in 1964 by British rock group the Animals, was a number one hit on the UK Singles Chart and also in the United States and France. As a traditional folk song recorded by an electric rock band, it has been described as the ""first folk-rock hit"".",who wrote the song the house of the rising sun
what states do not collect sales tax from amazon,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Amazon_tax.html', 'https://www.cnbc.com/2017/06/28/despite-president-trumps-tweet-amazon-already-collects-sales-taxes.html', 'https://www.forbes.com/sites/kellyphillipserb/2017/03/27/tax-free-no-more-amazon-to-begin-collecting-sales-tax-nationwide-on-april-1/', 'https://www.lasvegasbookkeeping.com/blog/tag/Amazon', 'https://www.taxpolicycenter.org/daily-deduction/who-knew-tax-reform-could-be-so-complicated', 'https://www.inetstart.com/how-to-obtain-your-sales-tax-license-resellers-license.html', 'http://twru.com/newsletters/september-2017-newsletter/']","Many U.S. states have passed online shopping sales tax laws designed to compel Amazon.com and other e-commerce retailers to collect state and local sales taxes from its customers. Amazon.com originally collected sales tax only from five states as of 2011, but as of April 2017 collects sales taxes from customers in all 45 states that have a state sales tax and in Washington, D.C. Amazon does not collect sales taxes from Alaska, Delaware, Montana, New Hampshire, and Oregon, since those states do not have state sales taxes. Additionally, approximately half of all Amazon.com purchases are sold on the Amazon Marketplace through 3rd-party vendors, and these purchases remain free of tax except for in Washington state, where these purchases (starting in 2018) are now taxed.",what states do not collect sales tax from amazon
when did life in the uk test start,['http://www.professional-tutors.org.uk/life-in-the-uk-test'],"A pass in the test fulfils the requirements for ""sufficient knowledge of life in the United Kingdom"" which were introduced for naturalisation on 1 November 2005 and which were introduced for settlement on 2 April 2007. It simultaneously fulfils the language requirement by demonstrating ""a sufficient knowledge"" of the English language.",when did life in the uk test start
who came up with the 12 principles of animation,"['https://forums.newtek.com/archive/index.php/t-157007.html?s=2632fb09e9e7e6200ca1494656b1805a', 'http://koolcapture.com/glossary', 'https://raphaeloo.com/the-12-principles-of-animation/', 'https://www.suryadatta.org/institutes/animation-and-multimedia-college-in-pune.html', 'http://golfari.com/western-australia/how-to-make-movement-more-natural-after-effects.php', 'http://thepignextdoor.com/new-south-wales/illusion-of-life-pdf-download.php', 'https://www.fattypepper.com/best-way-to-export-animation-in-blender/']","Disney's Twelve Basic Principles of Animation were introduced by the Disney animators Ollie Johnston and Frank Thomas in their 1981 book The Illusion of Life: Disney Animation. Johnston and Thomas in turn based their book on the work of the leading Disney animators from the 1930s onwards, and their effort to produce more realistic animations. The main purpose of the principles was to produce an illusion of characters adhering to the basic laws of physics, but they also dealt with more abstract issues, such as emotional timing and character appeal.",who came up with the 12 principles of animation
in the middle east during neolithic times the development of agriculture brought about,"['http://www.scienceforums.com/topic/28780-are-we-too-dependent-on-technology/page-2', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Neolithic_Revolution', 'http://atlantipedia.ie/samples/archive-3344/', 'https://sites.google.com/site/1ancientcivilizationsforkids/ancient-iraq-mesopotamia']","These developments, sometimes called the Neolithic package, provided the basis for centralized administrations and political structures, hierarchical ideologies, depersonalized systems of knowledge (e.g. writing), densely populated settlements, specialization and division of labour, more trade, the development of non-portable art and architecture, and property ownership. The earliest known civilization developed in Sumer in southern Mesopotamia (c. 6,500 BP); its emergence also heralded the beginning of the Bronze Age.",in the middle east during neolithic times the development of agriculture brought about
what do the winners of the nobel prize get,"['http://mathisfunforum.com/viewtopic.php?id=24036&amp;p=13', 'https://pasmov.com/wiki/nobel-prizes/', 'https://worldinshort.com/nobel-prize-winners-2017/', 'http://uskings.us/news/usa-awards-academy/uskings-top-100-famous-award-in-us-p-01-nobel-prize', 'http://why-not.com/prince-edward-island/nobel-prize-winners-list-pdf-with-photo.php', 'https://sttialphakappa.org/gerd-blobel-email/', 'http://raphd.com/saskatchewan/nobel-prize-winners-2014-list-pdf.php']","Between 1901 and 2018, the Nobel Prizes (and the Prizes in Economic Sciences, from 1969 on) were awarded 590 times to 935 people and organizations. With some receiving the Nobel Prize more than once, this makes a total of 27 organizations and 908 individuals. The prize ceremonies take place annually in Stockholm, Sweden (with the exception of the Peace Prize ceremony, which is held in Oslo, Norway). Each recipient (known as a ""laureate"") receives a gold medal, a diploma, and a sum of money that has been decided by the Nobel Foundation. (As of 2017, each prize is worth 9,000,000 SEK, or about US $1,110,000, € 944,000, £ 836,000 or ₹ 73,800,000.) Medals made before 1980 were struck in 23 carat gold, and later in 18 carat green gold plated with a 24 carat gold coating.",what do the winners of the nobel prize get
why is crop rotation considered a good agricultural practice,"['http://www.tanakafarms.com/responsible-methods/', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/history-of-agriculture-and-farm-machinery-4074382', 'https://blog.sanhedrinnursery.com/2010/04/', 'https://doctorgardening.com/organic-gardening/', 'https://www.annabel-langbein.com/annabel/blog/crop-rotation/', 'https://www.goodsweetearth.com/blog/record-amount-of-crop-losses-in-2012bad-soil-practices-to-blame', 'https://www.onegreenplanet.org/animalsandnature/monoculture-crops-environment/']","Growing the same crop in the same place for many years in a row (monocropping) disproportionately depletes the soil of certain nutrients. With rotation, a crop that leaches the soil of one kind of nutrient is followed during the next growing season by a dissimilar crop that returns that nutrient to the soil or draws a different ratio of nutrients. In addition, crop rotation mitigates the buildup of pathogens and pests that often occurs when one species is continuously cropped, and can also improve soil structure and fertility by increasing biomass from varied root structures.",why is crop rotation considered a good agricultural practice
why is the super bowl trophy vince lombardi,"['http://blog.gospikes.com/?m=201502', 'https://blog.ticketcity.com/nfl/super-bowl/super-bowl-history/', 'https://rethinkreport.com/2017/02/02/thursday-thoughts-on-leadership-winning-is-a-habit/', 'https://www.convert-unix-timestamp.com/unixtime/948127036', 'https://fs64sports.blogspot.com/2014_12_13_archive.html', 'https://ux.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/01/25/new-york-sports-championship-droughts-yankees-mets-giants-jets-devils-knicks-nets-rangers-islanders/2642705002/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/1970_Baltimore_Colts_season.html']","Even though it is a national tournament, the award was initially inscribed with the words ""World Professional Football Championship"". It was officially renamed in 1970 in memory of NFL head coach Vince Lombardi, after his death from cancer. It was thus presented for the first time as the Vince Lombardi Trophy in Super Bowl V when the Baltimore Colts defeated the Dallas Cowboys 16-13. It has also been referred to as the ""Tiffany Trophy"" after the Tiffany & Co.",why is the super bowl trophy vince lombardi
what is the definition of a romantic date,"['https://veerpay.com/payment-gateway-solutions-for-dating/', 'http://4599.info/singles-dating-holidays.html', 'http://5092.info/matchmaker-dating-tips.htm', 'http://ayakbilegiprotezi.com/cat7/how-to-write-a-personal-statement-for-dating-site.html', 'https://www.samusicnews.co.za/local-music/cape-town-indie-rockers-mobbing-bali-release-video-latest-single/', 'http://www.lacueillettedequinsac.com/uncomplicated-secrets-in-mingle-2-across-the-uk-2/', 'http://www.wilispersadautama.com/category/ladadate/']","Dating is a stage of romantic relationships in humans whereby two people meet socially with the aim of each assessing the other's suitability as a prospective partner in an intimate relationship or marriage. It is a form of courtship, consisting of social activities done by the couple, either alone or with others. The protocols and practices of dating, and the terms used to describe it, vary considerably from country to country and over time. While the term has several meanings, the most frequent usage refers to two people exploring whether they are romantically or sexually compatible by participating in dates with the other. With the use of modern technology, people can date via telephone or computer or meet in person.",what is the definition of a romantic date
who played katniss everdeen in the hunger games,"['https://hellomystar.com/jennifer-lawrence.html', 'https://www.kidzworld.com/article/25435-jennifer-lawrence-bio', 'http://pix.realinfo.tv/2018/04/jennifer-lawrence.html', 'https://celebcenter.net/jennifer-lawrence-wiki-biography-age-net-worth-oscar-husband/', 'https://tony88.blog/louisonurmark/21015/', 'http://celebritiesphotos.net/jennifer-lawrence-american-actress-oscar-winner-pictures/', 'https://entertainment.ava360.com/jennifer-lawrence-filmography-through-the-years-before-and-now_3ff64263f.html']","Lawrence's fame continued to grow with her starring role as Katniss Everdeen in the Hunger Games film series (2012 -- 2015), which established her as the highest-grossing action heroine of all time. She went on to earn various accolades for her collaborations with director David O. Russell. Her performance as a depressed and bipolar widow in the romance film Silver Linings Playbook (2012) earned her an Academy Award for Best Actress, making her the second-youngest winner of the award. Lawrence subsequently won a BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for playing a troubled wife in the black comedy American Hustle (2013). She also received Golden Globe Awards for her roles in both of these films and for her performance as Joy Mangano in the biopic Joy (2015).",who played katniss everdeen in the hunger games
where is the country of belize on a map,"['http://www.prudentdubai.com/belize.html', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/belize', 'http://xpertise.co.in/America/Columbus%20Central%20University', 'https://www.flyfishbonehead.com/map/belize/', 'https://www.tkofarms.com/about-belize/', 'https://francobollidelmondo.blogspot.com/2012/05/bird-stamps-from-belize.html', 'http://commcourses.com/www/index.php/belize']","Belize (/ bəˈliːz / (listen)), formerly British Honduras, is an independent country on the eastern coast of Central America. Belize is bordered on the north by Mexico, on the south and west by Guatemala, and on the east by the Caribbean Sea. Its mainland is about 290 km (180 mi) long and 110 km (68 mi) wide.",where is the country of belize on a map
