when did the eagles last win the super bowl,"['https://tattoodesignpic.info/nike-oakland-raiders-black-sideline-elite-coaches-team-color-performance-polo.htm', 'https://comset.info/nike-philadelphia-phillies-red-true-big-apple-snapback-adjustable-hat.asp', 'https://thenflgame.com/', 'https://printflyers.info/new-era-philadelphia-eagles-green-2017-nfl-draft-on-stage-39thirty-flex-hat.php', 'https://majorleaguepets.com/blogs/coach-johns-corner/pre-season-top-ten-nfl-teams-and-the-gear-to-cheer-2018-major-league-pets', 'https://submitastory.info/nike-paul-worrilow-atlanta-falcons-red-game-patch-jersey.html', 'https://famouslinersonline.info/nike-philadelphia-phillies-gray-elite-half-zip-pullover-jacket.htm']","The Philadelphia Eagles are a professional American football franchise based in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. The Eagles compete in the National Football League (NFL) as a member club of the league's National Football Conference (NFC) East division. They are Super Bowl champions, having won Super Bowl LII; their first Super Bowl in franchise history, and their fourth NFL title overall, after winning the Championship Game in 1948, 1949, and 1960.",when did the eagles last win the super bowl
what is the difference between bat mitzvah and bar mitzvah,"['https://bnlk.info/adult-matchmaking-salvador.htm', 'https://arnoldzwicky.org/2018/03/24/three-saturday-lingtoons/', 'https://yaiy.org/Magazine/articles/1205speaking.html', 'https://www.inspectd.com/h7gvwog479/post-why-you-should-168977.html', 'http://www.balloonssoundgreat.com/', 'https://interclubbrescia.com/government/', 'http://www.desmondgv.com/banquets/bar-bat-mitzvah-packages/bar-mitzvah-israel/']","Bar Mitzvah (Hebrew: בַּר מִצְוָה ‬) is a Jewish coming of age ritual for boys. Bat Mitzvah (Hebrew: בַּת מִצְוָה ‬; Ashkenazi pronunciation: Bas Mitzvah) is a Jewish coming of age ritual for girls. The plural is B'nai Mitzvah for boys, and B'not Mitzvah (Ashkenazi pronunciation: B'nos Mitzvah) for girls.",what is the difference between bat mitzvah and bar mitzvah
when does the school year end in america,"['https://schoolholiday.co.za/', 'https://www.aubergedegevrieux.com/where-to-vacation-in-march-in-united-states/', 'http://rabota24corp.com/topic-4001.html', 'https://www.oldorchardparkcampground.com/easter-school-holidays-england/', 'https://owlcation.com/humanities/What-is-Darwin-Day-and-Why-Is-It-Celebrated', 'http://bestdownloads.onlinewebshop.net/practicals_in_physical_chemistry_ebook_download/', 'http://owjn.org/19446-tools-to-help-write-an-essay/']","In the United States, the academic year typically has about 180 school days for K-12, running from the early (Northern Hemisphere) fall to early summer. Colleges and universities often have shorter years. School holidays (also referred to as vacations, breaks, and recess) are the periods during which schools are closed.",when does the school year end in america
when did little red riding hood come out,"['https://thegenealogyofstyle.wordpress.com/tag/pescucci/', 'http://www.factbites.com/topics/Red-Riding-Hood', 'http://boj.pntic.mec.es/~jmarto1/01tradicion-oral/tradicionoral.html', 'http://storylovers.net/a-tale-of-werewolf-the-gray-wolf-fantasy-legend-audiobook/', 'https://malikuvhnusadech.eu/red-riding-hood-schauspieler.html', 'https://video-divertenti.eu/red-ridding-hood.html', 'https://coursing-club-cote-amour.eu/red-riding-hood-schauspieler.html']","The origins of the Little Red Riding Hood story can be traced to versions from various European countries and more than likely preceding the 17th century, of which several exist, some significantly different from the currently known, Grimms-inspired version. It was told by French peasants in the 10th century and recorded by the cathedral schoolmaster Egbert of Liege. In Italy, the Little Red Riding Hood was told by peasants in the fourteenth century, where a number of versions exist, including La finta nonna (The False Grandmother), written among others by Italo Calvino in the Italian Folktales collection. It has also been called ""The Story of Grandmother"". It is also possible that this early tale has roots in very similar East Asian tales (e.g. ""Grandaunt Tiger"").",when did little red riding hood come out
what is the stock market in the great depression,"['https://majormike.us/2016/10/29/today-in-history-102916/', 'https://beyondtheflow.wordpress.com/tag/christianity/', 'https://www.ajc.com/news/national/these-are-the-biggest-stock-market-crashes-history/XAS0qPBaFbTY25OGZV4jXK/', 'https://www.open.edu/openlearn/money-business/personal-finance/timeline-financial-services', 'https://www.dailynewsmagazine.in/category/business/feed/', 'https://www.betterblockokc.com/did-the-stock-market-crash-cause-the-great-depression/', 'http://eon-agraphashin.gq/bbbs/long-term-causes-of-great-depression-jul.php']","The Wall Street Crash of 1929, also known as Black Tuesday (October 29), the Great Crash, or the Stock Market Crash of 1929, began on October 24, 1929 (""Black Thursday""), and was the most devastating stock market crash in the history of the United States, when taking into consideration the full extent and duration of its after effects. The crash, which followed the London Stock Exchange's crash of September, signalled the beginning of the 12-year Great Depression that affected all Western industrialized countries.",what is the stock market in the great depression
how much money does the world series of poker winner get,"['http://us.playstation.com/ps3/shows-and-tv-series/world-series-of-poker.html', 'http://downloadapkinstaller.com/slots/80683-world-series-of-poker.html', 'http://downloadapkinstaller.com/58025-play-online-poker-with-world-series-of.html', 'http://myshoplah.com/2019/01/san-marco-bracelet-14k/', 'https://www.pokerhands.poker/wsop-world-series-poker-tournaments/', 'http://www.web-site-test.com/special-promo/', 'http://gero-spa.info/viewtopic.php?t=47241']","The winner of each event receives a World Series of Poker bracelet and a monetary prize based on the number of entrants and buy-in amounts. Over the years, the tournament has grown in both the number of events and in the number of participants. Each year, the WSOP culminates with the $10,000 no-limit hold'em ""Main Event,"" which, since 2004, has attracted entrants numbering in the thousands. The victor receives a multi-million dollar cash prize and a bracelet, which has become the most coveted award a poker player can win. The winner of the World Series of Poker Main Event is considered to be the World Champion of Poker.",how much money does the world series of poker winner get
where is the middle ear located in the skull,"['https://www.anatomynext.com/middle-ear', 'http://bsrhospitals.com/ossiculoplasty', 'http://en.creationwiki.org/Ears', 'https://www.emedicinehealth.com/image-gallery/ear_picture/images.htm', 'http://simplyknowledge.com/popular/gk_detail/ears', 'https://hullhearing.com/services', 'http://beecohearing.com/Home/Hearing']","The middle ear is the portion of the ear internal to the eardrum, and external to the oval window of the inner ear. The mammalian middle ear contains three ossicles, which transfer the vibrations of the eardrum into waves in the fluid and membranes of the inner ear. The hollow space of the middle ear is also known as the tympanic cavity and is surrounded by the tympani bone. The auditory tube (also known as the Eustachian tube or the pharyngotympanic tube) joins the tympanic cavity with the nasal cavity (nasopharynx), allowing pressure to equalize between the middle ear and throat.",where is the middle ear located in the skull
the significance of the cross of gold speech was that,"['http://thepandorasociety.com/july-9th-1896-silver-vs-gold/', 'http://unitedyam.com/cross-gold-speech-word-cloud-william-j-bryan/', 'https://www.naqt.com/you-gotta-know/modern-speeches.html', 'http://hhfo.weebly.com/the-blog/this-week-in-history-7-13-july', 'https://theimaginativeconservative.org/2015/07/cross-of-gold-speech.html', 'http://www.themoneymasters.com/the-wonderful-wizard-of-oz-a-monetary-reformers-brief-symbol-glossary/']","The Cross of Gold speech was delivered by William Jennings Bryan, a former United States Representative from Nebraska, at the Democratic National Convention in Chicago on July 9, 1896. In the address, Bryan supported bimetallism or ""free silver"", which he believed would bring the nation prosperity. He decried the gold standard, concluding the speech, ""you shall not crucify mankind upon a cross of gold"". Bryan's address helped catapult him to the Democratic Party's presidential nomination; it is considered one of the greatest political speeches in American history.",the significance of the cross of gold speech was that
when do senate elections take place and who votes for them,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1960_Republican_National_Convention', 'http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/United_States_Senate', 'https://aizmanlaw.com/civics-government-kids-lessons-activities-guides/', 'https://www.arlingtoncardinal.com/category/politics/political-maps/senate/', 'http://footwww.academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/United_States_Senate', 'https://www.scottbradford.us/2016/11/03/the-congressional-district-method/', 'https://everipedia.org/wiki/lang_en/United_States_Senate/']","The composition and powers of the Senate are established by Article One of the United States Constitution. The Senate is composed of senators, each of whom represents a single state in its entirety, with each state being equally represented by two senators, regardless of its population, serving staggered terms of six years; with 50 states currently in the Union, there are 100 U.S. Senators. From 1789 until 1913, Senators were appointed by legislatures of the states they represented; following the ratification of the Seventeenth Amendment in 1913, they are now popularly elected. The Senate chamber is located in the north wing of the Capitol, in Washington, D.C.",when do senate elections take place and who votes for them
where does the term friday the 13th come from,"['https://ucanr.edu/blogs/bugsquad/index.cfm?tagname=tropical%20milkweed', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Common_year_starting_on_Thursday', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Friday_the_13th', 'http://www.differencebetween.net/miscellaneous/difference-between-halloween-and-friday-the-13th/', 'https://masterflex-ukblog.com/author/masterflexblogger/', 'https://www.giftemporium.co.za/blogs/gift-emporium-has-lauched/friday-the-13th', 'http://m-byte.tk/men-dating-in-your-30s.html']","Friday the 13th is considered an unlucky day in Western superstition. It occurs when the 13th day of the month in the Gregorian calendar falls on a Friday, which happens at least once every year but can occur up to three times in the same year. In 2017, it occurred twice, on January 13 and October 13. There will be two Friday the 13ths per year until 2020, where 2021 and 2022 will have just one occurrence.",where does the term friday the 13th come from
what is the definition of the word bible,"['https://fineartamerica.com/featured/bible-andrea-anderegg.html?product=tapestry', 'https://en.m.wikisource.org/wiki/New_Testament', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Holy_Bible.html', 'http://e-library.net/Spirituality.htm', 'https://thereisnodebt.wordpress.com/2016/01/22/poland-terrorism-obedience-sustainable-development-the-loss-of-freedoms-for-the-people-of-the-world-and-the-simple-solution-part-iv/', 'https://www.catholicireland.net/glossary-of-terms/', 'http://thegenesisrevelation.com/']","The Bible (from Koine Greek τὰ βιβλία, tà biblía, ""the books"") is a collection of sacred texts or scriptures that Jews and Christians consider to be a product of divine inspiration and a record of the relationship between God and humans.",what is the definition of the word bible
where does the rodriguez last name come from,"['https://wn.com/Scott_Rodrigues', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/rodriguez-last-name-meaning-and-origin-1422604']","The ""ez"" signifies ""son of"". The name Rodrigo is the Spanish form of Roderick, meaning ""famous power"", from the Germanic elements ""hrod"" (fame) and ""ric"" (power). It was the name of Roderic, the last Visigothic King before the Muslim conquest, and the subject of many legends. The surname Rodríguez could have originated in the 9th century when patronymic names originated.",where does the rodriguez last name come from
what is the purpose of the map sensor,"['http://bavariandominator.co.uk/pages/map_sensors_123861.cfm', 'https://www.autocodes.com/p0107_jaguar.html', 'http://utamosynamahu.gq/a8df37692034b.html', 'http://cupoyydyvagocov.ml/c82216ae7092.html', 'https://mechanicbase.com/engine/map-sensor-symptoms/', 'http://withoutannette.net/australian-capital-territory/how-to-fix-mass-air-flow-sensor.php', 'http://portaldelfreelancer.com/Pennsylvania/jeep-error-code-p0108.html']","Engines that use a MAP sensor are typically fuel injected. The manifold absolute pressure sensor provides instantaneous manifold pressure information to the engine's electronic control unit (ECU). The data is used to calculate air density and determine the engine's air mass flow rate, which in turn determines the required fuel metering for optimum combustion (see stoichiometry) and influence the advance or retard of ignition timing. A fuel-injected engine may alternatively use a mass airflow sensor (MAF sensor) to detect the intake airflow. A typical naturally aspirated engine configuration employs one or the other, whereas forced induction engines typically use both; a MAF sensor on the intake tract pre-turbo and a MAP sensor on the charge pipe leading to the throttle body.",what is the purpose of the map sensor
who's life is a star is born based on,"['https://www.eventsinuk.net/10-05-2019-joshua-bradley-outdoor-cinema-season-3828811', 'https://bbomovies.com/movie/a-star-is-born/', 'http://www.kentwell.co.uk/events/evening/open-air-cinema-star-born', 'http://freeaddon.com/a-star-is-born-hd-wallpapers-new-tab-themes/', 'https://www.vinylrecords.sg/shop/a-star-is-born-original-soundtrack/', 'https://films4tenby.wordpress.com/2019/03/21/a-star-is-born-on-april-2nd-7-30pm-at-the-de-valence/', 'https://www.gaurvx.com/a-star-is-born-movie-download/']","A Star Is Born is a 2018 American music-themed romantic drama film produced and directed by Bradley Cooper (in his directorial debut) and written by Cooper, Eric Roth and Will Fetters. A remake of the 1937 film of the same name, it stars Cooper, Lady Gaga, Andrew Dice Clay, Dave Chappelle, and Sam Elliott, and follows a hard-drinking musician (Cooper) who discovers and falls in love with a young singer (Gaga). It marks the fourth remake of the original 1937 film, after the 1954 musical, the 1976 rock musical and the 2013 Bollywood romance film.",who's life is a star is born based on
virtual pc download for windows 10 64 bit,"['http://honwk.info/news.php?action=show&id=35555', 'http://wwebb.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=36514', 'http://categorykiller.info/?page_id=36678', 'http://aslsocial.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=24474', 'http://nutraburn10.info/viewtopic.php?t=4188', 'http://portekizce.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=11304', 'http://ozekiphone.com/voip-ozeki-phone-system-xe-in-virtualized-systems-185.html']","Windows Virtual PC (successor to Microsoft Virtual PC 2007, Microsoft Virtual PC 2004, and Connectix Virtual PC) is a virtualization program for Microsoft Windows. In July 2006 Microsoft released the Windows version as a free product. In August 2006, Microsoft announced the Macintosh version would not be ported to Intel-based Macintosh computers, effectively discontinuing the product as PowerPC-based Macintosh computers are no longer manufactured. The newest release, Windows Virtual PC, does not run on versions of Windows earlier than Windows 7, and does not officially support MS-DOS or operating systems earlier than Windows XP Professional SP3 as guests. The older versions, which support a wider range of host and guest operating systems, remain available. Starting with Windows 8, Hyper-V supersedes Windows Virtual PC.",virtual pc download for windows 10 64 bit
who did korea fight in the korean war,"['https://mediadrumworld.com/2017/07/05/10287/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/06-25/all', 'https://mediadrumworld.com/2019/04/10/korean-war-colourised/', 'https://navy.togetherweserved.com/usn/servlet/tws.webapp.WebApp?cmd=SBVTimeLine&type=Person&ID=541629', 'https://navy.togetherweserved.com/usn/servlet/tws.webapp.WebApp?cmd=ShadowBoxProfile&type=BattleMemoryExt&ID=216465', 'https://pvtimes.com/news/pahrump-area-veterans-offer-insights-on-u-s-north-korean-summit/', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-ushistory/chapter/the-korean-war/']","The Korean War (in South Korean Hangul: 한국 전쟁; Hanja: 韓國 戰爭; RR: Hanguk Jeonjaeng, ""Korean War""; in North Korean Chosŏn'gŭl: 조국 해방 전쟁; Hancha: 祖國 解放 戰爭; MR: Choguk haebang chǒnjaeng, ""Fatherland Liberation War""; 25 June 1950 -- 27 July 1953) was a war between North Korea (with the support of China and the Soviet Union) and South Korea (with the principal support of the United States). The war began on 25 June 1950 when North Korea invaded South Korea following a series of clashes along the border. The United Nations, with the United States as the principal force, came to the aid of South Korea. China came to the aid of North Korea, and the Soviet Union also gave some assistance to the North.",who did korea fight in the korean war
what does a picker do in a warehouse,"['https://sipmm.edu.sg/five-essential-methods-efficient-warehouse-operation/', 'https://www.sihs.com/category/order-picking/', 'https://www.hrugvedengineering.com/single-mast-aluminium-alloy-lifting-platforms.html', 'http://dreamstartsocceracademies.com/']",The order picking or order preparation operation is one of a logistic warehouse's processes. It consists in taking and collecting articles in a specified quantity before shipment to satisfy customers' orders. It is a basic warehousing process and has an important influence on supply chain's productivity. This makes order picking one of the most controlled logistic processes.,what does a picker do in a warehouse
who has been the eldest football player to score a goal in a world cup,"['http://stylishsports.blogspot.com/2011/07/alexandre-pato_01.html', 'https://warriortraveller.com/2017/08/23/countries-their-legends-africa/', 'http://toeslayer2000.blogspot.com/2018/03/1990-fifa-world-cup-tm.html', 'http://www.ghanaforum.com/archive/index.php/t-235.html?s=411011100c7a45fc740bb236db35ffc4', 'https://afrikanza.com/best-national-football-teams-in-african-history/', 'http://lesotho.blogspot.com/2003/07/bolo-football-or-soccer.html', 'https://www.aljazeera.com/archive/2006/06/2008410135336208331.html']","He achieved international stardom at 38 years old, an age at which most forward-playing footballers have retired, by scoring four goals at the 1990 FIFA World Cup. He helped Cameroon become the first African team to reach the World Cup quarter-finals. Four years later, at the age of 42, he became the oldest goalscorer in World Cup history by scoring against Russia in the 1994 FIFA World Cup.",who has been the eldest football player to score a goal in a world cup
where are the hips located on the human body,"['https://patents.google.com/patent/US9554935B2/en', 'http://orthopedics.imedpub.com/special-issues.php', 'http://www.taniabrownyoga.co.uk/happy_hips', 'https://bodytomy.com/labeled-human-skeleton-diagram']","The hip region is located lateral and anterior to the gluteal region (i.e., the buttock), inferior to the iliac crest, and overlying the greater trochanter of the femur, or ""thigh bone"". In adults, three of the bones of the pelvis have fused into the hip bone or acetabulum which forms part of the hip region.",where are the hips located on the human body
where is the border between israel and syria,"['https://www.wikispooks.com/wiki/Israel/Borders', 'http://fouman.com/Y/Wiki.php?eterm=Israel', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Status_of_Jerusalem', 'https://www.factbuddies.com/2018/05/amazing-facts-israel.html', 'http://www.traveljournal.com/country.php?iso=ISR', 'https://globetrooper.com/israel/', 'https://www.worldhospitalsearch.org/israel/']","According to interpretations of the Green Line of the 1949 Armistice Agreements, Israel borders Lebanon in the north, the Golan Heights and Syria in the northeast, the West Bank and Jordan in the east, the Gaza Strip and Egypt in the southwest. The border with Egypt is the international border demarcated in 1906 between United Kingdom and the Ottoman Empire.",where is the border between israel and syria
where does the term high noon come from,"['http://www.rockart-va.org/blackberry.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Noon', 'https://www.climateprediction.net/climate-science/glossary/tropics/', 'https://mediamonitors.net/direction-of-al-qiblah/', 'https://www.arlingtoncardinal.com/2017/12/astronomical-winter-arrives-today-at-1044-am-cst-with-the-winter-solstice-and-the-harp-twins/', 'https://www.factmonster.com/world/world-geography/geography-glossary', 'https://www.clarityforlife.training/solstice.html']","Solar noon (informally high noon) is the moment when the Sun contacts the observer's meridian, reaching its highest position above the horizon on that day (""Sun transit time""). This is also the origin of the terms ante meridiem (a.m.) and post meridiem (p.m.), as noted below. The Sun is directly overhead at solar noon at the Equator on the equinoxes, at the Tropic of Cancer (latitude 23 ° 26 ′ 12.6"" N) on the June solstice and at the Tropic of Capricorn (23 ° 26 ′ 12.6"" S) on the December solstice. In the Northern Hemisphere, north of the Tropic of Cancer, the Sun is due south of the observer at solar noon; in the Southern Hemisphere, south of the Tropic of Capricorn, it is due north.",where did the term high noon come from
why did dorothy go to the wizard of oz,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/The_Wizard_of_Oz_(1939_film)', 'https://www.uv-digimart.com/products/wizard-of-oz-digital-copy-download-code-uv-ultra-violet-vudu-hd-hdx', 'http://www.grandrapidshistoricalsociety.org/historical-society-news.html', 'https://fcchocolatebar.com/wizard-of-oz-coloring-sheets/', 'http://ournext.eu/wizard-of-oz-slots-online-no-download.html', 'http://northallertonmusicaltheatrecompany.org.uk/previous-productions/wizard-of-oz-2011', 'http://www.classicmovietime.com/the-wizard-of-oz/']","The farmhouse crashes in Munchkinland in the Land of Oz, where the film changes to Technicolor. Glinda the Good Witch of the North and the Munchkins welcome her as their heroine, as the house has landed on and killed the Wicked Witch of the East, leaving only her stocking feet exposed. The Wicked Witch of the West arrives to claim her sister's ruby slippers, but Glinda transports them onto Dorothy's feet first. The Wicked Witch of the West swears revenge on Dorothy for her sister's death. Glinda tells Dorothy to follow the yellow brick road to the Emerald City, where the Wizard of Oz might be able to help her get back home.",why did dorothy go to the wizard of oz
what is the history of the phantom of the opera,"['https://www.goldsborobooks.com/product/the-phantom-of-the-opera', 'https://www.spotonentertainment.co.uk/viva-la-musicals/', 'https://estellaelisheva.com/2017/08/28/practicing-violin-playing-the-phantom-of-the-opera-by-andrew-lloyd-webber/', 'https://ebfinder.com/genre/horror.html?page=4', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=2&ads=1&author=system&auto=Hamburg+opera&standalone=1&domain_name=hamburgopera.com&title=Hamburg+opera&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Hamburg+opera', 'http://vistrel-club.ru/paul-leroux-visual-selling-capture-the/', 'http://nerdipop.co.za/the-phantom-of-the-opera/']","The Phantom of the Opera (French: Le Fantôme de l'Opéra) is a novel by French writer Gaston Leroux. It was first published as a serialization in Le Gaulois from 23 September 1909, to 8 January 1910. It was published in volume form in late March 1910 by Pierre Lafitte. The novel is partly inspired by historical events at the Paris Opera during the nineteenth century and an apocryphal tale concerning the use of a former ballet pupil's skeleton in Carl Maria von Weber's 1841 production of Der Freischütz. It has been successfully adapted into various stage and film adaptations, most notable of which are the 1925 film depiction featuring Lon Chaney, and Andrew Lloyd Webber's 1986 musical.",what is the history of the phantom of the opera
what is the ultimate hitchhiker's guide to the galaxy about,"['https://ikindlebooks.com/literature/the-ultimate-hitchhikers-guide-to-the-galaxy', 'https://www.charlotteonthecheap.com/citizens-universe-presents-hitchhikers-guide-galaxy-live-pay-can/', 'http://bitgator.pro/liftarens-guide-till-galaxen-99/', 'https://www.britishclassiccomedy.co.uk/the-hitchhikers-guide-to-the-galaxy-radio', 'http://linksoflondonstore.com/radio-4-hitchhikers-guide-to-the-galaxy.html', 'http://murderiseverywhere.blogspot.com/2016/04/whats-your-three-favourite-books.html', 'https://theportalist.com/neil-gaiman-books']","The broad narrative of Hitchhiker follows the misadventures of the last surviving man, Arthur Dent, following the demolition of the planet Earth by a Vogon constructor fleet to make way for a hyperspace bypass. Dent is rescued from Earth's destruction by Ford Prefect, a human-like alien writer for the eccentric, electronic travel guide The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, by hitchhiking onto a passing Vogon spacecraft. Following his rescue, Dent explores the galaxy with Prefect and encounters Trillian, another human that had been taken from Earth prior to its destruction by the President of the Galaxy, the two-headed Zaphod Beeblebrox, and the depressed Marvin, the Paranoid Android. Certain narrative details were changed between the various adaptations.",what is the ultimate hitchhiker's guide to the galaxy about
where did ice cream sundae get its name,"['https://www.cute-calendar.com/event/national-strawberry-sundae-day/35151.html', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2018/11/11/', 'http://pinoysuperkitchenmasterchef.blogspot.com/2011/04/google-celebrate-119th-birthday-of-ice.html']","According to the Oxford English Dictionary, the origin of the term sundae is obscure; however, it is generally accepted that the spelling ""sundae"" derives from the English word ""Sunday ''. (1)",where did ice cream sundae get its name
the gond forest community belongs to which state of india,"['http://www.mysteryofindia.com/2014/12/indus-valley-drawing-discovered-near-hampi.html', 'https://indianbirds.thedynamicnature.com/2018/01/rosy-minivet-pericrocotus-roseus.html', 'https://www.downtoearth.org.in/news/natural-disasters/supreme-court-directs-centre-to-prepare-national-disaster-plan-to-tackle-drought-53915', 'http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/Yadav', 'https://www.gktoday.in/gk-current-affairs-september-3-4-2015/', 'http://changeforbetter.org.in/perspectives/545-weather-agricultural-growth', 'https://www.hindustantimes.com/india/major-naxalite-outfits/story-0veBIOPZoV4HdB5La2w7dM.html']","The Gondi (Gōndi) or Gond people are Adivasi people of central India, spread over the states of Madhya Pradesh, eastern Maharashtra (Vidarbha), Chhattisgarh, Uttar Pradesh, Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Bihar and Western Odisha.",the gond forest community belongs to which state of india
how did missouri get the name show me state,"['http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Missouri', 'https://www.hgh.tv/usa-hgh-clinics/missouri/', 'https://familypedia.wikia.org/wiki/Missouri', 'http://www.khs65blog.com/2009/07/im-from-missouri-youve-got-to.html', 'https://arnoldcoin.com/2003-Missouri-Quarter.html?cat=305', 'https://virtualmarketadvantage.com/missouri-seo/', 'https://shopflyoverpress.com/blogs/news']","There is no official state nickname. However, Missouri's unofficial nickname is the ""Show Me State"", which appears on its license plates. This phrase has several origins. One is popularly ascribed to a speech by Congressman Willard Vandiver in 1899, who declared that ""I come from a state that raises corn and cotton, cockleburs and Democrats, and frothy eloquence neither convinces nor satisfies me. I'm from Missouri, and you have got to show me."" This is in keeping with the saying ""I'm from Missouri"" which means ""I'm skeptical of the matter and not easily convinced."" However, according to researchers, the phrase ""show me"" was already in use before the 1890s. Another one states that it is a reference to Missouri miners who were taken to Leadville, Colorado to replace striking workers. Since the new men were unfamiliar with the mining methods, they required frequent instruction.",how did missouri get the name show me state
how many trophy has arsene wenger won at arsenal,"['http://flynewz.com/2018/04/20/arsene-wenger-leave-arsenal-end-season/', 'https://www.laureus.com/world-sports-awards/2019/laureus-lifetime-achievement/arsene-wenger', 'https://www.inquisitr.com/3294864/england-is-my-second-country-arsene-wenger-wont-rule-out-becoming-england-manager/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/FA_Cup', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Liverpool_F.C', 'http://tdifh.blogspot.com/2014/06/', 'http://www.odds24.co.uk/football/will-the-next-arsenal-manager-fabio-capello/']","Wenger was named manager of Arsenal in 1996 and two years later led the club to a league and FA Cup double. The club won another league and cup double in 2002 and retained the FA Cup a year later. In 2004, Wenger managed Arsenal to an undefeated league season, a feat last accomplished by Preston North End, 115 years previously. Arsenal later eclipsed Nottingham Forest's record of 42 league matches unbeaten and went seven more matches before losing in October 2004. The club made their first appearance in a Champions League final in 2006, though they lost to Barcelona. After a period of almost nine years without a trophy, which coincided with the club relocating to the Emirates Stadium, Wenger guided Arsenal to further FA Cup success in 2014, 2015 and 2017.",how many trophy has arsene wenger won at arsenal
what is the structure of an ip packet,['https://www.ukessays.com/essays/information-systems/vpn.php'],An IP packet consists of a header section and a data section.,what is the structure of an ip packet
is wilmington ca part of the city of los angeles,"['https://www.mobilewash.com/cities-we-serve/wilmington-mobile-car-wash/', 'https://www.nickersonins.com/wilmington/', 'http://topagentrealestate.com/properties-for-sale/wilmington', 'https://www.walchlaw.com/truck-accident-in-wilmington.html', 'https://wagwalking.com/dog-walking/ca-los-angeles/wilmington', 'http://topagentrealestate.com/properties-for-sale/harbor-city', 'https://www.publicstorage.com/california/self-storage-wilmington-ca']","Wilmington is a neighborhood in the Los Angeles Harbor Region area of Los Angeles, California, covering 9.14 square miles.",is wilmington ca part of the city of los angeles
what is the difference between atlantic ocean and caribbean sea,"['http://www.thecaribbeanpet.com/the-islands/', 'http://bluebird-electric.net/oceanography/Caribbean_Sea.htm', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=3&ads=1&author=system&auto=Curacao+accommodation&standalone=1&domain_name=curacaoaccommodation.com&title=Curacao+accommodation&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Curacao+accommodation', 'https://boards.cruisecritic.co.uk/topic/2646081-koningsdam-in-the-caribbean/page/8/', 'http://everything.explained.today/Caribbean_Sea/', 'http://www.gmanemwwcomicsenc.uk/home/chapters-of-the-encyclopedia/by-categories/publishers-category/dc-comics/caribbean-sea-location-dc-comics', 'https://svguidinglight.com/travel-guides/caribbean-travel-guide/']","The Caribbean Sea (Spanish: Mar Caribe; French: Mer des Caraïbes Dutch: Caraïbische Zee) is a sea of the Atlantic Ocean in the tropics of the Western Hemisphere. It is bounded by Mexico and Central America to the west and south west, to the north by the Greater Antilles starting with Cuba, to the east by the Lesser Antilles, and to the south by the north coast of South America.",what is the difference between atlantic ocean and caribbean sea
what is the poem on the statue of liberty,"['http://www.threecentersofcreativity.com/tag/freedom/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Statue_of_Liberty', 'https://www.rhodesguide.com/travelguide/colossus_rhodes.php', 'https://jeannetorrencefinley.com/tag/noel-paul-stookey/', 'https://www.beertrumpshate.com/events/2018/2/22/bth-benefit-for-rewa-rooftop-brew-co', 'https://www.catspawdynamics.com/give-me-your-tired-your-poor-your-huddled-masses/', 'https://www.winterwatch.net/2018/01/liberty-lazarus-and-colossal-lies/']","""The New Colossus"" is a sonnet that American poet Emma Lazarus (1849 -- 1887) wrote in 1883 to raise money for the construction of a pedestal for the Statue of Liberty. In 1903, the poem was cast onto a bronze plaque and mounted inside the pedestal's lower level.",what is the poem on the statue of liberty
which famous frontiersman died during the alamo siege,"['https://seamusdubhghaill.com/tag/texas/', 'https://www.elixirpresents.com/gentle-reminders-blog/david-crockett-thursday-september-29', 'https://aaforringer.com/2018/01/', 'http://thisiscommonsense.com/2018/08/17/david-crockett-7-2/', 'http://www.westernbitters.com/2015/06/', 'https://www.brainz.org/10-interesting-facts-about-tennessee/', 'https://texashillcountry.com/death-david-crockett-texas-memory/']","Crockett grew up in East Tennessee, where he gained a reputation for hunting and storytelling. He was made a colonel in the militia of Lawrence County, Tennessee and was elected to the Tennessee state legislature in 1821. In 1827, he was elected to the U.S. Congress where he vehemently opposed many of the policies of President Andrew Jackson, especially the Indian Removal Act. Crockett's opposition to Jackson's policies led to his defeat in the 1831 elections. He was re-elected in 1833, then narrowly lost in 1835, prompting his angry departure to Texas (then the Mexican state of Tejas) shortly thereafter. In early 1836, he took part in the Texas Revolution and was killed at the Battle of the Alamo in March.",which famous frontiersman died during the alamo siege
who was involved in the 7 years war,"['https://media.timetoast.com/timelines/imperialism-97684597-9db4-4f65-aaa1-8865663f6268', 'https://majormike.us/2017/05/18/today-in-history-051817/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Royal_Marines', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-worldhistory/chapter/the-seven-years-war/', 'https://majormike.us/2018/05/18/today-in-history-051818/', 'https://www.josephinecoins.com/p/1752-george-ii-shield-guinea', 'https://www.timetoast.com/timelines/the-british-in-india-65f5ff94-2087-412f-8d9e-1d6953e5724c']","The Seven Years' War was a global conflict fought between 1756 and 1763. It involved every European great power of the time and spanned five continents, affecting Europe, the Americas, West Africa, India, and the Philippines. The conflict split Europe into two coalitions, led by the Kingdom of Great Britain (including Prussia, Portugal, Hanover, and other small German states) on one side and the Kingdom of France (including the Austrian-led Holy Roman Empire, the Russian Empire, Bourbon Spain, and Sweden) on the other. Meanwhile, in India, some regional polities within the increasingly fragmented Mughal Empire, with the support of the French, tried to crush a British attempt to conquer Bengal. The war's extent has led some historians to describe it as ""World War Zero"", similar in scale to other world wars.",who was involved in the 7 years war
where did the saying houston we have a problem come from,"['https://ourplnt.com/spacewalker-russian-film/', 'http://www.cerebra.com.tr/en/insights-news-insights-houston-we-have-a-problem-acfe-2018-report-reveals-incredibly-large-fraud-losses.html', 'https://ourplnt.com/tag/apollo-13/']","""Houston, we have a problem"" is a popular but erroneous quote from the radio communications between the Apollo 13 astronaut John (""Jack"") Swigert and the NASA Mission Control Center (""Houston"") during the Apollo 13 spaceflight, as the astronauts communicated their discovery of the explosion that crippled their spacecraft. The erroneous wording was popularized by the 1995 film Apollo 13, a dramatization of the Apollo 13 mission, in which actor Tom Hanks, portraying Mission Commander Jim Lovell, uses that wording, which became one of the film's taglines.",where does the term houston we have a problem
where is grey matter found in the brain,"['https://blablawriting.com/p2x-receptors-distribution-essay', 'http://www.guidetopharmacology.org/GRAC/ObjectDisplayForward?objectId=415', 'http://www.guidetopharmacology.org/GRAC/ObjectDisplayForward?objectId=367', 'https://cerebrovortex.com/2012/02/19/fractional-anistrophy-of-white-matter-lesions-in-mtbi/', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fvets.2016.00078/full', 'https://patents.google.com/patent/US20070027498A1/en', 'https://brainaacn.org/memory-and-learning-ii/']","Grey matter is distributed at the surface of the cerebral hemispheres (cerebral cortex) and of the cerebellum (cerebellar cortex), as well as in the depths of the cerebrum (thalamus; hypothalamus; subthalamus, basal ganglia -- putamen, globus pallidus, nucleus accumbens; septal nuclei), cerebellar (deep cerebellar nuclei -- dentate nucleus, globose nucleus, emboliform nucleus, fastigial nucleus), brainstem (substantia nigra, red nucleus, olivary nuclei, cranial nerve nuclei).",where is grey matter found in the brain
what is the land size of hong kong,"['https://www.chinabeijingprivatetour.com/side/popular_china_city_tours.htm', 'https://www.turipo.com/views/tripPage.php?trip_id=638', 'http://www.maqbulah.com/holiday-package/25/extravaganza-hongkong-family-tour', 'http://everything.explained.today/Hong_Kong/', 'https://goldprice.org/it/gold-price-hong-kong.html', 'http://wetherillfamily.com/shaffner.html', 'https://www.levelupvillage.com/gps/hongkong/']","Hong Kong, officially the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China, is an autonomous territory south to Mainland China and east to Macao in East Asia. With around 7.2 million Hong Kongers of various nationalities in a territory of 1,104 km, Hong Kong is the world's fourth most densely populated country or territory.",what is the land size of hong kong
where do most hurricanes typhoons and cyclones originate,"['http://planeta42.com/geography/ushurricanes/', 'https://satorirei.com/2017/04/08/wax-on-wax-off/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Atlantic_hurricane_season', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Atmospheric_instability', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=tornado+hurricane+typhoon+difference&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://sciencestruck.com/where-do-hurricanes-occur', 'http://www.oxfordbibliographies.com/view/document/obo-9780199874002/obo-9780199874002-0036.xml']","A typhoon differs from a cyclone or hurricane only on the basis of location. A hurricane is a storm that occurs in the Atlantic Ocean and northeastern Pacific Ocean, a typhoon occurs in the northwestern Pacific Ocean, and a cyclone occurs in the south Pacific or Indian Ocean.",where do most hurricanes typhoons and cyclones originate
when did japan attack china in world war 2,"['https://www.webstagram.biz/tag/battle', 'https://blogs.loc.gov/international-collections/2017/06/', 'https://wiki.kidzsearch.com/wiki/Second_Sino-Japanese_War', 'http://www.pmimchat.com/forum/showthread.php?s=8986a123a9ac6afcf12088f0f4722e3a&p=18252', 'http://www.combatsim.com/topics/combat-flight-sim/flying-tigers-shadows-over-china/', 'http://countriesquest.com/asia/philippines/history/world_war_ii_and_japanese_occupation.htm', 'https://www.theclassroom.com/world-war-ii-the-complete-guide-to-ace-your-test-13711607.html']","The Second Sino-Japanese War was a military conflict fought primarily between the Republic of China and the Empire of Japan from July 7, 1937 to September 9, 1945. It began with the Marco Polo Bridge Incident in 1937 in which a dispute between Japanese and Chinese troops escalated into a battle. The conflict then escalated further into a full-scale war. It ended with the unconditional surrender of Japan on September 2, 1945 to the Allies of World War II.",when did japan attack china in world war 2
what region of the world is fiji located in,"['http://howwas.org/', 'http://www.mapsguidesandmore.com/Fiji', 'http://www.mapnall.com/en/language/English-language_444.html', 'http://fiji-jo.com/en/index.php/meet-the-consol/itemlist/user/921-super-user', 'https://networthroll.com/fiji-net-worth-2/', 'https://www.travelerbase.com/index.php?proc=search&term=10+Best+Places+to+Visit+in+Tonga', 'https://upge.wn.com/?from=fijimuseum.com&ads=1&title=Fiji+museum&auto=Fiji+museum&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Fiji+museum&pagenum=2']","Fiji (/ ˈfiːdʒiː / (listen) FEE-jee; Fijian: Viti (ˈβitʃi); Fiji Hindi: फ़िजी), officially the Republic of Fiji (Fijian: Matanitu Tugalala o Viti; Fiji Hindi: फ़िजी गणराज्य), is an island country in Melanesia in the South Pacific Ocean about 1,100 nautical miles (2,000 km; 1,300 mi) northeast of New Zealand's North Island. Its closest neighbours are Vanuatu to the west, New Caledonia to the southwest, New Zealand's Kermadec Islands to the southeast, Tonga to the east, the Samoas and France's Wallis and Futuna to the northeast, and Tuvalu to the north.",what region of the world is fiji located in
what is a digestive biscuit called in america,"['https://dessertswithbenefits.com/graham-crackers-gluten-free-version/', 'https://beingawordsmith.com/2013/08/pinterest-to-the-rescue.html', 'https://cupcakesandotherstuff.wordpress.com/category/tradition/', 'https://www.tinnedtomatoes.com/2019/01/easy-peanut-butter-bars-vegan-recipe.html', 'https://sugarness.com/2013/05/13/chocolate-rubble-slab/', 'http://hiddenponies.com/2012/12/saturday-sweets-best-ever-nanaimo-bars/', 'http://katethebake.blogspot.com/2010/01/daring-bakers-nanaimo-bars-january-2010.html']","Digestive biscuits are similar enough to graham crackers that each can be used as a substitute for the other, such as in the United States where digestive biscuits are uncommon, and in places like Australia where Graham Crackers are unavailable.",what is a digestive biscuit called in america
what makes a computer a general purpose computer,"['http://cfc.co.uk/', 'http://kamuran-ozdogan.com/app/dating-apps-for-sexagesimal-notation-software-3063726.html', 'http://computerpedia.com/index.html', 'https://gkgujarat.wordpress.com/computer-material/what-is-computer/', 'https://www.gktoday.in/quizbase/computer-awareness-02-functions-and-capabilities-o', 'https://www.uaex.edu/support-units/information-technology/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Computer']","A general purpose computer has four main components: the arithmetic logic unit (ALU), the control unit, the memory, and the input and output devices (collectively termed I / O). These parts are interconnected by buses, often made of groups of wires. Inside each of these parts are thousands to trillions of small electrical circuits which can be turned off or on by means of an electronic switch. Each circuit represents a bit (binary digit) of information so that when the circuit is on it represents a ""1"", and when off it represents a ""0"" (in positive logic representation). The circuits are arranged in logic gates so that one or more of the circuits may control the state of one or more of the other circuits.",what makes a computer a general purpose computer
when does gnomeo and juliet 2 come out,"['https://www.netpaak.com/%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%84%D9%88%D8%AF-%D8%A7%D9%86%DB%8C%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B4%D9%86-%D8%B4%D8%B1%D9%84%D9%88%DA%A9-%D9%86%D9%88%D9%85%D8%B2-sherlock-gnomes-2018-%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%A8%D9%84%D9%87-%D9%81/', 'http://putlockerfun.com/sherlock-gnomes-2018-movie/', 'https://filmhds.com/sherlockgnomes/', 'http://www.listsinfo.com/2017/11', 'https://www.pinewoodgroup.com/pinewood-today/credits/sherlock-gnomes', 'http://digitaleleinwand.de/2011/10/04/disney-bringt-weitere-klassiker-als-3d-rerelease-ins-kino-die-schoene-und-das-biest-arielle-die-meerjungfrau-pixars-findet-nemo-und-die-monster-ag/', 'http://www.nookl.com/page/What_Men_Want_(2019_film)']","Sherlock Gnomes is a 2018 3D computer-animated comedy film directed by John Stevenson. A sequel to Gnomeo & Juliet (2011), the film stars the voices of James McAvoy, Emily Blunt, Chiwetel Ejiofor, Mary J. Blige, and Johnny Depp. It was produced by Paramount Animation, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, and Rocket Pictures, with the animation service provided by Mikros Image. It is the first film from Paramount Animation to be entirely animated, and the first animated film from Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer since 2008's Igor. The film was released in the United States on March 23, 2018, by Paramount Pictures, unlike its predecessor, which was distributed by Touchstone Pictures. It has grossed $76 million worldwide.",when does gnomeo and juliet 2 come out
who writes the meeting minutes in a business meeting,"['https://www.makemyassignments.com/blog/importance-of-making-minutes-of-meeting/', 'http://www.primidi.com/minutes', 'https://www.allformtemplates.com/meeting-minutes-templates10-project-meeting-minutes-templates-formats/']","Minutes may be created during the meeting by a typist or court reporter, who may use shorthand notation and then prepare the minutes and issue them to the participants afterwards. Alternatively, the meeting can be audio recorded, video recorded, or a group's appointed or informally assigned secretary may take notes, with minutes prepared later. Many government agencies use minutes recording software to record and prepare all minutes in real-time.",who writes the meeting minutes in a business meeting
when are itemized deductions used in computing taxable income,"['https://www.globalpropertyguide.com/North-America/United-States/Living-There', 'https://financesolutions.org/top-10-tax-terms-to-know-before-you-file/', 'https://www.chamberofcommerce.org/detailed-guide-to-schedule-c-tax-form/', 'https://crummeyestateplan.com/tag/standard-deduction/', 'https://www.llbcpa.com/will-new-tax-law-affect-business-owners-2018/', 'https://www.bctaxrelief.com/what-tax-terminology-you-need-to-know/', 'http://wwa.kiplinger.com/article/taxes/T054-C000-S001-kiplinger-s-tax-glossary-tax-terms-you-need-to-kno.html']","Most taxpayers are allowed a choice between the itemized deductions and the standard deduction. After computing their adjusted gross income (AGI), taxpayers can itemize deductions (from a list of allowable items) and subtract those itemized deductions (and any applicable personal exemption deductions) from their AGI amount to arrive at the taxable income. Alternatively, they can elect to subtract the standard deduction for their filing status (and any applicable personal exemption deduction) to arrive at the taxable income. In other words, the taxpayer may generally deduct the total itemized deduction amount, or the applicable standard deduction amount, whichever is greater.",when are itemized deductions used in computing taxable income
where is the football team the rams from,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/History_of_the_St._Louis_Cardinals_(NFL)', 'https://www.thechampionrings.com/nfl-super-bowl-rings/st-louis-rams.html', 'https://highnoteblog.com/super-bowl-liii-music-prop-bets/', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Cleveland_Rams', 'https://www.statista.com/topics/4348/los-angeles-rams/', 'https://deadline.com/2016/01/3-nfl-times-file-to-relocate-to-los-angeles-1201676036/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Chad_Lavalais']","The professional American football franchise now known as the Los Angeles Rams played in St. Louis, Missouri, as the St. Louis Rams from the 1995 through the 2015 seasons before relocating back to Los Angeles where the team played from the 1946 season to the 1994 season. The Rams franchise relocated from Los Angeles to St. Louis in 1995, which had been without a National Football League (NFL) team since the Cardinals moved to Phoenix, Arizona, in 1988. The Rams' first home game in St. Louis was at Busch Memorial Stadium against the New Orleans Saints on September 10, 1995, before the Trans World Dome (later the Edward Jones Dome, and now known as The Dome at America's Center) was completed for their November 12 game against the Carolina Panthers. Their last game played at the Edward Jones Dome in St. Louis was against the Tampa Bay Buccaneers on December 17, 2015, which they won, 31 -- 23. The Rams' last game as a St. Louis-based club was on January 3, 2016, against the San Francisco 49ers at Levi's Stadium, where they lost in overtime 19 -- 16.",where is the football team the rams from
what is the difference between nfc and nfl,"['https://www.thechampionrings.com/other-champions-rings/afc-nfc-rings.html', 'http://wikien3.appspot.com/wiki/American_Football_Conference', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/National_Football_Conference', 'https://www.gambling360.com/nfl/american-football-conference/', 'http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/NFL', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/National_Football_League', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/National_Football_Conference']","The National Football Conference (NFC) is one of the two conferences of the National Football League (NFL), the highest professional level of American football in the United States. This conference and its counterpart, the American Football Conference (AFC), currently contain 16 teams each, making up the 32 teams of the NFL. Both conferences were created as part of the 1970 merger with the rival American Football League (AFL), with all ten of the former AFL teams and three NFL teams forming the AFC while the remaining thirteen NFL clubs formed the NFC. A series of league expansions and division realignments have occurred since the merger, thus making the current total 16 clubs per conference.",what is the difference between nfc and nfl
moscato d'asti is from which italian wine growing region,"['https://www.getswill.com/products/white-moscato/', 'https://nofailrecipe.com/recipe_wine_pairing/moscato-dasti/', 'https://www.winealign.com/top/Moscato+d%27Asti', 'https://www.liquidassetsri.com/posts/tastings-on-may-4-and-5-2018/', 'https://feastandwest.com/2015/03/02/kindred-spirits-champagne-guide/', 'https://vinoindiana.com/italian-wines/', 'https://www.grapeescapes.net/destinations/piedmont/the-wines/']","Moscato d'Asti is a DOCG sparkling white wine produced mainly in the province of Asti, northwest Italy, and in smaller nearby regions in the provinces of Alessandria and Cuneo. The wine is sweet and low in alcohol, and is considered a dessert wine. It is from the Moscato bianco grape. A related wine, Asti, is produced in the same area from the same grape.",moscato d'asti is from which italian wine growing region
what is the longest made field goal in nfl history,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/List_of_Atlanta_Falcons_starting_quarterbacks', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Three-point_field_goal', 'https://www.pore.rocks/carolina-panthers/', 'https://campaignpage.ca/category-girls/08-06-2018-3290.php', 'https://www.stack.com/a/broncos-kicker-brandon-mcmanus-thinks-justin-tucker-cant-kick-84-yard-field-goal', 'http://dearsportsfan.com/2015/07/27/whats-special-about-the-denver-broncos/', 'https://www.baltimoreravens.com/news/more-proof-that-justin-tucker-is-a-madman-he-wanted-a-72-yard-attempt-19227359']","The longest field goal kick in NFL history is 64 yards, a record set by Matt Prater on December 8, 2013. The previous record was 63, originally set by Tom Dempsey and then matched by Jason Elam, Sebastian Janikowski, and David Akers. High school, college and most professional football leagues offer only a three-point field goal; however, some professional leagues have encouraged more rare kicks through four-point field goals. NFL Europe encouraged long field goals of 50 yards or more by making those worth four points instead of three (much like Australian rules' Super Goal or basketball's three-point line), a rule since adopted by the Stars Football League. Similarly, the sport of arena football sought (unsuccessfully) to repopularize the drop kick by making that worth four points; it failed, since only one kicker (Brian Mitchell) was able to do it with any semblance of proficiency. (In six-man football, where there is no offensive line, all field goals are worth four points instead of the usual three.)",what is the longest made field goal in nfl history
in the documentary film paris is burning the houses are,['http://normalisierung.blogsport.de/category/video-und-film/'],"Jennie Livingston, who moved to New York after graduating from Yale to work in film, and who spent six years making Paris Is Burning, concentrated on interviews with key figures in the ball world, many of whom contribute monologues that shed light on the ball culture as well as on their own personalities. In the film, titles such as ""house,"" ""mother,"" and ""reading"" emphasize how the subculture the film depicts has taken words from the straight and white worlds, and imbued them with alternate meanings, just as the ""houses"" serve as surrogate families for young ball-walkers whose sexual orientations have sometimes made acceptance and love within their own families hard to come by.",in the documentary film paris is burning the houses are
what does it take to join augusta national golf club,"['https://betnewjersey.com/sports-betting/masters/', 'http://raycharlesblues.blogspot.com/2011/04/two-nationals-but-are-they-grand.html', 'http://academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/Augusta_National_Golf_Club', 'http://dnwahx.info/06134-essay-on-bobby-jones-in-augusta-ga/', 'http://ttt-hiweb.newscyclecloud.com/sports/2019/04/13/coffee-shop-encounter-leads-to-once-in-a-lifetime-trip-to-masters/', 'http://sterlinggrouphouston.org/', 'https://www.clublender.com/2018/04/02/masters-privacy-remarkable-man/']","Augusta National Golf Club has about 300 members at any given time. Membership is strictly by invitation: there is no application process. In 2004, USA Today published a list of all the current members. Membership is believed to cost between $10,000 and $30,000 and annual dues were estimated in 2009 to be less than $10,000 per year.",what does it take to join augusta national golf club
what is the setting of a farewell to arms,"['http://fontidelvulture.it/a-farewell-to-arms-author.html', 'http://wwebb.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=202', 'https://www.studymode.com/essays/a-Farewell-To-Arms-43432633.html', 'https://colatowncurated.com/2015/05/09/ex-libris-online-a-farewell-to-arms/']","A Farewell to Arms is about a love affair between the expatriate American Frederic Henry and Catherine Barkley against the backdrop of the First World War, cynical soldiers, fighting and the displacement of populations. The publication of A Farewell to Arms cemented Hemingway's stature as a modern American writer, became his first best-seller, and is described by biographer Michael Reynolds as ""the premier American war novel from that debacle World War I.""",what is the setting of a farewell to arms
where is the bachelor winter games filmed at,['https://www.realitytvworld.com/pophollywood/the-bachelor-winter-games/'],"The series reunite previous contestants from The Bachelor and The Bachelorette at a winter resort in Manchester, Vermont, where they are competing with contestants from the various international adaptations of the franchise in various winter sports challenges.",where is the bachelor winter games filmed at
when does the 8th season of the walking dead start,"['https://www.dailymotion.com/video/x5wy1i3', 'http://suresuccess.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=207', 'http://mastermotion.info/?newsid=40739', 'http://gero-spa.info/viewtopic.php?t=31327', 'http://freeinfocontent.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=21892', 'http://pmc-s.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=18437', 'http://wu-taichi.info/?page_id=43862']","The eighth season of The Walking Dead, an American post-apocalyptic horror television series on AMC, premiered on October 22, 2017, and concluded on April 15, 2018, consisting of 16 episodes. Developed for television by Frank Darabont, the series is based on the eponymous series of comic books by Robert Kirkman, Tony Moore, and Charlie Adlard. The executive producers are Kirkman, David Alpert, Scott M. Gimple, Greg Nicotero, Tom Luse, and Gale Anne Hurd, with Gimple as showrunner for his fifth and final season. The eighth season received positive reviews from critics. It was nominated for multiple awards and won two, including Best Horror Television Series for the third consecutive year, at the 44th Saturn Awards.",when does the 8th season of the walking dead start
what is the game the last of us,"['http://deloitte-ouch.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=28774', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=3&ads=1&author=system&auto=Us+drawing&standalone=1&domain_name=usdrawing.com&title=Us+drawing&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Us+drawing', 'http://newtorrentgame.com/the-last-of-us-remastered-torrent-ps4/', 'https://www.gbposters.com/the-last-of-us', 'https://radiolaurier.com/2017/01/25/press-start-to-bgn-25012017-recap/', 'http://playstationgamesdownload.tk/the-last-of-us', 'https://www.createcg.net/the-making-of-the-last-of-us-behind-the-scenes/']","The Last of Us is an action-adventure survival horror video game developed by Naughty Dog and published by Sony Computer Entertainment. It was released for the PlayStation 3 worldwide on June 14, 2013. Players control Joel, a smuggler tasked with escorting a teenage girl named Ellie across a post-apocalyptic United States. The Last of Us is played from a third-person perspective; players use firearms and improvised weapons, and can use stealth to defend against hostile humans and cannibalistic creatures infected by a mutated strain of the Cordyceps fungus. In the game's online multiplayer mode, up to eight players engage in cooperative and competitive gameplay.",what is the game the last of us
review the nigeria biafra civil war of 1967 through 1970,"['https://www.nigerianelitesforum.com/history-of-nigerian-civil-war/?share=google-plus-1', 'https://www.ronburtonphotographer.com/topics/all', 'https://www.tipsissuesonline.com/2016/02/nnamdi-kanu-hero-or-villain.html', 'http://www.thebiafraherald.co/2016/10/the-economic-blockade-and-starvation-as.html', 'http://mediaforjusticenigeria.org/aggregator/sources/9?page=133', 'https://globalvoices.org/2015/10/16/did-pele-stop-the-bloodiest-civil-war-in-nigerias-history-for-48-hours/', 'https://www.angelwelt.info/pvivyjnecncregurfvffgngrzragf7797ff0c9.html']","The Nigerian Civil War, commonly known as the Biafran War, (6 July 1967 -- 15 January 1970), was a war fought between the government of Nigeria and the secessionist state of Biafra. Biafra represented nationalist aspirations of the Igbo people, whose leadership felt they could no longer coexist with the Northern-dominated federal government. The conflict resulted from political, economic, ethnic, cultural and religious tensions which preceded Britain's formal decolonisation of Nigeria from 1960 to 1963. Immediate causes of the war in 1966 included a military coup, a counter-coup, and persecution of Igbo living in Northern Nigeria. Control over oil production in the Niger Delta played a vital strategic role.",causes of nigerian civil war of 1967 pdf
need and importance of railway transport in india,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Indian_Railways', 'https://www.govtjobsclub.in/railway-jobs-indian-railway-recruitment/', 'http://techsciencenews.com/directory/wp/r/Rail_transport_in_India.htm', 'http://ibpsindia.com/courses/', 'http://www.eceway.com/2016/10/indian-railway-2016-recruitment-of.html', 'https://www.classboat.com/class-pune/railway-exam-class-11298', 'https://www.rail.ind.in/']","All main-line rail operations in India are handled by Indian Railways (IR), a state-owned organization of the Ministry of Railways. As of 31 March 2016 the rail network traverses the length and breadth of the country comprising 119,630 km (74,330 mi) of track over a route of 66,687 km (41,437 mi) and 7,216 stations. It is the fourth-largest railway network in the world (after those of the United States, Russia and China). It is one of the busiest networks in the world, transporting 8.107 billion passengers and over 1.108 billion tonnes of freight annually, as of 2016. Indian Railways is the world's largest commercial or utility employer, with more than 1.4 million employees. Indian Railways' rolling stock includes over 200,000 (freight) wagons, 50,000 coaches and 8,000 locomotives.",need and importance of railway transport in india
what is the significance of eating 12 grapes on new years eve,"['https://www.aplin.co.uk/2015/12/5-christmas-traditions-from-around-the-world/', 'https://budhasubba.com/4279', 'https://www.ibtimes.co.uk/new-years-eve-2015-unusual-traditions-customs-celebrate-new-year-around-world-1481367', 'https://www.ibericarestaurants.com/whats-on/nye-at-iberica-canary-wharf/', 'https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/nye-at-iberica-canary-wharf-tickets-53055931720']","The tradition consists of eating a grape with each bell strike at midnight of December 31. According to the tradition, that leads to a year of prosperity. In some areas, it is believed that the tradition wards away witches and general evil, although this ""magic"" is treated like an old heritage, and in modern days it's viewed as a cultural tradition to welcome the new year.",what is the significance of eating 12 grapes on new years eve
the battle of midway signaled to the american military that,"['https://www.minister.defence.gov.au/minister/david-feeney/media-releases/parliamentary-secretary-defence-solomon-islands-scouts-and', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/2005', 'http://www.arlingtoncemetery.net/mrbrowning.htm', 'https://blog.togetherweserved.com/2015/08/26/battle-chronicles-midway-and-guadalcanal/', 'http://aeroscale.co.uk/modules.php?op=modload&name=Reviews&file=index&req=showcontent&id=10423']","Although the Japanese continued to try to secure more territory, and the U.S. did not move from a state of naval parity to one of supremacy until after several more months of hard combat, Midway allowed the Allies to switch to the strategic initiative, paving the way for the landings on Guadalcanal and the prolonged attrition of the Solomon Islands campaign. Midway allowed this to occur before the first of the new Essex-class fleet carriers became available at the end of 1942. The Guadalcanal Campaign is also regarded by some as a turning point in the Pacific War.",the battle of midway signaled to the american military that
how many times did the falcons win the super bowl,"['https://www.falcons-tickets.org/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Georgia_Dome', 'https://nationalticketagency.com/atlanta-falcons-tickets.html', 'https://majorleaguepets.com/blogs/coach-johns-corner/pre-season-top-ten-nfl-teams-and-the-gear-to-cheer-2018-major-league-pets', 'https://fanmail.com/professional/team/atlanta_falcons/football', 'https://www.detroitnews.com/story/sports/nfl/lions/2019/01/16/detroit-lions-name-darrell-bevell-new-offensive-coordinator/2596420002/', 'https://www.footballbuzz.club/NFL-Super-Bowl-Ring/NFC-South/NFL-Atlanta-Falcons']","In their 51 years of existence (through 2016), the Falcons have compiled a record of 350 -- 450 -- 6 (341 -- 437 -- 6 in the regular season and 9 -- 13 in the playoffs), winning division championships in 1980, 1998, 2004, 2010, 2012, and 2016. The Falcons have appeared in two Super Bowls, the first during the 1998 season in Super Bowl XXXIII, where they lost to the Denver Broncos 34 -- 19, and the second was eighteen years later, a 34 -- 28 overtime defeat by the New England Patriots in Super Bowl LI.",how many times did the falcons win the super bowl
who is luke in the gospel of luke,"['http://muslimprophets.com/videos.php?search=Luke+21%3A20', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Apostles', 'http://albertolima.tk/andy-mic-dating.html']","Luke -- Acts does not name its author. According to Church tradition this was Luke the Evangelist, the companion of Paul, but while this view is still occasionally put forward the scholarly consensus emphasises the many contradictions between Acts and the authentic Pauline letters. The most probable date for its composition is around 80 -- 110 AD, and there is evidence that it was still being revised well into the 2nd century.",who is luke in the gospel of luke
what was the original concept of vitruvian man,"['https://coin-brothers.com/catalog/coin733', 'http://www.ridevelo.cc/blog/2016/8/14/atelier-passoni', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Renaissance_Humanism.html', 'https://www.lifeofanarchitect.com/scale-and-proportion-the-architects-domain/', 'https://archichazz.com/2012/12/19/seven-simple-layers/', 'http://designblog.rietveldacademie.nl/?tag=wim-crouwel', 'http://wheresmydrink.com/rainmeter-vitruvian-man-suite-for-windows-7/']",The drawing is based on the correlations of ideal human proportions with geometry described by the ancient Roman architect Vitruvius in Book III of his treatise De architectura. Vitruvius described the human figure as being the principal source of proportion among the classical orders of architecture. Vitruvius determined that the ideal body should be eight heads high. Leonardo's drawing is traditionally named in honor of the architect.,what was the original concept of vitruvian man
which country collaborated in the establishment of bokaro and bhilai steel plants,"['http://rejoicebc.co.za/19241_manganese-plant-machinery-in-india.html', 'https://www.brigthcareers.com/sail-bokaro-steel-plant-recruitment/', 'http://www.currentaffairsindia.info/2013/08/industrialization-in-india-after-independence.html', 'https://www.sarahndipity.co.za/18/12/24/43967_brahma_group_coal_mining_company.html', 'http://rejoicebc.co.za/13227_steel-melting-shop-process-flow-sheet.html', 'https://www.indiantribune.com/union-steel-minister-chaudhary-birender-singh-shares-termination-chief-executive-officer-bhilai-steel-plant', 'https://beervisits.eu/pub-bar-visit/pv-england/135-pv-greater-manchester/462-central-manchester-city-arms']",Bokaro Steel Plant (BSP) is located in the Bokaro district of Jharkhand ... It is the fourth integrated public sector steel plant in India built with Soviet help. It was incorporated as a limited company in 1964. It was later merged with the state-owned Steel Authority of India Limited (SAIL).,which country collaborated in the establishment of bokaro and bhilai steel plants
where is yemen located on the world map,"['http://danir19.com/', 'https://mapio.net/a/105146168/?lang=en', 'https://latitude.to/map/ye/yemen', 'http://raqeb.co/en/countries/yemen', 'https://redefineschool.com/yemen/', 'https://artofscubadiving.com/yemen/', 'https://proeliumlaw.com/country-reports/country-profile-yemen/']","Yemen (/ ˈjɛmən / (listen); Arabic: اليَمَن ‎ ‎ al-Yaman), officially known as the Republic of Yemen (الجمهورية اليمنية al-Jumhūrīyah al-Yamanīyah), is an Arab country in Western Asia at the southern end of the Arabian Peninsula. Yemen is the second-largest country in the peninsula, occupying 527,970 km (203,850 sq mi). The coastline stretches for about 2,000 km (1,200 mi). It is bordered by Saudi Arabia to the north, the Red Sea to the west, the Gulf of Aden and Arabian Sea to the south, and Oman to the east-northeast. Although Yemen's constitutionally stated capital is the city of Sana'a, the city has been under rebel control since February 2015. Because of this, Yemen's capital has been temporarily relocated to the port city of Aden, on the southern coast. Yemen's territory includes more than 200 islands; the largest of these is Socotra.",where is yemen located on the world map
what is the most accepted form of scientific ideas,"['https://phys.org/news/2017-05-physicists-lithium-oxide-tokamak-walls.html', 'http://indemaak.info/news.php?action=show&id=27221', 'http://walter.bislins.ch/bloge/index.asp?page=Flat+Earth+Dome+Model', 'https://fohilao.palmolive2day.com/explain-what-is-means-to-have-34939lq.html', 'https://sciencebriefss.com/science-explained/scientific-concepts/five-important-scientific-theories-that-have-changed-the-world-science-explained', 'http://markmueller.info/search?q=Principles%20of%20arguments', 'http://qva.com.au/what-is-the-difference-between-a-theory-and-scientific-law.html']","A scientific theory is an explanation of an aspect of the natural world that can be repeatedly tested, in accordance with the scientific method, using a predefined protocol of observation and experiment. Established scientific theories have withstood rigorous scrutiny and embody scientific knowledge.",what is the most accepted form of scientific ideas
a room of one's own virginia woolf short summary,"['https://modernmrsdarcy.com/books/a-room-of-ones-own/', 'http://www.elefant.ro/carti/carte-straina/language-linguistics/language-reference-general/a-room-of-ones-own-paperback-486435.html', 'http://www.jamaicaobserver.com/style-spotlight/10-must-reads-for-2019-dr-claudine-leiwis-cardiologist_154104?profile=1237', 'http://wisehouse-classics.com/project/a-room-of-ones-own/', 'https://www.bookrepublic.it/book/9786050467642-a-room-of-ones-own/', 'https://www.bookbeat.co.uk/book/room-ones-own-24269', 'https://www.overdrive.com/media/1382767/a-room-of-ones-own']","A Room of One's Own is an extended essay by Virginia Woolf. First published on 24 October 1929, the essay was based on a series of lectures she delivered at Newnham College and Girton College, two women's colleges at Cambridge University in October 1928. While this extended essay in fact employs a fictional narrator and narrative to explore women both as writers of and characters in fiction, the manuscript for the delivery of the series of lectures, titled ""Women and Fiction"", which was published in Forum March 1929, and hence the essay, are considered non-fiction. The essay is generally seen as a feminist text and is noted in its argument for both a literal and figurative space for women writers within a literary tradition dominated by men.",a room of one's own virginia woolf short summary
who used the silk road in ancient china,"['http://mtvufmmn.info/?newsid=31445', 'http://einfach-reisen.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=37260', 'http://fustaiferro.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=1348', 'http://allhookedup.net/10976/silk-road-definition.html', 'http://bruce-humes.com/archives/category/new-silk-road-one-belt-one-road-%E4%B8%80%E5%B8%A6%E4%B8%80%E8%B7%AF', 'http://outlookafghanistan.net/editorialdetail.php?post_id=21764', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Charax_Spasinu']","The Silk Road was an ancient network of trade routes that connected the East and West. It was central to cultural interaction between the regions for many centuries. The Silk Road refers to both the terrestrial and the maritime routes connecting East Asia and Southeast Asia with East Africa, West Asia and Southern Europe.",who used the silk road in ancient china
what is the primary function of the pituitary gland,"['https://motherhoodng.com/your-hormones-after-childbirth/', 'https://www.totalfitnessdvds.com/Kundalini-Yoga-for-Your-Week-Monday-Volume-1-p/182.htm', 'https://yourfertilityfriend.com/how-does-pcos-affect-ivf/', 'http://www.nationalreflexology.ie/articles', 'http://subent.com/pituitary-tumor-removal-in-conjuction-with-neurosurgery']","Hormones secreted from the pituitary gland help control: growth, blood pressure, certain functions of the sex organs, thyroid glands and metabolism as well as some aspects of pregnancy, childbirth, nursing, water / salt concentration at the kidneys, temperature regulation and pain relief.",what is the primary function of the pituitary gland
where are the bahamas islands located on a map,"['https://www.bnesim.com/best-sim-card-for/bahamas/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=5&ads=1&author=system&auto=Nassau+accommodation&standalone=1&domain_name=nassauaccommodation.com&title=Nassau+accommodation&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Nassau+accommodation', 'http://www.easybranches.pro/yachts/destinations/caribbean-bahamas/', 'https://www.hit-tuner.net/en/worldwide/radio/10001318.html', 'https://infactcollaborative.com/countries/facts-about-the-bahamas.html', 'https://www.dekhnews.com/bahamas-independence-day-2015-quotes-sayings-wishes-images-whatsapp-status-fb-dp/', 'http://boatpartymiami.com/miami-yacht-charter-contact/']","The Bahamas (/ bəˈhɑːməz / (listen)), known officially as the Commonwealth of The Bahamas, is an archipelagic state within the Lucayan Archipelago. It consists of more than 700 islands, cays, and islets in the Atlantic Ocean, and is located north of Cuba and Hispaniola (Haiti and the Dominican Republic), northwest of the Turks and Caicos Islands, southeast of the United States state of Florida, and east of the Florida Keys. The capital is Nassau on the island of New Providence. The designation of ""the Bahamas"" can refer either to the country or to the larger island chain that it shares with the Turks and Caicos Islands. The Royal Bahamas Defence Force describes the Bahamas territory as encompassing 470,000 km (180,000 sq mi) of ocean space.",where are the bahamas islands located on a map
what is the difference between muslin and calico,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Rep_(fabric)', 'https://www.quality-fabrics.co.uk/natural-calico-62-c.asp', 'https://www.minervacrafts.com/help/shopping/fabric-glossary', 'http://www.maddogprint.com.au/full-colour-printed-calico-bags-get-noticed/', 'http://wiki.pathfindersonline.org/index.php?title=Adventist_Youth_Honors_Answer_Book/Arts_and_Crafts/Upholstery&oldid=128223&diff=231202', 'https://iwcpgardeninggroup.blogspot.com/2017/', 'https://www.ezypromos.com.au/bags/']","Calico (in British usage since 1505) is a plain-woven textile made from unbleached and often not fully processed cotton. It may contain unseparated husk parts, for example. The fabric is far less fine than muslin, but less coarse and thick than canvas or denim, but it is still very cheap owing to its unfinished and undyed appearance.",what is the difference between muslin and calico
what is the name of the airport in kansas city kansas,"['https://www.riyadh-airport.com/', 'https://dodgereviews.us/read/flying-j-dodge-city-ks', 'https://www.kansas-city-airport.com/?tp=0', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/New_Caledonia', 'https://newstalkkit.com/fewer-passengers-fly-from-yakima-airport-in-2018/', 'http://www.achieve.co.uk/supporters/', 'https://www.amman-airport.com/']","Kansas City International Airport (IATA: MCI, ICAO: KMCI, FAA LID: MCI) (originally Mid-Continent International Airport) is a public airport 15 miles (24 km) northwest of downtown Kansas City in Platte County, Missouri. In 2017, 11.50 million passengers used the airport.",what is the name of the airport in kansas city kansas
is new zealand part of asia or australia,"['https://thegrid.co.nz/new-zealand/', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/New_Zealand', 'https://www.factsmania.org/oceania/facts-about-oceania.htm', 'https://globalhealthaging.org/category/australia/page/2/', 'https://dreammountain.net/around-the-world/', 'https://dreammountain.net/australia/', 'http://myscienceschool.org/index.php?/archives/7327-What-are-the-seven-continents-of-the-world.html']","The Australian continent, being part of the Indo-Australian plate, is the lowest, flattest, and oldest landmass on Earth and it has had a relatively stable geological history. New Zealand is not part of the continent of Australia, but of the separate, submerged continent of Zealandia. New Zealand and Australia are both part of the Oceanian sub-region known as Australasia, with New Guinea being in Melanesia. The term Oceania is often used to denote the region encompassing the Australian continent, Zealandia and various islands in the Pacific Ocean that are not included in the seven-continent model.",is new zealand part of asia or australia
what kind of weapons did the confederate soldiers use,"['http://www.taichinederland.nl/en/the-first-and-the-last/', 'https://www.varsitytutors.com/ged_social_studies-help/united-states-history/content-areas/civil-war', 'https://www.encyclopedia.com/history/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/urbanization-0', 'https://nationalheritagemuseum.typepad.com/library_and_archives/american_history_19th_century/', 'https://www.cram.com/essay/Abraham-Lincoln-And-The-Civil-War/PKKAXDP2BXYW', 'https://dokumen.tips/documents/black-history-month-catalog.html', 'http://www.civil-conflict.org/']","The American Civil War, fought between the Union and Confederate forces, took place from 1861 to 1865. During the war, a variety of weapons were used on both sides. These weapons include edged weapons such as knives and swords, firearms such as, rifled-muskets, breech loaders and repeating weapons, various field guns such as artillery, and new weapons such as the early grenade and machine gun.",what kind of weapons did the confederate soldiers use
