how much gold is in 24 karat gold,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Carat_(purity).html', 'https://www.2shapes.com/blog/fineness-gold-world']","Various ways of expressing fineness have been used and two remain in common use: millesimal fineness expressed in units of parts per 1,000 and karats used only for gold. Karats measure the parts per 24, so that 18 karat = ​ ⁄ = 75% and 24 karat gold is considered 100% gold.",how much gold is in 24 karat gold
where did the term buffalo soldiers come from,"['https://www.upandcomingweekly.com/views/5232-the-buffalo-soldiers', 'https://thelorenetwork.com/2017/06/15/0a0x-nightmask/', 'http://burnettpublishing.com/lamp2016/', 'http://www.cuppaonline.com/buffalo-soldiers-mugs/', 'http://www.buffalosoldierstacoma.org/historical-facts---education-program.html', 'http://www.jamesriverarts.net/artist-profiles/2016/1/24/stan-webb-graphic-artist', 'https://upstanderconnection.wordpress.com/']","Buffalo Soldiers originally were members of the 10th Cavalry Regiment of the United States Army, formed on September 21, 1866, at Fort Leavenworth, Kansas. This nickname was given to the Negro Cavalry by Native American tribes who fought in the Indian Wars. The term eventually became synonymous with all of the African American regiments formed in 1866:",where did the term buffalo soldiers come from
how many languages are spoken in washington state,"['http://telephoneusa.net/phonenumber/804-895-6193.html', 'https://www.hgh.tv/usa-hgh-clinics/virginia/', 'http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Demographics_of_New_York', 'https://churchlady.net/resources/', 'http://bronx.com/census.html', 'https://sphsp.org/find-a-chapter/usa/stat-of-missouri/state-missouri/', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/St._Louis,_Missouri']","In 2010, 82.51% (5,060,313) of Washington residents age 5 and older spoke English at home as a primary language, while 7.79% (477,566) spoke Spanish, 1.19% (72,552) Chinese (which includes Cantonese and Mandarin), 0.94% (57,895) Vietnamese, 0.84% (51,301) Tagalog, 0.83% (50,757) Korean, 0.80% (49,282) Russian, and German was spoken as a main language by 0.55% (33,744) of the population over the age of five. In total, 17.49% (1,073,002) of Washington's population age 5 and older spoke a mother language other than English.",how many languages are spoken in washington state
where is macau located on the world map,"['https://vectormap.info/product/printable-map-macau-china-vector-street-g-view-level-12-5-km-scale-map-full-editable-in-english-adobe-illustrator/', 'https://www.thelaw.com/threads/cheater-sites-wont-remove-posting.72502/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/180205001-geographic-regions', 'https://www.mapsland.com/asia/macau', 'https://realtyww.info/search/country,HK', 'http://www.maqbulah.com/holiday-package/25/extravaganza-hongkong-family-tour', 'https://alchetron.com/Macau']","Macau (Chinese: 澳門, Cantonese: (ōu. mǔːn), / məˈkaʊ / (listen); Portuguese: Macau), officially the Macao Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China, is an autonomous territory on the western side of the Pearl River estuary in East Asia. Along with Hong Kong, Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Zhuhai, and several other major cities in Guangdong, the territory forms a core part of the Pearl River Delta metropolitan region, the most populated area in the world. With a population of 650,900 in an area of 30.5 km (11.8 sq mi), it is the most densely populated region in the world.",where is macau located on the world map
why does an archerfish need to be still,"['http://www.bruning.com/about/fish/archerfish/', 'https://www.sosassociates.com/blog/2015-08-19-biomimicry']","Archerfish are remarkably accurate in their shooting; an adult fish almost always hits the target on the first shot. They can bring down insects and other prey up to 3 m (10 ft) above the water's surface. This is partially due to their good eyesight, but also to their ability to compensate for the refraction of light as it passes through the air-water interface when aiming at their prey. They typically spit at prey at a mean angle of about 74 ° from the horizontal but can still aim accurately when spitting at angles between 45 ° and 110 °.",why does an archerfish need to be still
who sings he lives in you lion king,"['http://fucinantica.com/casual/he-lives-in-you-english.php', 'http://www.inmusicwetrust.com/articles/16a01.html', 'http://www.disneycentralplaza.com/t34053p75-hong-kong-disneyland-nouveaux-lands-en-prevision', 'http://www.madridtourist.info/']","""He Lives in You"" is a song written and performed by Lebo M. and his South African Choir for the album Rhythm of the Pride Lands. A shorter version of the song was used for the opening of The Lion King II: Simba's Pride. It is also performed twice in the musical version of The Lion King. The song was co-written by Mark Mancina and Jay Rifkin.",who sings he lives in you lion king
where was the garden of eden according to the bible,"['http://craft-art.info/42840-the-fall-of-eden-and-its-inhabitants/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Garden_of_Eden.html', 'http://viddy.com/garden-of-eden-utopia.html', 'http://indiracesarine.com/exhibits/eden-spring-break-art-show-2019/', 'https://www.softpower.ug/full-statement-integrate-or-perish-museveni-tells-africa/', 'https://sandiborgens.com/news', 'http://articles.ochristian.com/article1931.shtml']","According to the Bible, the location of Eden is described in the Book of Genesis, chapter 2, verses 10 -- 14 as the source of four tributaries. However, the Garden of Eden is considered to be mythological by most scholars. Among those that consider it to have been real there have been various suggestions for its location: for example, at the head of the Persian Gulf, in southern Mesopotamia (now Iraq) where the Tigris and Euphrates rivers run into the sea; and in the Armenian Highlands or Armenian Plateau, among other proposed locations.",where was the garden of eden according to the bible
why is the nobel prize for literature awarded,"['https://wikimili.com/en/List_of_Italian_Nobel_laureates', 'http://mlmconsultant.info/search?q=Articles%20on%20nobel%20prize', 'https://wikimili.com/en/List_of_Indian_Nobel_laureates', 'http://bilbo.economicoutlook.net/blog/?p=5079', 'https://www.marinabaysands.com/museum/exhibition-archive/the-nobel-prize-ideas-changing-the-world.html', 'https://www.marinabaysands.com/museum/exhibition-archive/the-nobel-prize-ideas-changing-the-world/the-exhibition.html', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/nobel-peace-prize']","The Nobel Prize in Literature (Swedish: Nobelpriset i litteratur) has been awarded annually, since 1901, to an author from any country who has, in the words of the will of Alfred Nobel, produced ""in the field of literature the most outstanding work in an ideal direction"" (original Swedish: den som inom litteraturen har producerat det mest framstående verket i en idealisk riktning). Though individual works are sometimes cited as being particularly noteworthy, here ""work"" refers to an author's work as a whole. The Swedish Academy decides who, if anyone, will receive the prize in any given year. The academy announces the name of the chosen laureate in early October. It is one of the five Nobel Prizes established by the will of Alfred Nobel in 1895; the others are the Nobel Prize in Chemistry, Nobel Prize in Physics, Nobel Peace Prize, and Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine.",why is the nobel prize for literature awarded
when did zika virus come to the us,"['https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/powerpost/wp/2016/09/06/another-failed-zika-vote-could-be-the-start-of-a-resolution/', 'https://www.aol.com/article/news/2016/11/21/florida-county-to-fight-zika-with-genetically-modified-mosquitoes/21610893/', 'https://www.newscientist.com/article/2099798-there-could-already-be-40000-people-carrying-zika-in-the-us/', 'https://www.texasstandard.org/stories/researchers-at-utmb-look-to-existing-drugs-for-zika-treatment/']","United States On 29 July 2016, the CDC confirms 4 cases of locally transmitted cases of Zika infection in Miami, Florida, the first locally transmitted cases confirmed in the mainland US.",when did zika virus come to the us
why is world aids day important and what does it aim to achieve,"['https://1901.ajli.org/world-aids-day/', 'http://worthydavis.com/321.html', 'http://secretsdoll.com/adventure/aids-day-slogans.php', 'http://www.pngall.com/world-aids-day-png', 'https://aho.org/events/', 'http://www.cafca.org/index.cfm?alias=news&categoryID=13', 'https://ifpnews.com/exclusive/over-8000-rapid-hiv-testing-centres-active-in-iran/']","World AIDS Day, designated on 1 December every year since 1988, is dedicated to raising awareness of the AIDS pandemic caused by the spread of HIV infection, and mourning those who have died of the disease. Government and health officials, non-governmental organizations and individuals around the world observe the day, often with education on AIDS prevention and control.",why is world aids day important and what does it aim to achieve
where is trinidad and tobago located on the map,"['http://vagabundsa.com/index.php/vagabund-log-2013/vagabund-log-2013-trinidad.html', 'https://www.exportportal.com/category/computer-cables-and-connectors/405/country/trinidad-and-tobago-226', 'http://1234christmas.com/christmas-in-trinidad-and-tobago/1344/', 'http://pense.com.br/early-childhood-education-in-trinidad-and-tobago.html', 'https://factsking.com/countries/trinidad-and-tobago/', 'https://www.caribbeanopus.com/en/jobs/island/trinidad-tobago', 'http://www.alooha.net/travel_population_Trinidad-and-Tobago_tt.html']","Trinidad and Tobago (/ ˈtrɪnɪˌdæd ən təˈbeɪɡoʊ / (listen), /-toʊˈ-/), officially the Republic of Trinidad and Tobago, is a twin island country situated off the northern edge of the South American mainland, lying just 11 kilometres (6.8 miles) off the coast of northeastern Venezuela and 130 kilometres (81 miles) south of Grenada. Bordering other Caribbean nations to the north, it shares maritime boundaries with other nations including Barbados to the northeast, Grenada to the northwest, Guyana to the southeast, and Venezuela to the south and west.",where is trinidad and tobago located on the map
