is toronto north or south of the equator,"['http://explorer.natureserve.org/servlet/NatureServe?searchName=Carex+vaginata', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/45th_parallel_north.html', 'http://www.showersandmore.com/ss.php', 'https://notveryfar.net/2018/05/30/i-finally-found-it/', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/countries-that-border-only-one-country.html', 'http://akstp.com/alaskahighway/historicmile1221.html', 'http://www.roverlandcampers.co.uk/6-reasons-why-we-love-our-truck-after-12-months/']","In North America, the 45th parallel forms some boundaries, and passes through the U.S. states of Oregon, Idaho, South Dakota, Minnesota, Wisconsin, Michigan, New York, Vermont, New Hampshire and Maine and through the Canadian provinces of Ontario, Quebec, New Brunswick and Nova Scotia.",is toronto north or south of the equator
where is the heart found in your body,"['https://pdmhorizon.fandom.com/wiki/Human_Heart_Report', 'https://knowledgist9.com/how-the-heart-works-step-by-step/', 'http://sakkampress.com/www-human-heart-structure-com.html', 'http://ictm-ists-conference.info/?newsid=30754', 'http://ahw-ft2-htt-ea.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=28254', 'http://milkdud40.info/?newsid=28762', 'http://dramaworkshops.info/?page_id=49223']","The human heart is situated in the middle mediastinum, at the level of thoracic vertebrae T5-T8. A double-membraned sac called the pericardium surrounds the heart and attaches to the mediastinum. The back surface of the heart lies near the vertebral column, and the front surface sits behind the sternum and rib cartilages. The upper part of the heart is the attachment point for several large blood vessels -- the venae cavae, aorta and pulmonary trunk. The upper part of the heart is located at the level of the third costal cartilage. The lower tip of the heart, the apex, lies to the left of the sternum (8 to 9 cm from the midsternal line) between the junction of the fourth and fifth ribs near their articulation with the costal cartilages.",where is the heart found in your body
where is catalonia what is the most important city in catalonia,"['http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Catalonia', 'http://www.fact-index.com/c/ca/catalonia.html', 'https://drokov.com/region/catalonia', 'https://www.world-travel-directory.net/europe/spain/catalonia/', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Catalonia', 'https://www.insightsonindia.com/2018/04/08/solutions-insights-revision-test-for-preliminary-exam-2018-test-17/', 'http://turismoencatalunya.es/en/Catalonia-General-information.html']","Catalonia (Catalan: Catalunya, Occitan: Catalonha, Spanish: Cataluña) is an autonomous community of Spain located on the northeastern extremity of the Iberian Peninsula. It is one of Spain's eight communities which are designated as a nationality by their Statute of Autonomy. Catalonia consists of four provinces: Barcelona, Girona, Lleida, and Tarragona. The capital and largest city is Barcelona, the second-most populated municipality in Spain and the core of the seventh most populous urban area in the European Union. Catalonia comprises most of the territory of the former Principality of Catalonia (with the remainder Roussillon now part of France's Pyrénées-Orientales). It is bordered by France and Andorra to the north, the Mediterranean Sea to the east, and the Spanish autonomous communities of Aragon to the west and Valencia to the south. The official languages are Catalan, Spanish, and the Aranese dialect of Occitan.",where is catalonia what is the most important city in catalonia
which is better for you purified water or distilled water,"['https://www.reference.com/web?q=distilled+water+deionized+water+difference&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://iytmed.com/drinking-distilled-water/', 'https://www.veoliawatertechnologies.co.uk/?page=2', 'https://www.veoliawatertechnologies.co.uk/blog', 'http://ketek.ca/2018/10/10/the-science-of-pumping-water/', 'http://drinkingwatertap.com/drinking-water-tap-accessories/drinking-water-treatment-process.html', 'https://top5best.org/the-differences-between-distilled-water-and-deionized-water/']","Distilled water is water that has been boiled into steam and condensed back into liquid in a separate container. Impurities in the original water that do not boil below or at the boiling point of water remain in the original container. Thus, distilled water is one type of purified water.",which is better for you purified water or distilled water
where is alaska range located on a map,"['https://www.worldatlas.com/webimage/countrys/namerica/usstates/akassortedphotos.htm', 'https://majormike.us/photographs/year-of-2017/233/', 'http://alaskaweatherwatch.com/dwCamHR2.php', 'https://kateamirault.com/2018/11/07/while-we-were-driving-north-through-british-columbia/', 'http://universal-denizen.blogspot.com/2011/', 'https://basecampmagazine.com/2017/03/08/the-seven-summits-according-to-messner/', 'https://www.ezilon.com/maps/north-america-physical-maps.html']","The Alaska Range is a relatively narrow, 650-km-long (400 mi) mountain range in the southcentral region of the U.S. state of Alaska, from Lake Clark at its southwest end to the White River in Canada's Yukon Territory in the southeast. The highest mountain in North America, Denali, is in the Alaska Range. It is part of the American Cordillera.",where is alaska range located on a map
write a note on the history of linux,"['https://www.elprocus.com/linux-operating-system/', 'http://www.wikidifference.com/difference-between-windows-and-linux/', 'https://www.jeffreykopcak.com/category/amateur-radio/page/2/', 'https://forum.kernelnewbies.org/read.php?10,118081,page=2', 'http://linuxplace.net/articles/article_0002.php', 'http://www.kitsonlinetrainings.com/linux-online-training.html', 'https://www.androidhit.in/2018/10/windows-vs-linux-who-win-and-why.html']","The history of Linux began in 1991 with the commencement of a personal project by Finnish student Linus Torvalds to create a new free operating system kernel. Since then, the resulting Linux kernel has been marked by constant growth throughout its history. Since the initial release of its source code in 1991, it has grown from a small number of C files under a license prohibiting commercial distribution to the 4.2. 3 version in 2015 with more than 18 million lines of source code under the GNU General Public License v2.",write a note on the history of linux
who played in the 2000 afl grand final,"['https://lisaravinteet.info/16025.htm', 'https://guidedoc.tv/documentary/1990-afl-grand-final-documentary-film/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Matt_Stevic', 'https://www.superstarsonline.com.au/product/adelaide-crows/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Carlton_Football_Club', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Showdown_(AFL)', 'https://getawaytrekking.com.au/australia/holidays-and-festivals/']","The 2000 AFL Grand Final was an Australian rules football game contested between the Melbourne Football Club and the Essendon Football Club, held at the Melbourne Cricket Ground in Melbourne on 2 September 2000. It was the 104th annual Grand Final of the Australian Football League (formerly the Victorian Football League), staged to determine the premiers for the 2000 AFL season. The match, attended by 96,249 spectators, was won by Essendon by a margin of 60 points, marking that club's 16th premiership victory (following Carlton Football Club who also have 16 premierships).",who played in the 2000 afl grand final
where did i dream of jeannie come from,['http://inwoodhood.tripod.com/jea.html'],"The series was created and produced by Sidney Sheldon in response to the great success of rival network ABC's Bewitched series, which had debuted in 1964 as the second-most watched program in the United States. Sheldon, inspired by the movie The Brass Bottle, which had starred Tony Randall, Barbara Eden, and Burl Ives as the jinn Fakrash, conceived of the idea for a beautiful female genie. Both I Dream of Jeannie and Bewitched were Screen Gems productions. The show debuted at 8 pm, Saturday, September 18, 1965, on NBC.",where did i dream of jeannie come from
what kind of car is a subaru outback,"['https://www.bidgolive.com/Nigeria/Used-Subaru-Outback-For-Sale-At-IAA.html', 'https://difference.guru/difference-between-subaru-wrx-and-sti/', 'https://www.patrickssubaru.com/blog/2019/april/10/we-have-the-used-vehicle-options-you-want-at-patrick-subaru.htm?locale=en_US', 'https://www.cannonsubaru.com/subaru-outback-lease-specials.htm', 'http://pulseclassicgold.co.uk/', 'https://bestlocksmithbrisbane.com.au/lost-car-keys/subaru.html', 'https://www.garminheaven.com/category/vehicles-car/']","The Subaru Outback is an automotive nameplate used by the Japanese automobile manufacturer Fuji Heavy Industries (FHI) since 1994. The ""Outback"" name has been utilized on two different Subaru branded vehicles. One of these models is based on the mid-sized Subaru Legacy and the other derived from the hatchback version of the Subaru Impreza. The model is named after the vast, remote, and arid outback regions in Australia; the name is intended to emphasize the moderate off-road capability of the vehicle, while also giving a nod to the original design, which had a larger trunk ""out back"" than the Legacy.",what kind of car is a subaru outback
what is the main difference between lymph and interstitial fluid,"['http://wortherkunft.de/~e/u_/uk-anatom.html', 'https://www.cliftonmassage.co.uk/the-lymphatic-system/', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Lymph', 'https://www.healthyandnaturalworld.com/ultimate-anti-inflammatory-smoothie/', 'https://www.basepaws.com/blog/autoimmune-lymphoproliferative-syndrome-alps', 'http://dbpedia.org/page/Lymph', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/lymphatic']","Lymph is the fluid that circulates throughout the lymphatic system. The lymph is formed when the interstitial fluid (the fluid which lies in the interstices of all body tissues) is collected through lymph capillaries. It is then transported through larger lymphatic vessels to lymph nodes, where it is cleaned by lymphocytes, before emptying ultimately into the right or the left subclavian vein, where it mixes back with the blood.",what is the main difference between lymph and interstitial fluid
whats the difference between a canyon and a gorge,"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Canyon', 'http://www.primidi.com/what_is_canyon', 'http://travellers-world.info/3003-yosemite-slot-canyon.php', 'http://as806.tk/casino-i-70-kansas.html']","The word canyon is Spanish in origin (cañón, pronounced (kaˈɲon)), with the same meaning. The word canyon is generally used in North America while the words gorge and ravine are used in Europe and Oceania, though gorge and ravine are also used in some parts of North America. In the United States, place names generally use canyon in the southwest and gorge in the northeast, with the rest of the country graduating between these two according to geography. In Canada, a gorge is usually narrow while a ravine is more open and often wooded. The military-derived word defile is occasionally used in the United Kingdom.",whats the difference between a canyon and a gorge
who wrote the song one toke over the line,"['http://www.josephburke.com/broadcast/', 'http://www.e-profession.com/records/Brewer_And_Shipley_Mobile_record.html', 'http://www.codaconcerthouse.com/brewship', 'http://www.bytownukulele.ca/AllPosts/tabid/906/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/4040/One-Toke-Over-The-Line.aspx']","Brewer & Shipley are an American folk rock duo who enjoyed their peak success in the late 1960s through the 1970s, consisting of singer-songwriters Mike Brewer and Tom Shipley. They were known for their intricate guitar work, vocal harmonies, and socially conscious lyrics which reflected the concerns of their generation -- especially the Vietnam War, and the struggles for personal and political freedom. Their greatest commercial success was the song ""One Toke Over the Line"" from their 1970 album Tarkio. They had two other singles on the Billboard charts: ""Tarkio Road"" (1970) and ""Shake Off The Demon"" (1971). They continue to perform, both separately and together, usually in the Midwest of the USA.",who wrote the song one toke over the line
how far is phoenix az from chandler az,['https://bankruptcy-az.com/experienced-consumer-bankruptcy-attorneys-chandler-az/'],"Chandler has reached its physical limits save for some remaining county islands and cannot expand outward anymore due to being bound in by the Gila River Indian Community, Tempe, Mesa, Gilbert, and Phoenix.",how far is phoenix az from chandler az
why did the civil war in el salvador start,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Meyer_Brownstone', 'http://priphistory.weebly.com/salvadorian-civil-war.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Central_American_crisis', 'http://amesnews.com.au/latest-articles/analysis-has-us-meddling-in-central-america-come-home-to-roost/']","The Salvadoran Civil War was a conflict between the military-led government of El Salvador and the Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front (FMLN), a coalition or ""umbrella organization"" of several left-wing groups. A coup on October 15, 1979, led to the killings of anti-coup protesters by the government as well as anti-disorder protesters by the guerrillas, and is widely seen as the tipping point toward civil war.",why did the civil war in el salvador start
when would an emergency session of congress be held,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Military_history_of_Canada_during_World_War_II', 'https://definitions.uslegal.com/s/special-session/']","In a legislature, a special session (also extraordinary session) is a period when the body convenes outside of the normal legislative session. This most frequently occurs in order to complete unfinished tasks for the year (often delayed by conflict between political parties), such as outlining the government's budget for the next fiscal year, biennium, or other period. Special sessions may also be called during an economic downturn in order to cut the budget. In other cases, a special session may be convened to address special topics, or emergencies such as war or natural disaster.",when would an emergency session of congress be held
what impact did world war i have on the ottoman empire,"['http://www.fouman.com/Y/Wiki.php?eterm=Turkey', 'http://francona.blogspot.com/2018/03/what-are-erdogans-intentions-after-fall.html', 'https://www.intrepidtravel.com/us/turkey', 'https://ottomanhistory.net/node/48', 'https://wiki.kidzsearch.com/wiki/Turkey', 'https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/countries/23424969/', 'http://ehbed.witnesstoday.org/index.php/categories/44-reference/history/world-history/271-ottoman-empire']","The Ottoman Empire participated in World War I as one of the Central Powers. The Ottoman Empire entered the war by carrying out a surprise attack on Russia's Black Sea coast on 29 October 1914, with Russia responding by declaring war on 5 November 1914. Ottoman forces fought the Entente in the Balkans and the Middle Eastern theatre of World War I. The Ottoman Empire's defeat in the war in 1918 was crucial in the eventual dissolution of the empire in 1921.",what impact did world war i have on the ottoman empire
modern psychology is defined as the science of the mind,"['http://blogathome06.com/q0zd1d9m7.html', 'https://www.kenyon.edu/directories/campus-directory/biography/leah-dickens/', 'http://www.ccna-ccnp-training.com/nu,cna-courses-nmu.asp', 'https://graduateway.com/schools-thoughts-psychology/', 'https://www.vivekananthahomeoclinic.com/2014/11/the-psychologist-psychological.html', 'http://sunnysidemagazine.org/2014/12/', 'https://mentalhealth.global-summit.com/']","Today, psychology is defined as ""the scientific study of behavior and mental processes."" Philosophical interest in the mind and behavior dates back to the ancient civilizations of Egypt, Persia, Greece, China, and India.",modern psychology is defined as the science of the mind
what inspired whitney houston to become a singer,"['https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2017/02/11/', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2015/02/11/', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2012/08/09/', 'http://today-this-musician-died.blogspot.com/2012/02/', 'https://www.siluriabaptist.com/blog/2016/10/16/gods-word-is-clear-on-choosing-a-mate']","At the age of 11, Houston started performing as a soloist in the junior gospel choir at the New Hope Baptist Church in Newark, where she also learned to play the piano. Her first solo performance in the church was ""Guide Me, O Thou Great Jehovah"". When Houston was a teenager, she attended Mount Saint Dominic Academy, a Catholic girls' high school in Caldwell, New Jersey, where she met her best friend Robyn Crawford, whom she described as the ""sister she never had"". While Houston was still in school, her mother continued to teach her how to sing. Houston was also exposed to the music of Chaka Khan, Gladys Knight, and Roberta Flack, most of whom would have an influence on her as a singer and performer.",what inspired whitney houston to become a singer
majestic theatre majestic theatre broadway 245 west 44th st,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Schoenfeld_Theatre', 'http://www.nycmanhattan.org/p/majestic-theater.html', 'https://www.capitalcitytickets.com/Phantom-of-the-Opera-Tickets', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Shenandoah_(musical)', 'https://www.tixtm.com/wicked-tickets-gershwin-theatre-new-york-ny-3718299/', 'http://www.ibroadwaytickets.com/events/al-hirschfeld-theatre', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Helen_Hayes']","The Majestic Theatre is a Broadway theatre located at 245 West 44th Street in midtown Manhattan. It is one of the largest Broadway theatres with 1,645 seats, and traditionally has been used as a venue for major musical theatre productions. Among the notable shows that have premiered at the Majestic are Carousel (1945), South Pacific (1949), The Music Man (1957), Camelot (1960), A Little Night Music (1973), and The Wiz (1975). It was also the second home of 42nd Street and the third home of 1776. The theatre has housed The Phantom of the Opera since it opened on January 26, 1988. With a record-breaking 12,139 performances to date, it is currently the longest-running production in Broadway history.",majestic theatre majestic theatre broadway 245 west 44th st
who is the nra and what do they do,"['https://cindyforminnesota.com/endorsements', 'http://soonertactical.com/html/training.html', 'https://www.showmastersgunshows.com/affiliates.html', 'http://dsarange.com/second-amendment-associations/', 'https://beyondthegrassyknoll.com/what-is-the-nra-national-rifle-association/', 'http://kagayakuzyosi.info/viewtopic.php?t=47952', 'http://wwebb.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=25335']","The National Rifle Association of America (NRA) is an American nonprofit organization that advocates for gun rights. Founded in 1871, the group has informed its members about firearm-related legislation since 1934, and it has directly lobbied for and against firearms legislation since 1975.",who is the nra and what do they do
what's the 25th amendment to the constitution,"['http://www.mobilestec.com/25th-amendment/', 'https://llb2.com/2018/09/13/did-the-caine-mutiny-shape-the-original-public-meaning-of-the-25th-amendment/', 'http://trailmix.cc/home/2019/02/10/sunday-serendipity-141/', 'http://webot.org/info/en/?search=Article_Two_of_the_United_States_Constitution', 'https://thinkwingradio.com/2017/02/20/thinkwing-mon2202017-9pm-kpfthouston-90-1fm-topics-not-my-presidents-day-what-happens-in-sweden-a-govt-by-generals-billionaires-what-sayeth-the-1st/', 'https://bexuquy.teachereducationexchange.com/essays-written-to-urged-ratification-of-the-constitution-7938xf.html', 'http://williamcalvin.com/bk2/bk2ch12.htm']","The Twenty-fifth Amendment (Amendment XXV) to the United States Constitution deals with issues related to presidential succession and disability. It clarifies that the vice president becomes president (as opposed to acting president) if the president dies, resigns, or is removed from office; and establishes procedures for filling a vacancy in the office of the vice president and for responding to presidential disabilities. The Twenty-fifth Amendment was submitted to the states on July 6, 1965, by the 89th Congress and was adopted on February 10, 1967.",what's the 25th amendment to the constitution
where was the emperor in a new hope,"['http://hotindiareport.com/tv-movies/star-wars-series-the-mandalorians-first-footage-unveiled/', 'http://buncbimaca.cf/star-wars-toys-ru-lyt.php', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Return_of_the_Jedi', 'http://arv8.info/viewtopic.php?t=21663', 'http://silvertrendz.com/star-wars-destiny-deck-list.html', 'https://av321.info/9216c5321e.html', 'http://if-yu.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=42004']","The Emperor is briefly mentioned in the original Star Wars, the first film in the original trilogy. Grand Moff Tarkin explains to his fellow Imperials that the Emperor has dissolved the Senate.",where was the emperor in a new hope
who were the group of american leaders representing the colonies,"['http://webot.org/info/en/?search=Patriot_(American_Revolution)', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Patriot_(American_Revolution)']","As a group, Patriots represented a wide array of social, economic and ethnic backgrounds. They included lawyers like John Adams and Alexander Hamilton; planters like Thomas Jefferson and George Mason; merchants like Alexander McDougall and John Hancock; and ordinary farmers like Daniel Shays and Joseph Plumb Martin. Patriots also included slaves and freemen such as Crispus Attucks, a free man and the first martyr of the American Revolution; James Armistead Lafayette, who served as a double agent for the Continental Army; and Jack Sisson, who, under the command of Colonel William Barton, was leader of the first successful black operation mission in American history, resulting in the capture of British General Richard Prescott.",who were the group of american leaders representing the colonies
the 3rd amendment prohibition on forced boarding of soldiers,"['https://communiquerenligne.com/photo/be-the-third-owner-ever-of-this-18th-century-dutch-house.html', 'http://godliterature.tk/ssso/bill-of-rights-paper-meki.php', 'https://southwritlarge.com/articles/kosher-pork/', 'https://www.smore.com/5j8h1', 'https://www.majortests.com/essay/Bill-Of-Rights-523260.html', 'https://www.justipedia.com/definition/5611/third-amendment', 'http://www.spectacle.org/496/clark.html']","The Third Amendment (Amendment III) to the United States Constitution places restrictions on the quartering of soldiers in private homes without the owner's consent, forbidding the practice in peacetime. The amendment is a response to Quartering Acts passed by the British parliament during the buildup to the American Revolutionary War, which had allowed the British Army to lodge soldiers in private residences.",the 3rd amendment prohibition on forced boarding of soldiers
what are in and out burgers made of,"['http://dlhweblog.blogspot.com/2013/07/in-n-out-burger-and-be-entertained.html', 'https://eatingisthehardpart.com/2011/04/26/in-n-out-burger-baldwin-park-california/', 'http://www.allaboutceil.com/2017/05/burgs-by-project-warung-quality-burgers.html']","All burgers consist of zero (in the case of a' grilled cheese') or more 2 oz (57 g) beef patties cooked to ""medium-well"", and served on a toasted bun. The standard style of burger includes tomato, hand-leafed lettuce and ""spread"", a sauce similar to Thousand Island dressing.",what are in and out burgers made of
what is the purpose of the nasal conchae,['http://vetsci.co.uk/2010/05/05/specialsensessmell/'],"In humans, the turbinates divide the nasal airway into 4 groove-like air passages, and are responsible for forcing inhaled air to flow in a steady, regular pattern around the largest possible surface area of nasal mucosa, which, as a ciliated mucous membrane with shallow blood supply, cleans and warms the inhaled air in preparation for the lungs.",what is the purpose of the nasal conchae
what is the weather like in canada in the winter,"['https://simplexitytravel.com/destinations/north-america/canada', 'https://skyrockliving.com/coldest-city-in-canada/', 'http://www.theindependentbd.com/arcprint/details/185744/2019-02-02', 'https://sekhriacademy.com/canada.php', 'https://blog.moneysmart.sg/opinion/migrate-canada/', 'http://thomastraveltales.com/manitoba/how-to-avoid-typical-canadian-winter-weather.php', 'http://nihpodcast.blogspot.com/']","The major Canadian city that falls outside the continental climate schema is Vancouver, which experiences an oceanic climate with a marked summer dry season. Of the eight largest Canadian cities, Ottawa, Montreal and Toronto have the warmest summers, Winnipeg the coldest winters, while Vancouver's winters are far milder than any other large city in Canada.",what is the weather like in canada in the winter
how many fights did ali and frazier have,"['https://worldinsport.com/joe-frazier-smokin-joe/', 'https://blackthen.com/remembering-boxing-great-smokin-joe-frazier/', 'https://www.ducksters.com/biography/athletes/muhammad_ali.php']","Ali and Frazier met for the third and final time in Quezon City (a district within the metropolitan area of Manila), the Philippines, on October 1, 1975: the ""Thrilla in Manila"". Prior to the fight, Ali took opportunities to mock Frazier by calling him a' ""gorilla"", and generally trying to irritate him.",how many fights did ali and frazier have
what are the parts of a watch strap called,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Watch_strap.html', 'http://www.bistrofrancaisdc.com/page/2/', 'https://www.hodinkee.com/articles/the-patek-philippe-reference-5208t-010-in-titanium-for-only-watch-2017', 'https://wristreview.com/oris-aquis-depth-guage-chronograph-watch/', 'https://ukwatchstrap.co.uk/Fluco-Zeppelin-White-K.html', 'http://www.jewelwatch.co.nz/watches.php?brand=Hublot']","Watch straps may close with a buckle or a folding clasp. Expanding watch straps are designed to expand elastically, often by the use of metal springs in a segmented design, and may be slipped on like a bracelet. Attachment points for the strap to the watch are largely standardized, with a spring-loaded double-ended pin used to anchor the watch strap to holes in a bracket that is integral to the watch case, allowing worn watch straps to be replaced or swapped with new straps for fashion purposes.",what are the parts of a watch strap called
where does the name strictly come dancing come from,"['http://www.top10christmas.co.uk/strictly_come_dancersize_dvd.php', 'https://richtopia.com/entity/strictly-come-dancing', 'http://kris-wu.tk/black-speed-dating-london-2013.html', 'https://www.famechain.com/search/association/605/strictly-come-dancing-2004-contestants-series-2', 'http://blakenhall.tk/top-matchmaking-rating-dota-2.html', 'http://blakenhall.tk/shrinathji-haveli-in-bangalore-dating-2019.html', 'http://honeysoft.tk/hazel-evers-american-horror-story-actress-dating.html']","Strictly Come Dancing (informally known as Strictly) is a British television dance contest, featuring celebrity contestants, with professional dance partners competing in a ballroom and Latin dance competition. Each couple is scored out of 10 by a panel of judges. The title of the show suggests a continuation of the long-running series Come Dancing, with an allusion to the film Strictly Ballroom. The format has been exported to over 40 other countries, and has also inspired a modern dance-themed spin-off Strictly Dance Fever. The show is currently presented by Tess Daly and Claudia Winkleman.",where does the name strictly come dancing come from
