what is the captain of a ship called,"['http://seamanjobs.ph/blog/', 'http://electrotechnical-officer.com/all-about-merchant-marine-rank-with-pictures/', 'https://crewaboard.com/captain', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=cruise+ship+captain+qualifications&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'http://withoutannette.net/victoria/how-to-get-captains-hat.php', 'http://penangseow.blogspot.com/2009/06/captain-seow.html', 'http://marinerbootcamp.com/deck-department/']","A sea captain, ship's captain, captain, master, or shipmaster, is a high-grade licensed mariner in ultimate command of the merchant vessel. The captain is responsible for its safe and efficient operation, including: ship's seaworthiness, ship's safety and security conditions, cargo operations, navigation, crew management and ensuring that the vessel complies with local and international laws, as well as company and flag state policies. All persons on board, particularly during navigation, including, public authorities, state authorities, officers and crew, other shipboard staff members, passengers, guests and pilots, are under the captain's authority and are his or her ultimate responsibility.",what is the captain of a ship called
are ipad air and ipad air 2 same size,"['http://battlefield-3-beta.tk/rns-310-sd-slot-defekt.html', 'http://christian-life.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=34331', 'http://haggisofnorway.tk/gambling-diseases.html', 'http://go2mob.tk/roulette-high-win.html', 'http://claytonjunior.tk/significato-di-roulette-russa.html', 'http://hydsex.tk/tickets-casino-rama.html', 'https://www.smemarkethub.com/stores/harumala/products/145402/apple-ipad-air-2-16gb/']","The iPad Air 2 is the second-generation iPad Air tablet computer designed, developed, and marketed by Apple Inc. It was announced on October 16, 2014 alongside the iPad Mini 3, both of which were released on October 22, 2014. The iPad Air 2 is thinner and faster than its predecessor, the iPad Air, and features Touch ID with the height and screen size the same as the iPad Air.",are ipad air and ipad air 2 same size
what is the largest inner city park in the world,"['http://countrylicious.com/australia/tourist-attractions', 'https://islandtravels.com.au/perth/', 'http://999photos.com/australia/kings_park_perth.shtml', 'https://spark.adobe.com/page/mtfhHuoBqBQBf/', 'https://www.hertz.co.uk/p/car-hire/netherlands/zoetermeer', 'https://www.perthluxurytours.com/tours/', 'http://www.weekends-in-france.com/holiday-in-paris/']","It is the largest inner city park in the world and the most popular visitor destination in Western Australia, being visited by over five million people each year. The park is larger than New York's Central Park which is 3.41 km2.",what is the largest inner city park in the world
what is the difference between croque monsieur and madame,"['https://jesseyancy.com/2018/04/', 'https://www.theydrawandcook.com/search/results?search%5Bconditions%5D%5Bingredients%5D=Ham', 'https://www.africanbites.com/croque-madame/', 'http://www.twocouplescooking.com/recipe/croque-madame/', 'https://storyinshort.com/different-types-of-sandwiches-around-the-globe-you-must-try-at-least-once-in-your-life/', 'http://www.food-recipes.me/croque-senor/', 'http://youarecurrent.com/2018/10/18/the-croque-monsieur-a-french-twist/']","A croque monsieur (French pronunciation: ​ (kʁɔk məsˈjøː); French for ""mister crunch"") is a baked or fried boiled ham and cheese sandwich. The dish originated in French cafés and bars as a quick snack. A croque madame is a version of the dish topped with a fried egg.",what is the difference between croque monsieur and madame
when did the stolen generation start and end,"['https://alterlinks.ca/Info/WWWHeading1180.htm', 'https://bbs.chinadaily.com.cn/thread-1857933-1-1.html', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/6923750', 'http://blogs.bluebec.com/david-van-gend-arse-hat-of-the-week/', 'https://formaementis.wordpress.com/category/oceania/australia/', 'http://blog.simonhay.com.au/2016/08/energysoul-healing-heals-trans.html', 'https://thetheatretimes.com/churning-waters-muffled-voices-flow/']","The Stolen Generations (also known as Stolen Children) were the children of Australian Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent who were removed from their families by the Australian Federal and State government agencies and church missions, under acts of their respective parliaments. The removals of those referred to as ""half-caste"" children were conducted in the period between approximately 1905 and 1967, although in some places mixed-race children were still being taken into the 1970s.",when did the stolen generation start and end
where is the capital of new york located,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Fort_Wayne_Komets', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=albanyreal.com&ads=1&author=system&auto=Albany+real&title=Albany+real&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Albany+real&pagenum=3', 'https://globalquiz.org/en/toughest-map-riddles/', 'http://albany.city.live/', 'https://jbesheer.equitasny.com/neighborhood-city/27174/Albany', 'https://albany-factoring-companies.factoringcompanyaccount.com/', 'https://www.mapquest.com/us/ny/albany-282038956']",Albany (/ ˈɔːlbəni / (listen) ALL-bə-nee) is the capital of the U.S. state of New York and the seat of Albany County. Albany is located on the west bank of the Hudson River approximately 10 miles (16 km) south of its confluence with the Mohawk River and approximately 150 miles (240 km) north of New York City.,where is the capital of new york located
when did polynesian settlers arrived in new zealand (approximately),"['http://www.spiritwrestler.com/catalog/index.php?q=M%C4%81ori&amp;sort=6d&amp;page=9', 'http://www.hinemihi.co.uk/page.php?id=19', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/M%C4%81ori_people', 'https://joyofmuseums.com/museums/australasia-museums/new-zealand-museums/museums-in-auckland/auckland-art-gallery-toi-o-tamaki/masterpieces-and-historical-objects-of-the-auckland-art-gallery-toi-o-tamaki/paratene-te-manu-by-gottfried-lindauer/', 'https://blog.lareviewofbooks.org/arts-culture/art/art-inside-fieldnotes-2/', 'https://wn.com/Maori_post?from=maoripost.com', 'http://desnuda.top/Keisha%20Castle-Hughes']","The Māori (/ ˈmaʊri /; Māori pronunciation: (ˈmaːɔɾi), listen) are the indigenous Polynesian people of New Zealand. Māori originated with settlers from eastern Polynesia, who arrived in New Zealand in several waves of canoe voyages some time between 1250 and 1300. Over several centuries in isolation, the Polynesian settlers developed a unique culture, with their own language, a rich mythology, and distinctive crafts and performing arts. Early Māori formed tribal groups based on eastern Polynesian social customs and organisation. Horticulture flourished using plants they introduced; later, a prominent warrior culture emerged.",when did polynesian settlers arrived in new zealand (approximately)
what is the elevation of myrtle beach sc,"['https://www.torta-a-porta.com/broadway-at-the-beach-oceanfront-hotels-21st-street-myrtle-beach/', 'http://www.dustbust.us/myrtle-beach-maid.html', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Myrtle%20Beach%2C%20South%20Carolina.html', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/Myrtle_Beach,_South_Carolina', 'https://www.homesnacks.net/sc/myrtle-beach/', 'https://americanpurespringwater.com/myrtle-beach-bottled-water-delivery/', 'http://pay4golf.com/city.php?cityId=570']","Myrtle Beach is a coastal city on the East Coast of the United States in Horry County, South Carolina. It is situated on the center of a large and continuous 60-mile stretch of beach known as ""The Grand Strand"" in northeastern South Carolina.",what is the elevation of myrtle beach sc
who built the san francisco de asis mission,"['https://capturinggrace.org/capturinggrace/2013/03/09/san-francisco-the-oregoncalifornia-coastal-adventure-comes-to-a-conclusion/', 'https://pilgrimage.ph/mission-churches-guadalupe', 'http://owj.ca/vacations/2008/2008-01-03-san-francisco/san-francisco-eng.html', 'https://rentalcarmomma.com/dollar/san-francisco-rental-car.htm']","Mission San Francisco de Asís, or Mission Dolores, is the oldest surviving structure in San Francisco and the sixth religious settlement established as part of the California chain of missions. The Mission was founded on June 29, 1776, by Lieutenant José Joaquin Moraga and Francisco Palóu (a companion of Junípero Serra), both members of the de Anza Expedition, which had been charged with bringing Spanish settlers to Alta (upper) California, and evangelizing the local Natives, the Ohlone.",who built the san francisco de asis mission
where is bile produced and where is it stored,"['http://party-net.info/?page_id=40543', 'https://pediaa.com/what-is-the-difference-between-hepatic-bile-and-gallbladder-bile/', 'http://www.liverfoundation-ne.org/', 'http://www.pudaschemes.com/baking-soda-tattoo-removal/', 'https://www.vitalityherbsandclay.com/blogs/vital-health-newsletter-blog/q-a-what-everyone-ought-to-know-about-digestive-enzymes-and-bile-supplements', 'https://biology.stackexchange.com/questions/55927/cholesterol-and-fatty-acids-role-in-bile', 'https://www.newcrosshealthcare.com/knowledge-base/glossary/b']","Bile or gall is a dark green to yellowish brown fluid, produced by the liver of most vertebrates, that aids the digestion of lipids in the small intestine. In humans, bile is produced continuously by the liver (liver bile), and stored and concentrated in the gallbladder (gallbladder bile). After eating, this stored bile is discharged into the duodenum. The composition of gallbladder bile is 97% water, 0.7% bile salts, 0.2% bilirubin, 0.51% fats (cholesterol, fatty acids and lecithin), and 200 meq / l inorganic salts.",where is bile produced and where is it stored
who said most of an atoms mass is in the nucleus,"['http://julianrouw.tk/atomic-structure-a-level-physics-formula-sheet.html', 'https://www.nuclear-power.net/nuclear-power/reactor-physics/atomic-nuclear-physics/atom-properties-of-atoms/atomic-nucleus/', 'https://nuclear-energy.net/definitions/atomic-nucleus.html', 'http://encyclopedia2.thefreedictionary.com/Infundibular+nucleus', 'https://wymarad.palmolive2day.com/nuclear-energy-essay-introduction-26749ba.html', 'https://rastanj.me/post/2011-f-150-interior-fuse-diagram', 'https://www.shutterstock.com/video/search/proton']","The atomic nucleus is the small, dense region consisting of protons and neutrons at the center of an atom, discovered in 1911 by Ernest Rutherford based on the 1909 Geiger -- Marsden gold foil experiment. After the discovery of the neutron in 1932, models for a nucleus composed of protons and neutrons were quickly developed by Dmitri Ivanenko and Werner Heisenberg. Almost all of the mass of an atom is located in the nucleus, with a very small contribution from the electron cloud. Protons and neutrons are bound together to form a nucleus by the nuclear force.",who said most of an atoms mass is in the nucleus
what is the squiggly line above spanish words called,"['https://www.lynnecameron.com/blog/2017/2/16/tilde', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Unicode', 'https://puzzles.blainesville.com/2018/07/npr-sunday-puzzle-jul-1-2018-your-title.html', 'https://english.stackexchange.com/questions/28601/appropriate-dash-to-use-when-attributing-a-quotation']","The tilde (/ ˈtɪldə / or / ˈtɪldi /; _̃ or ~) is a grapheme with several uses. The name of the character came into English from Spanish and from Portuguese, which in turn came from the Latin titulus, meaning ""title"" or ""superscription"".",what is the squiggly line above spanish words called
how many us states border the gulf of mexico,"['http://bossbitch.tk/flowers-slots-review.html', 'http://csetest.tk/deambulateur-a-roulette-bastide.html', 'http://lochoadau.tk/blackjack-frame-machine.html', 'http://enigma-hq.tk/norwegian-dawn-casino-age.html', 'http://apstats.tk/casino-2000-luxembourg-review.html', 'http://befored.tk/blackjack-retaining-wall.html', 'http://distancias.tk/blackjack-week-6.html']","The Gulf Coast of the United States is the coastline along which the Southern United States meets the Gulf of Mexico. The coastal states that have a shoreline on the Gulf of Mexico are Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama, and Florida, and these are known as the Gulf States.",how many us states border the gulf of mexico
where does the term 4 20 come from,"['http://www.windermeresun.com/2018/04/20/origin-of-weed-day-420-has-come-a-long-way/', 'https://www.wallyhood.org/2018/04/420-party-420/', 'https://happytravelersweedtours.com/420-national-cannabis-day-the-history-celebrations-and-things-to-do/', 'http://www.takamineforum.com/forum3/viewtopic.php?f=8&p=77301', 'https://valetudocafe.wordpress.com/tag/smoke-out/', 'https://daedalushowell.com/blog/the-origin-of-420/', 'https://www.cute-calendar.com/event/420-weed-day/36551.html']","In 1971, five high school students -- Steve Capper, Dave Reddix, Jeffrey Noel, Larry Schwartz, and Mark Gravich -- in San Rafael, California, calling themselves the Waldos because ""their chosen hang-out spot was a wall outside the school"", used the term in connection with a 1971 plan to search for an abandoned cannabis crop that they had learned about, based on a treasure map made by the grower. The Waldos designated the Louis Pasteur statue on the grounds of San Rafael High School as their meeting place, and 4: 20 p.m. as their meeting time. The Waldos referred to this plan with the phrase ""4: 20 Louis"". After several failed attempts to find the crop, the group eventually shortened their phrase to simply ""4: 20"", which ultimately evolved into a codeword that the teens used to mean consuming cannabis.",where does the term 4 20 come from
who made up the central powers in world war i,"[""https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Kitchener's_Army"", 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Central_Powers', 'http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Central_Powers', 'http://welladjustedbabies.com/queensland/the-summer-before-the-war-pdf.php', 'http://links.org.au/1918-good-bye-to-all-that-but-not-for-everyone', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Greek_genocide.html', 'http://cheminsdememoire.gouv.fr/en/la-premiere-guerre-mondiale-1914-1918']","The Central Powers (German: Mittelmächte; Hungarian: Központi hatalmak; Turkish: İttifak Devletleri / Bağlaşma Devletleri; Bulgarian: Централни сили, translit. Tsentralni sili), consisting of Germany, Austria-Hungary, the Ottoman Empire and Bulgaria -- hence also known as the Quadruple Alliance (German: Vierbund) -- was one of the two main factions during World War I (1914 -- 18). It faced and was defeated by the Allied Powers that had formed around the Triple Entente. The Powers' origin was the alliance of Germany and Austria-Hungary in 1879. The Ottoman Empire and Bulgaria did not join until after World War I had begun, although the Ottoman Empire retained close relations with both Germany and Austria-Hungary since the beginning of the 20th century.",who made up the central powers in world war i
where do you find portuguese man of war,"['https://literock969.com/thats-no-jellyfish-lbi-lifeguards-find-potentially-deadly-man-o-war/', 'http://www.annoocrochetdesigns.com/2013/03/my-friendly-version-of-portuguese-man-o.html', 'https://www.zmescience.com/science/oceanography/portuguese-man-of-war-06072015/']","The Atlantic Portuguese man o' war lives at the surface of the ocean. The gas-filled bladder, or pneumatophore, remains at the surface, while the remainder is submerged. As the Portuguese man o' war has no means of propulsion, they move according to the winds, currents, and tides. Although they are most commonly found in the open ocean in tropical and subtropical regions, they have been found as far north as the Bay of Fundy, Cape Breton and the Hebrides.",where do you find portuguese man of war
where is sunderban delta located in india map,"['https://comedymood.com/top-10-wildlife-sanctuaries-of-india/', 'https://www.visit2himalaya.com/sundarban-information.php', 'http://blogsauthor.com/best-travel-spot/', 'http://ksch.org.in/elementor-731/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171218015-forests', 'https://sevenwonders.org/asia/bangladesh/', 'http://bagerhat.gov.bd/site/top_banner/cef16c30-1c3a-11e7-8f57-286ed488c766']","The Sundarbans is a vast forest in the coastal region of the Bay of Bengal, considered one of the natural wonders of the world, it was recognised in 1997 as a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Located in the delta region of Padma, Meghna and Brahmaputra river basins, this unique forest area extends across South 24 Parganas and, North 24 Parganas districts of West Bengal State, India and Khulna, Satkhira, Bagerhat districts of Bangladesh. The Sundarbans is the worlds largest coastal mangrove forest, with an area of approximately 10,000 sq km; of which approximately 6,000 sq km is situated in Bangladesh and approximately 4,000 sq km in India. The Bangladeshi and Indian parts of the Sundarbans, while in fact adjacent parts of the uninterrupted landmark, have been listed separately in the UNESCO World Heritage List: as ""Sundarbans"" and ""Sundarban National Park"" respectively. The Sundarbans are a network of marine streams, mud shores and mangrove forests. The region is known to contain numerous species of animals, birds and reptiles, including Royal Bengal Tiger, Chital Deer, Crocodile and Snakes. On 21 May 1992, the Sundarbans was recognized as a Ramsar Site of ecological importance.",where is sunderban delta located in india map
is the star in scrabble a double word,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Newtown%2C_Connecticut', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Scrabble', 'https://marahabout.fandom.com/wiki/Scrabble', 'http://menapia-scrabble-club.yolasite.com/what-is-scrabble.php', 'http://www.shwegames.com/boardgame/word-war-i']","The board is marked with ""premium"" squares, which multiply the number of points awarded: eight dark red ""triple-word"" squares, 17 pale red ""double-word"" squares, of which one, the center square (H8), is marked with a star or other symbol; 12 dark blue ""triple-letter"" squares, and 24 pale blue ""double-letter"" squares. In 2008, Hasbro changed the colors of the premium squares to orange for TW, red for DW, blue for DL, and green for TL. Despite this, the original premium square color scheme is still the preferred scheme for Scrabble boards used in tournaments.",is the star in scrabble a double word
which breakaway russian republic had grozny as its capital,"['https://centr-bk.kazan.wscentr-bk.kazan.ws/cgi-bin/eng/view.pl?idr=12&mr=11', 'https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Place:Chechnya%2C_Yuzhny%2C_Russia', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/North_Caucasus', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/where-is-chechnya.html', 'https://www.llrx.com/2002/04/features-researching-tajik-law-a-guide-to-the-tajik-legal-system/', 'http://earthcharter.org/news-post/tatarstan-surges-forward-to-implement-the-principles-of-the-charter/', 'https://islandprofiles.com/a-short-history-of-corsica']","It is located in the North Caucasus, situated in the southernmost part of Eastern Europe, and within 100 kilometres (62 miles) of the Caspian Sea. The capital of the republic is the city of Grozny. As of the 2010 Russian Census, the republic was reported to have a population of 1,268,989 people; however, that number has been questioned by multiple demographers, who think such population growth after two deadly wars is highly implausible.",which breakaway russian republic had grozny as its capital
what is dear evan hansen the musical about,"['https://www.silive.com/entertainment/arts/2018/05/wagner_grad_alex_boniello_join.html', 'https://archive.triblive.com/aande/theaterarts/13455921-74/pittsburgh-hamilton-dates-pnc-broadway-series-announced', 'https://www.mylondon.news/whats-on/music-nightlife-news/dear-evan-hansen-tickets-presale-16001875', 'https://www.collegemarching.com/content/michigan-salutes-dear-evan-hansen', 'http://hcseattle.clubs.harvard.edu/article.html?aid=449', 'http://www.waynetwp-il.org/event/trip_2019-02_-_Oriental_Theatre/calendar_list', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/12-04/all']","The titular character, Evan Hansen, is a high school senior with severe social anxiety, which inhibits his ability to connect with other people and make friends. After the death of one of his classmates, he fabricates a lie that inadvertently brings him closer to the classmate's family, while also allowing him to gain his own sense of purpose.",what is dear evan hansen the musical about
who is the main officer in the department's office located at the district level,"['https://basti.nic.in/collectorate/', 'https://ambedkarnagar.nic.in/collectrate/', 'http://rebelle.club/2018/11/page/4']","A district collector, often abbreviated to collector, is an Indian Administrative Service (IAS) officer in charge of revenue collection and administration of a district in India. Since district collectors are senior-most executive magistrate in the district, the post is also referred to as the district magistrate and as the office-bearer works under the supervision of a divisional commissioner, the post is also known as deputy commissioner.",who is the main officer in the department's office located at the district level
what is the theme of the story baba yaga,"['http://thomas-kurniawan.blogspot.com/2014/02/doodle-10-babayaga.html', 'http://blog.annatsp.com/2014/04/atozchallenge-baba-yaga.html', 'http://www.onceuponabookcase.co.uk/2019/03/legendary-beings-well-known-witches.html', 'https://intlxpatr.wordpress.com/category/paris/', 'http://www.courtney-foxworthy.com/legendary-creatures', 'https://www.laserbrainpatchco.com/shop/product/1533708528_baba-yaga-witch-house', 'http://selectcarapp.ml/afrikaans-baba-name-1649.php']","In Slavic folklore, Baba Yaga / ˈbɑːbə jəˈɡɑː / (Russian: Баба-яга, Polish: Baba Jaga) is a supernatural being (or one of a trio of sisters of the same name) who appears as a deformed and / or ferocious-looking witch. Baba Yaga flies around in a mortar, wields a pestle, and dwells deep in the forest in a hut usually described as standing on chicken legs (or sometimes a single chicken leg). Baba Yaga may help or hinder those that encounter or seek her out. She sometimes plays a maternal role, and also has associations with forest wildlife. According to Vladimir Propp's folktale morphology, Baba Yaga commonly appears as either a donor or villain, or may be altogether ambiguous.",what is the theme of the story baba yaga
where do alligators live in the united states,"['http://animal-wildlife.blogspot.com/2011/10/alligator.html', 'https://a-z-animals.com/animals/alligator/', 'https://owlcation.com/stem/Whats-the-difference-between-alligators-and-crocodiles', 'https://www.pinellascountyparks.org/2015/03/alligators-and-crocodiles-part-1.html', 'http://1stpip.com/watch-out-the-most-dangerous-animals-in-florida/', 'https://www.experiencekissimmee.com/blog/7-fun-kissimmee-facts', 'https://www.worldanimalfoundation.com/advocate/wild-animals/params/post/1294335/alligators']","American alligators are found in the southeast United States: all of Florida and Louisiana; the southern parts of Georgia, Alabama, and Mississippi; coastal South and North Carolina; East Texas, the southeast corner of Oklahoma, and the southern tip of Arkansas. According to the 2005 Scholastic Book of World Records, Louisiana has the largest alligator population. The majority of American alligators inhabit Florida and Louisiana, with over a million alligators in each state. Southern Florida is the only place where both alligators and crocodiles live side by side.",where do alligators live in the united states
the central idea of theory of constraints (toc) is based on the,"['https://patents.google.com/patent/US7440907B2/en', 'http://gregepp.com/the-theory-of-constraints/', 'https://essayzoo.org/book-report/apa/accounting/stocks-for-the-long-run.php', 'https://www.safalniveshak.com/latticework-of-mental-models-theory-of-constraints/', 'https://readingraphics.com/book-summary-the-goal-a-process-of-ongoing-improvement/', 'http://vitecgroup.it/the-goal-a-process-of-ongoing-improvement.html', 'https://scioncreative.net/goal-teen-essays/']","The underlying premise of the theory of constraints is that organizations can be measured and controlled by variations on three measures: throughput, operational expense, and inventory. Inventory is all the money that the system has invested in purchasing things which it intends to sell. Operational expense is all the money the system spends in order to turn inventory into throughput. Throughput is the rate at which the system generates money through sales.",the central idea of theory of constraints (toc) is based on the
what did rahab ask the spies to do for her,"['https://biblehub.com/joshua/2-10.htm', 'http://biblical.ie/page.php?fl=NRSV/Joshua', 'https://www.blythwood.org/index.php/sermons/406', 'https://biblehub.com/joshua/2-11.htm', 'http://wiki.mrlocke.net/index.php?title=Sermon_for_November_30th,_2014&amp;action=history', 'https://www.amazingfacts.org/media-library/media/e/946/t/joshua-part-2--from-jordan-to-jericho', 'https://yearinthebible.com/2012/06/']","I know that the LORD has given you the land, and that dread of you has fallen on us, and that all the inhabitants of the land melt in fear before you. For we have heard how the LORD dried up the water of the Red Sea before you when you came out of Egypt, and what you did to the two kings of the Amorites that were beyond the Jordan, to Sihon and Og, whom you utterly destroyed. As soon as we heard it, our hearts melted, and there was no courage left in any of us because of you. The LORD your God is indeed God in heaven above and on earth below. Now then, since I have dealt kindly with you, swear to me by the LORD that you in turn will deal kindly with my family. Give me a sign of good faith that you will spare my father and mother, my brothers and sisters, and all who belong to them, and deliver our lives from death.",what did rahab ask the spies to do for her
what does the message at the bottom of the pow mia flag mean,"['https://2nddistrict.webs.com/', 'https://holy-cuteness.info/opening-ceremony-black-and-navy-striped-varsity-sweater.asp', 'https://www.mcarbo.com/pow-/-mia-die-cut-vinyl-decal-sticker.aspx', 'http://www.canyon-news.com/congress-displays-flags-supporting-transgender-community/90459', 'https://www.vfw.org/Flag']","The National League of Families POW / MIA flag, also known as the POW / MIA flag, consists of a silhouette of a prisoner of war (POW) before a guard tower and barbed wire in white on a black field. ""POW / MIA"" appears above the silhouette and the words ""You Are Not Forgotten"" appear below in white on the black field.",what does the message at the bottom of the pow mia flag mean
where does the term wendy house come from,"['http://www.ahwendyhouses.co.za/cp/21663/history-of-the-wendy-house.php', 'https://www.perform.org.uk/about-perform/meet-lucy/2018/05/10-things-you-never-knew-about-neverland/', 'https://www.allroundfun.co.uk/outdoor-play/playhouses/tp-toys-skye-wooden-playhouse--slide', 'https://www.dictionary.com/browse/peter-pan', 'https://www.latestdeals.co.uk/tags/playhouse', 'https://www.audible.com/pd/The-Little-Mermaid-Audiobook/B07C4H6P3M', 'http://lewistonchamber.org/tasmania/peter-pan-jm-barrie-pdf-download.php']","The original was built for Wendy Darling in J.M. Barrie's play, Peter Pan, or The Boy Who Wouldn't Grow Up. Wendy was shot by the Lost Boy Tootles after arriving in Neverland, so Peter Pan and the Lost Boys built a small house around her where she had fallen. It was inspired by the wash-house behind Barrie's childhood home in Kirriemuir and first appeared in story form in The Little White Bird in which fairies build a house around Mamie Mannering -- the prototype for Wendy -- so protecting her from the cold.",where does the term wendy house come from
what is year 0 in the jewish calendar,"['https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/70016/jewish/The-Jewish-Leap-Year.htm', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Jewish_calendar.html', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Hebrew_calendar', 'https://www.mywesternwall.net/2010/12/12/how-is-this-year-different-from-all-other-years.html']","The Jewish calendar is based on the Metonic cycle of 19 years, of which 12 are common (non-leap) years of 12 months and 7 are leap years of 13 months. To determine whether a Jewish year is a leap year, one must find its position in the 19-year Metonic cycle. This position is calculated by dividing the Jewish year number by 19 and finding the remainder. For example, the Jewish year 5778 divided by 19 results in a remainder of 2, indicating that it is year 2 of the Metonic cycle. Since there is no year 0, a remainder of 0 indicates that the year is year 19 of the cycle.",what is year 0 in the jewish calendar
how many teams make the playoff in mlb,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Wild_card_(sports)', 'https://news.wagertalk.com/mlb-prop-bets/odds-to-win-2019-wild-card-game-rockies-9-1', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Major_League_Baseball_postseason.html', 'http://recomparison.com/comparisons/101322/wild-card-vs-non-wild-card-how-are-they-different/', 'http://loyolaphoenix.com/2015/09/30-chicago-names-you-should-know/', 'https://vtcynic.com/sports/mlbwildcard/']","In Major League Baseball (MLB), the wild card teams are the two teams in each of the two leagues (American and National) that have qualified for the postseason despite failing to win their division. Both teams in each league possess the two best winning percentages in their respective league after the three division winners. The wild card was first instituted in MLB in 1994, with one wild-card team per league advancing to the Division Series in the postseason to face a division winner. In 2012, the system was modified to add a second wild-card team per league and put each league's wild-card teams against each other in a play-in game -- the MLB Wild Card Game -- the winner of which would then advance to the Division Series and play the team with the best record. This system ensures that the team with the second-best record in each league, after the three division winners and the team with the first-best record in the league that is a non-division winner, will also get a postseason berth, even if it isn't a division champion.",how many teams make the playoff in mlb
what was the tax rate in the 1980s,"['http://govlocations.uk/tax-office-leeds-telephone-number-information-on-government-locations/', 'https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2017/03/19/tax-burden-wealthy-has-trebled-since-1970s-telegraph-analysis/', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Taxation_in_the_United_Kingdom', 'https://www.economicshelp.org/blog/11697/debt/post-war-boom/']","The Government of Margaret Thatcher, who favoured indirect taxation, reduced personal income tax rates during the 1980s. In the first budget after her election victory in 1979, the top rate was reduced from 83% to 60% and the basic rate from 33% to 30%. The basic rate was also cut for three successive budgets -- to 29% in the 1986 budget, 27% in 1987 and to 25% in 1988. The top rate of income tax was cut to 40% in the 1988 budget. The investment income surcharge was abolished in 1985.",what was the tax rate in the 1980s
why was harry potter name in the goblet of fire,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Harry_Potter_and_the_Goblet_of_Fire_(film).html', 'http://harrypotter.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Severus_Snape', 'https://harrypotter.fandom.com/wiki/Second_Wizarding_War', 'https://harrypotter.fandom.com/wiki/Cedric_Diggory', 'https://hpaudiobooks.club/goblet-of-fire-audiobook-stephen-fry/10/', 'https://janeaustenrunsmylife.wordpress.com/tag/mistreated/', 'http://hplf.forumotion.com/t311-godric-s-hollow']","Harry tells Dumbledore that Voldemort returned and killed Cedric. Moody takes Harry back to his office to interrogate him about Voldemort, but inadvertently blows his cover by asking Harry whether there were ""others in the graveyard"", despite Harry not mentioning a graveyard. Moody reveals that he submitted Harry's name to the Goblet of Fire and manipulated Harry throughout the tournament to ensure he would win. Moody attempts to attack Harry, but Dumbledore, Snape, and Minerva McGonagall intervene and subdue him. The teachers force Moody to drink Veritaserum, a truth-telling potion, and he reveals that the real Moody is imprisoned in a magical trunk. The impostor's Polyjuice Potion wears off, revealing him as Crouch Jr., who is then returned to Azkaban.",why was harry potter name in the goblet of fire
what are the main constituents of moulding sand,"['https://www.ijert.org/structural-behaviour-of-rc-beam-and-concrete-filled-steel-tubes-retrofitted-with-natural-rubber-sheet', 'https://www.charlesprogers.com/glossary.html', 'https://www.nytimes.com/1998/07/26/nyregion/home-repair-the-techniques-for-creating-textured-surfaces.html', 'https://cfpub.epa.gov/ncer_abstracts/index.cfm/fuseaction/display.abstractDetail/abstract/2177']","Green sand is an aggregate of sand, bentonite clay, pulverized coal and water. Its principal use is in making molds for metal casting. The largest portion of the aggregate is always sand, which can be either silica. There are many recipes for the proportion of clay, but they all strike different balances between moldability, surface finish, and ability of the hot molten metal to degas. The coal, typically referred to in as sea-coal, which is present at a ratio of less than 5%, partially combusts in the surface of the molten metal leading to offgassing of organic vapors.",what are the main constituents of moulding sand
parts of these states made up the mexican border district,"['http://m.american-historama.org/mexican-migration.htm', 'http://www.immigrationwatchdog.com/cat_16/', 'http://wsppn.org/resources/u-s-mexico-border/', 'http://votersedge.library.ca.gov/ca/en/ballot/election/area/39/contests/contest/10813?election_authority_id=33', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/us-states-that-border-mexico.html', 'https://www.ars.usda.gov/research/publications/publication/?seqNo115=309278', 'http://infographic.replacenafta.org/nafta-at-25-promises-vs-reality/']","The U.S. states along the border, from west to east, are California, Arizona, New Mexico, and Texas. The Mexican states along the border are Baja California, Sonora, Chihuahua, Coahuila, Nuevo León, and Tamaulipas.",parts of these states made up the mexican border district
why did raiders and patriots play in mexico,"['https://theinscribermag.com/nfl-sets-international-series-schedule/', 'http://ahw-ft2-htt-ea.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=22073', 'http://bufetesabogados.info/viewtopic.php?t=46976', 'http://juniormarvel.tk/average-league-1-attendances-sheet.html', 'https://www.woodywoodmusic.com/packer-game-live-stream.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Twickenham_Stadium', 'http://www.eastlondonlines.co.uk/2013/02/american-cheerleaders-to-cheer-on-crystal-palace/']","Starting in the 2007 season, the National Football League (NFL) has hosted regular season American football games outside the United States every year. Collectively officially known through 2016 as the NFL International Series, from 2017 the series currently has two sub-series, the NFL London Games in London, which has been in place since 2007, and the NFL Mexico Game in Mexico City, which began in 2016 with a predecessor game in 2005.",why did raiders and patriots play in mexico
what is the legal blood alcohol limit in texas,"['http://fastbuddha.com/south-australia/how-to-get-alcohol-under-21-reddit.php', 'http://stephanvee.com/2017/08/07/how-to-behave-following-an-arrest-under-suspicion-of-dui/', 'https://www.scottmackenzie.com/criminal-law/dui-dwi/', 'http://aboutlittlerock.com/dui-dwi-laws-in-arkansas/', 'https://www.terrybryant.com/what-the-legal-process-for-drunk-driving-car-accidents', 'http://www.alcohollaws.org/arkansasalcohollaws.html', 'https://bubbahead.com/case-wins-georgia-judge-blocks-field-sobriety-test/']","An operator of a motor vehicle is considered under the influence of alcohol if a chemical screening test shows a blood-alcohol content of 0.08 percent or higher. No other evidence (such as Field Sobriety tests) need be presented to the court to obtain a DUI (driving under the influence) conviction. A driver testing 0.15 percent or more over the legal limit of 0.08 percent faces more severe penalties for enhanced BAC. When under the age of 21, a driver in Texas must not test positive for any blood-alcohol content (BAC) and may be charged with DUI even if the amount tested is under 0.08 percent.",what is the legal blood alcohol limit in texas
who said i came i saw i conquered when and where did it happen,"['http://www.youngblizzymusic.com/2015_04_22_archive.html', 'https://mursalan.wordpress.com/2017/11/', 'https://kenyachessmasala.com/2015/12/im-elijah-emojong-wins-the-2015-tanzania-open.html', 'https://mentalitch.com/greatest-quotes-from-roman-emperors/']","Veni, vidi, vici (Classical Latin: (ˈweːniː ˈwiːdiː ˈwiːkiː); Ecclesiastical Latin: (ˈvɛni ˈvidi ˈvitʃi); ""I came; I saw; I conquered"") is a Latin phrase popularly attributed to Julius Caesar who, according to Appian, used the phrase in a letter to the Roman Senate around 47 BC after he had achieved a quick victory in his short war against Pharnaces II of Pontus at the Battle of Zela. The phrase is used to refer to a swift, conclusive victory.",who said i came i saw i conquered when and where did it happen
why are world wars i and ii called total wars,"['http://sheepfold-ministries.org/SERMONFILES/2016%20sermons/HTML/20160710%20ENGAGING%20IN%20SPIRITUAL%20WARFARE.html', 'http://terranchronicles.com/blog/world-at-war', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/World_war', 'http://www.liquisearch.com/world_war', 'https://richtopia.com/entity/world-war', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Sint-Petrus-en-Pauluskerk', 'http://wdtprs.com/blog/2010/05/benedict-xvis-sermon-in-fatima-references-to-second-secret-maternity-of-god/']","A world war is a large-scale war involving many of the countries of the world or many of the most powerful and populous ones. World wars span multiple countries on multiple continents, with battles fought in many theaters. While a variety of global conflicts have been subjectively deemed ""world wars"", such as the Cold War and the War on Terror, the term is widely and generally accepted only as it is retrospectively applied to two major international conflicts that occurred during the 20th century: World War I (1914 -- 1918) and World War II (1939 -- 1945).",why are world wars i and ii called total wars
why is the secret service in charge of counterfeiting,"['http://www.thefullwiki.org/United_States_Secret_Service', 'https://pastandpresent.com/2018/11/27/origins-of-the-secret-service/', 'https://coinsblog.ws/collectors-reference/u-s-coin-and-currency-production', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Frank_J._Larkin', 'https://www.federallawenforcement.org/secret-service/what-is-the-secret-service/', 'http://pheeds.com/info/guide/u/un/united_states_secret_service_1.html', 'http://www.faqs.org/espionage/Re-Se/Secret-Service-United-States.html']","With a reported one third of the currency in circulation being counterfeit at the time, the Secret Service was created on July 5, 1865 in Washington, D.C., to suppress counterfeit currency. Chief William P. Wood was sworn in by Secretary of the Treasury Hugh McCulloch. It was commissioned in Washington, D.C. as the ""Secret Service Division"" of the Department of the Treasury with the mission of suppressing counterfeiting. The legislation creating the agency was on Abraham Lincoln's desk the night he was assassinated. At the time, the only other federal law enforcement agencies were the United States Park Police, the U.S. Post Office Department's Office of Instructions and Mail Depredations (now known as the United States Postal Inspection Service), and the U.S. Marshals Service. The Marshals did not have the manpower to investigate all crime under federal jurisdiction, so the Secret Service began to investigate everything from murder to bank robbery to illegal gambling. After the assassination of President William McKinley in 1901, Congress informally requested that the Secret Service provide presidential protection. A year later, the Secret Service assumed full-time responsibility for presidential protection. In 1902, William Craig became the first Secret Service agent to die while serving, in a road accident while riding in the presidential carriage.",why is the secret service in charge of counterfeiting
bible story about building your house on the rock,['https://herbertrsim.com/the-blessings-of-the-latter-rain-in-the-year-of-earth-pig/'],"The Parable of the Wise and the Foolish Builders, (also known as the House on the Rock), is a parable of Jesus appearing in the Gospel of Matthew (7: 24 -- 27) and Luke (6: 46 -- 49).",bible story about building your house on the rock
where does the dark reaction get its energy from,"['https://www.tsijournals.com/articles/making-science-that-really-explain-things-13433.html', 'https://trinhmanhdo.com/all-over-the-universe/', 'http://publishedauthors.forumotion.com/t12002-abe', 'https://thebiggestpicture.net/Dimensions', 'https://www.lemodesittjr.com/2018/01/', 'https://www.scienceworldreport.com/articles/59290/20170511/nasa-provides-detectors-esas-euclid-spacecraft-study-dark-matter-energy.htm', 'https://berternie.com/portfolio/digital-abstract-painting-dark-energy/']","Assuming that the standard model of cosmology is correct, the best current measurements indicate that dark energy contributes 68.3% of the total energy in the present-day observable universe. The mass -- energy of dark matter and ordinary (baryonic) matter contribute 26.8% and 4.9%, respectively, and other components such as neutrinos and photons contribute a very small amount. The density of dark energy (~ 7 × 10 g / cm) is very low, much less than the density of ordinary matter or dark matter within galaxies. However, it dominates the mass -- energy of the universe because it is uniform across space.",where does the dark reaction get its energy from
what is the point in no mans sky,"['http://www.daseuroforum.com/how-to-make-money-fast-still-make-millions-no-mans-sky-next-guide-see-pin/', 'https://www.sc-compressed.com/2017/08/no-mans-sky-pc-game-repack-compressed.html', 'http://gamehostz.net/videos/so-i-used-a-rare-fortnite-account-generator-and-it-actually-worked', 'https://www.gurubasics.com/top-5-games-deserve-attention/', 'http://congtu.tk/black-jack-allbud.html', 'https://forumbanter.com/threads/no-mans-sky.438/', 'http://gameshug.com/video/upcoming-games-in-june-2016-gameplay-compilation-gameplay-of-the-best-games-in-june']","No Man's Sky is an action-adventure survival game developed and published by the indie studio Hello Games. It was released worldwide for PlayStation 4 and Microsoft Windows in August 2016, and for Xbox One in July 2018. The game is built around four pillars: exploration, survival, combat, and trading. Players are free to perform within the entirety of a procedurally generated deterministic open world universe, which includes over 18 quintillion planets. Through the game's procedural generation system, planets have their own ecosystems with unique forms of flora and fauna, and various sentient alien species may engage the player in combat or trade within planetary systems. Players advance in the game by mining for resources to power and improve their spacecraft, tools, and spacesuit for survival, buying and selling resources using credits earned by documenting flora and fauna, and otherwise seeking out the mystery around the Atlas, an entity at the center of the universe.",what is the point of no mans sky
what is the significance of 777 in the bible,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/777_(number).html', 'https://www.gospelherald.com/archives/articles/tags/2016-presidential-election', 'https://bibleforums.org/archive/index.php/t-271521.html?s=17c60c540019babbba7c2d2947a25717', 'http://torahrapministry.blogspot.com/2008/07/bit-of-hebrew-religion.html?showComment=1217712120000', 'http://www.jacksmithprophecy.org/2015/09/23/blood-moon-tetrad-embedded-in-muslim-and-jewish-feast-days/', 'https://thelostcityofcarcosa.com/2015/02/', 'http://thisisouranthem.com/2018/01/the-believer-and-the-desert/']","Christian denominations consider seven to be a holy number because Genesis says that God rested on the 7th day and man was created on the 6th day. Because God rested on the 7th day, that is the reason for the observance of the Hebrew Sabbath on the last day of the week. The 7th day of the week is indicated on the Hebrew Lunar calendar containing 13 months of four weeks each. According to the American publication, the Orthodox Study Bible, 777 represents the threefold perfection of the Trinity.",what is the significance of 777 in the bible
what is the difference between uae and saudi arabia,"['http://almanac.afpc.org/Yemen', 'https://en.hdhod.com/Anti-Saudi-protests-in-Iran-as-row-smoulders_a15607.html', 'https://www.breitbart.com/tag/united-arab-emirates-uae/', 'https://www.sfchronicle.com/world/article/Attack-on-Iranian-military-parade-kills-at-least-13250306.php', 'https://geopoliticsalert.com/saudi-arabia-uae-yemen-africa-imperialism', 'https://concentricadvisors.com/crisis-in-the-gulf/', 'https://cvir.st-andrews.ac.uk/articles/10.15664/jtr.881/']","However, the UAE and Saudi Arabia continue to take somewhat differing stances on regional conflicts such the Yemeni Civil War, where the UAE opposes Al-Islah, and supports the Southern Movement, which has fought against Saudi-backed forces, and the Syrian Civil War, where the UAE has disagreed with Saudi support for Islamist movements.",what is the difference between uae and saudi arabia
what factors helped the european economy to expand in the high middle ages,['http://www.writeopinions.com/high-middle-ages'],"Key historical trends of the High Middle Ages include the rapidly increasing population of Europe, which brought about great social and political change from the preceding era, and the Renaissance of the 12th century, including the first developments of rural exodus and urbanization. By 1250 the robust population increase greatly benefited the European economy, reaching levels that would not be seen again in some areas until the 19th century. This trend faltered in the Late Middle Ages due to a series of calamities, notably the Black Death but also including numerous wars and economic stagnation.",what factors helped the european economy to expand in the high middle ages
gadar ek prem katha movie box office collection,"['http://misbeee.blogspot.com/2015/11/digital-africa-exploring-new-frontiers.html?updated-min=2015-01-01T00:00:00Z&updated-max=2016-01-01T00:00:00Z&max-results=36', 'https://msbwrites.co.uk/2015/11/15/digital-africa-exploring-new-frontiers-in-tv-and-film/', 'http://cinemazworld.com/old-hindi-movies-list-1980-super-hit-hindi-films/']","Gadar collected ₹ 78.6 crores in its initial theatrical run and its adjusted gross in 2017 ticket sales is 468 crores approx it was declared as ""All Time Blockbuster"" in box office Gadar ranks among the top three Indian films in all time highest footfalls. In the United Kingdom, Gadar grossed around £ 280,000.",gadar ek prem katha movie box office collection
who elected congress under the articles of confederation,"['http://www.revwartalk.com/03-01-1781-independence-congress-of-the-confederation-established-the-longer-running-congress-made-up-of-delegates-from-the-second-continental-congress/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Congress_of_the_Confederation', 'https://christianheritagefellowship.com/preacher-becomes-first-speaker-of-congress/', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Continental_Congress', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Confederation_Period', 'https://www.encyclopedia.com/history/united-states-and-canada/us-history/continental-congress', 'https://www.articlesofconfederation.com/']","The Congress of the Confederation, or the Confederation Congress, formally referred to as the United States in Congress Assembled, was the governing body of the United States of America that existed from March 1, 1781, to March 4, 1789. A unicameral body with legislative and executive function, it comprised delegates appointed by the legislatures of the several states. Each state delegation had one vote. It was preceded by the Second Continental Congress (1775 -- 1781) and governed under the newly adopted Articles of Confederation and Perpetual Union, which were proposed 1776 -- 1777, adopted by the Continental Congress in July 1778 and finally agreed to by a unanimous vote of all thirteen states by 1781, held up by a long dispute over the cession of western territories beyond the Appalachian Mountains to the central government led by Maryland and a coalition of smaller states without western claims, the plan introduced by Maryland politician John Hanson; the plan is referred to as' The Hanson Plan'. The newly reorganized Congress at the time continued to refer itself as the Continental Congress throughout its eight-year history, although modern historians separate it from the earlier bodies, which operated under slightly different rules and procedures until the later part of American Revolutionary War. The membership of the Second Continental Congress automatically carried over to the Congress of the Confederation when the latter was created by the ratification of the Articles of Confederation. It had the same secretary as the Second Continental Congress, namely Charles Thomson. The Congress of the Confederation was succeeded by the Congress of the United States as provided for in the new Constitution of the United States, proposed September 17, 1787, in Philadelphia and ratified by the states through 1787 to 1788 and even into 1789 and 1790.",who elected congress under the articles of confederation
where did the name six sigma come from,"['http://www.homezweethome.info/2013/04/getting-best-production-results.html', 'http://www.7starservice.com/articles/what-makes-general-electric-and-other-fortune-500-companies-so-successful', 'https://eolas.ie/job_tag/six-sigma/', 'https://www.kanbanchi.com/lean-management', 'https://www.britecoatings.com/awards-and-memberships.html', 'https://www.exceldashboardtemplates.com/friday-challenge-analyzing-attendance-records-with-six-sigma-charts/', 'http://www.alalamalaan.com/?page=course/lean-six-sigma-black-belt-iassc-accredited-with-official-iassc-exam/']","The term Six Sigma (capitalized because it was written that way when registered as a Motorola trademark on December 28, 1993) originated from terminology associated with statistical modeling of manufacturing processes. The maturity of a manufacturing process can be described by a sigma rating indicating its yield or the percentage of defect-free products it creates. A six sigma process is one in which 99.99966% of all opportunities to produce some feature of a part are statistically expected to be free of defects (3.4 defective features per million opportunities). Motorola set a goal of ""six sigma"" for all of its manufacturing operations, and this goal became a by-word for the management and engineering practices used to achieve it.",where did the name six sigma come from
who sings the song just enough for the city,"['https://www.jakereichbart.com/news-blog.html?start=248', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/wyclef-jeans-greatest-hits-2851752', 'https://www.the-paulmccartney-project.com/song/aint-that-a-shame/', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/earth-wind-and-fire-classics-2851557', 'http://www.jackson5abc.com/2015/08/16/the-jackson-5-ten-greatest-hits/', 'http://billiejean.be/Discography/The_Jackson_5_Albums_1.html', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Tracy_Chapman']","""Living for the City"" is a 1973 single by Stevie Wonder from his Innervisions album. It reached number 8 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart and number 1 on the R&B chart. Rolling Stone ranked the song number 105 on their list of the ""500 Greatest Songs of All Time"".",who sings the song just enough for the city
when did karachi become the capital of pakistan,"['http://bagskart.com/early-problems-of-pakistan.html', 'https://meetcornor.wordpress.com/category/history/history-of-karachi/', 'https://gr.skyscanner.com/trip/karachi-pakistan', 'https://www.pakeproperty.com/societies/Karachi', 'http://worldpopulationreview.com/world-cities/karachi-population/', 'https://www.ready.pk/latest-jobs-in-karachi', 'http://www.airfaresflights.com.au/Holidays/Karachi']","Karachi was chosen as the capital city of Pakistan. After the independence of Pakistan, the city population increased dramatically when hundreds of thousands of Muslim Muhajirs from India fleeing from anti-Muslim pogroms and from other parts of South Asia came to settle in Karachi. As a consequence, the demographics of the city also changed drastically. The Government of Pakistan through Public Works Department bought land to settle the Muslim refugees. However, it still maintained a great cultural diversity as its new inhabitants arrived from the different parts of the South Asia. In 1959, the capital of Pakistan was shifted from Karachi to Islamabad and Karachi became the capital of Sindh.",when did karachi become the capital of pakistan
what book is song of songs in the bible,"['http://switchforfree.info/news.php?action=show&id=21248', 'http://objectembed.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=18157', 'http://ictm-ists-conference.info/?newsid=20602', 'http://jocbiliard.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=22529', 'http://salopette.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=25828', 'http://flatpress-fr.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=20163', 'http://zippo-lighter.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=30791']","The Song of Songs, also Song of Solomon or Canticles (Hebrew: שִׁיר הַשִּׁירִים ‬ Šîr HaŠîrîm, Greek: Ancient Greek: ᾎσμα ᾈσμάτων Âisma Āismátōn), is one of the megillot (scrolls) found in the last section of the Tanakh, known as the Ketuvim (or ""Writings""), and a book of the Old Testament.",what book is song of songs in the bible
what keyboard layout do we use in australia,"['http://eatyourheartoutboston.com/australian-capital-territory/how-to-get-pound-sign-on-australian-keyboard.php', 'http://www.englishgratis.com/1/wikibooks/americanenglish/britishandamericankeyboards.htm', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Australian_English', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Computer_keyboard', 'http://michelemcleodbarrelhorses.com/pronunciation-differences-between-american-and-australian-dating-wojaj13712n.php', 'http://usduconcno.cba.pl/beatles-happy-birthday-mp3-download-free.html']","There are two major English language computer keyboard layouts, the United States layout and the United Kingdom layout defined in BS 4822 (48-key version). Both are QWERTY layouts. Users in the United States do not frequently need to make use of the £ (pound) and € (euro) currency symbols, which are common needs in the United Kingdom and Ireland, although the $(dollar sign) symbol is also provided as standard on UK and Irish keyboards. In New Zealand the US keyboard layout is the de facto standard. In Australia, Canada, the Netherlands, Pakistan, Poland and India, the US keyboard might also be used.",what keyboard layout do we use in australia
how far is sandy springs from atlanta georgia,"['http://liveatlantaga.com/communities/sandy-springs/', 'https://www.metroatlantahome.com/about-sandy-springs/', 'https://www.atlantaintown.com/atlanta-neighborhoods/sandy-springs', 'http://www.atlanta-apartments-lofts.com/Sandy+Springs', 'https://georgiainfo.galileo.usg.edu/topics/historical_markers/county/fulton/the-history-of-the-city-of-sandy-springs-georgia', 'http://www.collettemcdonald.com/atlanta-neighborhoods/', 'http://liveatlantaga.com/communities/roswell/']","The boundaries of Sandy Springs are Atlanta to the south, Cobb County (at the Chattahoochee River) to the west and north, Roswell (also at the river) to the north, and Dunwoody and Brookhaven, at the DeKalb County line, to the east. A small panhandle in the northeast extends between the Chattahoochee River to the north and Dunwoody to the south, ending in a very small border with Peachtree Corners in Gwinnett County.",how far is sandy springs from atlanta georgia
the treaty of guadalupe hidalgo ending the mexican war provided for,"['http://teapartyeconomist.com/2014/04/16/showdown-nevada/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Presidency_of_James_K._Polk', 'https://susanharbagepage.com/new-and-ongoing-projects/', 'https://www.archives.gov/education/lessons/guadalupe-hidalgo', 'https://millercenter.org/president/james-k-polk/key-events', 'http://navajopeople.org/blog/category/navajo-history/', 'https://portside.org/node/1688/printable/print']","With the defeat of its army and the fall of its capital, Mexico entered into negotiations to end the war. The treaty called for the U.S. to pay USD $15 million to Mexico and to pay off the claims of American citizens against Mexico up to USD $3.25 million. It gave the United States the Rio Grande as a boundary for Texas, and gave the U.S. ownership of California and a large area comprising roughly half of New Mexico, most of Arizona, Nevada, and Utah, and parts of Wyoming and Colorado. Mexicans in those annexed areas had the choice of relocating to within Mexico's new boundaries or receiving American citizenship with full civil rights.",the treaty of guadalupe hidalgo ending the mexican war provided for
what is the star signs for each month,"['https://www.encyclopedia.com/science-and-technology/astronomy-and-space-exploration/constellations/constellations', 'https://www.myfreemasonry.com/threads/i-saw-the-sign-and-it-opened-up-my-eyes.12910/', 'https://tangierhotels.net/astronmy-vs-astrology-3817/', 'https://psychicscience.org/astroclock.aspx', 'http://cornwallschoolmysteryandmagick.uk/whats-astrology-your-sign', 'http://www.anwrnews.com/tag/historic', 'http://wordables.com/words-about-the-universe/']","In Western astrology, and formerly astronomy, the zodiac is divided into twelve signs, each occupying 30 ° of celestial longitude and roughly corresponding to the constellations Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer, Leo, Virgo, Libra, Scorpio, Sagittarius, Capricorn, Aquarius and Pisces.",what is the star signs for each month
how long were soldiers on the beach at dunkirk,"['https://www.livingcoramdeo.com/2017/07/17/dunkirks-darkest-hour/', 'http://www.rondoids.com/2017/05/fw-thelist-4465.html', 'https://ilifejourney.wordpress.com/tag/courage/', 'https://indy-amps.weebly.com/operation-dynamo-dunkirk-1940-coloring-book.html', 'http://www.emlii.com/b6ec1de6/Events-Across-100-Years-That-Completely-Changed-The-World', 'https://kinghamhillschooldays.co.uk/newsite/our-history/the-war-years/item/907-born-out-of-necessity-in-1940.html', 'https://redstarcafe.wordpress.com/']","The Dunkirk evacuation, code-named Operation Dynamo, and also known as the Miracle of Dunkirk, was the evacuation of Allied soldiers during World War II from the beaches and harbour of Dunkirk, in the north of France, between 26 May and 4 June 1940. The operation commenced after large numbers of Belgian, British, and French troops were cut off and surrounded by German troops around the mid-point of the six-week long Battle of France. In a speech to the House of Commons, British Prime Minister Winston Churchill called this ""a colossal military disaster"", saying ""the whole root and core and brain of the British Army"" had been stranded at Dunkirk and seemed about to perish or be captured. In his ""we shall fight on the beaches"" speech on 4 June, he hailed their rescue as a ""miracle of deliverance"".",how long were soldiers on the beach at dunkirk
what kind of animal is a fisher cat,"['https://daisymae2017.wordpress.com/tag/country/', 'https://charlespaddockzoo.org/mammals/fisher/', 'http://thegreenmiles.blogspot.com/2015/04/americas-worst-named-wildlife-fisher.html', 'http://wyominguntrapped.org/news/u-s-fish-wildlife-service-consider-northern-rocky-mountain-fisher-population-esa-protection/', 'https://carnivora.net/showthread.php?tid=5868', 'https://feralfront.com/thread/2606543-aloha-%E2%9D%80-storage/', 'http://www.echidnawalkabout.com.au/tours/wild-top-end/']","The fisher (Pekania pennanti) is a small carnivorous mammal native to North America. It is a member of the mustelid family (commonly referred to as the weasel family) and is in the monospecific genus Pekania. The fisher is closely related to but larger than the American marten (Martes americana). The fisher is a forest-dwelling creature whose range covers much of the boreal forest in Canada to the northern United States. Names derived from aboriginal languages include pekan, pequam, wejack, and woolang. It is also called a fisher cat, although it is not a feline.",what kind of animal is a fisher cat
is halong bay in north or south vietnam,"['https://evolutionblog.blogspot.com/2006/04/monty-hall-problem-part-two.html', 'http://www.find4sites.com/articles-detail.php?id=6019', 'http://www.stylishandtrendy.com/travel/h%E1%BA%A1-long-bay-a-beautiful-tropical-travel-destination/', 'https://www.indochinatrek.com/halong-bay-the-world-heritage-site', 'https://www.cbd.int/countries/profile/?country=gy', 'https://slidervilla.com/roster/2011/06/halong-bay-quang-ninh-province-vietnam/', 'https://snehatravelbuff.blogspot.com/2015/06/wonderful-hanoi.html']","Ha Long Bay is located in northeastern Vietnam, from E106 ° 55' to E107 ° 37' and from N20 ° 43' to N21 ° 09'. The bay stretches from Yen Hung district, past Ha Long city, Cam Pha town to Van Don District, bordered on the south and southeast by Lan Ha Bay, on the north by Ha Long city, and on the west by Bai Tu Long Bay. The bay has a 120 km long coastline and is approximately 1,553 km2 in size with about 2,000 islets. The area designated by UNESCO as the World Natural Heritage Site incorporates 434 km2 with 775 islets, of which the core zone is delimited by 69 points: Dau Go island on the west, Ba Ham lake on the south and Cong Tay island on the east. The protected area is from the Cái Dăm petrol store to Quang Hanh commune, Cam Pha town and the surrounding zone.",is halong bay in north or south vietnam
where is tanzania located on the world map,"['http://www.thetravelboss.com/top-ten-208-2-20.html', 'https://judith-wilfred.weebly.com/travelblog/category/tanzania', 'http://www.wandelgek.nl/?page_id=6940&lang=en', 'http://mxmexhibitions.com/agropoultry/tanzania.html', 'http://www.maestrotravel.com.au/consumer-tanzania', 'http://www.globalmissionsinc.org/tanzania.html', 'https://wyldfamilytravel.com/visiting-tanzania/']","Tanzania (/ ˌtænzəˈniːə /), officially the United Republic of Tanzania (Swahili: Jamhuri ya Muungano wa Tanzania), is a sovereign state in eastern Africa within the African Great Lakes region. It borders Kenya and Uganda to the north; Rwanda, Burundi, and the Democratic Republic of the Congo to the west; Zambia, Malawi, and Mozambique to the south; and the Indian Ocean to the east. Mount Kilimanjaro, Africa's highest mountain, is in north-eastern Tanzania.",where is tanzania located on the world map
what is the real meaning of forbidden fruit,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Forbidden_fruit.html', 'https://redeeminggod.com/why-nature-is-destructive/', 'https://akbrodie.wordpress.com/tag/logos/', 'https://samples.essaytopicsmasters.com/expository/dramatic-elements-in-the-film-year-one-essay-example', 'https://scottquillin.com/genesis-chapter-9/', 'https://www.bibletools.org/index.cfm/fuseaction/Library.sr/CT/RA/k/1358/Ask-It-Will-Be-Given.htm', 'http://www.aldrinnavo.com/2009/02/wonder-of-gods-love.html']","Forbidden fruit is a phrase that originates from the Book of Genesis concerning Adam and Eve in Genesis 2: 16 -- 17. In the narrative, Adam and Eve eat the fruit of knowledge of good and evil in the Garden of Eden, which they had been commanded not to do by God. As a metaphor, the phrase typically refers to any indulgence or pleasure that is considered illegal or immoral.",what is the real meaning of forbidden fruit
where is the congo river located on a world map,"['https://kids.kiddle.co/Congo_river', 'https://www.touristlink.com/africa/congo-river/overview.html', 'http://unbiasedreviews.website/top-10-longest-rivers-in-the-world/', 'http://naturalwondersofafrica.com/congo-river/', 'https://www.kimpavitapress.no/congolese-officials-stop-greenpeace-africa-awareness-campaign-about-the-importance-of-the-congo-basin-forest/', 'http://www.eosnap.com/tag/drc/', 'http://www.fonlon.org/category/uncategorized']","The river and its tributaries flow through the Congo Rainforest, the second largest rain forest area in the world, second only to the Amazon Rainforest in South America. The river also has the second-largest flow in the world, behind the Amazon; the third-largest drainage basin of any river, behind the Amazon and Plate rivers; and is one of the deepest rivers in the world, at depths greater than 220 m (720 ft). Because its drainage basin includes areas both north and south of the equator, its flow is stable, as there is always at least one part of the river experiencing a rainy season.",where is the congo river located on a world map
what islands are off the coast of georgia,"['https://americanroads.net/usa_winter2017.htm', 'https://www.goldenisles.com/?gclid=Cj0KCQiA4aXiBRCRARIsAMBZGz99nFMYP9dt8WKDuvtRL6nIHnHkrV5p6u31qN7vzF8LgK6NSS_NwMIaAvr3EALw_wcB', 'http://www.timesoftheislands.com/categories/travel?page=2', 'http://joeloehle.com/', 'https://ssirentals.com/things-to-do/st-simons-jeykll-island-segway-tours/', 'http://www.georgiatouristguide.com/Display_Area.asp?openMenuArea=2', 'https://www.touropia.com/best-places-to-visit-in-georgia-state/?source=page']","The Golden Isles of Georgia are a group of four barrier islands and the mainland port city of Brunswick on the 100-mile-long coast of the U.S. state of Georgia on the Atlantic Ocean. They include St. Simons Island, Sea Island, Jekyll Island, Little St. Simons Island, and Historic Brunswick.",what islands are off the coast of georgia
cast of don't worry be happy video,['http://lukasesch.tk/sheet-music-stars-mv-ferrin.html'],"The comedic original music video for the song stars McFerrin, Robin Williams, and Bill Irwin, and is somewhat shorter than the album version.",cast of don't worry be happy video
what types of insurance does liberty mutual offer,"['https://www.insurance-canada.ca/2018/09/17/liberty-mutual-ironshore-rebrand/', 'http://www.tollfreecontact.com/liberty-mutual-insurance-855-995-1867-toll-free-phone-number/', 'https://www.injurytriallawyer.com/library/legal-action-against-liberty-mutual-davis-law-group.cfm', 'https://www.indianalongtermdisabilitylawyer-blog.com/category/liberty-mutual/', 'https://dev.insurancenewsnet.com/press-releases/Wilson-Shepherd-Honored-as-Company-Representative-of-the-Year-by-the-National-As-a-558373', 'https://www.insurance-canada.ca/2008/04/01/liberty-mutual-group-to-acquire-safeco-corporation-for-6-2-billion/', 'https://www.insure.com/companies/liberty-life-insurance.html']","Liberty Mutual Group, more commonly known by the name of its primary line of business, Liberty Mutual Insurance, is an American diversified global insurer, and the fourth-largest property and casualty insurer in the United States. It ranks 76th on the Fortune 100 list of largest corporations in the United States based on 2013 revenue. Based in Boston, Massachusetts, it employs over 50,000 people in more than 900 locations throughout the world. As of December 31, 2016, Liberty Mutual Insurance had $121.7 billion in consolidated assets, $102.5 billion in consolidated liabilities, and $38.3 billion in annual consolidated revenue. The company, founded in 1912, offers a wide range of insurance products and services, including personal automobile, homeowners, workers' compensation, commercial multiple peril, commercial automobile, general liability, global specialty, group disability, fire and surety.",what types of insurance does liberty mutual offer
where does neapolitan ice cream get its name,"['http://www.mostlymuppet.com/2006/04/27/spumoni/', 'https://juditbakes.com/2013/10/26/a-scoop-of-neopolitan-chocolate-vanilla-cupcake-with-strawberry-icing/', 'http://juneberry-lane.blogspot.com/2011/04/neapolitan-dessert-delights.html', 'https://magazine.vapiano.com/en/blog/grilled-vegetables-delicious-whatever-the-season/', 'https://about-france.com/dictionary/t.htm', 'https://www.tastefulketo.com/keto-recipes/chocolate-milkshake', 'https://allfare.wordpress.com/tag/cupcakes/']","Neapolitan ice cream was named in the late 19th century as a reflection of its presumed origins in the cuisine of the Italian city of Naples, and the many Neapolitan immigrants who brought their expertise in frozen desserts with them to the United States. Spumone was introduced to the United States in the 1870s as Neapolitan-style ice cream. Early recipes used a variety of flavors; however, the number of three molded together was a common denominator, to resemble the Italian flag (cf. insalata tricolore). More than likely, chocolate, vanilla, and strawberry became the standard for the reason that they were the most popular flavors in the United States at the time of introduction.",where does neapolitan ice cream get its name
what is the prize for the national spelling bee,"['http://bhcourier.com/2011/05/31/students-from-l-a-orange-counties-set-to-compete-in-national-spelling-bee/', 'https://resources.greathomeschoolconventions.com/texas/jewett-homeschooling/']","The winner of the Scripps National Spelling Bee receives a $40,000 cash prize and an engraved loving cup trophy from Scripps, a $2,500 savings bond, a reference library from Merriam-Webster, $2,600 in reference works and a lifetime membership to Britannica Online Premium from Encyclopædia Britannica', and an online course and a Nook eReader from K12 Inc.",what is the prize for the national spelling bee
what the difference between colby jack and monterey jack cheese,"['http://www.christinespantry.com/2012/03/bobbys-lighter-baked-spaghetti.html', 'https://praycookblog.com/bacon-wrapped-cream-cheese-stuffed-chicken-breast/', 'https://passioncheese.com/products/', 'https://www.healthbenefitstimes.com/monterey-jack-cheese/', 'http://www.whereiseduy.com/2018/05/real-california-milk-cheese/', 'https://www.cookipedia.co.uk/recipes_wiki/American_cheese', 'https://www.mullinscheese.com/index.php/monterey-jack']","Monterey Jack (sometimes shortened simply to Jack cheese) is an American semi-hard cheese, customarily white, made using cow's milk. It is commonly sold by itself or mixed with Colby cheese to make a marbled cheese known as Colby-Jack (or Co-Jack). Cheddar-Jack (with a yellow cheddar) and Pepper Jack (with chili peppers) varieties are also available. An aged variety is known as Dry Jack.",what the difference between colby jack and monterey jack cheese
where can a hospital corpsman be stationed at,"['https://www.pitchandrudder.com/product/hm-lapel-pin/', 'https://www.thebalancecareers.com/hospital-corpsman-3345823', 'https://www.operationmilitarykids.org/navy-jobs/?share=google-plus-1', 'https://goodgriefcook.com/tag/spring/', 'https://www.navy.mil/ah_online/deptStory.asp?dep=4&id=106010', 'https://westgacnaclass.com/', 'http://www.drthomaswind.com/new-page']","They may function as clinical or specialty technicians, medical administrative personnel and health care providers at medical treatment facilities. They also serve as battlefield corpsmen with the Marine Corps, rendering emergency medical treatment to include initial treatment in a combat environment. Qualified hospital corpsmen may be assigned the responsibility of independent duty aboard ships and submarines; Fleet Marine Force, SEAL and Seabee units, and at isolated duty stations where no medical officer is available.",where can a hospital corpsman be stationed at
who is eligible to vote in indonesian elections,['https://theaseanpost.com/article/indonesian-politics-too-dirty-and-too-boring'],"The voting age in Indonesia is 17 but anyone who has an ID card (Indonesian: Kartu Tanda Penduduk (KTP)) can vote, since persons under 17 who are or were married can get a KTP.",who is eligible to vote in indonesian elections
when was the colt single action army made,"['https://www.spectroom.com/category/171114007-pistols', 'http://552tactical.com/colt-saa-bolt-hand/', 'http://552tactical.com/colt-saa-reduced-power-spring-kit/', 'http://552tactical.com/blued-colt-saa-cylinder/', 'http://www.firearmsassurefreedom.com/history-of-colt-saa.html', 'http://552tactical.com/colt-peacemaker-parts-complete-screw-set/', 'http://www.softairgun.eu/product_info.php?products_id=1954&osCsid=d989d7cb89f77d547a139c897e8830a2']","The Colt Single Action Army, also known as the Single Action Army, SAA, Model P, Peacemaker, M1873, and Colt. 45 is a single-action revolver with a revolving cylinder holding six metallic cartridges. It was designed for the U.S. government service revolver trials of 1872 by Colt's Patent Firearms Manufacturing Company -- today's Colt's Manufacturing Company -- and was adopted as the standard military service revolver until 1892.",when was the colt single action army made
settlement in which britain recognized the united states as a new nation,"['https://www.classicalimages.com/collections/maps/products/1794-thomas-pownall-kitchin-large-post-revolutionary-war-map-of-north-america', 'https://patriotsforamericausa.com/2018/01/14/proclaiming-peace-january-14-1784-ratification-of-the-treaty-of-paris/', 'https://defendingthetruth.com/threads/defending-the-truth.109281/page-2', 'http://wikien3.appspot.com/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1783)', 'https://majormike.us/2017/09/03/today-in-history-090317/', 'https://www.americanhistorycentral.com/entries/treaty-of-paris-1783/', 'https://2001-2009.state.gov/r/pa/ho/time/ar/14313.htm']","This treaty and the separate peace treaties between Great Britain and the nations that supported the American cause -- France, Spain, and the Dutch Republic -- are known collectively as the Peace of Paris. Only Article 1 of the treaty, which acknowledges the United States' existence as free sovereign and independent states, remains in force.",settlement in which britain recognized the united states as a new nation
does malaysia and indonesia speak the same language,"['http://chuyenphatnhanh.co/Sexy-Women-Kalgoorlie%E2%80%93Boulder/malay-and', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Indonesian_language.html', 'https://greatives.eu/themes/movedo/movedo-hosting/pricing/', 'https://www.fasttranslator.ca/Malay-Translations.htm', 'https://veqta.com/malaysian-translation/', 'https://www.scribd.com/document/74207149/22-1', 'https://www.euroasia.co.nz/Courses/LanguageCourses/IndonesianLanguageCourses.aspx']","The Malaysian and Indonesian are both standardised registers of Malay language in Malaysia and Indonesia, respectively. Both languages are generally mutually intelligible, yet there are differences in spelling, grammar, pronunciation and vocabulary, as well as the predominant source of loanwords. The differences can range from those mutually unintelligible with one another, to those having a closer familial resemblance. The regionalised and localised varieties of Malay can become a catalyst for intercultural conflict, especially in higher education.",does malaysia and indonesia speak the same language
which type of current involves charge flow in a single direction,"['http://agritourismquebec.com/audio-technica-atw-702-81/', 'http://verdon.mobi/m-audio-ozonic-12/', 'http://definedelectric.com/basic-definitions-direct-current/', 'https://www.electrical4u.net/electrical-basic/what-is-electric-current-fundamental-types-of-current/', 'https://www.solar-ray.net/faq-s.html', 'https://www.edinformatics.com/math_science/what-is-an-electric-current.html', 'http://enginesound.cn/services/testing.html']","In contrast, direct current (DC) is the unidirectional flow of electric charge, or a system in which the movement of electric charge is in one direction only. Direct current is produced by sources such as batteries, thermocouples, solar cells, and commutator-type electric machines of the dynamo type. Direct current may flow in a conductor such as a wire, but can also flow through semiconductors, insulators, or even through a vacuum as in electron or ion beams. An old name for direct current was galvanic current.",which type of current involves charge flow in a single direction
what does the kangaroo represent on the australian coat of arms,"['https://notescollector.eu/pages/en/notes.php?noteId=1883', 'https://coin-brothers.com/catalog/coin1481', 'https://allbrawnnobrains.blog/2018/10/04/sydney-to-melbourne-pt-2-a-designer-city/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Australia']","The Red Kangaroo and Emu that support the shield have never been designated as official animal emblems of the nation. They owe their unofficial recognition to the fact that they are endemic Australian fauna (found only on that continent), and likely chosen because they are the most well-known native Australian animals large enough to be positioned together in scale holding up the shield. They were chosen to symbolise a nation moving forward, based on the fact that neither animal can move backwards easily -- i.e. symbolising progress. It has been claimed that the kangaroo is, and must be seen to be, male.",what does the kangaroo represent on the australian coat of arms
when was the shot heard round the world,['http://carynschulenberg.com/2019/02/'],"""The shot heard round the world"" is a phrase referring to several historical incidents, particularly the opening of the American Revolutionary War in 1775 and the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand in 1914.",when was the shot heard round the world
who died in the plane crash of lynyrd skynyrd,"['http://musiccitynashville.org/music-feature/nashville-film-festival-focusing-on-rock-legends/', 'https://www.orlandosentinel.com/news/os-xpm-1988-05-22-0040200042-story.html', 'http://www.check-six.com/Crash_Sites/LynyrdSkynyrd-N55VM.htm', 'http://www.wlup.com/2016/10/20/lynyrd-skynyrd-plane-crash-was-39-years-ago-today/', 'https://talkingloudandsayingnothingparts3and4.wordpress.com/2013/08/', 'https://i95rock.com/lynyrd-skynyrd-plane-crashes/', 'https://www.metro.us/news/body-of-taiwan-crash-hero-pilot-found-still-clinging-to-plane-controls/zsJobf---7HjwFT8QmUmE']","Lead vocalist / founding member Ronnie Van Zant, guitarist / vocalist Steve Gaines, backing vocalist Cassie Gaines (Steve's older sister), assistant road manager Dean Kilpatrick, pilot Walter McCreary, and co-pilot William Gray all died as a result of the crash. Twenty others survived.",who died in the plane crash of lynyrd skynyrd
what are the characteristics of the baroque style of art,"['https://www.robertraymond.com/if-it-aint-baroque-dog-ear/', 'https://www.antiessays.com/free-essays/Baroque-507123.html', 'http://www.academicroom.com/humanities/art-history/special-topics-art-history/renaissance-and-baroque-art', 'https://shop.latin-accents.com/c/traditional-clay-body-mexican-talavera-tiles_baroque-styles', 'http://www.tutorsglobe.com/homework-help/baroque-art-assignment-help-73825.aspx', 'https://www.citychoirdunedin.org.nz/2012/03/tuesday-rehearsal-for-beauty-of-baroque.html', 'http://www.artandpopularculture.com/Baroque']","The Baroque (US: / bəˈroʊk / or UK: / bəˈrɒk /) is a period of artistic style that used exaggerated motion and clear, easily interpreted detail to produce drama, tension, exuberance, and grandeur in sculpture, painting, architecture, literature, dance, theatre, and music. The style began around 1600 in Rome and Italy, and spread to most of Europe.",what are the characteristics of the baroque style of art
what is the elevation of yosemite national park,"['http://traveltripjourney.blogspot.com/search?updated-max=2012-12-22T21:41:00-08:00&amp;max-results=7', 'http://bestcitiestravel.com/yosemite/', 'https://findinghistory.net/california/california-national-parks/yosemite', 'http://www.lataupe.net/time-off-in-the-nature/', 'http://millionstarhotel.com/tag/national-park/', 'http://www.sullivanslist.com/view/yosemite', 'http://whmnet.org/collection/site.php?site=308']","Yosemite is one of the largest and least fragmented habitat blocks in the Sierra Nevada, and the park supports a diversity of plants and animals. The park has an elevation range from 2,127 to 13,114 feet (648 to 3,997 m) and contains five major vegetation zones: chaparral and oak woodland, lower montane forest, upper montane forest, subalpine zone, and alpine. Of California's 7,000 plant species, about 50% occur in the Sierra Nevada and more than 20% within Yosemite. There is suitable habitat for more than 160 rare plants in the park, with rare local geologic formations and unique soils characterizing the restricted ranges many of these plants occupy.",what is the elevation of yosemite national park
how do you make the mcdonald's all american basketball team,"['https://amateursports365.wordpress.com/tag/duke/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/McDonald%27s', 'http://10thyearseniors.com/2017/01/16/ayton-named-mcdonalds-all-american/?v=9a231c14a341', 'https://www.desotoeagleeye.org/2016/02/12/marques-bolden-mcdonalds-all-american-player/', 'https://www.rubywilbur.com/james-madison-high-school-homeschool/']","The McDonald's All-American Game refers to each of the all-star basketball games played each year for American and Canadian boys' and girls' high-school basketball graduates. Consisting of the top players, each team plays a single exhibition game after the conclusion of the high-school basketball season, in an East vs. West format. As part of the annual event, boys and girls compete in a slam dunk contest, a three-point shooting competition, and an overall timed skills competition. It is rarely common for the girls to compete in the slam dunk contest sans, 2004 champion, Candace Parker. The boys' game has been contested annually since 1978, and the girls game has been played each year since it was added in 2002.",how do you make the mcdonald's all american basketball team
where are most crops grown in the us,"['https://bohatala.com/comparison-of-pakistan-agriculture-with-other-countries/', 'https://www.vividmaps.com/2019/04/mapping-the-most-valuable-agricultural-commodity-in-each-u-s-state.html', 'http://colonialagropecuaria.com/agriculture/american-agriculture-has-been-real-cultivation-and-gathering-practices/', 'http://colonialagropecuaria.com/agriculture/american-agriculture-success-communities-are-reverential-spiritual-overtones/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Agriculture_in_the_United_States', 'http://www.englishvs.com/ingilizce-sozluk/kelimeler/ingilizce-kelimeler/a-ile-baslayan-ingilizce-kelimeler/agriculture', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171115100-agriculture']","Agriculture is a major industry in the United States, which is a net exporter of food. As of the 2007 census of agriculture, there were 2.2 million farms, covering an area of 922 million acres (3,730,000 km), an average of 418 acres (169 hectares) per farm. Although agricultural activity occurs in all states, it is particularly concentrated in the Great Plains, a vast expanse of flat, arable land in the center of the United States and in the region around the Great Lakes known as the Corn Belt.",where are most crops grown in the us
who played christopher pike in the original star trek,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/It%27s_Only_a_Paper_Moon_(Star_Trek:_Deep_Space_Nine)', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/180124102-fictional-characters', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/James_T._Kirk', 'https://www.slashfilm.com/rumor-tom-cruise-to-cameo-in-jj-abrams-star-trek/', 'https://www.ign.com/articles/2018/10/11/star-trek-discoverys-sonequa-martin-green-on-burnhams-highly-emotional-relationship-with-spock', 'http://mygosport.org/info_pages_htm/sons_david_bogue.htm', 'https://www.thestar.com/entertainment/television/2019/01/11/the-man-trap-was-the-first-star-trek-episode-to-air-but-the-star-was-there-first.html?fbclid=IwAR2tDgqyy52aCGG7bwdXv3Y6d1VuiZ86FQoC912Q_WkhhhZu0OK-QXBFhWI']","Christopher Pike is a character in the Star Trek science fiction franchise. He was portrayed by Jeffrey Hunter in the original Star Trek pilot episode, ""The Cage"", as captain of the USS Enterprise. The pilot was rejected, and the character was dropped during development of the second pilot when Hunter decided that he did not want to continue with the series. Sean Kenney portrayed the physically disabled Christopher Pike in new footage filmed for a subsequent Star Trek episode, ""The Menagerie"", which also re-uses original footage featuring Hunter from ""The Cage"". Bruce Greenwood portrays Pike in the 2009 film Star Trek and its 2013 sequel, Star Trek Into Darkness. Captain Pike and the Enterprise appear in the second season of Star Trek: Discovery; the trailer for the season shows Pike (Anson Mount) taking temporary command of the USS Discovery in a crisis situation.",who played christopher pike in the original star trek
who were the soldiers in band of brothers,"['https://www.stephenscountyga.com/band-of-brothers.cfm', 'http://mujersegura.info/in-theaters/hanks-band-of-brothers.php', 'https://sharkoschool.blogspot.com/2008/10/', 'http://www.cityoftoccoa.com/currahee-military-museum.cfm', 'http://footballforum.tk/upstate-ny-casino-bids.html', 'http://nyanglish.com/exploit', 'http://classic-legends.tk/casino-us-map.html']","Band of Brothers is a dramatized account of ""Easy Company"" (part of the 2nd Battalion, 506th Parachute Infantry Regiment), assigned to the United States Army's 101st Airborne Division during World War II. Over ten episodes the series details the company's exploits during the war. Starting with jump training at Camp Toccoa, Georgia, Band of Brothers follows the unit through the American airborne landings in Normandy, Operation Market Garden, the Siege of Bastogne, and on to the war's end. It includes the taking of the Kehlsteinhaus (Eagle's Nest) at Obersalzberg in Berchtesgaden and refers to the surrender of Japan. Major Richard Winters (1918 -- 2011) is the central character, shown working to accomplish the company's missions and keep his men together and safe. While the series features a large ensemble cast, each episode generally focuses on a single character, following his action.",who were the soldiers in band of brothers
how many games are played in a 16 team double elimination tournament,"['https://topfilme.info/weimar-kennenlernen/26-man-single-elimination-bracket.php', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/2016_All-Ireland_Senior_Hurling_Championship', 'http://mxtrax.co.uk/24-team-bracket-double-elimination.html']","As with single-elimination tournaments, most often the number of competitors is equal to a power of two (8, 16, 32, etc.) so that in each round there is an even number of competitors and never any byes. The maximum number of games in a double-elimination tournament is one less than twice the number of teams participating (e.g., 8 teams -- 15 games). The minimum number is two less than twice the number of teams (e.g., 8 teams -- 14 games).",how many games are played in a 16 team double elimination tournament
when did school of rock open in london,['https://thrillcall.com/concerts/2934125-school-of-rock-school-of-rock-the-musical-touring-timesunion-moran-theater-jacksonville-2019'],"On 20 May 2016 the musical was confirmed at the Gillian Lynne Theatre instead of the Palladium with previews starting on 24 October 2016, opening night on 14 November 2016, and public booking opening on 25 May 2016. Lloyd Webber revealed that the production was able to open several months earlier than anticipated due to finding the child musician actors easily.",when did school of rock open in london
is principal financial group a fortune 500 company,"['https://customer.guru/net-promoter-score/principal-financial', 'http://dtxpc.org/principal-financial-group/', 'http://www.insurancezing.com/principal-financial-group/company.html', 'https://www.chinamobileltd.com/en/media/news.php?year=2015&scroll2title=1', 'https://www.chinamobileltd.com/en/media/news.php?year=2018&scroll2title=1', 'https://www.chinamobileltd.com/en/media/news.php?year=2016&scroll2title=1', 'https://www.chinamobileltd.com/en/media/news.php?year=2014&scroll2title=1']","In 2014, Principal was ranked 298th on Fortune magazine's list of the 500 largest U.S. corporations (May 2014). In 2013, Principal earned the top spot in its category for the second year in a row of Pensions & Investments' annual survey of ""Best Places to Work"" in Money Management. In 2013, Principal ranked 528th on the Forbes Global 2000 list, which recognizes the world's biggest and most powerful companies, as measured by a composite ranking for sales profits, assets and market value (as of April 2013).",is principal financial group a fortune 500 company
which instruments formed the core of the baroque orchestra,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/European_classical_music.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Classical_music', 'https://www.dfaffiliates.com/the-classical-orchestra-was-much-smaller-than-the-baroque-orchestra/', 'http://nutramed.com/persona.nutramed.com/Counterpoint/counterpoint3.htm', 'http://www.kathysterndahl.com/2013/05/from-knights-hospitaller-to-bach-and.html', 'http://catacoustic.com/what-we-do/', 'http://www.russellgilmour.co.uk/blog/index.php?id=4998388704568191636']","The Baroque orchestra is the type of large ensemble for mixed instruments that existed during the Baroque Era of Western Classical music, commonly identified as 1600 -- 1750. Baroque orchestras are typically much smaller, in terms of the number of performers, than Romantic music era orchestras from the 1800s. Baroque orchestras originated in France where Jean-Baptiste Lully added the newly re-designed hautbois (oboe) and transverse flutes to his vingt-quatre violons du Roy (this translates as ""The twenty-four violins of the King""). As well as violins and woodwinds, the baroque orchestra contained basso continuo instruments such as the theorbo, lute, harpsichord and / or pipe organ.",which instruments formed the core of the baroque orchestra
what type of weathering involves the reaction of materials with natural or biological chemicals,"['https://lessknownfacts.com/10-facts-about-mechanical-weathering/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Weathering', 'http://www.bcompetitive.in/rock-cycle-weathering/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Weathering', 'http://www.riversdalecc.com/erosion/', 'https://www.academicde-stressor.com/how-does-man-contribute-to-weathering-and-erosion/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Salar_de_Arizaro']","Two important classifications of weathering processes exist -- physical and chemical weathering; each sometimes involves a biological component. Mechanical or physical weathering involves the breakdown of rocks and soils through direct contact with atmospheric conditions, such as heat, water, ice and pressure. The second classification, chemical weathering, involves the direct effect of atmospheric chemicals or biologically produced chemicals also known as biological weathering in the breakdown of rocks, soils and minerals. While physical weathering is accentuated in very cold or very dry environments, chemical reactions are most intense where the climate is wet and hot. However, both types of weathering occur together, and each tends to accelerate the other. For example, physical abrasion (rubbing together) decreases the size of particles and therefore increases their surface area, making them more susceptible to rapid chemical reactions. The various agents act in concert to convert primary minerals (feldspars and micas) to secondary minerals (clays and carbonates) and release plant nutrient elements in soluble forms.",what type of weathering involves the reaction of materials with natural or biological chemicals
how did france get the statue of liberty to america,"['http://thepandorasociety.com/this-week-in-history-june-13th-to-19th/', 'http://telemailer.info/51662-find-files-on-date-holstebro.html', 'https://xconomy.com/national/2011/11/08/the-wisdom-of-the-crowd-social-networking-meets-capital-formation/']","On June 17, 1885, the French steamer Isère, laden with the Statue of Liberty, reached the New York port safely. New Yorkers displayed their new-found enthusiasm for the statue, as the French vessel arrived with the crates holding the disassembled statue on board. Two hundred thousand people lined the docks and hundreds of boats put to sea to welcome the Isère. After five months of daily calls to donate to the statue fund, on August 11, 1885, the World announced that $102,000 had been raised from 120,000 donors, and that 80 percent of the total had been received in sums of less than one dollar.",how did france get the statue of liberty to america
what is the contribution made to the development of the microscope by anton van leeuwenhoek,"['http://www.bononiaemicroscope.com/en/the-microscopes/replica.html', 'https://threadb.com/why-thread/', 'http://en.citizendium.org/wiki?title=Antonie_van_Leeuwenhoek&amp;diff=100732625&amp;oldid=100001239', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Antonie_van_Leeuwenhoek', 'https://www.q-files.com/technology/famous-inventors/antonie-van-leeuwenhoek/', 'http://m.q-files.com/science/great-scientists/', 'http://www.assignmentpoint.com/arts/biography/biography-of-antonie-van-leeuwenhoek.html']","By placing the middle of a small rod of soda lime glass in a hot flame, van Leeuwenhoek could pull the hot section apart to create two long whiskers of glass. Then, by reinserting the end of one whisker into the flame, he could create a very small, high-quality glass sphere. These spheres became the lenses of his microscopes, with the smallest spheres providing the highest magnifications.",what is the contribution made to the development of the microscope by anton van leeuwenhoek
what kinds of programs made up the new deal during the 1930s and who were they trying to help,"['https://americanhistoryusa.com/topic/new-deal/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Dewey_Jackson_Short', 'https://www.co.seneca.ny.us/category/environmental-health-services/', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-politicalscience/chapter/the-history-of-economic-policy/', 'https://www.ntdtv.com/b5/2018/10/26/a1396785.html', 'https://angrywoodchucksblog.com/2012/11/19/the-socialists-are-still-here-in-congress-in-labor-unions-in-lobby-groups-upton-sinclair-of-the-jungle-prediction/', 'http://blog.bearing-consulting.com/2012/09/03/the-power-of-country-visions/']","The New Deal was a series of programs, public work projects, financial reforms and regulations enacted in the United States between 1933 and 1936 in response to the Great Depression. Some of these federal programs included the Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC), the Civil Works Administration (CWA), the Farm Security Administration (FSA), the National Industrial Recovery Act of 1933 (NIRA) and the Social Security Administration (SSA). These programs included support for farmers, the unemployed, youth and the elderly. It included new constraints and safeguards on the banking industry and efforts to re-inflate the economy after prices had fallen sharply. New Deal programs included both laws passed by Congress as well as presidential executive orders during the first term of the presidency of Franklin D. Roosevelt. The programs focused on what historians refer to as the ""3 Rs"": relief for the unemployed and poor, recovery of the economy back to normal levels and reform of the financial system to prevent a repeat depression. The New Deal produced a political realignment, making the Democratic Party the majority (as well as the party that held the White House for seven out of the nine presidential terms from 1933 -- 1969) with its base in liberal ideas, the South, traditional Democrats, big city machines and the newly empowered labor unions and ethnic minorities. The Republicans were split, with conservatives opposing the entire New Deal as hostile to business and economic growth and liberals in support. The realignment crystallized into the New Deal coalition that dominated presidential elections into the 1960s while the opposing conservative coalition largely controlled Congress in domestic affairs from 1937 -- 1964.",what kinds of programs made up the new deal during the 1930s and who were they trying to help
where are the pennines mountains located on a map,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Fiddlers_Ferry_power_station', 'http://jayandkaycoachtours.co.uk/pennine-explorer/', 'https://www.walkingenglishman.com/pennines.html', 'http://www.umhc.org.uk/wiki/hiking_destinations/', 'https://ndla.no/en/subjects/subject:39/topic:1:188922/topic:1:188924/resource:1:6477', 'https://www.nmrs.org.uk/mines-map/metal/lake-district/']","Often described as the ""backbone of England"", the Pennine Hills form a more-or-less continuous range stretching northwards from the Peak District in the northern Midlands, through the South Pennines, Yorkshire Dales and North Pennines up to the Tyne Gap, which separates the range from the Cheviot Hills. South of the Aire Gap is a western spur into east Lancashire, comprising the Rossendale Fells, West Pennine Moors and the Bowland Fells in North Lancashire. The Howgill Fells in Cumbria are sometimes considered to be a Pennine spur to the west of the range. The Pennines are an important water catchment area with numerous reservoirs in the head streams of the river valleys.",where are the pennines mountains located on a map
who is the titan that holds the world,"['https://4815162342execute.wordpress.com/season-3/dharma-initiative/mike/', 'https://www.samstorms.com/all-articles/post/knowing-who-s-in-charge-makes-all-the-difference-in-the-world--revelation-101-11']","A common misconception today is that Atlas was forced to hold the Earth on his shoulders, but Classical art shows Atlas holding the celestial spheres, not a globe; the solidity of the marble globe borne by the renowned Farnese Atlas may have aided the conflation, reinforced in the 16th century by the developing usage of atlas to describe a corpus of terrestrial maps.",who is the titan that holds the world
what is the difference between senate and house of rep,"['http://iiwiki.com/wiki/Christian_States_Congress', 'https://wikivivid.com/wiki/National_Archives_and_Records_Administration', 'https://tnar.org/?p=206', 'https://www.scholastic.com/teachers/articles/teaching-content/united-states-government/', 'https://studyres.com/concepts/18631/united-states-congress', 'https://itlaw.wikia.org/wiki/U.S._Congress', 'https://www.shusterman.com/congressusimmigration/']","The members of the House of Representatives serve two-year terms representing the people of a single constituency, known as a ""district"". Congressional districts are apportioned to states by population using the United States Census results, provided that each state has at least one congressional representative. Each state, regardless of population or size, has two senators. Currently, there are 100 senators representing the 50 states. Each senator is elected at-large in their state for a six-year term, with terms staggered, so every two years approximately one-third of the Senate is up for election.",what is the difference between senate and house of rep
who was allowed to vote in the brexit referendum,"['http://wikielections.com/europe-elections/united-kingdom/united-kingdom-referendum-election-2017-voting-live/', 'https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-36370522', 'https://blog.education.nationalgeographic.org/2016/02/23/what-is-the-brexit/', 'https://winebutik.eu/england-referendum.html', 'http://www.bayradio.fm/brexiteer-warns-remoaners-attempts-to-thwart-brexit-are-a-threat-to-democracy/', 'http://conservatives-paris.org/New_Weblog/?m=201206', 'http://funandgames.org/brexit-2nd-referendum/']","The right to vote in the referendum in the United Kingdom is defined by the legislation as limited to residents of the United Kingdom who were either also Commonwealth citizens under the British Nationality Act 1948 (which include British citizens and other British nationals), or those who were also citizens of the Republic of Ireland, or both. Members of the House of Lords, who could not vote in general elections, were able to vote in the referendum.",who was allowed to vote in the brexit referendum
what characteristic of helium makes it a major constituent of the pulsating star mechanism,"['http://www.creationscience.co.uk/stellar/', 'http://sciencechatforum.com/viewtopic.php?p=323527', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Nu3_Canis_Majoris', 'https://www.spacetv.net/chandra-space-telescope/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Main_sequence', 'https://archive.briankoberlein.com/2013/10/16/burning-metal/', 'http://chandra.harvard.edu/photo/2013/47tuc/more.html']","Nuclear fusion powers a star for most of its life. Initially the energy is generated by the fusion of hydrogen atoms at the core of the main-sequence star. Later, as the preponderance of atoms at the core becomes helium, stars like the Sun begin to fuse hydrogen along a spherical shell surrounding the core. This process causes the star to gradually grow in size, passing through the subgiant stage until it reaches the red giant phase. Stars with at least half the mass of the Sun can also begin to generate energy through the fusion of helium at their core, whereas more-massive stars can fuse heavier elements along a series of concentric shells. Once a star like the Sun has exhausted its nuclear fuel, its core collapses into a dense white dwarf and the outer layers are expelled as a planetary nebula. Stars with around ten or more times the mass of the Sun can explode in a supernova as their inert iron cores collapse into an extremely dense neutron star or black hole. Although the universe is not old enough for any of the smallest red dwarfs to have reached the end of their lives, stellar models suggest they will slowly become brighter and hotter before running out of hydrogen fuel and becoming low-mass white dwarfs.",what characteristic of helium makes it a major constituent of the pulsating star mechanism
where do beta fish live in the wild,"['https://www.petfishforsale.com/pet-freshwater-fish-for-sale/pet-betta-fish-for-sale-siamese-fighting-fish/', 'https://www.coinbazaar.in/buy-limited-edition-mint-collector-coin-online-india/1963-fighting-fish-shades-of-nature-silver-coin-2016-25-grams-999-purity-by-cook-islands.html', 'https://eol.org/pages/981571', 'https://eol.org/pages/327284', 'https://eol.org/pages/328074', 'https://www.himalaiiasclasses.com/blog/upsc-ncert-ecology-and-environment-animal-community-2/', 'http://www.theultimatehobbies.com/2018/11/siamese-fighting-fish-care.html']","This species is native to the Mekong basin of Laos, Cambodia, Vietnam and Thailand. The fish can be found in standing waters of canals, rice paddies and floodplains. It is listed as Vulnerable by the IUCN.",where do beta fish live in the wild
scotland rejected the referendum for independence from uk by,"['http://www.socialwork.ed.ac.uk/centenary/timeline/events/scottish_referendum_on_independence', 'http://whatscotlandthinks.org/questions/should-scotland-be-an-independent-country', 'https://ineng.co.za/western-cape-independence/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/2014_Scottish_independence_referendum', 'http://www.thebiafratimes.co/2017/08/biafra-biafra-referendum-is-inevitable.html', 'http://keiba-kikka.info/news.php?action=show&id=13378', 'https://www.longitude.it/article/separatisms/']","A referendum on Scottish independence from the United Kingdom took place on 18 September 2014. The referendum question, which voters answered with ""Yes"" or ""No"", was ""Should Scotland be an independent country?"" The ""No"" side won, with 2,001,926 (55.3%) voting against independence and 1,617,989 (44.7%) voting in favour. The turnout of 84.6% was the highest recorded for an election or referendum in the United Kingdom since the introduction of universal suffrage.",scotland rejected the referendum for independence from uk by
who plays in the new american horror story,"['https://putlockerstoday.wordpress.com/tag/gomovies/', 'https://www.comparama.com/topic/american-horror-story/', 'https://anchor.fm/americanhorrorstory', 'http://nutraburn10.info/viewtopic.php?t=21591', 'http://desnuda.top/Allison%20Scagliotti', 'http://platinum-line.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=25413', 'http://favoritetv.me/hulu/']","American Horror Story: Cult is the seventh season of the FX horror anthology television series American Horror Story. The season was picked up on October 4, 2016, and premiered on September 5, 2017. The season will consist of a total of 11 episodes. Returning cast members from previous seasons include: Sarah Paulson, Evan Peters, Cheyenne Jackson, Adina Porter, Chaz Bono, John Carroll Lynch, Emma Roberts, James Morosini, Mare Winningham, Jamie Brewer and Frances Conroy, along with new cast members Billie Lourd and Alison Pill.",who plays in the new american horror story
what happens when you dial 112 in india,"['https://www.lifehacker.com.au/2019/01/what-to-do-when-000-is-down-and-you-have-an-emergency/', 'https://www.hamogelo.gr/gr/en/ta-nea-mas/eiropaki-imera-eiaisthitopoiisis-gia-ton-eiropako-arithmo-ektaktis-anagkis-112-4/', 'https://www.learncroatian.eu/blog/useful-croatian-in-case-of-an-emergency', 'https://www.insurance.fr/blog/single-european-emergency-number-112', 'https://www.cntraveler.com/stories/2009-01-14/tech-tools-for-dialing-out-of-disaster', 'http://www.15august.in/2016/03/112-india-single-national-emergency-number.html', 'http://brisbaneradiosociety.net/home/']","112 is a part of the GSM standard and all GSM-compatible telephone handsets are able to dial 112 even when locked or, in some countries, with no SIM card present. It is also the common emergency number in India and in nearly all member states of the European Union as well as several other countries of Europe and the world. 112 is often available alongside other numbers traditionally used in the given country to access emergency services. In some countries, calls to 112 are not connected directly but forwarded by the GSM network to local emergency numbers (e.g., 911 in North America or 000 in Australia).",what happens when you dial 112 in india
how long does dapoxetine stay in your system,"['http://northwoodseducation.info/glucophage-xr-buy-online.html', 'http://kozycore.com/buy-viagra-online-now.html', 'https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/medicine/804/SPC/Largactil+Injection/', 'https://www.drugs.com/pro/lanoxin.html', 'https://www.cancertreatmentsresearch.com/amanita-phalloides-a-direct-attack-on-tumors-with-a-mushroom/', 'http://www.foodconsumer.org/777/8/printer_Grilled_chicken_contains_cancer-causing_agent.shtml', 'http://holisticonline.com/Remedies/Parkinson/pd_levodopa.htm']","Dapoxetine is absorbed and distributed rapidly in the body. Greater than 99% of dapoxetine is bound to the plasma protein. The mean steady state volume is 162 L. Its initial half-life is 1.31 hours (30 mg dose) and 1.42 hours (60 mg dose,) and its terminal half life is 18.7 hours (30 mg dose) and 21.9 hours (60 mg dose).",how long does dapoxetine stay in your system
where is michigan located in the united states,"['http://knowledgebase.lookseek.com/Michigan.html', 'https://companies.jrank.org/pages/2757/Michigan-National-Corporation.html', 'http://cittacattolica.com/pdf.php?q=download-introductory-notes-in-discrete-mathematics/', 'http://us.byregion.net/region/MI', 'https://advowastemedical.com/michigan-medical-waste-disposal', 'http://asfa.net/country/115-usa-michigan.html', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Michigan']","The Great Lakes that border Michigan from east to west are Lake Erie, Lake Huron, Lake Michigan and Lake Superior. It has more public golf courses, registered boats, and lighthouses than any other state. The state is bounded on the south by the states of Ohio and Indiana, sharing land and water boundaries with both. Michigan's western boundaries are almost entirely water boundaries, from south to north, with Illinois and Wisconsin in Lake Michigan; then a land boundary with Wisconsin and the Upper Peninsula, that is principally demarcated by the Menominee and Montreal Rivers; then water boundaries again, in Lake Superior, with Wisconsin and Minnesota to the west, capped around by the Canadian province of Ontario to the north and east.",where is michigan located in the united states
how does a person change their last name,['https://www.help4youoc.com/services/name-change/'],"The procedures and ease of a name change vary between jurisdictions. In general, common law jurisdictions have loose procedures for a name change while civil law jurisdictions are more restrictive.",how does a person change their last name
where did yellowstone national park get its name,"['https://happydance.blog/2018/08/18/pine-trees-on-the-moon/', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Yellowstone_National_Park', 'https://thebesttravelplaces.com/yellowstone/']","The park contains the headwaters of the Yellowstone River, from which it takes its historical name. Near the end of the 18th century, French trappers named the river Roche Jaune, which is probably a translation of the Hidatsa name Mi tsi a-da-zi (""Yellow Rock River""). Later, American trappers rendered the French name in English as ""Yellow Stone"". Although it is commonly believed that the river was named for the yellow rocks seen in the Grand Canyon of the Yellowstone, the Native American name source is unclear.",where did yellowstone national park get its name
what is the skin that grows under the nail,"['http://www.bestonlinemd.com/causes-of-peeling-fingernails/', 'http://topdot.com/victoria/how-to-grow-nail-bed.php', 'http://toenailfungustreatments.com/', 'http://www.lakeshorenatural.com/promog/ConditionCenter.asp?ConditionID=17&ArticleID=355&StoreID=B75B2480472D4A75904E2247FDB32683', 'http://amazingfacts4u.com/nail/', 'http://www.doctorlawrencejaeger.com/importance-of-good-nail-care/', 'http://tarotcanada.tripod.com/Fingernails.html']","The nail bed is the skin beneath the nail plate. Like all skin, it is made of two types of tissues: the deeper dermis, the living tissue which includes capillaries and glands, and the epidermis, the layer just beneath the nail plate, which moves toward the finger tip with the plate. The epidermis is attached to the dermis by tiny longitudinal ""grooves"" called matrix crests (cristae matricis unguis). In old age, the nail plate becomes thinner, and these grooves become more visible.",what is the skin that grows under the nail
where is the cape horn located on a map,"['http://lacgeo.com/cape-horn-diego-ramirez-islands-drake-passage-south-america', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Cape_Horn', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171228301-peninsulas', 'https://www.electricscotland.com/kids/rolfins_orb/book10_chap13.htm', 'https://tourdumondealavoile.com/page/2/', 'http://grease-musical.tk/favorable-winds-del-verde-lasagna-sheets.html', 'http://channelchallenge.nl/taxonomy/term/64']","Cape Horn (Dutch: Kaap Hoorn (help info), Spanish: Cabo de Hornos), named after the city of Hoorn in the Netherlands, is the southernmost headland of the Tierra del Fuego archipelago of southern Chile, and is located on the small Hornos Island. Although not the most southerly point of South America (which are the Diego Ramírez Islands), Cape Horn marks the northern boundary of the Drake Passage and marks where the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans meet.",where is the cape horn located on a map
where are the valence electrons in an atom,"['http://bop-protocol.org/queensland/valence-electrons-how-to-find.php', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Valence_electron', 'https://www.thecurriculumchoice.com/covalent-bonding-home-science-tools/', 'https://chem.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Introductory_Chemistry/Book%3A_Introductory_Chemistry_Online!_(Young)/03%3A_Chemical_Bonding_and_Nomenclature/3.02%3A_Covalent_Bonding', 'http://topdot.com/wales/how-to-know-what-type-of-bond-is-formed.php', 'https://www.futurelearn.com/courses/everyday-chemistry/2/steps/173809', 'https://sciencetrends.com/covalent-bond-examples-and-properties/']","In chemistry, a valence electron is an outer shell electron that is associated with an atom, and that can participate in the formation of a chemical bond if the outer shell is not closed; in a single covalent bond, both atoms in the bond contribute one valence electron in order to form a shared pair. The presence of valence electrons can determine the element's chemical properties, such as its valence -- whether it may bond with other elements and, if so, how readily and with how many. For a main group element, a valence electron can exist only in the outermost electron shell; in a transition metal, a valence electron can also be in an inner shell.",where are the valence electrons in an atom
where did french and indian war take place,"['https://rjmautographsandantiques.com/products/french-indian-war-father-ralles-war-garrison-soldiers-names-found-in-early-ma-documents', 'https://military.wikia.org/wiki/French_and_Indian_War', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Continental_Army', 'https://www.classicalimages.com/products/1756-homann-large-antique-map-of-the-colonial-united-states-french-indian-war', 'https://www.teachingcolumbus.org/colonization-to-independence.html', 'http://cameran.jp/st-franois-du-lac.html', 'https://www.casanovashadows.com/881-2/']","Fighting took place primarily along the frontiers between New France and the British colonies, from Virginia in the south to Newfoundland in the north. It began with a dispute over control of the confluence of the Allegheny and Monongahela rivers called the Forks of the Ohio, and the site of the French Fort Duquesne within present-day Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. The dispute erupted into violence in the Battle of Jumonville Glen in May 1754, during which Virginia militiamen under the command of 22-year-old George Washington ambushed a French patrol.",where did french and indian war take place
the sequence of contraction of the heart chambers is,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Cardiac_cycle', 'https://hyperleap.com/topic/Ventricle_(heart)']","There are two atrial and two ventricle chambers of the heart; they are paired as the left heart and the right heart -- that is, the left atrium with the left ventricle, the right atrium with the right ventricle -- and they work in concert to traverse the cardiac cycle continuously, (see circular diagram at right margin). At the ""Start"" of the cycle, during ventricular diastole -- early, the heart relaxes and expands while receiving blood into both ventricles through both atria; then, near the end of ventricular diastole -- late, the two atria begin to contract (atrial systole), and each atrium pumps blood into the ventricle' below' it. During ventricular systole the ventricles are contracting and vigorously pulsing (or ejecting) two separated blood supplies from the heart -- one to the lungs and one to all other body organs and systems -- while the two atria are relaxed (atrial diastole). This coordination ensures that blood is efficiently collected and circulated throughout the body.",the sequence of contraction of the heart chambers is
what is the angle of tilt for the earth's axis,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Ecliptic', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Ceres_(dwarf_planet)', 'http://library.rstheory.org/books/bpom/12.html', 'https://dannyvanpoucke.be/tag/time/']","At an obliquity of zero, the two axes point in the same direction; i.e., the rotational axis is perpendicular to the orbital plane. Earth's obliquity oscillates between 22.1 and 24.5 degrees on a 41,000-year cycle; the earth's mean obliquity is currently 23 ° 26 ′ 13.1"" (or 23.43699 °) and decreasing.",what is the angle of tilt for the earth's axis
who gave the slogan swaraj is my right and i shall have it,"['http://www.brzesko.pl/?p=24210', 'https://gaathastory.com/lokmanya-bal-gangadhar-tilak-tale-from-his-childhood/', 'https://www.sampspeak.in/2016/07/', 'https://www.scribd.com/document/352153317/1-2-pdf', 'http://answers.gkplanet.in/2018/05/swaraj-is-my-birthright-and-i-shall-have-it.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Category:Indian_nationalists', 'http://hometownfamilycare.com/stories-written-by-sarojini-naidu.html']","Tilak was one of the first and strongest advocates of Swaraj (""self-rule"") and a strong radical in Indian consciousness. He is known for his quote in Marathi: ""Swarajya is my birthright and I shall have it!"". He formed a close alliance with many Indian National Congress leaders including Bipin Chandra Pal, Lala Lajpat Rai, Aurobindo Ghose, V.O. Chidambaram Pillai and Muhammad Ali Jinnah.",who gave the slogan swaraj is my right and i shall have it
who made black ops 3 for xbox 360,"['https://freepcgamesden.com/call-of-duty-black-ops-iii-free-game-full-download/', 'http://mtvufmmn.info/?newsid=47527', 'https://allroe.info/19ab64021.php', 'http://e-rakuen.info/?newsid=16776', 'http://wu-taichi.info/?page_id=24543', 'http://gourmetking.info/?newsid=38343', 'http://jailrecordsfind.info/?newsid=19851']","Call of Duty: Black Ops III is a first-person shooter video game, developed by Treyarch and published by Activision. It is the twelfth entry in the Call of Duty series and the sequel to the 2012 video game Call of Duty: Black Ops II. It was released on Microsoft Windows, PlayStation 4, and Xbox One on November 6, 2015. A feature-limited version developed by Beenox and Mercenary Technology that only supports multiplayer modes was released on PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360 and was also the final Call of Duty title released on those platforms.",who made black ops 3 for xbox 360
when was the first fridge invented and by whom,"['https://wikimili.com/en/William_Cullen', 'http://feic31.com/2465/a-brief-history-of-refrigeration/', 'https://maliburemodeling.com/', 'http://www.historyofrefrigeration.com/refrigeration-history/history-of-refrigerator/', 'http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Freezer', 'https://www.contractingbusiness.com/hvacrdb/recruiting-cold-industry', 'https://www.dtssydney.com/blog/jugaad_thinking_%E2%80%93_do_more_with_less']","The history of artificial refrigeration began when Scottish professor William Cullen designed a small refrigerating machine in 1755. Cullen used a pump to create a partial vacuum over a container of diethyl ether, which then boiled, absorbing heat from the surrounding air. The experiment even created a small amount of ice, but had no practical application at that time.",when was the first fridge invented and by whom
what is the elevation of the dead sea,"['http://brandweermiddendelfland.info/search?q=Dead%20sea%20mud%20spa', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/dead-sea', 'http://xautoman.com/3486-whyistheresomuchsaltinthedeadsea.html', 'http://www.easy-car-rental.com/index.php/ar/component/content/article/34-easy-rentals-/92-dead-sea-cheap-rentals', 'https://nature.new7wonders.com/wonders/dead-sea-israel-jordan-palestine', 'https://travel.siliconindia.com/travel-article/The-Dead-Sea-Israel-aid-4747.html', 'http://www.jordantowerhotel.com/miscellaneous-interests']","The Dead Sea (Hebrew: יָם הַמֶּלַח ‬ Yam ha-Melah lit. Sea of Salt; Arabic: البحر الميت ‎ Al-Bahr al-Mayyit) is a salt lake bordered by Jordan to the east and Israel and Palestine to the west. Its surface and shores are 430.5 metres (1,412 ft) below sea level, Earth's lowest elevation on land. The Dead Sea is 304 m (997 ft) deep, the deepest hypersaline lake in the world. With a salinity of 342 g / kg, or 34.2%, (in 2011), it is 9.6 times as salty as the ocean and one of the world's saltiest bodies of water. This salinity makes for a harsh environment in which plants and animals cannot flourish, hence its name. The Dead Sea's main, northern basin is 50 kilometres (31 mi) long and 15 kilometres (9 mi) wide at its widest point. It lies in the Jordan Rift Valley, and its main tributary is the Jordan River.",what is the elevation of the dead sea
when does the x files i want to believe take place,"['http://encyclopedia2.thefreedictionary.com/drummy', 'https://fatespensieve.wordpress.com/tag/movies/', 'http://www.wreckmybrain.com/2018/03/x-files-rewatch-soft-light_22.html', 'https://carmensuarez.com/2018/12/02/ten-things-that-may-surprise-you-about-me/', 'https://pastasworld.com/2018/08/09/the-x-files-s02-ep05-duane-berry/', 'http://www.giantfreakinrobot.com/topic/helix/page/3', 'https://pastasworld.com/2017/08/13/the-x-files-s01-ep23-roland/']","Dana Scully, a former FBI agent, is now a staff physician at a Catholic hospital; she is treating Christian, a young boy with symptoms similar to Sandhoff disease. FBI agent Mosely Drummy approaches Scully for help in locating her former partner, Fox Mulder, who has been in hiding as a fugitive for several years. Drummy states that the FBI will call off its manhunt for Mulder if he helps investigate the disappearances of several women in West Virginia, the latest of whom is a young FBI agent named Monica Bannan. Scully agrees and convinces a reluctant Mulder to help.",when does the x files i want to believe take place
where did the american staffordshire terrier come from,"['https://www.perfectpedigreethailand.com/american-staffordshire-terrier.html', 'http://dougbittinger.com/thoughts/truth-behind-pit-bull/', 'https://www.soulslingerkennel.com/breed-infos-1/history/', 'https://www.petwave.com/Dogs/Breeds/American-Pit-Bull-Terrier.aspx', 'http://www.canismajor.com/dog/amerpit.html', 'http://www.amstaff.org/history.html', 'https://canadogs.ca/american-pitbull-terrier/']","Despite its name, the Staffordshire Terrier's ancestor (Bull and Terrier) was first bred in the nineteenth century in Birmingham, West Midlands, rather than in the English county of Staffordshire where it was then later bred. The early ancestors of this breed came from England where, until the first part of the 19th century, the Bulldog was bred. Bulldogs pictured as late as 1870 resemble contemporary American Staffordshire Terriers to a greater degree than present-day Bulldogs. Some writers contend it was the White English Terrier, Fox Terrier, or the Black and Tan Terrier that was crossed with the Bulldog to develop the Staffordshire Bull Terrier; all three breeds shared many traits, the greatest differences being in color and spirit. The cross of Bulldog and Terrier was called by several names, including Bull-and-Terrier Dog, ""Pit Bull Terrier"" (Bull terrier used to fight on pit), or Half and Half. Later, it assumed the name of Staffordshire Bull Terrier in England. These dogs began to find their way into America as early as 1850. It became a new breed and was recognized by the United Kennel Club in 10 February, 1898, with the name American Pit Bull Terrier. In 1936 some pit bulls were accepted for registration in the American Kennel Club (AKC) Stud Book as Staffordshire Terriers with a new standard and purpose, belonging to the terrier and molosser groups. The name of the breed was revised January 1, 1969 to American Staffordshire Terrier; breeders in the United States had developed a variety which was heavier in weight than the Staffordshire Bull Terrier of England. The name change was to distinguish them as separate breeds.",where did the american staffordshire terrier come from
what is the population of la paz mexico,"['http://frankelforjudge.com/laaz-christmas-30176.html', 'http://bajainsider.com/article/map-la-paz-baja-california-sur-mexico', 'http://www.diamanteassociates.com/', 'https://cnaedu.com/tag/pa/', 'https://onthedottranslations.com/largest-cities-new-york-state/', 'https://us.housenode.com/midwest/south-dakota/aberdeen', 'https://www.tidebuy.com/top/sale-mens-shirts-aberdeen-102100-1242.html']","La Paz (pronounced (la ˈpas) (listen), Peace) is the capital city of the Mexican state of Baja California Sur and an important regional commercial center. The city had a 2015 census population of 244,219 inhabitants, making it the most populous city in the state. Its metropolitan population is somewhat larger because of the surrounding towns, such as El Centenario, Chametla and San Pedro. It is in La Paz Municipality, which is the fourth-largest municipality in Mexico in geographical size and reported a population of 290,286 inhabitants on a land area of 20,275 km (7,828 sq mi).",what is the population of la paz mexico
what does the symbol on the un flag mean,"['https://www.timeanddate.com/holidays/un/international-day-against-drug-abuse', 'https://www.timeanddate.com/holidays/un/public-service-day', 'http://heraldika.stamatovski.com/en/zname-on/', 'https://www.timeanddate.com/holidays/un/world-population-day', 'https://lingua-translations.com/international-day-of-the-worlds-indigenous-peoples/', 'https://happydays-365.com/international-youth-day/international-youth-day-august-12/', 'http://www.loeser.us/flags/un.html']","The olive branches are a symbol for peace, and the world map represents all the people and the countries of the world.",what does the symbol on the un flag mean
how many episodes left in the originals season 5,"['http://www.lyricszoo.com/the-originals/', 'http://www.poputrade.com/wholesale-the-originals-fifth-season-3dvd-50pcslot-p-7065.html', 'https://www.khatrimazas.com/the-originals-season-4-download/', 'http://rms-hg.com/western-australia/vampire-diaries-book-4-pdf-free.php', 'http://www.poputrade.com/wholesale-the-originals-fifth-season-3dvd-10pcslot-p-7064.html', 'https://www.visitrichmondbc.com/entering-storybrooke/once-faqs/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/TV_Land']","The Originals, a one-hour American supernatural drama, was renewed for a fifth season by The CW on May 10, 2017. The 2016 -- 17 United States television season debut of The Originals was pushed to midseason, as with the fourth-season premiere. On July 20, 2017, Julie Plec announced via Twitter that the upcoming season would be the series' last. The fifth season consists of 13 episodes and debuted on April 18, 2018. The series finale aired on August 1, 2018.",how many episodes left in the originals season 5
cyanobacteria (blue-green algae) is an example of what type of plankton,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Blue', 'http://kalikasan-philippines.org/index.php?option=com_content&amp;view=category&amp;layout=blog&amp;id=121&amp;Itemid=459', 'http://www.crawlist.net/2016/05/top-10-oldest-animal-species-in-world.html', 'http://oknara.ru/9apr9gqv.php', 'https://blueplanetarchive.photoshelter.com/gallery/Stromatolite/G00003HE3mUgnRE4/C0000_cakUtQmGaA', 'http://reto.cn/php/esperanto/etimologia-vortaro-de-esperanto/', 'https://readtiger.com/wkp/en/Messianism']","Cyanobacteria / saɪˌænoʊbækˈtɪəriə /, also known as Cyanophyta, are a phylum of bacteria that obtain their energy through photosynthesis, and are the only photosynthetic prokaryotes able to produce oxygen. The name ""cyanobacteria"" comes from the color of the bacteria (Greek: κυανός, translit. kyanós, lit.' blue'). Cyanobacteria (which are prokaryotes) used to be called ""blue-green algae"". They have been renamed' cyanobacteria' in order to avoid the term ""algae"", which in modern usage is restricted to eukaryotes.",cyanobacteria (blue-green algae) is an example of what type of plankton
who was responsible for the bombing of dresden,"['https://majormike.us/subjects/1633/', 'http://www.asdnyi.com/dresden-bombing/', 'https://dresdenradio.com/', 'https://www.stolenhistory.org/threads/what-weapon-was-used-to-bomb-ww2-dresden.371/', 'https://artistmichaelbarrett.com/artwork/4138080-Dear-Dresden.html', 'http://historyhubulster.co.uk/2015/02/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/02-13/all']","The bombing of Dresden was a British / American aerial bombing attack on the city of Dresden, the capital of the German state of Saxony, during World War II in the European Theatre. In four raids between 13 and 15 February 1945, 722 heavy bombers of the British Royal Air Force (RAF) and 527 of the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF) dropped more than 3,900 tons of high-explosive bombs and incendiary devices on the city. The bombing and the resulting firestorm destroyed over 1,600 acres (6.5 km) of the city centre. An estimated 22,700 to 25,000 people were killed, although larger casualty figures have been claimed. Three more USAAF air raids followed, two occurring on 2 March aimed at the city's railway marshalling yard and one smaller raid on 17 April aimed at industrial areas.",who was responsible for the bombing of dresden
who came up with the no child left behind act,"['https://www.greenwichtime.com/news/article/Letters-Another-vote-for-literacy-4961155.php', 'http://www.nheld.com/BTN25.htm', 'http://www.transportation-finance.org/funding_financing/legislation_regulations/federal_legislation/federal_legislative_process.aspx', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/pros-cons-no-child-left-behind-3325245', 'http://www.techlawjournal.com/topstories/2012/20120703.asp', 'http://blog.heartland.org/2015/03/the-death-throes-of-common-core/', 'https://patimes.org/servant-parted-friends/']","It was coauthored by Representatives John Boehner (R-OH), George Miller (D-CA), and Senators Edward Kennedy (D-MA) and Judd Gregg (R-NH). The United States House of Representatives passed the bill on December 13, 2001 (voting 381 -- 41), and the United States Senate passed it on December 18, 2001 (voting 87 -- 10). President Bush signed it into law on January 8, 2002.",who came up with the no child left behind act
who needs a visa to go to turkey,"['https://www.pettravel.com/passports_third_countries.cfm', 'https://en.calypsotour.com/pages/visa-policy-of-turkey', 'http://largechinesevase.com/tag/famille/', 'https://scholarship-positions.com/kiit-university-india-scholarships-program-international-students-india/2017/07/05/', 'https://www.wanderlass.com/others/visa-challenge/how-to-apply-tourist-visa-to-tonga.html', 'https://www.kiwiland.com/cannabis-seeds/dna-genetics/dna-genetics-60-day-lemon-40854.html', 'http://www.traveljournal.com/guide.php?cc=SLB']","Even though Turkey is a candidate country for the membership in the European Union, it has a more complex visa policy than the visa policy of the Schengen Area. Turkey requires visas from citizens of certain EU member states and Schengen Annex II countries and territories -- Antigua and Barbuda, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Bahamas, Barbados, Canada, Croatia, Cyprus, Dominica, East Timor, Grenada, Ireland, Kiribati, Malta, Marshall Islands, Mauritius, Mexico, Micronesia, Norway, Netherlands, Palau, Poland, Portugal, Saint Lucia, Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Spain, Taiwan, Tonga, Tuvalu, United Arab Emirates, United Kingdom, United States, and Vanuatu. On the other hand, Turkey grants visa-free access to citizens of other countries and territories -- Azerbaijan, Belarus, Belize, Bolivia, Ecuador, Iran, Kosovo, Kyrgyzstan, Jordan, Lebanon, Mongolia, Morocco, Qatar, Russia, Tajikistan, Thailand, Tunisia, Turkmenistan and Uzbekistan.",who needs a visa to go to turkey
what does wagon wheel by darius rucker mean,"['https://jestimous.wordpress.com/category/a-to-z-challenge/', 'https://songsinirish.com/wagon-wheel-as-gaeilge/']","The song describes a hitchhiking journey south along the eastern coast of the United States, from New England in the northeast, through Roanoke, Virginia with the intended destination of Raleigh, North Carolina, where the narrator hopes to see his lover. As the narrator is walking south of Roanoke, he catches a ride with a trucker who is traveling from Philadelphia through Virginia westward toward the Cumberland Gap and Johnson City, Tennessee.",what does wagon wheel by darius rucker mean
after flash thompson finished bullying peter parker he became,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Madison_Jeffries', 'http://stargate-rasa.info/62/03794-agent-venom-costume.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Flash_Thompson.html', 'http://tonsoffacts.com/category/comics/page/3/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171220003-superheroes', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Bucky_Barnes', 'https://britishcomics.wordpress.com/2017/03/03/killpower/']","Eugene ""Flash"" Thompson is a fictional character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. He is a star high school football player who mercilessly bullies his high school classmate Peter Parker but greatly admires Spider-Man, an irony in which the superhero takes some gratification, though he and Peter become close friends in college. After graduation, he joins the United States Army and is haunted by his combat experiences, leading to alcoholism. After losing both of his legs in the Iraq War, he was bound to the Venom Symbiote as Agent Venom, a superhero and the first to control the organism.",after flash thompson finished bullying peter parker he became
who made the first lens in the world,"['http://www.loreescience.ca/2018-2019-s1-blog/week-10-lenses-refraction-phenomena', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Nikon', 'https://visionplusmag.com/global/evolution-of-lens-technology/']","The earliest known lenses were made from polished crystal, often quartz, and have been dated as early as 750 BC for Assyrian lenses such as the Nimrud / Layard lens. There are many similar lenses from ancient Egypt, Greece and Babylon. The ancient Romans and Greeks filled glass spheres with water to make lenses. However, glass lenses were not thought of until the Middle Ages.",who made the first lens in the world
what frame is the smith and wesson governor,['https://www.gunsandammo.com/editorial/sw-announces-addition-to-mp-bodyguard-38-revolver-series/247764'],The Smith & Wesson Governor is a snub-nosed (2.75 inch barrel) single-action / double-action revolver built on the Z-frame (a stretched N-frame) and utilizes a K-frame grip with a lightweight scandium alloy or stainless steel frame.,what frame is the smith and wesson governor
who has 3 stars on the hollywood walk of fame,"['https://jesswaid.com/2012/11/', 'http://medallic.medalcraft.com/about/world-famous-plaques-hollywood-walk-of-fame.php']","The original selection committees chose to recognize some entertainers' contributions in multiple categories with multiple stars. Gene Autry is the only honoree with stars in all five categories. Bob Hope, Mickey Rooney, Roy Rogers, and Tony Martin each have stars in four categories -- Rooney has three of his own and a fourth with his eighth and final wife, Jan, while Rogers also has three of his own, and a fourth with his band, Sons of the Pioneers. Thirty-three people, including Bing Crosby, Frank Sinatra, Dean Martin, Dinah Shore, Gale Storm, Danny Kaye, Douglas Fairbanks Jr., and Jack Benny, have stars in three categories.",who has 3 stars on the hollywood walk of fame
who is the girl in the rosanna video by toto,['https://informationcradle.com/usa/cynthia-rhodes/'],"Rhodes also appeared as a dancer in music videos, such as ""Rosanna"" by the band Toto, ""The Woman in You"" by the Bee Gees, and ""Don't Mean Nothing"" by Richard Marx. She was a dancer for the glam rock band The Tubes when they toured in the early 1980s. Rhodes later joined the 1980s pop group Animotion, replacing the group's singer Astrid Plane for the recording of its third album of original material. Though the group's single ""Room to Move"" rose to No. 9 on the Billboard charts, the album failed to match the group's earlier success, peaking at only No. 110 on the pop charts; shortly thereafter, the group disbanded. In 2002, Rhodes co-wrote the smooth jazz track ""Perfect Day"" with then-husband Richard Marx for December, trumpeter Chris Botti's holiday album.",who is the girl in the rosanna video by toto
who is paying for the curse of oak island,"['https://www.tvovermind.com/can-curse-oak-island-continue-season/', 'https://jokermag.com/great-oak-island-debate/', 'https://frostsnow.com/brothers-rick-lagina-and-marty-lagina-have-worked-on-the-curse-of-oak-island-rick-s-career', 'http://agiasma.ru/', 'https://www.cordcuttingreviews.com/stream-brooklyn-nine-nine-online/', 'https://www.comparama.com/topic/american-horror-story/', 'https://buydvdsonline.co.uk/dvd-releases-uk/american-horror-story-cult-season-7/']","Having started in 2014, The Curse of Oak Island is currently in its fifth season. On August 2, 2016, it was announced that Nova Scotia Business Inc. approved $1,271,546 in film funding for the production of the 4th season. In October 2017, a fifth season was announced, which began airing on November 7, 2017.",who is paying for the curse of oak island
when is the last time a total solar eclipse happened,"['https://www.earthnetworks.com/blog/eclipses/', 'http://www.ournewplanets.info/2018/01/super-blue-blood-moon-total-lunar.html', 'https://earthsky.org/tonight/middle-of-eclipse-season-on-july-28', 'https://guardian.ng/tag/solar-eclipse/', 'https://dcmp.org/media/10759-ask-a-scientist-what-s-happening-on-august-21-2017-and-what-can-people-potentially-see', 'https://www.atwoodvacations.com/blog/2017-solar-eclipse', 'http://www.sermonindex.net/modules/newbb/viewtopic.php?topic_id=59886&forum=35&start=20']","The next solar eclipse (Partial) will occur on February 15, 2018; the last solar eclipse (Total) occurred on August 21, 2017.",when is the last time a total solar eclipse happened
advantages of a plant that produces woody tissue,"['http://sccoplanning.com/PlanningHome/Environmental/Riparian/WhatisaRiparianCorridor.aspx', 'https://www.thetortoisetable.org.uk/resources/glossary-of-plant-terms/', 'http://herbarium.usu.edu/resources/learning_about_plants/classification', 'http://news.vanbnursery.com/current/', 'https://dralbertojieh.blogspot.com/2010/10/five-branches-of-traditional-medicine.html', 'https://gardeningwow.com/a-5-part-introduction-to-adding-garden-perennials-for-beginners/', 'http://theprairieproject.okstate.edu/plants/grasses/big-bluestem.html/plants/woody-plants']","A woody plant is a plant that produces wood as its structural tissue. Woody plants are usually either trees, shrubs, or lianas. These are usually perennial plants whose stems and larger roots are reinforced with wood produced from secondary xylem. The main stem, larger branches, and roots of these plants are usually covered by a layer of bark. Wood is a structural cellular adaptation that allows woody plants to grow from above ground stems year after year, thus making some woody plants the largest and tallest terrestrial plants.",advantages of a plant that produces woody tissue
the roger's commission had concluded that the problem in the challenger case was,"['http://downwithtyranny.blogspot.com/2010/05/deja-vu-all-over-again-who-could-have.html', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/Christa_McAuliffe', 'https://donnagore.com/2016/07/20/success-and-trauma-three-women-in-space/', 'https://www.nasaspaceflight.com/2012/07/sally-ride-legacy-true-shuttle-pioneer/']","The commission found that the Challenger accident was caused by a failure in the O-rings sealing the aft field joint on the right solid rocket booster, causing pressurized hot gases and eventually flame to ""blow by"" the O-ring and contact the adjacent external tank, causing structural failure. The failure of the O-rings was attributed to a design flaw, as their performance could be too easily compromised by factors including the low temperature on the day of launch.",the roger's commission had concluded that the problem in the challenger case was
when did venus and serena start playing tennis,"['http://www.allcelebritylifestyle.com/serena-williams-net-worth/', 'http://articlebio.com/serena-williams']","Williams was born in Saginaw, Michigan, to Richard Williams and Oracene Price, and is the youngest of Price's five daughters: half-sisters Yetunde, Lyndrea, and Isha Price, and full sister Venus. When the children were young, the family moved to Compton, California, where Williams started playing tennis at the age of three. Her father, Richard, home-schooled Serena and her sister Venus. While he and subsequently her mother, Oracene, have been the official coaches, other mentors who helped her learn the game included Richard Williams, a Compton man who shared her father's name and would go on to found The Venus and Serena Williams Tennis / Tutorial Academy.",when did venus and serena start playing tennis
initially what was the main purpose of private health insurance in the us,"['http://www.stibroker.com/texas-health-insurance/', 'http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/Health_insurance_in_the_United_States', 'http://www.freedom-meditech.com/thema/first-health-insurance', 'https://www.redmagicstyle.com/well-being-insurance-group.html', 'http://jerneskakklub.dk/insurance-23/insurance-jobs-ireland.html', 'http://www.placemats4you.net/insurance-2/american-life-health-insurance.html', 'http://deqignerteq.us/page/3']","Accident insurance was first offered in the United States by the Franklin Health Assurance Company of Massachusetts. This firm, founded in 1850, offered insurance against injuries arising from railroad and steamboat accidents. Sixty organizations were offering accident insurance in the US by 1866, but the industry consolidated rapidly soon thereafter. While there were earlier experiments, sickness coverage in the US effectively dates from 1890. The first employer-sponsored group disability policy was issued in 1911, but this plan's primary purpose was replacing wages lost because the worker was unable to work, not medical expenses.",initially what was the main purpose of private health insurance in the us
what bill divided the united states into 13 judicial districts,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Presidency_of_George_Washington', 'https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/United_States_Statutes_at_Large/Volume_1/1st_Congress/1st_Session/Chapter_20', 'https://www.usmarshals.gov/history/firstmarshals/marshals1.htm', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/District_attorney', 'http://constitution.islaws.com/article-3-of-the-constitution', 'http://www.vawd.uscourts.gov/court-information.aspx', 'https://familypedia.wikia.org/wiki/Bourbon_County,_Kentucky']","The Act also created 13 judicial districts within the 11 states that had then ratified the Constitution (North Carolina and Rhode Island were added as judicial districts in 1790, and other states as they were admitted to the Union). Each state comprised one district, except for Virginia and Massachusetts, each of which comprised two. Massachusetts was divided into the District of Maine (which was then part of Massachusetts) and the District of Massachusetts (which covered modern-day Massachusetts). Virginia was divided into the District of Kentucky (which was then part of Virginia) and the District of Virginia (which covered modern-day West Virginia and Virginia).",what bill divided the united states into 13 judicial districts
where does the mercedes benz name come from,"['http://blog.luxurycare.org/mercedes-benz-combination-of-luxury-and-performance/', 'https://hintng.com/cars-in-nigeria-most-common-them-all/', 'https://ssahib12.home.blog/', 'http://www.internationalcarspotters.com/mercedes-benz.html', 'https://myntransportblog.com/2016/03/16/mercedes-benz-daimler-ag/', 'http://www.kawanaautowreckers.com.au/mercedes-benz-new-and-used-parts-and-accessories/', 'https://thecomplaintpoint.com/mercedes-benz-complaints-email-phone-number']","Mercedes-Benz traces its origins to Daimler-Motoren-Gesellschaft's 1901 Mercedes and Karl Benz's 1886 Benz Patent-Motorwagen, which is widely regarded as the first gasoline-powered automobile. The slogan for the brand is ""the best or nothing"".",where does the mercedes benz name come from
where did the legend of merlin come from,"['http://bringingupsalamanders.blogspot.com/2010/04/', 'https://kingarthur.fandom.com/wiki/Merlin', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Cadwaladr', 'http://hereticaloracles.com/2018/02/01/asteroid-files-merlin/', 'https://heaven-light.de.tl/Witches-and-Wizareds.htm', 'https://www.in.com/business/halloween-2018-bill-gates-and-warren-buffet-are-the-stuff-of-legends-237309.htm', 'http://archive.constantcontact.com/fs091/1101811920551/archive/1108996836951.html']","Merlin (Welsh: Myrddin) is a legendary figure best known as the wizard featured in Arthurian legend and medieval Welsh poetry. The standard depiction of the character first appears in Geoffrey of Monmouth's Historia Regum Britanniae, written c. 1136, and is based on an amalgamation of previous historical and legendary figures. Geoffrey combined existing stories of Myrddin Wyllt (Merlinus Caledonensis), a North Brythonic prophet and madman with no connection to King Arthur, with tales of the Romano-British war leader Ambrosius Aurelianus to form the composite figure he called Merlin Ambrosius (Welsh: Myrddin Emrys). He is allegedly buried in the Broceliande forest, near Paimpont in Brittany.",where did the legend of merlin come from
how many championships did lebron win at miami,"['https://xtradonaire.wordpress.com/2018/01/17/a-tribute-to-lebron-james/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1998%E2%80%9399_NBA_lockout', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/LeBron_James', 'http://www.efans.com/lebronjames', 'http://www.directsportslink.com/speaker/lebron-james', 'https://memorabiliacenter.com/product/lebron-james-autographed-8-x-10-photo/', 'https://sontlive.com/the-dominant-20-athletes-of-the-last-20-years/']","James played high school basketball at St. Vincent -- St. Mary High School in his hometown of Akron, Ohio, where he was highly promoted in the national media as a future NBA superstar. After graduating, he was selected by his home team, the Cleveland Cavaliers, as the first overall pick of the 2003 NBA draft. James led Cleveland to the franchise's first Finals appearance in 2007, ultimately losing to the San Antonio Spurs. In 2010, he left the Cavaliers for the Miami Heat in a highly publicized ESPN special titled The Decision. James spent four seasons with the Heat, reaching the Finals all four years and winning back-to-back championships in 2012 and 2013. In 2013, he led Miami on a 27-game winning streak, the third longest in league history. Following his final season with the Heat, James opted out of his contract and returned to the Cavaliers. He led the Cavaliers to three consecutive Finals series between 2015 and 2017, winning his third championship in 2016 to end Cleveland's 52-year professional sports title drought.",how many championships did lebron win at miami
what causes your bones to make a cracking sound,"['https://www.highgatehospital.co.uk/gp-news/medical-expert-explains-the-health-risks-in-cracking-your-joints/', 'http://advancedacupunctureclinic.com/2016/07/06/hernia-facts/', 'http://www.articleinsider.com/health-and-fitness/back-pain/shoulder-joint-pain', 'http://www.healthyeatingandyou.com/3-main-types-of-treatments-for-your-back-pain/']","The act of cracking joints means bending a person's joints to produce a distinct cracking or popping sound, often followed by a feeling of satisfaction or relaxation to the person. It is sometimes done as part of a joint adjustment / mobilization routinely performed by a chiropractor, osteopath or physical therapist.",what causes your bones to make a cracking sound
