when did we start using ce instead of ad,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Common_Era', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Calendar', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Common_Era', 'http://thingiverse-production.s3.amazonaws.com/when-did-christianity-begin-bce.html', 'https://human.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/History/Book%3A_World_History_(Boundless)/Chapter_1%3A_The_Study_of_History_and_the_Rise_of_Civilization/Section_4%3A_Dates_and_Calendars', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/%27Illish']","The expression has been traced back to 1615, when it first appeared in a book by Johannes Kepler as the Latin usage vulgaris aerae, and to 1635 in English as ""Vulgar Era"". The term ""Common Era"" can be found in English as early as 1708, and became more widely used in the mid-19th century by Jewish academics. In the later 20th century, the use of CE and BCE was popularized in academic and scientific publications, and more generally by authors and publishers wishing to emphasize secularism or sensitivity to non-Christians, by not explicitly referencing Jesus as ""Christ"" and Dominus (""Lord"") through use of the abbreviation ""AD"".",when did we start using ce instead of ad
where did the term man cave come from,"['https://tararuby.com/my-special-space/', 'http://freeinfocontent.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=39224', 'http://ssbsavannah.ning.com/profiles/blogs/read-russ-and-the-firehouse-day-with-russ-ios', 'http://wiki.mrlocke.net/index.php?title=Sermon_for_July_22nd,_2012&action=edit', 'http://www.blog.resurrectantiques.com/category/uncategorized/', 'http://www.roadabode.us/2014/12/why-rv-trumps-man-cave.html', 'http://actualcorp.ru/girl_version_of_man_cave.html']","A man cave or manspace, and less commonly a manland or mantuary is a male retreat or sanctuary in a home, such as a specially equipped garage, spare bedroom, media room, den, or basement. The term ""man cave"" is a metaphor describing a room inside the house such as the basement or garage or attic or office, or outside the house such as a wood shed or tool room where ""guys can do as they please"", without fear of upsetting any female sensibility about house decor or design. Paula Aymer of Tufts University calls it the ""last bastion of masculinity"". The phrase is thought to come from the 1993 publication, Men Are from Mars, Women Are from Venus.",where did the term man cave come from
what do you mean by ho chi minh trail,"['http://www.thelongridehome.com.au/day_24_of_riding_chi_thanh_to_dai_lanh', 'https://wikimili.com/en/%C4%90%E1%BB%93ng_S%C4%A9_Nguy%C3%AAn', 'http://trekkingvietnam.net/vietnam-road-cycling-9-days/', 'https://motorcycletours.journeyexpedition.com/product/memorable-vietnam-motorbike-tour-on-ho-chi-minh-trail-11-days/', 'http://www.artandpopularculture.com/Cambodian_Campaign', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Vietcong', 'http://www.travelswop.com/blog/vietnam/tours/ho-chi-minh-trail-motorcycle-tours.html']","The Hồ Chí Minh trail (also known in Vietnam as the ""Trường Sơn trail"") was a logistical system that ran from the Democratic Republic of Vietnam (North Vietnam) to the Republic of Vietnam (South Vietnam) through the kingdoms of Laos and Cambodia. The system provided support, in the form of manpower and materiel, to the National Front for the Liberation of South Vietnam (called the Viet Cong or ""VC"" by its opponents) and the People's Army of Vietnam (PAVN), or North Vietnamese Army, during the Vietnam War.",what do you mean by ho chi minh trail
who issued the edict of milan making christianity a legally recognized religion in the roman empire,"['https://wikimili.com/en/June_13', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=milanlegal.com&ads=1&title=Milan+legal&auto=Milan+legal&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Milan+legal&pagenum=5', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Constantine_the_Great_and_Christianity', 'https://www.preceden.com/timelines/305459-catholic-history-timeline-mcclements', 'http://the-jesus-realm.com/dokuwiki/doku.php?id=devotional:june&amp;tab_files=search&amp;do=media&amp;ns=devotional', 'https://lifehopeandtruth.com/change/the-church/church-history-constantine/', 'https://tableprepared.com/2016/05/06/the-lines-are-drawn-good-news-for-faithful-christians-in-a-chaotic-world/']","The Edict of Milan (Latin: Edictum Mediolanense) was the February 313 AD agreement to treat Christians benevolently within the Roman Empire. Western Roman Emperor Constantine I and Licinius, who controlled the Balkans, met in Milan and, among other things, agreed to change policies towards Christians following the Edict of Toleration by Galerius issued two years earlier in Serdica. The Edict of Milan gave Christianity a legal status, but did not make Christianity the State church of the Roman Empire; this took place under Emperor Theodosius I in 380 AD with the Edict of Thessalonica.",who issued the edict of milan making christianity a legally recognized religion in the roman empire
when does luke find out darth vader is his father,"['https://www.all80s.co.uk/the-empire-strikes-back-1980/', 'http://starwarsconnection.com/the-empire-strikes-back-movie-overview', 'https://www.ibtimes.co.uk/star-wars-new-hope-empire-strikes-back-return-jedi-recap-ahead-force-awakens-1533287', 'https://canonkillerbase.com/product/star-wars-episode-v-the-empire-strikes-back/', 'http://simongeake.co.uk/Empire%20Strikes%20Back.htm', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2017/05/21/', 'https://nafirstlaunch.com/2017/01/05/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-2/']","Vader intends to hold Luke in suspended animation via carbon freezing, and selects Han to be frozen as a test subject. Han survives the process and is given to Fett, who intends to deliver Han to Jabba the Hutt. Lando initiates an escape and frees Leia and the others, but they are too late to stop Fett from departing with Han. They fight their way back to the Falcon and flee Cloud City. Meanwhile, Luke arrives at Cloud City and engages with Vader in a lightsaber duel that leads them over the city's central air shaft. Vader severs Luke's right hand, disarming him; when Luke refuses to join Vader against the Emperor, accusing him of murdering his father, Vader reveals that he, in fact, is his father. Horrified by the truth, Luke intentionally falls into the air shaft and is ejected beneath the floating city, where he grabs onto an antenna. He makes a telepathic plea to Leia, who senses it and persuades Lando to return for him in the Falcon. After Luke is brought on board, they are chased by TIE fighters but R2-D2 reactivates the Falcon's hyperdrive, allowing them to escape.",when does luke find out darth vader is his father
what is the approximate latitudinal and longitudinal extent of india,"['http://shikshaportal.com/exams/upsc/indian-geography-physiography-boundaries-india-other-country', 'http://www.jobguj.in/2017/04/indian-geography-information-detailed.html', 'https://www.4eb.org.au/indian', 'http://brandbharat.com/english/Indian%20geography.html', 'http://conf.racurs.ru/conf2016/eng/location/country.php', 'http://www.accessbudgetsafaris.com/index.php/uganda/explore-uganda.html', 'http://discoveredindia.com/india-at-a-glance/geography.htm']","India lies on the Indian Plate, the northern portion of the Indo-Australian Plate, whose continental crust forms the Indian subcontinent. The country is situated north of the equator between 8 ° 4' to 35 ° 3' north latitude and 68 ° 7' to 97 ° 25' east longitude. It is the seventh-largest country in the world, with a total area of 3,287,469 square kilometres (1,269,299 sq mi). India measures 3,055 km (1,898 mi) from north to south and 2,933 km (1,822 mi) from east to west. It has a land frontier of 15,106.7 km (9,387 mi) and a coastline of 7,516.6 km (4,671 mi).",what is the approximate latitudinal and longitudinal extent of india
what is the use of bacteria that reside in our intestine,"['https://www.healthyhorses.ca/equine-choice-products/', 'https://mysolluna.com/blog/2015/06/02/the-down-and-dirty-on-soil-based-organisms/', 'https://www.clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT03325023', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-microbiology/chapter/overview-of-immunity/', 'http://www.traviscooks.com/2011/06/', 'https://scidoc.org/IJGPMB-2577-4336-01-101.php', 'https://shop.purelyinspired.com/products/7-day-cleanse/']","The relationship between some gut flora and humans is not merely commensal (a non-harmful coexistence), but rather a mutualistic relationship. Some human gut microorganisms benefit the host by fermenting dietary fiber into short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), such as acetic acid and butyric acid, which are then absorbed by the host. Intestinal bacteria also play a role in synthesizing vitamin B and vitamin K as well as metabolizing bile acids, sterols, and xenobiotics. The systemic importance of the SCFAs and other compounds they produce are like hormones and the gut flora itself appears to function like an endocrine organ, and dysregulation of the gut flora has been correlated with a host of inflammatory and autoimmune conditions.",what is the use of bacteria that reside in our intestine
when are the mysteries of the rosary said,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Rosary', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Our_Lady_of_La_Salette', 'http://rosary-prayers.eu/', 'https://www.praywithme.com/the-rosary-prayer.html', 'https://www.catholicireland.net/glossary-of-terms/', 'http://site.mawebcenters.com/personalizedrosaries2/pray.html', 'https://www.brookvilleparishes.com/']","The prayers that essentially compose the Rosary are arranged in sets of ten Hail Marys with each set preceded by one Lord's Prayer and followed by one Glory Be, with perhaps the ""Oh My Jesus"" added, based on the apparitions at Fátima in 1917. During recitation of each set, known as a decade, thought is given to one of the Mysteries of the Rosary, which recall events in the lives of Jesus and Mary. The Glorious mysteries are said on Sunday and Wednesday, the Joyful on Monday and Saturday, the Sorrowful on Tuesday and Friday, and the Luminous Mysteries are said on Thursday. Normally, five decades are recited in a session. Various prayers are sometimes added after each decade (for example, the Fátima Prayer), at the beginning (in particular, the Apostles' Creed), and at the end (in particular, the Hail, Holy Queen). The rosary as a material object is an aid towards saying these prayers in the proper sequence.",when are the mysteries of the rosary said
what is a master of public health degree,"['https://www.collegeaffordabilityguide.org/subjects/public-health/', 'https://www.collegedisha.com/difference-between-msc-and-mph-degree', 'http://umeshg.com.np/mph-in-nepal/', 'https://borealist.com/masters-degree-in-public-policy/', 'http://www.excite.com/education/healthcare/public-health', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/1012364', 'https://www.guidetoonlineschools.com/degrees/public-health']","The Master of Public Health (M.P.H.), Master of Science in Public Health (MSPH), Master of Medical Science in Public Health (MMSPH) and the Doctor of Public Health (Dr. P.H.), International Masters for Health Leadership (IMHL) are multi-disciplinary professional degrees awarded for studies in areas related to public health. The MPH degree focuses on public health practice, as opposed to research or teaching. Master of Public Health programs are available throughout the world in Programs in Public Health, Medical Schools, Schools of Public Health, and Schools of Public Affairs.",what is a master of public health degree
alvin and the chipmunks with the chipettes movie,['https://jonstewart2018.com/358.html'],"The film, directed by Janice Karman and written by Karman and Ross Bagdasarian, stars the voices of Karman, Bagdasarian, and Dody Goodman, and follows the Chipmunks and the Chipettes as they go on a hot air balloon race around the world that is the cover for a diamond smuggling ring.",alvin and the chipmunks with the chipettes movie
when would a bill go to a conference committee in congress,"['https://www.reference.com/web?q=how+are+congressional+committees+formed&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Committee', 'https://www.house.leg.state.mn.us/cco/rules/jtrule/jt203.htm', 'https://www.bcseeds.com/changes-to-cannabis-legislation/', 'https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/2/1801', 'http://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?path=/prelim@title31&edition=prelim', 'http://milesuponmyshoes.blogspot.com/2013/08/']",A conference committee is a committee of the United States Congress appointed by the House of Representatives and Senate to resolve disagreements on a particular bill. A conference committee is usually composed of senior Members of the standing committees of each House that originally considered the legislation.,when would a bill go to a conference committee in congress
what does the g stand for in vibgyor,"['https://aerbook.com/books/Roy_G_Biv_is_Mad_at_Me_Because_I_Love_Pink-13067.html?store_id=92&product_id=559463', 'http://bloggerseomaster.ml/53405-2019/roy-gee-biv-vyx.php', 'https://www.aaronwallis.co.uk/candidates/advice/memory-part-two.aspx', 'https://www.feedspot.com/infiniterss.php?q=site:http%3A%2F%2Ffeeds.feedburner.com%2FSundaySchoolLessons', 'https://blog.tamipotter.com/design_each_moment/', 'https://anentrepreneurswords.com/tag/entrepreneurship/', 'https://bcrc.org/memory-strategies-tips-tricks-for-everyday-life-by-lesley-addison-khan-farooqi/']","ROYGBIV or Roy G. Biv is an acronym for the sequence of hues commonly described as making up a rainbow: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.",what does the g stand for in vibgyor
how does an enzyme cause a reaction to increase in rate,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/%28R%29-2-methylmalate_dehydratase', 'http://www.imedpub.com/insights-in-enzyme-research/']","The mechanism of enzyme catalysis is similar in principle to other types of chemical catalysis. By providing an alternative reaction route the enzyme reduces the energy required to reach the highest energy transition state of the reaction. The reduction of activation energy (Ea) increases the amount of reactant molecules that achieve a sufficient level of energy, such that they reach the activation energy and form the product. As with other catalysts, the enzyme is not consumed during the reaction (as a substrate is) but is recycled such that a single enzyme performs many rounds of catalysis.",how does an enzyme cause a reaction to increase in rate
do you need a helmet to ride a bike in california,"['https://www.eliteresorts.com/strawberry-park/reservation/rules/', 'https://bikeitorhikeit.org/saratoga_national_historical_park.htm', 'https://www.lipconlawfirm.com/floridas-bike-helmet-headlight-laws/', 'https://www.ottawainjury.ca/lawyers/accident-benefits-insurance-claims/ottawa-bicycle-accidents-cycling-safety-in-ottawa-what-to-look-for-in-a-helmet/', 'https://www.cyclelifehq.com/en/destinations/usa/georgia/atlanta', 'http://www.sunfoxcampground.com/sunfox-rules/', 'http://www.velascolawyers.com/en/motor-and-marine-law/180-new-road-regulations-2014.html']",CVC 21212 requires cyclists under the age of 18 to wear helmets.,do you need a helmet to ride a bike in california
what type of martial art is kung fu,"['https://wn.com/Kungfu_superhero?from=kungfusuperhero.com', 'http://www.primidi.com/chinese_martial_arts', 'https://www.kungfu4less.com/kungfu-page.html', 'http://1000games.com/1000Games/index.php?n=1&lang=_en&a=9&b=1&game=0&count=0', 'https://ikkaido.eu/kung-fu/', 'http://wushuacademy.com.au/about/kung-fu-wu-shu/', 'https://www.southerncrossmats.com.au/kung-fu/']","Chinese martial arts, often named under the umbrella terms kung fu (/ ˈkʊŋ ˈfuː /; Chinese: 功夫; pinyin: gōngfu; Cantonese Yale: gūng fū) and wushu (武術; wǔshù), are the several hundred fighting styles that have developed over the centuries in China. These fighting styles are often classified according to common traits, identified as ""families"" (家; jiā), ""sects"" (派; pài) or ""schools"" (門; mén) of martial arts. Examples of such traits include Shaolinquan (少林拳) physical exercises involving Five Animals (五 形) mimicry, or training methods inspired by Old Chinese philosophies, religions and legends. Styles that focus on qi manipulation are called internal (内 家 拳; nèijiāquán), while others that concentrate on improving muscle and cardiovascular fitness are called ""external"" (外 家 拳; wàijiāquán). Geographical association, as in northern (北 拳; běiquán) and ""southern"" (南 拳; nánquán), is another popular classification method.",what type of martial art is kung fu
what was coca cola used for as a medicine,"['https://www.amusingplanet.com/2012/08/the-world-of-coca-cola-museum-in-atlanta.html', 'https://blog.darwinex.com/trading-is-intellectual-property/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Archive', 'https://companies.jrank.org/pages/1007/Coca-Cola-Enterprises-Inc.html', 'http://wesleytyler.com/2013/11/i-love-coca-cola.html', 'http://appalachianmagazine.com/2017/10/27/map-explains-why-you-say-pop-soda-or-coke/', 'https://www.thebushypath.com/2017/10/coca-cola-7-effective-lessons-to-learn.html']","In 1885, Pemberton registered his French Wine Coca nerve tonic. In 1886, when Atlanta and Fulton County passed prohibition legislation, Pemberton responded by developing Coca-Cola, a nonalcoholic version of French Wine Coca. The first sales were at Jacob's Pharmacy in Atlanta, Georgia, on May 8, 1886. It was initially sold as a patent medicine for five cents a glass at soda fountains, which were popular in the United States at the time due to the belief that carbonated water was good for the health. Pemberton claimed Coca-Cola cured many diseases, including morphine addiction, indigestion, nerve disorders, headaches, and impotence. Pemberton ran the first advertisement for the beverage on May 29 of the same year in the Atlanta Journal.",what was coca cola used for as a medicine
who sang the original version of feeling good,['https://musescore.com/groups/minecraft/sheetmusic'],"""Feeling Good"" (also known as ""Feelin' Good"") is a song written by English composers Anthony Newley and Leslie Bricusse for the musical The Roar of the Greasepaint -- The Smell of the Crowd. It was first performed on stage in 1964 by Cy Grant on the UK tour and by Gilbert Price in 1965 with the original Broadway cast.",who sang the original version of feeling good
where did the president of argentina go to college,"['http://firstthing.dailymaverick.co.za/article?id=105256', 'http://en.libertadyprogresonline.org/2018/05/16/tough-lessons-from-populism-in-argentina/', 'https://www.ncaacademy.com/for-all-defence-aspirants-ndacdsafcat-part-2/', 'https://in.reuters.com/finance/stocks/company-officers/IDR.MC', 'https://sputniknews.com/latam/201610101046188513-latin-america-education/']","Born in Tandil, Buenos Aires Province, Macri is the son of Francesco Macri, a prominent Italian businessman in the industrial and construction sectors, and was raised in an upper class home. He received a bachelor's degree in civil engineering from the Pontifical Catholic University of Argentina and studied at Columbia Business School in New York City. Macri became president of Boca Juniors, one of Argentina's two most popular football clubs, in 1995. In 2005, he created the centre-right Republican Proposal party (Propuesta Republicana, also known as PRO).",where did the president of argentina go to college
where does variation in the traits of a population come from,"['http://qvprep.com/biologylessons/11-2.html', 'http://intelligentreasoning.blogspot.com/2011/12/kevin-r-mccarthy-still-spewing-and.html', 'https://www.qsstudy.com/biology/significance-of-meiosis', 'https://www.simply.science/genetic-diversity', 'https://biologyboom.com/and-gene-frequencie/', 'https://biologyboom.com/evolutionary-mechanisms/', 'https://biologyboom.com/the-nature-of-evolutionary-forces/']","Genetic variation is brought about, fundamentally, by mutation, which is a permanent change in the chemical structure of chromosomes. Genetic recombination also produces changes within alleles.",where does variation in the traits of a population come from
how wide is a standard 2 lane road,"['https://www.helpwikileaks.co.za/tag/driveway-paving-price-and-driveway-sealing-cost/', 'http://www.co.summit.co.us/926/Summit-Cove-Loop-Feedback', 'http://raisethehammer.org/article/2360/', 'http://www.roadstothefuture.com/I64_Widening_NNH.html']","The Interstate Highway standards for the U.S. Interstate Highway System use a 12-foot (3.7 m) standard lane width, while narrower lanes are used on lower classification roads. In Europe, laws and road widths vary by country; the minimum widths of lanes are generally between 2.5 to 3.25 metres (8.2 to 10.7 ft). The federal Bundesstraße interurban network in Germany defines a minimum of 3.5 metres (11 ft 6 in) for each lane for the smallest two lane roads, with an additional 0.25 metres (9.84 in) on the outer sides and shoulders being at least 1.5 metres (59.06 in) on each side. A modern Autobahn divided highway with two lanes per direction has lanes 3.75 metres (12 ft 4 in) wide with an additional clearance of 0.50 metres (19.69 in) on each side;, with three lanes per direction this becomes 3.75 metres (12 ft 4 in) for the rightmost lane and 3.5 metres (11 ft 6 in) for the other lanes. Urban access roads and roads in low-density areas may have lanes as narrow as 2.75 metres (9 ft 0 in) in width per lane, with shoulders at least 1 metre (3 ft 3 in) wide.",how wide is a standard 2 lane road
who plays gamora from guardians of the galaxy,"['https://www.screamingtoilet.com/on-screen/guardians-of-the-galaxy-vol2-2017-spoiler-free-first-section', 'https://celebsline.com/batista/', 'https://tvseans.com/en/person/6497/karen-gillan', 'https://wikipops.com/?wiki=Karen+Gillan', 'https://www.atomtickets.com/movies/missing-link/271425/trivia', 'https://movieweb.com/guardians-of-galaxy-2-500-million-milestone-box-office/', 'https://gravityspeakers.com/speaker/erin-sarofsky/']",Saldana in the Marvel Cinematic Universe portrays Gamora beginning with Guardians of the Galaxy (2014) and later also in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 (2017) and Avengers: Infinity War (2018).,who plays gamora from guardians of the galaxy
who has the power to remove a president from office,"['https://www.thoughtco.com/impeachment-the-unthinkable-process-3322171', 'https://elitewritings.com/essays/process/the-presidential-impeachment-process-essay.html', 'https://www.quillproject.net/commentary_collections/10', 'http://m.american-historama.org/1990-present-modern-era/impeachment.htm', 'https://www.consource.org/document/north-carolina-ratification-convention-debates-1788-7-25/', 'https://law.marquette.edu/facultyblog/2010/09/23/a-modest-proposal-for-ending-gridlock-in-washington/', 'http://www.israelnationalnews.com/Articles/Article.aspx/22148']","At the federal level, Article Two of the United States Constitution states in Section 4 that ""The President, Vice President, and all civil Officers of the United States shall be removed from Office on Impeachment for, and conviction of, Treason, Bribery, or other High Crimes and Misdemeanors."" The House of Representatives has the sole power of impeaching, while the United States Senate has the sole power to try all impeachments. The removal of impeached officials is automatic upon conviction in the Senate. In Nixon v. United States (1993), the Supreme Court determined that the federal judiciary cannot review such proceedings.",who has the power to remove a president from office
when did bharat got its name as india,"['https://www.answers.com/Q/What_is_India', 'https://indianopedia.com/index', 'https://www.iamgreatindian.com/india-indian-indian-culture-traditional-values/', 'http://mind-tech.in/dmitsoftwarereportsdmittestdmitbusinessopportunitiesdmitfranchise/', 'http://www.tangoindia.in/about/', 'http://dilipkumar.in/india/', 'http://gloriousindia.in/india-an-overview/history-and-etymology/']","The name India is derived from Indus, which originates from the Old Persian word Hindu. The latter term stems from the Sanskrit word Sindhu, which was the historical local appellation for the Indus River. The ancient Greeks referred to the Indians as Indoi (Ἰνδοί), which translates as ""The people of the Indus"".",when did bharat got its name as india
what is the purpose of the trade union,"['http://chartsbin.com/view/42893', 'http://realseriousbusiness.com/start-plumbing-business-overland-park/', 'https://www.dallasapwu.org/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Business', 'http://www.newagebd.net/article/35789/worker-right-to-form-and-operate-trade-union', 'http://www.saveandread.com/blog/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Open-source_unionism']","A trade union or trades union, also called a labour union (Canada) or labor union (US), is an organization of workers who have come together to achieve common goals such as protecting the integrity of its trade, improving safety standards, achieving higher pay and benefits such as health care and retirement, increasing the number of employees an employer assigns to complete the work, and better working conditions. The trade union, through its leadership, bargains with the employer on behalf of union members (rank and file members) and negotiates labour contracts (collective bargaining) with employers. The most common purpose of these associations or unions is ""maintaining or improving the conditions of their employment"". This may include the negotiation of wages, work rules, complaint procedures, rules governing hiring, firing and promotion of workers, benefits, workplace safety and policies.",what is the purpose of the trade union
how to get cocoa butter from cocoa beans,"['https://drchockenstein.com/blogs/news/everything-you-need-to-know-about-eating-chocolate-on-the-paleo-diet', 'https://www.personalbeautywellness.com/products?url=raw-cocoa-butter-natural', 'https://shop.keynoteintl.com/product/cocoa-butter-unrefined-raw-700-g/', 'https://www.zliving.com/health/natural-remedies/natural-healing-tips-cocoa-butter-101-much-more-than-a-lubricant-2898/', 'http://freight.tips/cocoa-butter/', 'https://npknaturals.com/ingredient-information/', 'https://majesticpure.com/collections/body/products/cocoa-butter']","Cocoa butter is obtained from whole cocoa beans, which are fermented, roasted, and then separated from their hulls. About 54 -- 58% of the residue is cocoa butter. Chocolate liquor is pressed to separate the cocoa butter from the cocoa solids. The Broma process is used to extract cocoa butter from ground cocoa beans. Cocoa butter is sometimes deodorized to remove strong or undesirable tastes.",how to get cocoa butter from cocoa beans
list of harry potter rides at universal orlando,"['https://wizardingworldpark.com/harry-potter-park-video-tour-2/2012/08/19/', 'https://coasterglobe.com/2015/03/13/wizarding-world-of-harry-potter-now-spans-two-universal-parks/', 'http://closedb.com/place/529525720723724/Harry-Potter-And-The-Escape-From-Gringotts', 'https://myvirtualcontent.me/2015/12/31/the-wizarding-world-of-harry-potter/', 'http://scifiology.com/news/topics/places/', 'https://www.knowbeforeugo.com/blog/2014-universal-orlando-wizarding-world-of-harry-potters-diagon-alley/', 'http://www.bitlanders.com/blogs/wizarding-world-of-harry-potter/67771']","The first phase was officially announced for Islands of Adventure on May 31, 2007, and after a two-and-a-half-year construction period, the area officially opened to the public on June 18, 2010. The area's flagship attraction is Harry Potter and the Forbidden Journey, which exists within a re-creation of Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry. It takes riders on a journey through Harry Potter's wizarding world. Other attractions include Dragon Challenge, a now-closed pair of inverted roller coasters, and Flight of the Hippogriff, a family roller coaster. The area also features a re-creation of Hogsmeade containing many gift shops and restaurants from the novels including Dervish and Banges, Honeydukes, Ollivanders, Zonko's Joke Shop (though it houses Honeydukes), the Three Broomsticks, and the Hog's Head.",list of harry potter rides at universal orlando
what is the ninth amendment to the constitution,"['https://www.jpods.com/selfreliance', 'https://www.americasuncommonsense.com/category/science-engineeing-climate-change/page/2/', 'https://epn.xyz/2018/11/05/migration-is-a-human-right/', 'http://libertybob.com/index.php?category=politics&article=24', 'http://www.keepandbeararms.com/information/XcIBViewItem.asp?ID=3116', 'https://fanniefreddiesecrets.org/', 'https://www.wd-pl.com/civil-rights/']","The Ninth Amendment (Amendment IX) to the United States Constitution addresses rights, retained by the people, that are not specifically enumerated in the Constitution. It is part of the Bill of Rights.",what is the ninth amendment to the constitution
what does it mean when a cat has one blue eye and one green eye,"['https://savvypetcare.com/odd-eyed-cats/', 'https://www.thedodo.com/close-to-home/two-different-colored-eyes-dogs-cats', 'https://www.life-with-siamese-cats.com/facts-about-siamese-cats.html', 'https://www.different-cat-breeds.com/types-of-cats.html']","The odd-eyed coloring is caused when either the epistatic (dominant) white gene (which masks any other color genes and turns a cat completely white) or the white spotting gene (which is the gene responsible for bicolor and tuxedo cats) prevents melanin (pigment) granules from reaching one eye during development, resulting in a cat with one blue eye and one green, yellow, or brown eye. The condition only rarely occurs in cats that lack both the dominant white and the white spotting gene.",what does it mean when a cat has one blue eye and one green eye
the fundamental doctrine of the hindu faith is,"['https://hinducouncil.com.au/new/hinduism/hinduism-doctrine-and-beliefs/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Kohistani_people', 'https://www.navhindu.com/category/hinduism/page/2/', 'http://thenewbostonteaparty.com/tag/judaism/', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/hinduism', 'http://outoftheordinary101.blogspot.com/2016/06/top-6-religions-of-world.html', 'http://omin.me/maitri-upanishad-40/']","Prominent themes in Hindu beliefs include the four Puruṣārthas, the proper goals or aims of human life, namely Dharma (ethics / duties), Artha (prosperity / work), Kama (desires / passions) and Moksha (liberation / freedom / salvation); karma (action, intent and consequences), Saṃsāra (cycle of rebirth), and the various Yogas (paths or practices to attain moksha). Hindu practices include rituals such as puja (worship) and recitations, meditation, family-oriented rites of passage, annual festivals, and occasional pilgrimages. Some Hindus leave their social world and material possessions, then engage in lifelong Sannyasa (monastic practices) to achieve Moksha. Hinduism prescribes the eternal duties, such as honesty, refraining from injuring living beings (ahimsa), patience, forbearance, self-restraint, and compassion, among others. The four largest denominations of Hinduism are the Vaishnavism, Shaivism, Shaktism and Smartism.",the fundamental doctrine of the hindu faith is
what is earnings before interest taxes depreciation and amortization,"['https://en.unionpedia.org/3_(telecommunications)', 'https://informeanualintegrado2018.ferrovial.com/en/appendix/glossary-of-terms/', 'https://navms.com/mliml-bitcoin-and-stock-newspaper-2/', 'https://navms.com/1199-bitcoin-and-stock-newspaper/', 'https://navms.com/1738-bitcoin-official-archive/', 'https://aestheticsjournal.com/feature/using-share-schemes', 'https://www.simplysafedividends.com/intelligent-income/posts/32-top-10-financial-ratios-for-successful-dividend-investing']","A company's earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortization (commonly abbreviated EBITDA, pronounced / iː bɪtˈdɑː /, / əˈbɪtdɑː /, or / ˈɛbɪtdɑː /) is an accounting measure calculated using a company's net earnings, before interest expenses, taxes, depreciation, and amortization are subtracted, as a proxy for a company's current operating profitability (i.e., how much profit it makes with its present assets and its operations on the products it produces and sells, as well as providing a proxy for cash flow).",what is earnings before interest taxes depreciation and amortization
marriage that is considered invalid from the beginning,"['http://ayakbilegiprotezi.com/cat1/catholic-annulment-dating.html', 'https://www.thedivorcelawfirm.in/annulment-marriage/', 'https://www.bilodeaucapalbo.com/blog/category/divorce/', 'https://www.specof.com/2017/09/how-much-annulment-in-philippines.html', 'https://www.commonwealthtourism.com/five-important-jargons-and-concepts-you-must-know/', 'https://www.justia.com/family/divorce/docs/ending-a-marriage-faq/', 'http://reedlawva.com/manassas-family-law-attorney/annulments-attorney-prince-william-lawyer/']","Annulment is a legal procedure for declaring a marriage null and void. Unlike divorce, it is usually retroactive, meaning that an annulled marriage is considered to be invalid from the beginning almost as if it had never taken place (though some jurisdictions provide that the marriage is only void from the date of the annulment; for example, this is the case in section 12 of the Matrimonial Causes Act 1973 in England and Wales). In legal terminology, an annulment makes a void marriage or a voidable marriage null.",marriage that is considered invalid from the beginning
when did the high five became a thing,['https://acelebrationofwomen.org/2015/04/national-high-five-day-2015/'],"There are many origin stories of the high five, but the two most documented candidates are Dusty Baker and Glenn Burke of the Los Angeles Dodgers professional baseball team on October 2, 1977, and Wiley Brown and Derek Smith of the Louisville Cardinals men's college basketball team during the 1978 -- 1979 season.",when did the high five became a thing
what is the meaning of the book of lamentations,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Book_of_Lamentations.html', 'https://www.patheos.com/blogs/freelancechristianity/keeping-hope-alive/', 'http://mbhumanistsatheists.ca/part-eight-esther-and-job/', 'https://www.understandchristianity.com/bible/lamentations/', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/5', 'http://artsfuse.org/167392/concert-review-cantata-singers-music-that-bears-witness-to-catastrophe/', 'http://1amendmentcont.blogspot.com/2012/04/melito-of-sardis-roberts-donaldson.html']","The Book of Lamentations (Hebrew: אֵיכָה ‬,' Êykhôh, from its incipit meaning ""how"") is a collection of poetic laments for the destruction of Jerusalem. In the Hebrew Bible it appears in the Ketuvim (""Writings""), beside the Song of Songs, Book of Ruth, Ecclesiastes and the Book of Esther (the Megilloth or ""Five Scrolls""), although there is no set order; in the Christian Old Testament it follows the Book of Jeremiah, as the prophet Jeremiah is its traditional author. Jeremiah's authorship is no longer generally accepted, although it is generally accepted that the destruction of Jerusalem by Babylon in 586 BC forms the background to the poems. The book is partly a traditional ""city lament"" mourning the desertion of the city by God, its destruction, and the ultimate return of the divinity, and partly a funeral dirge in which the bereaved bewails and addresses the dead. The tone is bleak: God does not speak, the degree of suffering is presented as undeserved, and expectations of future redemption are minimal.",what is the meaning of the book of lamentations
what was the importance of the sinking of the lusitania,"['https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-worldhistory/chapter/the-end-of-world-war-i/', 'http://salopette.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=45976', 'http://www.henrysmilitarycollectables.com.au/products/medals-and-badges/ww1-sinking-of-the-rms-lusitania-medallion-and-box-british-issue.aspx', 'https://www.irishnewsarchive.com/wp/2016/02', 'https://www.nationalbookauctions.com/07082012/8july128.htm', 'http://phos-alethinon.blogspot.com/2012/05/sinking-of-lusitania.html', 'http://mfo.me.uk/browsemedia.php?mediatypeID=ships']","The sinking of the Cunard ocean liner RMS Lusitania occurred on Friday, 7 May 1915 during the First World War, as Germany waged submarine warfare against the United Kingdom which had implemented a naval blockade of Germany. The ship was identified and torpedoed by the German U-boat U-20 and sank in 18 minutes. The vessel went down 11 miles (18 km) off the Old Head of Kinsale, Ireland, killing 1,198 and leaving 761 survivors. The sinking turned public opinion in many countries against Germany, contributed to the American entry into World War I and became an iconic symbol in military recruiting campaigns of why the war was being fought.",what was the importance of the sinking of the lusitania
broken windows the police and neighborhood safety summary,"['https://jonbrouse.com/theories/', 'https://littlegreynotepad.com/2016/09/11/nairobi-and-the-broken-windows-theory/', 'https://www.cookfilms.co/blog/community-involvement-trash-jeffrey-cook-videography', 'http://www.brokenwindows.info/', 'https://wn.com/Got_broken_windows?upload_time=all_time&orderby=relevance', 'http://corneliussullivan.com/Moor%20Fountain.htm', 'http://www.pearltrees.com/u/9072700-transcranial-encyclopedia']","The broken windows theory is a criminological theory of the norm-setting and signaling effect of urban disorder and vandalism on additional crime and anti-social behavior. The theory states that maintaining and monitoring urban environments to prevent small crimes such as vandalism, public drinking, and turnstile-jumping helps to create an atmosphere of order and lawfulness, thereby preventing more serious crimes from happening.",broken windows the police and neighborhood safety summary
what is the historical significance of the french and indian war,"['https://media.timetoast.com/timelines/imperialism-97684597-9db4-4f65-aaa1-8865663f6268', 'https://majormike.us/2018/05/18/today-in-history-051818/', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-worldhistory/chapter/the-seven-years-war/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Royal_Marines', 'https://www.josephinecoins.com/p/1752-george-ii-shield-guinea', 'https://www.timetoast.com/timelines/the-british-in-india-65f5ff94-2087-412f-8d9e-1d6953e5724c', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Kingdom_of_Etruria']","The Seven Years' War was a global conflict fought between 1756 and 1763. It involved every European great power of the time and spanned five continents, affecting Europe, the Americas, West Africa, India, and the Philippines. The conflict split Europe into two coalitions, led by the Kingdom of Great Britain (including Prussia, Portugal, Hanover, and other small German states) on one side and the Kingdom of France (including the Austrian-led Holy Roman Empire, the Russian Empire, Bourbon Spain, and Sweden) on the other. Meanwhile, in India, the Mughal Empire, with the support of the French, tried to crush a British attempt to conquer Bengal.",what is the historical significance of the french and indian war
who is the president of china and how old is he,"['https://www.wikinow.co/topic/xi-jinping', 'https://www.thegeniusmedia.com.ng/2019/01/14/2018-forbes-here-are-the-6-most-powerful-world-leaders/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=4&ads=1&author=system&auto=Qingdao+post&standalone=1&domain_name=qingdaopost.com&title=Qingdao+post&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Qingdao+post', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Xi_Jinping', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/President_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China', 'https://m.wikiwordbook.info/x', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Xi_Jinping']","Xi Jinping (/ ʃiː /; Chinese: 习近平; pinyin: Xí Jìnpíng; born 15 June 1953) is a Chinese politician currently serving as General Secretary of the Communist Party of China, President of the People's Republic of China, and Chairman of the Central Military Commission. As Xi holds the top offices of the party, the state, and the military, he is sometimes referred to as China's ""paramount leader""; in 2016, the party officially gave him the title of ""core"" leader. As General Secretary, Xi holds an ex-officio seat on the Politburo Standing Committee of the Communist Party of China, China's top decision-making body.",who is the president of china and how old is he
list of battles in ultimate general civil war,"['http://civilwarsaga.com/women-soldiers-in-the-civil-war/', 'http://www.americacivilwar.org/faq', 'http://www.2theadvocate.net/louisiana_facts.php', 'http://www.thomaslegion.net/americancivilwar/arkansascivilwarhistory.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Arkansas_in_the_American_Civil_War', 'http://www.historyanimated.com/Atlanta.html', 'https://minerdescent.com/2010/07/08/simon-newcomb/']","The full edition includes well-known conflicts such as Battle of Aquia Creek, Battle of Philippi (West Virginia), 1st Battle of Bull Run, Battle of Shiloh, Battle of Gaines' Mill, Battle of Malvern Hill, 2nd Battle of Bull Run, Battle of Antietam, Battle of Fredericksburg, Battle of Stones River, Battle of Chancellorsville, Battle of Gettysburg, Battle of Chickamauga, Battle of Cold Harbor, and Battle of Richmond.",list of battles in ultimate general civil war
what do you mean by body mass index,"['http://www.swasthlife.com/healthcalc/BMI-CALCULATOR', 'http://www.laststrikefitness.com/what-is-bmi-2/', 'http://www.pattayamail.com/ourcommunity/surgery-may-answer-166028', 'https://www.myassignmenthelp.net/health-guidance', 'https://spineina.com/2019/01/17/the-connection-between-weight-and-back-pain/', 'https://apchemistry.info/news.php?action=show&id=19386', 'https://modapk.io/my-bmi-tracker-pro']","The BMI is an attempt to quantify the amount of tissue mass (muscle, fat, and bone) in an individual, and then categorize that person as underweight, normal weight, overweight, or obese based on that value. That categorization is the subject of some debate about where on the BMI scale the dividing lines between categories should be placed. Commonly accepted BMI ranges are underweight: under 18.5 kg / m, normal weight: 18.5 to 25, overweight: 25 to 30, obese: over 30. People of Asian descent have different associations between BMI, percentage of body fat, and health risks than those of European descent, with a higher risk of type 2 diabetes mellitus and atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease at BMIs lower than the WHO cut-off point for overweight, 25 kg / m, although the cutoff for observed risk varies among different Asian populations.",what do you mean by body mass index
what are the 6 continents of the world,"['https://syskool.com/seven-continents/', 'https://ifantasynamegenerator.com/fantasy-continent-name-generator/', 'https://www.bankersadda.com/p/frequently-asked-questions-of-static_359.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/List_of_transcontinental_countries', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Continent', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/why-isn-t-the-arctic-considered-to-be-a-continent.html', 'https://www.mapsofworld.com/continents/']","A continent is one of several very large landmasses of the world. Generally identified by convention rather than any strict criteria, up to seven regions are commonly regarded as continents. Ordered from largest in area to smallest, they are: Asia, Africa, North America, South America, Antarctica, Europe, and Australia.",what are the 6 continents of the world
where did the la lakers name come from,"['https://www.discoverlosangeles.com/event/2019/03/29/los-angeles-lakers-vscharlotte-hornets', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Cedric_Maxwell', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Los_Angeles_Lakers']","The Lakers' franchise began in 1947 when Ben Berger and Morris Chalfen of Minnesota purchased the recently disbanded Detroit Gems of the National Basketball League (NBL) for $15,000 from Gems owner Maury Winston. Minneapolis sportswriter Sid Hartman played a key behind the scenes role in helping put together the deal and later the team. Inspired by Minnesota's nickname, ""Land of 10,000 Lakes"", the team christened themselves the Lakers. Hartman helped them hire John Kundla from College of St. Thomas, to be their first head coach, by meeting with him and selling him on the team.",where did the la lakers name come from
define the location of india in the world,"['http://mind-tech.in/dmitsoftwarereportsdmittestdmitbusinessopportunitiesdmitfranchise/', 'http://mind-tech.in/midbrainactivation-midbrainactivationindia-midbrainmidbrainfranchiseindia-midbrainactivationprogramindia-midbrainactivationworkshopindia-midbrainactivationacademyindia/', 'https://www.nepaldream.com/en/destination/india', 'https://therevelationpaintingjournals.wordpress.com/tag/global/', 'http://vintagesilverplateflatware.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=27689', 'http://travellerpanda.com/the-hidden-charm-of-india/', 'https://www.spainexchange.com/schools/study-india/']","India (IAST: Bhārat), also called the Republic of India (IAST: Bhārat Gaṇarājya), is a country in South Asia. It is the seventh-largest country by area, the second-most populous country (with over 1.2 billion people), and the most populous democracy in the world. It is bounded by the Indian Ocean on the south, the Arabian Sea on the southwest, and the Bay of Bengal on the southeast. It shares land borders with Pakistan to the west; China, Nepal, and Bhutan to the northeast; and Bangladesh and Myanmar to the east. In the Indian Ocean, India is in the vicinity of Sri Lanka and the Maldives. India's Andaman and Nicobar Islands share a maritime border with Thailand and Indonesia.",define the location of india in the world
where is the worlds largest single block of tidal halophytic mangrove forest located,"['http://sundarbancruise.com/index.php', 'https://www.visit2himalaya.com/sundarban-information.php', 'https://comedymood.com/top-10-wildlife-sanctuaries-of-india/', 'http://blogsauthor.com/best-travel-spot/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171218015-forests', 'https://www.zeomac.com/top-10-best-places-to-visit-in-bangladesh/', 'http://bagerhat.gov.bd/site/top_banner/cef16c30-1c3a-11e7-8f57-286ed488c766']","The Sundarbans is a vast forest in the coastal region of the Bay of Bengal and considered one of the natural wonders of the world. Located in the delta region of Padma, Meghna and Brahmaputra river basins, this unique forest extends across Khulna, Satkhira, Bagerhat districts of Bangladesh and South 24 Parganas, North 24 Parganas districts of West Bengal, India. The Sundarbans contain the world's largest coastal mangrove forest, with an area of about 10,000 km (3,900 sq mi), of which about 6,000 km (2,300 sq mi) are located in Bangladesh and about 4,000 km (1,500 sq mi) in India. The Bangladeshi and Indian parts of the Sundarbans, while in fact adjacent parts of the uninterrupted landscape, have been listed separately in the UNESCO World Heritage List: as The Sundarbans and Sundarbans National Park, respectively. The Bangladeshi part encompasses three wildlife sanctuaries, viz Sundarbans West Wildlife Sanctuary, Sundarbans South Wildlife Sanctuary and Sundarbans East Wildlife Sanctuary, and is recognized as a Ramsar site named Sundarbans Reserved Forest.",where is the worlds largest single block of tidal halophytic mangrove forest located
when did the qin dynasty begin and end,"['https://efsantabarbaranews.com/category/culture/page/2/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Shang_Yang', 'http://fustaiferro.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=27938', 'https://2eyeswatching.wordpress.com/2012/02/08/shaanxi-provincial-museum-qin-galleryshaanxi-provincial-museum-qin-gallery/', 'https://www.worldcheckin.com/services/united-states/food-delivery-services/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Rizhao', 'http://www.his-xian.com/houses/']","The Qin dynasty (Chinese: 秦 朝; pinyin: Qín Cháo; Wade -- Giles: Ch'in Ch'ao) was the first dynasty of Imperial China, lasting from 221 to 206 BC. Named for its heartland in Qin state (modern Gansu and Shaanxi), the dynasty was founded by Qin Shi Huang, the First Emperor of Qin. The strength of the Qin state was greatly increased by the Legalist reforms of Shang Yang in the fourth century BC, during the Warring States period. In the mid and late third century BC, the Qin state carried out a series of swift conquests, first ending the powerless Zhou dynasty, and eventually conquering the other six of the Seven Warring States. Its 15 years was the shortest major dynasty in Chinese history, consisting of only two emperors, but inaugurated an imperial system that lasted, with interruption and adaptation, until 1912.",when did the qin dynasty begin and end
when did the february revolution start and end,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Russian_Revolution', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/February_Revolution', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/February_Revolution', 'https://imgur.com/gallery/Sg4UC', 'https://www.preceden.com/timelines/69761-1750-present-', 'http://footwww.academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/February_Revolution', 'https://en.historylapse.org/february-revolution']","The main events of the revolution took place in and near Petrograd (present-day St. Petersburg), the then-capital of Russia, where longstanding discontent with the monarchy erupted into mass protests against food rationing on 23 February Old Style (8 March New Style). Revolutionary activity lasted about eight days. It involved mass demonstrations and violent armed clashes with police and gendarmes, the last loyal forces of the Russian monarchy. On 27 February O.S. (12 March N.S.) mutinous Russian Army forces sided with the revolutionaries. Three days later the Tsar Nicholas II abdicated, ending Romanov dynastic rule, and the Imperial Russia. A Russian Provisional Government under Prince Georgy Lvov replaced the Russian Council of Ministers.",when did the february revolution start and end
actor who plays jon snow in game of thrones,"['https://www.clickthecity.com/movies/profile/14hHms/kit-harington', 'https://gossipgist.com/kit-harington', 'https://marriedwiki.com/wiki/kit-harington', 'https://short-biography.com/kit-harington.htm', 'http://new-networth.com/kit-harington-net-worth-game-thrones-profile-height/', 'https://www.movieranker.com/talent/2HfT21NacUsfWMe/Kit-Harington', 'http://beauty-around.com/en/tops/item/1559-most-handsome-serials-actors']","Since 2011, Harington has risen to prominence playing the role of Jon Snow in the HBO television series Game of Thrones, which garnered him a nomination for the 2016 Primetime Emmy Award. In 2017, Harington became one of the highest paid actors on television and earned £ 2 million per episode of Game of Thrones.",actor who plays jon snow in game of thrones
how many players can play in a nba game,"['http://sportsanity.com.sg/landing/basketball/index', 'https://www.disabled-world.com/sports/wheelchair/rugby.php', 'http://www.espn.com/espn/page2/story?page=shah/110523_SlamBall', 'https://www.toprankers.com/exams/afcat-answer-key/', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Wheelchair_rugby', 'https://theworldgames2021.com/sport/wheelchair-rugby/', 'http://www.jolietcatholicfootball.com/category/sports/basketball/page/2']","Five players from each team may be on the court at one time. Substitutions are unlimited but can only be done when play is stopped. Teams also have a coach, who oversees the development and strategies of the team, and other team personnel such as assistant coaches, managers, statisticians, doctors and trainers.",how many players can play in a nba game
where do north korea and south korea meet,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Korean_Demilitarized_Zone', 'http://suitma10.org/hotel/tour/post', 'https://www.leesvilledailyleader.com/news/20190414/veteran-snapshot-tim-white', 'http://www.sub-stances.com/all-articles/and-the-stalemate-continues-gabriella-gricius', 'http://ccmr2019.org/venue/dmz-demilitarized-zone/', 'https://www.outofyourcomfortzone.net/en/the-cheapest-way-to-visit-the-dmz-demilitarized-zone-and-the-jsa-joint-security-area-in-south-korea/', 'https://interestingengineering.com/15-of-the-greatest-wall-constructs-ever-built-from-antiquity-to-today']","The Korean Demilitarized Zone (DMZ; Hangul: 한반도 비무장 지대; Hanja: 韓 半島 非 武裝 地帶), informally known as the 38th Parallel, is a strip of land running across the Korean Peninsula. It is established by the provisions of the Korean Armistice Agreement to serve as a buffer zone between the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (North Korea) and the Republic of Korea (South Korea). The Demilitarized zone (DMZ) is a border barrier that divides the Korean Peninsula roughly in half. It was created by agreement between North Korea, China and the United Nations in 1953. The DMZ is 250 kilometres (160 miles) long, and about 4 kilometres (2.5 miles) wide.",where do north korea and south korea meet
who wrote uncle tom's cabin and why was it important,"['http://kristinpalitza.com/11028.html', 'https://rjmautographsandantiques.com/products/rhode-island-woman-photographer-creates-cdv-of-uncle-toms-cabin-characters-tom-and-little-eva', 'http://www.appalbum.com/review/books-that-changed-the-world/', 'http://raymondsaumure.com/simulation/uncle-toms-cabin-audiobook.php', 'http://growshopeurotop.eu/72359-essay-marcos-is-not-a-hero.html', 'https://blackfacts.com/fact/uncle-toms-cabin-0', 'https://www.downloadcollection.com/freeware/american-civil-war-timeline.htm']","Uncle Tom's Cabin; or, Life Among the Lowly, is an anti-slavery novel by American author Harriet Beecher Stowe. Published in 1852, the novel had a profound effect on attitudes toward African Americans and slavery in the U.S. and is said to have ""helped lay the groundwork for the Civil War"".",who wrote uncle tom's cabin and why was it important
what's the difference between a specialist and a generalist,"['http://www.dtsato.com/blog/tag/xp/', 'https://digitalplumbing.co/', 'https://architects2zebras.com/2010/07/04/are-you-a-koala-or-raccoon/', 'http://www.biochemj.org/content/474/5/611.full', 'https://bethanywatkinsblog.wordpress.com/tag/photography/']","A generalist species is able to thrive in a wide variety of environmental conditions and can make use of a variety of different resources (for example, a heterotroph with a varied diet). A specialist species can thrive only in a narrow range of environmental conditions or has a limited diet. Most organisms do not all fit neatly into either group, however. Some species are highly specialized (the most extreme case being monophagy), others less so, and some can tolerate many different environments. In other words, there is a continuum from highly-specialized to broadly-generalist species.",what's the difference between a specialist and a generalist
title ix of the education amendments of 1972 definition,"['https://www.nl.edu/studentrightsandinformation/anti-discriminationpolicy/', 'https://thefederalregister.org/82-FR/Issue-195', 'http://dcps.k12.md.us/title-ix-compliance-notice']","No person in the United States shall, on the basis of sex, be excluded from participation in, be denied the benefits of, or be subjected to discrimination under any education program or activity receiving Federal financial assistance.",title ix of the education amendments of 1972 definition
when does cedar point close for the year,"['https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=2&ads=1&author=system&auto=Ohio+cabaret&standalone=1&domain_name=ohiocabaret.com&title=Ohio+cabaret&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Ohio+cabaret', 'http://countrylicious.com/united-states/tourist-attractions', 'http://www.camvista.com/webdir/Google-Street-View-Maps/1000184,6,50.html', 'https://www.magx.com/tag/usa', 'http://mysonslist.com/cedar-point-ohio-amusement-park', 'https://vacationidea.com/ohio/best-amusement-parks-in-ohio.html', 'https://www.skyscanner.co.nz/flights-to/ohio_/cheap-flights-to-ohio.html']","Cedar Point's normal operating season runs from early May until Labor Day in September. The park then reopens only on weekends until the end of October or early November for a Halloween-themed event known as HalloWeekends. Other attractions near the park include a one-mile-long (1.6 km) white-sand beach, an outdoor water park called Cedar Point Shores, an indoor water park called Castaway Bay, two marinas, an outdoor sports complex called Cedar Point Sports Center, and several nearby resorts.",when does cedar point close for the year
during which naval battle did the allies severely crippled japan’s navy,"['http://ltt.ink/video/id/nJncgftlXcc', 'https://navy.togetherweserved.com/usn/servlet/tws.webapp.WebApp?cmd=ShadowBoxProfile&type=BattleMemoryExt&ID=155965', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/1942/5/4/battle-of-the-coral-sea', 'https://www.sas1946.com/main/index.php/topic,60237.msg664251.html', 'https://stevecochrane823.com/2015/09/19/for-your-tomorrows-we-gave-our-todays/', 'https://www.worldreligionnews.com/issues/australian-evangelists-are-praying-for-americas-future']","Although a tactical victory for the Japanese in terms of ships sunk, the battle would prove to be a strategic victory for the Allies for several reasons. The battle marked the first time since the start of the war that a major Japanese advance had been checked by the Allies. More importantly, the Japanese fleet carriers Shōkaku and Zuikaku -- the former damaged and the latter with a depleted aircraft complement -- were unable to participate in the Battle of Midway the following month, while Yorktown did participate, ensuring a rough parity in aircraft between the two adversaries and contributing significantly to the U.S. victory in that battle. The severe losses in carriers at Midway prevented the Japanese from reattempting to invade Port Moresby from the ocean and helped prompt their ill-fated land offensive over the Kokoda trail. Two months later, the Allies took advantage of Japan's resulting strategic vulnerability in the South Pacific and launched the Guadalcanal Campaign; this, along with the New Guinea Campaign, eventually broke Japanese defenses in the South Pacific and was a significant contributing factor to Japan's ultimate surrender in World War II.",during which naval battle did the allies severely crippled japan’s navy
what to do when school bus lights flash,"['https://drivinglaws.aaa.com/tag/school-buses/', 'https://www.trackschoolbus.com/blog/school-bus-traffic-stop-laws/', 'https://www.edriving.com/three60/country-united-states/', 'https://www2.gnb.ca/content/gnb/en/gateways/about_nb/transportation.html', 'https://drivinglaws.aaa.com/category/us-motor-laws/colorado/', 'https://drivinglaws.aaa.com/category/us-motor-laws/delaware/', 'http://www.grllaw.com/blog/grl-law/school-bus-safety-and-kadyns-law.aspx']","Generally, if a stopped school bus is displaying a flashing, alternating red lamp, a driver of a vehicle meeting or overtaking the stopped bus from either direction (front or back) must stop and wait until the bus moves again or the red light is off. Police officers, school crossing guards, and even school bus drivers themselves may have the power to wave traffic on, even when a red light is flashing.",what to do when school bus lights flash
what is the myers briggs test used for,"['https://www.repeatable.co.nz/blog/post/19102/Do-You-Need-A-Personal-Brand/', 'https://policehour.co.uk/article-feed/', 'http://www.z-edge.in/mbti/', 'http://www.dfcoaching.com/personality-profiling/myers-briggs-type-indicator-mbti/', 'https://www.deniselevybsw.com/personality-assessments.html', 'https://www.crosstimbersgazette.com/2019/02/10/duo-helps-women-find-their-strengths/', 'https://www.gotoevents.co.uk/myers-briggs/']",The Myers -- Briggs Type Indicator (MBTI) is an introspective self-report questionnaire with the purpose of indicating differing psychological preferences in how people perceive the world around them and make decisions.,what is the myers briggs test used for
what is the mechanism of action of anticholinergic drugs,"['https://health.10ztalk.com/2019/02/11/anticholinergic-drugs-rogue-pharmacology-medium/', 'https://ussromantics.com/2014/12/24/bronchiectasis-updated/', 'https://realwellnessdoc.com/tag/depression/', 'https://www.drugbank.ca/drugs/DB01625', 'https://drjockers.com/dementia-natural-treatment/', 'https://www.amboss.com/us/knowledge/Muscarinic_antagonists', 'https://healthandlovepage.com/prevent-alzheimers-disease/?utm_source=TheHealthGuide&utm_medium=FacebookPage&utm_campaign=TheHealthGuide']","An anticholinergic agent is a substance that blocks the neurotransmitter acetylcholine in the central and the peripheral nervous system. These agents inhibit parasympathetic nerve impulses by selectively blocking the binding of the neurotransmitter acetylcholine to its receptor in nerve cells. The nerve fibers of the parasympathetic system are responsible for the involuntary movement of smooth muscles present in the gastrointestinal tract, urinary tract, lungs, and many other parts of the body. Anticholinergics are divided into three categories in accordance with their specific targets in the central and peripheral nervous system: antimuscarinic agents, ganglionic blockers, and neuromuscular blockers.",what is the mechanism of action of anticholinergic drugs
the snow-eater wind of the rocky mountains is also called the,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Chinook_wind', 'https://tossoffbowlines.com/2016/01/26/chinook-calgarys-heat-wave/', 'https://www.best-banff-vacations.com/Banff-Weather.html']","Chinook is claimed by popular folk-etymology to mean' ice-eater', however it is the name of the people in the region where the usage was first derived. The reference to a wind or weather system, simply' a Chinook', originally meant a warming wind from the ocean into the interior regions of the Pacific Northwest of the USA (the Chinook people lived near the ocean, along the lower Columbia River).",the snow-eater wind of the rocky mountains is also called the
what is the theme of the man who walked between the towers,"['https://www.readgeek.com/author/Norton_Juster_(The_Phantom_Tollbooth)', 'http://booksbyrotten.blogspot.com/', 'http://www.oakridgeschool.org.uk/news/123/68/Class-2-Topic-Update.php']","The Man Who Walked Between the Towers is a children's picture book written and illustrated by American Mordicai Gerstein. Published in 2003, the book recounts the heart-stopping achievement of Philippe Petit, a French man who, on an August morning in 1974, walked, lay, knelt and danced on a tightrope wire between the roofs of the twin towers of the World Trade Center, a quarter mile above the ground. Gerstein won the 2004 Caldecott Medal for his illustrations. The book has been adapted to film and ballet.",what is the theme of the man who walked between the towers
what age was queen elizabeth when she became queen,"['https://baron-magazine.com/2018/09/11/queen-elizabeth-ii/', 'https://www.debretts.com/the-royal-family/the-queen/', 'http://shondacolleenkelleyformayor2012.info/coronation-street-gifts-canada.html', 'https://unitedchurchferndown.org.uk/sermons/discarded-cornerstone-chosen-people?player=audio', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2014/04/21/', 'https://poshchicago.com/products/vintage-queen-elizabeth-ii-coronationtea-cup-and-saucer', 'https://bigslide.ru/angliyskiy-yazik/5119-britis-monarc-ueen-elizabet-ii.html']","During 1951, George VI's health declined, and Elizabeth frequently stood in for him at public events. When she toured Canada and visited President Harry S. Truman in Washington, D.C., in October 1951, her private secretary, Martin Charteris, carried a draft accession declaration in case the King died while she was on tour. In early 1952, Elizabeth and Philip set out for a tour of Australia and New Zealand by way of Kenya. On 6 February 1952, they had just returned to their Kenyan home, Sagana Lodge, after a night spent at Treetops Hotel, when word arrived of the death of the King and consequently Elizabeth's immediate accession to the throne. Philip broke the news to the new queen. Martin Charteris asked her to choose a regnal name; she chose to remain Elizabeth, ""of course"". She was proclaimed queen throughout her realms and the royal party hastily returned to the United Kingdom. She and the Duke of Edinburgh moved into Buckingham Palace.",what age was queen elizabeth when she became queen
where is the rocky statue located in philadelphia,"['https://www.shortlist.com/entertainment/films/15-things-you-probably-didnt-know-about-rocky-iii/88535', 'http://www.retetour.com/PhiladelphiaMuseum/philadelphia-museum-of-art-rocky', 'http://seattlebloggers.com/running-rocky-steps-philadelphia/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Russ_Saunders']","Before Rocky III, released in 1982, Stallone commissioned A. Thomas Schomberg to create a bronze statue of Rocky. Three 2-ton, 10-foot-tall copies were cast. One was installed atop the steps for the filming of Rocky III, and was ultimately relocated at the bottom of the steps. The second Rocky is in the San Diego Hall of Champions Sports Museum in San Diego, California. The third was planned, but was not cast.",where is the rocky statue located in philadelphia
when were the knights of the templar founded,"['https://tube-sosok.info/under-armour-army-black-knights-white-playoff-stripe-performance-polo.asp', 'http://oicho.info/?newsid=27570', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/Knights_Templar', 'http://gentrekker.com/browsemedia.php?mediatypeID=histories', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Tomb_effigy', 'http://agaunews.com/portfolio-items/2016-2017-warriors-history-new-zealand-mint/?portfolioCats=357%2C201%2C110%2C131%2C114%2C198%2C109%2C150%2C133%2C229%2C262%2C284%2C219%2C132%2C251%2C286%2C311%2C227%2C287', 'http://adoptadognortheast.co.uk/20878671-knights-of-the-wizard/']","The Poor Fellow-Soldiers of Christ and of the Temple of Solomon (Latin: Pauperes commilitones Christi Templique Salomonici), also known as the Order of Solomon's Temple, the Knights Templar or simply as Templars, were a Catholic military order recognised in 1139 by papal bull Omne Datum Optimum of the Holy See. The order was founded in 1119 and active from about 1129 to 1312.",when were the knights of the templar founded
why is the pizza hut logo a hat,"['http://design-webaby.ru/56327-mexico-chiquito-coupons.html', 'http://problog.info/17343-imos-coupons-printable.html', 'http://carinsurancequoteras.info/85584-cupon-papa-johns-chile.html', 'http://everythingworld.eu/79688-kfc-nl-coupons/', 'http://industrium.biz/87121-pizza-hut-delivery-coupon-code.html', 'http://6o3ibk4qcvi.ru/14731-pizza-hut-meal-coupons.html', 'http://micramacra.ru/98556-pizza-hut-coupons-usa/']","Pizza Hut sponsored the film Back to the Future Part II (1989) and offered a free pair of futuristic sunglasses, known as ""Solar Shades"", with the purchase of Pizza Hut pizza. Pizza Hut also engaged in product placement within the film, having a futuristic version of their logo with their trademarked red hut printed on the side of a mylar dehydrated pizza wrapper in the McFly family dinner scene, and appear on a storefront in Hill Valley in the year 2015.",why is the pizza hut logo a hat
where is the oldest oceanic crust under the atlantic ocean likely to be found,"['https://www.hindawi.com/journals/ahep/2013/425693/', 'https://www.i4u.com/2016/08/114376/scientists-find-world-s-oldest-oceanic-crust-mediterranean-sea']","The oldest large scale oceanic crust is in the west Pacific and north-west Atlantic-both are about up to 180-200 million years old. However, parts of the eastern Mediterranean Sea are remnants of the much older Tethys ocean, at about 270 and up to 340 million years old.",where is the oldest oceanic crust under the atlantic ocean likely to be found
what type of government system does pakistan have,"['https://wikimili.com/en/President_of_Pakistan', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/Zubaida_Jalal_Khan', 'https://paperpk.com/government-jobs.php', 'http://forum.pakdiscussion.com/showthread.php/174511-Chief-Internal-Auditor-National-Fertilizer-Corporation-of-Pakistan-Lahore?s=7794e40bdab29c633a0ecec6aa7d4ee1', 'https://www.allbestessays.com/essay/Subcontinental-Politics-with-Supporting-Evidence/70272.html', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/what-type-of-government-does-pakistan-have.html', 'https://energypedia.info/wiki/Pakistan_Energy_Situation']","The Government of Pakistan (Urdu: حکومتِ پاکستان ‬ ‎) is a federal government established by the Constitution of Pakistan as a constituted governing authority of the four provinces of a proclaimed and established parliamentary democratic republic, constitutionally called the Islamic Republic of Pakistan.",what type of government system does pakistan have
what can you use a soldering iron for,"['http://www.noelindia.com/blog/2016/02/26/where-can-you-obtain-the-best-soldering-iron-in-delhi/', 'https://www.myemssolutions.com/buying-guide-soldering-tools/', 'https://fanyit.com/review/best-soldering-irons-for-you/', 'http://guide150.com/best-soldering-iron', 'https://www.idealresources.in/cunsumable.html', 'https://www.babaheatingedge.com/heating-element-soldering-irons.html', 'http://m.pbss.in/mobile-phone-repairing-tools.html']","Soldering irons are most often used for installation, repairs, and limited production work in electronics assembly. High-volume production lines use other soldering methods. Large irons may be used for soldering joints in sheet metal objects. Less common uses include pyrography (burning designs into wood) and plastic welding.",what can you use a soldering iron for
what is the average size of a rainbow trout,"['https://newwavetaxidermy.com/fish-mounts/rainbow-trout-mounts/', 'https://myfishingplace.com.au/fish/trout-rainbow', 'http://redshadegames.us/doku.php?id=rainbow_trout', 'http://www.howtocatchfishnetwork.com/freshwater-fishing-tips/rainbow-trout/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/List_of_Utah_state_symbols', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Rainbow_trout', 'http://www.thetaxidermystore.com/rainbow-trout-taxidermy-freshwater-fish-mount-for-sale-20136.html']","Adult freshwater stream rainbow trout average between 1 and 5 lb (0.5 and 2.3 kg), while lake-dwelling and anadromous forms may reach 20 lb (9 kg). Coloration varies widely based on subspecies, forms and habitat. Adult fish are distinguished by a broad reddish stripe along the lateral line, from gills to the tail, which is most vivid in breeding males.",what is the average size of a rainbow trout
how many goals has messi scored for club and country,"['https://www.wikinow.co/topic/lionel-messi', 'https://www.parkhighstanmore.org.uk/page/?title=Messi+or+Ronaldo&pid=366', 'http://www.kaosbolaonline.com/2011/11/fcbarcelona20112012.html', 'http://uprutuadobib.info/author/UCV6n8RTZk_dRXaWSWkjhtNQ/Mnf+News', 'https://allstarpics.famousfix.com/pictures/lionel-messi', 'http://rock-cafe.info/posts/lionel-messi-quotes-about-soccer-6c696f6e656c.html', 'https://m.onenewspage.co.uk/current/mcgjq60/Lionel-Messi.htm']","Lionel Andrés ""Leo"" Messi (Spanish pronunciation: (ljoˈnel anˈðɾeθ ˈmesi) (listen); born 24 June 1987) is an Argentine professional footballer who plays as a forward for Spanish club Barcelona and the Argentina national team. Often considered the best player in the world and regarded by many as the greatest of all time, Messi is the only player in history to win five FIFA Ballon d'Or awards, four of which he won consecutively, and a record-tying four European Golden Shoes. He has won 29 trophies with Barcelona, including eight La Liga titles, four UEFA Champions League titles, and five Copas del Rey. Both a prolific goalscorer and a creative playmaker, Messi holds the records for most official goals scored in La Liga (360), a La Liga season (50) and a club football season in Europe (73), a calendar year (91), as well as those for most assists made in La Liga (139) and the Copa América (11). He has scored over 600 senior career goals for club and country.",how many goals has messi scored for club and country
where did the phrase ignorance is bliss come from,['https://dhalk.wordpress.com/tag/darrell-halk/'],"""Ignorance is bliss"" is a phrase coined by Thomas Gray in his Ode on a Distant Prospect of Eton College.",where did the phrase ignorance is bliss come from
a legislative ombudsman is an independent agency that assists in,"['http://www.thepatriot.co.bw/news/item/216-who-can-save-khama-from-himself.html', 'https://bentcops.org/what-does-the-word-ombudsman-actually-mean/', 'https://www.kaieteurnewsonline.com/2016/10/31/afc-expects-new-ombudsman-by-january-2017/', 'http://www.new-home-blog.co.uk/category/new-homes/new-home-problems/', 'https://www.insightsonindia.com/2019/01/23/rajya-sabha-tv-the-big-picture-lokpal-lokayukts/', 'https://www.thestar.com.my/metro/views/2015/05/05/ensuring-our-access-rights-sustainable-development-in-pj-can-happen-only-with-more-transparent-proce/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1994_amendment_of_the_Constitution_of_Argentina']","An ombudsman, ombud, or public advocate is an official who is charged with representing the interests of the public by investigating and addressing complaints of maladministration or a violation of rights. The ombudsman is usually appointed by the government or by parliament, but with a significant degree of independence. In some countries an inspector general, citizen advocate or other official may have duties similar to those of a national ombudsman, and may also be appointed by a legislature. Below the national level an ombudsman may be appointed by a state, local or municipal government. Unofficial ombudsmen may be appointed by, or even work for, a corporation such as a utility supplier, newspaper, NGO, or professional regulatory body.",a legislative ombudsman is an independent agency that assists in
what is the central disagreement in we are seven,"['https://cunninghamsway.com/2012/10/19/we-are-seven/', 'http://cityraven.com/we-are-seven-poem.html', 'https://www.venice-hotel-danieli.com/the-poem-michael-by-william-wordsworth/', 'https://www.matthewandlarissa.com/william-wordsworth-the-idiot-boy/', 'https://kprudchenko.wordpress.com/category/romantic-poetry/', 'https://www.pdf-2-flashbook.com/books/506141961/lyrical-ballads-with-other-poems-1800-volume-2.pdf', 'https://www.litpriest.com/browse/poetry/the-tables-turned-analysis/']","""We are Seven"" is a poem written by William Wordsworth and published in his Lyrical Ballads. It describes a discussion between an adult poetic speaker and a ""little cottage girl"" about the number of brothers and sisters who dwell with her. The poem turns on the question of whether to account two dead siblings as part of the family.",what is the central disagreement in we are seven
when did the pirates of the caribbean ride open at disney world,"['https://www.thepurplepumpkinblog.co.uk/walt-disney-world-photo-alphabet-n-z/', 'http://guscade.blogspot.com/2013/09/stern-pinball-disneys-pirates-of.html', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=special-pirates.com&ads=1&title=Special+pirates&auto=Special+pirates&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Special+pirates&pagenum=5', 'http://by-portal.tk/croupier-poker-evenementiel.html', 'https://www.frugalfocus.com/disneyland/', 'https://www.dapsmagic.com/2017/02/pirates-caribbean-battle-sunken-treasure-shanghai-disneyland-receives-visual-effects-society-award/', 'http://www.blackpearlminute.com/the-disneyland-ride/']","Pirates of the Caribbean is a dark ride attraction at Disneyland, the Magic Kingdom, Tokyo Disneyland, and Disneyland Park in Paris. The original version at Disneyland, which opened in 1967, was the last attraction whose construction was overseen by Walt Disney; he died three months before it opened. The ride, which tells the story of a band of pirates and their troubles and exploits, was replicated at the Magic Kingdom in 1973, at Tokyo Disneyland in 1983, and at Disneyland Paris in 1992. Each of the initial four versions of the ride has a different façade but a similar ride experience. A reimagined version of the ride, Pirates of the Caribbean: Battle for the Sunken Treasure, opened at the Shanghai Disneyland Park in 2016.",when did the pirates of the caribbean ride open at disney world
who wrote walk me out in the morning dew,['https://fleurmach.com/2016/03/27/the-national-morning-dew/'],"""Morning Dew"", also known as ""(Walk Me Out in the) Morning Dew"", is a post-apocalyptic folk rock song written by Canadian folk singer Bonnie Dobson and made famous by the Grateful Dead.",who wrote walk me out in the morning dew
when was the phantom of the opera play written,"['https://master.dev.camdram.net/shows/2018-the-phantom-of-the-opera', 'http://discountedtickets.blogspot.com/2013_05_19_archive.html', 'http://www.happyvideonetwork.com/the-phantom-of-the-opera-theme-song/', 'http://theatregold1.mybigcommerce.com/phantom-of-the-opera-16/', 'http://www.secseats.com/phantom-of-the-opera-tickets.aspx', 'http://www.euro-ticket.com/tickets/musicals/zakaz_biletov_phantom_of_the_opera_tickets/', 'http://www.nycmanhattan.org/2011/01/phantom-of-opera-broadway.html']","The musical opened in London's West End in 1986, and on Broadway in 1988. It won the 1986 Olivier Award and the 1988 Tony Award for Best Musical, and Michael Crawford (in the title role) won the Olivier and Tony Awards for Best Actor in a Musical. It is the longest running show in Broadway history by a wide margin, and celebrated its 10,000 th Broadway performance on 11 February 2012, the first production ever to do so. It is the second longest-running West End musical, after Les Misérables, and the third longest-running West End show overall, after The Mousetrap.",when was the phantom of the opera play written
where does the name las vegas come from,"['http://ecgame.tk/calculator-poker-download.html', 'https://hotspotcitynet.com/casino-equipment-rental-santa-clarita-casino-kings-parties-corporate-events/', 'http://drumcullengaa.tk/gummies26-poker.html', 'http://geofun.tk/juego-de-poker-informacion.html', 'https://www.restorekewaunee.com/las-vegas-hotels-m/', 'https://www.torta-a-porta.com/new-hotels-reflect-rising-tourism-in-county/', 'http://footballforum.tk/spin-palace-casino-phone-number.html']","The name Las Vegas was given to the area in 1821 by Rafael Rivera, a member of the Antonio Armijo trading party that was traveling to Los Angeles, and stopped for water there on the Old Spanish Trail from New Mexico. At that time, several parts of the valley contained artesian wells surrounded by extensive green areas; Las Vegas means the meadows in Spanish. The flows from the wells fed the Las Vegas Wash, which runs to the Colorado River.",where does the name las vegas come from
where is azerbaijan located on the world map,"['http://danir19.com/', 'https://halberdbastion.com/intelligence/countries-nations/azerbaijan', 'http://asfa.net/country/193-azerbaijan.html', 'http://zoos.mono.net/11331/Azerbaijan', 'http://www.leader.co.hu/azerbaijan/', 'http://baptistfriends.org/country/azerbaijan/baku/', 'https://www.whatpassport.com/countries/Azerbaijan']","Azerbaijan (/ ˌæzərbaɪˈdʒɑːn / AZ-ər-by-JAHN; Azerbaijani: Azərbaycan (ɑːzæɾbɑjˈd͡ʒɑn)), officially the Republic of Azerbaijan (Azerbaijani: Azərbaycan Respublikası (ɑːzæɾbɑjˈd͡ʒɑn ɾespublikɑˈsɯ)), is a country in the South Caucasus region of Eurasia at the crossroads of Eastern Europe and Western Asia. It is bounded by the Caspian Sea to the east, Russia to the north, Georgia to the northwest, Armenia to the west and Iran to the south. The exclave of Nakhchivan is bound by Armenia to the north and east, Iran to the south and west, and has an 11 km long border with Turkey in the north west.",where is azerbaijan located on the world map
what breeds are in a black russian terrier,"['http://www.dogzone.com/breeds/russian-black-terrier/', 'https://www.dog-harnesses-store.co.uk/black-russian-terrier-c-77/', 'https://masterclip.co.uk/product-range/productcategory/black-russian-terrier/group/a5-german-steel-blades', 'https://brtagent007.com/html/gl-en.htm', 'http://www.bigrussiansoul.org/black-russian-terrier/', 'https://www.betterbred.com/breedpage/?link=5', 'https://www.greensboroughvets.com.au/stories/29-client-stories/161-archie-o-neill.html']","Despite its name, the Black Russian Terrier is not a true terrier: it is believed that about seventeen breeds were used in its development, including the Airedale, the Giant Schnauzer, the Rottweiler, the Newfoundland, the Caucasian Shepherd Dog and other breeds.",what breeds are in a black russian terrier
when did feudalism start and end in europe,"['https://www.engagewithease.com/journal-32---ldquofeudalism-in-europerdquo.html', 'http://pqefqkc.webz.cz/269-medieval-social-structure-essay.php', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Feudalism', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/6686', 'https://houstonthermalinspections.com/notes-on-civil-and-common-legal-system/', 'http://worldbuildfan.tripod.com/id25.html', 'http://www.artandpopularculture.com/Feudalism']","Feudalism was a combination of legal and military customs in medieval Europe that flourished between the 9th and 15th centuries. Broadly defined, it was a way of structuring society around relationships derived from the holding of land in exchange for service or labour. Although derived from the Latin word feodum or feudum (fief), then in use, the term feudalism and the system it describes were not conceived of as a formal political system by the people living in the Middle Ages. In its classic definition, by François-Louis Ganshof (1944), feudalism describes a set of reciprocal legal and military obligations among the warrior nobility revolving around the three key concepts of lords, vassals and fiefs.",when did feudalism start and end in europe
where did the peace sign with two fingers come from,"['https://www.whaleoil.co.nz/2015/02/photo-day-536/', 'https://fsymbols.com/signs/peace/', 'https://therongolianstar.com/2012/09/22/signs-of-peace-all-over-the-world/']","Protesters against the Vietnam War (and subsequent anti-war protests) and counterculture activists adopted the gesture as a sign of peace. Because the hippies of the day often flashed this sign (palm out) while saying ""Peace"", it became popularly known (through association) as the peace sign.",where did the peace sign with two fingers come from
when does the pineal gland develop in a fetus,"['https://psychology.wikia.org/wiki/Pineal_body', 'http://londonosteopathiccare.com/blog/4586855944/How-to-look-after-your-Pineal-gland/10586865', 'http://andygreek1.forumchitchat.com/post/psychic-development-6731449?trail=', 'https://bodytomy.com/pineal-gland-function', 'https://hubpages.com/education/Every-Organ-Tells-a-Story-6-A-History-of-Anatomical-Terms', 'http://s3.amazonaws.com/right4cash/control-your-subconscious-mind-quiz.html']","The human pineal gland grows in size until about 1 -- 2 years of age, remaining stable thereafter, although its weight increases gradually from puberty onwards. The abundant melatonin levels in children are believed to inhibit sexual development, and pineal tumors have been linked with precocious puberty. When puberty arrives, melatonin production is reduced.",when does the pineal gland develop in a fetus
how does a hair dryer dry your hair,"['http://www.wackyowl.com/tag/hair/', 'https://www.galaxus.ch/en/s6/product/remington-advanced-colour-protect-ac8605-hairdryers-9868619', 'https://www.uptobrain.com/coolest-gadgets-launched-at-ces-in-2019/', 'http://besthairstraightener.in/13-best-hair-dryer-online-in-india-2019/', 'https://www.storeone.pk/womens/mozerhairdrayer', 'https://www.nikeflyknitid.cc/deals-black-friday-uk-cloud-mining-hashflare-march.html', 'http://preorderblackinfrared6s.org/category/general-article/page/3']","A hair dryer, hairdryer or blow dryer is an electromechanical device designed to blow normal or hot air over damp hair to accelerate the evaporation of water particles and dry the hair. Blow dryers allow better control over the shape and style of hair, by accelerating and controlling the formation of temporary hydrogen bonds inside each strand. These hydrogen bonds are powerful (allowing for stronger hair shaping than the sulfur bonds formed by permanent waving products) but are temporary and extremely vulnerable to humidity. They disappear with a single washing of the hair.",how does a hair dryer dry your hair
who is the current prime minister of brazil,['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Empire_of_Brazil'],The political position of Prime Minister of Brazil existed in two different parliamentary periods in the country's history: from 1847 to 1889 (during most of the Empire) and from 1961 to 1963 (during the last years of the Second Republic).,who is the current prime minister of brazil
when will the world's population reach 10 billion,"['https://curionic.com/blog/2018/1/11/the-rate-of-world-population-growth-is-now-decreasing', 'http://www.thebullsheet.com/show-prep/july/july-11-2017', 'http://www.dancingwithsource.com/archives/news_55_0310.php', 'https://www.foreignaffairs.com/articles/2012-08-30/growth-interrupted', 'https://schibsted.com/2018/06/28/reduce-reuse-rethink/', 'https://www.friendsjournal.org/forum-june-july-2018/', 'https://channels.theinnovationenterprise.com/articles/5-areas-ai-will-make-a-difference-in-2017']","According to current projections, the global population will reach eight billion by 2024, and will likely reach around nine billion by 2042. Alternative scenarios for 2050 range from a low of 7.4 billion to a high of more than 10.6 billion. Projected figures vary depending on underlying statistical assumptions and the variables used in projection calculations, especially the fertility variable. Long-range predictions to 2150 range from a population decline to 3.2 billion in the ""low scenario"", to ""high scenarios"" of 24.8 billion. One extreme scenario predicted a massive increase to 256 billion by 2150, assuming the global fertility rate remained at its 1995 level of 3.04 children per woman; however, by 2010 the global fertility rate had declined to 2.52.",when will the world's population reach 10 billion
when did sunderland last win the fa cup,"['https://wikimili.com/en/David_Healy_(footballer)', 'https://the-premier-league.com/club/sunderland/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Nicky_Law_%28footballer%2C_born_1988%29', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Martin_Rowlands', 'http://www.jonsigns.co.uk/signage-case-studies/leisure', 'https://shadow.com/football-soccer-teams?release=5', 'https://www.wlv.ac.uk/business-services/employer-partners/']","Sunderland Association Football Club (/ ˈsʌndərlənd / (listen), locally / ˈsʊndlən /) is an English professional football club based in the city of Sunderland, Tyne and Wear. Sunderland currently plays in League One, the third tier of English football. Since its formation in 1879, the club has won six top-flight (First Division, now the Premier League) titles (1892, 1893, 1895, 1902, 1913 and 1936), a total only bettered by five other clubs, and has finished runners-up five times. The club has also won the FA Cup twice (1937 and 1973) and been runners-up twice (1913 and 1992), as well as winning the FA Community Shield in 1936 and being finalists the following year. Sunderland have also been Football League Cup finalists in 1985 and 2014.",when did sunderland last win the fa cup
who is the female on drake's in my feelings,"['http://lyricsondemand.com/d/drakelyrics/inmyfeelingslyrics.html', 'https://talepost.com/kikichallenge/', 'https://www.crossword-clues.com/clue/2018-drake-top-10-single-that-samples-mariah-carey-crossword/', 'https://www.theaudiodb.com/track/35007872', 'https://www.dchsdodger.com/reviews/2019/04/15/blog-4-top-songs-of-the-summer/', 'http://lyricsondemand.com/d/drakelyrics/imupsetlyrics.html', 'http://topnaija.ng/download-post-malone-better-now/']","""In My Feelings"" is a song by Canadian musician Drake from his fifth studio album Scorpion (2018). It was released to rhythmic and contemporary hit radio on July 10, 2018, as the album's fifth single. The song features additional vocals by the City Girls, though they are not credited on the official version.",who is the female on drake's in my feelings
