can felons vote in the state of illinois,"['https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/67/ss/ss6713a1.htm?s_cid=ss6713a1_w', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Disfranchisement.html', 'https://www.criminallegalnews.org/cln-news/2017/hrdc-associate-director-quoted-re-felon-disenfranchisement/', 'https://www.tnwp.uscourts.gov/faq', 'https://www.actionadvocacy.com/services/exemptions/', 'http://ngssblog.nsta.org/page/25/', 'http://ngssblog.nsta.org/page/29/']","In fourteen states and the District of Columbia, disenfranchisement ends after incarceration is complete: District of Columbia, Hawaii, Illinois, Indiana, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Montana, New Hampshire, North Dakota, Ohio, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, and Utah.",can felons vote in the state of illinois
who said a little party never killed nobody,"['http://www.lsgwl.co/video-fergie-f-q-tip.html', 'http://thersapeebles.netai.net/?pibiwa=muzyku_fergie_feat_q_tip_goonrock_a_little_party_never_killed_nob', 'http://elnorafee.webege.com/tekst-pesni-fergie-feat-q-tip-goonrock-a-little-party-never-killed-nobody/']","""A Little Party Never Killed Nobody (All We Got)"" is a 2013 song recorded by Fergie, Q-Tip and GoonRock for the soundtrack to the 2013 film The Great Gatsby, an adaptation of F. Scott Fitzgerald's novel of the same name, released through Interscope Records on May 6, 2013.",who said a little party never killed nobody
who came up with eating turkey on thanksgiving,"['https://cbird1057.wordpress.com/2009/11/', 'http://americanclub.de/events/thanksgiving-dinner-at-the-hotel-park-hyatt/', 'http://www.at-home-nepal.com/?page_id=173&from=5570&select=558', 'https://stevevictor.blogcreek.com/tag/turkey/', 'http://xautoman.com/16002-whydoweeatturkeyforthanksgivingandchristmas.html', 'https://theweatheredgreytable.com/2018/10/29/a-new-england-thanksgiving/', 'https://persysplace.com/celebrating-thanksgiving-in-massachusetts-and-rhode-island/']","The use of the turkey in the US for Thanksgiving precedes Lincoln's nationalization of the holiday in 1863. Alexander Hamilton proclaimed that no ""Citizen of the United States should refrain from turkey on Thanksgiving Day,"" and Benjamin Franklin had high regard for the wild turkey as an American icon, but turkey was uncommon as Thanksgiving fare until after 1800. By 1857, turkey had become part of the traditional dinner in New England.",who came up with eating turkey on thanksgiving
what does the fn key do on a laptop,"['http://support.hystou.com/introduce-of-fn-key-compact-layout-keyboard/', 'http://www.techcity.info/blog/tag/linux/', 'https://www.instantfundas.com/2012/04/sfunkey-keeps-laptop-fn-keys-on-or.html', 'https://perixx.com/blog/who-is-ghosting-my-keyboard.html/', 'http://thundercloud.net/infoave/premium/2019/week-806.htm', 'https://www.unbilbainoenjapon.com/how-to-use-f-keys-on-asus-laptop/', 'http://vietjetair.mobi/samsung-fn-key-96/']","The Fn key, short form for function, is a modifier key on many keyboards, especially on laptops, used in a compact layout to combine keys which are usually kept separate. It is typically found on laptops due to their keyboard size restrictions. It is also found on many full-sized ""multimedia"" keyboards as the F-Lock key. It is mainly for the purpose of changing display or audio settings quickly, such as brightness, contrast, or volume, and is held down in conjunction with the appropriate key to change the settings.",what does the fn key do on a laptop
