when did orange is the new black end,"['https://fciwomenswrestling.com/we-told-you-so-curvy-girls-are-a-wrestling-fantasy/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/07-27/all', 'https://switzerlandposts.com/orange-is-the-new-black-healthcare-for-prisoners', 'https://www.top10review.in/top-10-popular-shows-on-netflix/', 'http://supertabthemes.com/orange-is-the-new-black-hd-wallpaper-2019/', 'http://hexserver.tk/calder-casino-birthday-promotions.html', 'http://dominospizzaapp.tk/jacksonville-poker-room-regency.html']","Orange Is the New Black (sometimes abbreviated to OITNB) is an American comedy-drama web television series created by Jenji Kohan for Netflix. The series is based on Piper Kerman's memoir, Orange Is the New Black: My Year in a Women's Prison (2010), about her experiences at FCI Danbury, a minimum-security federal prison. Orange Is the New Black premiered on July 11, 2013 on the streaming service Netflix. In February 2016, the series was renewed for a fifth, sixth, and seventh season. The fifth season was released on June 9, 2017. The sixth season is scheduled to be released on July 27, 2018. The series is produced by Tilted Productions in association with Lionsgate Television.",when did orange is the new black end
who plays wanda in captain america civil war,"['https://www.wallpaperpimper.com/people/celebrities/elizabeth-olsen', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/November_17', 'https://celebvogue.com/american-actress-elizabeth-olsen-wiki-bio-age-affairs-and-net-worth/', 'https://www.topplanetinfo.com/elizabeth-olsen-lifestyle/', 'http://bookcelebrities.com/cobie-smulders/', 'https://eventi.cinemacityravenna.it/cast/scarlett-johansson/', 'https://www.amctheatres.com/movies/avengers-endgame-45840']","In the Marvel Cinematic Universe she plays the role of Wanda Maximoff / Scarlet Witch, with her first appearance in Captain America: The Winter Soldier (2014) in the end credit scene, then a lead in Avengers: Age of Ultron (2015), Captain America: Civil War (2016), Avengers: Infinity War (2018) and the upcoming Untitled Avengers film (2019).",who plays wanda in captain america civil war
what is the difference between jujube and dates,"['https://www.plantsguru.com/ziziphus-jujuba-seeds', 'https://self-cure.com/Knowledges/Herb/136', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Jujube', 'https://www.plantsguru.com/seeds-bulbs/fruit-plants-seeds', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Jujube.html', 'http://bluffviewnursery.org/1pinkdogwood.html', 'http://www.gardenology.org/wiki/Flowering_Dogwood']","It is a small deciduous tree or shrub reaching a height of 5 -- 12 metres (16 -- 39 ft), usually with thorny branches. The leaves are shiny-green, ovate-acute, 2 -- 7 centimetres (0.79 -- 2.76 in) long and 1 -- 3 centimetres (0.39 -- 1.18 in) wide, with three conspicuous veins at the base, and a finely toothed margin. The flowers are small, 5 mm (0.20 in) wide, with five inconspicuous yellowish-green petals. The fruit is an edible oval drupe 1.5 -- 3 centimetres (0.59 -- 1.18 in) deep; when immature it is smooth-green, with the consistency and taste of an apple, maturing brown to purplish-black, and eventually wrinkled, looking like a small date. There is a single hard seed similar to an olive pit.",what is the difference between jujube and dates
what happens to magnets at the north pole,"['https://kids.kiddle.co/Earth%27s_magnetic_field', 'https://www.idownloadblog.com/2017/04/28/how-to-iphone-compass-apple-maps-navigation/?utm_source=Related', 'https://wickedweatherwatch.org.uk/the-arctic/the-north-poles/', 'https://www.mountainrun.co.uk/news/intermediate-navigation-beyond-the-basics', 'https://www.hencovision.be/2015/11/19/15250-polemagnetic-pole-movement.html', 'http://www.tcms.com/Blog/', 'https://overthecircle.com/2019/01/21/follow-that-pole-the-worlds-magnetic-north-continues-to-wander/']","The North Magnetic Pole is the wandering point on the surface of Earth's Northern Hemisphere at which the planet's magnetic field points vertically downwards (in other words, if a magnetic compass needle is allowed to rotate about a horizontal axis, it will point straight down). There is only one location where this occurs, near (but distinct from) the Geographic North Pole and the Geomagnetic North Pole.",what happens to magnets at the north pole
what is the play the tempest by william shakespeare about,"['https://www.bookbeat.co.uk/book/tempest-69068', 'https://www.simonandschuster.ca/books/The-Tempest/William-Shakespeare/9781625589620', 'https://samannelizabeth.wordpress.com/tag/william-shakespeare/', 'http://www.thecanterburyplayers.co.uk/productions?page=7', 'https://www.preceden.com/timelines/70002-shakespeare-timeline', 'http://silenthillforum.com/viewtopic.php?f=30&t=22477&view=print', 'https://americanliterature.com/author/william-shakespeare/book/the-tempest/summary']","The Tempest is a play by William Shakespeare, believed to have been written in 1610 -- 1611, and thought by many critics to be the last play that Shakespeare wrote alone. It is set on a remote island, where the sorcerer Prospero, rightful Duke of Milan, plots to restore his daughter Miranda to her rightful place using illusion and skillful manipulation. He conjures up a storm, the eponymous tempest, to cause his usurping brother Antonio and the complicit King Alonso of Naples to believe they are shipwrecked and marooned on the island. There, his machinations bring about the revelation of Antonio's lowly nature, the redemption of the King, and the marriage of Miranda to Alonso's son, Ferdinand.",what is the play the tempest by william shakespeare about
how high is base camp of mount everest,"['http://www.asianhikingteam.com/print-itinerary.html?p_docid=82', 'https://www.imnepal.com/places-to-visit-in-nepal/', 'http://www.travelandtoursinnepal.com/tour-category/trekking/', 'https://www.allnepal.com/tours/everest-base-camp-trekking-nepal/', 'https://pngaa.org/site/blog/2019/04/17/dr-haydee-paiva-triumphantly-waves-png-and-solomon-island-flags-at-mt-everest-base-camp/', 'https://bymountainpeople.com/trip/everest-base-camp-trek-via-gokyo/', 'http://www.chinatourguide.com/tibet/mt.everest.html']","Everest Base Camp is either one of two base camps on opposite sides of Mount Everest (It could also be any Everest base camp on a given route, but this is less common since the two main routes became standardized). South Base Camp is in Nepal at an altitude of 5,364 metres (17,598 ft) (28 ° 0 ′ 26"" N 86 ° 51 ′ 34"" E ﻿ / ﻿ 28.00722 ° N 86.85944 ° E ﻿ / 28.00722; 86.85944), and North Base Camp is in Tibet at 5,150 metres (16,900 ft) (28 ° 8 ′ 29"" N 86 ° 51 ′ 5"" E ﻿ / ﻿ 28.14139 ° N 86.85139 ° E ﻿ / 28.14139; 86.85139 ﻿ (North Base Camp)). These camps are rudimentary campsites on Mount Everest that are used by mountain climbers during their ascent and descent. South Base Camp is used when climbing via the southeast ridge, while North Base Camp is used when climbing via the northeast ridge.",how high is base camp of mount everest
what subjects were taught in european universities during the middle ages,"['http://africaicea.org/index.php/media1/formal-education-in-the-middle-ages', 'http://eliteacademicessays.info/viewtopic.php?t=10241', 'http://cinecon.info/viewtopic.php?t=42185']","The first Western European institutions generally considered universities were established in the Kingdom of Italy (then part of the Holy Roman Empire), the Kingdom of England, the Kingdom of France, the Kingdom of Spain, and the Kingdom of Portugal between the 11th and 15th centuries for the study of the Arts and the higher disciplines of Theology, Law, and Medicine. These universities evolved from much older Christian cathedral schools and monastic schools, and it is difficult to define the exact date when they became true universities, though the lists of studia generalia for higher education in Europe held by the Vatican are a useful guide.",what subjects were taught in european universities during the middle ages
who sang i don't want to lose your love,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Mike_Reid_(singer)', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Travis_Tritt', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Earl_Thomas_Conley', 'https://www.whenthecowboysings.com/blog/?tag=John+Conlee', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Greg_Jennings', 'https://www.whenthecowboysings.com/crystal-gayle-the-sound-of-goodbye', 'https://www.whenthecowboysings.com/blog/?tag=That+Nashville+Music']","""I Don't Wanna Lose Your Love"" is a song written by Joey Carbone, and recorded by American country music artist Crystal Gayle. It was released in February 1984 as the second single from the album Cage the Songbird. The song reached number 2 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart. This is originally sung by John O'Banion in 1982.",who sang i don't want to lose your love
where did the stone of scone come from,"['https://peterpilt.org/2015/01/26/christianity-in-australian-culture-and-heritage/', 'http://peterweddeantiques.co.nz/silver.html', 'https://paulgauchi.wordpress.com/2018/05/', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Jewel_House', 'http://plheineman.net/stoneofdestiny.htm', 'https://ww2truth.com/2019/04/08/the-secret-masonic-victory-of-world-war-ii-by-dennis-wise/comment-page-1/', 'https://highlandtrails.com/scottish-highlands-castle-tour/']","The Stone of Scone (/ ˈskuːn /; Scottish Gaelic: An Lia Fàil, Scots: Stane o Scuin) -- also known as the Stone of Destiny, and often referred to in England as The Coronation Stone -- is an oblong block of red sandstone that was used for centuries in the coronation of the monarchs of Scotland, and later the monarchs of England and those of the United Kingdom. Historically, the artefact was kept at the now-ruined Scone Abbey in Scone, near Perth, Scotland. It is also known as Jacob's Pillow Stone and the Tanist Stone, and in Scottish Gaelic, clach-na-cinneamhain. Its size is approximately 660 mm (26 in) by 425 mm (16.7 in) by 267 mm (10.5 in) and its weight is approximately 152 kg (335 lb). A roughly incised cross is on one surface, and an iron ring at each end aids with transport. The Stone of Scone was last used in 1953 for the coronation of Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland.",where did the stone of scone come from
how much is 100 acres of land in miles,"['https://www.petrobasics.com/unit-convert', 'http://1899t.info/?newsid=1413', 'http://www.englishvs.com/ingilizce-sozluk/kelimeler/ingilizce-kelimeler/a-ile-baslayan-ingilizce-kelimeler/acre', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/how-many-feet-are-in-an-acre.html', 'https://www.fooddialogues.com/agriculture-101/', 'https://www.askdifference.com/acre-vs-hectare/', 'https://wikiwordbook.info/acr']","The acre is a unit of land area used in the imperial and US customary systems. It is defined as the area of 1 chain by 1 furlong (66 by 660 feet), which is exactly equal to ​ ⁄ of a square mile, 43,560 square feet, approximately 4,047 m, or about 40% of a hectare.",how much is 100 acres of land in miles
when does the movie ready player one come out,"['https://www.affiliatepromotional.com/inspiring-books-2017/', 'http://www.videoshows.com/vid/4193-ready-player-one-trailer-2018/', 'https://taylornetworkofpodcasts.com/2017/07/22/sdcc-ready-player-one-trailer/', 'http://www.man2tickle.com/2017/12/top-10-most-expected-films-of-2018.html', 'http://www.beentothemovies.com/2018/04/ready-player-one-movie-review.html', 'https://boxofficebuz.com/review/ready-player-one-review', 'http://missliterati.com/yts-hd-movies-hindi.html']","Ready Player One is an upcoming American science fiction adventure film co-produced and directed by Steven Spielberg and written by Zak Penn and Ernest Cline, based on Cline's novel of the same name. The film stars Tye Sheridan, Olivia Cooke, Ben Mendelsohn, Mark Rylance, Simon Pegg, and T.J. Miller. The film is scheduled to be released on March 30, 2018.",when does the movie ready player one come out
bmw 1 series is it front wheel drive,"['https://www.jdpower.com/cars/INFINITI/new-2013-infiniti', 'https://wikivivid.com/wiki/BMW', 'https://www.kijijiautos.ca/cars/sedan/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Car_classification', 'https://consumerguide.com/dodge/durango/', 'https://cars.usnews.com/cars-trucks/infiniti/g37/2013', 'https://www.reedmantollcdjrspringfield.com/2018-dodge-durango-philadelphia-pa.htm']","The 1 Series is BMW's entry level of model range. Unusually for a small car, the 1 Series range is mostly rear-wheel drive, (except for the F52 sedan, which is front-wheel drive) with optional all-wheel drive being available on some models.",bmw 1 series is it front wheel drive
what is not part of all contracts the offer time requirements premiums consideration,"['http://sacredlands.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=22246', 'http://mumbaidirectory.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=24577', 'http://taajuuslista.info/?page_id=35830', 'http://cusco-hotels.info/news.php?action=show&id=43009', 'http://kirschenbaumesq.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-a-contract-and-terms-and-conditions-dont-miss-out-on-the-concierge-program-january-16-2019', 'https://rocketspanish-review.com/car-insurance-best-comparison-site-build-it/third-party-car-insurance-cover-note-template/', 'https://www.friedman-lawfirm.com/practice_areas.html']","A contract is a promise or set of promises that are legally enforceable and, if violated, allow the injured party access to legal remedies. Contract law recognises and governs the rights and duties arising from agreements. In the Anglo-American common law, formation of a contract generally requires an offer, acceptance, consideration, and a mutual intent to be bound. Each party must have capacity to enter the contract. Although most oral contracts are binding, some types of contracts may require formalities, such as being in writing or by deed.",what is not part of all contracts the offer time requirements premiums consideration
where does the orient express start and finish,"['https://www.mulberrytravel.com/orient-express-history/', 'http://www.bookofdaystales.com/orient-express/', 'https://soundlandscapes.wordpress.com/category/paris-sounds/paris-railway-stations/']","The original route, which first ran on October 4, 1883, was from Paris, Gare de l'Est, to Giurgiu in Romania via Munich and Vienna. At Giurgiu, passengers were ferried across the Danube to Ruse, Bulgaria, to pick up another train to Varna. They then completed their journey to Constantinople by ferry. In 1885, another route began operations, this time reaching Istanbul via rail from Vienna to Belgrade and Niš, carriage to Plovdiv and rail again to Istanbul.",where does the orient express start and finish
who won in battle of alexander and porus,"['http://www.setmefreee.com/2012/03/', 'http://www.macedonianhistory.org/video-archives-center/indian-campaigns-of-alexander-the-great-and-battle-of-the-hydaspes', 'https://www.alexander-the-great.org/alexanders-campaign/battle-of-the-hydaspes.php', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Battle_of_Gaugamela', 'http://ssc.xaam.in/2018/09/ga-notes-important-battles-fought-in.html', 'https://www.britannica.com/event/Battle-of-Thermopylae-Greek-history-480-BC', 'http://murasaki69cube.hateblo.jp/entry/2017/09/20/000234']","The Battle of the Hydaspes was fought in 326 BC between Alexander the Great and King Porus of the Paurava kingdom on the banks of the river Jhelum (known to the Greeks as Hydaspes) in the Punjab region of the Indian subcontinent (modern-day Punjab, Pakistan). The battle resulted in a complete Greek victory and the annexation of Punjab, which lay beyond the far easternmost confines of the already absorbed Persian Empire, into the Macedonian Empire.",who won in battle of alexander and porus
