when did bausch and lomb sell ray ban,"['http://obriensopticians.co.uk/index.php?id=ray-ban', 'https://www.topcashback.co.uk/ray-ban/', 'http://raybanshop.ir/posts/ray-ban', 'http://eye-candy-optical.com/Eyewear_Collections/item/594/', 'https://mostvaluablebrands.com/the-aviators-choice-2/', 'https://www.shop4shades.co.uk/women/rayban.html', 'https://www.firstversions.com/2014/12/ray-ban.html']","In 1929, US Army Air Corps Colonel John A. Macready worked with Bausch & Lomb, a Rochester, New York-based medical equipment manufacturer, to create aviation sunglasses that would reduce the distraction for pilots caused by the intense blue and white hues of the sky. Specifically, MacCready was concerned about how pilots' goggles would fog up, greatly reducing visibility at high altitude. The prototype, created in 1936 and known as' Anti-Glare', had plastic frames and green lenses that could cut out the glare without obscuring vision. They also added impact-resistant lenses in 1938. The sunglasses were redesigned with a metal frame the following year and patented as the Ray-Ban Aviator. According to the BBC, the glasses used ""Kalichrome lenses designed to sharpen details and minimise haze by filtering out blue light, making them ideal for misty conditions.""",when did bausch and lomb sell ray ban
when does the chinese new year starts and ends,"['http://en.dangcongsan.vn/world-events-and-comments/news/countries-welcome-lunar-new-year-like-vietnam-512096.html', 'https://www.myboysclub.co.uk/2018/01/celebrate-chinese-new-year-north-east-england.html', 'https://www.torta-a-porta.com/new-bright-holiday-express-train-set/', 'http://nfonline.co.za/rwanda-china-cultural-exchange-grow-says-minister-uwacu/', 'https://majormike.us/photographs/year-of-2017/338/', 'https://www.buydeestore.com/2017/01/', 'https://masterflex-ukblog.com/2016/02/08/happy-chinese-new-year-2/']","Chinese New Year, also known as the Spring Festival in modern China, is an important Chinese festival celebrated at the turn of the traditional lunisolar Chinese calendar. It is one of several Lunar New Years in Asia. Celebrations traditionally run from the evening preceding the first day, to the Lantern Festival on the 15th day of the first calendar month. The first day of the New Year falls on the new moon between January 21 and February 20 In 2018, the first day of the Lunar New Year was on Friday, 16 February, initiating the year of the Dog.",when does the chinese new year starts and ends
where does hot and sour soup come from,"['http://raisepakistan.com/top-10-chinese-recipes-most-popular-in-the-world/', 'https://www.burmaspice.com/product/white-pepper-ground/', 'http://spicyworld.in/recipes-2.html']","Hot and sour soup is a variety of soups from several Asian culinary traditions. In all cases, the soup contains ingredients to make it both spicy and sour.",where does hot and sour soup come from
who has won more world series american or national,"['https://hyperleap.com/topic/World_Series', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/article/WHEBN0023489161/World%20Series', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/35616', 'http://www.salt-and-light-aa.com/home/online-study/advanced-class/play-ball', 'https://www.bestbrains.com/blogDetail?url=world-series', 'http://baberuthautographs.com/tickets-a-stubs/all-items9/ny-yankees-1st-ws-gm.html', 'https://hyperleap.com/topic/Oakland_Athletics']","In the American League, the New York Yankees have played in 40 World Series and won 27, the Philadelphia / Kansas City / Oakland Athletics have played in 14 and won 9, and the Boston Red Sox have played in 12 and won 8, including the first World Series. In the National League, the St. Louis Cardinals have appeared in 19 and won 11, the New York / San Francisco Giants have played in 20 and won 8, the Brooklyn / Los Angeles Dodgers have appeared in 19 and won 6, and the Cincinnati Reds have appeared in 9 and won 5.",who has won more world series american or national
what is a fellow of the royal society,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Fellow_of_the_Royal_Society', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Ronald_Ross', 'https://themindunleashed.com/2017/04/forced-abortion-advocate-population-control-professor-speaks-vatican-event.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Category:Fellows_of_the_Royal_Society']","Fellowship of the Royal Society (FRS, ForMemRS and HonFRS) is an award granted to individuals that the Royal Society judges to have made a ""substantial contribution to the improvement of natural knowledge, including mathematics, engineering science and medical science"".",what is a fellow of the royal society
what type of sleep do you need the most of,"['https://www.sleepassociation.org/about-sleep/', 'https://hintng.com/sleep-benefits-of-having-a-healthy-sleeping-life/', 'https://moreiknow.com/sentra-pm/', 'https://www.cosmopolitan.co.za/health-fitness/6-ways-you-could-be-accidentally-ruining-your-work-out/', 'https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/869941-overview', 'https://www.scitechnol.com/sleep-disorders-treatment-care.php', 'https://vietnamnews.vn/life-style/350537/to-your-health-losing-sleep-over-insomnia.html']","Sleep is divided into two broad types: non-rapid eye movement (non-REM or NREM sleep) and rapid eye movement (REM sleep). non-REM and REM sleep are so different that physiologists identify them as distinct behavioral states. Non-REM sleep occurs first and after a transitional period is called slow wave sleep or deep sleep. During this phase, body temperature and heart rate fall, and the brain uses less energy. REM sleep (also known as paradoxical sleep), a smaller portion of total sleep time and the main occasion for dreams (or nightmares), is associated with desynchronized and fast brain waves, eye movements, loss of muscle tone, and suspension of homeostasis.",what type of sleep do you need the most of
who is the actress that plays emily in pretty little liars,"['http://www.mr-mehra.com/2017/12/stunning-shay-mitchell-styles-that-you.html', 'https://www.imdb.com/list/ls072999815/', 'https://allstarbio.com/shay-mitchell-biography-ethnicity-nationality-profession-birthday-height-weight-boyfriend-husband-affair-marital-status-net-worth-career-fact/', 'http://9facts.info/fashion-girls-world/']","Shay Mitchell (born Shannon Ashley Mitchell; April 10, 1987) is a Canadian actress, model, entrepreneur and author. She rose to prominence starring as Emily Fields in the Freeform series Pretty Little Liars (2010 -- 2017).",who is the actress that plays emily in pretty little liars
what side did the confederate army fight for and what side did the union army fight for,"['https://post532.org/american-wars-page-1', 'https://www.blackfacts.com/fact/american-civil-war', 'http://www.rajeevmahajan.com/2016/10/the-battle-that-defined-nation.html', 'https://www.landscape-guides.com/product/free-sample-american-civil-war-letters-full-colour-images/', 'http://veteransparkhc.com/CivilWar.html', 'https://desotocountyveteranspark.com/2017/07/civil-war/', 'http://www.taichinederland.nl/en/the-first-and-the-last/']","Among the 34 U.S. states in February 1861, seven Southern slave states individually declared their secession from the U.S. to form the Confederate States of America, or the South. The Confederacy grew to include eleven slave states. The Confederacy was never diplomatically recognized by the United States government, nor was it recognized by any foreign country (although the United Kingdom and France granted it belligerent status). The states that remained loyal to the U.S. (including the border states where slavery was legal) were known as the Union or the North.",what side did the confederate army fight for and what side did the union army fight for
when did ireland gain its independence from great britain,"['http://irishkannadigaru.com/ireland.html', 'http://southfloridagaynews.com/tag/93-gay-history.html', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/British_isles', 'https://readtiger.com/wkp/en/Partition_of_Ireland', 'https://www.cs.mcgill.ca/~rwest/wikispeedia/wpcd/wp/r/Republic_of_Ireland.htm', 'http://www.tripleostudio.com/trip-to-northern-ireland/', 'http://letsfixit.co.uk/travel/ireland/']","In 1922, after the Irish War of Independence and the Anglo-Irish Treaty, most of Ireland seceded from the United Kingdom to become the independent Irish Free State, which after the 1937 constitution, began to call itself Ireland. The six northeastern counties, known as Northern Ireland, remained within the United Kingdom. The Irish Civil War followed soon after the War of Independence. The history of Northern Ireland has since been dominated by sporadic sectarian conflict between (mainly Catholic) Irish nationalists and (mainly Protestant) unionists. This conflict erupted into the Troubles in the late 1960s, until peace was achieved with the Belfast Agreement thirty years later.",when did ireland gain its independence from great britain
what does it mean to get a port put in,"['http://www.revivetosurvive.org/our-project', 'https://cvhealthclinic.com/about-air/services/', 'https://www.uabmedicine.org/patient-care/treatments/port-placement', 'https://www.advicesbooks.com/self-help-book-can-we-live-a-happier-life-by-dr-zeev-gilkis/', 'http://www.ilanoflife.com/2012/05/week-home.html', 'https://cancercentersocal.com/intravenous-chemotherapy/', 'http://www.haderermuller.com/portfolio-item/vortex-port/']","In medicine, a port is a small medical appliance that is installed beneath the skin. A catheter connects the port to a vein. Under the skin, the port has a septum through which drugs can be injected and blood samples can be drawn many times, usually with less discomfort for the patient than a more typical ""needle stick"".",what does it mean to get a port put in
is saigon the same as ho chi minh,"['https://nhatrangprivatecar.com/saigon-half-day-tour/', 'http://www.traveltill.com/destination/Vietnam/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/', 'http://lifeontheline.info/search?q=Ho%20chi%20minh%20sea', 'https://drokov.com/city/ho-chi-minh', 'http://kembarasufi.com/ho-chi-minh-4d-3n/', 'https://vietnam.travel-culture.com/vietnam/index.shtml', 'http://everything.explained.today/Ho_Chi_Minh_City/']","Ho Chi Minh City (Vietnamese: Thành phố Hồ Chí Minh; (thàn fǒ hò tɕǐ mɨ̄n) (listen) or (thàn fǒ hò cǐ mɨ̄n)), also informally known by its former name of Saigon (Vietnamese: Sài Gòn; (sàj ɣɔ̀ŋ) (listen)), is the largest city in Vietnam by population. It was known as Prey Nokor (Khmer: ព្រៃនគរ) prior to annexation by the Vietnamese in the 17th century. Under the name Saigon, it was the capital of the French colony of Cochinchina and later of the independent republic of South Vietnam 1955 -- 75. On 2 July 1976, Saigon merged with the surrounding Gia Định Province and was officially renamed Ho Chi Minh City after revolutionary leader Hồ Chí Minh (although the name Sài Gòn is still widely used).",is saigon the same as ho chi minh
which state is to the north of hp,"['http://aicps.org/contact-usdistrict-committees-himachal-pradeshdistrict-committee-shimla', 'http://election2019loksabha.com/himachal-pradesh-lok-sabha-general-election-results-2019/', 'https://www.shubhttc.com/india-tour-packages/himachal-tour-packages', 'https://www.sgpsholidays.com/tours/western-himalayas-42646', 'https://alchetron.com/Himachal-Pradesh', 'https://batterupwithsujata.wordpress.com/category/chana-madra/', 'https://cat1no.info/news.php?action=show&id=22383']","Himachal Pradesh ((ɦɪmaːtʃəl prəd̪eːʃ) (listen); literally ""Abode of Snow"") is a state of India located in North India. It is bordered by Jammu and Kashmir on the north, Punjab and Chandigarh on the west, Haryana on the southwest, Uttarakhand on the southeast, and the Tibet Autonomous Region on the east. At its southernmost point, it also touches the state of Uttar Pradesh. The name was coined from the Sanskrit -- Him means' snow' and achal means' land' or' abode' -- by Acharya Diwakar Datt Sharma, one of the state's eminent Sanskrit scholars.",which state is to the north of hp
why do i have callus on my hands,"['https://www.comfortfeet.com.au/clinical-podiatry/clinical-services/', 'https://www.tripmondo.com/spain/catalonia/barcelona/navas/', 'https://www.vancouverorthotics.ca/Corns-Calluses-Hyperkeratoses', 'https://www.2ft.com/index.php/2018/05/31/calluses/', 'https://davincifootandankle.com/podiatrist-greensboro-ga/2018/08/13/5-big-toe-bummers-common-causes-of-big-toe-pain/', 'https://www.drrengestotal.com/ailments/skin-2/corns-and-calluses/', 'https://zoemyhr.wordpress.com/category/foot-callous/']","A callus is an area of thickened skin that forms as a response to repeated friction, pressure, or other irritation. Since repeated contact is required, calluses are most often found on feet because of frequent walking and incorrectly fitting footwear. While they can be perceived as being unsightly, calluses are generally not harmful, but if neglected for long periods may sometimes lead to other problems, such as a skin ulceration or infection, or cause the sufferer to try and offload the affected painful area, which can place excessive stress on the asymptomatic side. Rubbing that is too frequent or forceful will cause blisters as opposed to calluses to form.",why do i have callus on my hands
why is it called the national hockey league,"['http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/National_Hockey_League', 'https://sportscasting.fandom.com/index.php?title=NHL', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/R%C3%B8dovre_Mighty_Bulls', 'https://newyorkessays.com/essay-charlie-chaplin-2731/', 'https://www.ticketnest.com/NHL.php', 'http://bartosza.eu/hockey-world-league-final_rr/650', 'http://www.greatesthockeylegends.com/2011/11/this-day-in-hockey-history-nov-26th.html']","The National Hockey League was established in 1917 as the successor to the National Hockey Association (NHA). Founded in 1909, the NHA began play one year later with seven teams in Ontario and Quebec, and was one of the first major leagues in professional ice hockey. But by the NHA's eighth season, a series of disputes with Toronto Blueshirts owner Eddie Livingstone led the other team owners, representing the Montreal Canadiens, Montreal Wanderers, Ottawa Senators, and Quebec Bulldogs to meet about the league's future. Realizing the NHA constitution left them unable to force Livingstone out, the four teams voted instead to suspend the NHA, and on November 26, 1917, formed the National Hockey League. Frank Calder was chosen as its first president, serving until his death in 1943.",why is it called the national hockey league
where did they shoot star wars the force awakens,"['https://weave.me/weave/?Nickelodeon_29th_Kids_Choice_Awards', 'https://twittersfantasyebookguide.wordpress.com/2015/12/', 'https://wn.com/Star_Wars%E2%80%9D_galaxy', 'https://www.postercollector.co.uk/star-wars-episode-vii-the-force-awakens-2015-coming-soon-uk-one-sheet/', 'https://www.designcodeblack.com/star-wars-the-force-awakens-trailer/', 'https://www.powercoin.it/es/new-zealand-mint/2250-bb-8-star-wars-the-force-awakens-1-oz-plata-proof-moneda-2-niue-2016.html', 'http://www.d3bris.de/blah-blah-star-wars-blah-blah/']","The Force Awakens was announced after The Walt Disney Company's acquisition of Lucasfilm in October 2012. The film was produced by Abrams, his longtime collaborator Bryan Burk, and Lucasfilm president Kathleen Kennedy. Abrams and Lawrence Kasdan, co-writer of the original trilogy films The Empire Strikes Back (1980) and Return of the Jedi (1983), rewrote an initial script by Michael Arndt. John Williams, the composer for the previous six films, returned to compose the film's score. Lucas served as creative consultant during the film's early production. Filming began in April 2014 in Abu Dhabi and Iceland, with principal photography also taking place in Ireland and Pinewood Studios in the United Kingdom, and concluded in November 2014. It is the first live-action Star Wars film since Revenge of the Sith (2005).",where did they shoot star wars the force awakens
when was weed made illegal in the united states,"['http://www.whitenationnetwork.com/archives/69503', 'https://www.capitol.hawaii.gov/session2019/bills/SB686_SD1_.htm', 'https://www.change.org/p/mr-president-and-government-officials-legalization-and-access-to-cannabis-end-prohibition-and-save-lives', 'https://www.thestreet.com/story/12785055/1/god-bless-united-states-hemp.html', 'https://theipcenter.com/2019/01/cannabis-patent-protection-is-getting-higher/', 'https://www.rbattinglaw.com/cannabis-medicine-usa-history/', 'https://gogusco.com/michigan-medical-marijuana-grow-lights/']","The legal history of cannabis in the United States relates to the regulation of cannabis (legal term marijuana) use for medical, recreational or industrial purposes in the United States. Increased restrictions and labeling of cannabis as a poison began in many states from 1906 onward, and outright prohibitions began in the 1920s. By the mid-1930s marijuana was regulated as a drug in every state, including 35 states that adopted the Uniform State Narcotic Drug Act. The first national regulation was the Marihuana Tax Act of 1937.",when was weed made illegal in the united states
who are the us senators from rhode island,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/List_of_United_States_Senators_from_Rhode_Island', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/List_of_United_States_Senators_from_Rhode_Island', 'https://dailycaller.com/2011/04/01/federal-judge-nominee-has-history-of-bias-against-business-democratic-activism/', 'https://www.earthforums.com/forums/forum/environment/congress-on-climate-change/rhode-island/', 'https://www.gamblingsites.org/news/federal-ruling-endangers-taunton-casino-plans/amp/', 'https://enhancingyoungminds.com/category/guestspeakers/page/5/', 'http://www.anchorrising.com/barnacles/003730.html']","This is a list of United States Senators from Rhode Island. Rhode Island ratified the Constitution on May 29, 1790, and its senators belong to Class 1 and Class 2. Rhode Island's current senators are Jack Reed and Sheldon Whitehouse.",who are the us senators from rhode island
why does the president have power to pardon,"['https://originalismblog.typepad.com/the-originalism-blog/2017/07/the-ability-to-self-pardon-is-not-absurd-but-it-is-nevertheless-not-allowed-by-the-us-constitution-t.html', 'https://legalinsurrection.com/2017/08/senator-kamala-harris-doesnt-know-how-a-pardon-works/', 'https://applicationforpardon.com/pardon-me-for-my-crime-2/', 'https://lawprofessors.typepad.com/conlaw/2017/07/daily-read-can-the-president-pardon-himself.html', 'https://feedimo.com/story/27644610/Late-Night-Hosts-Take-Jabs-at-Trumps-Self-Pardon-Tweet/', 'https://www.laprogressive.com/president-for-life/', 'https://p-2-p.org/trump-pardons-dsouza-and-the-left-goes-nuts-liberty-nation']","In the United States, the pardon power for federal crimes is granted to the President of the United States under Article II, Section 2 of the United States Constitution which states that the President ""shall have power to grant reprieves and pardons for offenses against the United States, except in cases of impeachment"". The U.S. Supreme Court has interpreted this language to include the power to grant pardons, conditional pardons, commutations of sentence, conditional commutations of sentence, remissions of fines and forfeitures, respites, and amnesties.",why does the president have power to pardon
when does assassins creed black flag take place,"['https://www.intoguide.com/15-ubisoft-best-action-games/', 'https://playfi.online/assassins-creed-iv-black-flag-download/', ""https://wn.com/Assassin's_Creed_IV:_Black_Flag"", 'https://ranktopten.com/top-10-best-assassin-s-creed-games-2099', 'http://crohasits.com/assassins-creed-4-black-flag-free-download/', 'https://itouchblog.de/frayed/assassins-creed-rogue-soundtrack.php', 'https://rootmasterapk.online/anvilnext-50/']","The plot is set in a fictional history of real world events and follows the centuries-old struggle between the Assassins, who fight for peace with free will, and the Templars, who desire peace through control. The framing story is set in the 21st century and describes the player as an Abstergo agent. The main story is set in the 18th century Caribbean during the Golden Age of Piracy, and follows notorious Welsh pirate Edward Kenway, grandfather and father of Assassin's Creed III protagonist and antagonist Ratonhnhaké: ton and Haytham Kenway respectively, who stumbles upon the Assassin / Templar conflict. The attempted establishment of a Republic of Pirates utopia (free from either British or Spanish rule) is a significant plot element.",when does assassins creed black flag take place
is london the capital of england or the uk,"['http://outlaw-urbanist.com/tag/united-kingdom/', 'https://www.p-l-a-n-e-t-b-l-o-g.com/2016/08/here-are-photos-that-brings-out-beauty.html', 'https://realtyww.info/search/q=,1+Bed+Flat+For+Sale+In+West+London,+London', 'https://www.heathrowgatwickcars.com/london/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'http://prestigetaxisheathrow.com/taxi-from-heathrow-to-london-transfer', 'http://www.peandle.com/destinations/london/', 'https://www.webwiki.co.uk/london']","London (/ ˈlʌndən / (listen) LUN-dən) is the capital and most populous city of England and the United Kingdom. Standing on the River Thames in the south east of the island of Great Britain, London has been a major settlement for two millennia. It was founded by the Romans, who named it Londinium. London's ancient core, the City of London, largely retains its 1.12-square-mile (2.9 km) medieval boundaries. Since at least the 19th century, ""London"" has also referred to the metropolis around this core, historically split between Middlesex, Essex, Surrey, Kent and Hertfordshire, which today largely makes up Greater London, a region governed by the Mayor of London and the London Assembly.",is london the capital of england or the uk
how many sets of twins are there in the us,"['https://www.tastydram.be/2018/10/gordon-macphail-launches-twin-casks.html', 'https://minerdescent.com/2012/04/11/twins/', 'http://theinfolist.com/php/SummaryGet.php?FindGo=Yoruba%20People', 'https://transterramedia.com/tags/7992-team']","The human twin birth rate in the United States, rose 76% from 1980 through 2009, from 18.9 to 33.3 per 1,000 births (about 80%) The Yoruba have the highest rate of twinning in the world, at 45 -- 50 twin sets (or 90 -- 100 twins) per 1,000 live births, possibly because of high consumption of a specific type of yam containing a natural phytoestrogen which may stimulate the ovaries to release an egg from each side.",how many sets of twins are there in the us
how many examination systems are at university level in pakistan,"['https://www.successcds.net/Distance-Education/top-bed-distance-education-universities-india.html', 'http://internetstrikers.blogspot.com/2012/06/top-bed-colleges-in-india.html', 'https://www.studysolutions.pk/nts-result-answer-key-of-all-tests', 'https://www.jntufastupdates.com/kcet-second-round-seat-allotment-results-2018/']","In Pakistan for undergraduate admissions the national universities have common entrance tests which are SAT based and are held according to provincial zones, the private universities hold their own entrance test which are also SAT based.",how many examination systems are at university level in pakistan
where do the energy capturing reactions of photosynthesis occur,"['http://www.juniorsbook.com/tell-me-why-numerous-questions-and-answers/what-is-photosynthesis/', 'http://www.light2015.org/Home/LearnAboutLight/Light-in-Nature.html', 'http://yourdemocracy.net.au/drupal/node/19214', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/15027', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Photosynthesis', 'https://royresearch.com/cellulosic-nitrogen-fertilizer/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Bramble']","Although photosynthesis is performed differently by different species, the process always begins when energy from light is absorbed by proteins called reaction centres that contain green chlorophyll pigments. In plants, these proteins are held inside organelles called chloroplasts, which are most abundant in leaf cells, while in bacteria they are embedded in the plasma membrane. In these light-dependent reactions, some energy is used to strip electrons from suitable substances, such as water, producing oxygen gas. The hydrogen freed by the splitting of water is used in the creation of two further compounds that act as an immediate energy storage means: reduced nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADPH) and adenosine triphosphate (ATP), the ""energy currency"" of cells.",where do the energy capturing reactions of photosynthesis occur
what is creed with arms wide open about,"['http://uprutuadobib.info/author/UCpbwpccUaN4RCaE9Y_SSbJg/DurBube', 'http://beatzone.eu/track/Creed/With+Arms+Wide+Open', 'http://beneric.tk/open-arms-piano-sheet-with-lyrics.html']","Scott Stapp wrote the lyrics when he found out, with great surprise, that he was going to be a father.",what is creed with arms wide open about
where did the story of dumbo come from,"['https://whyevolutionistrue.wordpress.com/2018/10/30/a-spotting-of-the-spectacular-and-rarely-seen-dumbo-octopus/', 'https://www.closerweekly.com/posts/new-dumbo-trailer/']","Dumbo is based upon a children's story written by Helen Aberson and illustrated by Harold Pearl that was prepared to demonstrate the prototype of a toy storytelling display device called Roll-A-Book, which was similar in principle to a panorama. It involved only eight drawings and just a few lines of text, and had Red Robin as Dumbo's ally instead of Timothy Mouse.",where did the story of dumbo come from
what states are on the border of canada,"['https://www.restorekewaunee.com/saskatchewan-blue-cross-travel-insurance/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Detroit', 'http://explorer.natureserve.org/servlet/NatureServe?searchName=Carex+vaginata', 'https://www.mapsofworld.com/usa/states/montana/', 'http://explorer.natureserve.org/servlet/NatureServe?searchSpeciesUid=ELEMENT_GLOBAL.2.133442', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Hudson_Bay', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/countries-that-border-only-one-country.html']","The Canada -- United States border (French: Frontière entre le Canada et les États-Unis), officially known as the International Boundary, is the longest international border in the world between two countries. It is shared between Canada and the United States, the second-and fourth-largest countries by area, respectively. The terrestrial boundary (including portions of maritime boundaries in the Great Lakes, and on the Atlantic, Pacific, and Arctic coasts) is 8,891 kilometres (5,525 mi) long, of which 2,475 kilometres (1,538 mi) is Canada's border with Alaska. Eight Canadian provinces and territories (Yukon, British Columbia, Alberta, Saskatchewan, Manitoba, Ontario, Quebec, and New Brunswick), and thirteen U.S. states (Alaska, Washington, Idaho, Montana, North Dakota, Minnesota, Michigan, Ohio, Pennsylvania, New York, Vermont, New Hampshire, and Maine) are located along the border.",what states are on the border of canada
when does the cold war start and end,"['https://gradesfixer.com/free-essay-examples/the-cold-war-between-the-united-states-and-the-soviet-union/', 'http://www.artandpopularculture.com/?title=Cold_War&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Pahlavi_dynasty', 'http://www.pearltrees.com/mamenfernandez/the-cold-war/id16733865', 'https://a-changing-world.fandom.com/wiki/Second_Cold_War', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Blood_in_the_Water_match', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Admiral_of_the_Fleet_(Royal_Navy)']","The Cold War was a state of geopolitical tension after World War II between powers in the Eastern Bloc (the Soviet Union and its satellite states) and powers in the Western Bloc (the United States, its NATO allies and others). Historians do not fully agree on the dates, but a common timeframe is the period between 1947, the year the Truman Doctrine, a U.S. foreign policy pledging to aid nations threatened by Soviet expansionism, was announced, and either 1989, when communism fell in Eastern Europe, or 1991, when the Soviet Union collapsed. The term ""cold"" is used because there was no large-scale fighting directly between the two sides, but they each supported major regional wars known as proxy wars.",when does the cold war start and end
the temptations papa was a rolling stone lyrics meaning,['http://tomclarkblog.blogspot.com/2018/02/all-young-dudes-clark-coolidge-two-new.html'],"Vocal duties are performed in a true ensemble style: Temptations singers Dennis Edwards, Melvin Franklin, Richard Street (who was a frequent fill-in for Paul Williams and his eventual replacement) and Damon Harris (who had replaced Eddie Kendricks as the group's falsetto singer the previous year) alternate vocal lines, taking the role of siblings questioning their mother about their now-dead father; their increasingly pointed questions, and the mother's repeated response (""Papa was a rollin' stone / wherever he laid his hat was his home / and when he died, all he left us was alone"") paint a somber picture for the children who have never seen their father and have ""never heard nothing but bad things about him.""",the temptations papa was a rolling stone lyrics meaning
how long does it take the earth to make a complete rotation,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Day', 'https://cluesforum.info/viewtopic.php?p=2407821&amp', 'https://www.universetoday.com/tag/arctic-circle/', 'https://www.reference.com/science/long-earth-completely-rotate-once-its-axis-8b33cd36858cccd1', 'https://socratic.org/questions/which-way-does-the-earth-rotate-and-why', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Earth%27s_rotation', 'http://michaeljacksonthemanthemythhismusic.blogspot.com/2013/09/september-thriller-night.html']","Earth rotates once in about 24 hours with respect to the Sun, but once every 23 hours, 56 minutes, and 4 seconds with respect to the stars (see below). Earth's rotation is slowing slightly with time; thus, a day was shorter in the past. This is due to the tidal effects the Moon has on Earth's rotation. Atomic clocks show that a modern day is longer by about 1.7 milliseconds than a century ago, slowly increasing the rate at which UTC is adjusted by leap seconds. Analysis of historical astronomical records shows a slowing trend of about 2.3 milliseconds per century since the 8th century BCE.",how long does it take the earth to make a complete rotation
what does it mean to have a hyphenated name,"['http://www.footnotemaven.com/2007/07/whats-in-name.html', 'https://www.maistraatti.fi/en/Services/marriage/', 'http://deedpollsonline.co.uk/AWomansRightsUponMarriage.html', 'http://ukdps.co.uk/ACouplesRightsUponACivilPartnership.html', 'https://www.uwb.edu/it/howdoi/articles/uwbid', 'https://btbcapitalgroupllc.com/curriculum-vitae-eglish.html', 'http://britishsurnames.co.uk/']","In the Western tradition of surnames, there are several types of double surname (also double-barrelled surname). If the two names are joined with a hyphen, it may also be called a hyphenated surname.",what does it mean to have a hyphenated name
where does the term april showers come from,"['https://www.reference.com/art-literature/examples-heroic-couplets-976a7cfbc0312294', 'http://thecramer5.com/post/44']","The proverb ""March winds and April showers bring forth May flowers"", first recorded in 1886, or the shorter, trochaic version ""April showers bring May flowers"" (originally ""Sweet April showers / Do spring May flowers"", part of a poem recorded in 1610) are common expressions in English speaking countries. The phrase is referenced in the General Prologue of The Canterbury Tales: ""Whan that Aprill, with his shoures soote The droghte of March hath perced to the roote"".",where does the term april showers come from
first president of united states under articles of confederation,"['https://truestrange.com/2017/07/13/the-1st-president-of-usa-not-george-washington/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'https://www.vaguelyinteresting.co.uk/2105/', 'https://www.americanroads.net/war_roads_11718.htm', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Elias_Boudinot']","In November 1781, he was elected as President of the United States in Congress Assembled, and became the first president (third overall) to serve a one-year term under the provisions of the Articles of Confederation. While George Washington is recognized by historians as the first President of the United States, since he began serving when the current United States Constitution went into effect in 1789, some biographies of Hanson have made arguments that Hanson was actually the first holder of the office of president since he began serving following the first election for a full one-year presidential term once the Articles of Confederation was ratified in 1781.",first president of united states under articles of confederation
what is the average temperature of the pacific ocean,"['https://deepoceanfacts.com/', 'https://academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/Pacific_Ocean', 'http://bdboard.forumotion.com/t484-water-characteristics', 'http://www.lincolnweather.org/Global-Temperature-Anomalies-2010.html', 'http://pheeds.com/info/guide/p/pa/pacific_ocean.html?indexes', 'http://www.wpcouncil.org/managed-fishery-ecosystems/pacific-pelagic/habitat-and-ecosystem-pelagics/', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Pacific_Ocean']","The volume of the Pacific Ocean, representing about 50.1 percent of the world's oceanic water, has been estimated at some 714 million cubic kilometers (171 million cubic miles). Surface water temperatures in the Pacific can vary from − 1.4 ° C (29.5 ° F), the freezing point of sea water, in the poleward areas to about 30 ° C (86 ° F) near the equator. Salinity also varies latitudinally, reaching a maximum of 37 parts per thousand in the southeastern area. The water near the equator, which can have a salinity as low as 34 parts per thousand, is less salty than that found in the mid-latitudes because of abundant equatorial precipitation throughout the year. The lowest counts of less than 32 parts per thousand are found in the far north as less evaporation of seawater takes place in these frigid areas. The motion of Pacific waters is generally clockwise in the Northern Hemisphere (the North Pacific gyre) and counter-clockwise in the Southern Hemisphere. The North Equatorial Current, driven westward along latitude 15 ° N by the trade winds, turns north near the Philippines to become the warm Japan or Kuroshio Current.",what is the average temperature of the pacific ocean
who hit the winning homerun in 1967 all star game,"['http://www.sportspicks.com/mlb-all-star-game-and-second-half-odds', 'http://baseballmlbjersey.biz/tag/trout/', 'https://nesn.com/2017/04/red-sox-notes-rick-porcello-ok-after-near-collision-with-tigers-coach/', 'https://hamptonscript.com/2015/07/15/2015-mlb-all-star-game-spared-by-mother-nature-al-defeats-nl-6-3-to-earn-world-series-advantage/', 'http://www.bluejaysrepublic.com/2017/09/11/quick-reaction-baltimore-orioles-3-toronto-blue-jays-4/', 'https://www.upi.com/Sports_News/MLB/2018/06/22/Nationals-Max-Scherzer-throws-curveball-into-umpires-shirt/3891529677426/?st_rec=1181529762125', 'https://sabr.org/bioproj/person/1c4baf33']","In the top of the 15th inning, Tony Pérez hit a one-out home run off of AL pitcher Catfish Hunter, then in his fifth inning of relief, to give the NL a lead it would not relinquish.",who hit the winning homerun in 1967 all star game
which countries in africa were affected by the arab spring,"['http://www.championnews.com.ng/people-said-no-president-arab-spring-african-political-sentience/', 'https://ipolitics.ca/2019/04/10/glimmers-of-arab-spring-seen-in-algeria-and-sudan/', 'http://tvnewswatch.blogspot.com/2011/12/goodbye-to-disastrous-2011.html', 'http://discountgoldandsilvertrading.net/e-newsletter/dgst-enewsletter-20120328.html', 'http://iosminaret.org/vol-6/issue17/arab_spring.php', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/MENA', 'http://www.rajeevmahajan.com/2016/11/morocco-discovering-its-true-identity.html']","The effects of the Tunisian Revolution spread strongly to five other countries: Libya, Egypt, Yemen, Syria and Bahrain, where either the regime was toppled or major uprisings and social violence occurred, including riots, civil wars or insurgencies. Sustained street demonstrations took place in Morocco, Iraq, Algeria, Iranian Khuzestan, Lebanon, Jordan, Kuwait, Oman and Sudan. Minor protests occurred in Djibouti, Mauritania, the Palestinian National Authority, Saudi Arabia, and the Moroccan-controlled Western Sahara. A major slogan of the demonstrators in the Arab world is ash-shaʻb yurīd isqāṭ an-niẓām (""the people want to bring down the regime"").",which countries in africa were affected by the arab spring
where is windsor castle located on the map,"['https://planergo.com/en/sights/windsor-castle/', 'https://www.wikizero.com/en/Windsor_Castle', 'http://www.castlesandmanorhouses.com/page.php?key=Windsor+Castle']","The Home Park adjoins the northern edge of the more extensive Windsor Great Park, occupying some 5,000 acres (2,020 ha) and including some of the oldest broadleaved woodlands in Europe. In the Home Park, to the north of the castle, stands a private school, St George's, which provides choristers to the chapel. Eton College is located within about half a mile of the castle, across the River Thames.",where is windsor castle located on the map
what is an example of criterion related validity,"['http://www.fitnyc.edu/ccps/courses/credit/mathematics.php', 'http://cpmponline.org/1st/cpmpfaq.html', 'http://circ.communityreport.org/micollegeaccess/reports/26/michigan-data-dashboard-community-report', 'https://collegereadiness.collegeboard.org/about/scores/benchmarks', 'https://catholicedaohct.org/school-resources/test-results', 'http://www.plhs.paplv.org/academics/math/', 'https://fairtest.org/10-myths-about-sat']",An example of concurrent validity is a comparison of the scores of the CLEP College Algebra exam with course grades in college algebra to determine the degree to which scores on the CLEP are related to performance in a college algebra class. An example of predictive validity is a comparison of scores on the SAT with first semester grade point average (GPA) in college; this assesses the degree to which SAT scores are predictive of college performance.,what is an example of criterion related validity
what are the seasons for american horror story,"['https://www.cordcuttingreviews.com/stream-american-horror-story-online/', 'https://cs.wn.com/Craig_Boydston', 'http://yousense.info/3134/00595-american-horror-story-season-3-wallpaper.html', 'http://wholesalehotdvd.com/american-horror-story-seasons-14-dvd-box-set-p-505.html', 'https://www.boonfair.lk/product/american-horror-story/', 'https://candicealexander.com/product/american-horror-story/', 'http://s2verify.info/category/motherboards/']","The first season, retroactively subtitled Murder House, takes place in Los Angeles, California, during the year 2011, and centers on a family that moves into a house haunted by its deceased former occupants. The second season, subtitled Asylum, takes place in Massachusetts during the year 1964, and follows the stories of the patients and staff of an institution for the criminally insane. The third season, subtitled Coven, takes place in New Orleans, Louisiana, during the year 2013, and follows a coven of witches who face off against those who wish to destroy them. The fourth season, subtitled Freak Show, takes place in Jupiter, Florida, during the year 1952, and centers around one of the few remaining American freak shows. The fifth season, subtitled Hotel, takes place in Los Angeles, California, during the year 2015, and focuses on the staff and guests of a supernatural hotel. The sixth season, subtitled Roanoke, takes place in North Carolina during the years 2014 -- 16, and focuses on the paranormal events that take place at an isolated farmhouse haunted by the deceased Roanoke colony. The seventh season, subtitled Cult, takes place in the fictional suburb of Brookfield Heights, Michigan, during the year 2017, and centers on a cult terrorizing the residents in the aftermath of the 2016 U.S. presidential election. The eighth season, subtitled Apocalypse, takes place in the American West Coast during the year 2021, and centers around an outpost sheltering survivors from the fallout of a global nuclear holocaust.",what are the seasons for american horror story
who sang the hit song oliver's army,"['http://borntolisten.com/2017/09/09/20-songs-released-in-1979-you-must-hear/', 'http://rathergood.co.uk/bomb-bass-beat-dis/', 'http://rathergood.co.uk/chris-rea-road-hell/']","""Oliver's Army"" is a song written by Elvis Costello, originally performed by Elvis Costello and The Attractions, and appearing on the album Armed Forces in 1979. It remains his most successful single in the United Kingdom, spending three weeks at number 2 in the UK Singles Chart.",who sang the hit song oliver's army
most common type of virus leading to rhinitis,"['http://blesdeal.com/childrens-cough.html', 'http://www.sundropsonline.com/category_s/191.htm', 'http://www.enetmd.com/content/pneumonia', 'https://bmcinfectdis.biomedcentral.com.preview-live.oscarjournals.springer.com/articles/10.1186/s12879-016-1516-0', 'https://guidelineshealth.com/health-care/top-five-home-remedies-for-common-ailments/', 'https://salinex.ca/health-tips/?article=1', 'https://www.newhealthguide.org/chest-tightness-from-cold.html']","Rhinitis is commonly caused by a viral or bacterial infection, including the common cold, which is caused by Rhinoviruses, Coronaviruses, and influenza viruses, others caused by adenoviruses, human parainfluenza viruses, human respiratory syncytial virus, enteroviruses other than rhinoviruses, metapneumovirus, and measles virus, or bacterial sinusitis, which is commonly caused by Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus influenzae, and Moraxella catarrhalis. Symptoms of the common cold include rhinorrhea, sneezing, sore throat (pharyngitis), cough, congestion, and slight headache.",most common type of virus leading to rhinitis
when did the lion sleeps tonight come out,"['http://mkmmasmilingloudly.loudsmiles.com/mkmma-wk11-i-am-a-lion/', 'https://learningukulele.com/lessons/code/UL104', 'https://www.abqjew.net/2012/09/wimoweh.html', 'http://www.timetravelrecords.co.uk/The-Tokens-The-Lion-Sleeps-Tonight-Wimoweh', 'http://www.bytownukulele.ca/AllPosts/tabid/906/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/325/Lion-Sleeps-Tonight-The.aspx', 'https://sheetmusic-free.com/the-lion-sleeps-tonight-sheet-music-the-lion-king/', 'https://www.eurohitlist.eu/category/hot-100-number-one-singles-of-1962/']","""The Lion Sleeps Tonight"" is a song written and recorded originally by Solomon Linda with the Evening Birds for the South African Gallo Record Company in 1939, under the title ""Mbube"". Composed in Zulu, it was adapted and covered internationally by many 1950s and' 60s pop and folk revival artists, including the Weavers, Jimmy Dorsey, Yma Sumac, Miriam Makeba and the Kingston Trio. In 1961, it became a number one hit in the United States as adapted in English with the best-known version by the doo-wop group the Tokens. It went on to earn at least US $15 million in royalties from cover versions and film licensing. The pop group Tight Fit had a number one hit in the UK with the song in 1982.",when did the lion sleeps tonight come out
what is the concept behind the millennium development goals,"['https://www.accord.org.za/conflict-trends/editorial-2015-3/', 'http://arhr.org.gh/2016/06/15/sustainable-development-goals-achieving-universal-health-coverage-in-ghana-through-primary-health-care/', 'http://web-catalogue.info/60167-hsc4564-budget-essay.html', 'http://textbook.stpauls.br/Development/printview.htm', 'http://gandhiashramsevagram.org/gandhi-articles/managing-rural-economy-in-gandhian-way.php', 'http://georgiajudges.org/millennium-development-project.html', 'https://www.mir-nayka.com/jour/article/view/50']","The MDGs originated from the United Nations Millennium Declaration. The Declaration asserted that every individual has dignity; and hence, the right to freedom, equality, a basic standard of living that includes freedom from hunger and violence and encourages tolerance and solidarity. The MDGs set concrete targets and indicators for poverty reduction in order to achieve the rights set forth in the Declaration.",what is the concept behind the millennium development goals
where is the next world cup held in 2030,"['http://blog.naadle.com/fifa-2018/', 'http://iksourceful.info/67413-huawei-p10-price-in-bangladesh.html']","The bidding procedure has not yet started, and these are the countries that confirmed an interest of hosting the 2030 FIFA World Cup.",where is the next world cup held in 2030
ppp theory predicts that foreign exchange rates are determined by,"['http://ccaconf.org/thesis-purchasing-power-parity.php', 'http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/Purchasing_power_parity', 'https://www.stat.fi/meta/kas/index_en.html?P', 'http://baby-387.info/llll/purchasing-power-parity-exchange-rate-sugy.php', 'https://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/publications/economic-letter/2000/february/do-currency-unions-increase-trade-a-gravity-approach/', 'http://piglix.com/piglix/Purchasing_power_parity', 'https://mymemory.translated.net/de/Englisch/Tagalog/disruption-of-production']","Purchasing power parity (PPP) is a neoclassical economic theory that states that the exchange rate between two countries is equal to the ratio of the currencies' respective purchasing power. Theories that invoke the purchasing power parity assume that in some circumstances (for example, as a long-run tendency) it would cost exactly the same number of, for example, US dollars to buy euros and then buy a market basket of goods as it would cost to directly purchase the market basket of goods with dollars. A fall in either currency's purchasing power would lead to a proportional decrease in that currency's valuation on the foreign exchange market.",ppp theory predicts that foreign exchange rates are determined by
what is a cas number on an msds,"['https://en.unionpedia.org/Trimethoxyamphetamine', 'https://www.ukfrs.com/glossary?q=/glossary&name=&field_acronym_value=&description__value=&items_per_page=25&page=1', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/109641', 'http://tw-shop.info/?page_id=46006', 'http://grease-musical.tk/azepine-msds-sheets.html', 'https://newsletter.echa.europa.eu/home/-/newsletter/entry/3_14_is-the-substance-identifier-in-your-registration-correct', 'http://directio12.tk/azepine-msds-sheets.html']","A CAS Registry Number, also referred to as CASRN or CAS Number, is a unique numerical identifier assigned by the Chemical Abstracts Service (CAS) to every chemical substance described in the open scientific literature (currently including those described from at least 1957 through the present), including organic and inorganic compounds, minerals, isotopes, alloys and nonstructurable materials (UVCBs, of unknown, variable composition, or biological origin).",what is a cas number on an msds
who named jupiter and what does it mean,"['https://www.manualidadesaraudales.com/2015/07/25/maqueta-3d-imprimible-del-planeta-jupiter/', 'https://codepoints.net/U+2643', 'https://www.rhyeen.com/other/solar-system/jupiter/index.html', 'http://wkberg.nl/jupiter.php', 'http://angoisso.tk/adrastea-moon-facts-sheet.html', 'http://www.boulderweather.org/template/plugins/solarSystem/index.php', 'https://www.thecelestialsolarsystem.com/jupiter.html']","Jupiter is the fifth planet from the Sun and the largest in the Solar System. It is a giant planet with a mass one-thousandth that of the Sun, but two-and-a-half times that of all the other planets in the Solar System combined. Jupiter and Saturn are gas giants; the other two giant planets, Uranus and Neptune are ice giants. Jupiter has been known to astronomers since antiquity. The Romans named it after their god Jupiter. When viewed from Earth, Jupiter can reach an apparent magnitude of − 2.94, bright enough for its reflected light to cast shadows, and making it on average the third-brightest object in the night sky after the Moon and Venus.",who named jupiter and what does it mean
what is the purpose of the alien tort claims act,"['https://www.sungazette.com/opinion/other-commentaries/2018/05/does-the-supreme-court-protect-terrorists/', 'https://www.ecocitytvnews.com.ng/2018/02/panic-in-nigeria-judiciary-as-ipob.html', 'http://www.lawschoolcasebriefs.net/2011/09/filartiga-v-pena-irala-case-brief-630.html', 'https://politicsofpoverty.oxfamamerica.org/2014/09/child-laborers-bring-case-food-companies-youre-enabling-enslavement/', 'https://www.theatlantic.com/national/archive/2011/11/how-suing-shell-could-backfire-on-human-rights-activists/248606/', 'https://www.wiggin.com/news/high-court-to-consider-arrests-abroad-alien-tort-act-used-in-war-on-terrorism-suits-for-damages-in-human-rights-cases/', 'https://www.harvard-jlpp.com/supreme-court-poised-to-reduce-american-involvement-in-foreign-human-rights-cases/']","The Alien Tort Statute (28 U.S.C. § 1350; ATS), also called the Alien Tort Claims Act (ATCA), is a section of the United States Code that reads: ""The district courts shall have original jurisdiction of any civil action by an alien for a tort only, committed in violation of the law of nations or a treaty of the United States."" Since 1980, courts have interpreted this statute to allow foreign citizens to seek remedies in U.S. courts for human-rights violations for conduct committed outside the United States.",what is the purpose of the alien tort claims act
the eighth amendment to the constitution deals largely with the issue of,"['https://mmabbasi.com/2010/08/23/yes-the-taliban-and-the-lynch-mob-were-muslims/', 'http://www.amendments1-27.com/2nd-amendment/', 'https://www.msbonding.com/blog/right-bail', 'http://accreditedbail.blogspot.com/2010/12/pretrial-release-using-proven-methods.html', 'https://allenpc.com/', 'https://legaldictionary.net/8th-amendment/', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=examples+of+8th+amendment+violations&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir']","The Eighth Amendment (Amendment VIII) of the United States Constitution prohibits the federal government from imposing excessive bail, excessive fines, or cruel and unusual punishments. The U.S. Supreme Court has ruled that this amendment's Cruel and Unusual Punishment Clause also applies to the states. The phrases in this amendment originated in the English Bill of Rights of 1689. This amendment was adopted on December 15, 1791, along with the rest of the United States Bill of Rights.",the eighth amendment to the constitution deals largely with the issue of
how deep is the deepest part of the dead sea,"['https://travel.siliconindia.com/travel-article/The-Dead-Sea-Israel-aid-4747.html', 'http://www.jordantowerhotel.com/miscellaneous-interests', 'http://xautoman.com/3486-whyistheresomuchsaltinthedeadsea.html', 'http://www.easy-car-rental.com/index.php/ar/component/content/article/34-easy-rentals-/92-dead-sea-cheap-rentals', 'https://nature.new7wonders.com/wonders/dead-sea-israel-jordan-palestine', 'http://brandweermiddendelfland.info/search?q=Dead%20sea%20mud%20spa', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/dead-sea']","The Dead Sea (Hebrew: יָם הַמֶּלַח ‎ Yam ha-Melah lit. Salt Sea; Arabic: البحر الميت ‎ ‎ Al-Bahr al-Mayyit) is a salt lake bordered by Jordan to the east and Israel and Palestine to the west. Its surface and shores are 430.5 metres (1,412 ft) below sea level, Earth's lowest elevation on land. The Dead Sea is 304 m (997 ft) deep, the deepest hypersaline lake in the world. With a salinity of 342 g / kg, or 34.2%, (in 2011), it is 9.6 times as salty as the ocean and one of the world's saltiest bodies of water. This salinity makes for a harsh environment in which plants and animals cannot flourish, hence its name. The Dead Sea is 50 kilometres (31 mi) long and 15 kilometres (9 mi) wide at its widest point. It lies in the Jordan Rift Valley, and its main tributary is the Jordan River.",how deep is the deepest part of the dead sea
what is the difference between sahel and sahara,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Werner_Bardenhewer', 'https://www.greenoptimistic.com/african-desert-great-green-wall-20190411/', 'https://oneworldrotary.org/Stories/treeline-in-sahel', 'https://human.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/History/Book%3A_World_History_(Boundless)/Chapter_16%3A_African_Civilizations/Section_4%3A_West_African_Empires', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Sudan_(region)', 'https://wikimili.com/en/White_settlement_in_Zimbabwe_before_1923', 'https://sites.uni.edu/becker/Swahili.html']","The Sahel (/ səˈhɛl /) is the ecoclimatic and biogeographic zone of transition in Africa between the Sahara to the north and the Sudanian Savanna to the south. Having a semi-arid climate, it stretches across the south-central latitudes of Northern Africa between the Atlantic Ocean and the Red Sea. The name is derived from the Arabic word sāḥil (ساحل, Arabic pronunciation: (ˈsaːħil)) meaning ""coast"" or ""shore"" in a figurative sense (in reference to the southern edge of the vast Sahara), while the name Swahili means ""coastal (dweller)"" in a literal sense.",what is the difference between sahel and sahara
who played the joker in the dark knight,"['https://watchmoviesnow.co/actor/heath-ledger/', 'https://jiji-blog.com/2018/08/26-incredible-persons-from-australia/', 'http://www.michaelkorsoutletninc.com/2018/10/heath-andrew-ledger_3.html', 'http://hrvcanada.blogspot.com/2011/12/heath-ledger.html', 'https://targetedindividualscanada.com/2011/12/30/heath-ledger/', 'http://fizzshevzenko.blogspot.com/2009/04/blog-post_20.html?widgetType=BlogArchive&widgetId=BlogArchive1&action=toggle&dir=open&toggle=MONTHLY-1233475200000&toggleopen=MONTHLY-1238569200000', 'https://celebsline.com/jamie-foxx/']","Ledger died on 22 January 2008 from an accidental intoxication from prescription drugs. A few months before his death, Ledger had finished filming his performance as the Joker in The Dark Knight. His death occurred during editing of The Dark Knight and in the midst of filming his last role as Tony in The Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus. His untimely death cast a shadow over the subsequent promotion of the $185 million Batman production. Ledger received numerous posthumous accolades for his critically acclaimed performance in the film, including the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, a Best Actor International Award at the 2008 Australian Film Institute Awards (for which he became the first actor to win an award posthumously), the 2008 Los Angeles Film Critics Association Award for Best Supporting Actor, the 2009 Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor -- Motion Picture, and the 2009 BAFTA Award for Best Supporting Actor.",who plays the joker in batman the dark knight
what kind of food is san diego known for,"['http://footwww.academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/San_Diego%2C_California', 'https://triplelights.com/japan/tour/hokkaido-besthakodatepanoramic-view-from-mt-hakodate-814', 'http://www.terrytreks.com/blog/quy-nhon-a-pleasant-seaside-city/', 'https://sharedreviews.com/review/myrtle-beach-south-carolina', 'https://carriedaway.blogs.com/carried_away/business_and_finance/', 'https://www.iceland-vacation-information.com/icelandic-restaurants.html', 'http://visitroo.com/place/Xpu_Ha_Beach_1435']","Because of its ethnic and cultural mix, San Diego has a wide range of cuisines. One can find Mexican, Italian, French, Spanish, Filipino, Vietnamese, Greek, Latin, German, Indian, Central and East Asian, Middle Eastern and Pacific Islander food throughout the city. In addition, there are numerous seafood restaurants and steakhouses. The city's long history and close proximity to Mexico has endowed the area with an extensive variety of authentic Mexican restaurants. Regional homemade specialties, border fare and haute cuisine are all readily available.",what kind of food is san diego known for
rita ora i will never let you down wiki,"['http://codigobarras.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=39464', 'http://side-3.info/viewtopic.php?t=25571', 'http://einfach-reisen.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=45326', 'http://mariboo.info/viewtopic.php?t=25032', 'http://vintagesilverplateflatware.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=20124', 'http://arv8.info/viewtopic.php?t=48492', 'http://adu-edsa1.info/news.php?action=show&id=19230']","""I Will Never Let You Down"" is a song by British singer Rita Ora, released on 31 March 2014, through Roc Nation and Columbia Records. The song debuted at number one on the UK Singles Chart, making it Ora's fourth overall UK number-one single (and third as a solo artist) within three years.",rita ora i will never let you down wiki
why do we celebrate independence day and republic day,"['https://www.fashionsky.in/republic-day-of-india-26-january-fashion/', 'https://www.blogsguru.net/2019/01/26th-january-republic-day-wishing-script.html', 'http://cutewallpaper4all.blogspot.com/2015/01/republic-day-messages-wallpaper-sms.html', 'https://indroyc.com/2017/01/26/republic-day-2017/', 'https://www.updateyou.in/2019/01/Republic-day-celebration-70th.html', 'https://happyrepublicday2019.com/celebrating-70th-republic-day.html', 'https://www.ritiriwaz.com/26-january-republic-day-of-india/']","India achieved independence from British Raj on 15 August 1947 following the Indian independence movement noted for largely peaceful non-violent resistance and civil disobedience led by Mahatma Gandhi. The independence came through the Indian Independence Act 1947 (10 & 11 Geo 6 c 30), an Act of the Parliament of the United Kingdom that partitioned British India into the two new independent Dominions of the British Commonwealth (later Commonwealth of Nations). India obtained its independence on 15 August 1947 as a constitutional monarchy with George VI as head of state and the Earl Mountbatten as governor-general. The country, though, did not yet have a permanent constitution; instead its laws were based on the modified colonial Government of India Act 1935. On 28 August 1947, the Drafting Committee was appointed to draft a permanent constitution, with Dr BR Ambedkar as chairman. While India's Independence Day celebrates its freedom from British Rule, the Republic Day celebrates the coming into force of its constitution. A draft constitution was prepared by the committee and submitted to the Constituent Assembly on 4 November 1947. The Assembly met, in sessions open to public, for 166 days, spread over a period of two years, 11 months and 18 days before adopting the Constitution. After many deliberations and some modifications, the 308 members of the Assembly signed two hand-written copies of the document (one each in Hindi and English) on 24 January 1950. Two days later which was on 26 January 1950, it came into effect throughout the whole nation. On that day began Dr. Rajendra Prasad's first term of office as President of the Indian Union. The Constituent Assembly became the Parliament of India under the transitional provisions of the new Constitution. This date is celebrated in India as the Republic Day.",why do we celebrate independence day and republic day
which member of the beatles is still alive,"['http://autographexamples.com/music/the-beatles/', 'https://www.rockarchive.com/artists/b/beatles-the', 'https://www.wallpaperpimper.com/people/artists/the-beatles', 'https://www.coverium.com/music-video/the-beatles-and-your-bird-can-sing-vocal-cover-by-sgtfolker/FgW-sj8kO9o', 'https://consequenceofsound.net/artist/the-beatles/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=slideshowlondon.com&ads=1&title=Slideshow+london&auto=Slideshow+london&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Slideshow+london&pagenum=2', 'http://mahmoodtabrizi.com/the-beatles-painting/']","The Beatles built their reputation playing clubs in Liverpool and Hamburg over a three-year period from 1960, with Stuart Sutcliffe initially serving as bass player. The core trio of Lennon, McCartney and Harrison, together since 1958, went through a succession of drummers, including Pete Best, before asking Starr to join them in 1962. Manager Brian Epstein moulded them into a professional act, and producer George Martin guided and developed their recordings, greatly expanding the group's popularity in the United Kingdom after their first hit, ""Love Me Do"", in late 1962. They acquired the nickname ""the Fab Four"" as Beatlemania grew in Britain over the next year, and by early 1964 became international stars, leading the ""British Invasion"" of the United States pop market. From 1965 onwards, the Beatles produced increasingly innovative recordings, including the albums Rubber Soul (1965), Revolver (1966), Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band (1967), The Beatles (also known as the ""White Album"", 1968) and Abbey Road (1969). After their break-up in 1970, they each enjoyed success as solo artists. Lennon was shot and killed in December 1980, and Harrison died of lung cancer in November 2001. McCartney and Starr remain musically active.",which member of the beatles is still alive
what is the chemical composition of hydrogen peroxide,"['https://www.dutch2.com/chemical-products/others/hydrogen-peroxide-35/', 'http://generik.tk/msds-sheet-for-hydrogen-peroxide.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Chemical_formula', 'http://m.wfrichem.com/news/buyhydrogenperoxideatthebestpricefromchinasupp-9683001.html', 'http://www.howtogetridofgnat.com/2015/04/how-to-kill-fungus-gnat-using-hydrogen-peroxide-insecticide.html?replytocom=2919', 'https://www.myhealthstep.com/how-to-whiten-yellow-stained-teeth/', 'http://infinitedomination.tk/hydrogen-gas-msds-sheet.html']","Hydrogen peroxide is a chemical compound with the formula H O. In its pure form, it is a pale blue, clear liquid, slightly more viscous than water. Hydrogen peroxide is the simplest peroxide (a compound with an oxygen -- oxygen single bond). It is used as an oxidizer, bleaching agent and antiseptic. Concentrated hydrogen peroxide, or ""high-test peroxide"", is a reactive oxygen species and has been used as a propellant in rocketry. Its chemistry is dominated by the nature of its unstable peroxide bond.",what is the chemical composition of hydrogen peroxide
who won the grey cup the most times,"['http://jamesalexandermichie.com/the-gray-cup-week-and-its-impact-national-post/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Robert_C._Wetenhall', 'https://losangelesseo5.info/horses-in-the-fog-by-allan-wallberg-photographic-print-on-wrapped-canvas.htm', 'https://news.wagertalk.com/cfl/odds-to-win-106th-grey-cup-september-10-2018', 'https://www.thechampionrings.com/other-champions-rings/cfl-grey-cup-rings.html', 'http://www.reston-connection.com/photos/2017/jul/31/119456/', 'https://thenewyorkclipper.com/photo/calgary-launch-of-miss-confederation-the-diary-of-mercy.html']","The Grey Cup (French: Coupe Grey) is the name of both the championship game of the Canadian Football League (CFL) and the trophy awarded to the victorious team playing Canadian football. It is contested between the winners of the CFL's East and West Divisional playoffs and is one of Canadian television's largest annual sporting events. The Toronto Argonauts have the most Grey Cup wins (17) since its introduction in 1909, while the Edmonton Eskimos have the most Grey Cup wins (11) since the creation of the professional CFL in 1958. The latest, the 105th Grey Cup, took place in Ottawa, Ontario, on November 26, 2017, when the Toronto Argonauts defeated the Calgary Stampeders 27-24.",who won the grey cup the most times
where is malta on the map of europe,"['https://www.know.cf/enciclopedia/en/Malta', 'http://www.mapnall.com/en/language/English-language_444.html', 'https://realtyww.info/search/country,MT/category,100', 'http://www.ashleycorr.com/malta/4594314897', 'https://www.avenuesabroad.in/our_service/malta/', 'https://www.travelerbase.com/index.php?proc=search&term=10%20Best%20Places%20to%20Visit%20in%20Malta', 'https://simonsblogpark.com/onlinegambling/simons-malta-gambling-guide/']","Malta (/ ˈmɒltə, ˈmɔːl-/ (listen); Maltese: (ˈmɐltɐ)), officially known as the Republic of Malta (Maltese: Repubblika ta' Malta), is a Southern European island country consisting of an archipelago in the Mediterranean Sea. It lies 80 km (50 mi) south of Italy, 284 km (176 mi) east of Tunisia, and 333 km (207 mi) north of Libya. Malta is one of the world's smallest and most densely populated countries, at over 316 km (122 sq mi) with a population of about 475,000. Its capital is Valletta, which is the smallest national capital in the European Union by area at 0.8 km. Its largest town is Birkirkara, while its chief economic centre is Sliema. The official languages are Maltese and English, with Maltese also recognised as the national language. Maltese is the only Semitic language to be officially recognised in the European Union. Italian is also spoken by most of the population.",where is malta on the map of europe
what is the meaning of the parable of ten virgins,"['http://www.liturgytools.net/2017/11/hymns-parable-wise-and-foolish-virgins-bridesmaids-women-be-prepared-for-when-the-master-comes.html', 'https://greekcitytimes.com/2018/04/03/holy-tuesday-of-holy-week/', 'http://eternalcall.com/blog/page/2/', 'http://www.religiousdoodles.com/ten-virgins-coloring-pages.html', 'http://christianitymalaysia.com/wp/rapture-coming-christ-prepare-pr-george-dass/', 'https://theheavensdeclare.net/the-five-wise-virgins-stars/', 'http://bhmcatholic.com/category/blog/eucharistic-congress']","The Parable of the Ten Virgins, also known as the Parable of the Wise and Foolish Virgins or the Parable of the ten bridesmaids, is one of the well known parables of Jesus. According to the Gospel of Matthew 25: 1-13, the five virgins who are prepared for the bridegroom's arrival are rewarded, while the five who are not prepared are disowned. The parable has a clear eschatological theme: be prepared for the Day of Judgment. It was one of the most popular parables in the Middle Ages, with enormous influence on Gothic art, sculpture and the architecture of German and French cathedrals.",what is the meaning of the parable of ten virgins
where did the song silent night come from,"['https://learningukulele.com/songs?page=2', 'http://www.20thcenturybattles.com/songs-of-the-first-world-war/', 'http://hiwarat-hurra.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=25248', 'https://andantemoderato.com/christmas-in-vienna-2008-full/', 'https://gingergarner.com/vocal-meditations-for-the-christmas-season/', 'https://superioracademyofmusic.com/evolution-holiday-music/', 'https://fretello.com/12-christmas-songs-you-should-learn/']","""Silent Night"" (German: Stille Nacht, heilige Nacht) is a popular Christmas carol, composed in 1818 by Franz Xaver Gruber to lyrics by Joseph Mohr in the small town of Oberndorf bei Salzburg, Austria. It was declared an intangible cultural heritage by UNESCO in 2011. The song has been recorded by a large number of singers from every music genre. The version sung by Bing Crosby is the third best-selling single of all-time.",where did the song silent night come from
where does elf on the shelf come from,"['https://www.upnorthparent.com/interesting-backstory-elf-on-the-shelf-holiday-tradition/', 'https://criticsrant.com/how-the-heck-did-elf-on-the-shelf-get-started/', 'http://redlightsocial.ml/how-to-elf-on-the-shelf-xup.php']","The Elf on the Shelf was written in 2004 by Carol Aebersold and daughter Chanda Bell over a cup of tea. Bell suggested they write a book about an old tradition of an elf sent from Santa who came to watch over them at Christmas time. Aebersold's other daughter, Christa Pitts, was recruited by the family to share her expertise in sales and marketing. Together, the trio devoted the next three years promoting their self-published book and attending book signings and trade shows.",where does elf on the shelf come from
when did the titanic sink exact date and time,"['http://www.veus-shipping.com/2017/04/105-years-ago-sinking-of-rms-titanic-on-14-april-1912/', 'https://kiwidutch.wordpress.com/category/art/lego/', 'https://radiochatter.wordpress.com/2016/10/10/sinking-of-the-titanic-now-in-real-time/', 'http://leehernly.me/2019/04/otd-in-1912-titanic-sinks-on-her-maiden-voyage/', 'https://majormike.us/subjects/1912/', 'https://maritimecyprus.com/2019/04/15/flashback-in-maritime-history-sinking-of-rms-titanic-on-14-april-1912-2/', 'https://www.scgniagara.com/2017/04/']","RMS Titanic sank in the early morning of 15 April 1912 in the North Atlantic Ocean, four days into the ship's maiden voyage from Southampton to New York City. The largest passenger liner in service at the time, Titanic had an estimated 2,224 people on board when she struck an iceberg at around 23: 40 (ship's time) on Sunday, 14 April 1912. Her sinking two hours and forty minutes later at 02: 20 (ship's time; 05: 18 GMT) on Monday, 15 April, resulted in the deaths of more than 1,500 people, which made it one of the deadliest peacetime maritime disasters in history.",when did the titanic sink exact date and time
who's playing in the world cup finale,"['https://b2b.partcommunity.com/community/knowledge/en/index/page/2', 'https://asiavpn.blogspot.com/2018/07/how-to-watch-2018-fifa-world-cup-final.html', 'http://getlatestbuzz.com/top-10-important-events-of-2018/', 'https://amarkhata.com/final-photos-fifa-2018-world-cup/', 'https://www.bestinsurancelaredo.com/tips-for-installing-a-patio-covers-images/wattpad-patio-covers-images/', 'https://live2soccer.com/russia-vs-saudi-arabia-live-india-world-cup-2018-telecast/', 'http://wickedtoplesswe.cf/pujem/score-rugby-world-cup-final-2018-myzo.php']","The 2018 FIFA World Cup Final was a football match that took place on 15 July 2018 to determine the winners of the 2018 FIFA World Cup. It was the final of the 21st FIFA World Cup, a quadrennial tournament contested by the men's national teams of the member associations of FIFA. The match was contested by France and Croatia, and held at the Luzhniki Stadium in Moscow, Russia.",who's playing in the world cup finale
when does a concussion become post concussion syndrome,"['http://www.personaltrainingandwellness.com/blog/2016/9/12/9acuu6e0qitfln3f6vrwfq2wiebmgp', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/Post-concussion_syndrome', 'https://www.atlasspinalcare.com/post-concussion-syndrome-contact-sports-upper-neck/', 'https://hellodoktor.com/disease/post-concussion-syndrome/', 'https://jplagaceod.wordpress.com/2015/11/24/concussions-and-vision-2/', 'http://www.liebellclinic.com/post-concussion-syndrome.html', 'https://www.healthline.com/health/post-concussion-syndrome']","Post-concussion syndrome, also known as postconcussive syndrome or PCS, is a set of symptoms that may continue for weeks, months, or a year or more after a concussion -- a mild form of traumatic brain injury (TBI). The rates of PCS vary, but most studies report that about 15% of individuals with a history of a single concussion develop persistent symptoms associated with the injury. A diagnosis may be made when symptoms resulting from concussion last for more than three months after the injury. Loss of consciousness is not required for a diagnosis of concussion or post-concussion syndrome.",when does a concussion become post concussion syndrome
where do animals and plants get the oxygen from in the aquatic environment,"['http://animalia.bio/aquatic-animals', 'http://microcosmevent.org/pond-building-guide', 'http://bestcoloringpages.com/animals-coloring-pages_1c19.html', 'https://exclusivepapers.com/essays/classification/classification-of-food.php', 'http://www.imedpub.com/scholarly/aquatic-plants-and-animals-journals-articles-ppts-list.php', 'http://top-10-list.org/tag/dangerous/', 'http://www.leereich.com/2011/09/as-curtain-slowly-closes-on-summer.html']","An aquatic animal is an animal, either vertebrate or invertebrate, which lives in the water for most or all of its lifetime. Many insects such as mosquitoes, mayflies, dragonflies and caddisflies have aquatic larvae, with winged adults. Aquatic animals may breathe air or extract oxygen that dissolved in water through specialised organs called gills, or directly through the skin. Natural environments and the animals that live in them can be categorized as aquatic (water) or terrestrial (land).",where do animals and plants get the oxygen from in the aquatic environment
who were the two opposing sides in the civil war,"['https://peegel.info/lk/the-issue-with-the-flag/', 'https://www.blackfacts.com/fact/american-civil-war', 'https://wikimili.com/en/1890_United_States_Census', 'https://www.freedomcircle.com/topic/american-war-between-states', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Infantry_in_the_American_Civil_War', 'http://www.civilwardocs.com/', 'https://post532.org/american-wars-page-1']","The American Civil War was fought in the United States from 1861 to 1865. The result of a long-standing controversy over slavery, war broke out in April 1861, when Confederates attacked Fort Sumter in South Carolina, shortly after President Abraham Lincoln was inaugurated. The nationalists of the Union proclaimed loyalty to the U.S. Constitution. They faced secessionists of the Confederate States, who advocated for states' rights to expand slavery.",who were the two opposing sides in the civil war
who has won the most trophies messi or ronaldo,"['https://franknaija.com/how-many-awards-does-messi-and-ronaldo-have/', 'http://wap.codedfilm.com/download/lionel-messi-vs-cristiano-ronaldo-vs-zlatan-ibrahimovic---despacito---the-greatest/w8YnLxJc4hE', 'https://pommiers.eu/vergleich-messi-ronaldo.html', 'http://www.arturofuerte.com/messi-vs-ronaldo/', 'http://greyhoundscansit.com/g4lj4j2i4.html', 'https://www.fifaworldcupnews.com/cristiano-ronaldo-vs-lionel-messi-vs-neymar-2018/', 'http://legendshub.com/Lionel-Messi/']","The Messi -- Ronaldo rivalry is a football rivalry between fans of Argentinian forward Lionel Messi and Portuguese forward Cristiano Ronaldo and supposedly between the athletes themselves. Having won a combined ten Ballon d'Or / FIFA Ballon d'Or awards (5 each), both are widely regarded not only as the two best players of their generation, but also regarded by many as the greatest of all time. Both players have regularly broken the 50 goal barrier in a single season and have scored over 600 goals each in their careers for club and country. Sports journalists and pundits regularly argue the individual merits of both players in an attempt to establish who they believe is the best player in modern football. It has been compared to past global sports rivalries such as the Muhammad Ali -- Joe Frazier rivalry in boxing, the Björn Borg -- John McEnroe rivalry in tennis and the Ayrton Senna -- Alain Prost rivalry in Formula One motor racing.",who has won the most trophies messi or ronaldo
