what ship did they use in the movie titanic,"['http://answers.jahirol.com/4788/live-%24streaming-watch-titanic-1997-online-free', 'https://mevidur.wordpress.com/category/vidurs-random-musings/miscellaneous/', 'https://moremoviedetails.com/titanic/', 'http://www.simplymarrimye.com/', 'http://sw.fanpop.com/clubs/titanic/articles', 'http://www.currentaffairs24x7.com/leonardo-di-caprio-star-of-hollywood/', 'http://carsandinsurance.info/gambling/james-davenport-poker.php']","Cameron's inspiration for the film came from his fascination with shipwrecks; he felt a love story interspersed with the human loss would be essential to convey the emotional impact of the disaster. Production began in 1995, when Cameron shot footage of the actual Titanic wreck. The modern scenes on the research vessel were shot on board the Akademik Mstislav Keldysh, which Cameron had used as a base when filming the wreck. Scale models, computer-generated imagery, and a reconstruction of the Titanic built at Baja Studios, at Playas de Rosarito in Baja California were used to re-create the sinking. The film was partially funded by Paramount Pictures and 20th Century Fox. It was the most expensive film ever made at the time, with a production budget of $200 million.",what ship did they use in the movie titanic
who does the voice of soos in gravity falls,"['https://celebbodysize.com/alex-hirsch-net-worth-know-twitter-new-show/', 'https://articlebio.com/alex-hirsch', 'https://www.shoutfactory.com/blog/gravity-falls-the-complete-series-beloved-disney-series-available-as-a-complete-series-box-set/comment-page-1/', 'https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/2016/08/first-live-action-pokemon-movie-enlists-guardians-of-the-galaxy-gravity-falls-writers', 'https://allmyfriendsarerighthere.com/2016/02/28/that-was-a-game-008-disney-infinity-3-0/']","Hirsch is most known for creating the series Gravity Falls for the Disney Channel. He provided the voice of Grunkle Stan, Soos, Old Man McGucket and Bill Cipher, as well as many other minor characters featured throughout the show.",who does the voice of soos in gravity falls
where is the euphrates river located on a world map,"['https://studyres.com/concepts/5355/euphrates', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Euphrates', 'http://spitfirephoto.com/tigris-and-euphrates-river-rap.html', 'https://www.erickbonnier-pictures.com/reports-travels/syria-along-the-euphrat-river/', 'http://apps.evemilano.com/entities/?query=euphrates', 'https://water.fanack.com/tag/euphrates/', 'https://search.credoreference.com/content/topic/euphrates']","The Euphrates (/ juː ˈfreɪtiːz / (listen); Sumerian: 𒌓𒄒𒉣 Buranuna, Akkadian: 𒌓𒄒𒉣 Purattu, Arabic: الفرات ‎ al-Furāt, Syriac: ̇ܦܪܬ ‎ Pǝrāt, Armenian: Եփրատ: Yeprat, Hebrew: פרת ‎ Perat, Turkish: Fırat, Kurdish: Firat ‎) is the longest and one of the most historically important rivers of Western Asia. Together with the Tigris, it is one of the two defining rivers of Mesopotamia (the ""Land between the Rivers""). Originating in eastern Turkey, the Euphrates flows through Syria and Iraq to join the Tigris in the Shatt al-Arab, which empties into the Persian Gulf.",where is the euphrates river located on a world map
who is in charge of the executive branch in texas,"['http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Texas', 'https://accidentpersonalinjurylawyers.com/find-lawyers-by-state/texas-personal-injury/', 'https://www.hgh.tv/usa-hgh-clinics/texas/dallas.php', 'http://www.samarthyam.org/academic-essay-example-on-the-topic-of-texas-government', 'https://alchetron.com/Texas', 'https://www.natlawreview.com/jurisdiction/all-states/texas', 'https://quizlet.com/216654402/texes-core-subjects-4-8-social-studies-flash-cards/']","The executive branch consists of the Governor, Lieutenant Governor, Comptroller of Public Accounts, Land Commissioner, Attorney General, Agriculture Commissioner, the three-member Texas Railroad Commission, the State Board of Education, and the Secretary of State. Texas has a plural executive branch system which limits the power of the Governor. Except for the Secretary of State, all executive officers are elected independently making them directly answerable to the public, not the Governor.",who is in charge of the executive branch in texas
where does billy costigan live in the film the depart what is the city,"['http://www.movie-mine.com/mm_info.php?/en/the_departed', 'http://www.articlesphere.com/Article/-The-Departed--Is-Best-Mob-Film-Since-Mario-Puzo-s--The-Godfather--In-1972/97909', 'https://www.reelmatt.com/2013/03/21/being-flynn.html', 'https://www.moviefone.com/photos/14-thrillers-based-on-real-life-crimes/', 'https://www.apluscollegeescorts.com/top-20-boston-films/', 'https://www.stmvirgin.org/the-angelus-our-newsletter/2016/8/8/from-the-rector-real-change-volume-18-number-35-july-24-2016']","The film takes place in Boston. Irish Mob boss Francis ""Frank"" Costello (Jack Nicholson) plants Colin Sullivan (Matt Damon) as a mole within the Massachusetts State Police; the two characters are loosely based on famous gangster Whitey Bulger and corrupt FBI agent John Connolly, who grew up with Bulger. Simultaneously, the police assign undercover state trooper William ""Billy"" Costigan (Leonardo DiCaprio) to infiltrate Costello's crew. When both sides realize the situation, Sullivan and Costigan both attempt to discover the other's identity before their covers are blown.",where does billy costigan live in the film the depart what is the city
where did the saying see a man about a dog come from,['http://jeffreymillerwrites.com/im-going-to-see-a-man-about-a-horse/'],"The earliest confirmed publication is the 1866 Dion Boucicault play Flying Scud in which a character knowingly breezes past a difficult situation saying, ""Excuse me Mr. Quail, I can't stop; I've got to see a man about a dog."" In a listing for a 1939 revival on the NBC Radio program America's Lost Plays, Time magazine observed that the phrase was the play's ""claim to fame"".",where did the saying see a man about a dog come from
who played maya on the suite life on deck,['https://craytel.fandom.com/wiki/Zoey_Deutch'],"Deutch began her career in 2010, at the age of 15, with a role on the Disney Channel original series The Suite Life on Deck as Maya, Zack Martin's love interest.",who played maya on the suite life on deck
where is vanuatu located on the world map,"['https://thereefexplorervanuatu.com/vanuatu-day-trips/', 'https://weblogtheworld.com/countries/pacific/vanuatu/vanuatu-history-culture-and-economy', 'http://bestplacesonearth.net/beautiful-planet/most-expensive-destinations/', 'https://www.asisbiz.com/Vanuatu.html', 'http://www.statemaster.com/encyclopedia/Pacific', 'https://revenuereview.gov.vu/index.php/en/auto-generate-from-title', 'http://www.citiesandplaces.com/where-is-vanuatu-located-on-the-world-map/']","Vanuatu (English: / ˌvɑːnuˈɑːtuː / (listen) VAH-noo-AH-too or / vænˈwɑːtuː / van-WAH-too; Bislama, French IPA: (vanuatu)), officially the Republic of Vanuatu (French: République de Vanuatu, Bislama: Ripablik blong Vanuatu), is a Pacific island nation located in the South Pacific Ocean. The archipelago, which is of volcanic origin, is 1,750 kilometres (1,090 mi) east of northern Australia, 540 kilometres (340 mi) northeast of New Caledonia, east of New Guinea, southeast of the Solomon Islands, and west of Fiji.",where is vanuatu located on the world map
who is the saint lawrence river named after,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Saint_Lawrence_River', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Saint_Lawrence_River', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Drainage_basin']","Though the Norse explored the Gulf of Saint Lawrence in the 11th century and were followed by fifteenth and early sixteenth century European mariners, such as John Cabot, the brothers Gaspar, Miguel Corte-Real, and Alonso Sanchez, the first European explorer known to have sailed up the Saint Lawrence River itself was Jacques Cartier. At that time, the land along the river was inhabited by the St. Lawrence Iroquoians; at the time of Cartier's second voyage in 1535. Because Cartier arrived in the estuary on Saint Lawrence's feast day, he named it the Gulf of Saint Lawrence. The Saint Lawrence River is partly within the U.S. and as such is that country's sixth oldest surviving European place-name.",who is the saint lawrence river named after
where is jamaica situated on the world map,"['http://www.easybranches.pro/yachts/destinations/caribbean-bahamas/', 'http://onlinedivecenter.com/listing-location/?acadp_location=jamaica', 'http://www.mapnall.com/en/language/English-language_444.html', 'https://ca.answers.yahoo.com/question/index?qid=20190227101105AAs2AjY', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/jamaica', 'http://www.excursionesjamaica.com/latest-offer-title-one/', 'http://www.xtremespots.com/water-sports/scuba-diving/tug-boat-negril-jamaica/']","Jamaica (/ dʒ əˈmeɪkə / (listen)) is an island country situated in the Caribbean Sea. Spanning 10,990 square kilometres (4,240 sq mi) in area, it is the third-largest island of the Greater Antilles and the fourth-largest island country in the Caribbean. Jamaica lies about 145 kilometres (90 mi) south of Cuba, and 191 kilometres (119 mi) west of Hispaniola (the island containing the countries of Haiti and the Dominican Republic).",where is jamaica situated on the world map
where are stomata found in a plant state their function,"['https://getrevising.co.uk/revision-cards/snab_topic_3_3', 'https://thewonderofscience.com/water-balance-in-plants', 'https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007%2F978-3-030-12153-2_2', 'https://wyquparimopi.agronumericus.com/experiment-of-onion-epidermal-cells-45910lab7067.html']","In botany, a stoma (plural ""stomata""), also called a stomata (plural ""stomates"") (from Greek στόμα, ""mouth""), is a pore, found in the epidermis of leaves, stems, and other organs, that facilitates gas exchange. The pore is bordered by a pair of specialized parenchyma cells known as guard cells that are responsible for regulating the size of the stomatal opening.",where are stomata found in a plant state their function
when did the berlin wall go up and down,"['https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-worldhistory/chapter/crisis-points-of-the-cold-war/', 'https://www.canstockphoto.com/berlin-wall-memorial-a-watchtower-in-15661132.html', 'https://en.wikiquote.org/wiki/Berlin_Wall', 'https://seekty.com/berlin/community-government/the-berlin-wall/', 'https://keepincalendar.com/November-9/Berlin%20Wall%20Opened/313', 'http://countrylicious.com/germany/tourist-attractions', 'https://www.preceden.com/timelines/169901-cold-war-events-timeline']","The Berlin Wall (German: Berliner Mauer, pronounced (bɛʁˈliːnɐ ˈmaʊ̯ɐ) (listen)) was a guarded concrete barrier that physically and ideologically divided Berlin from 1961 to 1989. Constructed by the German Democratic Republic (GDR, East Germany), starting on 13 August 1961, the Wall cut off (by land) West Berlin from virtually all of surrounding East Germany and East Berlin until government officials opened it in November 1989. Its demolition officially began on 13 June 1990 and finished in 1992. The barrier included guard towers placed along large concrete walls, accompanied by a wide area (later known as the ""death strip"") that contained anti-vehicle trenches, ""fakir beds"" and other defenses. The Eastern Bloc portrayed the Wall as protecting its population from fascist elements conspiring to prevent the ""will of the people"" in building a socialist state in East Germany. In practice, the Wall served to prevent the massive emigration and defection that had marked East Germany and the communist Eastern Bloc during the post-World War II period.",when did the berlin wall go up and down
when did freestyle skiing become an olympic sport,"['https://www.wisdomjobs.com/e-university/freestyle-skiing-interview-questions.html', 'http://www.kidsandonlinegames.com/sports/ski-sim/', 'https://www.olympic.org/athlete365/news/8-things-you-didnt-know-about-freestyle-skiing/', 'https://www.topendsports.com/events/winter/sports/freestyle-skiing.htm', 'https://usskiandsnowboard.org/teams/freestyle', 'https://www.olympic.org/sitecore/content/home/games/winter%20games/winter/albertville%201992', 'https://www.whistler-outdoors.com/freestyle-skiing.html']","Freestyle skiing was a demonstration sport at the 1988 Winter Olympics, with moguls, aerials, and ballet events. Moguls became an official medal sport at the 1992 games, while aerials and ballet were still demonstration events. At the 1994 games, aerials also became an official medal event and the ski ballet competition was dropped. For the 2010 Winter Olympics, ski cross was added to the program while for the 2014 Winter Olympics half-pipe and slopestyle were added.",when did freestyle skiing become an olympic sport
how many days are there in the jewish calendar,"['http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Hebrew_calendar', 'https://geraldsplace.blog/2019/04/05/the-ancient-zadokite-enochian-calendar-based-on-the-qumran-dead-sea-scrolls/', 'https://www.globalgranary.life/category/sociology/religion/judaism/', 'http://world.clndr.org/calendars/Hebrew-calendar', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Year', 'http://www.seraia.com/seraiauk/lexicon/Calendar.htm']","The Hebrew lunar year is about eleven days shorter than the solar year and uses the 19-year Metonic cycle to bring it into line with the solar year, with the addition of an intercalary month every two or three years, for a total of seven times per 19 years. Even with this intercalation, the average Hebrew calendar year is longer by about 6 minutes and 40 seconds than the current mean tropical year, so that every 216 years the Hebrew calendar will fall a day behind the current mean tropical year; and about every 231 years it will fall a day behind the mean Gregorian calendar year.",how many days are there in the jewish calendar
where is guam and who does it belong to,"['http://www.mapnall.com/en/language/English-language_444.html', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Miss_Universe_1999', 'https://www.goodonmuseum.com/free-land-usa-history/', 'https://bestmapof.com/map-of-guam.html', 'https://jukeboxtimemachine.com/category/2010s-songs/page/2/', 'https://yourfreetemplates.com/guam-map-template-download/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1872_Cavite_mutiny']","Guam (/ ˈɡwɑːm / (listen); Chamorro: Guåhån (ˈɡwɑhɑn)) is an unincorporated and organized territory of the United States in Micronesia in the western Pacific Ocean. The capital city of Guam is Hagåtña and the most populous city is Dededo. The inhabitants of Guam are called Guamanians, and they are American citizens by birth. Indigenous Guamanians are the Chamorros, who are related to other Austronesian natives to the west in the Philippines and Taiwan.",where is guam and who does it belong to
the first concern of the soviet union in 1945 was to,"['http://academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/Cold_War_%281947-1953%29_and_its_origins', 'http://dropbears.com/h/history/history_of_the_united_states.htm', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/History_of_the_Soviet_Union_(1927%E2%80%9353)']","Even so, the basic structures and tensions that marked the cold war were not yet in place in 1945 -- 46. Despite the necessary means of the United States to advance a different vision of postwar Europe, Joseph Stalin viewed the re-emergence of Germany and Japan as the Soviet Union's chief threats, not the United States. At the time, the prospects of an Anglo-American front against the USSR seemed slim from Stalin's standpoint. Economic advisers such as Eugen Varga reinforced this view, predicting a postwar crisis of overproduction in capitalist countries which would culminate by 1947 -- 48 in another great depression. For one, Stalin assumed that the capitalist camp would soon resume its internal rivalry over colonies and trade and not pose a threat to the Soviet Union.",the first concern of the soviet union in 1945 was to
who was involved in the breakup of yugoslavia,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Socialist_Federal_Republic_of_Yugoslavia', 'https://www.dmu.ac.uk/current-students/graduations/honorands/geert-hinrich-ahrens.aspx?ContensisTextOnly=true', 'https://honorharger.wordpress.com/2013/04/21/unmanned-aerial-ecologies-proto-drones-airspace-and-canaries-in-the-mine/', 'https://www.bookgorilla.com/author/B001IOH20I/adam-lebor', 'http://webster.nl/news/2018/student_in_the_spotlight_karen_harriss.html', 'https://www.geopoliticalmonitor.com/breaking-yugoslavia-936/', 'http://www.icty.org/sid/95']","The breakup of Yugoslavia occurred as a result of a series of political upheavals and conflicts during the early 1990s. After a period of political crisis in the 1980s, constituent republics of the Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia split apart, but the unresolved issues caused bitter inter-ethnic Yugoslav wars. The wars primarily affected Bosnia and Herzegovina and neighboring parts of Croatia.",who was involved in the breakup of yugoslavia
where did the name alfa romeo come from,"['https://myntransportblog.com/category/you-tube-videos/', 'https://vipsportgroup.com/%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%9F%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2-%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B4%E0%B9%82%E0%B8%AD/', 'http://blog.marilyncornwell.com/2018/04/hamlets-lament.html']","The company's name is a combination of the original name, ""A.L.F.A."" (""Anonima Lombarda Fabbrica Automobili""), and the last name of entrepreneur Nicola Romeo, who took control of the company in 1915.",where did the name alfa romeo come from
who makes the great value brand for walmart,"['http://dbschenkerrailbg.eu/96038-life-change-college-essay/', 'http://andries.ml/walmart-exclusive-brands-mi.php', 'https://fashion-history.lovetoknow.com/fashion-clothing-industry/labeling-laws', 'http://cemedomino.ml/dna-headphones-walmart-zygu.php']","Products offered through the Great Value brand are often claimed to be as good as national brand offerings, but are typically sold at a lower price because of lower marketing and advertising expense. As a house or store brand, the Great Value line does not consist of goods produced by Walmart, but is a labeling system for items manufactured and packaged by a number of agricultural and food corporations, such as ConAgra, and Sara Lee which, in addition to releasing products under its own brands and exclusively for Walmart, also manufactures and brands foods for a variety of other chain stores. Often, this labeling system, to the dismay of consumers, does not list location of manufacture of the product. Wal-Mart contends that all Great Value products are produced in the United States. Otherwise, the country of origin would be listed.",who makes the great value brand for walmart
requirements for seeking asylum in the united states,"['http://konyvtar.info/gay/mexican-transgender-gains-asylum-in-colorado.html', 'https://www.xpresstz.com/2018/05/register-for-free-and-book-your.html', 'https://chackolawfirm.com/immigration/']","Asylum has three basic requirements. First, an asylum applicant must establish that he or she fears persecution in their home country. Second, the applicant must prove that he or she would be persecuted on account of one of five protected grounds: race, religion, nationality, political opinion, or particular social group. Third, an applicant must establish that the government is either involved in the persecution, or unable to control the conduct of private actors.",requirements for seeking asylum in the united states
what part of florida is close to miami,"['http://allegra.webzdarma.cz/fritidshjemmet-ingstrup-allegra.html', 'https://wn.com/North_Florida_Community_College', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=4&ads=1&author=system&auto=Florida+poverty&standalone=1&domain_name=floridapoverty.com&title=Florida+poverty&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Florida+poverty', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=4&ads=1&author=system&auto=Concierge+florida&standalone=1&domain_name=conciergeflorida.com&title=Concierge+florida&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Concierge+florida', 'http://sosolisoairline.com/page/124/', 'http://www.matiskloedizioni.com/florida-in-the-winter/', 'https://www.bookcapecoralvacationrentals.com/blog/book-vacation-homes-on-rent-for-your-next-florida-trip/']","South Florida is a region of the U.S. state of Florida, comprising the southernmost part of the state. It is one of Florida's three most common ""directional"" regions, the others being Central Florida and North Florida. It includes the populous Miami metropolitan area, the Everglades, the Florida Keys, and other localities. South Florida is the only part of the continental United States with a tropical climate.",what part of florida is close to miami
what does it mean to platt a property,"['https://www.homeinfomax.com/Information/Real_Estate_Records/parcel_map_information.php', 'http://riz-al-atsary.info/jjjx/plat-organisasiestruktuur-pdf-sumy.php', 'http://www.familyheritagesearch.co.uk/2018/01/findmypast-friday-12-january-2018/', 'https://building.arlingtonva.us/glossary-of-terms/', 'https://www.gbtribune.com/news/local-news/commission-oks-subdivision-plat/', 'https://cadoutsourcedrafting.com/projects', 'http://www.maynardlifeoutdoors.com/2018/09/other-towns-named-maynard.html']","In the United States, a plat (/ plæt / or / plɑːt /) (plan or cadastral map) is a map, drawn to scale, showing the divisions of a piece of land. United States General Land Office surveyors drafted township plats of Public Lands Surveys to show the distance and bearing between section corners, sometimes including topographic or vegetation information. City, town or village plats show subdivisions into blocks with streets and alleys. Further refinement often splits blocks into individual lots, usually for the purpose of selling the described lots; this has become known as subdivision.",what does it mean to platt a property
where did the white elephant game come from,"['http://www.gone-ta-pott.com/white_elephant_gift_exchange.html', 'https://www.5percangol.hu/szokincsfejleszto_tananyagok/lets-go-to-the-flea-market']","The term white elephant refers to an extravagant but ineffectual gift that cannot be easily disposed of, based on the legend of the King of Siam giving rare albino elephants to courtiers who had displeased him, so that they might be ruined by the animals' upkeep costs. While the first use of this term remains a matter of contention among historians, one theory suggests that Ezra Cornell brought the term into the popular lexicon through his frequent social gatherings as early as 1828.",where did the white elephant game come from
what is the story of hamilton the play,"['https://charleshstewart.com/author/gregxto919/', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Leslie_Odom_Jr', 'https://www.austinlocal.com/things-to-do-in-austin-may-2019.html', 'https://joyofmuseums.com/museums/united-states-of-america/new-york-museums/metropolitan-museum-of-art/alexander-hamilton-by-john-trumbull/', 'https://yakimahumane.ejoinme.org/MyEvents/2017FurBallGalaAuction/LiveAuction/tabid/913012/Default.aspx', 'https://wikiwordbook.info/ha', 'https://thecitiview.com/nyc/broadway/']","Hamilton: An American Musical is a sung-and rapped-through musical about the life of American Founding Father Alexander Hamilton, with music, lyrics and book by Lin-Manuel Miranda, inspired by the 2004 biography Alexander Hamilton by historian Ron Chernow. Notably incorporating hip-hop, rhythm and blues, pop music, soul music, traditional-style show tunes and color-conscious casting of non-white actors as the Founding Fathers and other historical figures, the musical achieved both critical acclaim and box office success.",what is the story of hamilton the play
who has the most control over the united states defense spending,"['http://www.eiiff.com/budget/us/military.html', 'https://heavy.com/news/2017/05/armed-forces-day-week-history-origins/', 'https://www.moderaterepublican.org/news-not-linked/2017/3/17/president-trumps-fy-2018-skinny-budget', 'https://agovernmentofthepeople.com/2013/11/05/military-budget-of-the-united-states/', 'http://sharlamontemayor.freeiz.com/military-balance-2011-pdf/', 'https://forum.nationstates.net/viewtopic.php?p=31095233', 'https://dod.defense.gov/News/News-Releases/News-Release-View/Article/652687/department-of-defense-dod-releases-fiscal-year-2017-presidents-budget-proposal/']","The military budget is the portion of the discretionary United States federal budget allocated to the Department of Defense, or more broadly, the portion of the budget that goes to any military-related expenditures. The military budget pays the salaries, training, and health care of uniformed and civilian personnel, maintains arms, equipment and facilities, funds operations, and develops and buys new equipment. The budget funds 4 branches of the U.S. military: the Army, Marine Corps, Navy, and Air Force. In FY 2015, Pentagon and related spending totaled $598 billion, about 54% of the fiscal year 2015 U.S. discretionary budget. For FY 2017, President Obama proposed the base budget of $523.9 billion, which includes an increase of $2.2 billion over the FY 2016 enacted budget of $521.7 billion.",who has the most control over the united states defense spending
why was seinfeld called the show about nothing,"['https://www.oldtvshowondvd.com/topic-10-TV-Series-DVD-Box-Set.php/Seinfeld-Seasons-1-9-DVD-Boxset-FREE-SHIPPING.php', 'https://techincidents.com/best-hulu-series-shows-2018/', 'http://www.happyvideonetwork.com/the-very-best-of-seinfeld/', 'http://cine.gretor.tv/series/9552-seinfeld', 'https://seinfeld-episodes.com/', 'https://www.createquotes.com/90s_TV_SITCOM_Quotes.html', 'http://www.countrydetail.com/top-10-best-popular-tv-seasons-time-hit-list/']","Seinfeld is an American sitcom that ran for nine seasons on NBC, from 1989 to 1998. It was created by Larry David and Jerry Seinfeld, the latter starring as a fictionalized version of himself. Set predominantly in an apartment building in Manhattan's Upper West Side in New York City, the show features a handful of Jerry's friends and acquaintances, particularly best friend George Costanza (Jason Alexander), former girlfriend Elaine Benes (Julia Louis-Dreyfus), and neighbor across the hall Cosmo Kramer (Michael Richards). It is often described as being ""a show about nothing"", as many of its episodes are about the minutiae of daily life.",why was seinfeld called the show about nothing
why was there a civil war in england in 1642,"['http://www.aocibibletraininginstitute.org/christianityhistory-2.html', 'https://www.reenactor.net/index.php?amp;page=18', 'http://www.artandpopularculture.com/English_Civil_War', 'http://bucklinsociety.net/english-roots-history/wars-from-1600-1800-that-were-important-to-the-development-of-the-united-states/', 'https://military.wikia.org/wiki/English_Civil_War', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Irish_Confederate_Wars', 'https://www.preceden.com/timelines/217504-from-1648-to-1815']","The English Civil War (1642 -- 1651) was a series of armed conflicts and political machinations between Parliamentarians (""Roundheads"") and Royalists (""Cavaliers"") over, principally, the manner of England's government. The first (1642 -- 1646) and second (1648 -- 1649) wars pitted the supporters of King Charles I against the supporters of the Long Parliament, while the third (1649 -- 1651) saw fighting between supporters of King Charles II and supporters of the Rump Parliament. The war ended with the Parliamentarian victory at the Battle of Worcester on 3 September 1651.",why was there a civil war in england in 1642
what was the new deal during the great depression,"['https://americanhistoryusa.com/topic/new-deal/', 'https://www.co.seneca.ny.us/category/environmental-health-services/', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-politicalscience/chapter/the-history-of-economic-policy/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Dewey_Jackson_Short', 'https://angrywoodchucksblog.com/2012/11/19/the-socialists-are-still-here-in-congress-in-labor-unions-in-lobby-groups-upton-sinclair-of-the-jungle-prediction/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Social_programs_in_the_United_States', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/06-16/all']","The New Deal was a series of federal programs, public work projects, financial reforms and regulations enacted in the United States during the 1930s in response to the Great Depression. Some of these federal programs included the Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC), the Civil Works Administration (CWA), the Farm Security Administration (FSA), the National Industrial Recovery Act of 1933 (NIRA) and the Social Security Administration (SSA). These programs included support for farmers, the unemployed, youth and the elderly as well as new constraints and safeguards on the banking industry and changes to the monetary system. Most programs were enacted between 1933 -- 1938, though some were later. They included both laws passed by Congress as well as presidential executive orders, most during the first term of the presidency of Franklin D. Roosevelt. The programs focused on what historians refer to as the ""3 Rs"": relief for the unemployed and poor, recovery of the economy back to normal levels and reform of the financial system to prevent a repeat depression. The New Deal produced a political realignment, making the Democratic Party the majority (as well as the party that held the White House for seven out of the nine presidential terms from 1933 -- 1969) with its base in liberal ideas, the South, traditional Democrats, big city machines and the newly empowered labor unions and ethnic minorities. The Republicans were split, with conservatives opposing the entire New Deal as an alleged enemy of business and growth and liberals accepting some of it and promising to make it more efficient. The realignment crystallized into the New Deal coalition that dominated most presidential elections into the 1960s while the opposing conservative coalition largely controlled Congress from 1939 -- 1964.",what was the new deal during the great depression
day off in lieu of public holiday uk,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Public_holidays_in_the_United_Kingdom.html', 'https://www.farrer.co.uk/news-and-insights/blogs/bank-holidays-what-you-need-to-know/', 'https://www.jaluch.co.uk/hr-blast/8-need-to-know-employment-law-updates/', 'https://minutehr.com/knowledge-base/holiday-entitlement/', 'https://www.musiciansunion.org.uk/Home/Advice/Education/Getting-Paid', 'http://optionshr.co.uk/2013/11/', 'https://www.europeworldchampionship2014.com/employee-paid-public-holidays-in-malawi/']","Although there is no statutory right for workers to take paid leave on bank holidays, where paid leave is given (either because the business is closed or for other reasons), the bank holiday can count towards the minimum statutory holiday entitlement. Likewise, if people are required to work on a bank holiday, there is no statutory right to an enhanced pay rate nor to a day off in lieu, although many employers do give either or both. Any rights in this respect depend on the person's contract of employment. The statutory minimum paid holidays is 28 days or 5.6 weeks a year under the Working Time Regulations 1998 (including any bank holidays or public holidays that are taken).",day off in lieu of public holiday uk
what does a team get for winning the fa cup,"['https://www.sportzcraazy.com/fa-cup-2019/', 'http://www.mobilestec.com/fa-cup/', 'https://handlungsbereitschaft.eu/fa-cup-winners.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/FA_Cup', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/2017%E2%80%9318_A.F.C._Bournemouth_season', 'http://2048game.mobi/sizzling-hot/latest-fa-cup-scores.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Bill_Shankly']","Winners receive the FA Cup trophy, of which there have been two designs and five actual cups; the latest is a 2014 replica of the second design, introduced in 1911. Winners also qualify for the Europa League and a place in the FA Community Shield match. Chelsea are the current holders, having beaten Manchester United 1 -- 0 in the 2018 final. Arsenal are the most successful club with 13 titles. Arsenal's Arsène Wenger is the most successful manager in the competition with seven finals won.",what does a team get for winning the fa cup
where does the phrase rock and roll come from,['https://www.splinterwoodradio.uk/'],"The phrase rocking and rolling originally described the movement of a ship on the ocean, but it was used by the early twentieth century, both to describe a spiritual fervor and as a sexual analogy. Various gospel, blues and swing recordings used the phrase before it became used more frequently -- but still intermittently -- in the late 1930s and 1940s, principally on recordings and in reviews of what became known as rhythm and blues music aimed at a black audience. In 1951, Cleveland-based disc jockey Alan Freed began playing this music style while popularizing the term rock and roll to describe it.",where does the phrase rock and roll come from
where did the saying come from knock on wood,"['http://twinpeaks.popapostle.com/html/episodes/Lets-Rock.htm', 'http://oaks.nvg.org/folk-arts.html']","The origin of the custom may be in German folklore, wherein supernatural beings are thought to live in trees, and can be invoked for protection.",where did the tradition of knocking on wood come from
who sang the song sunny from the 60s,"['http://www.bytownukulele.ca/AllPosts/tabid/906/articleType/ArticleView/articleId/3753/Sunny.aspx', 'http://einfach-reisen.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=35475', 'http://googledictionary.freecollocation.com/meaning?word=sunny', 'https://learningukulele.com/lessons/100', 'https://desdelmeuracodemon.wordpress.com/tag/usa-1960s/']","""Sunny"" is a song written by Bobby Hebb, from 1966. It is one of the most performed and recorded popular songs, with hundreds of versions released. BMI rates ""Sunny"" number 25 in its ""Top 100 songs of the century"". The song is also known by its first line: ""Sunny, yesterday my life was filled with rain"".",who sang the song sunny from the 60s
who is the current secretary of the department of justice,"['https://graceland.fandom.com/wiki/Department_of_Justice', 'http://www.pearltrees.com/u/19933916-intelligence-encyclopedia', 'https://gulfofmexicooilspillblog.wordpress.com/category/gulf-of-mexico-oil-spill-blog/us-department-of-justice/', 'https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/social-issues/memo-from-commerce-secretary-seems-to-contradict-his-testimony-on-census-citizenship-question/2018/06/22/4a324666-7658-11e8-9780-b1dd6a09b549_story.html?noredirect=on&amp;utm_term=.c4b744cd0448', 'http://crcconnection.com/2017/02/24/ford-gt-competition-series-goes-hardcore.html', 'https://www.speakingprocentral.com/attorney/', 'http://nysepost.com/business/page617/']","The department is headed by the United States Attorney General, who is nominated by the President and confirmed by the Senate and is a member of the Cabinet. The current Attorney General is Jeff Sessions.",who is the current secretary of the department of justice
where did the phrase in god we trust come from,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/In_God_We_Trust', 'http://blog.thebuttonmonger.com/2011/10/start-spangled-banner.html', 'https://cpcfoundation.com/religious/in-god-we-trust/', 'https://www.ldshymns.com/lds-hymns-326-341/340-the-star-spangled-banner', 'http://southsidechurchofchrist.com/sermons/psalm-69-the-man-of-sorrows.html', 'https://www.answers.com/Q/What_was_happening_when_Francis_Scott_Key_wrote_The_Star_Spangled_Banner', 'http://westpalmbeachchurchofchrist.com/old-testament/psalms/psalm_69.html']","The phrase appears to have originated in ""The Star-Spangled Banner"", written by Francis Scott Key during the War of 1812. The fourth stanza includes the phrase, ""And this be our motto:' In God is our Trust.'"" This version of the motto made an early appearance on the twenty dollar interest bearing notes issued in 1864 along with the motto ""God and our Right"".",where did the phrase in god we trust come from
what is the role of a producer in a tv show,"['http://projectbailout.com/projects/producer.html', 'http://moviestaff.com/producers.htm', 'http://tribuna.asp2.cz/www-alienware-co-uk.html', 'https://www.allperfectstories.com/become-tv-show-producer/']","A television producer is a person who oversees all aspects of video production on a television program. Some producers take more of an executive role, in that they conceive new programs and pitch them to the television networks, but upon acceptance they focus on business matters, such as budgets and contracts. Other producers are more involved with the day-to-day workings, participating in activities such as screenwriting, set design, casting and directing.",what is the role of a producer in a tv show
why is the statue of liberty in tokyo,"['https://www.360cities.net/image/statue-de-la-libert-colmar-alsace-france-7121', 'https://ourladyliberty.wordpress.com/tag/statue-of-liberty/', 'http://www.atokyolifestyle.com/2015/03/odaiba-seaside-park.html', 'https://mommymanang.com/index.php/2019/03/20/our-museo-pambata-experience/', 'https://www.hands-free-segway.reviews/self-balancing-scooter/reviews/goboard-self-balancing-scooter-us-brand-supplier/', 'http://www.cascadianabroad.com/2014/07/29/where-are-we/']","The French Statue of Liberty from the Île aux Cygnes came to Odaiba, Tokyo, from April 1998 to May 1999 in commemoration of ""The French year in Japan"". Because of its popularity, in 2000 a replica of the French Statue of Liberty was erected at the same place. Also in Japan, a small Statue of Liberty is in the Amerika-mura (American Village) shopping district in Osaka, Japan. Another replica is in Oirase near the town of Shimoda south of Misawa in Aomori Prefecture, where the United States has an 8,000-person U.S. Air Force base. A replica of the Statue of Liberty in Ishinomaki, Miyagi Prefecture, was damaged by the 2011 Tōhoku earthquake and tsunami. There is also a replica in Oyabe, Toyama.",why is there a statue of liberty in odaiba
when is an object considered to be in motion,"['http://www.thricetwisted.com/Motion.php', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/motion-physics', 'https://dmander.wordpress.com/2015/04/', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Motion_(physics)', 'http://gazetadailys.tk/projectile-motion-equation-sheet-for-physics.html', 'http://www.alfonsoleonguillen.net/gravityisforce.html', 'https://ouijerome.com/portfolio/motion/']","In physics, motion is a change in position of an object over time. Motion is described in terms of displacement, distance, velocity, acceleration, time and speed. Motion of a body is observed by attaching a frame of reference to an observer and measuring the change in position of the body relative to that frame.",when is an object considered to be in motion
what is the nature of demand for carpets,"['https://rapp-id.eu/teppich-diamond.html', 'http://www.diamondcarpet.cn/index.php/company-new/Whats-the-carpet.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Ardabil_Carpet', 'https://perarugnapa.com/portfolio-item/our-rugs/', 'https://www.zayaanco.com/flooring/carpet-suppliers.html', 'http://www.mjaneross.com/?st=haziryqac', 'https://www.blogitwitharchana.com/15-modern-living-room-ideas/']","Carpets are used for a variety of purposes, including insulating a person's feet from a cold tile or concrete floor, making a room more comfortable as a place to sit on the floor (e.g., when playing with children or as a prayer rug), reducing sound from walking (particularly in apartment buildings) and adding decoration or colour to a room. Carpets can be made in any colour by using differently dyed fibers. Carpets can have many different types of patterns and motifs used to decorate the surface. In the 2000s, carpets are used in industrial and commercial establishments such as retail stores and hotels and in private homes. In the 2010s, a huge range of carpets and rugs are available at many price and quality levels, ranging from inexpensive, synthetic carpets that are mass-produced in factories and used in commercial buildings to costly hand-knotted wool rugs which are used in private homes of wealthy families.",what is the nature of demand for carpets
when was who let the dogs out made,['http://rathergood.co.uk/baha-men-let-dogs/'],"""Who Let the Dogs Out?"" is a song performed by the Bahamian group Baha Men, released as a single on July 26, 2000. Originally written by Anslem Douglas (titled ""Doggie"") for the Trinidad and Tobago Carnival season of 1998, it was covered by producer Jonathan King who sang it under the name Fat Jakk and his Pack of Pets. He brought the song to the attention of his friend Steve Greenberg, who then had the Baha Men cover the song. The song became the band's first hit in the United Kingdom and the United States, and it gained popularity after appearing in Rugrats in Paris: The Movie and its soundtrack album.",when was who let the dogs out made
where is palm beach fl on the map,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Palm_Beach,_Florida', 'http://shopwithcharacter.com/ontario/palm-beach-tan-application-pdf.php', 'https://arezza.org/2018/07/31/palm-beach-florida-and-the-maritime-museum/', 'https://www.onesothebysrealty.com/communities/palm-beach/', 'http://www.luxuryestatesplus.com/palm-beach-real-estate', 'https://www.langrealty.com/palm-beach.php', 'http://www.susanreiter.com/condo/palm-beach/']","Palm Beach is the easternmost town in Florida, located on a 18-mile (29 km) long barrier island between Lake Worth on the west and the Atlantic Ocean on the east. At no point is the island wider than three-quarters of a mile (1.2 km), and in places it is only 500 feet (150 m).",where is palm beach fl on the map
who administer oath to vice president of india,"['https://www.vicepresidentofindia.nic.in/election-vice-president', 'https://www.srdlawnotes.com/2017/12/the-vice-president-of-india.html', 'https://www.assignmenthelp.net/assignment-help/the-union-the-executive', 'http://bareactslive.com/WB/WB226.HTM', 'http://bareactslive.com/WB/WB159.HTM', 'http://stopthebull.com/inauguration-2017/', 'https://worldneighbours.ca/nepal-political-update/']","The article 69 of Indian Constitution provides the Oath of Affirmation for the Office of Vice President as under:-""I, ________ do swear in the name of God / solemnly affirm that I will bear true faith and allegiance to solemnly affirm the Constitution of India as by law established and that I will faithfully discharge the duty upon which I am about to enter."" The President administers the oath of office and secrecy to the Vice-President.",who administer oath to vice president of india
where is the bridge that collapsed in atlanta georgia,"['https://www.longeng.com/services/construction-engineering-inspection-cei/', 'https://wtvr.com/2017/04/02/i85-fire-suspect-basil-eleby-discussed-smoking-crack-crack-before-atlanta-interstate-collapse/', 'http://ninjapundit.blogspot.com/2018/03/interstate-85-bridge-collapse.html', 'https://transportationops.org/case-studies/i-85-bridge-collapse-and-rebuild']","A bridge collapsed on Interstate 85 (I-85) in Atlanta, Georgia, after a massive fire on the evening of March 30, 2017. After the collapse of the 100-foot-long (30 m) section, I-85 was closed to traffic over approximately two miles (3.2 km) between its split with I-75 and the interchange with State Route 400 (SR 400). Three sections of northbound I-85 and three sections of southbound I-85 were replaced. Repairs were completed by May 13, 2017.",where is the bridge that collapsed in atlanta georgia
when did djokovic win his first grand slam,"['http://en.pschitt.info/page/Richard+Gasquet', 'https://alexbaresi-shop.eu/djokovic-olympisches-gold.html', 'http://www.tennisserver.com/photofeed/2011/110127-australian_open.shtml', 'http://recomparison.com/comparisons/101263/roger-federer-vs-novak-djokovic-tennis-players-compared/', 'http://keepingscore.blogs.time.com/2014/01/21/stanislas-wawrinkas-win-is-just-what-mens-tennis-needs/', 'https://uttarakhandnewsnetwork.com/2019/01/rafael-nadal-one-step-away-from-18th-grand-slam-win/', 'https://www.tennisworldusa.org/tennis/news/Novak_Djokovic/66443/players-were-not-like-novak-djokovic-in-the-90s-says-amritraj/']","Djokovic started the year by playing the Hopman Cup with fellow Serbian world No. 3 Jelena Janković. While he won all his round-robin matches, the team lost 1 -- 2 in the final to the second-seeded American team of Serena Williams and Mardy Fish. At the Australian Open, Djokovic reached his second consecutive Grand Slam final without dropping a set, including a victory over two-time defending champion Federer in the semi-finals. By reaching the semi-finals, Djokovic became the youngest player to have reached the semi-finals in all four Grand Slam events. In the final, Djokovic defeated unseeded Frenchman Jo-Wilfried Tsonga in four sets to earn his first Grand Slam singles title. This marked the first time since the 2005 Australian Open that a Grand Slam singles title was not won by Federer or Nadal.",when did djokovic win his first grand slam
where does the name harley quinn come from,"['http://mediumisthemess.com/10-awesome-classic-harley-quin-drawing/', 'https://fenozi.com/suicide-squad-characters-movie/', 'https://popvinylfigure.com/harley-quinn-suicide-squad-funko', 'http://ydemoproject.eu/54023-character-book/', 'https://superheroabode.com/tag/harley-quinn/', 'http://www.ryan-mahendra.com/2016/09/harley-quinn_1.html', 'https://www.blog.apparelsearch.com/2016/11/']","Harley Quinn is a frequent accomplice and lover of the Joker, whom she met while working as a psychiatrist at Gotham City's Arkham Asylum, where the Joker was a patient. Her name is a play on the name ""Harlequin"", a character which originated in the commedia dell'arte. The character has teamed up with fellow villains Catwoman and Poison Ivy several times, the trio being known as the Gotham City Sirens. Poison Ivy is known to be a close friend and recurring ally of Harley, even being depicted as her girlfriend in recent comics. Since The New 52, she is now depicted as an antihero and has left her past as a supervillain behind. Harley Quinn has also been depicted as a member of the Suicide Squad.",where does the name harley quinn come from
what is the purpose of surveillance in epidemiology,"['https://www.sas.com/ko_kr/whitepapers/analytics-with-open-data-build-stronger-government-107499.html', 'http://blog.lab24.co.za/blog/dashboard-will-speed-up-sas-hiv-suppression-objectives/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/chronicdisease/data/index.htm', 'https://www.mdx.ac.uk/courses/undergraduate/public-health-bsc', 'https://www.odsp-ocrc.ca/', 'https://www.esr.cri.nz/our-services/consultancy/public-health/', 'http://www.alliedacademies.org/articles/substance-use-and-mental-health-preliminary-surveillance-findings-from-an-american-indian-population-8935.html']","Public health surveillance (also epidemiological surveillance, clinical surveillance or syndromic surveillance) is, according to the World Health Organization (WHO), ""the continuous, systematic collection, analysis and interpretation of health-related data needed for the planning, implementation, and evaluation of public health practice."" Public health surveillance may be used to ""serve as an early warning system for impending public health emergencies; document the impact of an intervention, or track progress towards specified goals; and monitor and clarify the epidemiology of health problems, to allow priorities to be set and to inform public health policy and strategies.""",what is the purpose of surveillance in epidemiology
what is the largest bill in circulation in the us,"['http://imperiosmu.tk/free-slots-sharkys.html', 'http://dominospizzaapp.tk/allegany-seneca-casino-concerts.html', 'http://www.dimensionsinfo.com/banknote-dimensions/', 'https://edaily.co.ke/entertainment/mitumba-hawker-loses-usd-1-million-windfall-gets-arrested-124335/crazy-world/', 'http://isivirginia.com/joomla2/index.php?option=com_content&amp;view=article&amp;id=22', 'https://www.currencyconverter.co.uk/currencies/american-dollar090326145355', 'https://www.ruitersportwatte.be/2018/05/42921_show_me_1_5_ton_ball_mill_price_in_pakistani_rupees.html']","Large denominations of United States currency greater than $100 were circulated by the United States Treasury until 1969. Since then, the U.S. dollar has only been issued in seven denominations: $1, $2, $5, $10, $20, $50, and $100.",what is the largest bill in circulation in the us
what is the bergamot in earl grey tea,"['http://anomaliablog.tk/660/what-is-grey-tea-1295.php', 'https://www.theteamakers.co.uk/blog/guide-to-earl-grey-tea.html', 'http://shopcatcarriers9.ml/71505-2019/oil-of-bergamot-in-tea-jif.php', 'http://www.galoor.com/tea/2033794-best-earl-grey-teas-reviews-and-buying-tips-tea-bags-loose-leaf', 'https://www.bubbleteaology.com/bubble-tea-brewing-guide/', 'http://www.plantjotter.com/joy-warmth-and-good-vibes-yellow-kitchen-curtains/grey-and-yellow-kitchen-curtains/', 'https://ratetea.com/style/earl-grey-green-tea/51/']","Earl Grey tea is a tea blend which has been flavoured with the addition of oil of bergamot. Bergamot is a variety of orange that is often grown in Italy and France. The rind's fragrant oil is added to black tea to give Earl Grey its signature pungent punch. Traditionally, Earl Grey was made from black teas, but tea companies have since begun to offer Earl Grey in other varieties as well, such as green or oolong.",what is the bergamot in earl grey tea
where is the pro bowl played in hawaii,"['https://www.capitalcitytickets.com/NFL-Pro-Bowl-Tickets', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/pro-bowl', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Carl_Pickens', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Chris_Samuels', 'http://raidersnation.com/raiders-news-former-safety-charles-woodson-named-2017-pro-bowl-legend-captain/2016/10/25/', 'https://www.offshoresportsbooks.com/news/2019-nfl-pro-bowl-betting-pick-and-prediction/', 'https://elhstalon.net/sports/2019/02/08/2019-pro-bowl/']","Between 1980 and 2016, the game was played at Aloha Stadium in Hawaii, save for two years. On June 1, 2016, the NFL announced that they reached a multi-year deal to move the game to Orlando, Florida as part of the league's ongoing efforts to make the game more relevant. For years, the game has suffered from lack of interest due to perceived low quality. The 2017 Pro Bowl marked a return to the AFC -- NFC format.",where is the pro bowl played in hawaii
where is the show wentworth supposed to take place,"['http://tvcaba.com/wentworth-season-3/', 'https://uselessthingsneedlovetoo.com/tag/kate-atkinson/', 'https://www.aprettylifeinthesuburbs.com/what-to-watch-on-netflix-right-now-streamteam/']","Wentworth is set in modern-day Australia and focuses on Bea Smith (Danielle Cormack) when she first enters prison after being charged with the attempted murder of her husband. Bea is separated from her daughter and sent to Wentworth on remand, where she lives in ""an uncertain limbo"" until she is sentenced. Starting at the bottom of Wentworth's hierarchy, Bea is forced to learn how to survive in prison.",where is the show wentworth supposed to take place
the ios operating system is found on which device ​,"['http://noticiasmvs.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=20689', 'https://assignable.io/task/ola-based-cab-booking-ios-application', 'https://punchng.com/organise-your-day-with-these-time-management-apps/', 'https://shiiba.info/?newsid=14335', 'http://seo-backlinks.info/viewtopic.php?t=5752', 'https://www.fluper.com/blog/android-vs-ios-mobile-application-platforms/', 'https://www.template.net/design-templates/icons/ios-app-icon/']","iOS (formerly iPhone OS) is a mobile operating system created and developed by Apple Inc. exclusively for its hardware. It is the operating system that presently powers many of the company's mobile devices, including the iPhone, iPad, and iPod Touch. It is the second most popular mobile operating system globally after Android.",the ios operating system is found on which device ​
the war powers resolution checks the presidents power by,"['https://occasionalplanet.org/2011/07/01/democrats-could-give-obama-cover-in-libya/', 'http://www.intlawgrrls.com/2012/02/how-presidential-war-power-is-made-or.html', 'https://www.the5thestate.asia/2016/01/us-army-launches-ground-offensive-in.html', 'http://jmepp.hkspublications.org/2019/03/21/current-law-constraining-the-president-options-to-limit-aid-to-saudi-arabia-part-2/', 'https://thefreqmedia.com/2018/12/26/analysis/patbristol70/reading-tea-leaves-for-christmas/', 'http://sensiblethought.com/2011/the-danger-of-launching-an-unpopular-war', 'http://www.raga.org/news/archives/04-2018']","The War Powers Resolution requires the President to notify Congress within 48 hours of committing armed forces to military action and forbids armed forces from remaining for more than 60 days, with a further 30-day withdrawal period, without a Congressional authorization for use of military force (AUMF) or a declaration of war by the United States. The resolution was passed by two-thirds of Congress, overriding the veto of the bill from President Nixon.",the war powers resolution checks the presidents power by
what happened 14 years after the wreck of the titan was written,"['http://theinnatstonington.com/new-south-wales/the-wreck-of-the-titan-1898-pdf.php', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Henry_B._Harris', 'https://endtimesprophecyreport.com/2018/10/08/end-times-prophecy-headlines-october-8-2018/', 'https://leaderonomics.com/leadership/why-reading-and-learning-from-what-you-read-is-critical-to-your-success', 'http://swissjournals.org/south-australia/the-wreck-of-the-titan-1898-pdf.php', 'https://www.paulsquiz.com/general-knowledge-quizzes-mainmenu-152/202-free-quiz-questions/25-general-knowledge/1962-pauls-quiz-186', 'https://www.thisisinsider.com/titanics-books-predicted-disaster-2018-4']","The Wreck of the Titan: Or, Futility (originally called Futility) is an 1898 novella written by Morgan Robertson. The story features the fictional ocean liner Titan, which sinks in the North Atlantic after striking an iceberg. The Titan and its sinking have been noted to be very similar to the real-life passenger ship RMS Titanic, which sank fourteen years later. Following the sinking of the Titanic, the novel was reissued with some changes, particularly in the ship's gross tonnage.",what happened 14 years after the wreck of the titan was written
difference between strength of materials and mechanics of materials,"['http://freeinfocontent.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=34432', 'https://easystudy.info/Thread-strength-of-material-book-a-p-dongre-pdf', 'http://trinityfiles.com/australian-capital-territory/statics-and-strength-of-materials-2nd-edition-pdf.php', 'http://easonhan.info/?page_id=43029', 'http://domainerfree.info/?page_id=21235', 'http://cannoncounty.info/viewtopic.php?t=15116', 'http://ardtunisia.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=45040']","Strength of materials, also called mechanics of materials, is a subject which deals with the behavior of solid objects subject to stresses and strains. The complete theory began with the consideration of the behavior of one and two dimensional members of structures, whose states of stress can be approximated as two dimensional, and was then generalized to three dimensions to develop a more complete theory of the elastic and plastic behavior of materials. An important founding pioneer in mechanics of materials was Stephen Timoshenko.",difference between strength of materials and mechanics of materials
where does the t bone cut come from,"['https://tallgrassmeat.com/products/beef', 'https://food52.com/hotline/2399-what-is-the-difference-between-a-t-bone-steak-and-a-porterhouse', 'https://www.kellysbutchershopanddeli.com/beef.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Pearl_Street_(Manhattan)', 'https://notamystery.com/2013/09/01/is-it-t-rex-no-its-a-porterhouse/', 'https://www.theinternationalman.com/restaurant-resources.php', 'http://www.recipefaire.com/MoreGoodStuff/CutsOfBeefDescription2.aspx']","The T-bone and porterhouse are steaks of beef cut from the short loin (called the sirloin in Commonwealth countries). Both steaks include a ""T-shaped"" bone with meat on each side. Porterhouse steaks are cut from the rear end of the short loin and thus include more tenderloin steak, along with (on the other side of the bone) a large strip steak. T-bone steaks are cut closer to the front, and contain a smaller section of tenderloin. The smaller portion of a T-bone, when sold alone, is known as a filet mignon, especially if it's cut from the small forward end of the tenderloin.",where does the t bone cut come from
where did the story of fairies come from,"['https://www.artfire.com/ext/shop/product_view/KatsAllThat/12633326/leaf_fairy_blue_leather_turquoise_picasso_druk_magatama_boho_bracelet/handmade/jewelry/bracelets/leather', 'http://fjojij.promsmesi.ru/black-black-dating-kryptonite-man-man-white-woman-445.html', 'https://rowenafoxelle.wordpress.com/', 'http://www.steelwood.org/elf/', 'https://lovetaliesinjewellery.co.uk/shop/tibetan-silver-charm/fairy-charm-pendant-and-earrings-set/']","Historical origins include various traditions of Celtics (Bretons, Welsh people), Gaelics (Irish, Scots), Germanic peoples, and of Middle French medieval romances. Fairie was used adjectivally, meaning ""enchanted"" (as in fairie knight, fairie queene), but also became a generic term for various ""enchanted"" creatures during the Late Middle English period. Literature of the Elizabethan era conflated elves with the fairies of Romance culture, rendering these terms somewhat interchangeable.",where did the story of fairies come from
what does the stone tiger's eye mean,"['http://328gallery.com/index.php/product/sn02-agate-tigers-eye-necklace/', 'https://www.prehistoricoregon.com/shop/metaphysical/healing-stone/tiger-eye-energy-stone-brazil-balance-and-vitality/?add-to-cart=1265', ""https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Tiger's_eye.html"", 'http://www.artsettechniques.com/en/', 'https://www.azbluerockers.com/tiger-eye/', 'https://www.loveamberx.co.uk/products/copy-of-leo-birthstone-adult-elasticated-chip-bracelet-gift-tigers-eye', 'http://shop.vendio.com/badgirldesigns/item/2135843803/index.html']","Tiger's eye (also called tiger eye) is a chatoyant gemstone that is usually a metamorphic rock with a golden to red-brown colour and a silky lustre. As members of the quartz group, tiger's eye and the related blue-coloured mineral hawk's eye gain their silky, lustrous appearance from the parallel intergrowth of quartz crystals and altered amphibole fibres that have mostly turned into limonite.",what does the stone tiger's eye mean
who were the pilgrims and what did they want,"['https://customer.guru/net-promoter-score/pilgrim-39-s-pride-corporation', 'https://www.whatisdomain.net/pilgrims.org/', 'http://www.lilfordhall.com/Pilgrims.asp', 'http://dollsfromtheattic.blogspot.com/2010/11/over-river-and-through-woods.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Myles_Standish', 'http://shopannies.blogspot.com/2017_09_10_archive.html', 'https://www.leidencityevents.nl/project/pilgrim-fathers/']","The Pilgrims or Pilgrim Fathers were early European settlers of the Plymouth Colony in present-day Plymouth, Massachusetts, United States. The Pilgrims' leadership came from the religious congregations of Brownist English Dissenters who had fled the volatile political environment in England for the relative calm and tolerance of 16th -- 17th century Holland in the Netherlands. The Pilgrims held Puritan Calvinist religious beliefs but, unlike other Puritans, they maintained that their congregations needed to be separated from the English state church. As a separatist group, they were also concerned that they might lose their English cultural identity if they remained in the Netherlands, so they arranged with English investors to establish a new colony in North America. The colony was established in 1620 and became the second successful English settlement in North America (after the founding of Jamestown, Virginia in 1607). The Pilgrims' story became a central theme of the history and culture of the United States.",who were the pilgrims and what did they want
where did the term shark week come from,"['https://plainsmenpost.com/2017/12/christmas-movies-to-enjoy-over-the-holiday-season/', 'http://blog.stevenwsmeltzer.com/category/underwater-photography/page/3/', 'https://reelgood.com/tv/list/vampire', 'https://kodiapps.com/tv-Hostile_Planet', 'https://www.mettle.com/shark-week-2016-discovery-vr/', 'https://perukel.com/index.php/tag/connected-tv/', 'https://caliope-couture.com/2017/07/']","Shark Week is an annual, week-long TV programming block created by Tom Golden at the Discovery Channel, which features shark-based programming. Shark Week originally premiered on July 17, 1988. Featured annually, in July and / or early August, it was originally devoted to conservation efforts and correcting misconceptions about sharks. Over time, it grew in popularity and became a hit on the Discovery Channel. Since 2010, it has been the longest-running cable television programming event in history. Broadcast in over 72 countries, Shark Week is promoted heavily via social networks like Facebook and Twitter. Episodes are also available for purchase on services like Google Play Movies & TV / YouTube, Amazon Video, and iTunes. Some episodes are free on subscription-based Hulu.",where did the term shark week come from
where is st lucia located on a world map,"['https://simonsblogpark.com/onlinegambling/simons-guide-st-lucia-casinos-gambling-lottery/', 'https://caribbean-tour.com/Information-about-St.-Lucia.html', 'https://www.silvertrader.uk/product/2018-st-lucia-silver-flamingo-1-oz-silver-bullion-coin/', 'http://www.theglobepress.com/5-top-worlds-most-beautiful-natural-places/', 'https://www.bhoma.com/mbbs-in-usa/spartan-health-science-university', 'https://realtyww.info/search/country,LC/category,66', 'http://gei.aerobaticsweb.org/st_lucia.html']","Saint Lucia (/ ˈluːʃə / (listen); French: Sainte-Lucie) is a sovereign island country in the West Indies in the eastern Caribbean Sea on the boundary with the Atlantic Ocean. Part of the Lesser Antilles, it is located north / northeast of the island of Saint Vincent, northwest of Barbados and south of Martinique. It covers a land area of 617 km (238 square miles) and reported a population of 165,595 in the 2010 census. Its capital is Castries.",where is st lucia located on a world map
who sets the closing date on a home,"['https://www.rvfinancingdirect.com/settlement-services/', 'https://www.ustitlerecords.com/real-estate-terms-definitions/', 'http://www.sandybakst.com/real-estate-attorney-baldwin-fl/', 'https://highlandsmortgage.com/agents/danielle-boote/', 'https://www.homebuyhub.com/conveyancing/solicitors/', 'https://blog.callthewalls.com/what-to-expect-when-closing/', 'https://gmfsmortgage.com/glossary/']","The closing date is set during the negotiation phase, and is usually several weeks after the offer is formally accepted. On the closing date, the ownership of the property is transferred to the buyer. In most jurisdictions, ownership is officially transferred when a deed from the seller is delivered to the buyer. Lenders providing a mortgage loan will often require title service, including title search and title insurance, appraisal, land survey, and attorneys to be involved.",who sets the closing date on a home
an account much abbreviated of the destruction of the indies sparknotes,['https://onartandaesthetics.com/2016/11/06/a-short-account-of-the-destruction-of-the-indies/'],A Short Account of the Destruction of the Indies (Spanish: Brevísima relación de la destrucción de las Indias) is an account written by the Spanish Dominican friar Bartolomé de las Casas in 1542 (published in 1552) about the mistreatment of and atrocities committed against the indigenous peoples of the Americas in colonial times and sent to then Prince Philip II of Spain.,an account much abbreviated of the destruction of the indies sparknotes
how many times did it take the wright brothers to fly,"['http://www.thefullwiki.org/Wright_brothers', 'http://www.plantcitymarket.com/newsletter-12172014.html', 'https://echarta.wordpress.com/tag/postcards/', 'http://wxcentre.ca/news/the-first-powered-flight', 'https://playingcarddecks.com/collections/lpcc/products/innovation-deck-playing-cards-poker-size-lpcc-custom-black-edition-new-sealed', 'http://netteranatomy.com/wright-here-wright-now.html', 'http://tut2learn.com/2017/04/the-wright-brothers/']","In camp at Kill Devil Hills, they endured weeks of delays caused by broken propeller shafts during engine tests. After the shafts were replaced (requiring two trips back to Dayton), Wilbur won a coin toss and made a three-second flight attempt on December 14, 1903, stalling after takeoff and causing minor damage to the Flyer. (Because December 13, 1903, was a Sunday, the brothers did not make any attempts that day, even though the weather was good, so their first powered test flight happened on the 121st anniversary of the first test flight that the Montgolfier brothers had done, on December 14, 1782.) In a message to their family, Wilbur referred to the trial as having ""only partial success"", stating ""the power is ample, and but for a trifling error due to lack of experience with this machine and this method of starting, the machine would undoubtedly have flown beautifully."" Following repairs, the Wrights finally took to the air on December 17, 1903, making two flights each from level ground into a freezing headwind gusting to 27 miles per hour (43 km / h). The first flight, by Orville at 10: 35 am, of 120 feet (37 m) in 12 seconds, at a speed of only 6.8 miles per hour (10.9 km / h) over the ground, was recorded in a famous photograph. The next two flights covered approximately 175 and 200 feet (53 and 61 m), by Wilbur and Orville respectively. Their altitude was about 10 feet (3.0 m) above the ground. The following is Orville Wright's account of the final flight of the day:",how many times did it take the wright brothers to fly
where does the phrase bend it like beckham come from,"['https://blog.tcea.org/google-sheets/', 'http://realworldmusic.com/project/bend-it-like-beckham/', 'http://benditnetworks.com/filmography/bilb-trailer/', 'https://www.iambirmingham.co.uk/2018/03/08/8-good-reads-local-female-authors-international-womens-day/', 'https://list.ly/list/P34-best-bollywood-sports-films', 'http://www.unite-it.eu/group/global-citizenship-education/forum/topics/women-s-rights-today?page=1&commentId=2058019%3AComment%3A121316&x=1']","The film's title refers to the football player David Beckham, and his skill at scoring from free kicks by curling the ball past a wall of defenders. It follows the 18-year-old daughter of Punjabi Sikhs in London. She is infatuated with football but her parents have forbidden her to play because she is a girl. She joins a local women's team, which makes its way to the top of the league.",where does the phrase bend it like beckham come from
what kinds of cases are heard in superior court,"['https://www.definition.net/users/1/definitions?page=2', 'https://www.save-ebone.com/qualifications-for-a-restraining-order/', 'http://constitutionnet.org/country/fiji', 'http://www.commonwealthgovernance.org/countries/asia/sri_lanka/judicial-system/', 'http://www.coface.com.au/Economic-Studies-and-Country-Risks/Indonesia', 'https://www.courtrecords.org/states/arkansas/', 'http://www.commonwealthofnations.org/sectors-malaysia/government/']","In common law systems, a superior court is a court of general competence which typically has unlimited jurisdiction with regard to civil and criminal legal cases. A superior court is ""superior"" relative to a court with limited jurisdiction (see lower court), which is restricted to civil cases involving monetary amounts with a specific limit, or criminal cases involving offenses of a less serious nature. A superior court may hear appeals from lower courts (see court of appeal).",what kinds of cases are heard in superior court
what is the temperature range of mars in fahrenheit,"['https://www.summitclimb.com/climb/everest-nepal-training-climb/', 'http://www.mars-one.com/technology/the-mars-suit', 'https://www.sharmtouring.com/sharm-el-sheikh/red-sea-boats-cruises/excursion-ras-mohamed-by-bussnorkeling/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Earth%27s_atmosphere', 'https://seasonsyear.com/Belize', 'https://flagholidays.in/package-details.php?pid=318', 'http://arihanttourstravels.com/destination_detail.aspx?page=51']","Differing in situ values have been reported for the average temperature on Mars, with a common value being − 55 ° C (218 K; − 67 ° F). Surface temperatures may reach a high of about 20 ° C (293 K; 68 ° F) at noon, at the equator, and a low of about − 153 ° C (120 K; − 243 ° F) at the poles. Actual temperature measurements at the Viking landers' site range from − 17.2 ° C (256.0 K; 1.0 ° F) to − 107 ° C (166 K; − 161 ° F). The warmest soil temperature estimated by the Viking Orbiter was 27 ° C (300 K; 81 ° F). The Spirit rover recorded a maximum daytime air temperature in the shade of 35 ° C (308 K; 95 ° F), and regularly recorded temperatures well above 0 ° C (273 K; 32 ° F), except in winter.",what is the temperature range of mars in fahrenheit
america's incarceration rate compared to other countries,"['https://spiegelmock.com/2017/05/19/drug-war-still-going-for-some-reason/', 'https://dnewshq.com/2016/09/16/us-kills-over-20-million-is-venezuela-next/', 'https://www.reidlawalabama.com/news/2016/8/10/is-marijuana-use-becoming-mainstream', 'https://www.projectempathyvr.com/recent-news/2016/9/21/walk-in-a-prisoners-shoes-with-virtual-reality-filmmaking', 'http://www.marxist.com/trump-s-advisers-slander-socialism-a-reply-to-white-house-lies-part-four/print.htm', 'http://www.theblackamericanmuslim.com/glossary', 'https://artvoice.com/2019/02/11/rep-alexandria-ocasio-cortez-our-system-is-innocent-until-proven-guilty-only-for-the-rich/']","In October 2013, the incarceration rate of the United States of America was the highest in the world, at 716 per 100,000 of the national population. While the United States represents about 4.4 percent of the world's population, it houses around 22 percent of the world's prisoners. Corrections (which includes prisons, jails, probation, and parole) cost around $74 billion in 2007 according to the U.S. Bureau of Justice Statistics.",america's incarceration rate compared to other countries
i can see so far because i stand on the shoulders of giants,"['https://rhaf.memberclicks.net/', 'https://redshoesrock.com/2018/07/05/early-diagnosis-changes-the-game/', 'http://www.johns-blog.com/?page_id=400']","The metaphor of dwarfs standing on the shoulders of giants (Latin: nanos gigantum humeris insidentes) expresses the meaning of ""discovering truth by building on previous discoveries"". This concept has been traced to the 12th century, attributed to Bernard of Chartres. Its most familiar expression in English is by Isaac Newton in 1675: ""If I have seen further it is by standing on the shoulders of Giants.""",i can see so far because i stand on the shoulders of giants
who sings the country song how do you like me now,"['https://es.scribd.com/doc/94542652/M-Commerce-Technologies-Services-And-Business-Models', 'http://www.countrymusicbookingagency.com/musician/toby-keith.php', 'https://www.bbparcodelcilento.com/people/46104-toby-keith', 'http://klihi.cation74.ru/great-expectation-online-dating-394.html', 'https://ja.scribd.com/document/80445217/9783642025242-c1', 'https://nightlifeco.com/omaha/event/toby-keith-jul-26-2018-1', 'https://www.scribd.com/document/58002709/Rural-Elect']","Signed to DreamWorks Records Nashville in 1998, Keith released his breakthrough single ""How Do You Like Me Now?!"" in late 1999. This song, the title track to his 1999 album of the same name, was the number one country song of 2000, and one of several chart-toppers during his tenure on DreamWorks Nashville. His next three albums, Pull My Chain, Unleashed, and Shock'n Y'all, produced three more number ones each, and all of the albums were certified 4x Platinum. A second Greatest Hits package followed in 2004, and after that, he released Honkytonk University.",who sings the country song how do you like me now
