who is the movie the blind side about,"['http://www.isnnews.net/zocalo/archive/05-02-2010.shtml', 'http://life.goodnewseverybody.com/mentoring.html', 'https://www.frutal.info/guroyvaqfvqrzbivrerivrjrffnl933d98d0a6.asp', 'http://www.isnnews.net/zocalo/archive/05-23-2010.shtml', 'https://smashingtops.com/people/10-sports-films-even-non-sports-fans-should-watch/', 'https://www.greatertalent.com/press/the-cleveland-daily-banner-tuohy-to-help-with-disaster-relief-efforts/', 'http://www.theindependentbd.com/arcprint/details/11111/2015-08-11']","The Blind Side is a 2009 American biographical sports drama film written and directed by John Lee Hancock, based on the 2006 book The Blind Side: Evolution of a Game by Michael Lewis. The storyline features Michael Oher, an offensive lineman who was drafted by the Baltimore Ravens of the National Football League (NFL). The film follows Oher from his impoverished upbringing, through his years at Wingate Christian School (a fictional representation of Briarcrest Christian School in Memphis, Tennessee), his adoption by Sean and Leigh Anne Tuohy, to his position as one of the most highly coveted prospects in college football, then finally becoming a first-round pick of the Ravens.",who is the movie the blind side about
is highway 8 in houston a toll road,"['https://www.milebymile.com/main/highway-2229.html', 'http://relocatingtohouston.org/article/13/3/', 'https://www.milebymile.com/main/highway-2223.html', 'https://hackettstownweekly.com/tier-1-law-1-9-truck-accident-by-area/', 'https://www.milebymile.com/main/highway-1883.html', 'https://www.houstonpublicmedia.org/articles/news/transportation/2015/05/15/212198/the-state-of-houston-toll-roads/', 'https://www.saint-paul-real-estate.com/vadnais-heights/']","Beltway 8, a state highway, runs mostly along the frontage roads of the tollway, only using the main lanes where they are free between Interstate Highway 45 (North Freeway) and Interstate Highway 69 / U.S. 59 (Eastex Freeway). The main lanes elsewhere are the Sam Houston Tollway, a toll road owned and operated by the Harris County Toll Road Authority (HCTRA). East of Houston, the Tollway crosses the Houston Ship Channel on the Sam Houston Ship Channel Bridge, a toll bridge; this forms a gap in Beltway 8 between Interstate Highway 10 (Baytown-East Freeway) and State Highway 225 (La Porte Freeway).",is highway 8 in houston a toll road
chemistry is usually classified as what type of science,"['https://worldscholarshipforum.com/top-25-masters-scholarship-for-chemistry-students/', 'https://chemistry.magnuscorpus.com/', 'http://xc365.info/73153-chemistry-in-daily-life-essay-in-urdu/', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/2792', 'http://ronbarceloviveahora.com/role-of-computer-in-chemistry.html', 'http://www.articleicon.com/chemistry/', 'https://www.drmiller.com/a-brief-history-of-system-theory/']","Chemistry occupies an intermediate position in a hierarchy of the sciences by reductive level between physics and biology. It is sometimes called the central science because it provides a foundation for understanding both basic and applied scientific disciplines at a fundamental level. Examples include plant chemistry (botany), the formation of igneous rocks (geology), how atmospheric ozone is formed and how environmental pollutants are degraded (ecology), the properties of the soil on the moon (astrophysics), how medications work (pharmacology), and how to collect DNA evidence at a crime scene (forensics).",chemistry is usually classified as what type of science
when did the dust bowl begin and end,"['http://www.pilotguides.com/articles/route-66-study-guide/', 'http://cowboykisses.blogspot.com/2015/03/', 'https://quizlet.com/24169268/music-160-chapters-5-7-flash-cards/', 'http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Dust_Bowl', 'http://hitchhikersgui.de/Dust_Bowl', 'http://web.archive.org/web/20170208062959/https:/www.ncdc.noaa.gov/paleo/drought/drght_history.html', 'https://forum.prisonplanet.com/index.php?topic=234353.0']","The Dust Bowl, also known as the Dirty Thirties, was a period of severe dust storms that greatly damaged the ecology and agriculture of the American and Canadian prairies during the 1930s; severe drought and a failure to apply dryland farming methods to prevent wind erosion (the Aeolian processes) caused the phenomenon. The drought came in three waves, 1934, 1936, and 1939 -- 1940, but some regions of the high plains experienced drought conditions for as many as eight years. With insufficient understanding of the ecology of the plains, farmers had conducted extensive deep plowing of the virgin topsoil of the Great Plains during the previous decade; this had displaced the native, deep-rooted grasses that normally trapped soil and moisture even during periods of drought and high winds. The rapid mechanization of farm equipment, especially small gasoline tractors, and widespread use of the combine harvester contributed to farmers' decisions to convert arid grassland (much of which received no more than 10 inches (~ 250 mm) of precipitation per year) to cultivated cropland.",when did the dust bowl begin and end
what is the most popular food in denmark,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/German_cuisine', 'https://www.tripinsiders.net/copenhagen-in-pictures-best-places-and-key-tips/', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/Meatball', 'http://www.thisveganlyfe.com/2012/02/', 'https://www.dphtrading.com/items/collectibles/plates/commemorative-jubilee-and-memorial-plates/brewery-plates', 'http://gogoanow.com/essentially-goa/', 'https://www.gavinsz.com/travel_65.shtml']","Danish cuisine (Danish: det danske køkken), originating from the peasant population's own local produce, was enhanced by cooking techniques developed in the late 19th century and the wider availability of goods after the Industrial Revolution. The open sandwiches, known as smørrebrød, which in their basic form are the usual fare for lunch, can be considered a national speciality when prepared and decorated with a variety of fine ingredients. Hot meals are traditionally prepared from ground meats, such as frikadeller (meat balls) and medisterpølse, or from more substantial meat and fish dishes such as flæskesteg (roast pork with crackling) or kogt torsk (poached cod) with mustard sauce and trimmings. Denmark is known for its Carlsberg and Tuborg beers and for its akvavit and bitters, but amongst the Danes themselves imported wine has gained in popularity since the 1960s.",what is the most popular food in denmark
where did the term ivory tower come from,"['http://www.thesubversivearchaeologist.com/2012/01/wacky-wednesdays-anyone.html', 'https://roeknowsbest.com/author/roemusicsblog/page/31/', 'http://www.yuetuinfo.ga/archives/date/2017/03', 'https://lionaid.org/news/tag/wildcru', 'http://www.gutenberg.us/articles/eng/Ivory_tower']","The term ivory tower originates in the Biblical Song of Solomon (7: 4) and was later used as an epithet for Mary. From the 19th century, it has been used to designate an environment of intellectual pursuit disconnected from the practical concerns of everyday life. In American English usage it is also used as shorthand for academia or the university.",where did the term ivory tower come from
what years did the revolutionary war take place,"['https://www.rubywilbur.com/american-revolution-list-of-soldiers/', 'http://www.factbites.com/topics/American-Revolutionary-War', 'https://www.cs.mcgill.ca/~rwest/wikispeedia/wpcd/wp/a/American_Revolutionary_War.htm', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/1st_American_Regiment_(1783%E2%80%931784)', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Charles_Willson_Peale', 'https://fallout.gamepedia.com/American_Revolutionary_War', 'https://kreditx0l33wx.webgarden.cz/rubriky/american-war-of-independence']","The American Revolutionary War (1775 -- 1783), also known as the American War of Independence, was a global war that began as a conflict between Great Britain and its Thirteen Colonies which declared independence as the United States of America.",what years did the revolutionary war take place
why is puerto rico a part of the us,"['https://yourfreetemplates.com/puerto-rico-map-download/', 'https://alchetron.com/Puerto-Rico', 'https://caribbean-tour.com/Information-about-Puerto-Rico.html', 'https://blog.sjvassoc.com/nitza_posts.html', 'http://www.fsa-law.com/english/martindale.asp?loc=profile', 'http://www.goh2otours.com/tours/puerto-rico/', 'https://residencies.io/residency/puerto-rico/temporary-residency/pr1']","An archipelago among the Greater Antilles, Puerto Rico includes the main island of Puerto Rico and a number of smaller ones, such as Mona, Culebra, and Vieques. The capital and most populous city is San Juan. Its official languages are Spanish and English, though Spanish predominates. The island's population is approximately 3.4 million. Puerto Rico's history, tropical climate, natural scenery, traditional cuisine, and tax incentives make it a destination for travelers from around the world.",why is puerto rico a part of the us
when did the eastern roman empire become the byzantine empire,"['http://growshopeurotop.eu/23865-importance-of-unity-short-essay.html', 'http://vikendpozitive.eu/65835-compare-contrast-egypt-mesopotamia-essay.html', 'http://aipef.info/70838-my-family-essay-in-japanese-language.html', 'http://ms4bio.eu/33482-spring-and-port-wine-essay.html', 'https://www.thenationalherald.com/220094/byzantium-for-beginners-at-holy-trinity-cathedral-in-manhattan/', 'http://melkite.org.au/node/6', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Tetrarchy']","The first use of the term ""Byzantine"" to label the later years of the Roman Empire was in 1557, when the German historian Hieronymus Wolf published his work Corpus Historiæ Byzantinæ, a collection of historical sources. The term comes from ""Byzantium"", the name of the city of Constantinople before it became Constantine's capital. This older name of the city would rarely be used from this point onward except in historical or poetic contexts. The publication in 1648 of the Byzantine du Louvre (Corpus Scriptorum Historiae Byzantinae), and in 1680 of Du Cange's Historia Byzantina further popularised the use of ""Byzantine"" among French authors, such as Montesquieu. However, it was not until the mid-19th century that the term came into general use in the Western world.",when did the eastern roman empire become the byzantine empire
