who votes for the president of the united states,"['https://sonsoflibertymedia.com/no-matter-happens-wont-know-next-president-will-december-19th/', 'http://miseryindex2008.blogspot.com/2008/11/obama-is-not-president-yet.html', 'https://www.fairvote.org/the_electoral_college', 'https://mail.sourcewatch.org/index.php?title=Presidential_Electoral_College', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Candidate', 'http://etaarifa.com/americans-ready-for-long-election-night/', 'http://wikielections.com/results/index.php/us-elections/us-election-results/37-us-past-result-history-winner-candidate-party-wise.html']","The election of President and Vice President of the United States is an indirect election in which citizens of the United States who are registered to vote in one of the 50 U.S. states or Washington, D.C. cast ballots for members of the U.S. Electoral College, known as electors. These electors then in turn cast direct votes, known as electoral votes, for President and Vice President. The candidate who receives an absolute majority of electoral votes for President or Vice President (currently, at least 270 out of a total of 538) is then elected to that office. If no candidate receives an absolute majority for President, the House of Representatives chooses the President; if no one receives a majority for Vice President, then the Senate chooses the Vice President.",who votes for the president of the united states
when was the american museum of natural history built,"['http://www.thefullwiki.org/American_Museum_of_Natural_History', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Aurora_Pyramid_of_Hope', 'https://rentalcarmomma.com/ace/manhattan.htm']","In 1874, the cornerstone was laid for the museum's first building, which is now hidden from view by the many buildings in the complex that today occupy most of Manhattan Square. The original Victorian Gothic building, which was opened in 1877, was designed by J. Wrey Mould, both already closely identified with the architecture of Central Park.",when was the american museum of natural history built
the corpus callosum is a region of white matter that,"['https://ascensionglossary.com/index.php/Corpus_Callosum', 'http://www.sciforums.com/threads/concept-of-ambiphrenia.132938/', 'https://med.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Anatomy_and_Physiology/Book%3A_Anatomy_and_Physiology_(Boundless)/11%3A_Central_Nervous_System/11.7%3A_The_Cerebrum/11.7C%3A_White_Matter_of_the_Cerebrum', 'https://www.disabled-world.com/definitions/braindef.php', 'http://psychology.children-of-the-amphioxus.com/table-of-contents/corpus-callosum', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=corpus+callosum+damage+effects&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://neuroscientificallychallenged.com/blog/2-minute-neuroscience-corpus-callosum']","The corpus callosum (/ ˈkɔːrpəs kəˈloʊsəm /; Latin for ""tough body""), also callosal commissure, is a wide commissure, a flat bundle of commissural fibers, about 10 cm long beneath the cerebral cortex in the brains of placental mammals. It spans part of the longitudinal fissure, connects the left and right cerebral hemispheres, and enables communication between the hemispheres. It is the largest white matter structure in the human brain, consisting of 200 -- 250 million axonal projections.",the corpus callosum is a region of white matter that
what does it mean to be on bath salts,"['https://allaboutheaven.org/science/bath-salts/121', 'https://uatests.com/drug-test-by-drug/bath_salts.php', 'https://druginfo.sl.nsw.gov.au/drugs-z-drugs/bath-salts', 'http://yourcountryside.info/88444-methylone-and-other-party-drugs/', 'https://ammonlabs.com/resources-bathsalts/', 'http://straightupvc.org/bath-salts-confusion-reality-and-danger/', 'https://www.buyatestkit.com/refine-by-drug/bath-salts/']","""Bath salts"" (also ""psychoactive bath salts"", ""PABS"" or in the United Kingdom monkey dust) is a term used to describe a number of recreational designer drugs. The name derives from instances in which the drugs were sold disguised as true bath salts. The white powder, granules, or crystals often resemble true bath salts such as Epsom salts, but are very different chemically. The drug's packaging often states ""not for human consumption"" in an attempt to circumvent drug prohibition laws. Recreational drugs have also been similarly disguised as plant food, hookah cleaner, and other products.",what does it mean to be on bath salts
which three veins empty into the porta vein,['https://patents.google.com/patent/WO2016009337A2/en'],"The portal vein is usually formed by the confluence of the superior mesenteric and splenic veins and also receives blood from the inferior mesenteric, gastric, and cystic veins.",which three veins empty into the porta vein
is mac short for macaroni or mac and cheese,"['https://www.charliesbbqandgrille.org/glossary/mac-cheese/', 'https://www.barrypopik.com/index.php/new_york_city/entry/the_mac_in_mac', 'https://www.thequiz.com/pick-or-pass-on-these-comfort-foods-to-find-out-how-many-kids-are-in-your-future-2/', 'https://www.easyanddelish.com/microwave-mac-and-cheese/', 'https://eatmeerecipes.co.za/american-food/creamiest-cheesiest-macaroni-cheese/', 'https://hurryupmom.com/category/lunch-box-idea/', 'https://www.pinoybisnes.com/food-business-ideas/25-macaroni-and-cheese-recipes/']","Macaroni and cheese -- also called mac and cheese in American, Canadian, and macaroni pie in Caribbean English; and macaroni cheese in the United Kingdom -- is a dish of English origin, consisting of cooked macaroni pasta and a cheese sauce, most commonly cheddar. It can also incorporate other ingredients, such as breadcrumbs, meat and vegetables.",is mac short for macaroni or mac and cheese
where does the delaware river start and end,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Gazela', 'http://www.primidi.com/delaware_river', 'https://ncsl.typepad.com/the_thicket/games/', 'https://www.exploringthelocallife.com/exploring-poconos-delaware-water-gap/', 'https://nurturenaturecenter.org/about-nnc/our-community/', 'https://www.americanrivers.org/river/delaware-river/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Delaware_River.html']","The Delaware River rises in two main branches that descend from the western flank of the Catskill Mountains in New York. The West Branch begins near Mount Jefferson in the Town of Jefferson in Schoharie County. The river's East Branch begins at Grand Gorge near Roxbury in Delaware County. These two branches flow west and merge near Hancock in Delaware County, and the combined waters flow as the Delaware River south. Through its course, the Delaware River forms the boundaries between Pennsylvania and New York, the entire boundary between New Jersey and Pennsylvania, and most of the boundary between Delaware and New Jersey. The river meets tide-water at the junction of Morrisville, Pennsylvania, and Trenton, New Jersey, at the Falls of the Delaware. The river's navigable, tidal section served as a conduit for shipping and transportation that aided the development of the industrial cities of Trenton, Camden, and Philadelphia. The mean freshwater discharge of the Delaware River into the estuary of Delaware Bay is 11,550 cubic feet per second (327 m / s).",where does the delaware river start and end
location of ahmedabad on political map of india,"['http://www.primidi.com/what_is_ahmedabad', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/ahmedabad', 'https://www.travelshelper.com/destinations/asia/india/ahmedabad/', 'https://latestjobs.co.in/current-jobs-in-ahmedabad/', 'http://www.abudhabi2.com/real-estate-property-builders-in-ahmedabad/', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Ahmedabad.html', 'http://www.groupbookings.in/node/4064']","Ahmedabad (/ ˈɑːmɪdəbɑːd / (listen)), also known as Amdavad or Karnavati, is the largest city and former capital of Gujarat, which is a state in India. It is the administrative headquarters of the Ahmedabad district and the seat of the Gujarat High Court. With a population of more than 6.3 million and an extended population of 7.8 million, it is the sixth largest city and seventh largest metropolitan area of India. Ahmedabad is located on the banks of the Sabarmati River, 30 km (19 mi) from the state capital Gandhinagar, which is its twin city.",location of ahmedabad on political map of india
how much of the united states is owned by other countries,"['https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Economy_of_the_United_States', 'http://aeon-solutions.info/yyyz/debt-to-income-ratio-chart-ceha.php', 'http://piglix.com/piglix/National_debt_of_the_United_States', 'https://www.debt.org/government/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Robert_Pollin', 'https://www.gold-eagle.com/article/dollar-index-breaks-below-100-rising-yields%E2%80%A6-wholesale-us-treasury-bond-dump-coming', 'http://whywait4years.com/?tag=murder']","As of April 30, 2018, debt held by the public was $15.3 trillion and intragovernmental holdings were $5.7 trillion, for a total or ""National Debt"" of $21 trillion. Debt held by the public was approximately 77% of GDP in 2017, ranked 43rd highest out of 207 countries. The Congressional Budget Office forecast in April 2018 that the ratio will rise to nearly 100% by 2028, perhaps higher if current policies are extended beyond their scheduled expiration date. As of December 2017, $6.3 trillion or approximately 45% of the debt held by the public was owned by foreign investors, the largest being China (about $1.18 trillion) then Japan (about $1.06 trillion).",how much of the united states is owned by other countries
who must approve treaties made by the president,"['http://mafirearmsafety.com/2012/07/u-n-arms-trade-treaty-worldwide-civilian-disarmament-plot-fails/', 'http://www.federaljack.com/state-secession-and-dissolution-from-the-union-on-the-horizon-pros-and-cons-behind-state-secession/', 'http://www.maggiesnotebook.com/2015/03/greta-lectures-obama-on-iran-treaty-he-cant-do-that-transcript/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Foreign_policy_of_the_United_States', 'http://www.adisgruntledrepublican.com/2015/09/senator-corker-opposes-implementation.html', 'https://www.conservativereview.com/news/bob-corker-wages-last-minute-blitz-lock-iran-nuclear-deal-permanently/', 'https://aconservativesmusings.com/2015/07/14/nuclear-agreement-with-iran-a-historical-disaster/']","The Treaty Clause is part of Article II, Section 2, Clause 2, of the United States Constitution, that empowers the President of the United States to propose and chiefly negotiate agreements between the United States and other countries, which, upon receiving the advice and consent of a two-thirds supermajority vote of the United States Senate, become treaties under international law.",who must approve treaties made by the president
who propounded entrepreneurship as a theory of business,"['http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Joseph_Schumpeter', 'http://marysplacect.com/ontario/schumpeter-theory-of-economic-growth-pdf.php', 'https://www.begegnungshof.info/creative-writing-cheltenham2098.asp']","Schumpeter's relationships with the ideas of other economists were quite complex in his most important contributions to economic analysis -- the theory of business cycles and development. Following neither Walras nor Keynes, Schumpeter starts in The Theory of Economic Development with a treatise of circular flow which, excluding any innovations and innovative activities, leads to a stationary state. The stationary state is, according to Schumpeter, described by Walrasian equilibrium. The hero of his story is the entrepreneur.",who propounded entrepreneurship as a theory of business
why and how did we once have a national speed limit,"['http://study-mail.info/speed-unlimited-maryland.html', 'http://leo-subs.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=8225', 'https://hootwisdom.org/td-monnex-meloche-car-insurance/car-insurance-bill-before-congress/', 'https://www.cliffsnotes.com/study-guides/american-government/public-policy/the-policymaking-process', 'https://www.good2go.com/blog/fast-and-furious-are-us-highway-speed-limits-getting-faster/', 'https://www.byrddavis.com/Motor-Vehicle-Accidents/Speeding-Accidents.shtml', 'http://bandbattle.tk/concord-casino-wien.html']","In response to the 1973 oil crisis, Congress enacted the National Maximum Speed Law that created the universal 55 miles per hour (89 km / h) speed limit. Whether this reduced gasoline consumption is debated and the impact on safety is unclear; studies and opinions of safety advocates are mixed.",why and how did we once have a national speed limit
when did the doctrine of papal infallibility begin,"['https://en.unionpedia.org/December_8', 'http://phos-alethinon.blogspot.com/2013/03/infallible-pope-and-inerrant-bible.html', 'https://rome.us/the-vatican-city/', 'https://francismary.org/papal-infallibility-explained-can-the-pope-never-be-wrong/', 'http://www.jesuit.org.uk/blog/dogma-%E2%80%9C-arrogant-declaration-opinion%E2%80%9D?page=1', 'http://www.pravmir.com/metropolitan-hilarion-volokolamskon-issue-primacy-universal-church/', 'http://www.exegeticalapologetics.com/2018/05/absence-of-papal-views-among-earliest.html']","This doctrine was defined dogmatically at the First Ecumenical Council of the Vatican of 1869 -- 1870, but had been defended before that, existing already in medieval theology and being the majority opinion at the time of the Counter-Reformation.",when did the doctrine of papal infallibility begin
where is mount logan located on a map,"['http://www.realmantravels.com/2017/08/mount-logan.html', 'https://globalquiz.org/en/toughest-mountains-riddles/', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Mount_Cook_(Saint_Elias_Mountains)', 'http://www.factbites.com/topics/Mount-Logan', 'https://gogeomatics.ca/ten-interesting-facts-about-the-geography-of-canada/', 'https://www.astis.com/products/logan', 'https://www.mountainguides.com/logan.shtml']","Mount Logan / ˈloʊɡən / is the highest mountain in Canada and the second-highest peak in North America, after Denali. The mountain was named after Sir William Edmond Logan, a Canadian geologist and founder of the Geological Survey of Canada (GSC). Mount Logan is located within Kluane National Park Reserve in southwestern Yukon, less than 40 kilometres (25 mi) north of the Yukon / Alaska border. Mount Logan is the source of the Hubbard and Logan Glaciers. Logan is believed to have the largest base circumference of any non-volcanic mountain on Earth (a large number of shield volcanoes are much larger in size and mass), including a massif with eleven peaks over 5,000 metres (16,400 ft).",where is mount logan located on a map
