what is the meaning of anger in english,"['https://memorable-scaring.gq/anger-management-series-download-19398', 'https://codepoints.net/U+1F4A2', 'https://www.50plus-club.ie/forum/stages-t63348.html', 'http://orangelt.us/p9rc9w6j3.html', 'https://www.counselling-directory.org.uk/counsellor-articles/anger-and-our-behaviour', 'http://participal.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=40967', 'http://getbanta.com/2018/01/26/6-ways-control-anger-moment/']","Anger or wrath is an intense emotional response. It is an emotion that involves a strong uncomfortable and hostile response to a perceived provocation, hurt or threat. Anger can occur when a person feels their personal boundaries are being or are going to be violated. Some have a learned tendency to react to anger through retaliation as a way of coping. Raymond Novaco of University of California Irvine, who since 1975 has published a plethora of literature on the subject, stratified anger into three modalities: cognitive (appraisals), somatic-affective (tension and agitations), and behavioral (withdrawal and antagonism). William DeFoore, an anger-management writer, described anger as a pressure cooker: we can only apply pressure against our anger for a certain amount of time until it explodes.",what is the meaning of anger in english
who played clarence the angel in it's a wonderful life,"['https://hip2save.com/tips/christmas-movie-bucket-list/comment-page-1/', 'http://dekalbcountycvb.com/event/egyptian-theatre-holiday-movie/', 'https://dekalbcountyonline.com/2017/12/its-a-wonderful-life-showing-downtown-dekalb-sunday/', 'https://dekalbcountyevents.com/events/2018/12/egyptian-theatre-presents-its-a-wonderful-life-in-35mm/', 'http://ashmann.uk/tag/film/', 'https://www.saultthisweek.com/news/local-news/northland-chorus-chooses-classic-tale-for-55th-show-2', 'http://www.warpedfactor.com/2015/12/slouch-potato-at-christmas.html']","The film stars James Stewart as George Bailey, a man who has given up his dreams in order to help others and whose imminent suicide on Christmas Eve brings about the intervention of his guardian angel, Clarence Odbody (Henry Travers). Clarence shows George all the lives he has touched and how different life in his community of Bedford Falls would be had he never been born.",who played clarence the angel in it's a wonderful life
what does the star mean on the texas flag,"['https://mail.dinesh.com/history_of_logos/nfl_logos/dallas_cowboys_logo_design_and_history.html', 'http://creativecustomknives.blogspot.com/2013/?widgetType=BlogArchive&widgetId=BlogArchive1&action=toggle&dir=open&toggle=WEEKLY-1398582000000&toggleopen=WEEKLY-1387699200000', 'https://starspangledflags.com/shop/nylon-texas-state-flag-subscription/', 'https://todocamarasreflex.com/online-payday-loans-dodson-la/', 'https://www.dixiememories.com/files/Confederate%20national%20flags.html']","The idea of the ""lone star"" is, in fact, an older symbol predating the flag which was used to symbolize Texans' solidarity in declaring independence from Mexico. A similar lone star was on the ""Burnet Flag,"" which was resembled the flag of the short-lived Republic of West Florida. The ""Lone Star"" is still seen today as a symbol of Texas' independent spirit, and gave rise to the state's official nickname ""The Lone Star State.""",what does the star mean on the texas flag
what is the main use of java script,"['https://test.opentutorials.org/module/3180/18883', 'http://afcraf.metod-portal.ru/profile?id=123', 'https://darrenjw.wordpress.com/tag/sampler/']","As a multi-paradigm language, JavaScript supports event-driven, functional, and imperative (including object-oriented and prototype-based) programming styles. It has an API for working with text, arrays, dates, regular expressions, and basic manipulation of the DOM, but does not include any I / O, such as networking, storage, or graphics facilities, relying for these upon the host environment in which it is embedded.",what is the main use of java script
which method is used in the election of members of lok sabha,"['http://www.gkplanet.in/2015/12/election-commission-of-india.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Election_Commission_of_India.html', 'https://blog.iascgl.com/2017/04/constitutional-bodies-in-india.html', 'https://eci.gov.in/about/about-eci/the-setup-r1/', 'http://indpaedia.com/ind/index.php/India_and_its_Polity_(administrative_structure)', 'https://www.timesofelection.com/what-is-the-election-system-in-india/', 'https://jharkhand.pscnotes.com/jharkhand-mains/paper-iv/polity-paper-iv/the-election-commission-of-india/']","Elections are conducted according to the constitutional provisions, supplemented by laws made by Parliament. The major laws are Representation of the People Act, 1950, which mainly deals with the preparation and revision of electoral rolls, the Representation of the People Act, 1951 which deals, in detail, with all aspects of conduct of elections and post election disputes. The Supreme Court of India has held that where the enacted laws are silent or make insufficient provision to deal with a given situation in the conduct of elections, the Election Commission has the residuary powers under the Constitution to act in an appropriate manner. Originally the commission had only a single Chief Election Commissioner. Two additional Commissioners were appointed to the commission for the first time on 16 October 1989, but they had a very short tenure until 1 January 1990. The Election Commissioner Amendment Act, 1993 made the Election Commission a multi-member body. Later, on 1 October 1993, two additional Election Commissioners were appointed. The concept of a multi-member Commission has been in operation since then, with decision-making power by majority vote.",which method is used in the election of members of lok sabha
what is the popular name for st stephens day,"['http://money-news-online.com/blog/2017/12/27/27-12-2017-daily-news-hyip-industry/', 'http://dniwolne.eu/en-Europe-holidays-Luxembourg.html', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2014/12/26/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Revised_Julian_calendar', 'http://greenlivingpedia.org/Boxing_Day', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2018/12/26/', 'https://planetdepos.com/holiday-traditions-from-around-the-world/']","Saint Stephen's Day, or the Feast of Saint Stephen, is a Christian saint's day to commemorate Saint Stephen, the first Christian martyr or protomartyr, celebrated on 26 December in the Latin Church and 27 December in Eastern Christianity. The Eastern Orthodox Church adheres to the Julian calendar and mark Saint Stephen's Day on 27 December according to that calendar, which places it on 9 January of the Gregorian calendar used in secular contexts. In Latin Christian denominations, Saint Stephen's Day marks the second day of Christmastide.",what is the popular name for st stephens day
money for nothing and chicks for free meaning,"['https://coachguitar.com/en/lesson/artist/direstraits/money-for-nothing-elec/guitar-tab/moneyfornothingelec', 'https://doyouremember.com/28205/name-that-tune', 'http://fikrinet.tk/money-for-nothing-sheet-music.html', 'http://www.totallyfuzzy.net/ourtube/dire-straits/money-for-nothing-wembley-arena-video_b44ff0a2e.html', 'http://tamtrangantoan.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=45608', 'http://earnmymoney.tk/provence-casino.html', 'http://grupostereosiete.com/?p=49111']","""Money for Nothing"" is a single by British rock band Dire Straits, taken from their 1985 studio album Brothers in Arms. The song's lyrics are written from the point of view of two working-class men watching music videos and commenting on what they see. The song features a guest appearance by Sting singing background vocals, providing both the signature falsetto introduction and backing chorus of, ""I want my MTV."" The groundbreaking video was the first to be aired on MTV Europe when the network launched on 1 August 1987.",money for nothing and chicks for free meaning
animal viruses that have an envelope enter cells by,"['http://www.sumobrain.com/patents/wipo/Affinity-ligand-purification-glycosylated-biomolecules/WO2017144099A1.html', 'https://pictures-of-cats.org/Feline-Aids.html', 'http://botanystudies.com/viruses-test-questions/', 'https://biologyboom.com/viruses/', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/differences-between-bacteria-and-viruses-4070311', 'https://ki.se/en/mbb/lentiviral-vectors']","Some viruses (e.g. influenza and many animal viruses) have viral envelopes covering their protective protein capsids. The envelopes are typically derived from portions of the host cell membranes (phospholipids and proteins), but include some viral glycoproteins. They may help viruses avoid the host immune system. Glycoproteins on the surface of the envelope serve to identify and bind to receptor sites on the host's membrane. The viral envelope then fuses with the host's membrane, allowing the capsid and viral genome to enter and infect the host.",animal viruses that have an envelope enter cells by
how my brother leon brought a wife author,['https://www.slideshare.net/marjorieostos/3-short-stories'],"He is known for his widely anthologized short story ""How My Brother Leon Brought Home a Wife,"" the main story in the collection How My Brother Leon Brought Home a Wife and Other Short Stories, which won first prize in the Commonwealth Literary Contest in 1940.","Downloaded 115 times
The story follows Baldo as he accompanies his brother Leon returning home after many years, bringing with him a beautiful woman named Maria. On their journey back to Nagrebcan, Maria is amazed by the natural beauty and lights of the countryside. When they arrive, Leon introduces Maria to his mother, who welcomes her warmly. The next day, under a mango tree, Leon tells Baldo that he plans to live there with Maria after they marry."
each dot that makes up a satellite image is called a pixel. true or false,"['http://gbeelectronics.com/index.php/articles-menu/18-cctv-and-surveillance-category', 'https://graphicdesign.stackexchange.com/questions/121616/creating-a-brand-book-resolution-difference-between-retina-non-retina', 'https://www.inthow.com/perfect-camera-guide/', 'https://freeyork.org/entity/pixel/', 'https://vectormap.info/map_design_tutorials/seam-carving-for-content-aware-image-resizing/', 'http://www.colorcopiesmn.com/%EF%BB%BFminnesota/wayzata-mn-inexpensive-business-cards/', 'http://velo-city2013.com/?page_id=2337&project_id=76']","In digital imaging, a pixel, pel, dots, or picture element is a physical point in a raster image, or the smallest addressable element in an all points addressable display device; so it is the smallest controllable element of a picture represented on the screen.",each dot that makes up a satellite image is called a pixel. true or false
who was involved in the whiskey rebellion and why were they protesting,"['http://www.ohiofarmmuseum.com/?p=1227', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Pennsylvania%27s_18th_congressional_district', 'https://whiskeyrebellioncumberland.com/history/', 'https://military.wikia.org/wiki/Whiskey_Rebellion', 'http://hitchhikersgui.de/Whiskey_tax', 'https://riversong.wordpress.com/the-new-anti-federalists/', 'https://progressivepacific.blogspot.com/2017/01/3-dissidents-in-american-politics.html']","The Whiskey Rebellion (also known as the Whiskey Insurrection) was a tax protest in the United States beginning in 1791 during the presidency of George Washington. The so-called ""whiskey tax"" was the first tax imposed on a domestic product by the newly formed federal government. It became law in 1791, and was intended to generate revenue for the war debt incurred during the Revolutionary War. The tax applied to all distilled spirits, but American whiskey was by far the country's most popular distilled beverage in the 18th century, so the excise became widely known as a ""whiskey tax"". Farmers of the western frontier were accustomed to distilling their surplus rye, barley, wheat, corn, or fermented grain mixtures into whiskey. These farmers resisted the tax. In these regions, whiskey often served as a medium of exchange. Many of the resisters were war veterans who believed that they were fighting for the principles of the American Revolution, in particular against taxation without local representation, while the federal government maintained that the taxes were the legal expression of Congressional taxation powers.",who was involved in the whiskey rebellion and why were they protesting
what was the purpose of film studios producing 'b' movies,"['https://www.artsybeedigital.com/film-posters-history.html', 'https://lottiesworldofcakesandbakes.eu/poker/bingo-brasil-throwback-significado-17-09-2018.php', 'https://karakon-hikakuranking.info/corrigan-studio-roman-8-light-led-chandelier.aspx', 'http://brothers-ink.com/tag/republic-pictures/', 'http://tvtool.info/b-movie.html', 'http://as806.tk/samurai-poker-staking.html', 'https://factonista.org/modern-kitchen-brigade-organizational-chart']","A B movie or B film is a low-budget commercial movie, but not an arthouse film. In its original usage, during the Golden Age of Hollywood, the term more precisely identified films intended for distribution as the less-publicized bottom half of a double feature (akin to B-sides for recorded music). Although the U.S. production of movies intended as second features largely ceased by the end of the 1950s, the term B movie continues to be used in its broader sense to this day. In its post -- Golden Age usage, there is ambiguity on both sides of the definition: on the one hand, the primary interest of many inexpensive exploitation films is prurient; on the other, many B movies display a high degree of craft and aesthetic ingenuity.",what was the purpose of film studios producing 'b' movies
what are examples of physical security controls that protect against specific threats,"['http://benchmarksolution.com/products-software', 'https://www.jacksons-security.co.uk/pages/common/Jacksons.aspx?pg=2597', 'http://bufetesabogados.info/viewtopic.php?t=923', 'http://nationaltheftsearchandrecovery.wikidot.com/system:national-theft-search-recovery', 'http://www.netcost-security.fr/', 'http://negociostip.info/business-plan', 'https://www.delta7group.com/physical-security.html']","Physical security describes security measures that are designed to deny unauthorized access to facilities, equipment and resources and to protect personnel and property from damage or harm (such as espionage, theft, or terrorist attacks). Physical security involves the use of multiple layers of interdependent systems which include CCTV surveillance, security guards, protective barriers, locks, access control protocols, and many other techniques.",what are examples of physical security controls that protect against specific threats
where do tarantulas live in the us map,"['http://reference.allrefer.com/the-most-venomous-spiders-in-the-world-4188', 'http://www.animalspot.net/greater-flamingo.html', 'http://encyclopedia2.thefreedictionary.com/snake', 'http://theredneckhunter.com/id43.html', 'https://esg.censible.co/companies/Laureate-Education', 'https://www.hotelosterport.dk/en/blog/a-family-affair-8-amazing-things-to-do-with-kids-in-copenhagen', 'https://www.qalaxia.com/questions/What-are-Armadillos']","Tarantulas of various species occur throughout the United States, Mexico, in Central America, and throughout South America. Other species occur variously throughout Africa, much of Asia, and all of Australia. In Europe, some species occur in Spain, Portugal, Turkey, Italy, and Cyprus.",where do tarantulas live in the us map
when was texas admitted to the united states,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Annexation', 'https://www.sanantonioeducationforum.com/featured/san-antonio-texas-united-states-history-economy-climate-etc/', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/History_of_Kansas', 'https://texas.hometownlocator.com/', 'http://www.thomaslegion.net/americancivilwar/texascivilwarhistory.html', 'http://thomaslegioncherokee.tripod.com/thetexasrevolutiontexaswarofindependencehistoryandbattlemaps.html', 'http://texasescapes.com/They-Shoe-Horses-Dont-They/Texas-and-the-California-Gold-Rush.htm']","The Texas Annexation was the 1845 incorporation of the Republic of Texas into the United States of America, which was admitted to the Union as the 28th state on December 29, 1845.",when was texas admitted to the united states
where is barbados located on a world map,"['https://barbadosoffice.com/', 'https://realtyww.info/search/country,BB/category,66', 'http://icoco.me/travel-software/palesa-ibheshu.php', 'http://www.academicroom.com/social-sciences/american-studies/caribbean/barbados', 'https://www.hobotraveler.com/offshore-countries/barbados.php', 'https://lastbedsaustralia.com.au/holiday-destinations/category/barbados', 'http://jim4x4.com/thailand-top-car-exporter-to-barbados.html']","Barbados (/ bɑːrˈbeɪdɒs / (listen) or / bɑːrˈbeɪdoʊs /) is an island country in the Lesser Antilles, in the Caribbean region of North America. It is 34 kilometres (21 miles) in length and up to 23 km (14 mi) in width, covering an area of 432 km (167 sq mi). It is situated in the western area of the North Atlantic and 100 km (62 mi) east of the Windward Islands and the Caribbean Sea; therein, it is about 168 km (104 mi) east of the islands of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines and 400 km (250 mi) north-east of Trinidad and Tobago. Barbados is outside of the principal Atlantic hurricane belt. Its capital and largest city is Bridgetown.",where is barbados located on a world map
history of the hymn rock of ages cleft for me,"['https://www.ldshymns.com/lds-hymns-101-125/111-rock-of-ages', 'https://www.pickenscountyteaparty.com/shovels-and-rope-lyrics/', 'https://www.matteorizzolli.net/christian-hymn-book/', 'http://www.petertepper.com/author/admin/page/11/']","Traditionally, it is held that Toplady drew his inspiration from an incident in the gorge of Burrington Combe in the Mendip Hills in England. Toplady, a preacher in the nearby village of Blagdon, was travelling along the gorge when he was caught in a storm. Finding shelter in a gap in the gorge, he was struck by the title and scribbled down the initial lyrics.",history of the hymn rock of ages cleft for me
what does it mean to be all nba first team,"['https://wikivivid.com/wiki/Kevin_Garnett', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Candace_Parker', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/All-NBA_First_Team', 'http://www.sports-trivia-nut.com/category/basketball-trivia-questions/page/2/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Ben_Wallace', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/NBA_All-Defensive_Team.html', 'http://www.edubilla.com/sport/basketball/players/michael-jordan/']","The All-NBA Team is an annual National Basketball Association (NBA) honor bestowed on the best players in the league following every NBA season. The voting is conducted by a panel of sportswriters and broadcasters throughout the United States and Canada. The team has been selected in every season of the league's existence, dating back to its inaugural season in 1946. The All-NBA Team originally had two teams, but since 1988 it is composed of three five-man lineups -- a first, second, and third team, typically comprising a total of 15 roster spots.",what does it mean to be all nba first team
who won academy awards for the color purple,"['http://www.etinside.com/?p=694', 'https://www.allaboutmovies.com.au/index.php/poster-formats/day-bill-posters/item/109726-the-color-purple-movie-poster-daybill-whoopi-goldberg-oprah-winfrey-steven-spielberg', 'https://hd-report.com/2010/02/19/new-streaming-hd-titles-from-netflix/']","The Color Purple was nominated for eleven Academy Awards, including Best Picture, Best Actress for Goldberg and Best Supporting Actress for both Avery and Winfrey. It failed to win any of them, tying the record set by 1977's The Turning Point for the most Oscar nominations without a single win.",who won academy awards for the color purple
where does the zambezi river begin and end,"['http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Zambezi_River', 'http://www.karibainns.com/-zambezi-river', 'https://www.sampspeak.in/2013/12/mugabe-wants-victoria-falls-renamed-as.html', 'http://www.geologypage.com/2014/11/zambezi-river.html', 'https://www.travelerbase.com/index.php?proc=search&term=10%20Best%20Places%20to%20Visit%20in%20Zambia', 'https://www.eastafricatravelcompany.com/destinations/victoria-falls/', 'http://www.gearthhacks.com/dlcat120/Dams,-Canals,-Rivers.htm']","The Zambezi (also spelled Zambeze and Zambesi) is the fourth-longest river in Africa, the longest east-flowing river in Africa and the largest flowing into the Indian Ocean from Africa. The area of its basin is 1,390,000 square kilometres (540,000 sq mi), slightly less than half of the Nile's. The 2,574-kilometre-long river (1,599 mi) rises in Zambia and flows through eastern Angola, along the eastern border of Namibia and the northern border of Botswana, then along the border between Zambia and Zimbabwe to Mozambique, where it crosses the country to empty into the Indian Ocean.",where does the zambezi river begin and end
where does the energy needed to produce atp come from,"['https://bioekuiliber.com/the-cell/', 'https://www.shomusbiology.com/biochemistry.html', 'https://www.simply.science/biology/cell-biology/cellular-respiration/introduction', 'https://www.passbiology.co.nz/biology-level-2/as-91155-demonstrate-understanding-of-adaptations-of-animals-to-their-way-of-life', 'https://biologywise.com/how-is-photosynthesis-related-to-cellular-respiration', 'https://www.lipovon.com/author/lpcom_admin/', 'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/mhccbiology101/chapter/7-4-an-overview-of-cellular-respiration/']","Cellular respiration is a set of metabolic reactions and processes that take place in the cells of organisms to convert biochemical energy from nutrients into adenosine triphosphate (ATP), and then release waste products. The reactions involved in respiration are catabolic reactions, which break large molecules into smaller ones, releasing energy in the process, as weak so-called ""high-energy"" bonds are replaced by stronger bonds in the products. Respiration is one of the key ways a cell releases chemical energy to fuel cellular activity. Cellular respiration is considered an exothermic redox reaction which releases heat. The overall reaction occurs in a series of biochemical steps, most of which are redox reactions themselves. Although cellular respiration is technically a combustion reaction, it clearly does not resemble one when it occurs in a living cell because of the slow release of energy from the series of reactions.",where does the energy needed to produce atp come from
who is the guy that plays the joker,"['http://www.michaelkorsoutletninc.com/2018/10/heath-andrew-ledger_3.html', 'http://wallpaperweb.org/wallpaper/boys/heath-ledger.html', 'http://hrvcanada.blogspot.com/2011/12/heath-ledger.html', 'https://targetedindividualscanada.com/2011/12/30/heath-ledger/', 'https://www.upi.com/topic/Heath_Ledger/news/', 'https://movieweb.com/heath-ledger-10th-anniversary-death-remembered-twitter/', 'https://www.lifetimetv.co.uk/people/heath-ledger']","In his penultimate film performance, Ledger played the Joker in Christopher Nolan's 2008 film The Dark Knight, released nearly six months after his death. While working on the film in London, Ledger told Sarah Lyall in their New York Times interview that he viewed The Dark Knight's Joker as a ""psychopathic, mass murdering, schizophrenic clown with zero empathy"". For his work on The Dark Knight, Ledger won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor with his family accepting it on his behalf, as well as numerous other posthumous awards, including the Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor, which Christopher Nolan accepted for him. At the time of his death on 22 January 2008, Ledger had completed about half of the work for his final film performance as Tony in Terry Gilliam's The Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus. Gilliam chose to adapt the film after his death by having fellow actors Johnny Depp, Jude Law, and Colin Farrell play ""fantasy transformations"" of his character so that Ledger's final performance could be seen in theatres.",who is the guy that plays the joker
what is the color guard in high school,"['http://www.statesboroband.com/home/color-guard/', 'http://www.ghsmusic.org/index.php/performing-groups/colorguard', 'http://www.ehsboosters.org/colorguard/', 'http://yhsband.weebly.com/color-guard--winter-guard.html', 'https://theotter.blog/category/film/', 'https://www.wgi.org/about-wgi/what-is-wgi/', 'https://www.colleyvilleheritageband.com/about.html']","Color guards can be found in most American colleges, universities, high schools, and middle schools, and independent drum corps. They use various equipment, including flags, rifles, and sabres, along with dance, to enhance the music of the marching band show. Usually, marching bands and color guards perform during football games at halftime. During marching band competitions, the guard adds to the overall score of the band and is also judged in a category usually called auxiliary.",what is the color guard in high school
what is the location of binghamton new york,"['https://sheepdogchurchsecurity.net/united-states-of-america/new%20york/general/church-security-in-binghamton-new-york/', 'https://www.assistedliving.com/new-york/binghamton/', 'http://newyorkstatefire.com/BinghamtonFD.htm', 'http://polukochevnik-download.gq/flight-club-new-york-store-145.php', 'https://bestchristianboardingschools.com/therapeutic-boarding-schools-in-binghamton-new-york/', 'https://www.roadsnacks.net/most-conservative-cities-in-ohio/', 'https://mohavecorealestate.com/']","Binghamton / ˈbɪŋəmtən / is a city in, and the county seat of, Broome County, New York, United States. It lies in the state's Southern Tier region near the Pennsylvania border, in a bowl-shaped valley at the confluence of the Susquehanna and Chenango Rivers. Binghamton is the principal city and cultural center of the Binghamton metropolitan area (also known as Greater Binghamton, or historically the Triple Cities), home to a quarter million people. The population of the city itself, according to the 2010 census, is 47,376.",what is the location of binghamton new york
how did the hundred years war marked the end of the feudal age in europe,"['https://military.wikia.org/wiki/Hundred_Years%27_War', 'https://www.ib-article.com/2012/11/war-shortest-and-oldest-in-world.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/November_24', 'http://michdioramas.com/crbst_217.html', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/11384', 'https://learnodo-newtonic.com/hundred-years-war-facts', 'http://commissarylounge.com/french-armies-of-the-hundred-years-war-1328-1429-men-at-arms-series-337.html']","The war owes its historical significance to multiple factors. By its end, feudal armies had been largely replaced by professional troops, and aristocratic dominance had yielded to a democratisation of the manpower and weapons of armies. Although primarily a dynastic conflict, the war gave impetus to ideas of French and English nationalism. The wider introduction of weapons and tactics supplanted the feudal armies where heavy cavalry had dominated, and artillery became important. The war precipitated the creation of the first standing armies in Western Europe since the time of the Western Roman Empire and thus helping to change their role in warfare. With respect to the belligerents, in France, civil wars, deadly epidemics, famines, and bandit free-companies of mercenaries reduced the population drastically. English political forces over time came to oppose the costly venture. The dissatisfaction of English nobles, resulting from the loss of their continental landholdings, became a factor leading to the civil wars known as the Wars of the Roses (1455 -- 1487).",how did the hundred years war marked the end of the feudal age in europe
how did the location of berlin enable the soviets to blockade the city successfully,"['https://www.poughkeepsiejournal.com/story/news/local/2018/12/06/seventy-years-after-united-nations-set-out-some-things-like-human-rights-universal-provisions-un/2125194002/', 'http://hasankeyf.info/34354-what-to-do-in-berlin-alone.html', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=how+many+days+was+the+berlin+airlift&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'https://suzannesmomsblog.com/tag/park/', 'https://nordic.businessinsider.com/inside-berlin-iconic-tempelhof-airport-2017-3/']","From July 17 to August 2, 1945, the victorious Allies reached the Potsdam Agreement on the fate of postwar Europe, calling for the division of defeated Germany into four temporary occupation zones (thus re-affirming principles laid out earlier by the Yalta Conference). These zones were located roughly around the then-current locations of the allied armies. Also divided into occupation zones, Berlin was located 100 miles (160 km) inside Soviet-controlled eastern Germany. The United States, United Kingdom, and France controlled western portions of the city, while Soviet troops controlled the eastern sector.",how did the location of berlin enable the soviets to blockade the city successfully
if there is a new zealand where is old zealand,"['http://www.mapsguidesandmore.com/Jordan', 'https://www.padmad.org/2014/12/important-and-prominent-islands-of.html', 'http://www.tourthenorth.com/packages/ghizer/', 'https://alchetron.com/Gitega-Province', 'http://www.cruisersforum.com/forums/f55/anybody-know-a-harbour-around-zeeland-with-drying-out-facilities-141171.html', 'https://drokov.com/region/zeeland', 'https://www.myrouteapp.com/en/library/countries/nl']","Zeeland (/ ˈziːlənd /; Dutch pronunciation: (ˈzeːlɑnt) (listen), Zeelandic: Zeêland (ˈzɪə̯lɑnt), historical English exonym Zealand) is the westernmost and least populous province of the Netherlands. The province, located in the south-west of the country, consists of a number of islands and peninsulas (hence its name, meaning ""Sealand"") and a strip bordering Belgium. Its capital is Middelburg. Its area is about 2,930 square kilometres (1,130 sq mi), of which almost 1,140 square kilometres (440 sq mi) is water, and it has a population of about 380,000.",if there is a new zealand where is old zealand
where does the phosphate come from in atp,"['https://rui-products.com/atp-adenosine-triphophate-15mg-ml-x-2ml/', 'http://worldheritage.org/article/WHEBN0000001800/Adenosine%20triphosphate', 'https://agriconlabsupply.com/product/atp-adenosine-triphophate-15mgml-x-2ml/', 'https://nutrilabproject.eu/atp-parts.html', 'https://aromaticstudies.com/prickly-pear-seed-oil/']","In terms of its structure, ATP consists of an adenine attached by the 9-nitrogen atom to the 1 ′ carbon atom of a sugar (ribose), which in turn is attached at the 5 ′ carbon atom of the sugar to a triphosphate group. In its many reactions related to metabolism, the adenine and sugar groups remain unchanged, but the triphosphate is converted to di-and monophosphate, giving respectively the derivatives ADP and AMP. The three phosphoryl groups are referred to as the alpha (α), beta (β), and, for the terminal phosphate, gamma (γ).",where does the phosphate come from in atp
where is fisherman's wharf located in san francisco,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Port_of_San_Francisco', 'http://worldneighborhoods.com/pictures/san-francisco-f67/civic-center-t355.html?sid=1f6d3a366bb9b1d9f39bdb23b4d8596f', 'http://www.ijustwantfood.com/2015/08/36hrs-layover-at-san-francsico-where-to.html', 'https://eatwelltraveleverywhereblog.wordpress.com/2017/05/05/an-introductory-guide-for-things-to-do-in-san-francisco/', 'http://www.ivanhenares.com/2008/06/fishermans-wharf-in-san-francisco.html', 'http://www.road-trip-usa.com/blog/9-reasons-to-visit-san-francisco-what-you-should-see-on-your-first-visit', 'http://infohostels.com/notizia.php?chiave=2736&title=3%20TOP%20to%20see%20in%20San%20Francisco']","Fisherman's Wharf is a neighborhood and popular tourist attraction in San Francisco, California. It roughly encompasses the northern waterfront area of San Francisco from Ghirardelli Square or Van Ness Avenue east to Pier 35 or Kearny Street. The F Market streetcar runs through the area, the Powell-Hyde cable car lines runs to Aquatic Park, at the edge of Fisherman's Wharf, and the Powell-Mason cable car line runs a few blocks away.",where is fisherman's wharf located in san francisco
what is the shortest distance from alaska to russia,"['https://www.baharmedia.net/2018/07/one-project-would-connect-the-world/', 'http://www.censoo.com/2015/03/russia-unveils-plans-for-high-speed-railway-and-superhighway-to-connect-europe-and-america/']","A Bering Strait crossing is a hypothetical bridge and / or tunnel spanning the relatively narrow and shallow Bering Strait between the Chukotka Peninsula in Russia and the Seward Peninsula in the U.S. state of Alaska. The bridge or tunnel would provide a connection linking North America (and potentially South America, see: Darién Gap) with Asia, Africa and Europe.",what is the shortest distance from alaska to russia
what does the yellow and green arrow mean,"['http://www.ben9166.com/2015/01/shoshinsha-wakaba-mark.html', 'https://codepoints.net/U+1F530']","The shoshinsha mark (初心者 マーク) or Wakaba mark (若葉 マーク), introduced in 1972, is a green and yellow V-shaped symbol that new Japanese drivers must display on their cars for one year. A driver must display this mark on the front and back of the car for one year after they obtain a standard driver's license. This obligation is only for a standard license, not for motorcycles, large vehicles, special cars, etc. Drivers who consider themselves beginners may continue to display the sign, even after the period of a year.",what does the yellow and green arrow mean
who is the actress that plays mary jane in spiderman,"['https://sex35.net/kirsten-dunst-upskirt-flashes-her-white-panties-in-los-angeles-2017.html', 'https://www.serienguide.tv/person/Kirsten-Dunst', 'https://celebritieswhogive.com/kirsten-dunst/', 'https://www.startiger.com/l?i=716', 'https://www.famousboard.com/threads/298-Kirsten-Dunst?s=6e6be0357ab712efb8b658dd5d6937e5', 'https://bikinimela.wordpress.com/category/kirsten-dunst-latest-movies/', 'http://viptrace.com/v/kirsten%20dunst']","Dunst achieved fame for her portrayal of Mary Jane Watson in Sam Raimi's Spider-Man trilogy (2002 -- 07). Since then, her films have included the romantic comedy Wimbledon (2004), the science fiction romantic comedy-drama Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind (2004) and Cameron Crowe's romantic tragicomedy Elizabethtown (2005). She played the title role in Sofia Coppola's biographical film Marie Antoinette (2006) and starred in the comedy film How to Lose Friends & Alienate People (2008). She won the Best Actress Award at the Cannes Film Festival and the Saturn Award for Best Actress for her performance in Lars von Trier's Melancholia (2011). She starred in the second season of the television series Fargo in 2015, playing the role of Peggy Blumquist, a hairdresser who gets mixed up in a war between two crime families. Her performance garnered widespread critical acclaim, leading to her winning the Critics' Choice Television Award for Best Actress and being nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress and the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Lead Actress in a Limited Series or Movie, losing to Lady Gaga and Sarah Paulson, respectively.",who is the actress that plays mary jane in spiderman
where is serbia on a map of europe,"['https://www.wikinow.co/topic/serbia', 'https://visaonlinevietnam.org/vietnam-embassy-in-yugoslavia/', 'https://www.vietnamvisaonline.net/vietnam-visa-requirements/serbia/', 'http://psihologijanis.rs/dpp/Serbia.asp', 'https://wn.com/Serbia_photos?from=serbiaphotos.com', 'https://www.apmex.com/category/29206/silver-other-coins-from-serbia', 'http://www.imeconf.org/about-serbia-and-belgrade/']","Serbia (/ ˈsɜːrbiə / (listen), Serbian: Србија / Srbija, IPA: (sř̩bija)), officially the Republic of Serbia (Serbian: Република Србија / Republika Srbija), is a landlocked country situated at the crossroads of Central and Southeast Europe in the southern Pannonian Plain and the central Balkans. It borders Hungary to the north; Romania and Bulgaria to the east; Macedonia to the south; Croatia, Bosnia, Montenegro to the west and claims a border with Albania through the disputed territory of Kosovo. Serbia numbers around 7 million residents; its capital, Belgrade, ranks among the oldest and largest cities in Southeastern Europe.",where is serbia on a map of europe
who plays dowager countess of grantham in downton abbey,"['http://legendshub.com/Maggie-Smith/', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Maggie_Smith', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Julie_Walters.html', 'https://master.dev.camdram.net/people/maggie-smith', 'http://www.getnetworth.com/maggie-smith-net-worth/', 'https://www.fitdib.com/then-and-now-what-happened-to-your-fave-80s-actresses/?utm_source=fitdib&utm_medium=bottom&utm_campaign=internal/']","Smith played Professor Minerva McGonagall in the Harry Potter film series (2001 -- 11). Other notable films include Love and Pain and the Whole Damn Thing (1973), Death on the Nile (1978), Clash of the Titans (1981), Evil Under the Sun (1982), Hook (1991), Sister Act (1992), The Secret Garden (1993), The Best Exotic Marigold Hotel (2012) and The Lady in the Van (2015). She won an Emmy Award in 2003 for My House in Umbria, to become one of the few actresses to have achieved the Triple Crown of Acting, and starred as Lady Violet Crawley, Dowager Countess of Grantham on Downton Abbey (2010 -- 15), for which she won three Emmys, her first non-ensemble Screen Actors Guild Award and her third Golden Globe. Her honorary awards include the BAFTA Special Award in 1993, the BAFTA Fellowship in 1996, and the Special Olivier Award in 2011. She received the Stratford Shakespeare Festival's Legacy Award in 2012, and the Bodley Medal by the University of Oxford's Bodleian Libraries in 2016.",who plays dowager countess of grantham in downton abbey
when does it start to snow in ireland,"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Climate_of_Ireland', 'https://www.donegalweatherchannel.ie/climate/', 'http://artmreza.com/info_for_foreigners.html', 'https://www.pax-house.com/dingle-weather/']","Severe cold weather is uncommon in Ireland with the majority of winter precipitation coming in the form of rain, although hills and mountainous regions in the country can commonly see up to 30 days of snowfall annually, with the Wicklow Mountains sometimes seeing 50 or more days of snowfall annually. Most low-lying regions of the island only see a few days of lying snow per year (from December to March inclusive), or may see no snow at all during some winters.",when does it start to snow in ireland
jama otolaryngology head and neck surgery impact factor,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Pediatrics_(journal)', 'https://www.knowpia.com/knowpedia/Journal_of_Systematic_Palaeontology', 'https://wn.com/Communication_theory', 'https://wn.com/Journal_of_Applied_Psychology', 'https://phys.org/journals/geophysical-research-letters/', 'https://phys.org/journals/american-politics-research/', 'https://balaipungut.com/']","According to the Journal Citation Reports, the journal has a 2016 impact factor of 2.915, ranking it 3rd out of 42 journals in the category ""Otorhinolaryngology"".",jama otolaryngology head and neck surgery impact factor
what is the standard notation for carbon dioxide,"['http://smartstones.nl/about-co2/about-co2/', 'https://www.hitechgas.com/carbon-dioxide/', 'http://www.revitaetechnologies.com/inventions/carbon-dioxide-problem-solved/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Fractional_crystallization_(geology)', 'https://minearc.com/blog/carbon-dioxide-carbon-monoxide/', 'https://www.bio-oxygen.com.au/carbon-dioxide-and-the-bio-oxygen-process/', 'https://www.encyclopedia.com/science-and-technology/technology/technology-terms-and-concepts/fossil-fuels']","Carbon dioxide (chemical formula CO) is a colorless gas with a density about 50% higher than that of dry air. Carbon dioxide consists of a carbon atom covalently double bonded to two oxygen atoms. It occurs naturally in Earth's atmosphere as a trace gas at a concentration of about 0.04 percent (400 ppm) by volume. Natural sources include volcanoes, hot springs and geysers, and it is freed from carbonate rocks by dissolution in water and acids. Because carbon dioxide is soluble in water, it occurs naturally in groundwater, rivers and lakes, ice caps, glaciers and seawater. It is present in deposits of petroleum and natural gas. Carbon dioxide is odorless at normally encountered concentrations, however at high concentrations it has a sharp and acidic odor.",what is the standard notation for carbon dioxide
they're made out of meat short story summary,"['https://mind-control.fandom.com/en/wiki/They%27re_Made_Out_of_Meat', 'https://followmehere.com/2011/07/10/theyre-made-out-of-meat/']","The two characters are intelligent beings capable of traveling faster than light, on a mission to ""contact, welcome and log in any and all sentient races or multibeings in this quadrant of the Universe."" Bisson's stage directions represent them as ""two lights moving like fireflies among the stars"" on a projection screen. They converse briefly on their bizarre discovery of carbon-based life, which they refer to incredulously as ""thinking meat"". They agree to ""erase the records and forget the whole thing"", marking the Solar System ""unoccupied"".",they're made out of meat short story summary
what is disney's a wrinkle in time,"['http://www.hollywood.tv/a-wrinkle-in-time-premieres-in-la/', 'http://www.netpaak.com/%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%84%D9%88%D8%AF-%D9%81%DB%8C%D9%84%D9%85-a-wrinkle-in-time-2018-%DA%86%D8%B1%D9%88%DA%A9%DB%8C-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D8%B2%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%A8%D9%84%D9%87-%D9%81%D8%A7/', 'https://www.rvagwc.com/2018/03/', 'http://www.bjstardom.com.ng/2018/02/musician-sade-adu-releases-new-song.html', 'https://egsz.info/45222/452222019-01-30-221259.php', 'https://boxofficebuz.com/review/a-wrinkle-in-time-review', 'https://www.affiliatepromotional.com/inspiring-books-2017/']","A Wrinkle in Time is a 2018 American science fantasy adventure film directed by Ava DuVernay and written by Jennifer Lee and Jeff Stockwell, based on the 1962 novel of the same name by Madeleine L'Engle. The film stars Oprah Winfrey, Reese Witherspoon, Mindy Kaling, Gugu Mbatha-Raw, Michael Peña, Storm Reid, Zach Galifianakis and Chris Pine, and follows a young girl who, with the help of three astral travelers, sets off on a quest to find her father, who went missing after discovering a new planet.",what is disney's a wrinkle in time
what advantages does england seem to have to start the industrial revolution,"['http://www.theinfolist.com/php/SummaryGet.php?FindGo=England', 'https://kmvs.eu/deutschland-england.html', 'http://tonyjollyimages.com/structures-6.shtml', 'http://www.best-uk-hotels.co.uk/author/admin/page/2/', 'https://skiptoncravenhistorysociety.com/skipton-history/skipton-buildings/railways/', 'http://canalrivertrustwaterfront.org.uk/community/weekender-pos1-the-waterfront-weekender-the-teesdale-way/', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Industrial_Revolution']","Under the newly formed Kingdom of Great Britain, output from the Royal Society and other English initiatives combined with the Scottish Enlightenment to create innovations in science and engineering, while the enormous growth in British overseas trade protected by the Royal Navy paved the way for the establishment of the British Empire. Domestically it drove the Industrial Revolution, a period of profound change in the socioeconomic and cultural conditions of England, resulting in industrialised agriculture, manufacture, engineering and mining, as well as new and pioneering road, rail and water networks to facilitate their expansion and development. The opening of Northwest England's Bridgewater Canal in 1761 ushered in the canal age in Britain. In 1825 the world's first permanent steam locomotive-hauled passenger railway -- the Stockton and Darlington Railway -- opened to the public.",what advantages does england seem to have to start the industrial revolution
when was the munich pact signed what was its importance,"['https://historicalsocietyofgermanmilitaryhistory.com/third-reich-nazi-germany/historic-events-of-the-third-reich-nazi-germany/annexation-sudentenland/', 'https://dailynewshungary.com/70th-anniversary-of-the-annexation-of-subcarpathia-to-the-ukrainian-soviet-socialist-republic/', 'https://majormike.us/subjects/vienna/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Villa_Tugendhat', 'https://www.tahoedailytribune.com/news/opinion/are-we-witnessing-a-repeat-of-the-munich-agreement/', 'https://newsblaze.com/world/israel/szymon-perski-aka-shimon-peres_65819/', 'https://www.preceden.com/timelines/69761-1750-present-']","The Munich Agreement was a settlement permitting Nazi Germany's annexation of portions of Czechoslovakia along the country's borders mainly inhabited by German speakers, for which a new territorial designation, the ""Sudetenland"", was coined. The agreement was signed in Munich, Germany on the early hours of 30 September 1938 (but dated 29 September) after being negotiated among the major powers of Europe, excluding the Soviet Union. The purpose of the conference was to discuss the future of the Sudetenland in the face of demands made by Adolf Hitler. The agreement was signed by Germany, France, the United Kingdom and Italy, but not Czechoslovakia, which was not invited to the conference The Sudetenland was of immense strategic importance to Czechoslovakia, as most of its border defenses and banks were situated there, as well as heavy industrial districts. The Agreement was soon followed by dismemberment of the Czech state.",when was the munich pact signed what was its importance
how many american troops were killed in the korean war,"['https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-ushistory/chapter/the-korean-war/', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/10102', 'https://lumieregallery.net/wp/category/whats_new/', 'http://www.derechos.org/peace/china/doc/usaprk118.html', 'https://www.history.com/news/korean-war-peace-treaty-pows?fbclid=IwAR3D00LqLDH4Pvy_1YMj5hvE4DSwa8L3LADLr0K6fi_02h0R7jURAnoyFVM', 'http://bitacoracultural.com/2019/02/09/kim-summit-u-s-diplomats-hold-productive-meeting-with-north/', 'https://uk.reuters.com/article/uk-northkorea-usa/trump-kim-summit-venue-shows-possibility-of-moving-beyond-conflict-state-dept-idUKKCN1PW2P7']","According to the data from the U.S. Department of Defense, the United States suffered 33,686 battle deaths, along with 2,830 non-battle deaths, during the Korean War. U.S. battle deaths were 8,516 up to their first engagement with the Chinese on 1 November 1950. South Korea reported some 373,599 civilian and 137,899 military deaths. Western sources estimate the PVA suffered about 400,000 killed and 486,000 wounded, while the KPA suffered 215,000 killed and 303,000 wounded.",how many american troops were killed in the korean war
why did the us use rationing during ww2,"['http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/Rationing', 'https://duarchives.coalliance.org/repositories/2/resources/116', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/American_open-wheel_car_racing']","In summer 1941 the British appealed to Americans to conserve food to provide more to go to Britons fighting in World War II. The Office of Price Administration warned Americans of potential gasoline, steel, aluminum, and electricity shortages. It believed that with factories converting to military production and consuming many critical supplies, rationing would become necessary if the country entered the war. It established a rationing system after the attack on Pearl Harbor.",why did the us use rationing during ww2
why did carthage and rome declare war on one another in 264 bce,"['http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Punic_Wars', 'https://www.red1st.com/axholme/showreport.php?reportID=56', 'https://www.commandsandcolors.net/ancients/maps/55-first-punic-war-264-241-bc.html', 'https://thejeopardyfan.com/2018/12/final-jeopardy-12-26-2018.html']","The First Punic War (264 -- 241 BC) was fought partly on land in Sicily and Africa, but was largely a naval war. It began as a local conflict in Sicily between Hiero II of Syracuse and the Mamertines of Messina. The Mamertines enlisted the aid of the Carthaginian navy, and subsequently betrayed them by entreating the Roman Senate for aid against Carthage. The Romans sent a garrison to secure Messina, so the outraged Carthaginians then lent aid to Syracuse. Tensions quickly escalated into a full-scale war between Carthage and Rome for the control of Sicily.",why did carthage and rome declare war on one another in 264 bce
role of rbi in the indian banking system,"['https://cawinners.com/functions-of-rbi/', 'https://manavidya.net/the-reserve-bank-of-india-rbi/', 'http://hubbabubbanascar.tk/wado/forex-faq-rbi-109.php', 'https://m.jagranjosh.com/general-knowledge/why-i-promise-to-pay-the-bearer-sum-of-100-rupees-is-written-on-the-indian-currency-1530011433-1?ref=list_gk', 'http://www.learntalkmoney.com/central-bank-rbi/', 'http://www.banktheories.com/2015/03/types-categories-of-bank.html', 'https://financial-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/BOE']","Reserve Bank of India is India's central bank, headquartered at Bombay. Central bank of a country execute multiple functions such as overseeing monetary policy, issuing currency, managing foreign exchange, working as a bank of government and as banker of scheduled commercial banks, etc. It also works for overall economic growth of the country. The Reserve Bank of India was established in 1935 with the provision of Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934. Though privately owned initially, it was nationalised in 1949 and since then fully owned by Government of India (GoI). The preamble of the Reserve Bank of India describes it main functions as:",role of rbi in the indian banking system
how the different method of preservation of food work,"['https://www.patheos.com/blogs/davearmstrong/2015/09/do-carnivores-on-the-ark-disprove-christianity.html', 'https://www.rawvittles.com/raw-food/', 'https://www.researchandmarkets.com/reports/4032412/global-industrial-dryers-market-for-agricultural', 'http://gurusfamily.net/news/topic.php?id=3027', 'http://www.agraz.com/products.html', 'https://www.ien.eu/article/energy-efficient-heat-pump-technology-for-food/', 'https://www.travel-trailer-rvcamping.com/tent-camping-checklist.html']","Food drying is a method of food preservation in which food is dried (dehydrated or desiccated). Drying inhibits the growth of bacteria, yeasts, and mold through the removal of water. Dehydration has been used widely for this purpose since ancient times; the earliest known practice is 12,000 B.C. by inhabitants of the modern Middle East and Asia regions. Water is traditionally removed through evaporation (air drying, sun drying, smoking or wind drying), although today electric food dehydrators or freeze-drying can be used to speed the drying process and ensure more consistent results.",how the different method of preservation of food work
what is the structure and function of the neuromuscular junction,"['https://www.naturphilosophie.co.uk/compound-interest-an-antidote-to-sarin/', 'https://www.basepaws.com/blog/congenital-myasthenic-syndrome-what-do-i-need-to-know', 'http://www.mananatomy.com/basic-anatomy/neuromuscular-junction', 'http://www.aestheticallybella.com/glossary/', 'http://rftp.com/what-happens-during-a-muscle-contraction.html', 'http://icm-institute.org/en/als/', 'http://antibodybeyond.com/reviews/cell-markers/synaptic-marker.htm']","A neuromuscular junction (or myoneural junction) is a chemical synapse formed by the contact between a motor neuron and a muscle fiber. It is at the neuromuscular junction that a motor neuron is able to transmit a signal to the muscle fiber, causing muscle contraction.",what is the structure and function of the neuromuscular junction
what is an equivalent representation of the full ipv6 address,"['https://www.dynu.com/Resources/Tutorials/DynamicDNS/CreateAAAARecord', 'https://blog.cdemi.io/beginners-guide-to-ipv6/', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/IPv6', 'http://www.novell.com/documentation/zenworks-2017-update-3/zen_ipv6/data/zen_ipv6.html', 'http://blog.weetech.co/search/label/IPv6', 'https://thecybersecurityman.com/2018/01/01/ip-addresses-version-6/', 'https://documentation.magnolia-cms.com/display/DOCS54/Subscribers']",The 128 bits of an IPv6 address are represented in 8 groups of 16 bits each. Each group is written as four hexadecimal digits (sometimes called hextets) and the groups are separated by colons (:). An example of this representation is 2001: 0db8: 0000: 0000: 0000: ff00: 0042: 8329.,what is an equivalent representation of the full ipv6 address
who sang would you like to swing on a star,"['http://nnhs65.com/01-12-19-NNHS-Swinging-on-a-Star.html', 'http://angoisso.tk/swing-on-a-star-sheet-music.html', 'https://www.fashiontv.com/post/ftv_blog/film-songs-part-3-james-bond-007/', 'http://specialtyluggagebirthdayclub.info/swinging-crosby.html', 'http://bolobooks.com/2015/12/triple-time-with-crime-and-music-by-holstein-love-zgorski/', 'https://sheetmusic-free.com/zip-dee-doo-dah-sheet-music-disney/', 'https://bonkersaway.blog/2017/04/27/daily-prompt-zip/']","""Swinging on a Star"" is an American pop standard with music composed by Jimmy Van Heusen and lyrics by Johnny Burke. It was introduced by Bing Crosby in the 1944 film Going My Way, winning an Academy Award for Best Original Song that year, and has been recorded by numerous artists since then. In 2004 it finished at #37 in AFI's 100 Years ... 100 Songs survey of top tunes in American cinema.",who sang would you like to swing on a star
flash arrow supergirl legends of tomorrow crossover order,['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/The_Flash_(2014_TV_series)'],"After beginning in the final scene of the November 28, 2016 episode of Supergirl, the first part on The Flash aired on November 29, followed by part two on Arrow on November 30, and concluding with part three on Legends of Tomorrow) on December 1, all on The CW.",flash arrow supergirl legends of tomorrow crossover order
what does a star mean on a dollar bill serial number,"['https://www.propertyroom.com/coins-glossary/currency-grading-terminology?utm_source=ONG&utm_medium=COINGLOSSARY&utm_term=COINGLOSSARY&utm_campaign=COINGLOSSARY', 'http://gkready.com/what-is-the-meaning-of-symbol-in-indian-currency-star-replacement-notes-of-rbi/', 'https://www.exonumi.com/publish-BN.1.34', 'https://www.exonumi.com/publish-BN.1.90', 'https://terrific-top10.com/2013/11/11/top-10-images-hidden-on-the-one-dollar-bill/']","A replacement banknote, commonly referred to as a star note, is a banknote that is printed to replace a faulty one and is used as a control mechanism for governments or monetary authorities to know the exact number of banknotes being printed. Also, since no two serial numbers can be the same, the bill is simply reprinted with a symbol in the serial number, identifying it as a replacement for an error note. Replacement bills have different symbols to mark the error around the world, although the most popular examples are ""star notes"".",what does a star mean on a dollar bill serial number
what is the poverty level in the united states of america,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Hunger_in_the_United_States', 'https://www.nationaldebtrelief.com/earn-extra-money-through-your-hobby/', 'http://jimpinto.com/enews/26feb2014.html', 'https://vipsportmaster.com/live-true4u/', 'https://quizlet.com/377245458/wsc-2019-history-combined-flash-cards/', 'https://www.geratol.info/4efb10d333-pnhfrf-bs-cbiregl-va-gur-hf-rffnl.shtml', 'https://www.lclifeline.org/more/poverty-resources/']","Estimates of the number of Americans living in poverty vary. One organization estimated that in 2015, 13.5% (43.1 million) of Americans lived in poverty. Yet other scholars put the number at around 100 million, equating to a third of the U.S. population. Starting in the 1930s, relative poverty rates have consistently exceeded those of other wealthy nations. The lowest poverty rates are found in New Hampshire, Vermont, Minnesota and Nebraska, which have between 8.7% and 9.1% of their population living in poverty.",what is the poverty level in the united states of america
what is the density of the continental crust,"['http://www.primidi.com/continental_crust', 'https://www.bachim.it/03-09_continental-crushing-crushers.html', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Continental_crust', 'https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/High_School_Earth_Science/Inside_Earth', 'https://socratic.org/questions/what-is-the-composition-of-the-earth-s-lithosphere', 'http://thierfelderwilliams.com/peppercornearthplanets/earthmoon.html', 'https://www.smore.com/mvqkh']","The continental crust consists of various layers, with a bulk composition that is intermediate to felsic. The average density of continental crust is about 2.7 g / cm, less dense than the ultramafic material that makes up the mantle, which has a density of around 3.3 g / cm. Continental crust is also less dense than oceanic crust, whose density is about 2.9 g / cm. At 25 to 70 km, continental crust is considerably thicker than oceanic crust, which has an average thickness of around 7 -- 10 km. About 40% of Earth's surface is currently occupied by continental crust. It makes up about 70% of the volume of Earth's crust.",what is the density of the continental crust
where did red and blue states come from,"['https://www.barrypopik.com/index.php/new_york_city/entry/purple_state', 'http://artandpopularculture.com/Red_state_vs._blue_state_divide', 'http://uniteourstates.com/category/politics', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Blue', 'http://grinabelel.tk/red-letter-days-offers-bogo.php', 'https://china.usembassy-china.org.cn/2018-mid-term-election/', 'http://www.greenwood.net/curiosity.php']","Since the 2000 United States presidential election, red states and blue states have referred to states of the United States whose residents predominantly vote for either the Republican Party (red) or Democratic Party (blue) presidential candidates. Since then, the use of the term has been expanded to differentiate between states being perceived as liberal and those perceived as conservative.",where did red and blue states come from
where does the boston post road start and end,['https://danielsdahlstromartist.com/blog/'],"The Boston Post Road was a system of mail-delivery routes between New York City and Boston, Massachusetts that evolved into one of the first major highways in the United States.",where does the boston post road start and end
who owns the means of production in a capitalist society,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Means_of_production.html', 'http://trinityfiles.com/queensland/difference-between-capitalism-and-socialism-pdf.php', 'https://dergi.ingilizedebiyati.net/cuidek/article/view/60', 'https://www.cleverism.com/socialism-characteristics-pros-cons-examples-and-types/', 'http://www.wealthstreamteam.com/free-enterprise-system-home-based-entrepreneur/', 'http://www.differencebetween.net/miscellaneous/politics/difference-between-socialism-and-progressivism/?replytocom=4846324', 'https://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Socialists']","Ownership of the means of production and control over the surplus product generated by their operation is the fundamental factor in delineating different modes of production. Capitalism is defined as private ownership and control over the means of production, where the surplus product becomes a source of unearned income for its owners. By contrast, socialism is defined as social ownership of the means of production so that the surplus product accrues to society at large.",who owns the means of production in a capitalist society
laali ki shaadi mein laddoo deewana movie story,"['http://www.bollytimes.in/2017/04/bollywood-movies-releasing-7-april-2017.html', 'https://reacho.in/discover/laali-ki-shaadi-mein-laaddoo-deewana-poster', 'http://www.washingtonbanglaradio.com/news']","The movie revolves around a royal marriage and quirky characters, who are trapped in their own tragedies.",laali ki shaadi mein laddoo deewana movie story
what is occupy wall street in simple terms,"['https://www.theblackvault.com/documentarchive/occupy-wall-street/', 'http://www.workersunion.org.tt/where-we-stand/nwu-news/fromthegroundupbydrgodfreyvincent', 'http://www.prospektphoto.net/stories/occupy-wall-street/', 'https://www.care2.com/c2c/people/profile.html?pid=873944763', 'https://dcbikeblogger.wordpress.com/tag/lafayette-square/', 'https://www.strategic-culture.org/news/2016/05/28/us-going-through-deep-changes-to-never-be-the-country-it-once-was.html', 'http://mypostcards.frankchang.org/2013/09/international-day-of-democracy.html']","The main issues raised by Occupy Wall Street were social and economic inequality, greed, corruption and the perceived undue influence of corporations on government -- particularly from the financial services sector. The OWS slogan, ""We are the 99%"", refers to income inequality and wealth distribution in the U.S. between the wealthiest 1% and the rest of the population. To achieve their goals, protesters acted on consensus-based decisions made in general assemblies which emphasized direct action over petitioning authorities for redress.",what is occupy wall street in simple terms
where do you get on the high line,"['http://nyfacts.com/the-high-line/', 'https://www.slingshothealth.com/blog/2018/08/08/10-free-and-cheap-ways-to-stay-active-in-nyc/', 'https://travel.usnews.com/Anaheim_Disneyland_CA/Things_To_Do/Yorba_Regional_Park_62338/', 'https://toilet-guru.com/sebastian-junger.php', 'https://www.thetravellingpinoys.com/free-things-to-do-in-new-york-city/', 'https://beyondguides.com/places-to-go/new-york-what-to-do-in-a-weeks-time/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'https://www.jcrcny.org/category/nypd/']","The park is open daily from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. in winter, until 10 p.m. in spring and fall, and until 11 p.m. in summer (except for the Interim Walkway west of 11th Avenue, which is open until dusk). It can be reached through eleven entrances, five of which are accessible to people with disabilities. The wheelchair-accessible entrances, each with stairs and an elevator, are at Gansevoort, 14th, 16th, 23rd, and 30th Streets. Additional staircase-only entrances are located at 18th, 20th, 26th, and 28th Streets, and 11th Avenue. Street-level access is available at 34th Street via the Interim Walkway, from 30th Street and 11th Avenue to 34th Street.",where do you get on the high line
(tco 3) what is a dmz and what is it used for,"['https://answers.dynatrace.com/spaces/482/dynatrace-open-qa/questions/216486/dynatrace-saas-active-gate-configuration.html', 'https://www.ibm.com/developerworks/community/blogs/aimsupport/entry/Fronting_WebSphere_Is_a_DMZ_zone_a_war_zone?lang=en', 'http://techdiary.in/dmz-demilitarized-zone-network/', 'http://www.n10-006-dumps.com/new-98-366-dumps100-success-braindump2go-98-366-pdf-dumps-240q-instant-downloadq23-q33.html', 'http://theantiquegique.com/networking/networking_acronyms.php', 'http://www.passit4suredumps.net/2017-new-lead2pass-2017-new-comptia-sy0-401-braindump-free-download-26-50.html', 'http://www.epass4sure.com/full-version-exam-312-50v9-pdf-free-instant-download-from-lead2pass-21-35.html']","In computer security, a DMZ or demilitarized zone (sometimes referred to as a perimeter network) is a physical or logical subnetwork that contains and exposes an organization's external-facing services to an untrusted network, usually a larger network such as the Internet. The purpose of a DMZ is to add an additional layer of security to an organization's local area network (LAN): an external network node can access only what is exposed in the DMZ, while the rest of the organization's network is firewalled. The DMZ functions as a small, isolated network positioned between the Internet and the private network and, if its design is effective, allows the organization extra time to detect and address breaches before they would further penetrate into the internal networks.",(tco 3) what is a dmz and what is it used for
why is it called a straw man argument,"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Straw_man', 'https://y8y8.us/your-argument/', 'https://www.booksie.com/posting/jr-ziegler/modern-day-view-of-the-wizard-of-oz-309099', 'http://wordcentral.com/buzzword/buzzword.php?month=12&day=01&year=2018', 'http://www.mythingsapp.com/appeal-to-spite.html']","The term's origins are unclear. The usage of the term in rhetoric suggests a human figure made of straw that is easy to knock down or destroy -- such as a military training dummy, scarecrow, or effigy. A common folk etymology is that it refers to men who stood outside courthouses with a straw in their shoe to signal their willingness to be a false witness.",why is it called a straw man argument
whose birthday do we celebrate as teacher's day in india,"['http://reference.allrefer.com/did-you-know-the-13-presidents-of-india-since-the-introduction-of-the-post-in-1950-5339', 'https://m.jagranjosh.com/general-knowledge/amp/dr-sarvepalli-radhakrishnan-1535713553-1?ref=amp_prev', 'http://answerangels.com.au/do-you-know-about-teachers-day/', 'http://williballenthin.com/teachers-day-essay-in-kannada-language.html', 'http://www.bhagwanbhajan.com/stories/read-story.php?my-story=who-is-dr-sarvepalli-radhakrishnan--845736', 'http://iasipstnpsc.in/gk-national-teachers-day-september-5/', 'http://iasipstnpsc.in/world-teachers-day-is-obseved-on-5-october/']","Radhakrishnan was awarded several high awards during his life, including a knighthood in 1931, the Bharat Ratna, the highest civilian award in India, in 1954, and honorary membership of the British Royal Order of Merit in 1963. He was also one of the founders of Helpage India a non profit organization for elderly underprivileged in India. Radhakrishnan believed that ""teachers should be the best minds in the country"". Since 1962, his birthday is being celebrated in India as Teachers' Day on 5 September.",whose birthday do we celebrate as teacher's day in india
who plays the thin man in charlie angels,"['http://outside.mydatinginfo.com/dating-format/3813312-who-are-mcfly-dating.php', 'https://www.mymoviepicker.com/personne/crispin-glover-1143.htm', 'https://www.clickthecity.com/movies/profile/7c1IXp/crispin-glover']","Glover is known for portraying eccentric people on screen, such as George McFly in Back to the Future, Layne in River's Edge, unfriendly recluse Rubin Farr in Rubin and Ed, mentally ill Cousin Dell in David Lynch's Wild at Heart, Andy Warhol in The Doors, the Thin Man in Charlie's Angels and its sequel, Willard Stiles in the Willard remake, Bobby McBurney in What's Eating Gilbert Grape, Ilosovic Stayne / The Knave of Hearts in Alice in Wonderland, Phil Wedmaier in Hot Tub Time Machine, and 6 in 9 (2009).",who plays the thin man in charlie angels
where do the cranial nerves branch off the brain,"['http://hitchhikersgui.de/Cranial_nerves', 'https://wellnessdoctorrx.com/structure-and-function-of-the-cranial-nerves-in-el-paso-tx/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Brainstem']","The terminal nerves, olfactory nerves (I) and optic nerves (II) emerge from the cerebrum or forebrain, and the remaining ten pairs arise from the brainstem, which is the lower part of the brain.",where do the cranial nerves branch off the brain
what is the difference between the bill of rights and the english bill of rights,"['https://www.preceden.com/timelines/217504-from-1648-to-1815', 'https://upge.wn.com/?from=americanrights.com&pagenum=4&language_id=1&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=american_rights', 'https://oldcurrencyexchange.com/2016/02/23/gunmoney-june-1689-timeline/', 'https://anglictina-maturita.cz/the-system-of-government-and-political-parties-in-the-uk/', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/Third_Amendment_to_the_United_States_Constitution', 'https://www.kurtfstone.com/blog/category/Make+Our+Voices+Heard', 'https://kalamatapremiumoliveoil.com/1215-magna-carta-king-john-of-england-is-forced-to-sign-the-magna-carta-by-members-of-the-english-aristocracy/']","The Bill of Rights, also known as the English Bill of Rights, is an Act of the Parliament of England that sets out certain basic civil rights and clarifies who would be next to inherit the Crown. It received the Royal Assent on 16 December 1689 and is a restatement in statutory form of the Declaration of Right presented by the Convention Parliament to William III and Mary II in February 1689, inviting them to become joint sovereigns of England. The Bill of Rights lays down limits on the powers of the monarch and sets out the rights of Parliament, including the requirement for regular parliaments, free elections, and freedom of speech in Parliament. It sets out certain rights of individuals including the prohibition of cruel and unusual punishment and reestablished the right of Protestants to have arms for their defence within the rule of law. Furthermore, the Bill of Rights described and condemned several misdeeds of James II of England.",what is the difference between the bill of rights and the english bill of rights
who sings to make you feel my love,"['https://www.eurohitlist.eu/category/songs-recorded-by-adele/', 'http://expertconsultbook.com/who-sings-to-make-you-feel-my-love-lyrics.html', 'http://rathergood.co.uk/adele-make-feel-love/', 'http://sheetspiano.com/make-you-feel-my-love-by-adele-free-piano-music-sheets/', 'http://dolateyar.tk/make-you-feel-my-love-sheet-music-adele.html', 'http://www.independentwaters.com/make-you-feel-my-love/', 'http://juniormarvel.tk/make-you-feel-my-love-sheet-music-bob-dylan.html']","""Make You Feel My Love"" is a song written by Bob Dylan from his album Time Out of Mind (1997). It was first released commercially by Billy Joel, under the title ""To Make You Feel My Love"", before Dylan's version appeared later that same year. It has since been covered by numerous performers and has proved to be a commercial success for recording artists such as Adele, Garth Brooks, Shane Filan, Bryan Ferry, Kelly Clarkson and Ane Brun. Two covers of the song (one by Garth Brooks and one by Trisha Yearwood) were featured on the soundtrack of the 1998 film Hope Floats. Dylan eventually released the song as a single.",who sings to make you feel my love
who wrote the song all you ever do is bring me down,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Mike_Reid_(singer)', 'https://wn.com/There_Goes_My_Heart', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Travis_Tritt', 'http://bilgisayarokulu.tk/brendan-coyle-dating.html', 'https://www.whenthecowboysings.com/blog/?tag=John+Conlee', 'http://botm.blackdogebooks.com/no-one-heard-her-scream/', ""https://www.whenthecowboysings.com/waylon-jennings-good-ol'-boys""]","""All You Ever Do Is Bring Me Down"" is a song written by Raul Malo and Al Anderson, and recorded by American country music group The Mavericks featuring accordionist Flaco Jiménez. It was released in January 1996 as the second single from the album Music for All Occasions. The song reached number 13 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart, representing the band's highest entry there, and Jiménez's only entry.",who wrote the song all you ever do is bring me down
how many members are there in new edition,"['http://thejasminebrand.com/2017/01/23/new-edition-receives-hollywood-star/', 'http://www.wscmradio.com/artist/new-edition/', 'https://www.shreveporttimes.com/story/entertainment/2018/07/30/ronny-bobby-ricky-mike-tour-hit-centurylink-center/864211002/', 'https://theaudiodb.com/artist/113031', 'https://payplay.fm/a25d53-new-edition', 'http://www.lyricszoo.com/new-edition/', 'https://www.eventfinda.sg/artist/new-edition']","New Edition is an American R&B group from the Roxbury neighborhood of Boston, Massachusetts formed in 1978. The group reached its height of popularity in the 1980s. During the group's first experience with fame in 1983, its members were Ricky Bell, Michael Bivins, Bobby Brown, Ronnie DeVoe and Ralph Tresvant. Early hits included ""Candy Girl,"" ""Cool It Now"", and ""Mr. Telephone Man"". Brown was voted out of the group in 1985 and embarked on a solo career. The group continued for a time with its remaining four members, but eventually recruited singer Johnny Gill, who would be introduced on their 1988 album Heart Break. The group went on hiatus in 1990, while its various members worked on side projects, such as the group Bell Biv DeVoe. Gill and Tresvant also recorded successful solo albums.",how many members are there in new edition
what type of cell is ribosomes found in,"['http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Ribosome', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Robert_W._Holley', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/Ribosomal', 'https://pingpdf.com/pdf-the-molecular-origins-of-life.html', 'http://whatimpossiblelife.com/entertainment-arts/what-do-ribosomes-assemble-amino.php', 'https://www.futurelearn.com/courses/biology-basic-concepts/1/steps/256561', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=ribosomes+animal+cell&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir']","The ribosome (/ ˈraɪbəˌsoʊm,-boʊ-/) is a complex molecular machine, found within all living cells, that serves as the site of biological protein synthesis (translation). Ribosomes link amino acids together in the order specified by messenger RNA (mRNA) molecules. Ribosomes consist of two major components: the small ribosomal subunit, which reads the RNA, and the large subunit, which joins amino acids to form a polypeptide chain. Each subunit is composed of one or more ribosomal RNA (rRNA) molecules and a variety of ribosomal proteins (r-protein or rProtein). The ribosomes and associated molecules are also known as the translational apparatus.",what type of cell is ribosomes found in
when do you receive a term sheet from an investor,"['http://angelscorner.com/articles/term_sheet.htm', 'https://blog.vcexperts.com/2016/11/', 'http://reemajainassociates.com/decoding-term-sheet/']","It is customary to begin the negotiation of a venture investment with the circulation of a term sheet, which is a summary of the terms the proposer (the issuer, the investor, or an intermediary) is prepared to accept. The term sheet is analogous to a letter of intent, a nonbinding outline of the principal points which the stock purchase agreement and related agreements will cover in detail.",when do you receive a term sheet from an investor
name the largest lagoon of india and the state where it is found,"['http://www.eosnap.com/tag/orissa/', 'https://teaabroad.com/irrawaddy-dolphin-spotting-chilika-lake', 'https://www.trover.com/d/1aMge-chilika-lake-india', 'https://www.tripoto.com/trip/odisha-vi-chilika-lake-and-the-conference-of-the-birds-5a5b5c04e4324', 'http://orissatrip.com/chilka', 'http://ourincredibleindia.in/temple-gallery/photo-gallery/orissa/', 'http://www.orissatribaltours.com/tour-packages/heritage-tourof-orissa-tour1.htm']","Chilika Lake is a brackish water lagoon, spread over the Puri, Khurda and Ganjam districts of Odisha state on the east coast of India, at the mouth of the Daya River, flowing into the Bay of Bengal, covering an area of over 1,100 km. It is the largest coastal lagoon in India and the second largest coastal lagoon in the world after The New Caledonian barrier reef in New Caledonia.",name the largest lagoon of india and the state where it is found
what does lord of the rings ring say,"['http://animereview.jp/one-ring-quote.html', 'https://www.usingenglish.com/forum/threads/119743-Diagramming-Tolkien-2-CAT-3', 'http://ozonahockey.com/new-south-wales/return-of-the-king-pdf-free-download.php', 'https://www.outland.no/the-one-ring-costume-version-gold-plated-replica', 'https://www.factinate.com/things/lord-of-the-rings-everything-facts/', 'http://grandescapades.net/in-the-land-of-mordor-where-the-shadows-lie/', 'https://www.thehobbitjewelry.com/lord-of-the-rings-lotr-jewelry-3/the-one-ring-lotr-1']","One ring to rule them all, one ring to find them, One ring to bring them all and in the darkness bind them.",what does lord of the rings ring say
when does the death cure come out in theaters,['https://www.join4films.com/movie/maze-runner-death-cure-2018/'],"Maze Runner: The Death Cure was originally set to be released on February 17, 2017, in the United States by 20th Century Fox, but the studio rescheduled the film for January 26, 2018 in 3D, 2D and IMAX 3D, allowing time for Dylan O'Brien to fully recover from his injuries sustained on-set.",when does the death cure come out in theaters
when was the last time the jaguars made it to the afc championship,"['https://de-club.eu/ran-nfl-logo.html', 'https://bangedupbills.com/tag/jacksonville-jaguars/', 'https://www.patriots.com/news/game-preview-patriots-at-steelers?campaign=sf:fanshare:facebook', 'https://kmhk.com/nfl-conference-championship-preview-2016/', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Kam_Chancellor', 'https://www.ticketchest.com/sports/NFL/TENNESSEE-TITANS', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Dan_Marino']","After their week 15 win over the Houston Texans, the Jaguars clinched their first playoff trip since 2007; they finished the season 10-6, a seven-game turnaround from the previous year. The Jaguars defeated the Buffalo Bills 10-3 in Jacksonville, marking the first playoff win in ten years. In the Divisional Round, on January 14, 2018, the Jaguars defeated the Pittsburgh Steelers 45-42 in Pittsburgh to advance to their 3rd AFC Championship Game, and their first since 1999. However, they narrowly fell to the New England Patriots 24-20. For the season, the defense earned the nickname ""Sacksonville"" because of its dominance.",when was the last time the jaguars made it to the afc championship
what is the sensory function of the ans,"['https://dictionary.babylon-software.com/autonomic_nervous_system/', 'https://psychology.jrank.org/pages/59/Autonomic-Nervous-System.html', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Peripheral_nervous_system', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Fight-or-flight_response.html', 'https://rsdadvisory.com/tag/1000-00-in-prizes/', 'https://biology.stackexchange.com/questions/70509/breathing-with-clogged-nose-during-sleep', 'http://fetranspordocs.com.br/comparison-between-somatic-and-autonomic-nervous-system.html']","The autonomic nervous system (ANS), formerly the vegetative nervous system, is a division of the peripheral nervous system that supplies smooth muscle and glands, and thus influences the function of internal organs. The autonomic nervous system is a control system that acts largely unconsciously and regulates bodily functions such as the heart rate, digestion, respiratory rate, pupillary response, urination, and sexual arousal. This system is the primary mechanism in control of the fight-or-flight response.",what is the sensory function of the ans
summary of alice through the looking glass book,"['https://www.sciencephoto.com/media/995905/view/alice-with-tweedledum-and-tweedledee', 'https://www.sciencephoto.com/media/995916/view/through-the-looking-glass-bread-and-butterfly', 'https://www.sciencephoto.com/media/995911/view/through-the-looking-glass-alice-and-the-white-knight', 'https://www.sciencephoto.com/media/995906/view/through-the-looking-glass-alice-battles-the-jabberwock', 'https://www.sciencephoto.com/media/995910/view/through-the-looking-glass-snap-dragonfly', 'http://www.savannahsoft.eu/book/429223235/download-alices-adventures-in-wonderland-bookbyte-digital.pdf', 'https://www.weltbild.de/artikel/ebook/general-press-through-the-looking-glass_25994001-1']","Through the Looking-Glass, and What Alice Found There (1872) is a novel by Lewis Carroll (Charles Lutwidge Dodgson), the sequel to Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865). Set some six months later than the earlier book, Alice again enters a fantastical world, this time by climbing through a mirror into the world that she can see beyond it. Through the Looking-Glass includes such celebrated verses as ""Jabberwocky"" and ""The Walrus and the Carpenter"", and the episode involving Tweedledum and Tweedledee. The mirror which inspired Carroll remains displayed in Charlton Kings.",summary of alice through the looking glass book
what is the difference between enamel cast iron and cast iron,"['http://welcometablepress.info/enamel-coated-cast-iron-griddle/', 'https://www.shaffer-berry.com/products/charcoal-cast-iron-frypan-30cm/', 'http://www.cookwaretalk.com/enameled-cast-iron-cookware.html', 'http://www.hocin.com/content/43-Enamel-cast-iron-cookware-best-cast-iron-cookware', 'http://letseathealthier.com/enameled-cast-iron-cookware.html', 'https://www.eco-novice.com/2011/08/cooking-without-teflon.html', 'http://cvhomemag.com/cookware-conundrum-what-should-i-buy/']","Enameled cast iron is cast iron that has a vitreous enamel glaze. The enamel coating over the cast iron prevents rusting, eliminates the need to season the metal, and allows more thorough cleaning. Furthermore, pigments used in the enameling process can produce vibrant colors. While enamel-coated cast iron doesn't have the seasoning and cleaning issues of bare cast iron, it can be several times more costly, and does not have some of the benefits of bare cast iron, such as the ability to withstand searing heat and resist sticking. It limits the leaching of dietary iron, and chipping of the enamel coating can be a concern.",what is the difference between enamel cast iron and cast iron
what are the various levels of education in nigeria,"['http://www.expat-quotes.com/guides/nigeria/education/international-schools-in-nigeria.htm', 'https://www.seekteachers.com/country-info.asp?country_id=62', 'https://www.bartleby.com/essay/The-Education-System-Of-Nigeria-FK5G4L29MWW', 'http://schindler-bs.net/630-essay-on-child-education-pdf.php', 'http://www.ekopearltowers.com/blog/2016/03/07/education-in-nigeria-top-5-schools-and-universities/', 'http://upowerafrica.org/upower-africa-targets-africa/', 'https://kitaab.com.pk/abroad/malaysia/what-is-the-education-system-in-malaysia-education-system-in-malaysia/']","Education in Nigeria is overseen by the Ministry of Education. Local authorities take responsibility for implementing policy for state-controlled public education and state schools at a regional level. The education system is divided into Kindergarten, Primary education, Secondary education and Tertiary education.",what are the various levels of education in nigeria
when did the boeing 707 go out of service,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Boeing_707', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/Boeing_707', 'http://oldmechanic.weebly.com/boeig-707.html', 'http://aviationexplorer.com/707_facts.htm', 'https://www.flightmemory.com/encyclopedia/Boeing_707.html', 'http://www.motoart.com/studio/airplane-history/aircraft-history-of-the-b-707', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Boeing_737']","Trans World Airlines flew the last scheduled 707 flight for passengers by a US carrier on October 30, 1983, although 707s remained in scheduled service by airlines from other nations for much longer. Middle East Airlines of Lebanon flew 707s and 720s in front-line passenger service until the end of the 1990s. Since LADE of Argentina took its 707-320Bs from regular service in 2007, Saha Airlines of Iran was the last airline to keep 707s in scheduled passenger service until April 2013.",when did the boeing 707 go out of service
what is the main difference between series and parallel circuits,"['http://www.wikidifference.com/difference-between-series-and-parallel-circuits/', 'http://stratosfountoulis.com/partition-5/how-to-control_m553.php', 'https://www.electrical4u.com/electric-circuit-or-electrical-network/', 'https://www.q-files.com/science/electricity-and-magnetism/electrical-circuits/', 'http://gordonwiebe.com/western-australia/how-to-draw-parallel-circuit.php', 'http://gpiper.org/wiring-diagram/simple-electrical-circuits-in-series-parallel-and-combination', 'http://swissjournals.org/new-brunswick/series-parallel-combination-circuit-problems-pdf.php']","A circuit composed solely of components connected in series is known as a series circuit; likewise, one connected completely in parallel is known as a parallel circuit.",what is the main difference between series and parallel circuits
who has the day off on columbus day,"['http://justbcause.com/2015/07/01/is-july-3-2015-a-federal-holiday/', 'https://www.dancingwithgarrey.com/national-holidays-united-states/', 'https://empirenews.net/tag/president-obama/', 'http://economyobzor.com/federal-holiday-pay-christmas-eve-36027.html', 'http://calendaroffice.com/2018-federal-holidays-calendar/', 'https://applianceart.com/celebrate-veterans-day-american-flag-appliance-covers/', 'http://cheekyvisionaries.com/post-1873.html']","In the United States, a federal holiday is an authorized holiday which has been recognized by the US government. Every year on a U.S. federal holiday, non-essential federal government offices are closed, and every federal employee is paid for the holiday. Private-sector employees required to work on a legal holiday may receive holiday pay in addition to their ordinary wages.",who has the day off on columbus day
where are the philippines located on the world map,"['http://iexploretravels.com/index.php/2015/08/17/ph-islands/', 'http://fouman.com/Y/Wiki.php?eterm=Philippines', 'http://www.kolumnmagazine.com/2017/01/10/procession-black-nazarene-atlantic/', 'http://www.studybooking.com/country/philippines', 'http://www.globalmissionsinc.org/philippines.html', 'https://www.conceptdraw.com/How-To-Guide/geo-map-asia-philippines', 'http://ofwpinoy1tv.su/page/143/']","The Philippines (/ ˈfɪlɪpiːnz / (listen); Filipino: Pilipinas (ˌpɪlɪˈpinɐs) or Filipinas (ˌfɪlɪˈpinɐs)), officially the Republic of the Philippines (Filipino: Republika ng Pilipinas), is a unitary sovereign state and island country in Southeast Asia. Situated in the western Pacific Ocean, it consists of about 7,641 islands that are categorized broadly under three main geographical divisions from north to south: Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao. The capital city of the Philippines is Manila and the most populous city is Quezon City, both part of Metro Manila. Bounded by the South China Sea on the west, the Philippine Sea on the east and the Celebes Sea on the southwest, the Philippines shares maritime borders with Taiwan to the north, Vietnam to the west, Palau to the east and Malaysia and Indonesia to the south.",where is the philippines located on a map
why is a day called a sol on mars,"['https://suporter.info/printable/printable-pocket-calendar-printable-360-degree.html', 'https://blog.world-mysteries.com/science/ancient-timekeepers-part4-calendars/', 'http://gourmetking.info/?newsid=45114']","The average length of a Martian sidereal day is 24 h 37 m 22.663 s (88,642.66300 seconds based on SI units), and the length of its solar day (often called a sol) is 24 h 39 m 35.244147 s (88,775.244147 seconds). The corresponding values for Earth are 23 h 56 m 4.0916 s and 24h 00 m 00.002 s, respectively. This yields a conversion factor of 1.02749125170 days / sol. Thus Mars' solar day is only about 2.7% longer than Earth's.",why is a day called a sol on mars
who is the president of north korea and how old is he,"['http://citationpod.com/episode-003-kim-jong-un/', 'http://www.hawaii.edu/korea/biblio/cho_family.html', 'http://www.hawaii.edu/korea/biblio/cho_social.html', 'https://www.scribd.com/doc/297053611/Readme', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-018-32800-9?error=cookies_not_supported&code=3ffb1e91-2e2b-40ee-b435-afd77acfe15d', 'http://www.hawaii.edu/korea/biblio/cho_government.html', 'http://www.friaryschool.com/custom-writings-reviews/']","Kim Jong-un (Chosŏn'gŭl: 김정은; Korean pronunciation: (kim. dzʌŋ. ɯn) or (kim. tsʌŋ. ɯn); born 8 January 1982 -- 84 or 5 July 1984) is the Chairman of the Workers' Party of Korea (WPK) and supreme leader of North Korea since 2011. Kim is the second child of Kim Jong-il (1941 -- 2011) and Ko Yong-hui. He is the first North Korean leader to have been born after the country's founding. Before taking power, Kim was rarely seen in public, and many of the activities of Kim and his government remain unknown. Even details such as what year he was born, and whether he did indeed attend a Western school under a pseudonym, are difficult to confirm.",who is the president of north korea and how old is he
who is the owner of kings xi punjab in 2018,"['http://crictoday.com/detail/if-ipl-franchises-were-to-be-named-after-famous-brands', 'https://sportzwiki.com/wiki/kings-xi-punjab-kxip', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171113118-cricket-teams', 'http://indemaak.info/news.php?action=show&id=44686', 'http://www.ipl-fixtures.com/kings-x1-punjab-team-players-list-2019/', 'https://ipl-2019.com/kings-xi-punjab-team-squad-2019/', 'http://www.isl2017livestreaming.com/2018/04/ipl-2018-match-12-kings-xi-punjab-kxip-vs-chennai-super-kings-csk-live-cricket-streaming.html']","The Kings XI Punjab (abbreviated as KXIP) are a franchise cricket team based in Mohali, Punjab, that plays in the Indian Premier League. Established in 2008, the franchise is jointly owned by Bollywood actress Preity Zinta, Wadia Group scion Ness Wadia, Dabur's Mohit Burman and Karan Paul. The team plays its home matches at the PCA Stadium, Mohali. Since the 2010 IPL, they have been playing some of their home games at Dharamsala and sometimes they also play some of their home games at Indore too.",who is the owner of kings xi punjab in 2018
what is the difference between freemasons and shriners,"['http://midcenturycarved.com/hand_carved_wood_karem_shriner_es_selamu_aleikum_mid_century_temple_decor.htm', 'http://www.nwotoday.com/history-home/freemasonry-global-level-illumination/aleister-crowley-the-ordo-templi-orientis', 'http://www.masonforum.com/viewthread/12026/P15/', 'http://nj8thdistrict.org/DDGM.aspx']","Shriners International, also commonly known as The Shriners, is a society established in 1870 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida, USA. It is an appendant body to Freemasonry.",what is the difference between freemasons and shriners
how did the tradition of christmas gift giving start,"['http://mainevernalpools.info/gift/why-do-we-put-gifts-under-a-christmas-tree.php', 'https://www.dailyjigsawpuzzles.net/christmas-jigsaws/christmas-shopping_1522.html', 'http://xautoman.com/23419-whydowegivegiftstoeachotheratchristmas.html', 'https://www.sweetandsavor.com/bourbon-pecan-pie-stuffed-cupcakes/', 'https://www.montemaggio.com/lang-en/blog/christmas-gift-memories-at-fattoria-di-montemaggio.html', 'https://shoppingbrake.com/category/wardrobe/', 'https://co-geeking.com/tag/rome/']","The tradition of gift-giving is an old one, but it became associated with Christmas more recently. It is a relic of a pagan custom, namely, the winter solstice which in Europe occurs in December. This was celebrated in ancient Rome with gift-giving during the Saturnalia holiday, which took place that month. As Christianity became increasingly widespread in the Roman lands, the custom of gift-giving continued. Around the year 336 AD the date of December 25 appears to have become established as the day of Jesus's birth, and the tradition of gift-giving was reinterpreted and tied to the story of three Magi giving gifts to baby Jesus; together with another story, that of Santa Claus based on the historical figure of Saint Nicholas, a fourth-century Greek bishop and gift-giver, it slowly became a part of Christmas celebrations.",how did the tradition of christmas gift giving start
what happened as a result of the kansas nebraska act,"['http://pandatimelines.com/v1/b42286cd', 'https://academicbuzznetwork.wordpress.com/2018/06/19/otd-in-history-june-17-19-1856-the-first-republican-convention-nominates-john-c-fremont-for-president/', 'http://www.brettschulte.net/CWBlog/civilwarmagazinesjournals/americas-civil-war/volumes21to30/volume22/number3/', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/10280', 'https://www.encyclopedia.com/history/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/test-article', 'https://tarpon.wordpress.com/category/state-run-media/', 'https://seeithistory.com/civilwar/causes/']","The Kansas -- Nebraska Act of 1854 (10 Stat. 277) created the territories of Kansas and Nebraska and was drafted by Democratic Senator Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois and President Franklin Pierce. The initial purpose of the Kansas -- Nebraska Act was to open up thousands of new farms and make feasible a Midwestern Transcontinental Railroad. The popular sovereignty clause of the law led pro-and anti-slavery elements to flood into Kansas with the goal of voting slavery up or down, resulting in Bleeding Kansas.",what happened as a result of the kansas nebraska act
where does the tennessee river start and where does it end,"['https://www.localwaters.us/find-local-water/find-your-water/tennessee-river/', 'https://www.luckytacklebox.com/blogs/fishing-reports/tennessee-river', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/East_Tennessee', 'https://www.stylecruises.co.uk/mississippi/', 'https://www.riverlorian.com/tennesseeriver.htm', 'http://florencehistory.org/mussles-and-fish-1900-to-1949/', 'http://www.factorytwofour.com/chattanooga-tennessee-outdoor-city/']","The Tennessee River is formed at the confluence of the Holston and French Broad rivers on the east side of present-day Knoxville, Tennessee. From Knoxville, it flows southwest through East Tennessee toward Chattanooga before crossing into Alabama. It loops through northern Alabama and eventually forms a small part of the state's border with Mississippi, before returning to Tennessee. At this point, it defines the boundary between two of Tennessee's Grand Divisions: Middle and West Tennessee.",where does the tennessee river start and where does it end
where did the term life hack come from,"['http://www.psychologicalscience.com/behaviorlearning/', 'http://sectorx.co.uk/loch/life-hack-mcdonalds-whiskey/']","The original definition of the term ""hack"" is ""to cut with rough or heavy blows."" In the modern vernacular it has often been used to describe an inelegant but effective solution to a specific computing problem, such as quick-and-dirty shell scripts and other command line utilities that filtered, munged and processed data streams like e-mail and RSS feeds. The term was later extended to life hack, in reference to a solution to a problem unrelated to computers that might occur in a programmer's everyday life. Examples of these types of life hacks might include utilities to synchronize files, track tasks, remind oneself of events, or filter e-mail.",where did the term life hack come from
the provision of environmental protection act in the constitution were made under,"['https://rslegal.in/environmental-law/', 'http://greenubuntu.com/what-is-the-environment-protection-act-steps-towards-green-living/', 'http://iced.cag.gov.in/?page_id=1026', 'https://rinolf.com/environment-protection-act-1986/', 'https://www.railelectrica.com/environment-and-pollution-control-sseje-study-material/study-material-on-environment-and-pollution-control-for-sse-and-je-exam-by-rrb/?replytocom=1030', 'http://lavecchiascalinata.com/media-video/environmental-protection-act-1986-ppt.php', 'https://0-bmcpublichealth-biomedcentral-com.brum.beds.ac.uk/articles/10.1186/1471-2458-10-629']","Environment Protection Act, 1986 is an Act of the Parliament of India. In the wake of the Bhopal Tragedy, the Government of India enacted the Environment Protection Act of 1986 under Article 253 of the Constitution. Passed in March 1986, it came into force on 19 November 1986.It has 26 sections. The purpose of the Act is to implement the decisions of the United Nations Conference on the Human Environments. They relate to the protection and improvement of the human environment and the prevention of hazards to human beings, other living creatures, plants and property. The Act is an ""umbrella"" legislation designed to provide a framework for central government coordination of the activities of various central and state authorities established under previous laws, such as the Water Act and the Air Act.",the provision of environmental protection act in the constitution were made under
where are isotopes found on the periodic table,"['https://www.thenakedscientists.com/forum/index.php?amp;action=profile;area=showposts;sa=messages;u=2212', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Isotope', 'https://www.examtestprep.com/CIE/IGCSE/Chemistry-0620-Specimen-Questions-with-Answers/Paper-1/Part-13.html', 'https://www.e-alyss.com/product/class/chapter-details/chapter/45', 'http://metaglossary.com/define/isotope+', 'https://insider.si.edu/2014/07/bones-can-talk-police-ask-smithsonian-scientists-help-20-year-old-mystery/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Molar_mass']","Isotopes are variants of a particular chemical element which differ in neutron number. All isotopes of a given element have the same number of protons in each atom. The term isotope is formed from the Greek roots isos (ἴσος ""equal"") and topos (τόπος ""place""), meaning ""the same place""; thus, the meaning behind the name is that different isotopes of a single element occupy the same position on the periodic table.",where are isotopes found on the periodic table
in any test of hypothesis to reject the null hypothesis is to,"['https://wikimili.com/en/False_positives_and_false_negatives', 'http://www.gemesyscanada.com/431369714', 'http://lokhj.webz.cz/450-how-to-formulate-a-null-hypothesis-statement-example.php', 'http://asnanombka.gq/business-plan/null-hyphothesis.htm', 'http://cacademy.info/accounting_cover_letter_pdf/', 'https://blogdejob.info/significance-of-hypothesis-in-research/', 'https://hyperleap.com/topic/Hypothesis']","In inferential statistics, the term ""null hypothesis"" is a general statement or default position that there is no relationship between two measured phenomena, or no association among groups. Rejecting or disproving the null hypothesis -- and thus concluding that there are grounds for believing that there is a relationship between two phenomena (e.g. that a potential treatment has a measurable effect) -- is a central task in the modern practice of science; the field of statistics gives precise criteria for rejecting a null hypothesis.",in any test of hypothesis to reject the null hypothesis is to
what is one role of the federal government's department of justice,"['https://www.justice.gov/usao-ndwv', 'https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/28/0.10', 'https://www.justice.gov/usao-nj/victim-witness/handbook', 'https://www.pogo.org/analysis/2018/06/frequently-asked-questions-criminal-prosecutions-on-border/', 'https://www.justice.gov/usao-edca/victim-witness-assistance/rights', 'https://work.chron.com/role-assistant-us-attorney-8443.html', 'https://msb1959.wordpress.com/category/now-playing/']","U.S. Attorneys and their offices are part of the Department of Justice. U.S. Attorneys receive oversight, supervision, and administrative support services through the Justice Department's Executive Office for United States Attorneys. Selected U.S. Attorneys participate in the Attorney General's Advisory Committee of United States Attorneys.",what is one role of the federal government's department of justice
where does the term heavy metal come from,"['https://wallpapersandroid.info/metal-music-download.html', 'http://www.luckeysclub.com/author/bird', 'https://wn.com/African_metal?upload_time=all_time&orderby=viewCount', ""https://wikimili.com/en/Sick_of_the_Studio_'07"", 'https://www.crowdact.com/wall/show/601', 'http://hmpf.forumotion.com/c2-metal-sub-genres', 'http://ortopedicke.info/?page_id=4686']","Heavy metal (or simply metal) is a genre of rock music that developed in the late 1960s and early 1970s, largely in the United Kingdom. With roots in blues rock and psychedelic / acid rock, the bands that created heavy metal developed a thick, massive sound, characterized by highly amplified distortion, extended guitar solos, emphatic beats, and overall loudness. Heavy metal lyrics and performance styles are sometimes associated with aggression and machismo.",where does the term heavy metal come from
where is kuwait located in the middle east,"['http://www.food.capital/facts.html', 'https://legacarta.intracen.org/country/kwt/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Euphrates', 'http://www.allgulfvacancy.com/2016/09/urgent-recruitment-to-oil-gas-jobs-in.html', 'http://www.q8egifts.com/about-kuwait', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Kuwait', 'https://ayearcookingtheworld.com/2016/09/11/kuwait/']","Kuwait (/ kʊˈweɪt / (listen); Arabic: الكويت ‎ ‎ al-Kuwait, Gulf Arabic pronunciation: (ɪl ‿ ɪkweːt) or (lɪkweːt)), officially the State of Kuwait (Arabic: دولة الكويت ‎ ‎ Dawlat al-Kuwait), is a country in Western Asia. Situated in the northern edge of Eastern Arabia at the tip of the Persian Gulf, it shares borders with Iraq and Saudi Arabia. As of 2016, Kuwait has a population of 4.2 million people; 1.3 million are Kuwaitis and 2.9 million are expatriates. Expatriates account for 70% of the population.",where is kuwait located in the middle east
what type of system does the russian constitution set up,"['http://visittoukraine.com/en/introducing-ukraine.html', 'https://anydayguide.com/calendar/1897', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Prime_Minister_of_Poland', 'http://primatesafari.com/primate-safaris-rwanda/', 'http://bti2006.bertelsmann-transformation-index.de/69.0.html?L=1']","In 1993 the new Russian Constitution was adopted. The new Constitution gained legitimacy through its bicameral legislature, independent judiciary, the position of the president and the prime minister, and democratic features. These democratic features included competitive multi-party elections, separation of powers, federalism, and protection of civil liberties.",what type of system does the russian constitution set up
which park is located in kensington central london,"['http://www.englishtowns.net/kensington-chelsea/', 'http://houseclearancesolutions.co.uk/house-clearance-Kensington.php']","In the north east, the large Royal Park of Kensington Gardens (contiguous with its eastern neighbour, Hyde Park) is a green buffer. The other main green area in Kensington is Holland Park, just north of Kensington High Street, a minority of roads have small residential garden squares.",which park is located in kensington central london
where is bering strait located on a map,"['http://mywallpapers.mobi/crossing-the-bering-straits/', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Bering_Strait', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Thunderbolt_(interface).html', 'http://www.glenwoodschoolemsworth.co.uk/ww1-legacy-100/', 'http://mexicanroutes.com/chichen-itza/', 'http://discoverarmenia.tours/en/trip/new-2019-year-in-armenia/', 'http://hitchhikersgui.de/Hohokam_Pima_National_Monument']","The Bering Strait is about 82 kilometres (51 mi) wide at its narrowest point, between Cape Dezhnev, Chukchi Peninsula, Russia, the easternmost point (169 ° 43' W) of the Asian continent and Cape Prince of Wales, Alaska, United States, the westernmost point (168 ° 05' W) of the North American continent. Its depth varies between 30 metres (98 ft) and 50 metres (160 ft). It borders with the Chukchi Sea (part of the Arctic Ocean) to north and with the Bering Sea to south.",where is bering strait located on a map
what role does collective bargaining play in labor relations,"['https://www.yourlawyer.com/labor-law-attorneys/', 'http://ufcw648.org/know-your-rights/', 'http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Collective_bargaining', 'https://www.paperrater.com/page/recur-vs-reoccur', 'http://sso-bernco.sks.com/Human-resources/policies-contracts.aspx', 'https://oregonfba.org/you-got-fired-heres-how-to-know-if-its-wrongful-termination/', 'https://hrglossary.xcelhr.com/collective-bargaining-agreement']","Collective bargaining is a process of negotiation between employers and a group of employees aimed at agreements to regulate working salaries, working conditions, benefits, and other aspects of workers' compensation and rights. The interests of the employees are commonly presented by representatives of a trade union to which the employees belong. The collective agreements reached by these negotiations usually set out wage scales, working hours, training, health and safety, overtime, grievance mechanisms, and rights to participate in workplace or company affairs.",what role does collective bargaining play in labor relations
how can i withdraw money from ppf account,"['https://taxadda.com/ppf-public-provident-fund/?utm_source=homepage/', 'http://dailytools.in/PPFCalculator/Article/PPF_KT_FeaturesOfPPF', 'https://investorsareidiots.com/retirement-investments-equity-fixed-income-currencies-commodities-economy/home/home-2/homespage/2015/03/public-provident-fund/', 'https://www.jagoinvestor.com/2012/02/how-ppf-interest-is-calculated-video.html', 'https://www.mymoneystore.in/public-provident-fund', 'https://www.madrasi.info/ppf.html']","There is a lock-in period of 15 years and the money can be withdrawn in full after its maturity period. However, pre-mature withdrawals can be made from the start of the seventh financial year. The maximum amount that can be withdrawn pre-maturely is equal to 50% of the amount that stood in the account at the end of 4th year preceding the year in which the amount is withdrawn or the end of the preceding year whichever is lower.",how can i withdraw money from ppf account
what makes you a saint in the catholic church,"['https://wn.com/Priesthood_(Latter_Day_Saints)', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/1274_in_poetry', 'http://www.primidi.com/saint', 'http://worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Saint', 'https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/18878165-the-epistle-of-polycarp-to-the-philippians', 'https://www.britannica.com/topic/saint', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Apostolic_Succession']","A saint (also historically known as a hallow) is a person who is recognized as having an exceptional degree of holiness or likeness or closeness to God. Depending on the context and denomination, the term also retains its original Christian meaning, as any believer who is ""in Christ"" and in whom Christ dwells, whether in Heaven or on Earth. In Anglican, Roman Catholic, Eastern Orthodox, Lutheran, and Oriental Orthodox doctrine, all of their faithful deceased in Heaven are considered to be saints, but some are considered worthy of greater honor or emulation; official ecclesiastical recognition, and consequently veneration, is given to some saints through the process of canonization in the Catholic Church or glorification in the Eastern Orthodox Church.",what makes you a saint in the catholic church
what does an mri of the brain check for,"['https://wkhs.com/imaging-radiology/services/mri', 'https://www.ebme.co.uk/articles/clinical-engineering/functional-magnetic-resonance-imaging-fmri', 'http://pk.deltaibiza.com/forums/topic/viagra-tablets-nebsshavakqv/', 'https://eng.kakprosto.ru/how-830791-what-is-mri-of-the-brain', 'http://www.digitaljournal.com/pr/1493292']","Physicians use fMRI to assess how risky brain surgery or similar invasive treatment is for a patient and to learn how a normal, diseased or injured brain is functioning. They map the brain with fMRI to identify regions linked to critical functions such as speaking, moving, sensing, or planning. This is useful to plan for surgery and radiation therapy of the brain. Clinicians also use fMRI to anatomically map the brain and detect the effects of tumors, stroke, head and brain injury, or diseases such as Alzheimer's, and developmental disabilities such as Autism etc ...",what does an mri of the brain check for
importance of foreign capital in indian stock exchange,"['http://kantieremisto.tk/tuweb/bombay-online-trading-system-wiki-878.php', 'http://www.distancelatlong.com/bse-nse-mcx-market-holiday-list/2019/', 'https://www.cheapstockbroker.com/best-broker-for-share-market-in-india/', 'https://www.mymoneykarma.com/share-market/psmspgmill.html', 'http://www.marketswiki.com/wiki/Bombay_Stock_Exchange', 'https://www.educba.com/stock-markets-in-india/', 'http://ilfsinvestmentmanagers.com/ilfs.aspx']","NSE was set up by a group of leading Indian financial institutions at the behest of the government of India to bring transparency to the Indian capital market. Based on the recommendations laid out by the government committee, NSE has been established with a diversified shareholding comprising domestic and global investors. The key domestic investors include Life Insurance Corporation of India, State Bank of India, IFCI Limited IDFC Limited and Stock Holding Corporation of India Limited. And the key global investors are Gagil FDI Limited, GS Strategic Investments Limited, SAIF II SE Investments Mauritius Limited, Aranda Investments (Mauritius) Pte Limited and PI Opportunities Fund I.",importance of foreign capital in indian stock exchange
where was the war for the planet of the apes filmed,['https://www.moviesmad.com/2017/06/war-for-planet-of-apes-2017-movie-wiki.html'],"Principal photography on the film began on October 14, 2015 in the Lower Mainland in Vancouver, under the working title Hidden Fortress. Filming was expected to take place there until early March 2016. Parts of the film were expected to shoot for up to five days in the Kananaskis in late January and early February. In March, Serkis confirmed that he had finished shooting his portions.",where was the war for the planet of the apes filmed
where did tradition of easter eggs come from,"['http://humanities-exchange.org/tag/spring-celebrations/', 'https://www.tinselbox.com/easter-eggs-inspired-decorating/', 'https://voyagevixens.com/2014/04/14/best-easter-egg-hunts-in-the-us/', 'https://wn.com/Easter_egg_hunting', 'http://www.htw.org.au/reflections-in-the-water---from-the-revd-bill-beagley/category/easter', 'https://www.ashcroftcachecreekjournal.com/community/striking-a-balance-birthdays-and-easter-eggs/', 'https://milliethom.com/2016/03/27/yum-easter-eggs/']","The practice of decorating eggshells as part of spring rituals is ancient, with decorated, engraved ostrich eggs found in Africa which are 60,000 years old. In the pre-dynastic period of Egypt and the early cultures of Mesopotamia and Crete, eggs were associated with death and rebirth, as well as with kingship, with decorated ostrich eggs, and representations of ostrich eggs in gold and silver, were commonly placed in graves of the ancient Sumerians and Egyptians as early as 5,000 years ago. These cultural relationships may have influenced early Christian and Islamic cultures in those areas, as well as through mercantile, religious, and political links from those areas around the Mediterranean.",where did tradition of easter eggs come from
