how long do you stay in the hole in prison,"['https://www.tremaisondasan.com/terms', 'http://www.abolishsolitary.com/author/Justin/', 'http://wegorzewo.tv/dzien-otwarty-dla-przedsiebiorczosci/', 'http://latest-law-news.blogspot.com/2015/09/solitary-confinement-in-india.html', 'https://www.demelolaw.com/a-step-forward-in-finding-justice-for-everyone-solitary-confinement-struck-down/', 'https://www.vice.com/en_us/article/8gdb9g/im-short-not-stupid-presents-le-labyrinthe-456', 'https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2019/jan/10/rich-alati-poker-player-bet-dark-room-isolation?CMP=Share_AndroidApp_Tweet']","Solitary confinement is a form of imprisonment in which an inmate is isolated from any human contact, often with the exception of members of prison staff, for 22 -- 24 hours a day, with a sentence ranging from days to decades. It is mostly employed as a form of punishment beyond incarceration for a prisoner, usually for violations of prison regulations. However, it is also used as an additional measure of protection for vulnerable inmates. In the case of prisoners at high risk of suicide, it can be used to prevent access to items that could allow the prisoner to self-harm.",how long do you stay in the hole in prison
difference between new nintendo 3ds and nintendo 3ds,"['http://studyindubai.info/jjjd/japan-ppi-wysu.php', 'https://videogamegeek.com/videogamehardware/172974/new-nintendo-3ds']","Improvements upon the previous models include upgraded processors and increased RAM, an analog pointing stick (C-Stick), two additional shoulder triggers (ZR and ZL), face detection for optimizing the auto stereoscopic 3D display, an included 4 GB microSD card and built-in NFC, as well as minor design changes (such as colored face buttons, and the availability of face plates for the smaller-size model).",difference between new nintendo 3ds and nintendo 3ds
what is the meaning of matter in chemistry,"['https://onlinephilosophyclub.com/forums/viewtopic.php?f=1&t=15178&view=print', 'http://www.undergroundcyberjungle.com/id18.html', 'https://chem.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Introductory_Chemistry/Map%3A_Introductory_Chemistry_(Tro)/03%3A_Matter_and_Energy', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Matter', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Fermion', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Chemical_matter']","In the classical physics observed in everyday life, matter is any substance that has mass and takes up space by having volume. This includes atoms and anything made up of these, but not other energy phenomena or waves such as light or sound. More generally, however, in modern physics, matter is not a fundamental concept because a universal definition of it is elusive; for example, the elementary constituents of atoms may be point particles, each having no volume individually.",what is the meaning of matter in chemistry
where did the symbol of the poppy come from,"['http://www.danmihailescu.ro/seashore-wildflowers', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Poppy', 'http://www.askliterature.com/poetry/critical-analysis-of-sylvia-plaths-poppies-in-october/', 'https://thebookaddictsreviews.wordpress.com/language-of-flowers-challenge/', 'http://justfunfacts.com/interesting-facts-about-poppies/', 'http://flowerisblossoms.blogspot.com/2011/03/attractive-color-of-poppy-flowers.html', 'https://vmhtdesign.com/tag/research/']","Poppies have long been used as a symbol of sleep, peace, and death: Sleep because the opium extracted from them is a sedative, and death because of the common blood-red color of the red poppy in particular. In Greek and Roman myths, poppies were used as offerings to the dead. Poppies used as emblems on tombstones symbolize eternal sleep. This symbolism was evoked in the children's novel The Wonderful Wizard of Oz, in which a magical poppy field threatened to make the protagonists sleep forever.",where did the symbol of the poppy come from
when did cinco de mayo became popular in the us,"['https://www.politico.com/story/2017/05/05/this-day-in-politics-may-5-1862-237817', 'https://segmation.com/blog/2013/04/10/enjoy-cinco-de-may-with-celebration-of-mexican-heritage-and-pride-in-america/', 'http://www.stylophyle.com/blog/2017/5/4/cincodewhat', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2018/05/05/', 'http://www.movies.com/movie-news/cine-latino-iexclque-viva-meacutexico-8-things-you-should-know-about-cinco-de-mayo/12088', 'https://lincolnandmexicoproject.wordpress.com/2017/05/03/what-is-cinco-de-mayo/']","A 2007 UCLA Newsroom article notes that, ""the holiday, which has been celebrated in California continuously since 1863, is virtually ignored in Mexico."" TIME magazine reports that ""Cinco de Mayo started to come into vogue in 1940s America during the rise of the Chicano Movement."" The holiday crossed over from California into the rest of the United States in the 1950s and 1960s but did not gain popularity until the 1980s when marketers, especially beer companies, capitalized on the celebratory nature of the day and began to promote it. It grew in popularity and evolved into a celebration of Mexican culture and heritage, first in areas with large Mexican-American populations, like Los Angeles, Chicago, Houston and San Jose.",when did cinco de mayo became popular in the us
where is the antarctic circle located on a world map,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Arctic_Circle', 'https://mocomi.com/antarctic-circle-facts/', 'http://cmsenvis.cmsindia.org/resources/newspaper/details.asp?id=4953', 'http://www.reefnews.com/reefnews/infopage/oceans/oceans.html', 'https://travel.argentinianexplorer.com/cruises-antarctic-sub-antarctic-islands.php', 'http://cruise.com.au/ports/view/161/antarctic+peninsula', 'http://usa2017.inumo.ru/news/weather-glossary.html']","The Antarctic Circle is roughly 17,662 kilometres (10,975 mi) long. The area south of the Circle is about 20,000,000 km (7,700,000 sq mi) and covers roughly 4% of Earth's surface. The continent of Antarctica covers much of the area within the Antarctic Circle.",where is the antarctic circle located on a world map
where did the name zip code come from,"['http://howto-tipstricks.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=30916', 'https://shipgsl.com/shipping-tools/zip-code-look-up/', 'https://zipcode.org/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Mail', 'http://einfach-reisen.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=42826', 'https://www.longislandcityprocessserver.com/process-server/new-york/nassau-county/long-island/11779', 'https://www.processserverdenver.com/process-server/colorado/denver-county/denver/80292']","ZIP Codes are a system of postal codes used by the United States Postal Service since 1963. The term ZIP, an acronym for Zone Improvement Plan, was chosen to suggest that the mail travels more efficiently, and therefore more quickly (zipping along), when senders use the code in the postal address. The basic format consists of five digits. An extended' ZIP + 4' code, introduced in 1983, includes the five digits of the ZIP Code, a hyphen, and four additional digits that determine a more specific location within a given ZIP Code.",where did the name zip code come from
where is the grantley adams international airport located,"['https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=2&ads=1&author=system&auto=Barbados+airports&standalone=1&domain_name=barbadosairports.com&title=Barbados+airports&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Barbados+airports', 'https://www.dutyfreeinformation.com/trinidad-piarco-airport-duty-free/', 'https://www.europcar.co.uk/locations/guadeloupe/pointe-a-pitre/pointe-a-pitre-airport', 'https://www.osac.gov/Pages/ContentReportDetails.aspx?cid=23807', 'http://www.nationnews.com/nationnews/news/203361/editor-notebook-visitors-history', 'https://library.avsim.net/esearch.php?DLID=158598', 'http://blog.pgmedica.com/facts-of-american-university-of-barbados/']","Grantley Adams International Airport (GAIA) (IATA: BGI, ICAO: TBPB) is the international airport of Barbados, located in Seawell, Christ Church. It is the only designated port of entry for persons arriving and departing by air in Barbados and operates as a major gateway to the Eastern Caribbean. The airport has direct service to destinations in the United States, Canada, Central America and Europe and serves as the second hub for LIAT. In 2016, the airport was the 8th busiest airport in the Caribbean region; and the third busiest airport in the Lesser Antilles; after Queen Beatrix International Airport located in Aruba, and Pointe-à-Pitre International Airport located in the Republic of France within the island of Guadeloupe. GAIA, also remains an important air-link for cruise ship passengers departing and arriving at the Port of Bridgetown, and a base of operations for the Regional Security System (RSS), and the Regional (Caribbean) Police Training Centre.",where is the grantley adams international airport located
what is the name of the file management tool in windows 8.1,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Proprietary_software', 'https://www.dailyhostnews.com/windows-file-manager-on-microsoft-store', 'https://wccftech.com/microsoft-open-sources-ms-dos/']","File Manager is a file manager program bundled with releases of Microsoft Windows between 1990 and 1999 and available from 6 April 2018 as an optional download for all modern releases of Windows, including Windows 10.",what is the name of the file management tool in windows 8.1
motion of earth is a combination of motion,"['http://www.thricetwisted.com/Motion.php', 'https://www.airports-worldwide.com/articles/article0620.php', 'https://www.encyclopedia.com/science-and-technology/astronomy-and-space-exploration/astronomy-general/rotation', 'https://www.enchantedlearning.com/subjects/astronomy/planets/earth/Speeds.shtml', 'https://janeandsita.com/blog/2019/1/17/cancer-changes-everything-and-nothing', 'http://c3f887211.raioid.com/', 'http://ynambu.com/6044406845']","The Earth is rotating or spinning around its axis. This is evidenced by day and night, at the equator the earth has an eastward velocity of 0.4651 kilometres per second (1,040 mph). The Earth is also orbiting around the Sun in an orbital revolution. A complete orbit around the sun takes one year, or about 365 days; it averages a speed of about 30 kilometres per second (67,000 mph).",motion of earth is a combination of motion
where do eastern bluebirds go in the winter,"['http://allaboutbirds.info/?m=20140203', 'https://kiwifoto.com/galleries/birds/eastern_bluebird/', 'http://windyacresnaturalfarm.blogspot.com/2014/01/', 'http://cwf-fcf.org/en/resources/for-educators/resource-sheets/build-life-support-systems.html?print=t', 'https://dnr.maryland.gov/wildlife/Pages/plants_wildlife/Gray_Catbird.aspx']","Fruits are especially important when insects are scarce in the winter. Some preferred winter food sources include dogwood, hawthorn, wild grape, and sumac, and hackberry seeds. Supplemental fruits eaten include black raspberries, bayberries, fruit of honeysuckle, Virginia creeper, eastern juniper, and pokeberries. Bluebirds feed by perching on a high point, such as a branch or fence post, and swooping down to catch insects on or near the ground. The availability of a winter food source will often determine whether or not a bird will migrate. If bluebirds do remain in a region for the winter, they group and seek cover in heavy thickets, orchards, or other areas in which adequate food and cover resources are available.",where do eastern bluebirds go in the winter
the epic of gilgamesh was the product of the civilization,"['http://www.evolveandascend.com/2015/01/02/3-lessons-the-epic-of-gilgamesh-can-teach-us-about-life/', 'https://nammu.com/eng/lapis-lazuli-legends/', 'https://www.booksread.stream/book/505934239/an-old-babylonian-version-of-the-gilgamesh-epic.html', 'https://tanitasonlineportfolio.weebly.com/gilgamesh.html', 'http://waterbridge47.com/western-australia/the-story-of-a-new-name-pdf.php', 'http://archaeologybriefs.blogspot.com/2015/10/', 'http://tamparealestate4you.com/tasmania/the-epic-of-gilgamesh-nk-sandars-pdf.php']","The Epic of Gilgamesh is an epic poem from ancient Mesopotamia that is often regarded as the earliest surviving great work of literature. The literary history of Gilgamesh begins with five Sumerian poems about' Bilgamesh' (Sumerian for' Gilgamesh'), king of Uruk, dating from the Third Dynasty of Ur (circa 2100 BC). These independent stories were later used as source material for a combined epic. The first surviving version of this combined epic, known as the ""Old Babylonian"" version, dates to the 18th century BC and is titled after its incipit, Shūtur eli sharrī (""Surpassing All Other Kings""). Only a few tablets of it have survived. The later ""Standard"" version dates from the 13th to the 10th centuries BC and bears the incipit Sha naqba īmuru (""He who Saw the Deep"", in modern terms: ""He who Sees the Unknown""). Approximately two thirds of this longer, twelve-tablet version have been recovered. Some of the best copies were discovered in the library ruins of the 7th-century BC Assyrian king Ashurbanipal.",the epic of gilgamesh was the product of the civilization
what type of venom does a rattlesnake have,"['https://critter.science/rattlesnake/', 'https://amadorvalleyvetcenter.com/LivesSaved/story.php?Kenji-Mendaros-33', 'http://www.reptilesmagazine.com/11-North-American-Rattlesnakes/', 'http://ed5015.tripod.com/BFierySerpents98.htm', 'https://pokerdoctor.blogspot.com/2010/08/well-hello-there-mr-snake.html', 'http://www.nicenfunny.com/2011/10/worlds-most-poisonous-and-deadliest.html', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Rattlesnake']","The venom is hemotoxic, destroying tissue, causing necrosis and coagulopathy (disrupted blood clotting). In the U.S., the tiger rattlesnake (C. tigris) and some varieties of the Mojave rattlesnake (C. scutulatus) also have a presynaptic neurotoxic venom component known as Mojave type A toxin, which can cause severe paralysis. Although it has a comparatively low venom yield, the venom toxicity of C. tigris is considered to be among the highest of all rattlesnake venoms, and among the highest of all snakes in the Western Hemisphere based on LD studies conducted on laboratory mice. C. scutulatus is also widely regarded as producing one of the most toxic snake venoms in the Americas, based on LD studies in laboratory mice.",what type of venom does a rattlesnake have
my love from the star go hye mi,"['http://mariboo.info/viewtopic.php?t=20731', 'http://nutraburn10.info/viewtopic.php?t=17417', 'http://info-info-info-info-info.info/?page_id=13467', 'http://www.mkvhub.org/2018/12/my-love-from-star-s01-complete-hindi.html', 'http://agenciatm.info/?newsid=39', 'https://www.hallyulife.com/a-beginners-dose-of-k-dramas-8-must-watch-korean-dramas/2315/', 'https://buddymantra.com/top-k-dramas-of-all-time/']","My Love from the Star (Hangul: 별 에서 온 그대; RR: Byeoreseo on geudae; literally You Who Came from the Stars) is a South Korean television series starring Jun Ji-hyun, Kim Soo-hyun, Park Hae-jin and Yoo In-na in lead. Written by Park Ji-eun, it is a romantic fantasy story about an alien who landed on Earth in the Joseon Dynasty and, 400 years later, falls in love with a top actress in the modern era. It aired on SBS from December 18, 2013 to February 27, 2014 on Wednesdays and Thursdays at 22: 00 for 21 episodes; the production company extended the original 20-episode run with one episode, due to high viewers' demand.",my love from the star go hye mi
name the ivy league colleges in the us,"['https://www.youngwonks.com/blog/What-Do-Ivy-League-Schools-Look-For-In-Their-Students', 'https://versus.com/en/pratt-school-of-engineering-vs-yale-faculty-of-engineering', 'https://markashwill.com/2015/08/19/whats-in-a-name-ivy-on-my-mind/', 'http://mitchj.info/new/ivy-league-logo.html', 'https://blogs.cul.columbia.edu/spotlights/', 'http://www.dlszobel.edu.ph/?p=14411', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Ivy_League']","The Ivy League is a collegiate athletic conference comprising sports teams from eight private institutions of higher education in the Northeastern United States. The conference name is also commonly used to refer to those eight schools as a group beyond the sports context. The eight institutions are Brown University, Columbia University, Cornell University, Dartmouth College, Harvard University, the University of Pennsylvania, Princeton University, and Yale University. The term Ivy League has connotations of academic excellence, selectivity in admissions, and social elitism.",name the ivy league colleges in the us
who is the owner of the baltimore orioles,"['https://eventseeker.com/baltimore/sep-14-2018/303480084-baltimore-orioles-vs-chicago-white-sox', 'https://www.sportsmemorabilia.com/team/baltimore_orioles', 'http://www.online-checks.net/baltimore-orioles/', 'https://www.nytimes.com/1998/05/16/sports/baseball-piazza-traded-for-what-s-left-of-the-marlins.html', 'https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_nj_042513/', 'https://eventseeker.com/new-york/mar-28-2019/344324622-baltimore-orioles-at-new-york-yankees-tickets', 'https://cheapconcerttickets.me/events/baltimore-orioles']","Angelos is also the majority owner of the Baltimore Orioles, a baseball team in the American League East Division.",who is the owner of the baltimore orioles
how much of the colorado river reaches the ocean,"['http://www.worldheritage.org/articles/eng/Colorado_River_(U.S.)', 'http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/Colorado_River', 'https://kids.britannica.com/students/article/Dnieper-River/274025', 'http://mavensphotoblog.com/2011/01/03/imperial-valleysalton-sea-road-trip-day-1/', 'https://urbanwatercyclesolutions.com/ballaratregionwatersystems/', 'http://caf.msinfo.info/php/buscar.php?base=biblo&cipar=biblo.par&epilogo=&Formato=w&Opcion=detalle&Expresion=?PAFRICA', 'http://aref.ab.ca/tag/2018/']","Flows at the mouth of the river have steadily declined since the beginning of the 20th century, and in most years after 1960 the Colorado River has run dry before reaching the Pacific Ocean. Irrigation, industrial, and municipal diversions, evaporation from reservoirs, natural runoff, and likely climate change, have all contributed to this substantial reduction in flow, threatening the water supply for the future. For example, the Gila River -- formerly one of the Colorado's largest tributaries -- contributes little more than a trickle in most years due to use of its water by cities and farms in central Arizona. The average flow rate of the Colorado at the northernmost point of the Mexico -- United States border (NIB, or Northerly International Boundary) is about 2,060 cubic feet per second (58 m / s), 1.49 million acre feet (1.84 km) per year -- less than a tenth of the natural flow -- due to upstream water use. Below this point, the remaining flow is diverted to irrigate the Mexicali Valley, leaving a dry riverbed from Morelos Dam to the sea that is supplemented by intermittent flows of irrigation drainage water. There have been exceptions, however, namely in the early to mid-1980s, when the Colorado once again reached the sea during several consecutive years of record-breaking precipitation and snowmelt. In 1984, so much excess runoff occurred that some 16.5 million acre feet (20.4 km), or 22,860 cubic feet per second (647 m / s), poured into the sea.",how much of the colorado river reaches the ocean
who played the first match in the world cup,"['http://www.fifaontherocks.com/2014/06/fifa-history-world-cup-2014.html', 'http://www.fairoakjunior.co.uk/news/detail/november-sports-news-1/', 'https://dzinepress.com/2010/06/the-ultimate-resource-about-football-world-cup-history/', 'http://toeslayer2000.blogspot.com/2017/11/history-of-fifa-world-cup-in-beginning.html', 'http://www.historyoftheworldcup.com/', 'http://adegic.com/read/200907/77449.shtml', 'https://www.pasoroblesmarathon.com/world-cup-qualifying-mexico-vs-usa-history/']","Thirteen teams (seven from South America, four from Europe and two from North America) entered the tournament. Only a few European teams chose to participate because of the difficulty of travelling to South America. The teams were divided into four groups, with the winner of each group progressing to the semi-finals. The first two World Cup matches took place simultaneously, and were won by France and the United States, who defeated Mexico 4 -- 1 and Belgium 3 -- 0, respectively. Lucien Laurent of France scored the first goal in World Cup history, while US goalkeeper Jimmy Douglas posted the first official ""clean sheet"" in the tournament.",who played the first match in the world cup
what was the ruling in brown v. board of education,"['https://www.huffpost.com/entry/dear-department-of-justic_b_10123938', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/1954/5/17/us-supreme-court-rules-on-brown-v-board-of-education', 'https://www.educationindex.com/essay/Plessy-V-Ferguson-Analysis-FKJF45H44Z', 'https://lrculturevulture.com/tag/supreme-court/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Education', 'https://mediarichlearning.com/lexicon/brown-v-board-of-education/', 'https://patimes.org/current-social-issues-play-law/']","Brown v. Board of Education of Topeka, 347 U.S. 483 (1954), was a landmark United States Supreme Court case in which the Court declared state laws establishing separate public schools for black and white students to be unconstitutional. The decision effectively overturned the Plessy v. Ferguson decision of 1896, which allowed state-sponsored segregation, insofar as it applied to public education. Handed down on May 17, 1954, the Warren Court's unanimous (9 -- 0) decision stated that ""separate educational facilities are inherently unequal."" As a result, de jure racial segregation was ruled a violation of the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment of the United States Constitution. This ruling paved the way for integration and was a major victory of the Civil Rights Movement, and a model for many future impact litigation cases. However, the decision's fourteen pages did not spell out any sort of method for ending racial segregation in schools, and the Court's second decision in Brown II (349 U.S. 294 (1955)) only ordered states to desegregate ""with all deliberate speed"".",what was the ruling in brown v. board of education
i need you but you don't need me,"['http://tellyourfriendsrock.com/news-magazines/u-need-me-i-dont-need-u-ed-sheeran.php', 'http://switchforfree.info/news.php?action=show&id=10311']","""You Need Me, I Don't Need You"" (or simply ""You Need Me"") is a song by English singer-songwriter Ed Sheeran. It was released as the second single from his first studio album, + (Pronounced ""Plus""), and was released on 26 August 2011 in the United Kingdom.",i need you but you don't need me
what is the position of akwa ibom state,"['https://www.rvolutionize.com/Thread-Nigeria-Description', 'http://erikdehaan.tk/tv-33-catalonia-online-dating-site.html', 'http://actasatech.com/index.php?q=volume.view.16', 'https://ijmbe.org.ng/ijmbbauchistate.php', 'https://mypastquestion.com/akwa-ibom-state-civil-service-commission-massive-recruitment-2019/', 'https://ijmb.org.ng/ijmb-in-akwaibom.php', 'https://ogavenue.com.ng/venues-in-kwara?utm_source=ov-home-page&utm_campaign=locations']","Akwa Ibom is a state in Nigeria. It is located in the coastal southern part of the country, lying between latitudes 4 ° 32 ′ N and 5 ° 33 ′ N, and longitudes 7 ° 25 ′ E and 8 ° 25 ′ E. The state is located in the South-South geopolitical zone, and is bordered on the east by Cross River State, on the west by Rivers State and Abia State, and on the south by the Atlantic Ocean and the southernmost tip of Cross River State.",what is the position of akwa ibom state
where did the name border collie come from,"['http://puppystoreatdoral.com/index.php?option=com_k2&view=item&id=150:border-collie-puppies-for-sale-miami', 'https://www.bordercollies.gr/border-collie/item/425-the-border-collie', 'https://www.dogspot.in/border-collie/', 'https://www.arcbcr.org/', 'http://juliueti.blogspot.com/2012/01/border-collie-is-my-best-love-pet.html', 'https://www.ukpets.com/dog-breeds/border-collie', 'http://www.dognamed.com/names/border-terrier-names']","The Border Collie is descended from landrace collies, a type found widely in the British Isles. The name for the breed came from its probable place of origin along the Anglo-Scottish border. Mention of the ""Collie"" or ""Colley"" type first appeared toward the end of the 19th century, although the word ""collie"" is older than this and has its origin in the Scots language. It is also thought that the word' collie' comes from the old Celtic word for useful. Many of the best Border Collies today can be traced back to a dog known as Old Hemp.",where did the name border collie come from
what primarily makes it difficult to observe the process of star formation,['http://www.universe-galaxies-stars.com/Star_formation.html'],"The structure of the molecular cloud and the effects of the protostar can be observed in near-IR extinction maps (where the number of stars are counted per unit area and compared to a nearby zero extinction area of sky), continuum dust emission and rotational transitions of CO and other molecules; these last two are observed in the millimeter and submillimeter range. The radiation from the protostar and early star has to be observed in infrared astronomy wavelengths, as the extinction caused by the rest of the cloud in which the star is forming is usually too big to allow us to observe it in the visual part of the spectrum. This presents considerable difficulties as the Earth's atmosphere is almost entirely opaque from 20μm to 850μm, with narrow windows at 200μm and 450μm. Even outside this range, atmospheric subtraction techniques must be used.",what primarily makes it difficult to observe the process of star formation
who played mary in the movie jesus of nazareth,['http://mitchj.info/new/olivia-hussey-juliet.html'],"In 1974, she appeared as the lead character, Jess, in the cult horror film Black Christmas. She would reunite with Zeffirelli in the miniseries Jesus of Nazareth (1977), as Mary, mother of Jesus, and appeared in John Guillermin's Agatha Christie adaptation Death on the Nile (1978). She would appear in several international productions throughout the 1980s, including the Japanese production Virus (1980), and the Australian horror film Turkey Shoot (1982). In 1990, she appeared in two other horror productions: Psycho IV: The Beginning and Stephen King's It.",who played mary in the movie jesus of nazareth
who would be covered under the dream act,"['https://thesouthwestjournal.com/tag/immigration/', 'https://silverspringcares.org/volunteer-advocate-guest-post-belkis-amador-ssc-board-member/', 'http://radio-solidarity.wsm.ie/c/dream-act-rally-dublin-peter-king-nov17?page=5', 'https://www.saddleback.edu/counseling/what-daca', 'http://www.sonsoflibertyradio.com/bradlee-dean/the-dean/daca-judicial-activism-teeing-it-up-for-sonia-sotomayor.html', 'https://www.bkreader.com/2018/01/29/local-town-hall-debates-future-daca/', 'https://onethinkingdude.com/']","The Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (DACA) was an American immigration policy that allowed some individuals who entered the country as minors, and had either entered or remained in the country illegally, to receive a renewable two-year period of deferred action from deportation and to be eligible for a work permit. As of 2017, approximately 800,000 individuals -- referred to as Dreamers after the DREAM Act bill -- were enrolled in the program created by DACA. The policy was established by the Obama administration in June 2012 and rescinded by the Trump administration in September 2017.",who would be covered under the dream act
how did they bring the statue of liberty to america,"['http://www.8monks.com/2016/04/25/construction-of-the-statue-of-liberty-in-1884/', 'http://www.howmanyarethere.us/new-york-statue-of-liberty-times-square/', 'http://blog.thebuttonmonger.com/2012/10/the-statues-head-on-exhibit-at.html', 'https://highlanderimagesphotography.com/2016/02/10/big-noise-new-york-iconic-images-of-the-big-apple/', 'https://codepoints.net/U+1F5FD', 'http://www.onthesetofnewyork.com/xmen.html', 'https://buyoya.com/travel-us-the-statue-of-liberty/']","The torch-bearing arm was displayed at the Centennial Exposition in Philadelphia in 1876, and in Madison Square Park in Manhattan from 1876 to 1882. Fundraising proved difficult, especially for the Americans, and by 1885 work on the pedestal was threatened by lack of funds. Publisher Joseph Pulitzer, of the New York World, started a drive for donations to finish the project and attracted more than 120,000 contributors, most of whom gave less than a dollar. The statue was built in France, shipped overseas in crates, and assembled on the completed pedestal on what was then called Bedloe's Island. The statue's completion was marked by New York's first ticker-tape parade and a dedication ceremony presided over by President Grover Cleveland.",how did they bring the statue of liberty to america
when was the last time an amature won the us open,['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Lee_Trevino'],"Goodman's victory 85 years ago was the eighth and most recent by an amateur at the U.S. Open; Bobby Jones won four, the last in 1930 was part of his grand slam.",when was the last time an amature won the us open
when did sweet potatoes come to north america,"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Sweet_potato', 'http://www.gardenology.org/wiki/Sweet_potato', 'http://thackermountainlodge.com/sweetpotatoinfo.html', 'http://personalloansxjil.org/Senegalese_cuisine.html', 'https://recipereminiscing.wordpress.com/category/vegetarian-dishes/', 'http://sernecportal.org/portal/taxa/index.php?taxon=digitaria%20horizontalis', 'https://arnoldzwicky.org/2015/09/07/returning-to-your-roots/']","Ipomoea batatas is native to the tropical regions in the Americas. Of the approximately 50 genera and more than 1,000 species of Convolvulaceae, I. batatas is the only crop plant of major importance -- some others are used locally (e.g., I. aquatica ""kangkong""), but many are poisonous. The genus Ipomoea that contains the sweet potato also includes several garden flowers called morning glories, though that term is not usually extended to Ipomoea batatas. Some cultivars of Ipomoea batatas are grown as ornamental plants under the name tuberous morning glory, used in a horticultural context.",when did sweet potatoes come to north america
the supreme court’s decision in obergefell v. hodges (2015) was significant because it,"['http://biblenews1.com/astrology/acharts/davis_kim.html', 'https://www.foxie105fm.com/category/local-news/page/3018/', 'https://www.nsba.org/amicusbriefs?page=5', 'http://azemikalaw.com/post-59-us-supreme-court-will-hear-prop--cases', 'https://constitutioncenter.org/blog/podcast-loving-v.-virginia-at-50']","Obergefell v. Hodges, 576 U.S. ___ (2015) (/ ˈoʊbərɡəfɛl / OH-bər-gə-fel), is a landmark civil rights case in which the United States Supreme Court ruled that the fundamental right to marry is guaranteed to same-sex couples by both the Due Process Clause and the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment to the United States Constitution in a 5 -- 4 decision.",the supreme court’s decision in obergefell v. hodges (2015) was significant because it
where did the idea of football come from,"['https://www.vintag.es/2018/03/american-football-players.html', 'http://www.island.lk/index.php?page_cat=article-details&page=article-details&code_title=59974', 'http://hmfly.info/?option=com_content&view=article&id=2', 'http://mutyabuena.info/?newsid=48096', 'http://lyrakonyvesbolt.info/news.php?action=show&id=9914', 'https://capacitivetouchscreen3.info/concepts-sport-los-angeles-chargers-navy-front-runner-french-terry-jam-shorts.asp', 'https://photoboothrental9.info/michigan-state-spartans-happy-holidays-glass-ball-ornament.php']","The history of American football can be traced to early versions of rugby football and association football. Both games have their origin in varieties of football played in Britain in the mid-19th century, in which a football is kicked at a goal or kicked over a line, which in turn were based on the varieties of English public school football games.",where did the idea of football come from
which book is game of thrones season 8,"['http://www.tripwiremagazine.co.uk/headlines/first-day-on-set-for-game-of-thrones-season-eight/', 'https://lovelytab.com/post/game-of-thrones-season-8-wallpaper-theme/', 'https://ushdtv.org/gameofthrones8online/', 'https://africainformer.org/author/refilwe/', 'https://www.phcracker.net/threads/5377/', 'http://gameofthroneswatchonline.com/show/season-7/?orderby=title', 'http://loneroad.info/viewtopic.php?t=47707']","The eighth and final season of the fantasy drama television series Game of Thrones was confirmed by HBO in July 2016. Unlike the first six seasons that all consisted of ten episodes, and the seventh which consisted of seven episodes, the eighth season will consist of only six episodes, and is set to air in 2019. Like the previous season, it will largely consist of original content currently not found in George R.R. Martin's A Song of Ice and Fire series, and will instead adapt material Martin revealed to showrunners about the upcoming novels in the series, The Winds of Winter and A Dream of Spring.",which book is game of thrones season 8
where is the capital city of arizona located,"['https://arizona.ablending.com/service-area/phoenix/', 'https://www.yourgreenpal.com/local/lawn-care-phoenix-az', 'https://www.zenrentpm.com/phoenix-property-management', 'https://www.fly-efi.com/destinations/United-States/West/flights-to-phoenix-arizona', 'https://www.mdjobsite.com/index2.cfm?page=JobsView&ID=21207878&Source=HotJobs', 'http://buffaloairwaysvirtual.com/index.php/schedules/brief/7051', 'https://www.lindasellsarizona.com/community/area/Phoenix%20and%20the%20Greater%20Metropolitan%20area/']","Phoenix is the anchor of the Phoenix metropolitan area, also known as the Valley of the Sun, which in turn is a part of the Salt River Valley. The metropolitan area is the 12th largest by population in the United States, with approximately 4.73 million people as of 2017. In addition, Phoenix is the seat of Maricopa County, and at 517.9 square miles (1,341 km), it is the largest city in the state, more than twice the size of Tucson and one of the largest cities in the United States.",where is the capital city of arizona located
what is the rank of ensign in the navy,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/United_States_Public_Health_Service_Commissioned_Corps', 'https://rankly.com/list/best-character-rank-off-all-time', 'http://www.infogalactic.com/info/Rear_Admiral_(United_States)', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Lieutenant_(junior_grade).html', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/Military_rank', 'http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Colonel_(United_States)', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/Master_Sergeant']","In the United States Navy, the rank of ensign superseded passed midshipman in 1862. Ensign is the junior commissioned officer rank in the United States Navy, the United States Coast Guard, the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration Commissioned Officer Corps, and the PHS Commissioned Corps. This rank is also used in the U.S. Maritime Service and the U.S. Naval Sea Cadet Corps. Ensign ranks below lieutenant junior grade, and it is equivalent to a second lieutenant in the U.S. Army, the Marine Corps, and the Air Force.",what is the rank of ensign in the navy
how.many times has mexico won the world cup,"['https://sportstarinfluencer.com/sports/football/world/mexico', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Sergio_Ordu%C3%B1a', 'https://fifa.fandom.com/wiki/France_national_team', 'https://www.cheap-football.com/mexico-c-1_9.html', 'https://rentalcarmomma.com/cities2/nantes.htm', 'http://bpea.co.uk/blog.php', 'https://www.livefootballtickets.com/world-cup/mexico-tickets.html']","Mexico has qualified to sixteen World Cups and has qualified consecutively since 1994, making it one of six countries to do so. The Mexico national team, along with Brazil are the only two nations to make it out of the group stage over the last seven World Cups. Along with Germany, Brazil, Italy, Argentina, France, Spain and Uruguay, Mexico is one of eight nations to have won two of the three most important football tournaments (the World Cup, Confederations Cup, and Summer Olympics), having won the 1999 FIFA Confederations Cup and the 2012 Summer Olympics.",how.many times has mexico won the world cup
where did the term third world country originated,"['https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=worldimmigrants.com&ads=1&title=World+immigrants&auto=World+immigrants&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=World+immigrants&pagenum=3', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Third_World', 'http://www.myanmar-image.com/topic/is-myanmar-a-third-world-country-2', 'http://dreamstrikes.com/asking/What-are-first-world-second-world-and-third-world-countries.shtml', 'https://endtimesprophecyreport.com/2018/07/28/is-the-united-states-now-a-third-world-country/', 'https://www.panoramas.pitt.edu/art-and-culture/dangerous-misconceptions-about-latin-america-and-%E2%80%9Cthird-world-countries%E2%80%9D', 'http://dawdlez.com/2015/09/08/10-history-myths-you-probably-believe-part-iii/']","According to Online Etymology Dictionary the term Third World was formulated in 1952 by French economic historian Alfred Sauvy to mean countries that were neither part of the West nor of the Iron Curtain. Thus the term originally had a political meaning as it arose during the Cold War to define countries that remained non-aligned with either NATO or the Communist Bloc. The United States, Canada, Japan, South Korea, Western European nations and their allies represented the First World, while the Soviet Union, China, Cuba and their allies represented the Second World. This terminology provided a way of broadly categorizing the nations of the Earth into three groups based on political and politically-related economic divisions.",where did the term third world country originated
how did the us marines get their name,"['http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/9892964', 'https://www.cowboyron.com/2016/07/21/marines-raise-flag-over-iwo-jima/', 'http://www.sacramentomarines.com/about/united-states-marine-corps/', 'https://worldwartwo.wikia.org/wiki/United_States_Marine_Corps', 'http://www.americanrevolutionarywar.net/', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=American_Revolutionary_War', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/United_States_Marines']","The United States Marine Corps traces its roots to the Continental Marines of the American Revolutionary War, formed by Captain Samuel Nicholas by a resolution of the Second Continental Congress on 10 November 1775, to raise two battalions of Marines. That date is regarded and celebrated as the date of the Marine Corps' birthday. At the end of the American Revolution, both the Continental Navy and Continental Marines were disbanded in April 1783. The institution itself would not be resurrected until 11 July 1798. At that time, in preparation for the Quasi-War with France, Congress created the United States Marine Corps. Marines had been enlisted by the War Department as early as August 1797 for service in the new-build frigates authorized by the Congressional ""Act to provide a Naval Armament"" of 18 March 1794, which specified the numbers of Marines to recruit for each frigate.",how did the us marines get their name
what types of transportation can be found in london,"['http://www.propertyuk.com/about-uk/london-guide', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/7_July_2005_London_bombings', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Public_transport', 'https://beta.southernrailway.com/tickets/smartcards-oyster-and-plusbus/oyster', 'http://www.greenabode.co.uk/days-out-train/', 'http://devilz-hell.dzh-esports.de/index/board/thread/where/5352/start/0', 'https://www.uktourcenter.com/getting-around-london/']","Public transport services are dominated by the executive agency for transport in London: Transport for London (TfL). TfL controls the majority of public transport, including the Underground, Buses, Tramlink, the Docklands Light Railway, London River Services and the London Overground. Other rail services are either franchised to train operating companies by the national Department for Transport (DfT). TfL also controls most major roads in London, but not minor roads. In addition, there are several independent airports operating in London, including Heathrow, the busiest airport in the United Kingdom.",what types of transportation can be found in london
in the song don bring me down who is bruce,"['http://www.wfmu.org/playlists/shows/68184', 'https://www.jinglejanglejungle.net/2014/12/elo-dont-bring-me-down.html']","A common mondegreen in the song is the perception that, following the title line, Lynne shouts ""Bruce!"". In the liner notes of the ELO compilation Flashback and elsewhere, Lynne has explained that he is singing a made-up word, ""Grooss,"" which some have suggested sounds like the German expression ""Gruß."" After the song's release, so many people had misinterpreted the word as ""Bruce"" that Lynne actually began to sing the word as ""Bruce"" for fun at live shows.",in the song don bring me down who is bruce
what does usp after a drug name mean,"['http://wasatch-labs.net/faq/', 'http://www.galeriasicart.com/the-success-was-only-moderate/?lang=CA', 'http://bellezza-med.com/services/vivier/', 'https://plymouth-homeopathy.co.uk/tag/health/', 'https://www.neurobiologix.com/aboutus.asp', 'http://allods-zone.ru/3537-usp-verified-garcinia-cambogia.php', 'http://ecstasy.com.ua/creatine']","USP also conducts verification programs for dietary supplement products and ingredients. These are testing and audit programs. Products that meet the requirements of the program can display the USP Verified Dietary Supplement Mark on their labels. This is different from seeing the letters ""USP"" alone on a dietary supplement label, which means that the manufacturer is claiming to adhere to USP standards. USP does not test such products as it does with USP Verified products.",what does usp after a drug name mean
why are there 64 teams in the ncaa tournament,"['http://www.southlondonhardcore.com/2014/05/episode-118-dj-aj-from-hardnoise.html', 'https://www.lebas.com/march-madness/', 'http://www.error418.org/2013/10/raspberry-pi-power-consumption-9-month.html', 'http://www.yougotthat.ca/2012/06/in-bowl-with-eisei-sugimoto.html', 'http://ricknicholsonline.com/2016/09/labor-day-wishes.html', 'http://www.quoteflicker.com/2016/06/optimists-and-pessimists.html', 'http://www.fionev.com/2014/11/afternoon-tea-at-macalister-mansion.html?showComment=1488888856743']","The tournament teams include champions from 32 Division I conferences (which receive automatic bids), and 36 teams which are awarded at-large berths. These ""at-large"" teams are chosen by an NCAA selection committee, then announced in a nationally televised event on the Sunday preceding the ""First Four"" play-in games, currently held in Dayton, Ohio, and dubbed Selection Sunday. The 68 teams are divided into four regions and organized into a single-elimination ""bracket"", which pre-determines, when a team wins a game, which team it will face next. Each team is ""seeded"", or ranked, within its region from 1 to 16. After the First Four, the tournament occurs during the course of three weekends, at pre-selected neutral sites across the United States. Teams, seeded by rank, proceed through a single-game elimination bracket beginning with a ""first four"" consisting of 8 low-seeded teams playing in 4 games for a position in the first round the Tuesday and Wednesday before the first round begins, a first round consisting of 64 teams playing in 32 games over the course of a week, the ""Sweet Sixteen"" and ""Elite Eight"" rounds the next week and weekend, respectively, and -- for the last weekend of the tournament -- the ""Final Four"" round. The Final Four is usually played during the first weekend of April. These four teams, one from each region (East, South, Midwest, and West), compete in a preselected location for the national championship.",why are there 64 teams in the ncaa tournament
in fetal circulation what blood vessels have the highest level of oxygen,"['https://pediaa.com/difference-between-blood-and-plasma/', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Fetal_circulation', 'http://www.newsinferno.com/exposure-to-911-toxic-cloud-linked-to-low-birth-weight-babies/', 'http://www.thenaturalcarnivore.com/blog/category/raw%20feeding', 'https://alevelbiology.co.uk/notes/the-biological-importance-of-water/', 'https://www.fortishealthcare.com/india/diseases/preeclampsia-871', 'https://birthinjuries.us/practice-areas/preeclampsia-eclampsia/']","The circulatory system of the mother is not directly connected to that of the fetus, so the placenta functions as the respiratory center for the fetus as well as a site of filtration for plasma nutrients and wastes. Water, glucose, amino acids, vitamins, and inorganic salts freely diffuse across the placenta along with oxygen. The uterine arteries carry blood to the placenta, and the blood permeates the sponge-like material there. Oxygen then diffuses from the placenta to the chorionic villus, an alveolus-like structure, where it is then carried to the umbilical vein.",in fetal circulation what blood vessels have the highest level of oxygen
who died in the lynyrd skynyrd band plane crash,"['http://musiccitynashville.org/music-feature/nashville-film-festival-focusing-on-rock-legends/', 'http://www.check-six.com/Crash_Sites/LynyrdSkynyrd-N55VM.htm', 'https://talkingloudandsayingnothingparts3and4.wordpress.com/2013/08/', 'http://www.wlup.com/2016/10/20/lynyrd-skynyrd-plane-crash-was-39-years-ago-today/', 'https://i95rock.com/lynyrd-skynyrd-plane-crashes/', 'http://melodicrock.com/tags/lynyrd-skynyrd', 'https://www.telegram.com/article/20090129/NEWS/901290731']","Lead vocalist / founding member Ronnie Van Zant, guitarist / vocalist Steve Gaines, backing vocalist Cassie Gaines (Steve's older sister), assistant road manager Dean Kilpatrick, pilot Walter McCreary, and co-pilot William Gray all died as a result of the crash; twenty others survived.",who died in the lynyrd skynyrd band plane crash
where is singapore located on the world map,"['https://www.levelupvillage.com/gps/singapore/', 'https://asiatourist.co/foods-and-drinks/how-to-eat-like-a-local-in-singapore.html', 'https://www.visitsingapore.org/travelguide/', 'http://www.reasonchapel.com/2018/03/04/singapore-at-53-from-swamp-to-skyscrapers-lawrence-afolabi/', 'https://wyldfamilytravel.com/singapore/page/2/', 'https://kipdf.com/3rd-global-congress-on-plant-biology-and-biotechnology_5b6eb1dcb7d7bced642a1243.html', 'http://hope2000education.com/destination.html']","Singapore (/ ˈsɪŋ (ɡ) əpɔːr / (listen)), officially the Republic of Singapore, is a sovereign city-state and island country in Southeast Asia. It lies one degree (137 kilometres or 85 miles) north of the equator, at the southern tip of the Malay Peninsula, with Indonesia's Riau Islands to the south and Peninsular Malaysia to the north. Singapore's territory consists of one main island along with 62 other islets. Since independence, extensive land reclamation has increased its total size by 23% (130 square kilometres or 50 square miles).",where is singapore located on the world map
theme of the poem the spider and the fly,"['https://www.leaveittoleslie.com.au/product/the-spider-and-the-fly/', 'https://www.taxconnections.com/taxblog/americans-abroad-and-irs-amnesty-offers-in-ovdp/', 'https://www.lifeonthepavement.com/the-last-wolf-poem/', 'http://southafricanartists.com/black-widow-108078', 'https://nics-spider-project.weebly.com/spider-poem.html']","The Spider and the Fly is a poem by Mary Howitt (1799 -- 1888), published in 1828. The first line of the poem is ""' Will you walk into my parlour?' said the Spider to the Fly."" The story tells of a cunning Spider who ensnares a naïve Fly through the use of seduction and flattery. The poem is a cautionary tale against those who use flattery and charm to disguise their true evil intentions.",theme of the poem the spider and the fly
how many times have the astros appeared in the world series,"['http://industrious.info/trends/06-10-2018/astros.html', 'https://nationalticketagency.com/houston-astros-tickets.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/2005_Major_League_Baseball_season', 'http://talkerofthetown.com/2019/03/22/third-time-is-the-charm-pruitt-tells-us-what-will-happen-pennant-race-19-in-eight-sestets-and-a-couplet/', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Orlando_Hern%C3%A1ndez', 'https://www.johnpielli.com/bases-empty-blog/category/hank-wyse', 'http://industrious.info/trends/10-10-2018/astros.html']","The Astros played in the NL from 1962 to 2012. They played in the West Division from 1969 to 1993, and the Central Division from 1994 to 2012. While a member of the NL, the Astros played in one World Series, in 2005, against the Chicago White Sox, in which they were swept in four games. In 2017, they became the first franchise in MLB history to have won a pennant in both the NL and the AL, when they defeated the New York Yankees in the ALCS. They subsequently won the 2017 World Series against the Los Angeles Dodgers, winning four games to three, earning the team, and Texas, its first World Series title.",how many times have the astros appeared in the world series
where are the us virgin islands on a map,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Left-_and_right-hand_traffic', 'http://www.stjohnarts.org/', 'https://www.islandrealestate.com/info/caribbean/us-virgin-islands/', 'https://www.european-yacht-charters.com/destinations/north-america-south-america-and-the-caribbean/us-virgin-islands/', 'https://www.exportportal.com/category/computer-cables-and-connectors/405/country/us-virgin-islands-240', 'https://www.restorekewaunee.com/holidays-in-british-virgin-islands/', 'https://www.skyscanner.com.sg/flights-to/vi/cheap-flights-to-us-virgin-islands.html']","The United States Virgin Islands (USVI; also called the American Virgin Islands), officially the Virgin Islands of the United States, is a group of islands in the Caribbean that is an insular area of the United States located 40 miles (64 km) east of Puerto Rico. The islands are geographically part of the Virgin Islands archipelago and are located in the Leeward Islands of the Lesser Antilles.",where are the us virgin islands on a map
what is the definition of a destination wedding,"['http://villainjamaica.com/events_destination-weddings.php', 'https://www.hobotraveler.com/wedding-and-honeymoon-travel/index.php', 'http://blog.magicholidays.info/2013/11/match-made-in-heavan-married-in-paradise.html', 'https://www.romanticbug.com/destination-weddings', 'https://www.weddingphotographerinchicago.com/destination-weddings-locations.html']","Not to be confused with an elopement, a destination wedding is one in which a wedding is hosted, often in a vacation-like setting, at a location to which most of the invited guests must travel and often stay for several days. This could be a beach ceremony in the tropics, a lavish event in a metropolitan resort, or a simple ceremony at the home of a geographically distant friend or relative. During the recession of 2009, destination weddings continued to see growth compared to traditional weddings, as the typically smaller size results in lower costs.",what is the definition of a destination wedding
when do new episodes of luke cage come out,"['https://www.upi.com/Entertainment_News/TV/2017/07/01/Olivia-de-Havilland-sues-FX-over-Feud-portrayal/8191498939534/', 'http://beingawordsmith.com/2017/08/why-you-must-watch-these-4-returning-fall-2017-tv-shows.html', 'https://renewcanceltv.com/ncis-los-angeles-season-10-premiere-on-cbs/', 'https://www.imdb.com/name/nm2377903/news', 'https://24celebs.com/celebrity/59223-peter-dinklage.html', 'https://www.simplemost.com/the-longest-running-tv-shows-that-are-still-on-the-air/', 'http://howtovideo.info/tag/game-of-thrones']",The season is set to premiere in 2018.,when do new episodes of luke cage come out
why does the tail of a comet always face away from the sun,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Comets', 'https://www.universetoday.com/40778/interesting-facts-about-comets/', 'http://www.newsflash.org/2004/02/si/si003060.htm', 'http://techsciencenews.com/directory/wp/c/Comet.htm', 'https://scrolls4all.org/feasts/feasts-of-the-lord/attonement/seven-seal-judgments/seven-trumpet-judgments/', 'https://peqezuleqopozib.agronumericus.com/a-study-of-comets-61410juf592.html', 'https://gravity.wikia.org/wiki/Comet']","In the outer Solar System, comets remain frozen and are extremely difficult or impossible to detect from Earth due to their small size. Statistical detections of inactive comet nuclei in the Kuiper belt have been reported from the Hubble Space Telescope observations, but these detections have been questioned, and have not yet been independently confirmed. As a comet approaches the inner Solar System, solar radiation causes the volatile materials within the comet to vaporize and stream out of the nucleus, carrying dust away with them. The streams of dust and gas thus released form a huge, extremely tenuous atmosphere around the comet called the coma, and the force exerted on the coma by the Sun's radiation pressure and solar wind cause an enormous tail to form, which points away from the Sun.",why does the tail of a comet always face away from the sun
where is angeles city located in the philippines,"['https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=pinoywoman.com&ads=1&title=Pinoy+woman&auto=Pinoy+woman&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Pinoy+woman&pagenum=4', 'https://www.torta-a-porta.com/economy-hotels-in-the-philippines/', 'https://nathscrap.be/39363-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%8F-%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%8F-%D1%83%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0-%D0%B2-%D0%9B%D0%BE%D1%81-%D0%90%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%B6%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%B5-pampanga-phillipines.html', 'http://drumcullengaa.tk/largest-casino-companies-in-us.html', 'http://mx.wowcity.com/guanajuato/', 'https://wn.com/Irapuato,_Guanajuato', 'https://www.britannica.com/place/Guanajuato-state-Mexico']","Angeles (Kapampangan: Lakanbalen ning Angeles; Filipino: Lungsod ng Angeles) is a highly urbanized city located geographically within the province of Pampanga in the Philippines. It is bordered by Mabalacat to the north; Mexico to the east; San Fernando to the southeast; Bacolor to the south; and Porac to the southwest and west. The city administers itself autonomously from Pampanga and, as of the 2015 census, it has a population of 411,634.",where is angeles city located in the philippines
when did harley davidson go to fuel injection,"['http://www.kuerpoactivo.com.ve/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-motorcycle-phone-mount.html', 'http://www.fapuv.org.ve/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-motorcycle-accessories.html', 'http://www.diariocatolico.com.ve/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-harley-davidson-parts.html', 'http://bad2credit2home2equity2loans.blogspot.com/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-harley-davidson.html', 'http://www.claroscuro.com.ve/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-motorcycle-insurance.html', 'http://www.consorciojusticia.org.ve/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-shoei-motorcycle.html', 'http://www.deportivoanzoategui.com.ve/2018/08/motorcycle-bike-harley-davidson-touring.html']","Starting in 1995, the company introduced Electronic Fuel Injection (EFI) as an option for the 30th anniversary edition Electra Glide. EFI became standard on all Harley-Davidson motorcycles, including Sportsters, upon the introduction of the 2007 product line.",when did harley davidson go to fuel injection
how many times has the miami dolphins won the super bowl,"['http://live-nfl.net/teams/miami-dolphins/', 'https://www.tix2games.com/nfl/miami-dolphins-tickets.html', 'https://fanmail.com/professional/team/miami_dolphins/football', 'http://tickets11.com/football/miami-dolphins-tickets.html', 'http://americafootballclub.com/?fp=XWcWcsrtn%2FIzG%2F6g%2B9Br7Uo7rrCjTtKwKQrfvg9HQE8%2Fq8sbnLbo8A8olsHJFUSatF%2F1i05Kp3KmqexhB%2Bat5Q%3D%3D&prvtof=u8tBiYdkgsANOOg%2BX7cAPBsTsMN56Xy6fAWjdktV9E4%3D&poru=JQhhD3hTDiOItebblPGjMQwAL3JNDVAP3fAkrdENKiaFN5Ywn6NZBuYY7OplrHDzk9RGEg%2FHgt0fLTauEzuH1w%3D%3D', 'http://www.mobilestec.com/miami-dolphins/', 'https://stock-markets-picks.info/nike-buffalo-bills-youth-royal-circuit-pullover-performance-hoodie.aspx']","The team made its first Super Bowl appearance in Super Bowl VI, but lost to the Dallas Cowboys, 24 -- 3. The following year, the Dolphins completed the NFL's only perfect season culminating in a Super Bowl win, winning all 14 of their regular-season games, both of their NFL playoff games, and also Super Bowl VII. The 1972 Dolphins were the third NFL team to accomplish a perfect regular season, and won Super Bowl VIII, becoming the first team to appear in three consecutive Super Bowls, and the second team (the first AFL / AFC team) to win back-to-back championships. Miami also appeared in Super Bowl XVII and Super Bowl XIX, losing both games.",how many times has the miami dolphins won the super bowl
who sang the parts in beauty and the beast 2017,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Beauty_and_the_Beast_(Disney_song)', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Sing:_Original_Motion_Picture_Soundtrack', 'http://thisdayindisneyhistory.homestead.com/Mar10.html', 'http://online-tvchannel.org/watch-beauty-and-the-beast-full-movies-online-free-2017/', 'http://news.comicui.com/movies/beauty-beast-official-trailer-3-2017/', 'http://www.beaufortonline.com/beauty-and-the-beast/', 'http://instantmovie.us/beauty-and-the-beast-2017-720p-1080p/']","The album, largely based on material from Disney's previous animated version, features songs and instrumental score composed by Alan Menken with lyrics by Howard Ashman and three new songs composed by Alan Menken with lyrics by Tim Rice. The songs feature vocal performances by the film's ensemble cast including Emma Watson, Dan Stevens, Luke Evans, Kevin Kline, Josh Gad, Ewan McGregor, Stanley Tucci, Audra McDonald, Gugu Mbatha-Raw, Nathan Mack, Ian McKellen, and Emma Thompson.",who sang the parts in beauty and the beast 2017
how many vietnam era veterans are still alive,['http://maartens.home.xs4all.nl/log/2017/NL170916a.html'],"In 2004, the US Census Bureau reported there were 8.2 million Vietnam era veterans who were living in the U.S., 2.59 million of them being reported to have actually served ""in country.""",how many vietnam era veterans are still alive
where was east india company established in india,"['http://met52ec.com/Expansion.html', 'http://www.historyhome.co.uk/c-eight/india/india.htm', 'http://londoni.co/index.php/history/40-history-of-bangladesh/1757-polashi/586-polashi-juddho-battle-of-plassey-1757-1947-mughal-vs-english-rivalry-maritime-importance-of-west-bengal-mughal-vs-french-british-vs-french-history-of-bangladesh', 'https://www.theeastindiacompany.com/the-east-india-company/timeline/', 'https://www.360cities.net/image/stthomas-cathedral-veer-nariman-road-fort-mumbai-india-humayunn-peerzaada?set=996', 'https://mumbaimaja.wordpress.com/category/religious/', 'http://www.simonsholidays.com/india-satya-sai-baba-puttaparthi-tour/']","The company, which benefited from the imperial patronage, soon expanded its commercial trading operations. It eclipsed the Portuguese Estado da Índia, which had established bases in Goa, Chittagong, and Bombay, which Portugal later ceded to England as part of the dowry of Catherine of Braganza on her marriage to King Charles II. The East India Company also launched a joint attack with the Dutch United East India Company (VOC) on Portuguese and Spanish ships off the coast of China, which helped secure EIC ports in China. The company established trading posts in Surat (1619), Madras (1639), Bombay (1668), and Calcutta (1690). By 1647, the company had 23 factories, each under the command of a factor or master merchant and governor, and 90 employees in India. The major factories became the walled forts of Fort William in Bengal, Fort St George in Madras, and Bombay Castle.",where was east india company established in india
how many countries does the us have diplomatic relations with,"['https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/countries-with-whom-the-us-has-no-diplomatic-relations.html', 'https://home.heinonline.org/blog/exploring-heinonline/page/2/', 'http://www.iorj.org/article/preview/22', 'https://www.middletownpress.com/opinion/article/Chris-Powell-Islamic-marketing-vs-human-nature-11782156.php', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Elective_monarchy', 'https://www.militarytimes.com/flashpoints/2018/03/09/trump-to-meet-north-korea-leader-kim-jong-un-by-may-south-korea-official-says/', 'https://ssi.armywarcollege.edu/pubs/display.cfm?pubID=1195']","The United States has formal diplomatic relations with most nations. This includes all U.N. member states except for Bhutan, Iran, North Korea, and Syria. Additionally, the U.S. has diplomatic relations with the European Union, the Holy See and Kosovo. The United States federal statutes relating to foreign relations can be found in Title 22 of the United States Code.",how many countries does the us have diplomatic relations with
when was in god we trust placed on us currency,"['http://labprolib.com/money-history-of-in-god-we-trust-no-it-wasnt-always-on-our-money/', 'https://fox13now.com/2016/03/21/gov-herbert-signs-in-god-we-trust-license-plate-bill/', 'https://cpcfoundation.com/religious/in-god-we-trust/', 'https://www.philadelphiafed.org/education/teachers/publications/symbols-on-american-money', 'https://www.globalresearch.ca/how-secular-is-the-west-the-u-s-britain-australia-secular-nation-states-so-help-me-god/5633185', 'https://patriotdepot.com/in-god-we-trust-tank-top/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Three-cent_nickel']","""In God We Trust"" first appeared on the Two-cent piece in 1864 and has appeared on paper currency since 1957. A law passed in a Joint Resolution by the 84th Congress (P.L. 84-140) and approved by President Dwight Eisenhower on July 30, 1956, declared ""In God We Trust"" must appear on American currency. This phrase was first used on paper money in 1957, when it appeared on the one-dollar silver certificate. The first paper currency bearing the phrase entered circulation on October 1, 1957. The 84th Congress later passed legislation (P.L. 84-851), also signed by President Eisenhower on July 30, 1956, declaring the phrase to be the national motto.",when was in god we trust placed on us currency
describe the spot welding process using a gmaw welder,"['http://www.orangememoriescarehome.com/2016-Jun-28/automatic-lid-screen-printer-for-sale.html', 'http://www.technocratplasma.com/arc-welding-machine.php', 'https://compare-bear.com/hobart-handler-140-mig-welder-115v-review/', 'http://metal-monster.com/MIG.html', 'http://www.keepsake.in/keepsake-services/welding-technologies/mig-tig/', 'http://www.norcalwelding.com/resources/welding-processes/', 'https://www.helandermetal.com/aerospace-welding']","Along with the wire electrode, a shielding gas feeds through the welding gun, which shields the process from contaminants in the air. The process can be semi-automatic or automatic. A constant voltage, direct current power source is most commonly used with GMAW, but constant current systems, as well as alternating current, can be used. There are four primary methods of metal transfer in GMAW, called globular, short-circuiting, spray, and pulsed-spray, each of which has distinct properties and corresponding advantages and limitations.",describe the spot welding process using a gmaw welder
when did the easter bunny come to be,"['https://fortheloveofsebastian.com/', 'https://myragreenjournalism.weebly.com/happy-easter-edition-2013.html', 'https://www.foodnwine.in/2018/04/01/easter-j-w-marriott/', 'https://paintlikeme.com/952', 'http://myblog.allthingsdigitalmarketing.com/2014/04/happy-2014th-easter-world-sunday-april.html', 'http://www.thesweetbunnyproject.org/easter.html', 'https://www.idolbin.com/interests?location=canada']","The Easter Bunny (also called the Easter Rabbit or Easter Hare) is a folkloric figure and symbol of Easter, depicted as a rabbit bringing Easter eggs. Originating among German Lutherans, the ""Easter Hare"" originally played the role of a judge, evaluating whether children were good or disobedient in behavior at the start of the season of Eastertide. The Easter Bunny is sometimes depicted with clothes. In legend, the creature carries colored eggs in his basket, candy, and sometimes also toys to the homes of children, and as such shows similarities to Santa Claus or the Christkind, as they both bring gifts to children on the night before their respective holidays. The custom was first mentioned in Georg Franck von Franckenau's De ovis paschalibus (' About Easter Eggs') in 1682, referring to a German tradition of an Easter Hare bringing Easter eggs for the children.",when did the easter bunny come to be
where is japan located on the world map,"['https://www.buttondown.tv/travel/hokkaido-calling-sherpas-cinema/', 'https://anstona.com/destinations/japan/', 'https://www.happymatches.com/jp/seeking-arrangement', 'https://winterwolficewind.blog/2016/11/28/japan-%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%AC-nippon-or-nihon-formally-%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%AC%E5%9B%BD-nippon-koku-or-nihon-koku-state-of-japan/', 'https://www.zchocolat.com/shop/en/international-gift-delivery/japan', 'https://www.ptpi.eu/japan/', 'https://travelo.club/en/guide/country/JP-japan']","Japan (Japanese: 日本; Nippon (ɲippoɴ) or Nihon (ɲihoɴ); formally 日本 国 Nippon-koku or Nihon-koku, lit. ""State of Japan"") is a sovereign island country in East Asia. Located in the Pacific Ocean, it lies off the eastern coast of the Asian mainland and stretches from the Sea of Okhotsk in the north to the East China Sea and China in the southwest. Coordinates: 35 ° N 136 ° E ﻿ / ﻿ 35 ° N 136 ° E ﻿ / 35; 136 The kanji that make up Japan's name mean ""sun origin"", and it is often called the ""Land of the Rising Sun"". Japan is a stratovolcanic archipelago consisting of about 6,852 islands. The four largest are Honshu, Hokkaido, Kyushu, and Shikoku, which make up about ninety-seven percent of Japan's land area and often are referred to as home islands. The country is divided into 47 prefectures in eight regions, with Hokkaido being the northernmost prefecture and Okinawa being the southernmost one. The population of 127 million is the world's tenth largest. Japanese people make up 98.5% of Japan's total population. About 9.1 million people live in Tokyo, the capital of Japan.",where is japan located on the world map
domestic and foreign tourists visiting india (statistical data),"['http://inter-corp.org/expertise/?pic=clientcoverage:-6', 'https://sitatourandtravels.com/Home/AboutUs', 'https://usefulresearchpapers.com/research-paper-on-tourism-in-india/', 'https://www.udaipuronline.in/city-guide/udaipur-tourism', 'https://www.india-tours.com/packages/golden-triangle-trip-with-varanasi.html', 'http://www.walkthroughindia.com/offbeat/10-international-female-travelers-exploring-incredible-india/', 'https://www.solvibrations.org/bangalore-the-impeccable-holiday-destination-in-south-india/']","About 88.90 lakh (8.89 million) foreign tourists arrived in India in 2016 compared to 80.27 lakh (8.027 million) in 2015, recording a growth of 10.7%. Domestic tourist visits to all states and Union Territories numbered 1,036.35 million in 2012, an increase of 16.5% from 2011. In 2014, Tamil Nadu, Maharashtra and Uttar Pradesh were the most popular states for tourists. Delhi, Mumbai, Chennai, Agra and Jaipur have been the five most visited cities of India by foreign tourists during the year 2015. Worldwide, Delhi is ranked at 28 by the number of foreign tourist arrivals, while Mumbai is ranked at 30, Chennai at 43, Agra at 45, Jaipur at 52 and Kolkata at 90.",domestic and foreign tourists visiting india (statistical data)
why are forests in alaska and the pacific northwest called old-growth forests,"['https://parks.ny.gov/parks/11/getting-there.aspx', 'http://artolook.com/Ancient_woodland.html', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Old-growth_forest', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/Lumber', 'https://de.tipeee.com/volod-hendrix', 'https://nusapenida.org/destination/nusa-penida/temeling/', 'http://australianprinter.realviewdigital.com/?iid=84159&startpage=page0000060']","An old-growth forest -- also termed primary forest, virgin forest, primeval forest, or late seral forest -- is a forest that has attained great age without significant disturbance and thereby exhibits unique ecological features and might be classified as a climax community. Old-growth features include diverse tree-related structures that provide diverse wildlife habitat that increases the biodiversity of the forested ecosystem. The concept of diverse tree structure includes multi-layered canopies and canopy gaps, greatly varying tree heights and diameters, and diverse tree species and classes and sizes of woody debris.",why are forests in alaska and the pacific northwest called old-growth forests
who was the state of washington named after,"['https://advowastemedical.com/washington-medical-waste-disposal', 'https://yque.com/wainviawi.html', 'https://washingtonshipping.com/', 'http://www.jerrys-trivia-corner.com/washington/', 'https://xn--j1ahfl.xn--p1ai/library/cultural_studies__in_teaching_english_184547.html', 'http://www.downloadpsdtemplates.com/washington-drivers-license-psd/', 'http://sports-entertainment-law-report.careers.org/education/colleges/138284?city=chipley&amp;name=florida-panhandle-technical-college&amp;state_or_country_name=florida']","Washington (/ ˈwɒʃɪŋtən / (listen)), officially the State of Washington, is a state in the Pacific Northwest region of the United States. Named after George Washington, the first president of the United States, the state was made out of the western part of the Washington Territory, which was ceded by Britain in 1846 in accordance with the Oregon Treaty in the settlement of the Oregon boundary dispute. It was admitted to the Union as the 42nd state in 1889. Olympia is the state capital. Washington is sometimes referred to as Washington State, to distinguish it from Washington, D.C., the capital of the United States, which is often shortened to Washington.",who was the state of washington named after
who invented the first version of photoshop and what was it known as,"['https://mandarapte.com/artanddesign/adobe-photoshop-it/', 'http://forum.daffodilvarsity.edu.bd/index.php/topic,2376.0.html', 'http://www.under5cents.com/2012/04/history-of-adobe-photoshop.html', 'http://techvideos.humourbox.info/2007/11/photoshop-tutorial-face-shaping.html', 'http://www.texnoworship.com.ar/2015/02/adobe-photoshop-celebrates-25/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/File:Polygala_elongata_in_Talakona,_AP_I_IMG_8388.jpg', 'http://www.gkbgraphics.com/?page_id=433']","Photoshop was developed in 1987 by the American brothers Thomas and John Knoll, who sold the distribution license to Adobe Systems Incorporated in 1988. Thomas Knoll, a PhD student at the University of Michigan, began writing a program on his Macintosh Plus to display grayscale images on a monochrome display. This program, called Display, caught the attention of his brother John Knoll, an Industrial Light & Magic employee, who recommended that Thomas turn it into a full-fledged image editing program. Thomas took a six-month break from his studies in 1988 to collaborate with his brother on the program. Thomas renamed the program ImagePro, but the name was already taken. Later that year, Thomas renamed his program Photoshop and worked out a short-term deal with scanner manufacturer Barneyscan to distribute copies of the program with a slide scanner; a ""total of about 200 copies of Photoshop were shipped"" this way.",who invented the first version of photoshop and what was it known as
when did the shang dynasty begin and end,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Shang_dynasty', 'http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Shang_dynasty', 'https://thesomathread.com/2016/09/11/ancient-china-egyptian-connection/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Shang_dynasty.html', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/2100BC/xia-dynasty-of-china', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Xia_dynasty.html', 'https://www.acupuncture-tuina-courses.co.uk/taoism/']","The Shang dynasty (/ ʃɑːŋ /; Chinese: 商 朝; pinyin: Shāng cháo) or Yin dynasty (/ jɪn /; 殷 代; Yīn dài), according to traditional historiography, ruled in the Yellow River valley in the second millennium BC, succeeding the Xia dynasty and followed by the Zhou dynasty. The classic account of the Shang comes from texts such as the Book of Documents, Bamboo Annals and Records of the Grand Historian. According to the traditional chronology based on calculations made approximately 2,000 years ago by Liu Xin, the Shang ruled from 1766 to 1122 BC, but according to the chronology based upon the ""current text"" of Bamboo Annals, they ruled from 1556 to 1046 BC. The Xia -- Shang -- Zhou Chronology Project dated them from c. 1600 to 1046 BC.",when did the shang dynasty begin and end
what does the g in freemasonry stand for,"['http://sedgh.ir/en/galamestan/1347', 'https://diversityflags.com/de-li/1029/freemason-flag', 'https://pokchilau.format.com/2488608-cuban-chinese-freemasons-book', 'https://themasonslady.com/2014/07/28/navigating-masonic-emblems-part-i/', 'http://m.lifeng-gift.com/masonic-items/masonic-keychain/masonic-master-compass-and-square-without-g.html']","In many English speaking countries, the Square and Compasses are depicted with the letter ""G"" in the center. The letter has multiple meanings, representing different words depending on the context in which it is discussed. The most common is that the ""G"" stands for Geometry, and is to remind Masons that Geometry and Freemasonry are synonymous terms described as being the ""noblest of sciences"", and ""the basis upon which the superstructure of Freemasonry, and everything in existence in the entire universe is erected. In this context it can also stand for Great Architect of the Universe (a non-denominational reference to God).""",what does the g in freemasonry stand for
how many countries are in the indian subcontinent,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Indian_subcontinent', 'http://lcgeography.preswex.ie/subcontinental-region-india.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Indian_Subcontinent.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Indian_subcontinent', 'http://indiaaura.com/', 'http://www.soarexcursions.com/travel-with-us/wildlife-and-nature/', 'http://www.factbites.com/topics/Karakorum']","The Indian subcontinent or the subcontinent, also called the Indian continent, is a southern region of Asia, mostly situated on the Indian Plate and projecting southwards into the Indian Ocean from the Himalayas. Geologically, the Indian subcontinent is related to the land mass that rifted from Gondwana and merged with the Eurasian plate nearly 55 million years ago. Geographically, it is the peninsular region in south-central Asia delineated by the Himalayas in the north, the Hindu Kush in the west, and the Arakanese in the east. Politically, the Indian subcontinent usually includes Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Maldives, Nepal, Pakistan and Sri Lanka.",how many countries are in the indian subcontinent
what type of party is lady windemere planning,"['https://seamusdubhghaill.com/2017/02/', 'http://www.currency.com.au/browse/comedy/lady-windermeres-fan/', 'https://polyuenglishdramaclub.weebly.com/performances.html', 'https://www.redlandsdailyfacts.com/2015/04/02/riverside-international-film-festival-includes-movie-filmed-at-edwards-mansion-in-redlands/', 'http://villanovaplayers.com/past_plays/Lady_Windermeres_Fan/index.html']","The story concerns Lady Windermere, who suspects that her husband is having an affair with another woman. She confronts him with it but although he denies it, he invites the other woman, Mrs Erlynne, to his wife's birthday ball. Angered by her husband's supposed unfaithfulness, Lady Windermere decides to leave her husband for another lover. After discovering what has transpired, Mrs Erlynne follows Lady Windermere and attempts to persuade her to return to her husband and in the course of this, Mrs Erlynne is discovered in a compromising position. It is then revealed Mrs Erlynne is Lady Windermere's mother, who abandoned her family twenty years before the time the play is set. Mrs Erlynne sacrifices herself and her reputation to save her daughter's marriage. The best-known line of the play sums up the central theme:",what type of party is lady windemere planning
what are the 4 most spoken branches of indo-europan family,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Indo-European.html', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Indo-European_languages', 'https://www.universal-translation-services.com/indo-european-languages/', 'https://homeland.sites.ku.dk/2018/06/', 'https://4chanint.fandom.com/wiki/Indo-European_languages', 'https://wiki.thingsandstuff.org/Language', 'https://hyperleap.com/topic/English_language']","There are about 445 living Indo-European languages, according to the estimate by Ethnologue, with over two thirds (313) of them belonging to the Indo-Iranian branch. The most widely spoken Indo-European languages by native speakers are Spanish, English, Hindustani (Hindi-Urdu), Portuguese, Bengali, Punjabi, Russian, each with over 100 million speakers, with German, French, and Persian also having significant numbers. Today, about 46% of the human population speaks an Indo-European language as a first language, by far the highest of any language family.","Indo-European languages Indo-European languages This article is about the family of languages found in much of Europe and Asia. For other uses, see Indo-European (disambiguation). Indo-EuropeanGeographicdistribution: Before the 16th century: Europe, West, Central, and South Asia; today: worldwideLinguistic classification: One of the world's primary language familiesProto-language: Proto-Indo-EuropeanSubdivisions: Albanian Anatolian (extinct) Armenian Balto-Slavic (Baltic and Slavic) Celtic Germanic Hellenic Indo-Iranian (Indo-Aryan, Iranian, and Nuristani) Italic (including Romance) Tocharian (extinct)ISO 639-2 / 5: ineGlottolog: indo1319[1] Present-day native distribution of Indo-European languages, within their homeland of Eurasia: Albanian Armenian Balto-Slavic (Baltic) Balto-Slavic (Slavic) Celtic Germanic Hellenic (Greek) Indo-Iranian (Indo-Aryan, Iranian, and Nuristani) Italic (Romance) Non-Indo-European languages Dotted/striped areas i