what was significant in the allied victory at the first battle of the marne,"['http://www.livingwarbirds.com/first-battle-of-the-marne.php', 'http://williballenthin.com/significance-of-the-second-battle-of-the-marne.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/First_Battle_of_the_Marne', 'https://csosoundsandstories.org/a-time-for-reflection-a-message-of-peace-the-great-war/', 'https://beartotheright.com/2018/12/09/candidates-for-chairman-of-the-california-republican-party-part-1-david-hadley/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'https://educheer.com/essays/allied-powers-war-germany-nation/', 'https://www.gettysburgflag.com/history-of-american-wars']","The battle of the Marne was a major turning point of World War I. By the end of August 1914, the whole Allied army on the Western Front had been forced into a general retreat back towards Paris. Meanwhile, the two main German armies continued through France. It seemed that Paris would be taken as both the French and the British fell back towards the Marne River. The war became a stalemate when the Allied Powers won the Battle of the Marne. It was the first major clash on the Western Front and one of the most important single events in the entire war. The German retreat left the Schlieffen Plan in ruins and Germany had no hope of a quick victory in France. Its army was left to fight a long war on two fronts.",what was significant in the allied victory at the first battle of the marne
when did the greek empire rise and fall,"['https://www.procaffenation.com/the-history-of-the-ancient-city-of-greece/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Play_(theatre)', 'https://www.touristorama.com/en/greece-travel-videos/?pl=PL70D434A8B2BCFF8D', 'https://innermegapower.com/home/history-of-ancient-greeks-and-myths-mythology-greek-alphabet/', 'http://www.cwvacations.ca/our-tours/', 'https://hellasart.gr/ancient-greece/', 'https://kidskonnect.com/history/ancient-greece/']","Ancient Greece was a civilization belonging to a period of Greek history from the Greek Dark Ages of the 13th -- 9th centuries BC to the end of antiquity (c. 600 AD). Immediately following this period was the beginning of the Early Middle Ages and the Byzantine era. Roughly three centuries after the Late Bronze Age collapse of Mycenaean Greece, Greek urban poleis began to form in the 8th century BC, ushering in the period of Archaic Greece and colonization of the Mediterranean Basin. This was followed by the period of Classical Greece, an era that began with the Greco-Persian Wars, lasting from the 5th to 4th centuries BC. Due to the conquests by Alexander the Great of Macedonia, Hellenistic civilization flourished from Central Asia to the western end of the Mediterranean Sea. The Hellenistic period came to an end with the conquests and annexations of the eastern Mediterranean world by the Roman Republic, which established the Roman province of Macedonia in Roman Greece, and later the province of Achaea during the Roman Empire.",when did the greek empire rise and fall
where is bangkok located on the world map,"['https://andrewharvardphotography.com/2016/02/05/bangkok/', 'https://akholidaysnepal.com/tour/bangkok/', 'http://bestplacesonearth.net/beautiful-planet/bangkok-thailand/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'https://www.turipo.com/views/tripPage.php?trip_id=248', 'http://holidayinvietnam.com/thailand/bangkok', 'https://clipstogo.at/asia/thailand/bangkok/', 'https://www.batikdlidir.com/batik-fabric-bangkok-thailand/']","Bangkok (UK: / bæŋˈkɒk /, US: / ˈbæŋkɒk /) is the capital and most populous city of Thailand. It is known in Thai as Krung Thep Maha Nakhon (กรุงเทพมหานคร, pronounced (krūŋ thêːp mahǎː nákhɔ̄ːn) (listen)) or simply Krung Thep (listen (help info)). The city occupies 1,568.7 square kilometres (605.7 sq mi) in the Chao Phraya River delta in Central Thailand, and has a population of over 8 million, or 12.6 percent of the country's population. Over 14 million people (22.2 percent) lived within the surrounding Bangkok Metropolitan Region at the 2010 census, making Bangkok an extreme primate city, significantly dwarfing Thailand's other urban centres in terms of importance.",where is bangkok located on the world map
how many teams in la liga qualify for champions league,"['http://startonlinegamesqq288.com/the-spanish-national-football-league/', 'https://www.bettingsites.bet/betting-guides/football-betting/dutch-eredivisie-betting/', 'https://www.bettingsites.bet/betting-guides/football-betting/english-premier-league-betting/', 'http://lingfluent.eu/your-1x2-betting-predictions.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/CD_Numancia', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/La_Liga', 'https://www.soccertipsters.net/spanish-la-liga']","The top teams in La Liga qualify for the UEFA Champions League. The first, second, third and fourth placed teams directly enter the group stage of UEFA Champions League. Teams placed fifth and sixth play in the UEFA Europa League, along with the cup winners. If the cup winners finish in the top six, an additional berth in the Europa League is given to the team that finishes in seventh.",how many teams in la liga qualify for champions league
what is the speed of the sound in air,"['http://phoenixfoundationpodcast.com/s4e19-unfinished-business/', 'https://bigdreamproducer.com/what-is-sound/', 'http://neoqqd.com/Speed_of_sound.html', 'https://www.cornelladelterri.org/sound-travels-best-through-what-medium/', 'https://blog.adafruit.com/2017/07/17/how-fast-is-mach-1/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171026007-physics', 'https://libertysflame.com/cgi-bin/readart.cgi?ArtNum=53025&Disp=35']","The speed of sound is the distance travelled per unit time by a sound wave as it propagates through an elastic medium. In dry air at 0 ° C (32 ° F), the speed of sound is 331.2 metres per second (1,087 ft / s; 1,192 km / h; 741 mph; 644 kn). At 20 ° C (68 ° F), the speed of sound is 343 metres per second (1,125 ft / s; 1,235 km / h; 767 mph; 667 kn), or a kilometre in 2.91 s or a mile in 4.69 s.",what is the speed of the sound in air
how many pirates of the caribbeans movies are there,"['http://wineaccess.ca/pirates-of-the-caribbean-all-parts-in-hindi.html', 'https://wn.com/Pirates_of_the_Caribbean_(film_series)', 'https://torrentsdownloadfree.com/fantasy/pirates-of-the-caribbean-6-free-torrent.html', 'http://mcp-media.s3.amazonaws.com/the-pirates-of-the-caribbean-torrent.html', 'https://katmoviehd.eu/pirates-of-the-caribbean-collection/', 'http://lemoigne-baptiste.info/?newsid=46059', 'https://lovelytab.com/post/pirates-of-the-caribbean-theme-new-tab/']","Directors of the series include Gore Verbinski (1 -- 3), Rob Marshall (4) and Joachim Rønning and Espen Sandberg (5). The series is primarily written by Ted Elliott and Terry Rossio (1 -- 4); other writers include Stuart Beattie (1), Jay Wolpert (1) and Jeff Nathanson (5). The stories follow the adventures of Captain Jack Sparrow (Johnny Depp), Will Turner (Orlando Bloom) and Elizabeth Swann (Keira Knightley). Characters such as Hector Barbossa (Geoffrey Rush) and Joshamee Gibbs (Kevin McNally) follow Jack, Will and Elizabeth in the course of the films. The fourth film features Blackbeard (Ian McShane) and Angelica (Penélope Cruz), while the fifth film features Armando Salazar (Javier Bardem), Henry Turner (Brenton Thwaites) and Carina Smyth (Kaya Scodelario). The films take place in a fictional historical setting; a world ruled by the British Empire, the East India Trading Company (based on the real East India Company) and the Spanish Empire, with pirates representing freedom from the ruling powers.",how many pirates of the caribbeans movies are there
who aided america in the struggle for independence,"['http://helvegr.com/2015/09/25/american-revolution-in-7-languages-a-wiki-study/', 'http://estrelitzia.eu/64146-american-revolution-battle-of-religion-and-politics/', 'http://mumbles.co.uk/american-revolution-collage.html', 'https://www.findtutorsnearme.com/ged-social-studies-test/', 'https://4travellingacrosstime.com/2016/10/02/american-revolutionary-war/', 'https://www.geographicus.com/P/AntiqueMap/theatredelageurre-briondelatour-1777', 'https://ohiopix.org/contentdm-search-results/?cdm-keywords=American%20Indian%20history&cdm-mode=all&cdm-field=subjec']","Tensions erupted into battle between Patriot militia and British regulars when the king's army attempted to capture and destroy Colonial military supplies at Lexington and Concord on April 19, 1775. The conflict then developed into a global war, during which the Patriots (and later their French, Spanish, and Dutch allies) fought the British and Loyalists in what became known as the American Revolutionary War (1775 -- 83). Each of the thirteen colonies formed a Provincial Congress that assumed power from the old colonial governments and suppressed Loyalism, and from there they built a Continental Army under the leadership of General George Washington. The Continental Congress determined King George's rule to be tyrannical and infringing the colonists' rights as Englishmen, and they declared the colonies free and independent states on July 2, 1776. The Patriot leadership professed the political philosophies of liberalism and republicanism to reject monarchy and aristocracy, and they proclaimed that all men are created equal.",who aided america in the struggle for independence
what is a deadlock lock on a door,"['http://www.blumsoft.eu/InternalDoor/internal-door-bolts', 'http://www.locksmithparkslope.org/mortise-cylinders-v-s-rim-cylinders/', 'https://lockandkey-houstonlocksmith.com/change-lock/', 'http://www.cfvrma.com/author/niccole/page/13/', 'https://locksandsafesonline.com/locks/deadbolts/pdq-deadbolts/', 'https://www.aaalocksmiths.co.za/locksmith-services/deadlocks-deadbolts/', 'http://wwebb.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=25438']","A dead bolt, deadbolt or dead lock is a locking mechanism distinct from a spring bolt lock because a deadbolt cannot be moved to the open position except by rotating the key. The more common spring bolt lock uses a spring to hold the bolt in place, allowing retraction by applying force to the bolt itself. A deadbolt can therefore make a door more resistant to entry without the correct key.",what is a deadlock lock on a door
what is now the european union began as which organization,"['http://www.fouman.com/Y/Wiki.php?eterm=EU', 'http://brsp.org.pk/donor_partner/european_union', 'https://alchetron.com/European-Union', 'http://www.assignmentpoint.com/business/report-on-world-trade-organization.html', 'https://eurboghana.eu/ebo/europe/', 'https://zeitgeist77.wordpress.com/category/my-note/wiki-doc/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/.eu']","The EU and European citizenship were established when the Maastricht Treaty was enacted in 1993. The EU traces its origins to the European Coal and Steel Community (ECSC) and the European Economic Community (EEC), established, respectively, by the 1951 Treaty of Paris and 1957 Treaty of Rome. The original members of what came to be known as the European Communities were the Inner Six: Belgium, France, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, and West Germany. The Communities and its successors have grown in size by the accession of new member states and in power by the addition of policy areas to its remit. The latest major amendment to the constitutional basis of the EU, the Treaty of Lisbon, came into force in 2009. While no member state has left the EU or its predecessors, the United Kingdom signified an intention to leave after a membership referendum in June 2016 and is negotiating its withdrawal.",what is now the european union began as which organization
what is a sacrament according to the catholic church,"['https://www.cathedralokc.org/sacraments/', 'http://iaskgod.com/blogs/iaskgod?page=13', 'http://wyattgraham.com/christ-will-build-his-church-but-which-church-is-his/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Penance', 'https://stisaac.org/', 'http://www.stjamesbelvidere.org/parish-life/sacramental-preparation/', 'https://www.hrsrchurch.org/journey_of_faith/archive_-_journey_of_faith__uscca___cst_/journey_of_faith_archive_2017/12-31-2017_the_celebration_of_the_paschal_mystery_']","There are seven sacraments of the Catholic Church, which according to Catholic theology were instituted by Jesus and entrusted to the Church. Sacraments are visible rites seen as signs and efficacious channels of the grace of God to all those who receive them with the proper disposition. The sevenfold list of sacraments is often organized into three groups: the sacraments of initiation (into the Church, the body of Christ), consisting of Baptism, Confirmation, and the Eucharist; the sacraments of healing, consisting of Penance and Anointing of the Sick; and the sacraments of service: Holy Orders and Matrimony.",what is a sacrament according to the catholic church
what side was spain on in the revolutionary war,"['https://dlwd.info/pardo-secretary-desk.htm', 'https://www.klixmag.com/events-calendar/?category=Family+Fun', 'http://webot.org/info/en/?search=Spain_in_the_American_Revolutionary_War', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Siege_of_Pensacola']","Spain's role in the independence of the United States was part of its dispute over colonial supremacy with the Kingdom of Great Britain. Spain declared war on Britain as an ally of France, and provided supplies and munitions to the American forces.",what side was spain on in the revolutionary war
how many seasons of little witch academia are there,"['https://objectionnetwork.com/2017/09/27/michaela-and-jason-review-little-witch-academia/', 'http://raymondsaumure.com/productivity/little-witch-academia-2013.php', 'https://japan-hack.com/japanese-famous-anime-trend-yo-kai-watch/', 'http://webinetry.com/medical/little-witch-academia-2013.php', 'http://kidsrkidscastlerock.com/casino/little-witch-academia.php', 'https://www.11know-how.info/yvggyrjvgpunpnqrzvnargsyvkeryrnfrqngr509e4b07c9.pdf', 'http://sabretoothlifestyle.com/western-australia/little-witch-academia-art-book-pdf.php']","Little Witch Academia (リトル ウィッチ アカデミア, Ritoru Witchi Akademia) is a Japanese anime franchise created by Yoh Yoshinari and produced by Trigger. The original short film, directed by Yoshinari and written by Masahiko Otsuka, was released in theaters on March 2, 2013 as part of the Young Animator Training Project's Anime Mirai 2013 project, and was later streamed with English subtitles on YouTube from April 19, 2013. A second short film partially funded through Kickstarter, Little Witch Academia: The Enchanted Parade, was released on October 9, 2015. An anime television series aired in Japan between January and June 2017, with its first 13 episodes available on Netflix worldwide beginning on June 30, 2017. The remaining 12 episodes of its first season was labeled as the show's second season and was made available on the platform on August 15, 2017. Two manga series have been published by Shueisha.",how many seasons of little witch academia are there
the ability of congress to override a presidential veto,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Veto.html', 'https://www.aaacn.org/how-bill-becomes-law', 'https://www.peo.gov.au/learning/closer-look/parliament-and-congress/operation-of-the-legislature.html', 'https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/what-type-of-government-does-zambia-have.html', 'https://twelvekey.com/2015/12/', 'https://www.carper.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/how-a-bill-becomes-a-law', 'http://techsciencenews.com/directory/wp/u/United_States_Congress.htm']","If the Congress overrides the veto by a two-thirds vote in each house, it becomes law without the President's signature. Otherwise, the bill fails to become law unless it is presented to the President again and the President chooses to sign it. Historically, the Congress overrides the Presidential veto 7% of the time.",the ability of congress to override a presidential veto
where does the last name munoz come from,"['http://smartel.mobi/darko-lazic-izaberi-nekog-da-na-mene-lici-53/', 'http://ilovetacos.info/viewtopic.php?t=1541', 'http://advertising101.info/?page_id=2175', 'https://www.ask.com/web?q=Roy%20Bethell&amp;qo=pagination&amp;qsrc=998&amp;page=5', 'https://www.archives.com/genealogy/family-history-campos.html', 'http://indiansforchrist.org/what-remains-in-the-eye/', 'http://dgmweb.net/FGS/Car/CarricoPeterI-_.html']",Muñoz is a Spanish-language surname -- with a Portuguese-language variant (Munhoz). Notable people with the surname include:,where does the last name aguilar originate from
who made up the allied forces in ww2,"['https://comoxairforcemuseum.ca/remembrance-week-the-allies-of-world-war-ii/', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/allies-of-world-war-ii', 'http://www.okddayallies.co/history/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=alliedenterprises.com&ads=1&title=Allied+enterprises&auto=Allied+enterprises&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Allied+enterprises&pagenum=4', 'https://ourjourneypeterborough.org/?s=WWI', 'https://www.memorialatpeninsula.org/?p=7523', 'https://war.wikia.org/wiki/Pearl_Harbour']","At the start of the war on 1 September 1939, the Allies consisted of France, Poland and the United Kingdom, and dependent states, such as the British India. Within days they were joined by the independent Dominions of the British Commonwealth: Australia, Canada, New Zealand and South Africa. After the start of the German invasion of North Europe till the Balkan Campaign, the Netherlands, Belgium, Greece and Yugoslavia joined the Allies. After first having cooperated with Germany in invading Poland whilst remaining neutral in the Allied-Axis conflict, the Soviet Union perforce joined the Allies in June 1941 after being invaded by Germany. The United States provided war materiel and money all along, and officially joined in December 1941 after the Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor. China had already been in a prolonged war with Japan since the Lugou Bridge Incident of 1937, but officially joined the Allies in 1941.",what nations were members of the allied powers
why is the nose on the sphinx missing,"['https://disneytheory.com/2014/10/05/aladdin-is-set-in-a-distant-post-apocalyptic-future-and-other-theories/', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Pyramids_of_Giza', 'https://thundergodblog.com/tag/construction/', 'https://historum.com/threads/are-there-any-pre-islamic-statues-in-middle-east-which-were-spared-and-preserved-by-medieval-muslim-dynasties.176032/page-2', 'https://4815162342execute.wordpress.com/lost-themes/pyramids/', 'https://best-writing-service.net/essays/research/culture-and-civilization-of-the-ancient-egypt.html']","The Arab historian al-Maqrīzī, writing in the 15th century, attributes the loss of the nose to iconoclasm by Muhammad Sa'im al-Dahr -- a Sufi Muslim from the khanqah of Sa'id al-Su'ada -- in AD 1378, upon finding the local peasants making offerings to the Sphinx in the hope of increasing their harvest. Enraged, he destroyed the nose, and was later hanged for vandalism. Al-Maqrīzī describes the Sphinx as the ""talisman of the Nile"" on which the locals believed the flood cycle depended.",why is the nose on the sphinx missing
what is the work of cpu in mobile,"['http://vietnamcoffee.asia/acer-aspire-4920-wireless-lan-98/', 'https://mobileslatest.com/top-seven-powerful-mobile-processors/', 'http://leisure-studies-association.info/dv2315nr-72/', 'http://renkonkisuta.info/satellite-a205-s4607-92/', 'http://sabah.live/category/webcams/', 'http://worldsef.space/category/sound-cards/page/3/', 'http://january-pop.info/toshiba-a205-s4607-29/']","A CPU chip is designed for portable computers, it is typically housed in a smaller chip package, but more importantly, in order to run cooler, it uses lower voltages than its desktop counterpart and has more sleep mode capability. A mobile processor can be throttled down to different power levels or sections of the chip can be turned off entirely when not in use. Further, the clock frequency may be stepped down under low processor loads. This stepping down conserves power and prolongs battery life.",what is the work of cpu in mobile
how many season of once upon a time on netflix,"['http://www.soundtrackdreams.com/2018/09/soundtrack-review-once-upon-a-time-season-7-mark-isham-cindy-oconnor-and-michael-d-simon-2018/', 'http://wwebb.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=1576', 'http://vintagesilverplateflatware.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=41571', 'http://freeinfocontent.info/forum.php?mod=viewthread&tid=43089', 'http://alternative3.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=13505', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/tv-shows-have-it-all/', 'http://www.retrokimmer.com/2018/10/kimmers-top-5-favorite.html']","Once Upon a Time is an American fantasy drama television series on ABC which debuted on October 23, 2011, and concluded on May 18, 2018. The first six seasons are largely set in the fictitious seaside town of Storybrooke, Maine, with the character of Emma Swan serving as the lead, while the seventh and final season takes place in a Seattle, Washington neighborhood called Hyperion Heights, with a new main narrative led by Swan's son, Henry Mills. The show borrows elements and characters from the Disney franchise and popular Western literature, folklore, and fairy tales.",how many season of once upon a time on netflix
what was the japanese motivation for bombing pearl harbor,"['http://www.tomorrowsalliance.com/tadec2018magazine.html', 'http://thepandorasociety.com/december-7th-1941-attack-on-pearl-harbor/', 'https://historybytez.com/2015/12/07/1941-world-war-ii-attack-on-pearl-harbor/', 'https://americanhistoryusa.com/topic/attack-on-pearl-harbor/', 'https://www.shrine.org.au/Remembrance/ServicesCalendar/%7Bmonth%7D/%7Byear%7D/Archive', 'http://prophotospots.com/Pearl-Harbor-Tora-Tora-Reenactment-Prodview.html', 'https://www.americanfreedombybarbara.com/2018/12/remember-pearl-harbor-judged-in-tokyo.html']","Japan intended the attack as a preventive action to keep the U.S. Pacific Fleet from interfering with its planned military actions in Southeast Asia against overseas territories of the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, and the United States. Over the course of seven hours there were coordinated Japanese attacks on the U.S.-held Philippines, Guam and Wake Island and on the British Empire in Malaya, Singapore, and Hong Kong.",what was the japanese motivation for bombing pearl harbor
how has the biomedical model influenced health care delivery in the united states,"['https://www.wisegeek.com/what-is-the-biomedical-model.htm', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Therapeutic_garden', 'http://lemurianembassy.com/biomedical-model-of-health-definition.html', 'http://therapeutic-journeys.com/what-is-socio-medical-model.html', 'https://myassignmenthelp.com/free-samples/wider-social-determinants-of-health-and-health-inequalities']","The biomedical model of health focuses on purely biological factors and excludes psychological, environmental, and social influences. It is considered to be the leading modern way for health care professionals to diagnose and treat a condition in most Western countries.",how has the biomedical model influenced health care delivery in the united states
where is the handmaid's tale take place,"['http://plansport1000.online/sluts-in-rhyn/classic-vintage-lesbian.php', 'http://listtop10.com/the-handmaids-tale/']","The Handmaid's Tale is set in the Republic of Gilead, a theonomic military dictatorship formed within the borders of what was formerly the United States of America.",where is the handmaid's tale take place
where did the washington wizards get their name,"['https://sportsteamhistory.com/timeline/new-nickname-wizards', 'https://sportsteamhistory.com/washington-wizards', 'https://www.trusttreetrademarks.com/2015/10/28/bullets/', 'https://www.prohockeyrumors.com/players/dmitry-orlov']","A contest was held to choose a new name and the choices were narrowed to the Dragons, Express, Stallions, Sea Dogs, and the Wizards. On May 15, 1997, the Bullets officially became the Wizards. The new name generated some controversy because ""Wizard"" is a rank in the Ku Klux Klan, and Washington has a large African American population. A new logo was unveiled and the team colors were changed from the traditional red, white and blue to a lighter shade of blue, black and bronze, the same colors as the Washington Capitals of the National Hockey League (NHL), also owned by Pollin. That same year the Wizards moved to the then MCI Center, now called Capital One Arena, which is home to the Capitals, the Washington Mystics of the Women's National Basketball Association and the Georgetown Hoyas men's college basketball team.",where did the washington wizards get their name
why does tropical cyclone originated over the seas,"['https://www.thoughtco.com/tropical-storm-definition-3444240', 'https://trackthetropics.com/learn-about-hurricanes/', 'https://www.diveplanit.com/diving/best-time-to-dive/', 'https://codepoints.net/U+1F300', 'https://www.slideserve.com/emily/naval-meteorology-and-oceanography-professional-development-center', 'https://buyessay.org/blog/dissertation-chapter-sample-on-tropical-cyclones/', 'http://metservice.gov.jm/glossary-of-terms/']","""Tropical"" refers to the geographical origin of these systems, which form almost exclusively over tropical seas. ""Cyclone"" refers to their winds moving in a circle, whirling round their central clear eye, with their winds blowing counterclockwise in the Northern Hemisphere and blowing clockwise in the Southern Hemisphere. The opposite direction of circulation is due to the Coriolis effect. Tropical cyclones typically form over large bodies of relatively warm water. They derive their energy through the evaporation of water from the ocean surface, which ultimately recondenses into clouds and rain when moist air rises and cools to saturation. This energy source differs from that of mid-latitude cyclonic storms, such as nor'easters and European windstorms, which are fueled primarily by horizontal temperature contrasts. Tropical cyclones are typically between 100 and 2,000 km (62 and 1,243 mi) in diameter.",why does tropical cyclone originated over the seas
where does the great wall begin and end,"['http://www.scheut.org/news.php?lng=fr&pg=147', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/220BC/great-wall-of-china-built', 'http://myexperttravel.com/worldfamous.html', 'http://www.sullivanslist.com/view/great_wall', 'http://www.pensionhotel.co.uk/country--44-hotels-guesthouses-holiday-houses-apartments-camps-restaurants-china', 'https://chinadelighttour.com/great-wall-of-china/', 'https://www.waitamoment.co.uk/museums-monuments/great-wall-china/great-china-wall-crowds']","The Great Wall stretches from Dandong in the east to Lop Lake in the west, along an arc that roughly delineates the southern edge of Inner Mongolia. A comprehensive archaeological survey, using advanced technologies, has concluded that the Ming walls measure 8,850 km (5,500 mi). This is made up of 6,259 km (3,889 mi) sections of actual wall, 359 km (223 mi) of trenches and 2,232 km (1,387 mi) of natural defensive barriers such as hills and rivers. Another archaeological survey found that the entire wall with all of its branches measure out to be 21,196 km (13,171 mi). Today, the Great Wall is generally recognized as one of the most impressive architectural feats in history.",where does the great wall begin and end
what is meant by the concept collective existence,"['http://www.austincooperatives.coop/', 'https://wn.com/Collective_lawyers?from=collectivelawyers.com', 'https://pancreaticcancercollective.org/', 'http://blog.accidentalyogist.com/2009/03/new-collective-force-in-town.html', 'http://turnstyle.org.au/pigglywiggly/', 'https://recoverycollective.bigcartel.com/about', 'https://www.helpmusicians.org.uk/creative-programme/current-opportunities/northern-ireland-opportunities/women-in-music-northern-ireland-fund']","A collective is a group of entities that share or are motivated by at least one common issue or interest, or work together to achieve a common objective. Collectives can differ from cooperatives in that they are not necessarily focused upon an economic benefit or saving, but can be that as well.",what is meant by the concept collective existence
why do you think the state of himachal pradesh has been given the name himachal,"['https://alchetron.com/Himachal-Pradesh', 'http://aicps.org/contact-usdistrict-committees-himachal-pradeshdistrict-committee-shimla', 'http://election2019loksabha.com/himachal-pradesh-lok-sabha-general-election-results-2019/', 'https://www.travocoaster.com/attraction/himachal-pradesh?id=191&stateId=14', 'https://www.shubhttc.com/india-tour-packages/himachal-tour-packages', 'https://www.sgpsholidays.com/tours/western-himalayas-42646', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Lists_of_people_from_India_by_state']","Himachal Pradesh ((ɦɪmaːtʃəl prəd̪eːʃ) (listen); literally ""snow-laden province"") is a state of India located in North India. Situated in the Western Himalayas, it is bordered by states of Jammu and Kashmir on the north, Punjab on the west, Haryana on the southwest, Uttarakhand on the southeast, and the Tibet Autonomous Region on the east. At its southernmost point, it also touches the state of Uttar Pradesh. The state's name was coined from the Sanskrit -- Him means' snow' and achal means' land' or' abode' -- by acharya Diwakar Datt Sharma, one of the state's eminent Sanskrit scholars.",why do you think the state of himachal pradesh has been given the name himachal
where was nubia located in relation to egypt,"['https://thereaderwiki.com/en/Nubia', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Ethiopia', 'http://dabuka.de/itinerary/aswan-nubian-adventure/', 'https://www.calibakers.com/collections/men/products/nubian-crew', 'https://www.stridetravel.com/trips/culturalcrossroads/educational-and-cultural-expedition-to-egypt', 'http://abrej.tk/totally-free-dating-for-single-parents.html', 'https://thinkafrica.net/2018/10/24/makuria-baqt/']","Nubia (/ ˈnuːbiə, ˈnjuː-/) is a region along the Nile river encompassing the area between Aswan in southern Egypt and Khartoum in central Sudan. It was the seat of one of the earliest civilizations of ancient Africa, with a history that can be traced from at least 2500 BC onward (Kerma culture), and was home to several empires, most prominently the kingdom of Kush, which for a while even ruled over Egypt. Its collapse in the 4th century AD after more than 1000 years of existence was precipitated by an invasion by Ethiopia's Kingdom of Aksum and saw the rise of three Christian kingdoms, Nobatia, Makuria and Alodia, the last two again lasting 1000 years. Their eventual decline initiated not only the partition of Nubia into the northern half conquered by the Ottomans and the southern half by the Sennar sultanate in the 16th century, but also a rapid Islamization and partial Arabization of the Nubian people. Nubia was again united under the Khedivate of Egypt in the 19th century. Today, Nubia is split between Egypt and Sudan.",where was nubia located in relation to egypt
where do country style pork ribs come from,"['http://bbqrestaurantsanclemente.com/', 'https://www.newportmeatnv.com/pork-cut-ribs', 'https://beatcancer2010.wordpress.com/category/crock-pot/', 'https://trendyexplore.com/balinese-cuisine/', 'https://camerausa.info/how-to-cut-country-style-ribs/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Rib', 'http://fast2eat.com/glossary-of-culinary-termsP/']","Pork ribs are a cut of pork popular in Western and Asian cuisines. The ribcage of a domestic pig, meat and bones together, is cut into usable pieces, prepared by smoking, grilling, or baking -- usually with a sauce, often barbecue -- and then served.",where do country style pork ribs come from
what is the main difference between deciduous and evergreen trees,"['https://dizpos.com/evergreen-foliage-plants', 'https://gardenarium.com.au/trees/evergreen-trees', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Theobroma_cacao', 'http://www.agrinovia.org/NomineesForBest/all-of-the-year', 'https://www.henmanperformancegroup.com/newsletters/developing-evergreen-clients/', 'https://www.ehow.co.uk/about_5415367_garden-plant-identification.html', 'https://www.theeverco.co/about']","In botany, an evergreen is a plant that has leaves throughout the year, always green. This is true even if the plant retains its foliage only in warm climates, and contrasts with deciduous plants, which completely lose their foliage during the winter or dry season. There are many different kinds of evergreen plants, both trees and shrubs. Evergreens include:",what is the main difference between deciduous and evergreen trees
where is hydrogen obtained from in the haber process,"['http://roundtaiwanround.com/fritz-haber-process.html', 'http://anz.ipni.net/article/ANZ-3006', 'https://biv.com/article/2018/11/advocates-float-hydrogen-export-industry-idea', 'https://www.torquenews.com/1079/circulatory-combustion-engine-extend-range-plug-hybrids', 'http://joannenova.com.au/2008/10/what-is-evidence/', 'https://www.holmegaardresource.com/greenhouse-gas-containing-hydrogen-and-oxygen/', 'http://greenpow.blogspot.com/2012/04/solar-energy-in-india.html']","The major source of hydrogen is methane from natural gas. The conversion, steam reforming, is conducted with steam in a high temperature and pressure tube inside a reformer with a nickel catalyst, separating the carbon and hydrogen atoms in the natural gas.",where is hydrogen obtained from in the haber process
what is the song she talks to angels by the black crowes about,['https://www.jinglejanglejungle.net/2014/10/rocktober-25-2014-black-crowes.html'],"In 2010, Chris Robinson explained in a webisode (part of a promotional internet series for the band's 2010 Croweology album) that the song is loosely based on a ""goth girl"" he was acquainted with in Atlanta who was ""into heroin"".",what is the song she talks to angels by the black crowes about
what is the right to work in ohio,"['https://www.bctv.org/2018/02/23/expert-panel-to-discuss-right-to-work-laws-as-part-of-consider-it-series-in-berks-county/', 'https://www.wanderings.net/blog/why-right-to-work-is-wrong-robert-reich/', 'http://dearbornff.org/?zone=/unionactive/view_article.cfm&HomeID=74396&page=archived20articles', 'https://sacratomatovillepost.com/tag/abortion-rights/', 'http://southbendvoice.com/2019/04/09/sanders-vows-to-ban-right-to-work-laws-in-all-50-states/', 'https://www.thenation.com/article/teachers-are-leading-the-working-class-insurgency/', 'https://pamplinmedia.com/bvt/15-news/401805-297750-high-court-local-impact?tmpl=component&print=1']","""Right-to-work laws"" are statutes in 28 U.S. states that prohibit union security agreements between companies and workers' unions. Under these laws, employees in unionized workplaces are banned from negotiating contracts which require all members who benefit from the union contract to contribute to the costs of union representation.",what is the right to work in ohio
who are james and john in the bible,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/James_the_Great.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/James%2C_son_of_Zebedee', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/James,_son_of_Zebedee', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Our_Lady_of_Guadalupe_in_Extremadura', 'https://www.irishcentral.com/roots/history/raise-a-pint-of-guinness-to-st-james-on-his-feast-day']","The son of Zebedee and Salome, James is styled ""the Greater"" to distinguish him from the Apostle James ""the Less"". He was the brother of John, the beloved disciple, and probably the elder of the two.",who are james and john in the bible
what is a chief warrant officer in the coast guard,"['http://hitchhikersgui.de/Organization_of_the_United_States_Coast_Guard', 'http://www.militaryranks.us/us-military-warrant-officer.htm', 'http://askthegunny.com/atg/index.php?p=default&cat=24', 'http://infogalactic.com/info/Warrent_officer', 'https://www.military-ranks.org/coast-guard/chief-petty-officer', 'https://www.federalpay.org/military/air-force/lieutenant-colonel', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Chief_Petty_Officer_(United_States).html']","Chief warrant officers in the Coast Guard may be found in command of larger small boat stations and patrol boats, as specialists and supervisors in other technical areas, and as special agents in the Coast Guard Investigative Service. They wear insignia essentially like that of their Navy counterparts, but with the USCG shield between the rank insignia and the specialty mark, as Coast Guard commissioned officers do with their rank insignia. Like their Navy counterparts, candidates for the rank of chief warrant officer must typically be serving in the chief petty officer grades (E-7 through E-9), however, the Coast Guard also permits selection of first class petty officers (E-6) who are chief petty officer selectees and who are in the top 50% on their advancement list to E-7. Like the Navy, the Coast Guard does not use the rank of warrant officer (WO-1). Although authorized in 1994, the Coast Guard does not currently use the CWO5 grade.",what is a chief warrant officer in the coast guard
what is a ride along with a police officer,"['http://www.newark.org/departments/police/how-to', 'http://www.newark.org/departments/police/how-to/request-ride-sit-along']","A ride-along is an arrangement for a civilian to spend a shift in the passenger seat of an emergency vehicle, observing the work day of a police officer, firefighter, or paramedic.",what is a ride along with a police officer
what is the size of the goliath bird eating spider,"['http://www.frankfiedler.com/category/world-of-insects/the-worlds-freakiest-insects/', 'https://www.tolearnenglish.com/exercises/exercise-english-2/exercise-english-95978.php', 'https://10mosttoday.com/10-coolest-spiders-in-the-world/', 'https://aerethcodex.com/2017/11/02/arachnids-insects/', 'https://petponder.com/goliath-birdeater-tarantula']","These spiders can have a leg span of up to 28 cm (11 in), a body length of up to 11.9 cm (4.7 in) and can weigh up to 175 g (6.2 oz). Birdeaters are one of the few tarantula species that lack tibial spurs, located on the first pair of legs of most adult males.",what is the size of the goliath bird eating spider
