what is the difference between emery board and nail file,"['https://www.farmaline.uk/beauty-hygiene/manicure-pedicure/nails/file/', 'http://houseofstylestories.com/houseofstylestories/thenailstylpstory', 'http://www.intimepromo.com/en_products/Promotional-Nail-Files-1176.html', 'https://www.ourvanity.com/beauty/nails/nail-files/', 'http://www.pgsuite.com/new-blog/2018/1/23/nail-it-down-f9db8', 'http://beautyhealth.tips/tag/finger/', 'https://www.niveamen.co.za/grooming-guides/body/put-the-man-in-manicure']","A nail file is a tool used to gently grind down and shape the edges of nails. They are often used in manicures and pedicures after the nail has been trimmed using appropriate nail clippers. Nail files may either be emery boards, ceramic, glass, crystal, plain metal files or metal files coated with corundum.",what is the difference between emery board and nail file
who ruled for one hundred days and when,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Hundred_Days', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Battle_of_Tamames', 'https://www.historyundressed.com/2012/04/guest-author-jack-caldwell-and-giveaway.html']","On 6 April 1814, Napoleon abdicated his throne, leading to the accession of Louis XVIII and the first Bourbon Restoration a month later. The defeated Napoleon was exiled to the island of Elba off the coast of Tuscany, while the victorious Coalition sought to redraw the map of Europe at the Congress of Vienna.",who ruled for one hundred days and when
where is the ohio river valley on a map,"['http://parlorsongs.com/issues/2018-2Q/thismonth/rivers.php', 'http://juventusfc.tk/regent-casino-events.html', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=ohioherbal.com&ads=1&title=Ohio+herbal&auto=Ohio+herbal&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Ohio+herbal&pagenum=4', 'http://community.worldheritage.org/articles/Ohio_River', 'http://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/13625', 'http://louisvillebedandbreakfast.org/cruising-into-spring/', 'https://www.farmland.org/initiatives/ohio-river']","The Ohio River, which streams westward from Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, to Cairo, Illinois, is the largest tributary, by volume, of the Mississippi River in the United States. At the confluence, the Ohio is considerably bigger than the Mississippi (Ohio at Cairo: 281,500 cu ft / s (7,960 m / s); Mississippi at Thebes: 208,200 cu ft / s (5,897 m / s)) and, thus, is hydrologically the main stream of the whole river system.",where is the ohio river valley on a map
how many kinds of chinese languages are there,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Syllable', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Varieties_of_Chinese', 'http://verbix.com/languages/chinese.html', 'https://wikimili.com/en/L', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Treaty_of_Shaoxing', 'https://www.translationservice.sg/chinese-translation-services/', 'https://rosiross.com/moving-to-china-to-do-list/']","Chinese, also known as Sinitic, is a branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family consisting of hundreds of local language varieties, many of which are not mutually intelligible. The differences are similar to those within the Romance languages, with variation particularly strong in the more rugged southeast. These varieties, often called ""dialects"", have been classified into seven to ten groups, the largest being Mandarin (e.g. Beijing dialect), Wu (e.g. Shanghainese), Min (e.g. Hokkien), and Yue (e.g. Cantonese).",how many kinds of chinese languages are there
where is the country georgia located on the map,"['https://www.zharoff.com/National-Geographic/Travel-diaries/04052017Georgia', 'https://steller.co/s/4qv98YCPLgf', 'http://www.genesisconsultancy.co.in/aboutgeorgia.html', 'https://ucsworld.com/study-mbbs-georgia/', 'http://kartutours.ge/en/about-us', 'http://www.east-site.com/travel-destinations/georgia', 'https://currentaffairs.gktoday.in/tags/fta']","Georgia (/ ˈdʒɔːrdʒə / (listen); Georgian: საქართველო, tr. Sakartvelo, IPA: (sɑkhɑrthvɛlɔ) (listen)) is a country in the Caucasus region of Eurasia. Located at the crossroads of Western Asia and Eastern Europe, it is bounded to the west by the Black Sea, to the north by Russia, to the south by Turkey and Armenia, and to the southeast by Azerbaijan. The capital and largest city is Tbilisi. Georgia covers a territory of 69,700 square kilometres (26,911 sq mi), and its 2017 population is about 3.718 million. Georgia is a unitary semi-presidential republic, with the government elected through a representative democracy.",where is the country georgia located on the map
who won the 2018 women's hockey gold medal,"['https://globalwomenshistory.com/2018/02/25/february-22-2018/', 'https://us.blastingnews.com/sports/2018/02/reactions-as-team-usa-beats-canada-to-capture-2018-womens-hockey-gold-medal-002381323.html']","In 1998, the Women's Olympic Hockey Team was named the USOC Team of the Year. In 2015, the Women's National Ice Hockey Team was named the USOC Team of the Month, in April. In 2018, the Women's Olympic Hockey Team won the gold medal in a 3-2 shootout, ending their 20-year drought.",who won the 2018 women's hockey gold medal
where did the concept of unicorns come from,"['http://blog.annatsp.com/2014/04/', 'https://coloringpagebase.com/collection/coloring-page-of-a-unicorn-full/', 'http://www.lunarwisdom.net/songs-of-a-cricket---blog/an-a-z-list-of-new-age-practices-to-embrace', 'http://www.mythicarticulations.com/unicorn-in-a-can.html', 'https://www.makecnc.com/browse-store/premium-patterns/mythological-and-imaginary/', 'http://www.heroulo.com/2019/02/luxurious-gold-jewelry-identification-marks/', 'http://tshirtsyndicate.com/blog/713/']","The unicorn is a legendary creature that has been described since antiquity as a beast with a single large, pointed, spiraling horn projecting from its forehead. The unicorn was depicted in ancient seals of the Indus Valley Civilization and was mentioned by the ancient Greeks in accounts of natural history by various writers, including Ctesias, Strabo, Pliny the Younger, and Aelian. The Bible also describes an animal, the re'em, which some versions translate as unicorn.",where did the concept of unicorns come from
who was irving berlin and what did he do,"['http://forotime.tk/irving-berlin-cheek-to-cheek-sheet-music.html', 'https://historyhop.com/famous-people/irving-berlin/bio', 'http://quotio.com/by/Irving-Berlin', 'https://snaccooperative.org/ark:/99166/w6xg9t7h', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/05-11/all', 'https://sing.fandom.com/wiki/Irving_Berlin', 'http://newyorkmusicmap.com/artist/irving-berlin/']","Irving Berlin (born Israel Beilin; May 11, 1888 -- September 22, 1989) was an American composer and lyricist, widely considered one of the greatest songwriters in American history. His music forms a great part of the Great American Songbook. Born in Imperial Russia, Berlin arrived in the United States at the age of five. He published his first song, ""Marie from Sunny Italy"", in 1907, receiving 33 cents for the publishing rights, and had his first major international hit, ""Alexander's Ragtime Band"" in 1911. He also was an owner of the Music Box Theatre on Broadway.",who was irving berlin and what did he do
when does the lens of the eye thicken,"['http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Presbyopia', 'http://www.assignmentpoint.com/science/biology/lens-anatomy.html', 'https://www.naturaleyecare.com/blog/eye-anatomy-disease/', 'http://www.maitlandvisioncenter.com/hyperopia-farsighted.html', 'http://resaube-competences.fr/marques-to-observe-the-celebrations/', 'http://www.greenchilis.at/wp/?p=9794', 'http://www.mairie-mondouzil.fr/2018/06/26/the-boyars-distribute-alms/']","The lens is flexible and its curvature is controlled by ciliary muscles through the zonules. By changing the curvature of the lens, one can focus the eye on objects at different distances from it. This process is called accommodation. At short focal distance the ciliary muscle contracts, zonule fibers loosen, and the lens thickens, resulting in a rounder shape and thus high refractive power. Changing focus to an object at a greater distance requires the relaxation of the lens and thus increasing the focal distance.",when does the lens of the eye thicken
to allah we belong and to him is our return in arabic,"['https://www.islamicboard.com/hadith/134349257-dua-thread-9.html?s=ad4846f5c1742cdce6e6fc2871de96e3', 'https://www.nairaland.com/4438563/captain-suleiman-muhammed-killed-armed', 'https://karimia.com/projects/welfare-social-services/', 'https://believesyednaqutbuddin.com/your-reflections/', 'http://www.techofheart.co/2006/03/what-is-perfection.html']","Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un (Arabic: إِنَّا لِلّهِ وَإِنَّـا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُونَ ‎) is a part of a verse from the Qur'an which translates to ""We belong to God and to Him we shall return."" The phrase is commonly recited by Muslims when a person experiences a tragedy in life, especially upon hearing news that a person has died. The phrase may also be recited in situations that involve risk of any sort.",to allah we belong and to him is our return in arabic
what is the difference between quebec and quebec city,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Quebec', 'http://everything.explained.today/Quebec_City/', 'https://familypedia.wikia.org/wiki/Quebec_City', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/Quebec_City', 'https://www.homesweethomestay.com/cities/quebec-city-quebec/', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Quebec%20City.html', 'https://quebeccultureblog.com/tag/english/']","Quebec City (pronounced / kwɪˈbɛk / (listen) or / kəˈbɛk /; French: Québec (kebɛk) (listen)); French: Ville de Québec), officially Québec, is the capital city of the Canadian province of Quebec. The city had a population estimate of 531,902 in July 2016, (an increase of 3.0% from 2011) and the metropolitan area had a population of 800,296 in July 2016, (an increase of 4.3% from 2011) making it the seventh-largest metropolitan area in Canada.",what is the difference between quebec and quebec city
where is amur river located on a map,"['http://unbiasedreviews.website/top-10-longest-rivers-in-the-world/', 'http://apps.evemilano.com/entities/?query=amur+river', 'http://www.china-travel-guide.net/province/heilongjiang/', 'https://www.chinadragontours.com/category/china-guide/china-rivers', 'https://www.pandaw.com/blog/cruise/laos-tribes-we-visit-along-the-way-and-other-attractions', 'http://mekongdeltadiscovery.com/sunset-on-sam-mountain-tra-su-cajuput-forest/', 'https://www.topchinatravel.com/china-guide/the-longest-rivers-in-china.htm']","The Amur River (Even: Тамур, Tamur; Russian: река́ Аму́р, IPA: (ɐˈmur)) or Heilong Jiang (Chinese: 黑龙江; pinyin: Hēilóng Jiāng, ""Black Dragon River""; Manchu: ᠰᠠᡥᠠᠯᡳᠶᠠᠨ ᡠᠯᠠ or ᡥᡝᠯᡠᠩ ᡤᡳᠶᠠᠩ; Möllendorff: sahaliyan ula / helung giyang; Abkai: sahaliyan ula / helung giyang, ""Black Water"") is the world's tenth longest river, forming the border between the Russian Far East and Northeastern China (Inner Manchuria). The largest fish species in the Amur is the kaluga, attaining a length as great as 5.6 metres (18 ft). The Amur River is the only river in the world in which subtropical Asian fish such as snakehead, coexist with Arctic Siberian fish, such as pike. The river is home to a variety of other large predatory fish such as Taimen, Amur Catfish, and yellowcheek.",where is amur river located on a map
how many seasons of the oc are there,"['https://upge.wn.com/?activate=details&pagenum=3&ads=1&author=system&auto=Movie+recruiting&standalone=1&domain_name=movierecruiting.com&title=Movie+recruiting&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Movie+recruiting', 'http://watchdesperatehousewives.com/seasons/desperate-housewives-season-1/', 'http://maksimovnafan1997.000webhostapp.com/series-1-breaking-bad/', 'http://zineyou.jp/the-oc-complete-season-4.html', 'https://925brands.com/shop/24-season-3-7-dvds-pack/', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/20_Hours_in_America', 'https://fusionanomaly.net/lost.html']","The fourth and final season of The O.C., an American teen drama television series, aired in the United States from November 2, 2006 to February 22, 2007 and consisted of sixteen episodes. The O.C's final season aired Thursdays at 9: 00 p.m. ET in the United States on Fox, a terrestrial television network. Fox tested a new timeslot by airing the second episode on Wednesday at 9: 00 p.m. ET against ABC's Lost and CBS's Criminal Minds. With Lost about to enter a three-month hiatus, Fox hoped that changing the timeslot for The O.C. would attract back viewers it had lost since the end of the previous season; however, the move was unsuccessful and the show returned to its Thursday timeslot.",how many seasons of the oc are there
how many states have common border with punjab,"['https://m.onenewspage.com/current/m2t_570/Punjab-India.htm', 'http://blog.vastu-india.com/vastu/best-vastu-consultant-in-punjab-vastu-expert-in-chandigarh/', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/karnataka', 'https://www.jagranjosh.com/general-knowledge/karnataka-at-a-glance-land-of-the-sun-rising-industry-1455088442-1', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Karnataka', 'http://www.cityindia.org/karnataka.html', 'http://www.top10encyclopedia.com/Detail/The-Punjab-A-Fertile-Land-of-Fun-Festival-and-Food-Punjab-State-Of-India-173']","Punjab (/ pʌnˈdʒɑːb / (listen)) is a state in northern India. Forming part of the larger Punjab region, the state is bordered by the Indian states of Jammu and Kashmir to the north, Himachal Pradesh to the east, Haryana to the south and southeast, Rajasthan to the southwest, and the Pakistan province of Punjab to the west. The state covers an area of 50,362 square kilometres or 1.53 percent of the total geographical area of India. It is the twentieth largest Indian state by area. With 27,704,236 inhabitants at the 2011 census, Punjab is the sixteenth largest state by population, comprising 22 districts. Punjabi, is the most widely spoken and official language of the state. The main ethnic group are the Punjabis, with Punjabi Sikhs (57.7 percent) forming the demographic majority followed by Hindus (38.5 percent). The state capital is located in Chandigarh, a Union Territory and also the capital of the neighboring state of Haryana. The five rivers are Sutlej, Ravi, Beas, Chenab and Jhelum.",how many states have common border with punjab
where are potatoes mostly grown in the world,"['https://www.sizzlingtastebuds.com/2011/02/chilly-potato-stir-fry.html', 'https://ayeshahaq.com/2009/05/16/vegetable-of-the-week-potato/', 'http://nikahreg.com/more-info/introduce/vegetables/', 'https://thekitchenlink.wordpress.com/2010/12/07/december-challenge/', 'http://www.anulaskitchen.com/2013/', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Plant', 'https://www.oawhealth.com/2014/05/02/19-super-health-benefits-of-raw-pumpkin-seeds/']","In 2014, world production of potatoes was 382 million tonnes, an increase of 4% over 2013 amounts and led by China with 25% of the world total (table). Other major producers were India, Russia, Ukraine and the United States. However, the local importance of potato is variable and rapidly changing. It remains an essential crop in Europe (especially eastern and central Europe), where per capita production is still the highest in the world, but the most rapid expansion over the past few decades has occurred in southern and eastern Asia.",where are potatoes mostly grown in the world
who were the original members of the eec and what was its purpose,"['https://selfstudyhistory.com/2014/12/30/world-historyeuropean-community-consolidation-and-expansion-of-european-community-european-union/?replytocom=4831', 'http://www.bookofdaystales.com/tag/treaty-of-paris/', 'http://www.factbites.com/topics/European-Common-Market', 'https://www.learn.marvelsystem.com/index.php/european-union/', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Ireland_and_the_European_Union', 'http://www.pearltrees.com/tfkempo/post-war-belgium/id10526720', 'http://party-net.info/?page_id=21644']","The Community's initial aim was to bring about economic integration, including a common market and customs union, among its six founding members: Belgium, France, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands and West Germany. It gained a common set of institutions along with the European Coal and Steel Community (ECSC) and the European Atomic Energy Community (EURATOM) as one of the European Communities under the 1965 Merger Treaty (Treaty of Brussels). In 1993, a complete single market was achieved, known as the internal market, which allowed for the free movement of goods, capital, services, and people within the EEC. In 1994, the internal market was formalised by the EEA agreement. This agreement also extended the internal market to include most of the member states of the European Free Trade Association, forming the European Economic Area covering 15 countries.",who were the original members of the eec and what was its purpose
what is the role of alternator in car,"['http://www.mdsdiesel.com/our-work/alternator-replacement', 'http://aaatalks.carolinas.aaa.com/car-care/what-s-an-alternator-9774/', 'https://www.sungardas.com/en-GB/blog/cto-labs-blog/object-storage--the-alternator-of-cloud-computing/', 'http://www.bangorautoparts.co.uk/electrical/', 'http://www.possumliving.com/2010/05/alternators-and-generators.html', 'https://www.robertsandson.com/page/alternators/', 'http://madabout-kitcars.com/kitcar/kb.php?aid=186']",Alternators are used in modern automobiles to charge the battery and to power the electrical system when its engine is running.,what is the role of alternator in car
what is considered a discipline in the humanities,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Humanities', 'http://linkdirectorylisting.com/arts_humanities/education/', 'https://singularity2030.ch/is-ai-changing-maslows-pyramid-of-needs/', 'http://nordan.daynal.org/wiki/index.php?title=Humanity&oldid=117270', 'http://studyabroad.co.in/course/', 'https://www.indiaassignmenthelp.com/humanities-assignment-help-india', 'https://dlsii.com/blog/tag/humanities-careers/']","The humanities use methods that are primarily critical, or speculative, and have a significant historical element -- as distinguished from the mainly empirical approaches of the natural sciences, yet, unlike the sciences, it has no central discipline. The humanities include ancient and modern languages, literature, philosophy, geography, history, religion, art and musicology.",what is considered a discipline in the humanities
where did the name soft drink come from,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Resort', 'https://www.copybook.com/soft-drinks', 'https://www.belastingdienst.nl/wps/wcm/connect/bldcontenten/belastingdienst/customs/excise_duty_and_consumer_tax/excise_duty_and_consumer_tax/particulars_per_type_excisable_product/particulars_per_exisable_product', 'http://www.achefshelp.com/category/1071/drinks-cocktails-and-smoothies', 'https://amazingshining.com/healthy-drink-strawberry-granita-recipe/', 'https://gurkka.com/news.do?id=21283', 'https://crispytheme.com/gotham-studio/magic-potion/']","Soft drinks are called ""soft"" in contrast with ""hard"" alcoholic beverages. Small amounts of alcohol may be present in a soft drink, but the alcohol content must be less than 0.5% of the total volume if the drink is to be considered non-alcoholic. Fruit punch, tea, and other such non-alcoholic beverages are technically soft drinks by this definition but are not generally referred to as such.",where did the name soft drink come from
does the us have an embargo on any country,"['https://wikimili.com/en/International_sanctions', 'http://ask.fedoraproject.org/en/question/64077/question-on-forbidden-items/', 'http://fryzjerzy.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=34549']","As of 2014, there are several United States embargoes and economic sanctions in force by the United States against several countries and activities, the most notable of which are against countries the federal government of the United States considers State Sponsors of Terrorism.",does the us have an embargo on any country
short term capital gains rate vs long term,"['https://learnlivingtrustblog.wordpress.com/2016/04/22/what-you-need-to-know-about-capital-gains-tax-and-inheritance/', 'http://developeconomies.com/foreign-policy/4441/', 'http://morgankenwood.com/commentary?start=155', 'https://www.dummies.com/personal-finance/investing/need-know-investment-taxes/', 'http://www.investorwords.com/16821/taxable_gain.html', 'https://www.fool.com/retirement/2017/01/13/5-things-to-know-about-capital-gains-tax.aspx', 'http://www.saferetirementincome.com/page/3/']","In the United States of America, individuals and corporations pay U.S. federal income tax on the net total of all their capital gains. The tax rate depends on both the investor's tax bracket and the amount of time the investment was held. Short-term capital gains are taxed at the investor's ordinary income tax rate and are defined as investments held for a year or less before being sold. Long-term capital gains, on dispositions of assets held for more than one year, are taxed at a lower rate.",short term capital gains rate vs long term
what does a compensator do for a gun,"['http://metaglossary.com/define/muzzle+brake', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/M2010_Enhanced_Sniper_Rifle', 'https://www.smokingbarrelusa.com/best-308-muzzle-brake/', 'http://www.vietnamtourpedia.com/stay-on-target-with-a-223-muzzle-brake/', 'https://hughesprecision.com/product/holy-moly-30-muzzle-brake/', 'https://www.rectifire.com/products/', 'https://o2gungroup.com/index.php/firearm-glossary/M']","A muzzle brake or recoil compensator is a device connected to the muzzle of a firearm or cannon that redirects propellant gases to counter recoil and unwanted rising of the barrel. The concept was first introduced for artillery and was a common feature on many anti-tank guns, especially those mounted on tanks, in order to reduce the area needed to take up the strokes of recoil and kickback. They have been used in various forms for rifles and pistols to help control recoil and the rising of the barrel that normally occurs after firing. They are used on pistols for practical pistol competitions, and are usually called compensators in this context.",what does a compensator do for a gun
when was the day of the dead created,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Day_of_the_Dead', 'https://www.streetfashion-magzzine.com/lifestyle-zz/archives/09-2015', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Day_of_the_Dead', 'https://shirleytwofeathers.com/The_Blog/pagancalendar/tag/giving-gifts/', 'http://www.esotericonline.net/group/ethnic-traditions/forum/topics/day-of-the-dead-mexico', 'https://traceyannemccartney.wordpress.com/tag/soul/', 'https://creativeadventurephotography.com/photo-workshop-oaxaca-mexico-day-of-the-dead/']","The Day of the Dead celebrations in Mexico developed from ancient traditions among its pre-Columbian cultures. Rituals celebrating the deaths of ancestors had been observed by these civilizations perhaps for as long as 2,500 -- 3,000 years. The festival that developed into the modern Day of the Dead fell in the ninth month of the Aztec calendar, about the beginning of August, and was celebrated for an entire month. The festivities were dedicated to the goddess known as the ""Lady of the Dead"", corresponding to the modern La Calavera Catrina.",when was the day of the dead created
who played in the movie terms of endearment,"['https://movs.io/movie/terms-of-endearment', 'https://www.allaboutmovies.com.au/index.php/poster-formats/day-bill-posters/item/85223-terms-of-endearment-daybill-movie-poster', 'http://buyretinaonlinenoprescription.tk/what-are-the-terms-of-the-loan', 'https://www11.movieonline.tv/movies/8-out-of-10-cats-season-21.html']","Terms of Endearment is a 1983 American comedy-drama film adapted from Larry McMurtry's 1975 novel, directed, written, and produced by James L. Brooks and starring Shirley MacLaine, Debra Winger, Jack Nicholson, Danny DeVito, Jeff Daniels, and John Lithgow. The film covers 30 years of the relationship between Aurora Greenway (MacLaine) and her daughter Emma (Winger).",who played in the movie terms of endearment
scientific research and experimental development tax credit program,"['https://learn.marsdd.com/mars-library/research-development-funding-programs/', 'https://globalventurecapital.wordpress.com/tag/international-vc/', 'https://startupangels.com/market/montreal/', 'http://ctap.ca/sred-check-list-download/', 'http://www.williamsandpartners.com/what-we-do/our-services/']","The Canadian Scientific Research and Experimental Development Tax Incentive Program (SRED or SR&ED) provides support in the form of tax credits and / or refunds, to corporations, partnerships or individuals who conduct scientific research or experimental development in Canada.",scientific research and experimental development tax credit program
where is the main source of the internet,"['http://yobelcool.blogspot.com/2011/11/what-is-internet.html', 'http://the21stcenturyworld-wideissues.blogspot.com/2009/12/internet.html', 'https://demo.htmly.com/archive/2014-01', 'https://frontview.wordpress.com/internetweb/', 'https://www.smtsa.net/backbone-networks-corporation.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/History_of_the_Internet', 'https://www.wikinow.co/topic/internet']","The Internet has no centralized governance in either technological implementation or policies for access and usage; each constituent network sets its own policies. Only the overreaching definitions of the two principal name spaces in the Internet, the Internet Protocol address (IP address) space and the Domain Name System (DNS), are directed by a maintainer organization, the Internet Corporation for Assigned Names and Numbers (ICANN). The technical underpinning and standardization of the core protocols is an activity of the Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF), a non-profit organization of loosely affiliated international participants that anyone may associate with by contributing technical expertise.",where is the main source of the internet
where is the first amendment in the constitution,"['https://briancimins.com/tag/submission/', 'https://issuu.com/prattinstitute/docs/prattfolio_fall2013_highres', 'https://bvtack.com/31564/multimedia/what-does-it-mean-to-be-free/', 'http://kinlane.com/2018/03/22/helping-folks-see-the-algorithmic-distortions-all-around-us/', 'https://soapboxie.com/social-issues/Religion-and-Animal-Sacrifice-Religion-Is-Not-Above-the-Law', 'https://www.radixanabaptism.com/which-amendment-guarantees-freedom-of-religion/', 'https://pcaw.co.uk/exposing-secrets-the-past-present-and-future-of-u-s-national-security-whistleblowing-and-government-secrecy/']","The First Amendment (Amendment I) to the United States Constitution prevents Congress from making any law respecting an establishment of religion, prohibiting the free exercise of religion, or abridging the freedom of speech, the freedom of the press, the right to peaceably assemble, or to petition for a governmental redress of grievances. It was adopted on December 15, 1791, as one of the ten amendments that constitute the Bill of Rights.","AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementTurn static files into dynamic content formats.Create a flipbookAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementIssuu converts static files into: digital portfoliosonline yearbooksonline catalogsdigital photo albums and more. Sign up and create your flipbook.Prattfolio Fall/Winter 2013 ""Visualizing Data"" Issue by Pratt Institute - Issuu"
where is the country of sri lanka located,"['http://wikien3.appspot.com/wiki/Portal:Sri_Lanka', 'http://blogandoblog.info/29/5080133-sri-lanka-urlaub.html', 'http://kozmetikwebsitesi.tk/how-soon-to-date-after-the-death-of-a-spouse.html', 'https://legacarta.intracen.org/country/lka/', 'https://www.srilankaforex.com/about-sri-lanka.php', 'https://www.photonicyatra.com/Destinations/Sri-Lanka/i-kfLm3B6/', 'http://countriesasia.com/Sri+Lanka']","Sri Lanka (/ sriː ˈlɑːŋkə,-ˈlæŋkə /, / ʃriː-/ (listen); Sinhala: ශ්‍රී ලංකා Śrī Laṃkā; Tamil: இலங்கை Ilaṅkai), officially the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka, is an island country in South Asia, located in the Indian Ocean to the southwest of the Bay of Bengal and to the southeast of the Arabian Sea. It is separated from the Indian subcontinent by the Gulf of Mannar and the Palk Strait. The legislative capital, Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte, is a suburb of the commercial capital and largest city, Colombo.",where is the country of sri lanka located
how did grape nuts cereal get its name,"['http://www.letsgopens.com/scripts/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1867795&sid=2b3b08bc8044f99680afe04791703668', 'https://www.top5.com/best-cereal-of-all-time/', 'http://forum.rifftrax.com/index.php?topic=34106.30', 'http://listwebonline.info/10098-post-grape-nuts-coupon-printable.html', 'http://www.edwardianpromenade.com/food/an-edwardian-breakfast/', 'https://www.postconsumerbrands.ca/questions-answers/2/']","Despite the name, the cereal contains neither grapes nor nuts; it is made with wheat and barley. Post believed that glucose (which he called ""grape sugar"") formed in the baking process. This, combined with the nutty flavor of the cereal, is said to have inspired its name. Another explanation originates from employees at Post, who claim that the cereal got its name due to a resemblance to grape seeds, or grape ""nuts"".",how did grape nuts cereal get its name
where is montana located in the united states,"['https://knowledge.allbest.ru/sport/3c0a65625b3ac68b5c53a89521206d36_0.html', 'http://ca.wowcity.com/northwestterritories/', 'http://holiday-calendar.com/montana-usa-public-holiday-calendar/5258/', 'https://familypedia.wikia.org/wiki/Montana', 'http://www.thefullwiki.org/Transportation_in_Montana', 'https://turtledove.fandom.com/wiki/Montana', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Montana']","Montana is one of the nine Mountain States, located in the north of the region known as the Western United States. It borders North Dakota and South Dakota to the east. Wyoming is to the south, Idaho is to the west and southwest, and three Canadian provinces, British Columbia, Alberta, and Saskatchewan, are to the north.",where is montana located in the united states
where do monarch butterflies migrate to in california,"['https://kiwifoto.com/galleries/butterflies/monarch/', 'http://centralambert.com/this-too-shall-pass-on-the-majestic-monarch-butterfly-now-in-diminished-numbers-flying-indomitable-but-for-how-long-look-up-in-awe-as-this-great-thing-of-beauty-soars-above-us-threatened/', 'http://tulsagentleman.blogspot.com/2010/10/', 'http://www.4to40.com/kids-encyclopedia/united-states-encyclopedia/california/']","The western population overwinters in various coastal sites in central and southern California, United States, notably in Pacific Grove, Santa Cruz, and Grover Beach. Western monarchs also overwinter in Baja, California's central valley, and the Sierra Nevada foothills.",where do monarch butterflies migrate to in california
changes in the us economy affect puerto rico because,"['https://alchetron.com/Puerto-Rico', 'https://www.cookprocessor.eu/19986_Mining-Equipment-Sales-Representative-Latin-America.html', 'https://www.mgiworld.com/newsroom/2019/march/mgi-north-america-welcomes-a-new-member-to-our-international-accounting-association-in-puerto-rico/', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Puerto_Rico', 'https://www.zonelektra.nl/19_03_19_39847_latin_america_mining_equipment_sales_representative.html', 'http://wikien4.appspot.com/wiki/Economy_of_Puerto_Rico', 'https://gitubycolim.agronumericus.com/moodys-key-grid-factors-85225ny2522.html']","The economy of Puerto Rico is classified as a high income economy by the World Bank and as the most competitive economy in Latin America by the World Economic Forum. The main drivers of its economy are manufacturing, primarily pharmaceuticals, textiles, petrochemicals, and electronics; followed by the service industry, notably finance, insurance, real estate, and tourism. The geography of Puerto Rico and its political status are both determining factors on its economic prosperity, primarily due to its relatively small size as an island; its lack of natural resources used to produce raw materials, and, consequently, its dependence on imports; as well as its suzerainty to the United States which controls its foreign policies while exerting trading restrictions, particularly in its shipping industry.",changes in the us economy affect puerto rico because
where is the sella located in the brain,"['https://howardgoldenberg.com/2016/03/04/out-of-hermes-way/', 'https://www.fidalgoweather.net/2012/10/seeing-forest.html', 'https://geekymedics.com/cranial-foramina/', 'http://mre.com.ua/modern-rock-ensemble-reviews', 'http://sashwath.in/completed_projects.html', 'https://archive.org/details/BBCNEWS_20190416_130000_Afternoon_Live', 'http://www.mostpopularrestaurantsinbeverlyhills.com/restaurants/Il-Cielo']","The sella turcica (Latin for Turkish seat) is a saddle-shaped depression in the body of the sphenoid bone of the human skull and of the skulls of other hominids including chimpanzees, orangutans, and gorillas. It serves as a cephalometric landmark. The pituitary gland or hypophysis is located within the most inferior aspect of the sella turcica, the hypophyseal fossa.",where is the sella located in the brain
where is the liver located at in the human body,"['https://danilouann.com/2016/07/11/liver-cleanse/', 'https://greenorganicsupplements.com/index.php/catalog/product/view/id/1022/s/liver-cleanser-restorer/category/12/', 'https://mobizone.ng/prevent-treat-liver-diseases/', 'http://rjppd.org/AbstractView.aspx?PID=2012-4-5-29', 'http://www.micropedia.org/category/biology', 'https://www.9tofine.net/en/health/how-fast-does-the-human-body-replace-itself/', 'http://www.liverfoundation-ne.org/']","The liver is a vital organ only found in vertebrates. In humans, it is located in the upper right quadrant of the abdomen, below the diaphragm. The liver has a wide range of functions, including detoxification of various metabolites, protein synthesis, and the production of biochemicals necessary for digestion. It also plays a role in metabolism, regulation of glycogen storage, decomposition of red blood cells and hormone production.",where is the liver located at in the human body
what is margin of error for confidence interval,"['http://www.sceneadvisor.com/Kentucky/margin-of-error-concept.html', 'http://duwanoe.xlx.pl/350.html', 'https://www.lecturio.com/magazine/confidence-intervals-for-proportions/', 'http://duwanoe.xlx.pl/646.html', 'http://programwiki.org/standard-error-of-estimate-calculator-ti-84/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/HD_49933', 'http://www.sceneadvisor.com/Kentucky/margin-of-error-equations.html']","The margin of error is usually defined as the ""radius"" (or half the width) of a confidence interval for a particular statistic from a survey. One example is the percent of people who prefer product A versus product B. When a single, global margin of error is reported for a survey, it refers to the maximum margin of error for all reported percentages using the full sample from the survey. If the statistic is a percentage, this maximum margin of error can be calculated as the radius of the confidence interval for a reported percentage of 50%.",what is margin of error for confidence interval
why is fleur de lis symbol of new orleans,"['http://www.cguiw.com/content-1337.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Fleurs-de-lys.html', 'https://www.shapeways.com/product/BF4JSYMSG/tie-clip-fleur-de-lis?optionId=63821149&li=marketplace', 'https://www.yapatkwatapestries.com/listing/252546707/joan-of-arc-coat-of-arms-fleur-de-lis', 'https://arwen-gold-fan.info/fleur-de-lis-finials.html', 'https://jjaustrian.com/', 'https://elizadashwood.co.uk/2014/05/20/writing-prompt-symbols-and-meanings/']","The fleur-de-lis / fleur-de-lys (plural: fleurs-de-lis / fleurs-de-lys) or flower-de-luce is a stylized lily (in French, fleur means ""flower"", and lis means ""lily"") that is used as a decorative design or motif, and many of the Catholic saints of France, particularly St. Joseph, are depicted with a lily. Since France is a historically Catholic nation, the fleur-de-lis became ""at one and the same time, religious, political, dynastic, artistic, emblematic, and symbolic"", especially in French heraldry.",why is fleur de lis symbol of new orleans
what was concrete made out of in ancient rome,"['http://hairlosstreament.info/2017/07/the-strongest-concrete-on-earth/', 'https://www.shorelineaggregate.com/how-durable-concrete-really']","Roman concrete, like any concrete, consists of an aggregate and hydraulic mortar -- a binder mixed with water that hardens over time. The aggregate varied, and included pieces of rock, ceramic tile, and brick rubble from the remains of previously demolished buildings.","Page not found - Shoreline Aggregate Skip to content 219-878-9991 orders@shorelineaggregate.com Facebook Twitter Youtube Linkedin Instagram The page can’t be found. It looks like nothing was found at this location. Construction Aggregates Limestone Gravel Sand Recycled Concrete Slag Trap Rock Red Granite Golf & Sports Turf Aggregates Bunker Sand Top Dressing Sand Divot And Tee Mixes Red Granite Sand Contact Us P: 219 - 878 - 9991 F: 219 - 878 - 9989 orders@shorelineaggregate.com Facebook X-twitter Instagram Linkedin © Copyright 2026. Shoreline Aggregate Solutions, Inc. All Rights Reserved."
how many champions league trophy has messi won,"['https://www.wikinow.co/topic/lionel-messi', 'http://www.kaosbolaonline.com/2011/11/fcbarcelona20112012.html', 'https://www.parkhighstanmore.org.uk/page/?title=Messi+or+Ronaldo&pid=366', 'http://uprutuadobib.info/author/UCV6n8RTZk_dRXaWSWkjhtNQ/Mnf+News', 'https://allstarpics.famousfix.com/pictures/lionel-messi', 'http://lifeontheline.info/search?q=Lionel%20messi%20magic%20skills%20dribbling', 'http://rock-cafe.info/posts/lionel-messi-quotes-about-soccer-6c696f6e656c.html']","Lionel Andrés ""Leo"" Messi Cuccittini (Spanish pronunciation: (ljoˈnel anˈðɾes ˈmesi) (listen); born 24 June 1987) is an Argentine professional footballer who plays as a forward for Spanish club FC Barcelona and the Argentina national team. Often considered the best player in the world and regarded by many as the greatest of all time, Messi is the only player in history to win five FIFA Ballon d'Or awards, four of which he won consecutively, and a record-tying four European Golden Shoes. He has won 29 trophies with Barcelona, including eight La Liga titles, four UEFA Champions League titles, and five Copas del Rey. Both a prolific goalscorer and a creative playmaker, Messi holds the records for most official goals scored in La Liga (361), a La Liga season (50), a club football season in Europe (73), a calendar year (91), as well as those for most assists made in La Liga (140) and the Copa América (11). He has scored over 600 senior career goals for club and country.","Wikinow • lionel-messi `.-://++oooooooo++//:-.` `-/+syyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyys+/-. .:osyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyo/-` `:+yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyo:. `:oyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyys/` -+yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy- `:syyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyo+/:--.````````..-:/+osyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy `:syyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyo/:.` ``-/oyyyyyyyyyyyyys -syyyyyyyyyyyyyyys+-` `-/oyyyyyyyys. .oyyyyyyyyyyyyyys+-` ./+ooo+-` :s