who stars in the movie keeping up with the joneses,"['http://helperprofile.weebly.com/blog/watch-keeping-up-with-the-joneses-movie-online-full-hd-2016', 'http://totalhollywoods.com/keeping-up-with-the-joneses/', 'http://newmoviesnewsandreviews.blogspot.com/', 'http://booredatwork.com/live-by-night-blu-ray-review/', 'https://www.netpaak.com/the-sisters-brothers-2018-dubbed/', 'https://cloudy.pk/keeping-up-with-the-joneses-2016-full-movie-watch-online-hdfree123/', 'http://www.dramastyle.com/mo_/Billy-Lynn--Long-Halftime-Walk/language/en']","Keeping Up with the Joneses is a 2016 American action comedy film directed by Greg Mottola and written by Michael LeSieur. Starring Zach Galifianakis, Jon Hamm, Isla Fisher and Gal Gadot, the film follows a suburban couple (Galifianakis and Fisher) who begin to suspect their new neighbors (Hamm and Gadot) are secret agents. The film was released on October 21, 2016 by 20th Century Fox, received generally negative reviews and was a box office bomb, grossing $29 million against its $40 million budget.",who stars in the movie keeping up with the joneses
what is the plot of the silence of the lambs,"['http://horrormoviezonline.com/2018/10/the-silence-of-the-lambs-full-horror-movie-online/', 'https://www.quirkybyte.com/blog/2016/11/must-watch-hollywood-thrillers-time/2/', 'http://cananalyze.blogspot.com/2010/04/the-silence-of-lambs-analysis-of-movie.html', 'http://bizkh.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=45150', 'https://www.popxo.com/2019/03/13-of-the-best-hollywood-suspense-movies-to-watch/', 'https://moviesdrop.com/movies-where-the-bad-guy-wins/387/', 'https://paulaacton.com/2013/07/10/stories-and-lists-july-blog-challenge-2013-day-8-list-your-10-all-time-favorite-movies/']","The Silence of the Lambs is a 1991 American psychological horror thriller film directed by Jonathan Demme from a screenplay written by Ted Tally, adapted from Thomas Harris's 1988 novel of the same name. The film stars Jodie Foster, Anthony Hopkins, Scott Glenn, Ted Levine, and Anthony Heald. In the film, Clarice Starling, a young FBI trainee, seeks the advice of the imprisoned Dr. Hannibal Lecter, a brilliant psychiatrist and cannibalistic serial killer to apprehend another serial killer, known only as ""Buffalo Bill"", who skins his female victims' corpses. The novel was Harris's first and second respectively to feature the characters of Starling and Lecter, and was the second adaptation of a Harris novel to feature Lecter, preceded by the Michael Mann-directed Manhunter (1986).",what is the plot of the silence of the lambs
explain the difference between a plebiscite and a referendum,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Plebiscite.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Sierra_Club', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Referendum', 'http://adobeegitim.com/queensland/how-to-get-a-plebisite-on-a-ballott.php', 'https://anzacday.org.au/ww1-an-overview-by-robert-lewis/', 'https://www.citizensinformation.ie/en/moving_country/moving_to_ireland/introduction_to_the_irish_system/right_to_vote.html', 'http://refoxblogger.blogspot.com/2014/01/here-is-vision-restore-australia.html']","Some definitions of' plebiscite' suggest that it is a type of vote to change the constitution or government of a country. However, some other countries define it differently. For example, Australia defines' referendum' as a vote to change the constitution, and' plebiscite' as a vote that does not affect the constitution. In Ireland, the vote to adopt its constitution was called a ""plebiscite"", but a subsequent vote to amend the constitution is called a' referendum', and so is a poll of the electorate on a non-constitutional bill.",explain the difference between a plebiscite and a referendum
where is brunei located in the world map,"['http://affiliateswork.com/healthybiz/wellness-Asia_Brunei.php', 'http://www.ata.my/brunei.php', 'http://www.nouahsark.com/en/infocenter/worldwide/asia/brunei/index.php', 'https://www.detectiveswilsons.com/private-investigators-brunei.html', 'https://latitude.to/map/bn/brunei', 'https://propelsteps.wordpress.com/tag/brunei-darussalam/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/List_of_agriculture_ministries']","Brunei (/ bruːˈnaɪ / (listen), broo-NYE), officially the Nation of Brunei, the Abode of Peace (Malay: Negara Brunei Darussalam, Jawi: نڬارا بروني دارالسلام ‎), is a sovereign state located on the north coast of the island of Borneo in Southeast Asia. Apart from its coastline with the South China Sea, the country is completely surrounded by the Malaysian state of Sarawak. It is separated into two parts by the Sarawak district of Limbang. Brunei is the only sovereign state completely on the island of Borneo; the remainder of the island's territory is divided between the nations of Malaysia and Indonesia. Brunei's population was 423,196 in 2016.",where is brunei located in the world map
where are dendritic cells located in the epidermis,"['http://theuniversalmatrix.com/pt-br/artigos/?cat=1635', 'https://statpearls.com/as/connective%20tissue/24017/', 'https://pediaa.com/what-is-the-difference-between-exogenous-and-endogenous-antigens/', 'https://www.verywellhealth.com/langerhans-cell-1069348', 'http://www.odermatol.com/issue-in-html/2013-3-2s-eponymsger/', 'https://stke.sciencemag.org/content/7/318/ec80', 'http://dr-baumann-international.co.uk/factsandillusions.html']","Langerhans cells are dendritic cells (antigen-presenting immune cells) of the skin, and contain organelles called Birbeck granules. They are present in all layers of the epidermis and are most prominent in the stratum spinosum. They also occur in the papillary dermis, particularly around blood vessels, as well as in the mucosa of the mouth, foreskin, and vaginal epithelium. They can be found in other tissues, such as lymph nodes, particularly in association with the condition Langerhans cell histiocytosis (LCH).",where are dendritic cells located in the epidermis
where does the last name novak come from,"['https://findwords.info/term/novak', 'https://europeisnotdead.com/europeans-surnames/', 'https://aleman.yabla.com/lessons.php?page=3', 'https://www.thefreedictionary.com/affects', 'https://www.syncrotranslation.com/translations/slovak-language/', 'https://wn.com/Slovak_Political?upload_time=all_time&orderby=relevance', 'https://beervisits.eu/pub-bar-visit/pv-england/133-pv-kent/630-dover-kent-cullins-yard']","Novak (in Serbo-Croatian and Slovene; Cyrillic: Новак), Novák (in Hungarian, Czech and Slovak), Nowak (in German and Polish) is a Slavic surname and masculine given name, derived from the word for ""new"" (e.g. Polish: nowy, Czech: nový, Serbo-Croatian: novo / ново), which depending on the exact language and usage, translates as ""novice"", ""new man"", ""newcomer"", or ""stranger"". The name was often given to a new arrival in a city or a convert to Christianity. It was also used for newcomers to an army and as an occupational surname for people who used the slash-and-burn method to create new arable land -- novina. It is pronounced almost the same way in most languages, with the stress on the first syllable. The main exception is Slovene, which places the stress on the last syllable.",where does the last name novak come from
how is the council of ministers formed in a state,"['http://meghalaya.gov.in/megportal/stateprofile', 'https://gkrefresher.wordpress.com/tag/directive-principles/', 'https://kerala-info.newkerala.com/Kerala/The-Government-of-Kerala.html', 'https://jharkhand.pscnotes.com/jharkhand-mains/paper-iv/polity-paper-iv/state-executive-powers-and-functions-of-chief-minister-and-the-council-of-ministers/', 'https://www.britannica.com/place/West-Bengal', 'http://www.infobarrel.com/India', 'http://www.rupeerains.com/governor-of-states/']",The Chief Minister is appointed by the Governor who also appoints other ministers on the advice of the Chief Minister. The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to legislative assembly of the State.,how is the council of ministers formed in a state
when did kabbalah become most prominent within judaism,"['https://telephone-psychics.absolutelypsychic.com/telephone-psychics/', 'https://www.successcentre.com.au/Category/new-age-books', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Mysticism', 'https://vitaltransformation.org/faq/?Display_FAQ=4320', 'http://iamtechnologyblog.com/practical-spirituality-kabballah/', 'https://en.metapedia.org/wiki/Cabala', 'http://christiandoctrine.com/christian-doctrine/other-religions-cults-and-sects/1350-the-kabbalah']","Traditional practitioners believe its earliest origins pre-date world religions, forming the primordial blueprint for Creation's philosophies, religions, sciences, arts, and political systems. Historically, Kabbalah emerged, after earlier forms of Jewish mysticism, in 12th-to 13th-century Southern France and Spain, becoming reinterpreted in the Jewish mystical renaissance of 16th-century Ottoman Palestine. Isaac Luria is considered the father of contemporary Kabbalah. It was popularised in the form of Hasidic Judaism from the 18th century onwards. Twentieth-century interest in Kabbalah has inspired cross-denominational Jewish renewal and contributed to wider non-Jewish contemporary spirituality, as well as engaging its flourishing emergence and historical re-emphasis through newly established academic investigation.",when did kabbalah become most prominent within judaism
