where is silver found and in what form (compound),"['https://www.fruitrevue.be/19-01-03-40263-soft_white_lustrous_transition_metal.html', 'https://tonyquintela.com/gold-silver-high-grade-ore-from-nevadas-comstock-for-sale/', 'http://blog.sevencreative.co.uk/index.php/page/2/', 'https://www.jewelry-auctioned.com/auctions/3815-cts-jade-silver-rings-size-9-sj1594-56022', 'http://huntlycentre.com.au/updates/posts/view/171', 'https://www.babyproofessionals.co.za/2019/39970-atomic-symbol-of-silver.html', 'https://anatometal.com/quality/silver-and-bronze/']","Silver is a chemical element with symbol Ag (from the Latin argentum, derived from the Greek ἀργός: ""shiny"" or ""white"") and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity, and reflectivity of any metal. The metal is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form (""native silver""), as an alloy with gold and other metals, and in minerals such as argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is produced as a byproduct of copper, gold, lead, and zinc refining.",where is silver found and in what form (compound)
what does the song nothing else matters mean,"['http://leontimes.com/category/video/music/page/2/', 'https://bothsidesnow.paulglover.net/home-stretch-the-4th-best-song-of-all-time-201308/', 'http://orthodoxylife.ru/watch/8SbUC-UaAxE', 'https://lifeofanelpasowoman.com/2016/08/21/sunday-song-8-21-16/', 'https://www.guitarworld.com/artists/20-best-rock-guitar-intros-all-time-video', 'http://id2sorties.com/slow-classic-rock-songs.html']","Lead singer and rhythm guitarist James Hetfield wrote the song (credited to Hetfield / Ulrich) in 1990 while he was on the phone with his then girlfriend. Since he held the phone with one hand, he plucked the four open strings of a standard E-minor chord with the other, which eventually made up the first two bars of the song. The lyrics, which talk about being ""so close, no matter how far"", were also dedicated to his girlfriend, indicating the bond they shared even when Hetfield was on tour. Initially, the song was not meant to be released, as Hetfield had written it for himself, but after drummer Lars Ulrich heard it, it was considered for the album.",what does the song nothing else matters mean
how many state do we have in germany,"['http://keyosk.online/destinations/germany/', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=bamberg.net&ads=1&title=Bamberg&auto=Bamberg&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Bamberg&pagenum=3', 'https://www.intlmovers.com/moving-from-brazil-to-germany.html', 'http://admission.ac/country_detail/ger', 'https://great-mapperdonian.fandom.com/wiki/Germany', 'https://latitude.to/map/de/germany', 'https://www.know.cf/enciclopedia/en/Germany']","Germany (German: Deutschland (ˈdɔʏtʃlant)), officially the Federal Republic of Germany (German: Bundesrepublik Deutschland, listen (help info)), is a sovereign state in central-western Europe. It includes 16 constituent states, covers an area of 357,386 square kilometres (137,988 sq mi), and has a largely temperate seasonal climate. With nearly 83 million inhabitants, Germany is the most populous member state of the European Union. Germany's capital and largest metropolis is Berlin, while its largest conurbation is the Ruhr, with its main centres of Dortmund and Essen. The country's other major cities are Hamburg, Munich, Cologne, Frankfurt, Stuttgart, Düsseldorf, Leipzig, Bremen, Dresden, Hannover, and Nuremberg.",how many state do we have in germany
how many superbowls have the patriots won in a row,"['http://launchpad.ticketgalaxy.com/home/archives/01-2018', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Dominique_Easley', 'http://bestbostontravelguide.com/new-england-patriots.php', 'http://www.directsportslink.com/professional-sports-team/new-england-patriots', 'https://www.djrpro.com/blog/rob-gronkowski-2008-arizona-wildcats-game-used-road-jersey', 'http://www.oranchak.com/?m=200802', 'http://recomparison.com/comparisons/101426/patriots-vs-vikings/']","The Patriots have won five Super Bowl championships (XXXVI, XXXVIII, XXXIX, XLIX, and LI). They also played in and lost Super Bowls XX, XXXI, XLII, XLVI, and Super Bowl LII. During the 2007 regular season, the Patriots became the only NFL team in history to win 16 games, and the first since the 1972 Miami Dolphins (in a 14-game season) to complete the regular campaign undefeated. Belichick's Patriots are one of only two teams to win three Super Bowls in four years (the other being the Dallas Cowboys from 1993 to 1996).",how many superbowls have the patriots won in a row
how many states touches the boundary of madhya pradesh,"['http://janpratinidhi.com/State/Madhya-Pradesh-14', 'http://www.eziitours.in/travelogue/interesting-places-madhya-pradesh/', 'http://www.clapdoor.com/location/madhya%20pradesh', 'https://upge.wn.com/?from=bhopaltravel.com&ads=1&title=Bhopal+travel&auto=Bhopal+travel&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Bhopal+travel&pagenum=4', 'https://latestjobs.co.in/current-jobs-in-madhya-pradesh/', 'http://www.anujobs.com/2016/07/madhya-pradesh-state-govt-jobs-vacancy-notification-recruitment.html', 'http://bharatmeragarv.com/madhya-pradesh-history/']","Madhya Pradesh (MP) (/ ˈmɑːdjə prəˈdɛʃ /, (help info), meaning Central Province) is a state in central India. Its capital is Bhopal and the largest city is Indore with Gwalior and Jabalpur being the other major cities. Nicknamed the ""heart of India"" due to its geographical location in India, Madhya Pradesh is the second-largest state in the country by area. With over 75 million inhabitants, it is the fifth-largest state in India by population. It borders the states of Uttar Pradesh to the northeast, Chhattisgarh to the southeast, Maharashtra to the south, Gujarat to the west, and Rajasthan to the northwest. Its total area is 308,252 km. Before 2000, when Chhattisgarh was a part of Madhya Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh was the largest state in India and the distance between the two furthest points inside the state, Singoli and Konta, was 1500 km.",how many states touches the boundary of madhya pradesh
whats the difference between the acropolis and the parthenon,"['https://www.olympicgamesathens2004.com/shop/olympic-games-2004/countries-pins/european-capitals/athens-greece-acropolis-athens-2004-olympic-pin/', 'https://erasmusrightnetmonuments.wordpress.com/', 'https://www.israel-in-photos.com/three-days-in-athens.html', 'https://onarviptransfer.com/tours/nautilus/', 'https://www.welcome-greece.gr/athens-acropolis/', 'https://www.foap.com/image-photo/very-old', 'http://www.athensbnb.net/en']","The Acropolis of Athens (Ancient Greek: Ἀκρόπολις, tr. Akrópolis; Modern Greek: Ακρόπολη Αθηνών, tr. Akrópoli Athenón (aˈkropoli aθiˈnon)) is an ancient citadel located on an extremely rocky outcrop above the city of Athens and contains the remains of several ancient buildings of great architectural and historic significance, the most famous being the Parthenon. The word acropolis comes from the Greek words ἄκρον (akron, ""highest point, extremity"") and πόλις (polis, ""city""). Although there are many other acropoleis in Greece, the significance of the Acropolis of Athens is such that it is commonly known as ""The Acropolis"" without qualification.",whats the difference between the acropolis and the parthenon
what is the girl with the dragon tattoo movie about,"['https://www.spectroom.com/category/171122202-mystery-movies', 'http://www.trailored.com/2011/09/the-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo-trailer/', 'http://secretsdoll.com/social/verblendung-daniel-craig.php', 'http://www.impulsegamer.com/bluraythegirlwiththedragontattoo.jpg.html', 'https://www.epicsound.com/2012/01/the-sound-and-music-of-the-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo/', 'http://itstotallytiffany.com/music/the-girl-with-the-dragon-tattoo-sweden.php', 'https://www.tuneskit.com/top-movies/10-bestselling-itunes-movies.html']","The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo is a 2011 Swedish-American psychological thriller film based on the novel of the same name by Stieg Larsson. This film adaptation was directed by David Fincher and written by Steven Zaillian. Starring Daniel Craig and Rooney Mara, it tells the story of journalist Mikael Blomkvist (Daniel Craig)'s investigation to find out what happened to a woman from a wealthy family who disappeared 40 years prior. He recruits the help of computer hacker Lisbeth Salander (Rooney Mara).",what is the girl with the dragon tattoo movie about
in ipl one team can play how many matches,"['https://waldo.villagesoup.com/p/waldo-county-teams-push-hard-to-regular-season-finish-line/1799741', 'https://waldo.villagesoup.com/p/vikings-mustangs-continue-to-battle-for-wins-down-home-stretch/1799297', 'https://waldo.villagesoup.com/p/no-snow-days-plenty-of-court-action-for-midcoast-teams-jan-7/1796097', 'https://www.legalonlinecasinos.in/sports/cricket/', 'http://bet-uk.com/cricket-betting/ipl-cricket-betting', 'https://indianhotdeal.com/top-fantasy-apps-in-india-to-play/', 'http://www.mumbaispider.com/resources/3632-mumbai-indians-qualified-quarter-finals.aspx']","Currently, with eight teams, each team plays each other twice in a home-and-away round-robin format in the league phase. At the conclusion of the league stage, the top four teams will qualify for the playoffs. The top two teams from the league phase will play against each other in the first Qualifying match, with the winner going straight to the IPL final and the loser getting another chance to qualify for the IPL final by playing the second Qualifying match. Meanwhile, the third and fourth place teams from league phase play against each other in an eliminator match and the winner from that match will play the loser from the first Qualifying match. The winner of the second Qualifying match will move onto the final to play the winner of the first Qualifying match in the IPL Final match, where the winner will be crowned the Indian Premier League champions.",in ipl one team can play how many matches
what limit does article 1 section 8 clause 1 place on taxation,"['https://lawaspect.com/united-states-constitution-6/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/U.S._state', 'http://abidesh.blogspot.com/2012/07/health-scare-for-everybody.html', 'https://law.justia.com/cases/federal/appellate-courts/F3/304/1320/474428/', 'https://law.justia.com/cases/federal/appellate-courts/F2/89/368/1473001/', 'https://www.investopedia.com/ask/answers/012715/who-sets-fiscal-policy-president-or-congress.asp', 'https://taxassociate.wordpress.com/category/subtitle-d-excise/']","The Taxing and Spending Clause (which contains provisions known as the General Welfare Clause) and the Uniformity Clause, Article I, Section 8, Clause 1 of the United States Constitution, grants the federal government of the United States its power of taxation. While authorizing Congress to levy taxes, this clause permits the levying of taxes for two purposes only: to pay the debts of the United States, and to provide for the common defense and general welfare of the United States. Taken together, these purposes have traditionally been held to imply and to constitute the federal government's taxing and spending power.",what limit does article 1 section 8 clause 1 place on taxation
what are the countries in united arab emirates,"['http://reference.allrefer.com/top-10-richest-countries-in-the-world-6295', 'https://jobsmag.org/new-uae-cruise-ship-recruitment.html', 'http://www.freesmsto.com/uae/', 'http://gulfjobsreporting.com/2017/07/01/uae-cruise-ship-new-jobs-apply-now/', 'http://hikerbible.com/united-arab-emirates/', 'http://smk-group.ru/3617480188.html', 'https://thelegant.com/UAE']","The country is a federation of seven emirates, and was established on 2 December 1971. The constituent emirates are Abu Dhabi (which serves as the capital), Ajman, Dubai, Fujairah, Ras al-Khaimah, Sharjah and Umm al-Quwain. Each emirate is governed by an absolute monarch; together, they jointly form the Federal Supreme Council. One of the monarchs (traditionally always the Emir of Abu Dhabi) is selected as the President of the United Arab Emirates. Islam is the official religion of the UAE and Arabic is the official language (although English, Urdu and Hindi are widely spoken, with English being the language of business and education particularly in Abu Dhabi and Dubai).",what are the countries in united arab emirates
the meaning of the om symbol in buddhism,"['http://themodernvedic.com/life/om-%E0%A5%90-aum/', 'https://www.wearamantra.com/themantra.html', 'https://www.reckonings.net/reckonings/2018/07/index.html', 'https://www.esoterism.ro/english/om-mani.php', 'http://www.katinkahesselink.net/tibet/dalai1.html', 'http://maniretreat.sg/explanation-of-the-six-syllable-mantra/', 'http://www.meditationiseasy.com/meditation-techniques/om-mani-padme-hum-the-tibetan-mantra-for-meditation/']","Oṃ has been described by the 14th Dalai Lama as ""composed of three pure letters, A, U, and M. These symbolize the impure body, speech, and mind of everyday unenlightened life of a practitioner; they also symbolize the pure exalted body, speech and mind of an enlightened Buddha."" According to Simpkins, Om is a part of many mantras in Tibetan Buddhism and is a symbolism for ""wholeness, perfection and the infinite"".",the meaning of the om symbol in buddhism
where does the right atrium recieve blood from,"['https://hyperleap.com/topic/Ventricle_(heart)', 'http://filefreevd.tk/lllf/essay-on-human-heart-1120.php', 'https://www.sentara.com/charlottesville-virginia/medicalservices/services/heart-arrhythmia/about-heart-arrhythmia.aspx', 'https://bodytomy.com/anatomy-of-human-heart', 'http://www.appliedcardiacsystems.com/ecp-external-counterpulsation-therapy/', 'https://www.storyboardthat.com/storyboards/willz/heart-circulation', 'http://www.medicalestudy.com/698-2/']","Humans have a four-chambered heart consisting of the right atrium, left atrium, right ventricle, and left ventricle. The atria are the two upper chambers. The right atrium receives and holds deoxygenated blood from the superior vena cava, inferior vena cava, anterior cardiac veins and smallest cardiac veins and the coronary sinus, which it then sends down to the right ventricle (through the tricuspid valve) which in turn sends it to the pulmonary artery for pulmonary circulation. The left atrium receives the oxygenated blood from the left and right pulmonary veins, which it pumps to the left ventricle (through the mitral valve) for pumping out through the aorta for systemic circulation.",where does the right atrium recieve blood from
what is a canon priest in the catholic church,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/Canon_(priest)', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Monastery']","Originally, a canon was a cleric living with others in a clergy house or, later, in one of the houses within the precinct of or close to a cathedral and conducting his life according to the orders or rules of the church. This way of life grew common (and is first documented) in the eighth century. In the eleventh century, some churches required clergy thus living together to adopt the rule first proposed by Saint Augustine that they renounce private wealth. Those who embraced this change were known as Augustinians or Canons Regular, whilst those who did not were known as secular canons.",what is a canon priest in the catholic church
what is the government in the united kingdom,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/The_London_Gazette', 'http://sentinels.forumotion.com/t300-government-of-the-united-kingdom', 'https://api.parliament.uk/historic-hansard/commons/2001/dec/03/dissemination-of-information', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/British_government.html', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/British_government', 'https://hunconcourt.hu/about-the-hungarian-legal-system/', 'https://www.wikizero.com/en/Portal:France']","The government is led by the Prime Minister, who selects all the remaining ministers. The prime minister and the other most senior ministers belong to the supreme decision-making committee, known as the Cabinet. The government ministers all sit in Parliament, and are accountable to it. The government is dependent on Parliament to make primary legislation, and since the Fixed-terms Parliaments Act 2011, general elections are held every five years to elect a new House of Commons, unless there is a successful vote of no confidence in the government or a two-thirds vote for a snap election (as was the case in 2017) in the House of Commons, in which case an election may be held sooner. After an election, the monarch (currently Queen Elizabeth II) selects as prime minister the leader of the party most likely to command the confidence of the House of Commons, usually by possessing a majority of MPs.",what is the government in the united kingdom
notre dame in paris is a famous cathedral built in the,"['http://musictick.com/cath%C3%A9drale-notre-dame-de-paris-paris,%20france-locations-classic-music.html?id_luogo=539689&filtro=4&dal=02/12/19', 'http://dannyozzycardsunesco.blogspot.com/2016/07/paris-banks-of-seine.html', 'http://www.toursandtravel.app/en/points-of-interests/paris/notre-dame-de-paris/363', 'http://annaritabarbaccip.blogspot.com/', 'https://www.voyagerschooltravel.com/school-tours-europe/school-trips-france/paris-parle-school-trip/', 'http://www.1000wondersoftheworld.com/details.php?id=5146', 'https://steller.co/s/3hNG3D26nLT']","Notre-Dame de Paris (French: (nɔtʁə dam də paʁi) (listen); meaning ""Our Lady of Paris""), also known as Notre-Dame Cathedral or simply Notre-Dame, is a medieval Catholic cathedral on the Île de la Cité in the fourth arrondissement of Paris, France. The cathedral is widely considered to be one of the finest examples of French Gothic architecture, and it is among the largest and best-known church buildings in the Catholic Church in France, and in the world. The naturalism of its sculptures and stained glass serve to contrast it with earlier Romanesque architecture.",notre dame in paris is a famous cathedral built in the
who split the atom for the first time,"['http://www.gnosis.us.com/category/people/scientists/', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/ernest-rutherford', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Royal_Society', 'https://whyevolutionistrue.wordpress.com/2017/03/29/new-zealand-a-sheep-station-and-mussel-lagniappe/', 'http://tonsoffacts.com/30-fascinating-and-interesting-facts-about-ernest-rutherford/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Arthur_W._Barton', 'http://www.whoinvent.com/who-discovered-proton/']","Rutherford moved in 1907 to the Victoria University of Manchester (today University of Manchester) in the UK, where he and Thomas Royds proved that alpha radiation is helium nuclei. Rutherford performed his most famous work after he became a Nobel laureate. In 1911, although he could not prove that it was positive or negative, he theorized that atoms have their charge concentrated in a very small nucleus, and thereby pioneered the Rutherford model of the atom, through his discovery and interpretation of Rutherford scattering by the gold foil experiment of Hans Geiger and Ernest Marsden. He conducted research that led to the first ""splitting"" of the atom in 1917 in a nuclear reaction between nitrogen and alpha particles, in which he also discovered (and named) the proton.",who split the atom for the first time
what topics are on the usmle step 1,"['https://www.drnajeeblectures.com/usmle', 'https://medschool.vcu.edu/about/deans-office/facultyaffairs/', 'https://www.educationtimes.com/article/44/2008110720081107151947811a152cd78', 'https://www.lecturio.com/usmle-step-1', 'https://ccvr.uic.edu/trainingandeducation/gems.html', 'https://www.hopemedicalinstitute.org/webinar/', 'https://studiesinaustralia.com/courses-in-australia/la-trobe-university/bachelor-of-commercebachelor-of-biomedicine']","Step 1 is designed to test the knowledge learned during the basic science years of medical school as applied in the form of clinical vignettes. This includes anatomy, behavioral sciences, biochemistry, microbiology, pathology, pharmacology, and physiology, as well as to interdisciplinary areas including genetics, aging, immunology, nutrition, and molecular and cell biology. Epidemiology, medical ethics and questions on empathy are also emphasized. Each exam is dynamically generated for each test taker; while the general proportion of questions derived from a particular subject is the same, some test takers report that certain subjects are either emphasized or deemphasized.",what topics are on the usmle step 1
what's the difference between a puma and a mountain lion,"['http://theworldofanimals.proboards.com/thread/661/cougar-deinonychus-antirrhopus', 'https://dramaslovsgmail.wordpress.com/2017/05/03/cougar-%EA%B0%95%EB%8F%99%EC%98%A4%ED%94%BC-%EA%B0%95%EB%8F%99%EA%B1%B4%EB%A7%88-%EC%98%A4%ED%94%BC%EC%93%B0-opss3-com/', 'http://denise.dreamwidth.org/71796.html', 'http://eidmubarak2014.tk/az-46-sheet-pile.html', 'http://explainwell.org/index.php/table-of-contents-synthesize-text/reading-the-text/', 'http://starsica.blogspot.com/2008/12/cougar-puma-concolor-part-i.html', 'http://wildlife-animals.com/cougar/commuter-bags.php']","The cougar (Puma concolor), also commonly known as the mountain lion, puma, panther, or catamount, is a large felid of the subfamily Felinae native to the Americas. Its range, from the Canadian Yukon to the southern Andes of South America, is the most widespread of any large wild terrestrial mammal in the Western Hemisphere. An adaptable, generalist species, the cougar is found in most American habitat types. It is the biggest cat in North America, and the second-heaviest cat in the New World after the jaguar. Secretive and largely solitary by nature, the cougar is properly considered both nocturnal and crepuscular, although daytime sightings do occur. The cougar is more closely related to smaller felines, including the domestic cat (subfamily Felinae), than to any species of subfamily Pantherinae, of which only the jaguar is native to the Americas.",what is the difference between panther and mountain lion
in 1945 the us dropped atomic bombs on the country of,"['https://majormike.us/subjects/atomic-bomb/', 'https://www.astrodocanil.com/2019/04/red-planet-mars-in-rohini-nakshatra-when-100-years-back-ketu-was-in-same-nakshatra-masacre-jallianwala-bagh-astrologer-anil-aggarwala/', 'http://proteinweightlossdiet.net/first-day-on-the-every-other-day-diet-and-hit-a-snag-already/', 'http://ibeacontrends.com/new-south-wales/how-to-make-a-nuclear-bomb.php', 'https://samslifeinjeddah.wordpress.com/tag/annapolis/', 'https://spectrum.ieee.org/aerospace/military/what-about-the-nukes', 'https://www.toptenz.net/10-weapons-changed-history-warfare.php']","During the final stage of World War II, the United States detonated two nuclear weapons over the Japanese cities of Hiroshima and Nagasaki on August 6 and 9, 1945, respectively. The United States dropped the bombs after obtaining the consent of the United Kingdom, as required by the Quebec Agreement. The two bombings killed at least 129,000 people, most of whom were civilians. They remain the only use of nuclear weapons in the history of warfare.",in 1945 the us dropped atomic bombs on the country of
what is coreldraw what are the roles in desktop publishing,"['http://wildrosesnowremoval.com/northwest-territories/how-to-change-pixel-size-in-coreldraw-home-and-student.php', 'https://toolhippo.com/corel-draw-graphics-suite-2019-free-download/', 'http://doublesneak.de/corel-draw-x3-manual-free.html', 'http://breath-of-fresh-air.us/tag/no-survey/page/2/', 'http://www.aswebinfo.com/corel-draw-training-in-mohali.php', 'http://bignedviga.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=10414', 'http://salkantay.info/?newsid=16916']","CorelDraw (styled CorelDRAW) is a vector graphics editor developed and marketed by Corel Corporation. It is also the name of Corel's Graphics Suite, which bundles CorelDraw with bitmap-image editor Corel Photo-Paint as well as other graphics-related programs (see below). The latest version is marketed as Graphics Suite 2017 (equivalent to version 19), and was released in April 2017. CorelDraw is designed to edit two-dimensional images such as logos and posters.",what is coreldraw what are the roles in desktop publishing
who was the jimmy dugan character based on,"['http://www.500hrc.com/500-hrc-articles/some-500-hr-club-members-managed-others-didn-t.html', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Jimmie_Foxx']","Tom Hanks' character Jimmy Dugan in the movie A League of Their Own was largely based on Foxx and Hack Wilson, although the producers took a number of liberties in creating the role.",who was the jimmy dugan character based on
when did samsung come out with smart tv,"['http://1899t.info/?newsid=34067', 'https://tvcomparison.net/samsung-un32j6300-vs-un32h6350-why-the-new-model-is-better/', 'https://tvcomparison.net/samsung-un65j6300-vs-un65j6200-whats-the-reason-to-choose-un65j6300/', 'http://lewistonchamber.org/western-australia/android-tv-box-user-manual-pdf.php', 'https://popularium.com/product/samsung-hdtv/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Samsung_Electronics.html', 'https://naijaquest.com/samsung-offices-in-lagos/']","In 2007, Samsung introduced the Internet TV, enabling the viewer to receive information from the Internet while at the same time watching conventional television programming. Samsung later developed ""Smart LED TV"" (now renamed to ""Samsung Smart TV""), which additionally supports downloaded apps. In 2008, the company launched the Power Infolink service, followed in 2009 by a whole new Internet@TV. In 2010, it started marketing the 3D television while unveiling the upgraded Internet@TV 2010, which offers free (or for-fee) download of applications from its Samsung Apps Store, in addition to existing services such as news, weather, stock market, YouTube videos, and movies.",when did samsung come out with smart tv
who has home ice advantage for stanley cup,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Stanley_Cup_playoffs', 'https://kids.kiddle.co/Stanley_Cup_playoffs', 'http://topofblogs.com/news/stanley-cup-hockey-playoffs/']","In the first two rounds, the higher-seeded team has home-ice advantage (regardless of point record). Thereafter, it goes to the team with the better regular season record (regardless of seeding); in the case of a tie, the league's standard tiebreaking procedure is applied. The team with home-ice advantage hosts games one, two, five, and seven, while the opponent hosts games three, four, and six (games five through seven are played if necessary).",who has home ice advantage for stanley cup
what happens when benzaldehyde is heated with conc. naoh,"['https://www.chemeurope.com/en/encyclopedia/Cannizzaro_reaction.html', 'https://energyfaculty.com/biodiesel/', 'https://classnotes.org.in/class11/chemistry/s-block-elements/chemical-properties-s-block-elements/', 'http://www.siliconagendasetters.com/a00/ani20.htm', 'https://www.speedlabs.in/icse/icse-class-10-chemistry-syllabus.html']","Cannizzaro first accomplished this transformation in 1853, when he obtained benzyl alcohol and potassium benzoate from the treatment of benzaldehyde with potash (potassium carbonate). More typically, the reaction would be conducted with sodium or potassium hydroxide:",what happens when benzaldehyde is heated with conc. naoh
areas near the equator have what kind of climate,"['https://mapuniversal.com/equator-line-countries-on-the-equator/', 'https://www.mapsofworld.com/world-ocean-map.htm', 'http://ed-u.com/background-of-countries-a.htm', 'http://www.hotfreebooks.com/book/The-2001-CIA-World-Factbook-United-States-Central-Intelligence-Agency--3.html', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Equator', 'http://www.physicalgeography.net/physgeoglos/o.html', 'https://www.thoughtco.com/the-new-fifth-ocean-1435095']","The Equator lies mostly on the three largest oceans: the Atlantic Ocean, the Indian Ocean, and the Pacific Ocean. Near the Equator there is little temperature fluctuation throughout the year, though there may be dramatic differences in rainfall and humidity. The terms summer, autumn, winter and spring do not generally apply. Lowlands around the Equator generally have a tropical rainforest climate, also known as an equatorial climate, though cold currents cause some regions to have tropical monsoon climates with a dry season in the middle of the year, and the Somali Current generated by the Asian monsoon due to continental heating via the high Tibetan Plateau causes Greater Somalia to have an arid climate despite its equatorial location.",areas near the equator have what kind of climate
what is a transaction account and why is it a demand deposit,"['https://mgtlocal.net/finance/savings/', 'https://www.homeyapp.net/glossary/', 'https://patents.justia.com/patent/20090164353', 'http://www.coolinterview.com/type.asp?iType=496', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Current_accounts.html', 'https://guardianassetadvisor.com/free-online-business-checking.html', 'http://internet-is.info/?newsid=48855']","A transaction account, checking account, current account or demand deposit account is a deposit account held at a bank or other financial institution. It is available to the account owner ""on demand"" and is available for frequent and immediate access by the account owner or to others as the account owner may direct. Access may be in a variety of ways, such as cash withdrawals, use of cheques (checks) and debit by electronic transfer. In economic terms, the funds held in a transaction account are regarded as liquid funds and in accounting terms they are considered as cash.",what is a transaction account and why is it a demand deposit
how far is central point oregon from medford oregon,"['http://www.wildernessroad-virginia.com/communities/washington-county/', 'https://www.clearviewhorizon.com/therapeutic-boarding-schools-for-girls-in-central-point-oregon/', 'http://runieuws.nl/central-point-oregon-map.html', 'https://www.rongalbreath.com/community/area/Central%20Point/', 'https://www.catrafficticket.com/san-luis-obispo-county/', 'https://www.thenetlender.com/locations/tnl-car-title-loans-richmond-richmond-ave/', 'https://www.catrafficticket.com/san-joaquin-county/']","Central Point is a city in Jackson County, Oregon, United States. The population was 17,169 as of 2010. The city shares its southern border with Medford and is a part of the Medford metropolitan area. Central Point is home of the Jackson County Fair that occurs in July.",how far is central point oregon from medford oregon
what is the purpose of the proclamation of 1763,"['https://bruceonthebruce.wordpress.com/2014/12/14/why-cananda-exists-today-our-true-legal-roots/', 'https://www.constitution150.ca/resources-1/historical-documents/', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Thirteen_Colonies', 'https://www.rbattinglaw.com/american-revolution-date-started/', 'http://www.city-data.com/forum/illegal-immigration/1850331-george-washington-illegal-immigrant.html', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/Ontario', 'https://www.theclassroom.com/american-colonial-perspective-proclamation-1763-9252.html']","The Royal Proclamation of 1763 was issued October 7, 1763, by King George III following Great Britain's acquisition of French territory in North America after the end of the French and Indian War / Seven Years' War, which forbade all settlement west of a line drawn along the Appalachian Mountains. It rendered worthless land grants given by the British government to Americans who fought for the crown against France. The Proclamation angered American colonists who wanted to continue their westward expansion into new farm lands and wanted to keep their control of local government. The Royal Proclamation continues to be of legal importance to First Nations in Canada. The 1763 proclamation line is similar to the Eastern Continental Divide's path running northwards from Georgia to the Pennsylvania -- New York border, and north-eastwards past the drainage divide on the St. Lawrence Divide from there northwards through New England.",what is the purpose of the proclamation of 1763
who is going to the college football national championship,"['http://www.roofapedia.com/Blog/Test-blog/July-2012/Guest-blog-post-Be-Energy-Smart.aspx', 'https://www.spectroom.com/category/171113126-american-football-matches', 'http://www.outandaboutinparis.com/2017/02/saint-valentines-shoulder-blade-is.html', 'https://ticketstub.com/sports/football/college', 'https://zackvogel.com/files/webDesign/studentProject2/NCAAChamp.html', 'https://nationalfinals-rodeo.de/tag/national-championship-2019/', 'http://intertwingly.net/blog/2015/01/28/Email-addresses']","The 2018 College Football Playoff National Championship is a college football bowl game that will determine the national champion in the NCAA Division I Football Bowl Subdivision for the 2017 season. It will be played at Mercedes-Benz Stadium in Atlanta, Georgia on January 8, 2018. As part of a three-year rotation, the game will be played between the winners of two semi-final bowl games which will be played on January 1, 2018: the Rose Bowl Game, and the Sugar Bowl. The participants in these two games will be determined following the conclusion of the 2017 regular season.",who is going to the college football national championship
what level of government is the prime minister,"['https://en.metapedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister', 'https://thesounddesignerblog.com/cape-breton-university-eassy-assignment-pols-2118-submitted-by/', 'https://www.mount-vema.com/prime-minister.html', 'https://college-papers-1.com/government-3/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Gangtok', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Government_of_India', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Prime_Minister_of_Nepal']","A prime minister, also known as a premier, is the head of a cabinet and the leader of the ministers in the executive branch of government, often in a parliamentary or semi-presidential system. In many systems, the prime minister selects and may dismiss other members of the cabinet, and allocates posts to members within the government. In most systems, the prime minister is the presiding member and chairman of the cabinet. In a minority of systems, notably in semi-presidential systems of government, a prime minister is the official who is appointed to manage the civil service and execute the directives of the head of state.",what level of government is the prime minister
who plays bones in the new star trek movies,"['http://www.karlurban.net/karl-urban-biography', 'http://urbanfantasies.net/']","In 2009, he played Dr. Leonard ""Bones"" McCoy, a role famously originated by DeForest Kelley, in the eleventh Star Trek film. A fan of the Star Trek franchise since childhood, Urban actively pursued a role in the film. His performance was widely embraced by the Star Trek fan community for its faithfulness to the spirit of Kelley's McCoy. In 2009, he also appeared as himself in the documentary film Reclaiming the Blade, discussing his sword-wielding experience in films such as The Lord of the Rings.",who plays bones in the new star trek movies
