what were the roots of the blues aesthetic,"['https://www.thebluesguitarist.net/easy-blues-acoustic-guitar-lesson/', 'http://www.writeopinions.com/blues-music', 'http://yiju.info/news.php?action=show&id=42548', 'https://wikimili.com/en/The_Black_Keys', 'http://little-merlins-frangula.tk/rocky-theme-song-sheet-music-trumpet.html', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Coathanger_Antennae', 'http://ajaxnetwerk.tk/chamber-blues-string-quartet-sheet.html']","Blues is a music genre and musical form originated by African Americans in the Deep South of the United States around the end of the 19th century. The genre developed from roots in African musical traditions, African-American work songs, spirituals, and the folk music of white Americans of European heritage. Blues incorporated spirituals, work songs, field hollers, shouts, chants, and rhymed simple narrative ballads. The blues form, ubiquitous in jazz, rhythm and blues and rock and roll, is characterized by the call-and-response pattern, the blues scale and specific chord progressions, of which the twelve-bar blues is the most common. Blue notes (or ""worried notes""), usually thirds or fifths flattened in pitch, are also an essential part of the sound. Blues shuffles or walking bass reinforce the trance-like rhythm and form a repetitive effect known as the groove.",what were the roots of the blues aesthetic
where is the information actually held within a dna molecule,"['http://www.ihcworld.com/smf/index.php?topic=6751.0', 'http://collegeinspector.com/engineering/biotechnology.php', 'http://en.turkcewiki.org/wiki/Life', 'http://kidpid.com/is-dna-the-future-of-data-storage/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/F-type_main-sequence_star', 'https://www.biospace.com/article/ambry-genetics-makes-advances-in-rna-genetic-testing/', 'http://richardmckie.net/index.php/travel/south-america']","DNA stores biological information. The DNA backbone is resistant to cleavage, and both strands of the double-stranded structure store the same biological information. This information is replicated as and when the two strands separate. A large part of DNA (more than 98% for humans) is non-coding, meaning that these sections do not serve as patterns for protein sequences.",where is the information actually held within a dna molecule
what's the difference between a graphic novel and a comic,"['http://celebrityenglish-alex.blogspot.com/2013/07/dragon.html', 'https://infernodotblog.wordpress.com/2017/11/04/dante-and-graphic-novels/', 'https://www.perkycoupons.com/blog/', 'http://comicsblog.uk.eu.org/index.php?SpecialSitePage=11', 'https://www.comicsineducation.com/home/comics-terminology-for-teachers-part-1-defining-the-genre', 'http://www.just-passing-thru.com/2013/10/', 'http://en.citizendium.org/wiki/Comics']","A graphic novel is a book made up of comics content. Although the word ""novel"" normally refers to long fictional works, the term ""graphic novel"" is applied broadly and includes fiction, non-fiction, and anthologized work. It is distinguished from the term ""comic book"", which is generally used for comics periodicals.",what's the difference between a graphic novel and a comic
who is performed at the super bowl 2017,"['http://ricknicholsonline.com/2016/09/labor-day-wishes.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/NRG_Stadium', 'https://www.sportsdisplaycases.com/football/nfl-super-bowl/sb51', 'http://www.bbcnewspoint.com/lady-gaga-to-rock-in-super-bowl-halftime-show-2017/', 'https://www.houstonrodeoonline.com/houston-rodeo-tickets/artist/Luke-Bryan.php']","The Super Bowl LI Halftime show took place on February 5, 2017, at NRG Stadium in Houston, Texas as part of Super Bowl LI. The show was headlined by Lady Gaga, who performed a medley of her songs, including newer material from her most recent studio album Joanne.",who is performed at the super bowl 2017
marsupials are found in north america and australia,"['https://www.koalaactioninc.org/glossary.php', 'https://evolution-outreach.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12052-016-0062-y', 'https://www.answers.com/Q/What_can_you_do_in_Venezuela', 'https://www.whatarethe7continents.com/comment-page-6/', 'http://www.empken.com/wiki/index.php5?title=Grey_Goshawk&amp;diff=prev&amp;oldid=5430', 'http://www.climateplus.info/2013/05/10/climate-clippings-73/', 'https://www.sustainableharvest.org/blog/celebrating-world-wildlife-day']","Marsupials represent the clade originating from the last common ancestor of extant metatherians. Like other mammals in the Metatheria, they give birth to relatively undeveloped young that often reside with the mother in a pouch, for a certain amount of time. Close to 70% of the 334 extant species occur on the Australian continent (the mainland, Tasmania, New Guinea and nearby islands). The remaining 100 are found in the Americas -- primarily in South America, but thirteen in Central America, and one in North America, north of Mexico.",marsupials are found in north america and australia
who is the guy who sings beauty school dropout,"['https://kanthaka.eu/frankie-avalon-casino.html', 'https://www.all-about-vinylrecords.com/frankie-avalon-oldies-music-lyrics.html', 'https://www.vintagemusic.fm/artist/12111/']","Materializing as a character called Teen Angel, his performance of ""Beauty School Dropout"" in the hit 1978 film of the musical Grease introduced Avalon to a new generation of viewers.",who is the guy who sings beauty school dropout
what are the main functions of the unep,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Ozone', 'https://www.greenkey.global/institutional-partners/', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Coral_bleaching', 'https://ngojobsinafrica.com/non-profit-organization/united-nations-environment-programme/', 'http://santodaime.eu/67547-the-nations-environmental-policy/', 'https://www.goingtruegreen.com/gtg-blog/category/united-nations', 'http://www.bcompetitive.in/google-partners-with-united-nations-to-monitor-human-impact-on-the-environment/']","The United Nations Environment Programme is an agency of United Nations and coordinates its environmental activities, assisting developing countries in implementing environmentally sound policies and practices. It was founded by Maurice Strong, its first director, as a result of the United Nations Conference on the Human Environment (Stockholm Conference) in June 1972 and has overall responsibility for environmental problems among United Nations agencies but international talks on specialized issues, such as addressing climate change or combating desertification, are overseen by other UN organizations, like the Bonn-based Secretariat of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change and the United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification. UN Environment activities cover a wide range of issues regarding the atmosphere, marine and terrestrial ecosystems, environmental governance and green economy. It has played a significant role in developing international environmental conventions, promoting environmental science and information and illustrating the way those can be implemented in conjunction with policy, working on the development and implementation of policy with national governments, regional institutions in conjunction with environmental non-governmental organizations (NGOs). UN Environment has also been active in funding and implementing environment related development projects.","Green Key — Institutional Partners Institutional Partners The Foundation for Environmental Education is partnered with some of the world's foremost organisations in the fields of education and the environment. These illustrious partners include UNESCO, UNEP, UNWTO, ISESCO, YMP and Earth Charter.The Foundation for Environmental Education has a signed Memorandum of Understanding with UNESCO, UNEP, ISESCO and, most recently, the Caribbean Hotel and Tourism Association (CHTA) which recognises the innate value of the hospitality and tourism sustainability initiatives introduced to the Caribbean by FEE, through the Green Key and Blue Flag programmes. In 2017, Green Key signed an agreement with Surrey University. Caribbean Hotel & Tourism AssociationThe Caribbean Hotel and Tourism Association (CHTA) is a not-for-profit corporation that aims to facilitate the full potential of the Caribbean hotel & tourism industry by serving member needs and building partnerships in a socially responsible and sustainable manner. UN TourismThe World Tourism Organization (UN Tourism) is the United Nations agency charged with the promotion of responsible, sustainable and universally accessible tourism. It is the leading international organisation in the field of tourism, which promotes the sector as a driver of economic growth, inclusive development and environmental sustainability and offers leadership and support in advancing knowledge and tourism policies worldwide. University of SurreyThe University of Surrey is a public research university located in the South East of England (United Kingdom). The university is ranked #5 in the world in tourism, hospitality and events. The School of Hospitality and Tourism Management at the University of Surrey works with Green Key on research related to monitoring and evaluation of the effect of sustainability programmes.University of West Indies, St. Augustine CampusThe Faculty of Social Sciences is the largest Faculty in the University of the West Indies, St. Augustine Campus comprising four departments including– the Department of Behavioural Sciences, the Department of Economics, the Department of Management Studies, and the Department of Political Science. Their vision is to be socially engaged, and solutions oriented by focusing on lifelong learning for sustainable impact."
where is austria located in the world map,"['http://www.catdrivers.com/Austria.html', 'https://clipstogo.at/europe/austria/', 'https://www.wallpaperpimper.com/location/countries/austria', 'https://www.bucketlist127.com/goal/visit-austria', 'https://www.mapsland.com/europe/austria', 'https://www.aircharteradvisors.com/private-jet-charter/austria/', 'http://5starseurope.com/en/austria/']","Austria (/ ˈɒstriə, ˈɔː-/ (listen); German: Österreich (ˈøːstɐˌʁaɪç) (listen)), officially the Republic of Austria (German: Republik Österreich, listen (help info)), is a federal republic and a landlocked country of over 8.7 million people in Central Europe. It is bordered by the Czech Republic and Germany to the north, Hungary and Slovakia to the east, Slovenia and Italy to the south, and Switzerland and Liechtenstein to the west. The territory of Austria covers 83,879 km (32,386 sq mi). The terrain is highly mountainous, lying within the Alps; only 32% of the country is below 500 m (1,640 ft), and its highest point is 3,798 m (12,461 ft). The majority of the population speaks local Bavarian dialects of German as their native language, and German in its standard form is the country's official language. Other local official languages are Hungarian, Burgenland Croatian, and Slovene.",where is austria located in the world map
who stars in the new power rangers movie,"['http://fairer.info/viewtopic.php?t=48420', 'http://whozwholive.ning.com/profiles/blogs/power-rangers-1', 'http://raphd.com/yukon/power-ranger-story-book-pdf.php', 'http://maciepabst.freeiz.com/?view=russkiy_2017_power_dvd', 'http://yiju.info/news.php?action=show&id=96', 'https://movieweb.com/power-rangers-beauty-and-beast-2017-box-office-predictions/', 'https://www.earnthenecklace.com/power-rangers-end-credits-scene-explained-the-past-throws-a-hint-about-the-future/']","Saban's Power Rangers (or simply Power Rangers) is a 2017 American superhero film based on the franchise of the same name, directed by Dean Israelite and written by John Gatins. It is the third Power Rangers film, and is a reboot. The film features the main characters of the Mighty Morphin Power Rangers television series with a new cast, starring Dacre Montgomery, Naomi Scott, RJ Cyler, Becky G, Ludi Lin, Bill Hader, Bryan Cranston, and Elizabeth Banks.",who stars in the new power rangers movie
what is the difference between hunter gatherers and farmers,"['https://courses.lumenlearning.com/boundless-sociology/chapter/the-transformation-of-economic-systems/', 'https://rashidfaridi.com/2019/04/04/peopling-of-india-indians-are-a-truly-mixed-people/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'http://cannoncounty.info/viewtopic.php?t=49210', 'https://carta.anthropogeny.org/glossary?page=1', 'http://paniit2008.org/FarmAnimals/animals-used-in-farming', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Grand_Teton_National_Park', 'https://edu.glogster.com/glog/russian-architecture/2a86gtvcq86?=glogpedia-source']","A hunter-gatherer is a human living in a society in which most or all food is obtained by foraging (collecting wild plants and pursuing wild animals), in contrast to agricultural societies, which rely mainly on domesticated species.",what is the difference between hunter gatherers and farmers
what are the bordering states of new york,"['https://www.crowdfundconnect.com/crowdfunding/new-york/', 'http://newyorkcityjob.net/new-york/', 'https://travelo.club/en/guide/city/579-new-york', 'http://tnkpps.info/busty/kattskill-bay-ny-single-gay-men&p=961.php', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Kankakee_County,_Illinois', 'http://flyingnorth.net/2015/02/08/seven-in-one-north-america/', 'http://www.answering-services-phone-messaging.com/New_York.html']","New York has a diverse geography. The state is bordered by New Jersey and Pennsylvania to the south and Connecticut, Massachusetts, and Vermont to the east. The state has a maritime border with Rhode Island, east of Long Island, as well as an international border with the Canadian provinces of Quebec to the north and Ontario to the northwest. The southern part of the state is in the Atlantic Coastal Plain and includes Long Island and several smaller associated islands, as well as New York City and the lower Hudson River Valley. The large Upstate New York region comprises several ranges of the wider Appalachian Mountains, and the Adirondack Mountains in the Northeastern lobe of the state. Two major river valleys -- the north-south Hudson River Valley and the east-west Mohawk River Valley -- bisect these more mountainous regions. Western New York is considered part of the Great Lakes Region and borders Lake Ontario, Lake Erie, and Niagara Falls. The central part of the state is dominated by the Finger Lakes, a popular vacation and tourist destination.",what are the bordering states of new york
when do the christmas markets begin in germany,"['https://mirellamccracken.wordpress.com/2012/12/', 'https://housefenway.com/tag/holidays/page/3/', 'https://www.redsevenleisure.co.uk/ideas/news/christmas-markets-with-red7/', 'https://thetrraveller.com/christmas-in-london/?shared=email&msg=fail', 'http://johnlrakestraw.com/village-green-resort-brings-life-old-world-christmas-markets/', 'http://newsletter.goethehyderabad.com/2014/', 'https://www.recycledbyrobin.com/events-1/2018/12/15/weihachtsmarkt-2018']","In many towns in Germany, Switzerland, and Austria, Advent is usually ushered in with the opening of the Christmas market or ""Weihnachtsmarkt"". In southern Germany, Switzerland and Austria, it is called a ""Christkind (e) l(s) (i) markt"" (German language, literally meaning ""Christ child market""). Traditionally held in the town square, the market has food, drink and seasonal items from open-air stalls accompanied by traditional singing and dancing. On opening night at the Christkindlesmarkt in Nuremberg, and in some other towns, onlookers welcome the ""Christkind"" (originally boy Jesus, but often depicted as an angel-like girl), acted out by a local child.",when do the christmas markets begin in germany
what is the defining element of a society,"['http://chartsbin.com/view/41328', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Social_science', 'http://www.mediathinkers.org/responsible_marketing.html', 'https://frontview.wordpress.com/society/', 'https://www.peoplespedia.org/wiki/Portal:Society', 'https://myproject.com.ng/products/role-cooperative-societies-nigeria-economy-case-study-cooperative-societies/', 'https://cosma.org/society/']","A society is a group of people involved in persistent social interaction, or a large social group sharing the same geographical or social territory, typically subject to the same political authority and dominant cultural expectations. Societies are characterized by patterns of relationships (social relations) between individuals who share a distinctive culture and institutions; a given society may be described as the sum total of such relationships among its constituent of members. In the social sciences, a larger society often evinces stratification or dominance patterns in subgroups.",what is the defining element of a society
where is the grey matter of the spinal cord located,"['https://reliawire.com/grey-matter/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Generalized_anxiety_disorder', 'https://www.imaios.com/en/e-Anatomy/Anatomical-Parts/Grey-substance5', 'http://www.scholarpedia.org/article/Spinal_cord']","Grey matter in the spinal cord is known as the grey column which travels down the spinal cord distributed in three grey columns that are presented in an ""H"" shape. The forward-facing column is the anterior grey column, the rear-facing one is the posterior grey column and the interlinking one is the lateral grey column. The grey matter on the left and right side is connected by the grey commissure. The grey matter in the spinal cord consists of interneurons, as well as the cell bodies of projection neurons.",where is the grey matter of the spinal cord located
when did the middle ages end and the renaissance began,"['https://en.m.wikiquote.org/wiki/Renaissance', 'http://www.counterspace.us/typography/timeline/', 'https://wn.com/Renaissance_design_studios?upload_time=all_time&orderby=relevance', 'https://juan-esteve-photo.format.com/3145237-renaissance', 'https://kidskonnect.com/history/renaissance/', 'https://themakeupgallery.info/period/renaissance/index.htm', 'https://www.ballardier.com/collections/maverick-series/products/renaissance']","The Renaissance (UK: / rɪˈneɪsəns /, US: / rɛnəˈsɑːns /) was a period in European history, from the 14th to the 17th century, regarded as the cultural bridge between the Middle Ages and modern history. It started as a cultural movement in Italy in the Medieval period and later spread to the rest of Europe, marking the beginning of the Modern age.",when did the middle ages end and the renaissance began
what poem inspired a raisin in the sun,"['http://www.kolumnmagazine.com/2016/05/19/chicago-celebrates-playwright-lorraine-hansberrys-life/', 'http://www.kolumnmagazine.com/2017/05/08/playwright-activist-lorraine-hansberry-young-gifted-black-new-york-amsterdam-news/', 'https://madison365.com/staged-reading-of-a-raisin-in-the-sun/', 'https://www.rubinjen.com/madison-social-action/category/all', 'https://www.educationindex.com/essay/Sun-Hydraulics-PKPMNQ6B4Z', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/A_Raisin_in_the_Sun', 'https://ourfaveplaces.co.uk/meet-the-locals/eclipse/']","A Raisin in the Sun is a play by Lorraine Hansberry that debuted on Broadway in 1959. The title comes from the poem ""Harlem"" (also known as ""A Dream Deferred"") by Langston Hughes. The story tells of a black family's experiences in the Washington Park Subdivision of Chicago's Woodlawn neighborhood as they attempt to ""better"" themselves with an insurance payout following the death of the father. The New York Drama Critics' Circle named it the best play of 1959.",what poem inspired a raisin in the sun
how many seasons are there in nurse jackie,"['http://boyaqq.ga/nyki/series-nurse-jackie-hoxa.php', 'https://allstarpics.famousfix.com/pictures/maron', 'https://www.livingordead.com/content/tv/maron', 'https://www.stitcher.com/podcast/the-verge/verge-esp', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Diego_Klattenhoff', 'https://some-assembly-required.fandom.com/wiki/Some_Assembly_Required', 'http://www.wholesalehotdvd.com/The-Chi-Seasons-1-2-dvd-box-set-p-3205.html']","Nurse Jackie is an American medical comedy-drama series. It premiered on Showtime on June 8, 2009. The show's seventh and final season premiered on April 12, 2015. The series finale aired on June 28, 2015.",how many seasons are there in nurse jackie
who is the acting prime minister of india,"['https://www.thisismyindia.com/chhattisgarh/news.html', 'https://thediplomat.com/2017/05/modis-strategic-foreign-policy-vision-a-glass-half-full/', 'https://nexia.com/insights/global-insight/doing-business-in-india-gets-easier-under-new-government/', 'https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/home/lok-sabha-elections-2014/news/Narendra-Modi-appointed-Prime-Minister-swearing-in-on-May-26/articleshow/35388297.cms', 'https://www.asiapacific.ca/canada-asia-agenda/modi-government-india-tough-road-ahead-economic-reforms', 'https://www.theindiapost.com/nation/narendra-modi-appointed-prime-minister-of-india/', 'https://www.indiagk.net/2014/05/narendra-modi-sworn-in-as-15th-prime.html']",The incumbent Prime Minister of India is Narendra Modi who has headed the BJP-led NDA government since 26 May 2014 which is India's first non-Congress single party majority government.,who is the acting prime minister of india
how many types of senses do we have,"['http://vivianlawry.com/body-awareness/', 'http://workflow.arts.ac.uk/view/view.php?id=120359&offset=270', 'http://www.silent-partners.co.uk/appendix', 'http://artandpopularculture.com/Senses', 'https://www.totalmsk.co.uk/sportsinjuryblog/articles/sportsinjury/ankleinjuries.html', 'http://sashnka.com/Taste_perception.html', 'http://highearthorbit.com/articles/collective-intelligence-a-camp']","Humans have a multitude of sensors. Sight (vision), hearing (audition), taste (gustation), smell (olfaction), and touch (somatosensation) are the five traditionally recognized senses. The ability to detect other stimuli beyond those governed by these most broadly recognized senses also exists, and these sensory modalities include temperature (thermoception), kinesthetic sense (proprioception), pain (nociception), balance (equilibrioception), vibration (mechanoreception), and various internal stimuli (e.g. the different chemoreceptors for detecting salt and carbon dioxide concentrations in the blood, or sense of hunger and sense of thirst). However, what constitutes a sense is a matter of some debate, leading to difficulties in defining what exactly a distinct sense is, and where the borders between responses to related stimuli lie.",how many types of senses do we have
what do you understand by rumen and rumination,"['http://www.happybeef.com/happy-beef/', 'https://acmathur.me/bio-degradable/polypropylene-film-replacement', 'https://agricarib.org/products/sheep-goats', 'http://patrickrhone.com/2013/05/15/ruminating/', 'https://psychology.wikia.org/wiki/Ruminants', 'https://ejje.weblio.jp/content/ruminant', 'https://kids.spcaeducation.org.nz/animal-care/cows/freedom-from-hunger-and-thirst/']","Ruminants are mammals that are able to acquire nutrients from plant-based food by fermenting it in a specialized stomach prior to digestion, principally through microbial actions. The process, which takes place in the front part of the digestion system and therefore is called foregut fermentation, typically requires the fermented ingesta (known as cud) to be regurgitated and chewed again. The process of rechewing the cud to further break down plant matter and stimulate digestion is called rumination. The word ""ruminant"" comes from the Latin ruminare, which means ""to chew over again"".",what do you understand by rumen and rumination
what connects the tongue to the floor of the mouth,"['https://www.atlantaperiodontics.com/frenectomy/frenectomy-tongue-tied/', 'https://www.olypd.com/services-frame/?page=frenectomy.php', 'https://med.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Anatomy_and_Physiology/Book%3A_Anatomy_and_Physiology_(OpenStax)/Unit_5%3A_Energy%2C_Maintenance%2C_and_Environmental_Exchange/23%3A_The_Digestive_System/23.03%3A_The_Mouth%2C_Pharynx%2C_and_Esophagus', 'https://www.regaldentistry.net/services-frame/?page=frenectomy.php', 'https://www.cldc.com.au/services/specialist/tongue-tie/', 'http://www.belairdentalcare.net/tongue-tie/', 'http://www.dentalimplant.com.es/articulos/beyond_teeth.html']",The frenulum of tongue or tongue web (also lingual frenulum or frenulum linguæ; also fraenulum) is a small fold of mucous membrane extending from the floor of the mouth to the midline of the underside of the tongue.,what connects the tongue to the floor of the mouth
where is south africa located on a map,"['https://antheamay.com/seo-south-africa/economic-background-south-africa/', 'http://za.wowcity.com/southafrica/', 'https://www.aircharteradvisors.com/private-jet-charter/south-africa/', 'https://vectormap.info/product/printable-map-south-africa-exact-vector-map-adobe-illustrator-editable-full-vector/', 'https://www.ethiousatour.com/tours/south-africa-2/', 'http://www.studybooking.com/country/southafrica', 'http://rasoitravel.blogspot.com/2016/']","South Africa, officially the Republic of South Africa (RSA), is the southernmost country in Africa. It is bounded on the south by 2,798 kilometres (1,739 mi) of coastline of Southern Africa stretching along the South Atlantic and Indian Oceans; on the north by the neighbouring countries of Namibia, Botswana, and Zimbabwe; and on the east and northeast by Mozambique and Swaziland; and surrounds the kingdom of Lesotho. South Africa is the 25th-largest country in the world by land area, with close to 56 million people, is the world's 24th-most populous nation and the largest in Southern Africa. It is the southernmost country on the mainland of the Old World or the Eastern Hemisphere. About 80 percent of South Africans are of Sub-Saharan African ancestry, divided among a variety of ethnic groups speaking different African languages, nine of which have official status. The remaining population consists of Africa's largest communities of European (white), Asian (Indian), and multiracial (coloured) ancestry.",where is south africa located on a map
what does it mean for waves to be in phase,"['https://www.assignmentexpert.com/homework-answers/physics/optics/question-25610', 'http://www.leonworldwide.com/finding-quantum-physics-definition-on-the-web-19/', 'http://businessingear.com/2019/03/28/the-secrets-of-quantum-physics-definition-exposed/', 'http://www.cafedealtura.com/cafe-de-altura/the-do-this-get-that-guide-on-what-does-quantum-mean-2.php', 'http://strikeforcemechanical.com/2019/04/15/the-do-this-get-that-guide-on-what-does-quantum-mean/', 'http://nangmuibocsun.com/the-debate-over-what-does-quantum-mean.html', 'http://hernefestehayat.com/author/yazaromer2/']","Phase difference is the difference, expressed in degrees or time, between two waves having the same frequency and referenced to the same point in time. Two oscillators that have the same frequency and no phase difference are said to be in phase. Two oscillators that have the same frequency and different phases have a phase difference, and the oscillators are said to be out of phase with each other.",what does it mean for waves to be in phase
what is the difference between min and max function,"['http://courses.aiu.edu/MATHEMATICS.html', 'http://lewistonchamber.org/victoria/application-of-maxima-and-minima-in-daily-life-pdf.php', 'https://www.educator.com/mathematics/calculus-i/switkes/absolute-minima-and-maxima.php', 'https://autoaiuto.info/0c810986.html', 'http://www.ipumusings.com/', 'https://wn.com/Minimize_your_payment?upload_time=all_time&orderby=rating']","In mathematical analysis, the maxima and minima (the respective plurals of maximum and minimum) of a function, known collectively as extrema (the plural of extremum), are the largest and smallest value of the function, either within a given range (the local or relative extrema) or on the entire domain of a function (the global or absolute extrema). Pierre de Fermat was one of the first mathematicians to propose a general technique, adequality, for finding the maxima and minima of functions.",what is the difference between min and max function
