what type of genre is lana del rey,['https://whspawprint.com/2019/01/27/the-young-beautiful-and-sad/'],"Associated with several styles, Del Rey's music has been tagged broadly as dream pop or baroque pop linked to various forms of rock, indie music, and trip hop, and often touching on styles such as hip hop, trap music, and psychedelic rock on particular releases. Of Born to Die, indie music journal Drowned in Sound wrote, ""She likes that whole hip hop thing though, has this whole swagger thing going that not many girls like her got"", adding that it sounded like a poppier Bond soundtrack.",what type of genre is lana del rey
why is there a bee on the manchester,"['https://popuppainting.com/2018/09/manchester-bee-with-inspiration-from-banksy/', 'https://theident.gallery/bbc1-2017-special.php', 'https://www.sdworx.co.uk/blog/let-us-tell-you-a-beeautiful-story', 'http://www.salefc.com/sponsor/beemanc?sp_year=2019&sp_month=3', 'https://www.96fm.ie/buzz/ariana-grande-s-subtle-tribute-to-manchester-in-ne/', 'https://www.hmc.org.uk/autumn-conference-2018/autumn-conference-2018-venue/', 'https://articles.aplus.com/a/ariana-grande-get-well-soon-track-length-manchester']","The worker bee is one of the best-known symbols of Manchester. It was adopted as a motif for Manchester during the Industrial Revolution, at a time when Manchester was taking a leading role in new forms of mass production, and symbolises Mancunians' hard work during this era and Manchester being a hive of activity in the 19th century.",why is there a bee on the manchester
in the most dangerous game what is the most dangerous game,"['https://www.globalgreyebooks.com/most-dangerous-game-ebook.html', 'https://www.activelylearn.com/catalog-texts/the-most-dangerous-game', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=the+most+dangerous+game+short+story+pdf&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'http://welladjustedbabies.com/new-south-wales/richard-connell-the-most-dangerous-game-pdf.php', 'http://donovanmeggs.host22.com/igru-success-story-russkaya-versiya/', 'https://www.legimi.pl/ebook-the-most-dangerous-game-richard-connell-s-original-masterpiece-richard-connell,b275426.html', 'http://www.booksthatgrow.com/the-most-dangerous-game/']","""The Most Dangerous Game"", also published as ""The Hounds of Zaroff"", is a short story by Richard Connell, first published in Collier's on January 19, 1924. The story features a big-game hunter from New York City who falls off a yacht and swims to what seems to be an abandoned and isolated island in the Caribbean, where he is hunted by a Russian aristocrat. The story is inspired by the big-game hunting safaris in Africa and South America that were particularly fashionable among wealthy Americans in the 1920s.",in the most dangerous game what is the most dangerous game
who is the actor who plays the good doctor,"['https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=doctorsadvert.com&ads=1&title=Doctors+advert&auto=Doctors+advert&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Doctors+advert&pagenum=4', 'https://www.sirial365.com/2017/09/freddie-highmore-good-doctor.html', 'https://celebsline.com/freddie-highmore/']","Highmore starred as Norman Bates in the A&E drama-thriller series Bates Motel (2013 -- 2017), for which he was nominated three times for the Critics' Choice Television Award for Best Actor in a Drama Series and won a People's Choice Award. In 2017, Highmore began producing and starring as Dr. Shaun Murphy in the ABC drama series The Good Doctor, for which he was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Actor.",who is the actor who plays the good doctor
journey to the centre of the earth novel,"['http://herbzinser.tripod.com/science03/index.blog/2297284/herbert-spencer-internal-earth-iron-core-messages/', 'http://classic-books.org/a-journey-to-the-center-of-the-earth-audio/', 'http://www.ozrk.tw/soft/fiction/booklist/692.html', 'https://ebfinder.com/book/the-three-musketeers-190120193200933.html', 'https://www.largeprintbookco.com/large-print-book-company-catalog/large-print-softcover-books/large-print-adventure-suspense-titles/4058-journey-to-the-center.html', 'https://www.lovereading4kids.co.uk/author/1110/Jules-Verne.html', 'https://zinser.jimdo.com/intellectual-products/earth-systems/earth-iron-copper-navigation-grid/']","Journey to the Center of the Earth (French: Voyage au centre de la Terre, also translated under the titles A Journey to the Centre of the Earth and A Journey to the Interior of the Earth) is an 1864 science fiction novel by Jules Verne. The story involves German professor Otto Lidenbrock who believes there are volcanic tubes going toward the centre of the Earth. He, his nephew Axel, and their guide Hans descend into the Icelandic volcano Snæfellsjökull, encountering many adventures, including prehistoric animals and natural hazards, before eventually coming to the surface again in southern Italy, at the Stromboli volcano.",journey to the centre of the earth novel
where is abbey road the beatles walked across,"['https://www.dreamstime.com/cover-famous-beatles-abbey-road-album-turntable-foreground-naples-image135052556', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Category:English_Heritage_sites_in_London', 'http://www.alanyacruiseport.com/en/52/off-the-beaten-track', 'https://fineartamerica.com/featured/abbey-road-crossing-chris-thaxter.html?product=art-print', 'http://www.metroeasy.com/london-tube-station-near-abbey-road.html', 'https://www.amazingmoves.co.uk/north-london/removals-st-johns-wood-nw8-nw3-nw6-manandvan.html', 'https://www.bowzwestchester.org/2018/02/gateless-gate-48-book-of-serenity-61.html']","Abbey Road is a thoroughfare in the borough of Camden and the City of Westminster in London, running roughly northwest to southeast through St. John's Wood, near Lord's Cricket Ground. It is part of the B507 road. This road is best known for the Abbey Road Studios and the 1969 album, Abbey Road, by The Beatles.",where is abbey road the beatles walked across
in the 8-bit signed 2’s complement representation the number of distinct numbers is,"['http://www.acorn-kernel.net/kernelunleashed/readarticle?ClassKey=ahJzfmFjb3JuLWtlcm5lbC1ocmRyDwsSB0FydGljbGUYybUQDA', 'https://www.d2l.ai/chapter_linear-networks/fashion-mnist.html', 'https://www.emusician.com/gear/making-waves', 'http://zx.rs/3/', 'https://www.computerlanguage.com/results.php?definition=integer', 'http://www.ntu.edu.sg/home/ehchua/programming/java/DataRepresentation.html', 'https://jarrodparkes.com/2013/12/13/data-representation/']","In two's complement notation, a non-negative number is represented by its ordinary binary representation; in this case, the most significant bit is 0. Though, the range of numbers represented is not the same as with unsigned binary numbers. For example, an 8-bit unsigned number can represent the values 0 to 255 (11111111). However a two's complement 8-bit number can only represent positive integers from 0 to 127 (01111111), because the rest of the bit combinations with the most significant bit as' 1' represent the negative integers − 1 to − 128.",in the 8-bit signed 2’s complement representation the number of distinct numbers is
what was the purpose of the third battle of ypres,"['http://orenstein6.blogspot.com/2014/09/', 'http://kieranmccarthy.ie/?p=13293', 'http://www.primidi.com/battle_of_passchendaele', 'http://yeovilhistory.info/ewens-lionelrichard.htm', 'http://www.hethe.org/about-hethe/the-war-years/', 'http://yeovilhistory.info/milton-john.htm', 'https://wartimes.ca/battle/world-war-i/battle-of-passchendaele/']","The Battle of Passchendaele (German: Flandernschlacht, French: Deuxième Bataille des Flandres), also known as the Third Battle of Ypres, was a campaign of the First World War, fought by the Allies against the German Empire. The battle took place on the Western Front, from July to November 1917, for control of the ridges south and east of the Belgian city of Ypres in West Flanders, as part of a strategy decided by the Allies at conferences in November 1916 and May 1917. Passchendaele lay on the last ridge east of Ypres, 5 mi (8.0 km) from a railway junction at Roulers, which was vital to the supply system of the German 4th Army. The next stage of the Allied plan was an advance to Thourout -- Couckelaere, to close the German-controlled railway running through Roulers and Thourout.",what was the purpose of the third battle of ypres
what's the difference between ox and bull,"['http://www.pngall.com/ox-animal-png', 'http://pyhiyolu.j.pl/884g-39.html', 'http://www.whatdoeat.com/whatdooxeneat.html', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Ox_(zodiac)', 'https://codepoints.net/U+1F402', 'http://osbfxzm.wz.sk/152-essay-on-ox-in-hindi.php']","An ox (plural oxen), also known as a bullock in Australia and India, is a bovine trained as a draft animal or riding animal. Oxen are commonly castrated adult male cattle; castration makes the animals easier to control. Cows (adult females) or bulls (intact males) may also be used in some areas.",what's the difference between ox and bull
where is prague czech republic on a world map,"['https://www.travelshelper.com/destinations/europe/czech-republic/prague/', 'https://hoteldonor.com/destination/prague/', 'http://easysegway.com/where-is-prague-located/']","Prague is situated on the Vltava river, at 50 ° 05 ""N and 14 ° 27"" E. in the centre of the Bohemian Basin. Prague is approximately at the same latitude as Frankfurt, Germany; Paris, France; and Vancouver, Canada.",where is prague czech republic on a world map
what is meant by the idea that mass is conserved,"['http://sammypiccolo.com/saskatchewan/law-of-conservation-of-mass-lab-pdf.php', 'https://www.debate.org/debates/Gods-existence-is-intrinsically-impossible/1/', 'https://doctorstrangemind.com/2017/11/17/far-beneath-the-abysmal-sea/', 'https://www.nuclear-power.net/laws-of-conservation/law-of-conservation-of-matter/', 'https://www.instructables.com/member/clay.in.co/', 'https://myhomeworkhelp.com/conservation-matter-homework-answers/', 'http://www.paradocracy.com/2019/02/whos-to-blame-for-poverty.html']","The law of conservation of mass or principle of mass conservation states that for any system closed to all transfers of matter and energy, the mass of the system must remain constant over time, as system mass cannot change quantity if it is not added or removed. Hence, the quantity of mass is ""conserved"" over time. The law implies that mass can neither be created nor destroyed, although it may be rearranged in space, or the entities associated with it may be changed in form, as for example when light or physical work is transformed into particles that contribute the same mass to the system as the light or work had contributed. Thus, during any chemical reaction, nuclear reaction, or radioactive decay in an isolated system, the total mass of the reactants or starting materials must be equal to the mass of the products.",what is meant by the idea that mass is conserved
when did construction start on the world trade center,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=1_World_Trade_Center', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/World_Trade_Center_(1973%E2%80%932001).html', 'http://www.mlecshs.com/newsletter/the-importance-of-9-11-history-and-now/', 'https://sefindia.org/forum/viewtopic.php?t=17583&amp', 'http://architectuul.com/architecture/world-trade-center', 'https://wikivivid.com/wiki/One_World_Trade_Center', 'https://www.bcnys.org/history']","Construction of the World Trade Center's North Tower began in August 1968, and the South Tower in 1969. Extensive use of prefabricated components helped to speed up the construction process. The first tenants moved into the North Tower in December 1970 and into the South Tower in January 1972. Four other low-level buildings were constructed as part of the World Trade Center in the 1970s, and the seventh building, 7 World Trade Center, was constructed in the mid-1980s.",when did construction start on the world trade center
what were the conditions of the kellogg briand pact,"['http://www.peacecouple.com/category/antiwar/page/2/', 'https://www.vietnamfulldisclosure.org/remarks-spring-action-2018-vfp/', 'https://www.spectroom.com/daily/08-27/all']","The Kellogg -- Briand Pact (or Pact of Paris, officially General Treaty for Renunciation of War as an Instrument of National Policy) is a 1928 international agreement in which signatory states promised not to use war to resolve ""disputes or conflicts of whatever nature or of whatever origin they may be, which may arise among them"". Parties failing to abide by this promise ""should be denied of the benefits furnished by this treaty"".",what were the conditions of the kellogg briand pact
where is kilauea located on a world map,"['http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Mauna_Loa', 'http://www.csa-apac.org/what-is-hawaiian-fashion-2.html', 'https://www.hawaii-aloha.com/blog/2013/09/14/does-mauna-loa-measure-up/', 'https://traveltipy.com/us-national-parks-us-holidays/']","Kīlauea is one of five subaerial volcanoes that make up the island of Hawai ʻi, created by the Hawaii hotspot. The oldest volcano on the island, Kohala, is more than a million years old, and Kīlauea, the youngest, is believed to be between 300,000 and 600,000 years of age; Lōʻihi Seamount on the island's flank is even younger, but has yet to breach the surface. Thus it is the second youngest volcano in the Hawaiian -- Emperor seamount chain, a chain of shield volcanoes and seamounts extending from Hawaii to the Kuril -- Kamchatka Trench in Russia.",where is kilauea located on a world map
european countries with english as their official language,"['http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/English_language_in_Europe', 'https://iclg.com/practice-areas/investor-state-arbitration-laws-and-regulations/united-kingdom', 'https://www.lexology.com/library/detail.aspx?g=d26a521e-a2e8-4a99-a56c-58445e6e52db', 'https://texteacher.com/blog/learnt-or-learned-know-the-difference', 'https://www.wanacoindoniaga.com/3671-spanish-dating-in-ireland-jobs.php', 'https://thecommongood.blog/2016/11/20/system-failure-power-profit-and-tax-avoidance/', 'https://www.familymoney.co.uk/financial-history/money-and-currencies/the-history-of-the-british-pound/']","The English language in Europe, as a native language, is mainly spoken in the United Kingdom and Ireland. Outside of these states, it has a special status in the Crown dependencies (Isle of Man, Jersey and Guernsey), Gibraltar (one of the British Overseas Territories) and Malta. In the Kingdom of the Netherlands, English has an official status as a regional language on the isles of Saba and Sint Eustatius. In other parts of Europe, English is spoken mainly by those who have learnt it as a second language, but also, to a lesser extent, natively by some expatriates from some countries in the English-speaking world.",european countries with english as their official language
what hospital is tv show er based on,"['http://maps.thefullwiki.org/ER_(TV_series)', 'http://www.markedbyteachers.com/as-and-a-level/drama/how-do-peter-benchley-and-steven-spielberg-build-up-tension-and-suspense-in-the-opening-chapter-of-the-novel-and-the-opening-scene-of-the-film.html', 'https://www.educationquizzes.com/in/specialist/books/author---michael-crichton-0001/', 'https://www.readbrightly.com/best-horse-books-for-kids-ages-8-12/', 'https://neofilm.blog/2012/11/28/westworld/', 'http://www.blogofdeath.com/2005/08/22/john-h-ostrom/', 'https://www.americanheritage.com/users/nathaniel-benchley']","In 1974, author Michael Crichton wrote a screenplay based on his own experiences as a medical student in a busy hospital emergency room. The screenplay went nowhere and Crichton focused on other topics. In 1990, he published the novel Jurassic Park, and in 1993 began a collaboration with director Steven Spielberg on the film adaptation of the book. Crichton and Spielberg then turned to ER, but decided to film the story as a two-hour pilot for a television series rather than as a feature film. Spielberg's Amblin Entertainment provided John Wells as the show's executive producer. The script used to shoot the pilot was virtually unchanged from what Crichton had written in 1974. The only substantive changes made by the producers in 1994 were that the Susan Lewis character became a woman and the Peter Benton character became an African-American, and the running time was shortened by about 20 minutes in order for the pilot to air in a two-hour block on network TV. Because of a lack of time and money necessary to build a set, the pilot episode of ER was filmed in the former Linda Vista Hospital in Los Angeles, an old facility that had ceased operating in 1990. A set modeled after Los Angeles County General Hospital's emergency room was built soon afterward at the Warner Bros. studios in Burbank, California, although the show makes extensive use of location shoots in Chicago, most notably the city's famous ""L"" train platforms.",what hospital is tv show er based on
where is baja california located on a map,"['http://www.factbites.com/topics/Municipalities-of-Baja-California', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/Ricardo_Barroso_Agramont', 'https://upge.wn.com/?activate=0&from=lapaztimes.com&ads=1&title=La+paz+times&auto=La+paz+times&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=La+paz+times&pagenum=3', 'http://mx.wowcity.com/bajacaliforniasur/', 'http://postal-code.org/State/MX/bajacalifornia', 'http://masnoticiasbcs.com/bcs', 'http://www.factbites.com/topics/Baja-California']","Baja California (Spanish pronunciation: (ˈbaxa kaliˈfoɾnja) (listen)), (English: Lower California), officially the Free and Sovereign State of Baja California (Spanish: Estado Libre y Soberano de Baja California), is a state in Mexico. It is the northernmost and westernmost of the 32 Federal Entities of Mexico. Before becoming a state in 1952, the area was known as the North Territory of Baja California (El Territorio Norte de Baja California). It has an area of 70,113 km (27,071 sq mi), or 3.57% of the land mass of Mexico and comprises the northern half of the Baja California Peninsula, north of the 28th parallel, plus oceanic Guadalupe Island. The mainland portion of the state is bordered on the west by the Pacific Ocean, on the east by Sonora, the U.S. state of Arizona, and the Gulf of California (also known as the ""Sea of Cortez""), and on the south by Baja California Sur. Its northern limit is the U.S. state of California.",where is baja california located on a map
who started the east coast west coast rivalry,"['http://aimtheory.com/the-history-of-hip-hop.html', 'https://mymmanews.com/tupac-vs-biggie-rivalry-resurfaces-ufc-202-main-event/', 'http://video.slimtrader.com/tag/eastcoast/', 'https://gwopmagazine.com/lists/27-club-and-under-celebrity-deaths-under-27/']","The East Coast -- West Coast hip hop rivalry was a feud between artists and fans of the East Coast hip hop and West Coast hip hop scenes in the United States, especially from the mid to late 1990s. Focal points of the feud were West Coast-based rapper Tupac Shakur (and his Los Angeles-based label, Death Row Records), and East Coast-based rapper The Notorious B.I.G. (and his New York-based label, Bad Boy Records), who were both fatally shot following drive-by shootings by unknown assailants in 1996 and 1997, respectively.",who started the east coast west coast rivalry
what is the name of the dam in the movie the fugitive,['http://www.coalcreekironworks.com/news/cheoah-dam'],"The dam was used as a filming location for the 1993 movie The Fugitive, starring Harrison Ford.",what is the name of the dam in the movie the fugitive
who wrote common sense and what was its intended message,"['https://www.audible.com/search?searchAuthor=Thomas+Paine', 'https://inventaire.io/entity/wd:Q843940', 'https://www.audible.ca/fr_CA/pd/Meditations-Livre-Audio/B072LD164J', 'https://www.colombotelegraph.com/index.php/a-candid-letter-to-mr-president-maithripala-sirisena/', 'https://www.colombotelegraph.com/index.php/the-left-center-urges-sri-lankans-to-support-maithripala/', 'https://www.libreriadelau.com/bw-common-sense-the-rights-of-man-words-of-a-visionary-that-sparked-the-revolution-and-remained-the-core-of-american-democratic-principles-musaicum-books-historia/p', 'http://www.lostpine.com/home/passions/patriots/thomas-paine/']","Common Sense is a pamphlet written by Thomas Paine in 1775 -- 76 advocating independence from Great Britain to people in the Thirteen Colonies. Written in clear and persuasive prose, Paine marshaled moral and political arguments to encourage common people in the Colonies to fight for egalitarian government. It was published anonymously on January 10, 1776, at the beginning of the American Revolution, and became an immediate sensation.",who wrote common sense and what was its intended message
where is the walk of fame located in los angeles,"['https://kids.kiddle.co/Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame', 'https://hollywoodphotographs.com/category/45-1/walk-of-fame/', 'https://hollywoodphotographs.com/blog/month/10-2011/', 'https://abritandasoutherner.com/best-things-hollywood/', 'http://dia-log.info/search?q=Hollywood%20city%20los%20angeles', 'http://www.fact-index.com/h/ho/hollywood_walk_of_fame.html', 'http://rockandrollroadmap.com/places/miscellaneous/los-angeles-area-miscellaneous/hollywood-walk-of-fame/']","The Walk of Fame runs 1.3 miles (2.1 km) east to west on Hollywood Boulevard from Gower Street to La Brea Avenue, plus a short segment of Marshfield Way that runs diagonally between Hollywood and La Brea; and 0.4 miles (0.64 km) north to south on Vine Street between Yucca Street and Sunset Boulevard. According to a 2003 report by the market research firm NPO Plog Research, the Walk attracts about 10 million visitors annually -- more than Sunset Strip, TCL Chinese Theatre (formerly Grauman's), the Queen Mary, and the Los Angeles County Museum of Art -- and has played an important role in making tourism the largest industry in Los Angeles County.",where is the walk of fame located in los angeles
what happens in rummikub when you run out of tiles,"['https://www.yourturnmyturn.com/rules/rummy.php', 'http://www.thehouseofcards.com/online-games/tile-rummy-web.html']","Once a player has made his initial meld, he can, on each turn, play one or more tiles from his rack, making or adding to groups and / or runs. If the player cannot (or chooses not to) play any tiles, he must pick a tile randomly from the pool and add it to his rack.",what happens in rummikub when you run out of tiles
what is meant by law of diminishing returns,"['https://qualitynotion.com/2012/01/04/mythical-man-month-with-due-respect-to-frederick-p-brooks/', 'https://walletimpact.com/how-to-make-next-year-your-most-successful-year/', 'https://blogs.timesofisrael.com/the-skeptics-kaddish-for-the-atheist-37/', 'https://beingcivil.typepad.com/my_weblog/2012/01/civil-3d-performance-part-iihow-much-ram-is-enough.html', 'https://dzone.com/articles/ideas-from-another-field', 'https://consultingbyrpm.com/blog/2015/11/in-the-long-run-were-all-earthlings.html', 'https://www.gscouncil.org/2014/01/']","The law of diminishing returns states that in all productive processes, adding more of one factor of production, while holding all others constant (""ceteris paribus""), will at some point yield lower incremental per-unit returns. The law of diminishing returns does not imply that adding more of a factor will decrease the total production, a condition known as negative returns, though in fact this is common.",what is meant by law of diminishing returns
which of the following is not a presumed cause of ice ages,"['https://forum.arctic-sea-ice.net/index.php/topic,1932.0.html', 'https://chiefio.wordpress.com/2009/04/06/bond-event-zero/', 'http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Paleoclimatology', 'https://timelinetothefuture.org/possible-earth-events/shift-in-crust']","The prevailing theory is that the Younger Dryas was caused by significant reduction or shutdown of the North Atlantic ""Conveyor"", which circulates warm tropical waters northward, in response to a sudden influx of fresh water from Lake Agassiz and deglaciation in North America. Geological evidence for such an event is so far lacking. The global climate would then have become locked into the new state until freezing removed the fresh water ""lid"" from the North Atlantic. An alternative theory suggests instead that the jet stream shifted northward in response to the changing topographic forcing of the melting North American ice sheet, which brought more rain to the North Atlantic, which freshened the ocean surface enough to slow the thermohaline circulation.",which of the following is not a presumed cause of ice ages
where does the last name palomo come from,"['http://smartel.mobi/darko-lazic-izaberi-nekog-da-na-mene-lici-53/', 'http://ilovetacos.info/viewtopic.php?t=1541', 'http://www.rasmussenreports.com/public_content/political_commentary/commentary_by_michael_barone/cheating_is_rife_in_colleges_by_admissions_officers', 'http://www.aberaeron.net/palomino-welsh-cobs/', 'http://dev.newmexicohistory.org/discussion/?threadID=0248', 'http://www.theinfolist.com/php/HTMLGet.php?FindGo=G%C3%B3mez', 'https://wn.com/Camilo_R._Gomez']",Palomo is a Spanish surname. Notable people with the surname include:,where does the last name aguilar originate from
what is a runner in the maze runner,"['https://jeevanshudhawan.wordpress.com/2016/02/05/the-maze-runner-film/', 'https://www.join4films.com/movie/maze-runner-2014/', 'https://www.mymoviepicker.com/films/theme/l-adolescence-1.htm', 'http://www.ramblingsonreadings.com/movie-review-the-maze-runner/', 'https://disboard.org/servers/tag/rp-server', 'http://villageat.org/2018/07/05/the-maze-runner-stands-out-amongst-its-dystopian-counterparts/']","A teenager wakes up inside an underground elevator with no memory of his identity. A group of male youths greet him in a large grassy area called the ""Glade"" enclosed by tall stone walls. The boys (""Gladers"") have formed a rudimentary society, with each assuming specialized tasks. Their leader, Alby, says that every boy eventually recalls his name but not his past. The boy learns that a vast Maze surrounding them may be the only way out. During the day, designated Runners search the Maze for an escape route, returning before nightfall when the entrance closes. No one has ever survived a night in the Maze.",what is a runner in the maze runner
a company limited by guarantee without share capital,"['https://www.register-my-company.ie/faq/', 'https://www.association-ecopower.com/code-of-conduct.html', 'https://www.ukplc.com/blog/a-guide-to-common-terms-you-may-encounter-when-forming-a-company.html', 'http://truthofthelie.com/2008/12/what-type-of-company-is-madeleines-fund-leaving-no-stone-unturned-ltd/', 'https://www.outofschoolalliance.co.uk/business-structure', 'https://www.stainternational.com/resources/small-business-advice/directors-liable-limited-companys-debts/', 'https://www.wdcvs.com/jargon-ary/c-d/']","In British and Irish company law, a company limited by guarantee (LBG) is an alternative type of corporation used primarily for non-profit organisations that require legal personality. A company limited by guarantee does not usually have a share capital or shareholders, but instead has members who act as guarantors. The guarantors give an undertaking to contribute a nominal amount (typically very small) in the event of the winding up of the company.",a company limited by guarantee without share capital
what do you call any two colors of light that combine to form white light,"['http://www.lightingschool.eu/portfolio/understanding-the-light/', 'http://planetlabelblog.com/2009/07/', 'https://www.wetheprinters.com/faq.html', 'http://greatermnprinting.com/index.php/glossary-of-terms/', 'http://orontechurm.com/northern-territory/how-to-use-filter-paper-cience-experiment.php', 'http://masterbeautyphotography.com/color-theory-color-management-for-digital-photography/', 'http://www.gamonline.com/catalog/colortheory/language.php']","Additive color is in contrast to subtractive color, in which colors are created by subtracting (absorbing) parts of the spectrum of light present in ordinary white light, by means of colored pigments or dyes, such as those in paints, inks, and the three dye layers in typical color photographs on film.",what do you call any two colors of light that combine to form white light
