where did the name t mobile come from,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/TaxSlayer_Center', 'http://hooraylabs.com/russkom/my-t-mobile-mobile-version.html', 'http://bluescripts.net/russkom/my-t-mobile-mobile-version.html', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/T-Mobile.html', 'https://companies.jrank.org/pages/1238/Deutsche-Telekom-Ag.html']","Deutsche Bundespost Telekom was renamed Deutsche Telekom AG on January 1, 1995 as part of phase two of the German communications reform. This process of deregulation continued in November 1996, when DT was privatized and had the largest European IPO at the time, with the stock abbreviation' DT 1'. That same year, DT began to brand its subsidiaries with the T-prefix, renaming the DeTeMobil subsidiary T-Mobil.",where did the name t mobile come from
when was the first ever roller coaster built,"['https://bestonamusement.com/roller-coaster-for-sale/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/100%25_%28Lotta_Engberg_%26_Triple_%26_Touch_song%29', 'https://www.barrypopik.com/index.php/new_york_city/entry/roller_coaster', 'https://wn.com/Hocking_Valley_Scenic_Railway', 'https://bestonparkrides.com/roller-coaster-for-sale/', 'https://bestonrollercoaster.com/steel-roller-coaster-manufacturer/', 'http://mmaconquest.com/northwest-territories/how-to-buy-a-roller-coaster.php']","A roller coaster is a type of amusement ride that employs a form of elevated railroad track designed with tight turns, steep slopes, and sometimes inversions. People ride along the track in open cars, and the rides are often found in amusement parks and theme parks around the world. LaMarcus Adna Thompson obtained one of the first known patents for a roller coaster design in 1885, related to the Switchback Railway that opened a year earlier at Coney Island. The track in a coaster design does not necessarily have to be a complete circuit, as shuttle roller coasters demonstrate. Most roller coasters have multiple cars in which passengers sit and are restrained. Two or more cars hooked together are called a train. Some roller coasters, notably wild mouse roller coasters, run with single cars.",when was the first ever roller coaster built
summary of the play tempest by william shakespeare,"['https://www.bookbeat.co.uk/book/tempest-69068', 'https://www.simonandschuster.ca/books/The-Tempest/William-Shakespeare/9781625589620', 'https://samannelizabeth.wordpress.com/tag/william-shakespeare/', 'http://silenthillforum.com/viewtopic.php?f=30&t=22477&view=print', 'https://americanliterature.com/author/william-shakespeare/book/the-tempest/summary', 'http://www.ljagilamplighter.com/works/prospero-daughter/887-2/', 'http://vesturport.com/theater/the-tempest/']","The Tempest is a play by William Shakespeare, believed to have been written in 1610 -- 11, and thought by many critics to be the last play that Shakespeare wrote alone. It is set on a remote island, where the sorcerer Prospero, rightful Duke of Milan, plots to restore his daughter Miranda to her rightful place using illusion and skillful manipulation. He conjures up a storm, the eponymous tempest, to cause his usurping brother Antonio and the complicit King Alonso of Naples to believe they are shipwrecked and marooned on the island. There, his machinations bring about the revelation of Antonio's lowly nature, the redemption of the King, and the marriage of Miranda to Alonso's son, Ferdinand.",what is the play the tempest by william shakespeare about
identify four problem affecting the mining industry in nigeria,"['https://www.vanguardngr.com/2017/02/mining-industry-entrepreneur-revolution-2/', 'https://www.thisdaylive.com/index.php/2016/04/20/solid-minerals-as-catalyst-for-national-devt-2/', 'https://t.guardian.ng/saturday-magazine/cover/alatise-we-must-prioritise-minerals-needed-for-industrialisation-infrastructure-requirements/', 'https://www.aggregatecrushing.net/solutions/mobile-rock-crusher-manufacturer.html', 'https://lagoonchallenge.co.za/Oct/30/mineral-resources-in-south-west-of-nigeria.html', 'https://bnbriet.nl/35649/geology-and-the-mining-industry-in-nigeria/', 'https://economicconfidential.com/2015/04/reviving-early-industries-for-job-creation/']","The mining of minerals in Nigeria accounts for only 0.3% of its GDP, due to the influence of its vast oil resources. The domestic mining industry is underdeveloped, leading to Nigeria having to import minerals that it could produce domestically, such as salt or iron ore. Rights to ownership of mineral resources is held by the Federal government of Nigeria, which grants titles to organizations to explore, mine, and sell mineral resources. Organized mining began in 1903 when the Mineral Survey of the Northern Protectorates was created by the British colonial government. A year later, the Mineral Survey of the Southern Protectorates was founded. By the 1940s, Nigeria was a major producer of tin, columbite, and coal. The discovery of oil in 1956 hurt the mineral extraction industries, as government and industry both began to focus on this new resource. The Nigerian Civil War in the late 1960s led many expatriate mining experts to leave the country. Mining regulation is handled by the Ministry of Solid Minerals Development, which oversees the management of all mineral resources. Mining law is codified in the Federal Minerals and Mining Act of 1999. Historically, Nigeria's mining industry was monopolized by state-owned public corporations. This led to a decline in productivity in almost all mineral industries. The Obasanjo administration began a process of selling off government-owned corporations to private investors in 1999.",identify four problem affecting the mining industry in nigeria
where do statutory and common laws come from,"['https://upge.wn.com/?from=maritimeadmiraltylaw.org&ads=1&title=Maritime+admiralty+law&auto=Maritime+admiralty+law&author=system&template=cheetah-photo-search%2Findex.txt&query=Maritime+admiralty+law&pagenum=5', 'https://www.worldattorney.eu/common-law/comment-page-1/', 'http://virahsawmy.com/usefulterms.aspx', 'http://parallelewelten.info/free-law-essays/common-law/common-law-is-developed-by-judges.php', 'http://megacomicsgroup.com/home/tag/martin-goodman/', 'http://heaven4u.tk/roulette-bet-xword.html', 'https://www.acs.edu.au/courses/legal-terminology-499.aspx']","Common law (also known as judicial precedent or judge-made law, or case law) is that body of law derived from judicial decisions of courts and similar tribunals. The defining characteristic of ""common law"" is that it arises as precedent. In cases where the parties disagree on what the law is, a common law court looks to past precedential decisions of relevant courts, and synthesizes the principles of those past cases as applicable to the current facts. If a similar dispute has been resolved in the past, the court is usually bound to follow the reasoning used in the prior decision (a principle known as stare decisis). If, however, the court finds that the current dispute is fundamentally distinct from all previous cases (called a ""matter of first impression""), and legislative statutes are either silent or ambiguous on the question, judges have the authority and duty to resolve the issue (one party or the other has to win, and on disagreements of law, judges make that decision). The court states an opinion that gives reasons for the decision, and those reasons agglomerate with past decisions as precedent to bind future judges and litigants. Common law, as the body of law made by judges, stands in contrast to and on equal footing with statutes which are adopted through the legislative process, and regulations which are promulgated by the executive branch (the interactions are explained later in this article). Stare decisis, the principle that cases should be decided according to consistent principled rules so that similar facts will yield similar results, lies at the heart of all common law systems.",where do statutory and common laws come from
difference between a cocker spaniel and springer spaniel,"['http://foto.tabiinu.com/about', 'https://www.europetnet.com/pet-resources/dog-breeds/item/1604-english-cocker-spaniel.html', 'http://vrbani.info/threesome/adult-weight-cocker-spaniel.html', 'https://perfectpets.com.au/pets/dogs/dog-breeds/dog-breeders/english-springer-spaniel', 'https://dutchgoesthephoto.net/tag/agility/', 'https://www.ecsca.info/whats-the-difference/', 'http://www.dogscountryclubandkennelresort.com.au/blog/archives/10-2017']","The English Springer Spaniel is similar to the English Cocker Spaniel and at first glance the only major difference is the latter's smaller size. However English Springers also tend to have shorter, and higher-set ears than English Cockers. In addition Springers also tend to have a longer muzzle; their eyes are not as prominent, and the coat is less abundant. The major differences between the Welsh Springer and the English Springer are that the Welsh have more limited colours and tend to be slightly smaller.",difference between a cocker spaniel and springer spaniel
is a sequence the same thing as a function,"['http://www.rebecamendez.com/works/show/37', 'http://www.rebecamendez.com/works/show/59', 'https://www.fxsolver.com/blog/2016/06/24/10x-series-and-progressions/', 'http://cusco-hotels.info/news.php?action=show&id=40899']","In mathematics, a recurrence relation is an equation that recursively defines a sequence or multidimensional array of values, once one or more initial terms are given: each further term of the sequence or array is defined as a function of the preceding terms.",is a sequence the same thing as a function
the u.s. supreme court's appellate jurisdiction derives from,"['https://www.reference.com/web?q=What+Is+an+Appellate+Jurisdiction%3F&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir', 'http://www.bcsstartup.com/first-principles/federalist-47/', 'http://qva.com.au/what-is-the-appellate-jurisdiction-of-the-supreme-court.html', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Appellate_jurisdiction', 'http://ducharmeweber.com/category/procedure/', 'https://courses.lumenlearning.com/odessa-texasgovernment/chapter/jurisdiction-types-of-law-and-the-selection-of-judges/', 'https://www.tthlaw.com/enotes-liability-december-2018/']","Appellate jurisdiction is the power of a higher court to review decisions and change outcomes of decisions of lower courts. Most appellate jurisdiction is legislatively created, and may consist of appeals by leave of the appellate court or by right. Depending on the type of case and the decision below, appellate review primarily consists of: an entirely new hearing (a non trial de novo); a hearing where the appellate court gives deference to factual findings of the lower court; or review of particular legal rulings made by the lower court (an appeal on the record).",the u.s. supreme court's appellate jurisdiction derives from
where is the parotid gland and what does it do,"['https://psychology.wikia.org/wiki/Parotid_gland', 'http://beta.anatomic.us/atlas/parotid-gland/', 'http://allergyasthmasleep.com/patient-education/glossary/', 'https://www.toxinmed.com/muscles/jaw', 'https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/852373-overview', 'https://factslegend.org/40-interesting-saliva-and-salivary-glands-facts/', 'https://www.soapcentral.com/oltl/news/2009/0223-smith_iview.php']","The parotid gland is a major salivary gland in many animals. In humans, the two parotid glands are present on either side of the mouth and in front of both ears. They are the largest of the salivary glands. Each parotid is wrapped around the mandibular ramus, and secretes serous saliva through the parotid duct into the mouth, to facilitate mastication and swallowing and to begin the digestion of starches.",where is the parotid gland and what does it do
who were the dadaists and what did they do,"['http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Dada', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Louis_Aragon', 'https://thewhispergallery.com/alessio-guano/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Kunstmuseum_Basel', 'http://sphinx.planetwaves.net/blog/?p=2532', 'http://www.bikinisandpassports.com/once-a-denim-girl-always-a-denim-girl/', 'https://kaggsysbookishramblings.wordpress.com/tag/tristan-tzara/']","Dada (/ ˈdɑːdɑː /) or Dadaism was an art movement of the European avant-garde in the early 20th century, with early centers in Zürich, Switzerland at the Cabaret Voltaire (circa 1916); New York Dada began circa 1915, and after 1920 Dada flourished in Paris. Developed in reaction to World War I, the Dada movement consisted of artists who rejected the logic, reason, and aestheticism of modern capitalist society, instead expressing nonsense, irrationality, and anti-bourgeois protest in their works. The art of the movement spanned visual, literary, and sound media, including collage, sound poetry, cut-up writing, and sculpture. Dadaist artists expressed their discontent with violence, war, and nationalism, and maintained political affinities with the radical left.",who were the dadaists and what did they do
what does the olive branch represent in the olympics,"['https://www.museummasters.gr/en/olive-wreath-silver-plated-en.html', 'http://www.hrchessclub.org/macarthur-center-spring-chess-festival/', 'https://www.littlenewtons.com/early-childhood-education/olympic-excitement/', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/Gold_medal.html', 'http://olympstats.com/2014/04/06/the-1st-modern-olympic-games/', 'http://www.thestoryandyou.com/2018/05/', 'https://bookofthrees.com/what-are-olympic-medals-made-of/?share=google-plus-1']","According to Pausanias it was introduced by Hercules as a prize for the running race winner to honor his father Zeus. In the ancient Olympic Games there were no gold, silver, or bronze medals. There was only one winner per event, crowned with an olive wreath made of wild-olive leaves from a sacred tree near the temple of Zeus at Olympia. Olive wreaths were given out during the 2004 Summer Olympics in Athens in honor of the ancient tradition, because the games were being held in Greece.",what does the olive branch represent in the olympics
who is the state of washington named after,"['https://advowastemedical.com/washington-medical-waste-disposal', 'https://yque.com/wainviawi.html', 'https://washingtonshipping.com/', 'http://www.jerrys-trivia-corner.com/washington/', 'https://xn--j1ahfl.xn--p1ai/library/cultural_studies__in_teaching_english_184547.html', 'http://www.downloadpsdtemplates.com/washington-drivers-license-psd/', 'http://sports-entertainment-law-report.careers.org/education/colleges/138284?city=chipley&amp;name=florida-panhandle-technical-college&amp;state_or_country_name=florida']","Washington (/ ˈwɒʃɪŋtən / (listen)), officially the State of Washington, is a state in the Pacific Northwest region of the United States. Named after George Washington, the first President of the United States, the state was made out of the western part of the Washington Territory, which was ceded by Britain in 1846 in accordance with the Oregon Treaty in the settlement of the Oregon boundary dispute. It was admitted to the Union as the 42nd state in 1889. Olympia is the state capital. Washington is sometimes referred to as Washington State to distinguish it from Washington, D.C., the capital of the United States, which is often shortened to Washington.",who was the state of washington named after
how many miles from nashville tennessee to atlanta georgia,"['https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Lawrenceburg%2C_Tennessee', 'http://allhookedup.net/11487/pipeline-hall-fame-magazine.html', 'https://tier-rack.com/tennessee/chattanooga.html', 'https://www.saygrace.net/profile3.html', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Chattanooga,_Tennessee', 'https://cielotech.wordpress.com/2014/05/', 'http://en.sistercity.info/sister-cities/Chattanooga%2C%20Tennessee.html']","Chattanooga is a city in the U.S. state of Tennessee, with a population of 176,588 in 2015. The fourth-largest Tennessee city, it is the seat of Hamilton County. Located in southeastern Tennessee in East Tennessee, on the Tennessee River, served by multiple railroads and Interstate highways, Chattanooga is a transit hub. Chattanooga lies 120 miles (190 km) northwest of Atlanta, Georgia, 120 miles (190 km) southwest of Knoxville, Tennessee, 135 miles (217 km) southeast of Nashville, Tennessee, 120 miles (190 km) northeast of Huntsville, Alabama, and 148 miles (238 km) northeast of Birmingham, Alabama.",how many miles from nashville tennessee to atlanta georgia
what's the difference between the army and the royal marines,"['https://majormike.us/subjects/royal-marines/', 'https://skilt.co.uk/product/royal-marines-kilt/', 'http://everything.explained.today/Royal_Marines/', 'https://www.redbubble.com/people/spacestuffplus/works/16904109-royal-marines-emblem?cat_context=u-bags&amp;grid_pos=67&amp;p=pouch&amp;rbs=ca3e99b8-15eb-4b0d-8fa1-521778d4375e&amp;ref=shop_grid', 'https://battlefield.fandom.com/wiki/Royal_Marines', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/All_England_Lawn_Tennis_and_Croquet_Club', 'https://wikimili.com/en/45_Commando']","The Corps of Royal Marines (RM) is the amphibious light infantry and one of the five fighting arms or branches of the Royal Navy. The Royal Marines were formed in 1755 as the Royal Navy's infantry troops. However, the marines can trace their origins back to the formation of the English Army's ""Duke of York and Albany's maritime regiment of Foot"" at the grounds of the Honourable Artillery Company on 28 October 1664.",what's the difference between the army and the royal marines
who did the declaration of independence apply to,"['http://mediablackberry.com/how-to-become-a-country-catalonia-and-ambazonia/', 'https://fcw.com/articles/2006/07/10/flipside.aspx', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence', 'https://www.acrolinx.com/blog/content-of-greatest-presidents/', 'https://en.unionpedia.org/8th_Connecticut_Regiment', 'http://mumbles.co.uk/main-purpose-of-the-declaration-of-independence.html', 'https://sivican.currclickblog.com/how-to-write-a-student-declaration-of-independence-21925mu.html']","The United States Declaration of Independence is the statement adopted by the Second Continental Congress meeting at the Pennsylvania State House (now known as Independence Hall) in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania on July 4, 1776. The Declaration announced that the Thirteen Colonies then at war with the Kingdom of Great Britain would regard themselves as thirteen independent sovereign states no longer under British rule. With the Declaration, these new states took a collective first step toward forming the United States of America. The declaration was signed by representatives from New Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay, Rhode Island, Connecticut, New York, New Jersey, Pennsylvania, Maryland, Delaware, Virginia, North Carolina, South Carolina, and Georgia.",who did the declaration of independence apply to
when did harry potter the movie come out,"['https://www.netpaak.com/%D9%87%D8%B1%DB%8C-%D9%BE%D8%A7%D8%AA%D8%B1/', 'https://www.mkvcinemas.cz/harry-potter-all-parts-collection-part-1-2-3-4-5-6-7-8-brrip-hindi-eng-400mb-480p/', 'https://www.moviesak47.me/harry-potter-collection-2001-2011-dual-audio-480p-720p-1080p/', 'http://normconway.info/?page_id=12822', 'https://www.thebookpeople.co.uk/webapp/wcs/stores/servlet/CategoryDisplay?categoryId=177728&catalogId=10051', 'http://www.focusworkoutdvd.com/category/entertainment', 'https://www.buttondown.tv/creative/fantastic-beasts-find-teaser-trailer-hd/']","Harry Potter is a British-American film series based on the Harry Potter novels by author J.K. Rowling. The series is distributed by Warner Bros. and consists of eight fantasy films, beginning with Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone (2001) and culminating with Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows -- Part 2 (2011). A spin-off prequel series will consist of five films, starting with Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them (2016). The Fantastic Beasts films mark the beginning of a shared media franchise known as J.K. Rowling's Wizarding World.",when did harry potter the movie come out
how many times did michael jordan win dpoy,"['http://signedsportsmemorabilia.name/tag/holo/', 'https://americannationaluniversity.wordpress.com/tag/basketball/', 'https://mghardie.wordpress.com/tag/championship/', 'http://www.sportsmuntra.com/top-10-greatest-nba-players-time/', 'http://brooklyn-flatbush.com/tag/basketball-hall-of-fame/', 'http://send-a-birthday-card.blogspot.com/2011/03/michael-jeffrey-jordan.html', 'http://www.sharegoodstuffs.com/2012/03/18-famous-person-with-incredible-acts.html']","Jordan's individual accolades and accomplishments include five Most Valuable Player (MVP) Awards, ten All-NBA First Team designations, nine All-Defensive First Team honors, fourteen NBA All-Star Game appearances, three All-Star Game MVP Awards, ten scoring titles, three steals titles, six NBA Finals MVP Awards, and the 1988 NBA Defensive Player of the Year Award. Among his numerous accomplishments, Jordan holds the NBA records for highest career regular season scoring average (30.12 points per game) and highest career playoff scoring average (33.45 points per game). In 1999, he was named the greatest North American athlete of the 20th century by ESPN, and was second to Babe Ruth on the Associated Press's list of athletes of the century. Jordan is a two-time inductee into the Basketball Hall of Fame, having been enshrined in 2009 for his individual career, and again in 2010 as part of the group induction of the 1992 United States men's Olympic basketball team (""The Dream Team""). He became a member of the FIBA Hall of Fame in 2015.",how many times did michael jordan win dpoy
difference between freedom of peaceful assembly and association,"['http://www.thefullwiki.org/Freedom_of_assembly', 'http://www.rangzen.net/2010/03/19/waiting-for-mangtso-iii/']","The terms freedom of assembly and freedom of association may be used to distinguish between the freedom to assemble in public places and the freedom to join an association. Freedom of assembly is often used in the context of the right to protest, while freedom of association is used in the context of labor rights and in the Constitution of the United States is interpreted to mean both the freedom to assemble and the freedom to join an association.",difference between freedom of peaceful assembly and association
where does the ruby throated hummingbird go in the winter,"['http://allaboutbirds.info/?m=20140221', 'https://kiwifoto.com/galleries/birds/ruby_throated_hummingbird/', 'https://bird.fandom.com/wiki/Ruby-Throated_Hummingbird', 'https://ourfinefeatheredfriends.com/category/hummingbirds/', 'https://glaszart.com/july-in-maine-what-types-of-birds-can-i-expect-to-see/', 'http://www.wsiltv.com/story/40276613/hummingbirds-are-arriving-with-spring']","The ruby-throated hummingbird is migratory, spending most of the winter in southern Mexico and Central America, as far south as extreme western Panama, the West Indies, and southern Florida. During migration, some birds embark on a nonstop 900-mile journey across the Gulf of Mexico and Caribbean from Panama to Gulf Coast. The bird breeds throughout the eastern United States, east of the 100th meridian, and in southern Canada, particularly Ontario, in eastern and mixed deciduous and broadleaved forest. In winter, it is seen mostly in Mexico and southern Florida.",where does the ruby throated hummingbird go in the winter
the battle of yorktown is significant in the american revolution because,"['http://silverhawkauthor.com/artillery-and-armoured-fighting-vehicles-preserved-in-the-usa-virginia-yorktown_931.html', 'https://www.americanhistorycentral.com/entries/battle-of-yorktown/view/external-links/', 'https://jeffersonianeducation.com/Aspects-of-the-Tour/founding-america-military.html', 'http://blog.thebuttonmonger.com/2011/10/siege-of-yorktown.html', 'https://scdbwiki.swem.wm.edu/wiki/index.php/Battle_of_Yorktown', 'http://storiesofusa.com/the-american-revolution-revolutionary-war-battles-timeline-1770-1783/', 'https://www.rbattinglaw.com/1st-battle-of-american-revolution/']","The Siege of Yorktown, also known as the Battle of Yorktown, the Surrender at Yorktown, German Battle or the Siege of Little York, ending on October 19, 1781, at Yorktown, Virginia, was a decisive victory by a combined force of American Continental Army troops led by General George Washington and French Army troops led by the Comte de Rochambeau over a British Army commanded by British peer and Lieutenant General Charles Cornwallis. The culmination of the Yorktown campaign, the siege proved to be the last major land battle of the American Revolutionary War in the North American theater, as the surrender by Cornwallis, and the capture of both him and his army, prompted the British government to negotiate an end to the conflict. The battle boosted faltering American morale and revived French enthusiasm for the war, as well as undermining popular support for the conflict in Great Britain.",the battle of yorktown is significant in the american revolution because
what is true about sap r/3,"['https://b2b.partcommunity.com/community/knowledge/en/detail/1267/SAP+R~3', 'https://mindmajix.com/sap-gts-interview-questions', 'http://leonsoftsolutions.com/sapsolutions.html', 'https://www.confaab.com/au/erp-decision-makers-email-lists.php', 'http://www.cursivetech.com/solutions/erp/web-based-erp.html', 'https://www.inoogabc.com/services/sap-erp/', 'https://super2008.net/enterprise-resource-planning-the-usefulness-benefits-and-problems/']","SAP R / 3 is the former name of the enterprise resource planning software produced by the German corporation SAP AG (now SAP SE). It is an enterprise-wide information system designed to coordinate all the resources, information, and activities needed to complete business processes such as order fulfillment, billing, human resource management, and production planning.",what is true about sap r/3
each county in texas has at least how many district courts,['https://weberscustominteriors.com/the-texas-judicial-system-the-texas-judicial-system-has-been-called-one-of-the-most-complex-in-the-united-states/'],"In more rural areas, as many as five counties share a district court; urban counties, on the other hand, have multiple district courts, which in some cases specialize in civil, criminal, family law or juvenile matters.",each county in texas has at least how many district courts
what type of gas is released in landfills (methane or co2,"['https://ose.directory/topics/landfill-gas/', 'https://tmcfluidsystems.com/Applications/landfill-gas.html', 'https://www.airtechusa.com/industries/environmental/landfill-gas-recovery-blowers-compressors/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Biofuel', 'https://genelco.gr/index.php?cPath=27&sess=ce7fkjqupocs0lfmhe8a0g93q3', 'http://wikien3.appspot.com/wiki/Landfill_gas', 'https://www.mwatoday.com/resources/renewable-energy-plant/default.aspx']","Landfill gas is a complex mix of different gases created by the action of microorganisms within a landfill. Landfill gas is approximately forty to sixty percent methane, with the remainder being mostly carbon dioxide. Trace amounts of other volatile organic compounds (VOCs) comprise the remainder (< 1%). These trace gases include a large array of species, mainly simple hydrocarbons.",what type of gas is released in landfills (methane or co2
where is guam compared to the united states,"['http://booking-otel.ru/index.php?p=1&lang=en&country=72', 'https://www.answers.com/Q/Where_is_Guam', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Guam', 'https://www.travellerspoint.com/guide/Guam/', 'http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Guam', 'http://skaphandrus.com/en/scuba-diving-sites/country/Guam', 'https://drtraveluk.com/2016/03/06/guam/']","Guam lies between 13.2 ° N and 13.7 ° N and between 144.6 ° E and 145.0 ° E, and has an area of 212 square miles (549 km), making it the 32nd largest island of the United States. It is the southernmost and largest island in the Mariana island chain and is also the largest island in Micronesia. This island chain was created by the colliding Pacific and Philippine Sea tectonic plates. Guam is the closest land mass to the Mariana Trench, a deep subduction zone, that lies beside the island chain to the east. Challenger Deep, the deepest surveyed point in the Oceans, is southwest of Guam at 35,797 feet (10,911 meters) deep. The highest point in Guam is Mount Lamlam at an elevation of 1,334 feet (407 meters).",where is guam compared to the united states
what are the 8 limbs of muay thai,"['http://www.hahnextremefitness.com/muay', 'https://championswayoflife.com/Programs/muay-thai', 'http://iowabjj.com/muay-thai/', 'https://www.realitysdc.com.au/muay-thai-adelaide.html', 'http://www.westamptonmartialarts.net/muay/', 'http://www.mastermehrdad.com/history-of-muay-thai-art-of-fighting/', 'https://cushtravel.com/tag/muay-thai/']","Muay Thai is referred to as the ""Art of Eight Limbs"" or the ""Science of Eight Limbs"", because it makes use of punches, kicks, elbows and knee strikes, thus using eight ""points of contact"", as opposed to ""two points"" (fists) in boxing and ""four points"" (hands and feet) used in other more regulated combat sports, such as kickboxing and savate. A practitioner of muay Thai is known as a nak muay. Western practitioners are sometimes called Nak Muay Farang, meaning ""foreign boxer.""",what are the 8 limbs of muay thai
when was the first mural made and what was it painted with,"['http://www.art-richardjbagguley.com/blogdetail.aspx?bid=126', 'http://www.atelier-cg.com/decor4.htm', 'http://artandpopularculture.com/Mural', 'https://www.aalekhyamurals.com/']","Murals of sorts date to Upper Paleolithic times such as the paintings in the Chauvet Cave in Ardèche department of southern France (around 30,000 BC). Many ancient murals have been found within ancient Egyptian tombs (around 3150 BC), the Minoan palaces (Middle period III of the Neopalatial period, 1700 -- 1600 BC) and in Pompeii (around 100 BC -- AD 79).",when was the first mural made and what was it painted with
when were bill of rights added to constitution,"['https://americanhistoryusa.com/topic/united-states-bill-of-rights/', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/October_2', 'https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2018/12/15/', 'http://legendshub.com/James-Madison/', 'https://criticalskillsblog.com/2019/02/01/federalist-papers-a-historical-review-and-timeline-for-ratification-of-the-constitution/', 'https://blog.dar.org/happy-constitution-week', 'https://www.reference.com/web?q=list+of+amendments+1+10&qo=contentPageRelatedSearch&o=600605&l=dir']","On June 8, 1789, Representative James Madison introduced nine amendments to the Constitution in the House of Representatives. Among his recommendations Madison proposed opening up the Constitution and inserting specific rights limiting the power of Congress in Article One, Section 9. Seven of these limitations would become part of the ten ratified Bill of Rights amendments. Ultimately, on September 25, 1789, Congress approved twelve articles of amendment to the Constitution, each consisting of one one-sentence paragraph, and submitted them to the states for ratification. Contrary to Madison's original proposal that the articles be incorporated into the main body of the Constitution, they were proposed as supplemental additions (codicils) to it. Articles Three through Twelve were ratified as additions to the Constitution on December 15, 1791, and became Amendments One through Ten of the Constitution. Article Two became part of the Constitution on May 5, 1992, as the Twenty-seventh Amendment. Article One is technically still pending before the states.",when were bill of rights added to constitution
when did the last civil war veterans die,"['http://ww2talk.com/index.php?threads/grand-army-of-the-republic.74310/', 'http://www.vipfaq.com/Albert%20Woolson.html', 'https://herbweiss.wordpress.com/2014/11/', 'http://famous-peoples.com/person/albert-woolson']","Albert Henry Woolson (February 11, 1850 -- August 2, 1956) was the last surviving member of the Union Army who served in the American Civil War. He was also the last surviving Civil War veteran on either side whose status is undisputed. At least three men who followed him in death claimed to be Confederate veterans, but one has been debunked and the other two are unverified. The last surviving Union soldier to see combat was James Hard (1841 -- 1953).",when did the last civil war veterans die
why philadelphia called the city of brotherly love,"['http://web.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Philadelphia', 'http://www.bycitylight.com/cities/us-pa-philadelphia-history.php', 'http://www.coachfactoryoutletonlin.us/', 'http://www.britishandproud.net/zphiladelphiapa.html', 'https://educationaldiscoverytours.com/destination/philadelphia-educational-tours/', 'https://theculturetrip.com/north-america/usa/pennsylvania/articles/philadelphia-got-name/', 'https://cottageholidays.ca/category-perverted/pensylvania-philadelphia-philly-centercity-14-04-2019.php']","In 1681, in partial repayment of a debt, Charles II of England granted Penn a charter for what would become the Pennsylvania colony. Despite the royal charter, Penn bought the land from the local Lenape to be on good terms with the Native Americans and ensure peace for his colony. Penn made a treaty of friendship with Lenape chief Tammany under an elm tree at Shackamaxon, in what is now the city's Fishtown neighborhood. Penn named the city Philadelphia, which is Greek for brotherly love (from philos, ""love"" or ""friendship"", and adelphos, ""brother""). As a Quaker, Penn had experienced religious persecution and wanted his colony to be a place where anyone could worship freely. This tolerance, far more than afforded by most other colonies, led to better relations with the local native tribes and fostered Philadelphia's rapid growth into America's most important city.",why philadelphia called the city of brotherly love
where is hell's kitchen new york city,"['http://futbolus.tk/casino-cruise-in-savannah.html', 'https://annefranklyspeaking.net/2017/09/27/', 'https://ecto-containment.com/media/extreme-reviews/back-in-the-saddle-part-1/', 'http://gojiberry-advance.tk/kunci-gitar-roulette.html', 'https://apartable.com/neighborhoods/hells-kitchen', 'http://ccglim.tk/extra-wide-slot-toasters.html', 'https://www.manhattanmotorcarsporsche.com/directions/porsche-dealership-near-hells-kitchen-ny/']","Hell's Kitchen, also known as Clinton, is a neighborhood on the West Side of Midtown Manhattan in New York City. It is traditionally considered to be bordered by 34th Street to the south, 59th Street to the north, Eighth Avenue to the east, and the Hudson River to the west. The area provides transport, medical, and warehouse-infrastructure support to Midtown's business district.",where is hell's kitchen new york city
who played max as a girl in wizards of waverly place,['http://pix.realinfo.tv/2018/05/bailee-madison.html'],"In 2011, Madison had a recurring role in the Disney Channel Original Series Wizards of Waverly Place as Maxine, the girl form of Max Russo. She also appeared in Just Go with It, alongside Adam Sandler and Jennifer Aniston, as Maggie Murphy, a young girl who wants to become an actress. Madison can be seen in the drama film, An Invisible Sign as the younger version of Jessica Alba's character Mona Gray. She starred in her first leading role in the horror film, Don't Be Afraid of the Dark, alongside Katie Holmes and Guy Pearce where she portrayed Sally Hurst, a lonely withdrawn child who is sent to live with her father and his new girlfriend.",who played max as a girl in wizards of waverly place
who plays loki in thor and the avengers,"['https://allstarpics.famousfix.com/pictures/tom-hiddleston', 'https://sillykhan.com/2013/11/09/thor-the-dark-world/', 'https://www.thetoptens.com/superheroes-villains-portrayed-by-actors/', 'http://rock-cafe.info/posts/tom-hiddleston-sad-smile-746f6d.html', 'https://99celebrity.com/tom-hiddleston/', 'http://rock-cafe.info/posts/tom-hiddleston-benedict-cumberbatch-gif-746f6d.html', 'http://movie-bar.com/actor/tom-hiddleston_45752/']","He came to wider public attention when cast as Loki in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, appearing in Thor (2011), The Avengers (2012), Thor: The Dark World (2013), and Thor: Ragnarok (2017). In 2011, he won the Empire Award for Best Male Newcomer and was nominated for the BAFTA Rising Star Award. Hiddleston has also appeared in Steven Spielberg's War Horse (2011), The Deep Blue Sea (2011), Woody Allen's romantic comedy Midnight in Paris (2011), the 2012 BBC series Henry IV and Henry V, and the romantic vampire film Only Lovers Left Alive (2013).",who plays loki in thor and the avengers
when did the triple entente form between france britain and russia,"['http://www.thefullwiki.org/Triple_Entente', 'https://www.studyblue.com/notes/note/n/study-guide-ww1/deck/21708186', 'https://wikivividly.com/wiki/History_of_Russia_(1892%E2%80%931917)', 'https://www.studyblue.com/notes/note/n/world-history-b-study-guide-2018-19-comer/deck/21707144', 'https://www.studyblue.com/notes/note/n/ww1-note-cards/deck/21707519', 'https://www.brainscape.com/flashcards/chapter-20-5864163/packs/8098282', 'https://carlow-nationalist.ie/2015/02/20/ireland-home-and-away-in-world-war-i-part-1/']","The Triple Entente (from French entente (ɑ̃tɑ̃t) ""friendship, understanding, agreement"") refers to the understanding linking the Russian Empire, the French Third Republic, and the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland after the signing of the Anglo-Russian Entente on 31 August 1907. The understanding between the three powers, supplemented by agreements with Japan and Portugal, was a powerful counterweight to the Triple Alliance of Germany, Austria-Hungary, and Italy.",when did the triple entente form between france britain and russia
where is the pearl district in portland oregon,"['https://www.coasthotels.com/hotels/oregon/portland/the-benson-hotel/local-guide/', 'http://www.cooperjacobspdx.com/goose-hollow-homes', 'https://www.streetadvisor.com/riverside-spokane-spokane-county-washington', 'https://www.marshmyers.com/blog/wandering-through-idaho-part-1', 'https://vivathelife.com/our-areas/washington-dc-2/foggy-bottom/', 'http://www.southportlandba.com/clinic-dogs-cats-coexist/', 'https://www.eugene-or.gov/1377/Harlow-Neighbors-Association']","The area is located just northwest of downtown between West Burnside Street on the south, the Willamette River on the north, NW Broadway on the east and the Interstate 405 freeway on the west.",where is the pearl district in portland oregon
what caused the earthquake in the movie san andreas,"['https://www.konsva.com/san-andreas-hollywood-movie-khmer-language/', 'https://www.dekhnews.com/watch-san-andreas-movie-world-television-tv-premiere-on-hbo-sunday-at-1-9-pm-6th-march-2016/', 'http://www.sholee.net/2015/10/mpov-san-andreas.html']","Raymond ""Ray"" Gaines is a Los Angeles Fire Department Air Rescue pilot in the midst of a divorce from his wife and planning a trip to San Francisco with his daughter Blake. Meanwhile, Caltech seismologist Dr. Lawrence Hayes and his colleague Dr. Kim Park are at Hoover Dam doing research for a new earthquake predicting model when a nearby and previously unknown fault ruptures. This triggers a 7.1 magnitude earthquake that collapses the dam and kills Park after he rescues a little girl and throws her to Hayes as he falls to the collapsing ground. When Ray is called into work because of this, Blake goes with her mother's new boyfriend Daniel Riddick to San Francisco, instead of Ray.",what caused the earthquake in the movie san andreas
who controls the factors of production in a free market economy,"['http://mlmconsultant.info/search?q=Economic%20system%20free%20market%20economy', 'http://www.global-econ.net/en/33-market-research.html', 'http://hitchhikersgui.de/Free_market_economy', 'https://www.readyratios.com/reference/business/market_economy.html', 'https://www.moneysavemoney.com/2017/04/in-market-economy-decisions-regarding-investment/', 'http://socialdemocracy21stcentury.blogspot.com/2013/', 'https://ahouserises2.wordpress.com/tag/politics/']","Market economies do not logically presuppose the existence of private ownership of the means of production. A market economy can and often does include various types of cooperatives, collectives, or autonomous state agencies that acquire and exchange capital goods in capital markets. These all utilize a market-determined free price system to allocate capital goods and labor. In addition, there are many variations of market socialism, some of which involve employee-owned enterprises based on self-management; as well as models that involve the combination of public ownership of the means of production with factor markets.",who controls the factors of production in a free market economy
where do bullets go when shot in the air,"['http://weirdfactss.com/2015/02/interesting-facts-bullets/', 'http://www.fwpd.org/celebratory-gunfire-illegal-122816/', 'https://outdoorever.com/how-far-can-a-bullet-travel/', 'https://www.crosman.com/airgunning/velocity', 'https://www.miamiherald.com/news/local/community/miami-dade/article191924834.html', 'http://www.newsflash.org/2004/02/pe/pe003794.htm']","Bullets fired into the air usually fall back with terminal velocities much lower than their muzzle velocity when they leave the barrel of a firearm. Nevertheless, people can be injured, sometimes fatally, when bullets discharged into the air fall back down to the ground. Bullets fired at angles less than vertical are more dangerous as the bullet maintains its angular ballistic trajectory and is far less likely to engage in tumbling motion; it therefore travels at speeds much higher than a bullet in free fall.",where do bullets go when shot in the air
what is a false positive or false negative,"['http://www.gabormelli.com/RKB/False_Positive_Prediction', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/False_positive', 'http://verticaldistinct.com/three-areas-to-concentrate-your-security-testing-efforts/']","In medical testing, and more generally in binary classification, a false positive is an error in data reporting in which a test result improperly indicates presence of a condition, such as a disease (the result is positive), when in reality it is not present, while a false negative is an error in which a test result improperly indicates no presence of a condition (the result is negative), when in reality it is present. These are the two kinds of errors in a binary test (and are contrasted with a correct result, either a true positive or a true negative.) They are also known in medicine as a false positive (respectively negative) diagnosis, and in statistical classification as a false positive (respectively negative) error. A false positive is distinct from overdiagnosis, and is also different from overtesting.",what is a false positive or false negative
as a response to the boston tea party parliament did this,"['https://fallenskiesblog.com/2016/08/23/boston-tea-party/', 'http://research.omicsgroup.org/index.php/Boston_Tea_Party', 'https://keepincalendar.com/December-16/Boston-Tea-Party/350', 'http://storiesofusa.com/the-american-revolution-revolutionary-war-battles-timeline-1770-1783/', 'http://www.paulksicinskilaw.com/blog/archives/01-2017', 'https://roughlydaily.com/tag/american-history/', 'http://coachoutleta.cf/kkkq/homework-help-boston-tea-party-bobo.php']","The Boston Tea Party was a significant event in the growth of the American Revolution. Parliament responded in 1774 with the Intolerable Acts, or Coercive Acts, which, among other provisions, ended local self-government in Massachusetts and closed Boston's commerce. Colonists up and down the Thirteen Colonies in turn responded to the Intolerable Acts with additional acts of protest, and by convening the First Continental Congress, which petitioned the British monarch for repeal of the acts and coordinated colonial resistance to them. The crisis escalated, and the American Revolutionary War began near Boston in 1775.",as a response to the boston tea party parliament did this
why are the ganesh statues immersed in water at the end of the festival,"['http://www.ganeshchaturthi2018images.in/', 'https://www.hotelrawalkot.com/tag/an-authentic-rajasthani-experience/', 'https://www.wikizero.com/en/Ganesh_Chaturthi', 'https://www.awesomenewyear.com/2018/05/ganesh-chaturthi-celebrations-in-india.html', 'https://healthyenvirosolutions.com/happy-ganesh-puja-2018/', 'https://www.smartpuja.com/Puja-Services-ganesha-chaturthi-puja-', 'https://www.123greetingmessage.net/ganesh-chaturthi-cartoon-funny-gif-videos-for-whatsapp-facebook-2017/']","Ganesh Chaturthi (IAST: Gaṇēśa Chaturthī), also known as Vinayaka Chaturthi (Vināyaka Chaturthī) is the Hindu festival that reveres god Ganesha. A ten-day festival, it starts on the fourth day of Hindu luni-solar calendar month Bhadrapada, which typically falls in Gregorian months of August or September. The festival is marked with installation of Ganesha clay idols privately in homes, or publicly on elaborate pandals (temporary stage). Observations include chanting of Vedic hymns and Hindu texts such as Ganapati Upanishad, prayers and vrata (fasting). Offerings and prasada from the daily prayers, that is distributed from the pandal to the community, include sweets such as modaka believed to be a favorite of the elephant-headed deity. The festival ends on the tenth day after start, wherein the idol is carried in a public procession with music and group chanting, then immersed in nearby water body such as a river or ocean, thereafter the clay idol dissolves and Ganesha is believed to return to Mount Kailash to Parvati and Shiva.",why are the ganesh statues immersed in water at the end of the festival
when is next part of sacred games coming,"['http://emeter.com/sacred-games-full-series-download.html', 'http://wikien3.appspot.com/wiki/Random_Acts_of_Flyness', 'http://emeter.com/sacred-games-season-2.html', 'http://www.projectcasting.com/casting-calls-acting-auditions/hbos-succession-season-2-is-now-casting-landscapers/', 'https://forums.stevehoffman.tv/threads/finished-deadwood-lost-mad-men-whats-next.338942/page-30', 'https://bestvseries.com/episodes/castle-rock-season-1-episode-8/', 'http://siluet.info/22/3122692-llama-llama-red-pajama-coloring-pages.html']","The first four episodes of Sacred Games premiered on 29 June 2018, with the full season of eight episodes released on Netflix on 6 July across 191 countries; it had subtitles in more than 20 languages. It received mostly positive reviews from critics, with particular praise for the performances and writing. In September 2018, it was announced that the series has been renewed for a second season.",when is next part of sacred games coming
name of a row in the periodic table,"['https://teesclawshirts.hatenadiary.com/entry/2018/11/03/005425', 'https://owlcation.com/stem/The-Wonders-of-the-Periodic-Table', 'http://ozonahockey.com/northwest-territories/chemistry-periodic-table-of-elements-with-names-pdf.php', 'http://conceptmap.cfapps.io/wikipage?lang=en&name=Periodic_table', 'http://pelangsingbadan.info/news.php?action=show&id=29552', 'http://agrogospodarstwa.info/news.php?subaction=showfull&id=6251', 'https://www.activityshelter.com/printable-periodic-tables/']","The periodic table is a tabular arrangement of the chemical elements, ordered by their atomic number, electron configuration, and recurring chemical properties, whose adopted structure shows periodic trends. Generally, within one row (period) the elements are metals on the left, and non-metals on the right, with the elements having similar chemical behaviours being placed in the same column. Table rows are commonly called periods and columns are called groups. Six groups have accepted names as well as assigned numbers: for example, group 17 elements are halogens; and group 18 are noble gases. Also displayed are four simple rectangular areas or blocks associated with the filling of different atomic orbitals.",name of a row in the periodic table
how do they figure out who goes to super bowl,"['https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Super_Bowl_LV', 'http://greenpoint.green/blogs/view/27265/super-bowl', 'http://galacticfootballleague.com/what-time-does-the-super-bowl-start/', 'https://www.haystack.tv/tag/superbowl', 'https://www.hartlepoolmail.co.uk/news/super-bowl-50-all-you-need-to-know-about-this-weekend-s-big-game-1-7717469', 'https://pontus-nilsson-kjce.squarespace.com/new-events', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Carl_Eller']","The game was created as part of a merger agreement between the NFL and its then-rival league, the American Football League (AFL). It was agreed that the two leagues' champion teams would play in the AFL -- NFL World Championship Game until the merger was to officially begin in 1970. After the merger, each league was redesignated as a ""conference"", and the game has since been played between the conference champions to determine the NFL's league champion. Currently, the National Football Conference (NFC) leads the league with 27 wins to 25 wins for the American Football Conference (AFC). The Pittsburgh Steelers have the most Super Bowl championship titles, with six. The New England Patriots have the most Super Bowl appearances, with ten. Charles Haley and Tom Brady both have five Super Bowl rings, which is the record for the most rings won by a single player.",how do they figure out who goes to super bowl
who created the 7 commandments in animal farm,"['https://rich1698.wordpress.com/2018/08/17/', 'https://www.antistudy.com/study-guide/id/171/animal-farm', 'https://www.mindmeister.com/1223121418/animal-farm', 'https://www.lovemombook.com/books/animal-farm-and-1984', 'https://wikimili.com/en/Animal_Farm', 'https://barbadostoday.bb/2016/06/01/barnyard-politics-we-have/', 'https://thegoodlifebunny.com/2017/02/26/sunday-book-club-animal-farm-by-george-orwell/']","When Major dies, two young pigs, Snowball and Napoleon, assume command and consider it a duty to prepare for the Rebellion. The animals revolt, driving the drunken, irresponsible farmer Mr Jones, as well as Mrs Jones and the other human caretakers and employees, off the farm, renaming it ""Animal Farm"". They adopt the Seven Commandments of Animalism, the most important of which is, ""All animals are equal"".",who created the 7 commandments in animal farm
when was the last time the lions won the superbowl,"['https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/List_of_Detroit_Lions_seasons.html', 'https://nationalticketagency.com/detroit-lions-tickets.html', 'https://crwflags.com/fotw/flags/us@f-lio.html', 'http://industrious.info/trends/03-12-2018/detroit-lions.html', 'http://www.nflonline.tv/Article/355/Live-Detroit-Lions/']","The Lions have won four NFL championships, tied for 9th overall in total championships amongst all 32 NFL franchises; however, their last was in 1957, which gives the club the second-longest NFL championship drought behind the Arizona Cardinals. They are one of four current teams and the only NFC team to have not yet played in the Super Bowl. They are also the only franchise to have been in operation for all 52 seasons of the Super Bowl era without having appeared in one. (The Cleveland Browns were not in operation for the 1996 to 1998 seasons.)",when was the last time the lions won the superbowl
does disney own the old star wars movies,"['https://uk-beta.animegami.com/shop/16/star-wars-episode-i-movie-masterpiece-action-figure-1-6-qui-gon-jinn-32-cm/', 'http://writingstudio.co.za/star-wars-the-force-awakens/', 'https://www.davidprasetyo.com/2015/05/download-movie-star-wars-episode-1-6-indowebster.html', 'https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars%3A_Episode_I_The_Phantom_Menace', 'https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Twentieth_Century_Fox_Film_Corporation', 'https://www.comicbookmovie.com/sci-fi/star_wars/', 'https://www.originalpeople.es/en/blogs/star-wars-sticker-decals.html']","In 2012, The Walt Disney Company bought Lucasfilm for US $4.06 billion and earned the distribution rights to all subsequent Star Wars films, beginning with the release of The Force Awakens in 2015. The former distributor, 20th Century Fox, was to retain the physical distribution rights for the first two Star Wars trilogies, was to own permanent rights for the original 1977 film and was to continue to hold the rights for the prequel trilogy and the first two sequels to A New Hope until May 2020. Walt Disney Studios currently owns digital distribution rights to all the Star Wars films, excluding A New Hope. On December 14, 2017, the Walt Disney Company announced its pending acquisition of 21st Century Fox, including the film studio and all distribution rights to A New Hope.",does disney own the old star wars movies
baroque is from the italian word barocco which means,"['https://blog.mararo.lk/2018/11/25/111/', 'http://viagraonlinegrs.com/where-was-viagra-invented-2/', 'https://www.nightofthemasked.ae/', 'https://www.majortests.com/essay/Music-Baroque-Period-538946.html', 'http://www.thelinguafile.com/2012/11/endonyms-and-exonyms-when-in-roma.html', 'https://www.barnebys.co.uk/blog/a-brief-history-of-design/', 'https://ritadicarne.com/page/2/']","The word baroque was a Portuguese term for a pearl (barocco) with an irregular shape. Cognates for the term in other Romance languages include: barroco in Portuguese, barrueco in Spanish, and barocco in Italian. It was used in French to describe pearls in a 1531 inventory of Charles V's treasures.",baroque is from the italian word barocco which means
how many times has the nba finals mvp been on the losing team,"['https://wikivivid.com/wiki/Hakeem_Olajuwon', 'https://infogalactic.com/info/Bill_Russell_NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player_Award', 'https://howlingpixel.com/i-en/Hakeem_Olajuwon', 'https://wikivisually.com/wiki/Larry_O%27Brien_Championship_Trophy', 'https://wn.com/Most_Improved_Player', 'http://wiki-offline.jakearchibald.com/wiki/Bill_Russell_NBA_Finals_Most_Valuable_Player_Award', 'https://ipfs.io/ipfs/QmXoypizjW3WknFiJnKLwHCnL72vedxjQkDDP1mXWo6uco/wiki/NBA_Defensive_Player_of_the_Year_Award.html']","Since its inception, the award has been given to 31 different players. Michael Jordan is a record six-time award winner. Magic Johnson, Shaquille O'Neal, Tim Duncan and LeBron James won the award three times in their careers. Jordan and O'Neal are the only players to win the award in three consecutive seasons (Jordan accomplished the feat on two separate occasions). Johnson is the only rookie ever to win the award, as well as the youngest at 20 years old. Andre Iguodala is the only winner to have not started every game in the series. Jerry West, the first ever awardee, is the only person to win the award while being on the losing team in the NBA Finals. Willis Reed, Kareem Abdul-Jabbar, Larry Bird, Hakeem Olajuwon, Kobe Bryant, and Kevin Durant won the award twice. Olajuwon, Durant, Bryant, and James have won the award in two consecutive seasons. Abdul-Jabbar and James are the only players to win the award for two different teams. Olajuwon of Nigeria, who became a naturalized U.S. citizen in 1993, Tony Parker of France, and Dirk Nowitzki of Germany are the only international players to win the award. Duncan is an American citizen, but is considered an ""international"" player by the NBA because he was not born in one of the fifty states or Washington, D.C. Parker and Nowitzki are the only winners to have been trained totally outside the U.S.; Olajuwon played college basketball at Houston and Duncan at Wake Forest. Cedric Maxwell is the only Finals MVP winner eligible for the Hall of Fame who has not been voted in.",how many times has the nba finals mvp been on the losing team
where did the battle of appomattox take place,"['https://wikimili.com/en/Abraham_Lincoln', 'http://thenewbostonteaparty.com/2016/01/page/2/', 'http://antietam.com/hagerstown-man-preserves-great-grandfathers', 'http://thomaslegioncherokee.tripod.com/battleofappomattoxcourthouse.html', 'https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/tag/appomattox/page/2/', 'https://worldhistoryproject.org/1865/4/9/battle-of-appomattox-court-house', 'https://www.redgreenlellow.com/battle-hymn-of-the-republic-meaning/']","The Battle of Appomattox Court House (Virginia, U.S.), fought on the morning of April 9, 1865, was one of the last battles of the American Civil War (1861-1865). It was the final engagement of Confederate States Army General-in-Chief, Robert E. Lee, and his Army of Northern Virginia before it surrendered to the Union Army / Army of the Potomac under the Commanding General of the United States, Ulysses S. Grant. Lee, having abandoned the Confederate capital of Richmond, Virginia, after the ten-month Siege of Petersburg and Richmond, retreated west, hoping to join his army with the remaining Confederate forces in North Carolina of the Army of Tennessee under Gen. Joseph E. Johnston. Union infantry and cavalry forces under Gen. Phillip Sheridan pursued and cut off the Confederates' retreat at the central Virginia village of Appomattox Court House. Lee launched a last-ditch attack to break through the Union forces to his front, assuming the Union force consisted entirely of lightly armed cavalry. When he realized that the cavalry was now backed up by two corps of Federal infantry, he had no choice but to surrender with his further avenue of retreat and escape now cut off.",where did the battle of appomattox take place
